 3D","de":"Three.js Builder: Framework für 3D-Web-Erlebnisse","pt":"Three.js Builder: Framework para Experiências Web 3D","ru":"Three.js Builder: Фреймворк для создания 3D-веб-опыта","ar":"Three.js Builder: إطار العمل لإنشاء تجارب ويب 3D","en":"threejs-builder"},"description":{"zh":"Three.js Builder是用于创建高性能、优雅的三维网页体验的框架。它支持现代ES模块，提供了易于使用的API","ja":"Three.js Builderは、高性能でエレガントな3Dウェブ体験を作成するためのフレームワークです。モダンなESモジュールをサポートしており、使用しやすいAPIを提供します","ko":"Three.js Builder는 고성능, 우아한 3D 웹 경험을 생성하기 위한 프레임워크입니다.现代 ES 모듈을 지원하며, 사용하기 쉬운 API를 제공합니다","es":"Three.js Builder es un framework para crear experiencias web 3D con módulos ES modernos. Ofrece una forma elegante y performante de crear aplicaciones web 3D","fr":"Three.js Builder est un cadre pour créer des expériences web 3D avec des modules ES modernes. Il offre une façon élégante et performante de créer des applica...","de":"Three.js Builder ist ein Framework für die Erstellung von 3D-Web-Erlebnissen mit modernen ES-Modulen. Es bietet eine elegante und performante Möglichkeit, 3D...","pt":"O Three.js Builder é um framework para criar experiências web 3D elegantes e de alto desempenho com módulos ES modernos.","ru":"Three.js Builder — это фреймворк для создания элегантных и производительных 3D-веб-опытов с современными модулями ES.","ar":"Three.js Builder هو إطار عمل لإنشاء تجارب ويب 3D أنيقة وذات أداء عالٍ باستخدام وحدات ES الحديثة.","en":"A vibe coded 3D game inspired by the Mario Party mini game. Made with Codex CLI and Agent Skills"},"definition":{"en":"A vibe coded 3D game inspired by the Mario Party mini game. Made with Codex CLI and Agent Skills"},"features":{"zh":["支持现代ES模块","高性能渲染","易于使用的API","支持GLTF模型加载","支持参考帧"],"ja":["モダンなESモジュールをサポート","高性能レンダリング","使用しやすいAPI","GLTFモデル読み込みのサポート","参考フレームのサポート"],"ko":["现代 ES 모듈 지원","고성능 렌더링","사용하기 쉬운 API","GLTF 모델 로딩 지원","참조 프레임 지원"],"es":["Carga y caché de modelos 3D","Compatibilidad con módulos ES modernos","Elegante y performante","Soporte para GLTF y Reference Frames","Guías de referencia para temas específicos"],"fr":["Chargement et mise en cache de modèles 3D","Compatibilité avec des modules ES modernes","Élégant et performant","Prise en charge de GLTF et de Reference Frames","Guides de référence pour des sujets spécifiques"],"de":["Laden und Cachen von 3D-Modellen","Kompatibilität mit modernen ES-Modulen","Elegant und performant","Unterstützung für GLTF und Reference Frames","Referenzhandbücher für spezifische Themen"],"pt":["Criação de experiências web 3D elegantes","Suporte a módulos ES modernos","Otimização para alto desempenho","Compatibilidade com o Codex CLI","Recursos de carregamento e cache de modelos 3D"],"ru":["Создание элегантных 3D-веб-опытов","Поддержка современных модулей ES","Оптимизация для высокой производительности","Совместимость с Codex CLI","Возможности загрузки и кэширования 3D-моделей"],"ar":["إنشاء تجارب ويب 3D أنيقة","دعم لوحدات ES الحديثة","تحسين الأداء العالي","توافق مع Codex CLI","ميزات تحميل وذاكرة التخزين المؤقتة لتنسيق 3D"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Three.js","三维网页体验","高性能渲染","现代ES模块","GLTF模型加载","参考帧","Codex-ready框架"],"ja":["Three.js","3Dウェブ体験","高性能レンダリング","モダンなESモジュール","GLTFモデル読み込み","参考フレーム","Codex-readyフレームワーク"],"ko":["Three.js","3D 웹 경험","고성능 렌더링","현대 ES 모듈","GLTF 모델 로딩","참조 프레임","Codex-ready 프레임워크"],"es":["Three.js","framework 3D","experiencias web 3D","módulos ES","GLTF","Reference Frames","desarrollo web 3D","aplicaciones web 3D"],"fr":["Three.js","cadre 3D","expériences web 3D","modules ES","GLTF","Reference Frames","développement web 3D","applications web 3D"],"de":["Three.js","Framework 3D","3D-Web-Erlebnisse","ES-Module","GLTF","Reference Frames","Web-Entwicklung 3D","3D-Web-Anwendungen"],"pt":["Three.js","Desenvolvimento web 3D","Experiências web 3D","Módulos ES","Codex CLI","Modelos 3D","Otimização de desempenho"],"ru":["Three.js","Разработка 3D-веб-опытов","3D-веб-опыты","Модули ES","Codex CLI","3D-модели","Оптимизация производительности"],"ar":["Three.js","تطوير ويب 3D","تجارب ويب 3D","وحدات ES","Codex CLI","نماذج 3D","تحسين الأداء"]}},"owner":"chongdashu","repo":"threejs-forest-census","repoPath":"chongdashu/threejs-forest-census","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.466Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"threejs-builder","description":"Design and implement lightweight Three.js (r150+) ES-module scenes—hero sections, interactive product viewers, particle backdrops, GLTF showcases, or quick prototypes—whenever prompts mention three.js/threejs scene, 3D web background, orbit controls, or WebGL demo.","bodyPreview":"# Three.js Builder\n\nA Codex-ready framework for shipping elegant, performant Three.js web experiences with modern ES modules.\n\n## Reference Files\n\n> **Read the appropriate reference when working on specific topics:**\n\n| Topic | File | Use When |\n|-------|------|----------|\n| **GLTF Models** | `references/gltf-loading-guide.md` | Loading, caching, cloning 3D models, SkeletonUtils |\n| **Reference Frames** | `references/reference-frame-contract.md` | Calibration, anchoring, axis correctness, debugg","body":"# Three.js Builder\n\nA Codex-ready framework for shipping elegant, performant Three.js web experiences with modern ES modules.\n\n## Reference Files\n\n> **Read the appropriate reference when working on specific topics:**\n\n| Topic | File | Use When |\n|-------|------|----------|\n| **GLTF Models** | `references/gltf-loading-guide.md` | Loading, caching, cloning 3D models, SkeletonUtils |\n| **Reference Frames** | `references/reference-frame-contract.md` | Calibration, anchoring, axis correctness, debugging |\n| **Game Development** | `references/game-patterns.md` | State machines, animation switching, parallax, pooling |\n| **Advanced Topics** | `references/advanced-topics.md` | Post-processing, shaders, physics, instancing |\n| **Calibration Helpers** | `scripts/README.md` | GLTF calibration helper installation and usage |\n\n---\n\n## Philosophy: Start from Scene Intent\n\nThree.js work lives inside a scene graph: parents transform children, and everything in `scene` is rendered.\n\n**Before writing code, ask**:\n- What is the core visual element or metaphor (hero object, particle field, data glyph)?\n- How should visitors manipulate or perceive it (static hero, orbit control, camera-relative movement)?\n- What level of hardware/performance do we target (mobile hero snippet vs. desktop interactive)?\n- Which animation best communicates the story (continuous rotation, bobbing, interaction-driven)?\n\n**Core principles**:\n1. **Scene graph first** – model hierarchy and transforms before materials.\n2. **Intent-driven primitives** – boxes, spheres, torus, planes cover 80% of hero cases; reach for GLTF only when fidelity demands it.\n3. **Animation as transformation** – treat animation as evolving position/rotation/scale with `renderer.setAnimationLoop`.\n4. **Performance through restraint** – reuse geometries/materials, clamp device pixel ratio, keep draw calls low.\n\n---\n\n## Foundational Principle: Lock a “Reference Frame Contract” First\n\nMost Three.js bugs are not “rendering bugs” — they’re **reference-frame bugs**: wrong origin, wrong up-axis assumption, wrong forward direction, wrong “ground = y=0” semantics, wrong color space, or wrong loading environment.\n\nTreat your scene like a contract you must prove once, then never violate:\n- **Axes**: which way is forward for gameplay, and how do models map to it?\n- **Anchors**: what does “on the ground” mean for each asset class?\n- **Units**: what is 1 unit (meter-ish? pixel-ish?) and how do imported assets fit?\n- **Color**: are textures and output color space correct?\n\nIf you don’t lock this contract early, you will chase symptoms: inverted movement, floating/sinking models, “wrongly loaded” textures, and end-state hangs caused by tangled state transitions.\n\n### The Calibration Pass (do this before building gameplay)\nDo a 60-second calibration scene and lock constants (axes/anchors/scale/color) before shipping gameplay systems.\n\nDeep guide + troubleshooting map: `references/reference-frame-contract.md`\n\n### Mesh Forward Verification (Do Not Guess)\nDon’t “eyeball rotate until it looks right” and don’t assume “GLTF faces `-Z`”.\n\nIn the calibration scene, **prove** each imported model’s forward direction and lock it as a constant (global `MODEL_YAW_OFFSET` or per-asset `yawOffset`).\n\nIf you want a reusable helper module instead of hand-rolling arrows/box helpers each time:\n- Install (repo-scoped): run `python3 .codex/skills/threejs-builder/scripts/install-gltf-calibration-helpers.py --out ./gltf-calibration-helpers.mjs`\n- Install (from within the skill folder): run `python3 scripts/install-gltf-calibration-helpers.py --out ./gltf-calibration-helpers.mjs`\n- Use: import and call `attachGltfCalibrationHelpers(...)` (see `scripts/README.md`)\n\nMinimal check:\n```js\n// In Three.js, an Object3D’s \"forward\" is its local -Z axis.\nconst localForward = new THREE.Vector3(0, 0, -1);\n\n// Attach a visible arrow to the model so you can *see* its forward.\nconst forwardArrow = new THREE.ArrowHelper(localForward, new THREE.Vector3(0, 1.2, 0), 1.2, 0xff00ff);\nmodelRoot.add(forwardArrow);\n\n// Also log the current world-forward for debugging (post-normalization and post-rotation).\nconst worldForward = new THREE.Vector3();\nmodelRoot.getWorldDirection(worldForward);\nconsole.log(''model world forward (-Z):'', worldForward.toArray());\n```\n\nThen decide:\n- If the mesh runs backward, set `yawOffset = Math.PI`.\n- If it faces the camera (common symptom), your yaw convention is wrong—flip the offset and re-check.\n\n## Coordinate System & Camera Awareness (Critical)\n\nThree.js is right-handed: +X right, +Y up, +Z toward the camera. Many GLTF assets are authored facing `-Z`, but **verify per pack** (don’t assume). Camera-relative controls must project the camera forward vector onto the XZ plane, normalize, then derive the right vector via a right-handed cross product to avoid inverted WASD when the camera orbits.\n\n```\nconst forward = new THREE.Vector3();\ncamera.getWorldDirection(forward);\nforward.y = 0;\nforward.normalize();\n// Right-handed basis (DON''T swap arguments): right = forward × up\nconst right = new THREE.Vector3().crossVectors(forward, new THREE.Vector3(0, 1, 0));\n```\n\nPractical rule:\n- If A/D is inverted, your cross product order is wrong (or you need to flip `forward` with `forward.negate()` depending on your convention). Fix the basis, not the key mapping.\n\n---\n\n## Origins & “Ground” Anchors (Stop Guessing)\n\nAnchoring is an asset-contract decision, not a “tweak until it looks right” decision.\n\nRule of thumb:\n- Characters/props: `minY = 0`\n- Ground tiles: often `maxY = 0` (walkable surface)\n\nDeep guide + example code: `references/reference-frame-contract.md`\n\n---\n\n## Build Flow\n\n### 1. Frame the Experience\n- Define the vibe (portfolio, gamey, data viz) and jot a mini mood board (colors, light style, animation verbs).\n- Choose interaction tier: static render, auto-rotation, OrbitControls, or custom camera/gameplay loop.\n- Sketch layout: do you need a ground plane, backdrop gradient, floating particles, or spotlight object?\n\n### 2. Establish Runtime Foundations\n- Use modern ES modules—no global `THREE`. Import from `three` package or CDN versions (>=0.150).\n- Minimal HTML template:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Three.js Scene</title>\n  <style>body{margin:0;overflow:hidden;background:#010103;}canvas{display:block;}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <script type=\"module\">\n    import * as THREE from ''https://unpkg.com/three@0.160.0/build/three.module.js'';\n\n    const scene = new THREE.Scene();\n    const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(60, innerWidth / innerHeight, 0.1, 2000);\n    camera.position.set(0, 1.5, 4.5);\n\n    const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true });\n    renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n    renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2));\n    renderer.outputColorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;\n    document.body.appendChild(renderer.domElement);\n\n    window.addEventListener(''resize'', () => {\n      camera.aspect = innerWidth / innerHeight;\n      camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n      renderer.setSize(innerWidth, innerHeight);\n    });\n  </script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n- Plug OrbitControls from `three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js` when interaction is needed, enable damping, and call `controls.update()` each frame.\n\n### 2.5 GLTF Loading Guardrails (When You Use Models)\n- Run via a local server (not `file://`) so relative resources resolve reliably.\n- For animated/skinned GLTF instancing, use `SkeletonUtils.clone()` (plain `.clone()` breaks skeleton links).\n- Always log animation clip names after load and select by exact string (avoid “best guess” name matching unless it’s a deliberate fallback).\n- If your asset pack uses an atlas, avoid “multiply tinting” materials (it can turn textured models into weird flat colors). Prefer leaving `material.color` at white and using emissive/lighting for emphasis.\n\n### 3. Compose the Scene\n- **Geometries**: prefer built-ins (Box, Sphere, Torus, Plane, Cone, Icosahedron). For particle clouds use `BufferGeometry` + `Float32Array` positions.\n- **Materials**: pick `MeshStandardMaterial` as default (tweak `roughness`/`metalness`), `MeshPhysicalMaterial` for glass/liquids, `MeshBasicMaterial` for unlit accents, `PointsMaterial` for particles.\n- **Lighting**: start with Ambient (0.3–0.5) + Directional key + colored fill; enable shadows only when necessary and set `renderer.shadowMap.enabled = true` + map sizes of 1024–2048.\n- **Color palettes**: define constants (e.g., `const COLORS = { primary: 0xff6600, accent: 0x0ff0ff }`) and keep backgrounds dark to let emissive tones pop.\n\n### 4. Animate & Interact\n- Implement animation loops with `renderer.setAnimationLoop((time) => { ... renderer.render(scene, camera); });`.\n- Common patterns:\n  - Continuous rotation with `mesh.rotation.y = time * 0.001`.\n  - Bobbing via `mesh.position.y = Math.sin(time * 0.002) * 0.4`.\n  - Mouse-reactive tilt: normalize pointer coords and lerp rotations for smoothness.\n  - Camera-relative character motion for interactive demos (see snippet above for direction vectors).\n- Store state outside the loop (e.g., `const inputState = { up: false, ... }`).\n\n### 4.5 State Machines & “Time Ran Out” Bugs\nIf your app “hangs” at time-out, it’s almost always because multiple systems are competing to transition state.\n\nGuardrails:\n- Use a single `state.mode` and a single transition function.\n- Treat `timeLeft <= 0` as terminal and clamp it once: `timeLeft = Math.max(0, timeLeft - dt)`.\n- Add a one-way latch like `hasEnded` so the end transition can only happen once.\n\n### 5. Polish & Performance\n- Cap `renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(devicePixelRatio, 2))` to keep 4K laptops smooth.\n- Reuse geometries/materials, avoid instantiating inside the animation loop.\n- Use helpers (GridHelper, AxesHelper) for debugging, but remove them for production scenes.\n- Separate setup helpers (e.g., `createLights()`/`createMeshes()`) to keep files navigable.\n\n---\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n❌ **Legacy global builds**: Using `<script src=\"three.js\"></script>` and accessing `THREE` globals breaks tree-shaking and OrbitControls imports. Use ES modules.\n\n❌ **Camera-blind controls**: Mapping WASD directly to world axes feels wrong once the camera rotates. Always derive movement vectors from the camera orientation.\n\n❌ **Floating/sinking fixes by “random y offsets”**: If you’re tweaking `position.y` in 5 places, your anchoring strategy is missing.\nWhy bad: you’ll never converge across ground tiles vs characters vs props.\nBetter: normalize each asset to a declared anchor (`minY` or `maxY`) at load time and only place the wrapper.\n\n❌ **Asset guessing**: Assuming GLTF forward direction, scale, or animation names without a calibration pass.\nBetter: build a 60-second calibration scene and lock constants (forward offsets, anchors, heights).\n\n❌ **Off-center canvases from transform math**: Mixing `translate()` + `scale()` with the wrong `transform-origin` makes the render area drift.\nBetter: center via layout (flex/grid) and apply `scale()` only, with `transform-origin: center`.\n\n❌ **Geometry churn inside loops**: Creating geometries/materials each frame tanks GC and FPS. Instantiate once and mutate transforms only.\n\n❌ **Overly dense primitives**: Jumping to `SphereGeometry(1, 128, 128)` without purpose wastes perf; start with defaults and scale segments only when silhouetted edges demand it.\n\n❌ **Unbounded pixel ratio**: Forgetting to clamp `devicePixelRatio` makes retina users suffer. Always clamp to ≤2 unless photorealism is mandatory.\n\n---\n\n## Variation Guidance\n\n- **Purpose-specific styling**:\n  - Portfolio hero → slow easing, glossy lighting, analogous palettes.\n  - Game prototype → punchy colors, contrasty lights, camera-relative controls, particles.\n  - Data viz → clean planes, grid helpers, consistent units, annotations.\n  - Background loop → subtle gradients, low-frequency motion, ambient glow.\n- **Mix geometry/material** choices: cycle through spheres, rounded boxes, low-poly icosahedrons, tubes. Experiment with `flatShading`, `wireframe`, emissive blooms.\n- **Camera moods**: alternate between dolly-in hero (z≈4), aerial tilt (camera.set(8, 11, -6)), or isometric (45° yaw). Pair with matching movement logic.\n- **Animation verbs**: rotate, pulse, orbit, flock, noise-driven drift. Avoid always rotating cubes at `0.001` speed.\n\n---\n\n## Remember\n\nThree.js scenes succeed when the mental model (scene graph + intent) guides the build. Lead with philosophy, respect the coordinate system, keep loops lean, and vary geometry, lighting, and animation so every experience feels purpose-built. Let these patterns unlock creativity—they are rails, not cages.\n\nFor specific topics, see the **Reference Files** table at the top of this document.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:22:22.844Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Frontend Agents needing advanced 3D web experience capabilities with Three.js and modern ES modules.","zh":"适用于需要高级 3D 网页体验能力的前端代理，支持 Three.js 和现代 ES 模块。","ja":"Three.js およびモダン ES モジュールを使用した高度な 3D Web エクスペリエンス機能を必要とするフロントエンド エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Three.js 및 현대적인 ES 모듈을 사용한 고급 3D 웹 경험 기능이 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes Frontend que necesitan capacidades de experiencia web 3D avanzadas con Three.js y módulos ES modernos.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Frontend ayant besoin de fonctionnalités de expérience web 3D avancées avec Three.js et des modules ES modernes.","de":"Ideal für Frontend-Agents, die erweiterte 3D-Web-Erfahrungsfunktionen mit Three.js und modernen ES-Modulen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de capacidades de experiência web 3D avançadas com Three.js e módulos ES modernos.","ru":"Идеально для фронтенд-агентов, требующих расширенных возможностей веб-опыта 3D с Three.js и современными модулями ES.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الواجهة الأمامية الذين يحتاجون إلى قدرات تجربة ويب ثلاثية الأبعاد متقدمة مع Three.js ووحدات ES الحديثة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to ship elegant, performant Three.js web experiences with features like GLTF model loading, caching, and cloning, utilizing SkeletonUtils and reference frames for calibration and anchoring.","zh":"赋予代理创建优雅、高性能的 Three.js 网页体验的能力，具有加载和缓存 GLTF 模型、使用 SkeletonUtils 和参考帧进行校准和锚定等功能。","ja":"Three.js Web エクスペリエンスの作成をエージェントに可能にし、GLTF モデルの読み込み、キャッシング、クローニングなどの機能を提供し、SkeletonUtils および参照フレームを使用して校準およびアンカーを行います。","ko":"에이전트가 Three.js 웹 경험을 우아하고 고성능으로 제공할 수 있도록 하며, GLTF 모델 로딩, 캐싱, 클론 생성 등의 기능과 SkeletonUtils 및 참조 프레임을 사용한 校準 및 앵커 지정 등을 활용합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes enviar experiencias web elegantes y de alto rendimiento con Three.js con características como carga de modelos GLTF, almacenamiento en caché y clonación, utilizando SkeletonUtils y marcos de referencia para calibración y anclaje.","fr":"Permet aux agents de diffuser des expériences web Three.js élégantes et performantes avec des fonctionnalités telles que le chargement de modèles GLTF, la mise en cache et le clonage, en utilisant SkeletonUtils et des cadres de référence pour l''étalonnage et l''ancrage.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, elegante und leistungsfähige Three.js-Web-Erfahrungen mit Funktionen wie GLTF-Modellladen, Zwischenspeichern und Klonen auszuliefern, wobei SkeletonUtils und Referenzrahmen für Kalibrierung und Verankerung verwendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a enviar experiências web Three.js elegantes e de alto desempenho com recursos como carregamento de modelos GLTF, cache e clonagem, utilizando SkeletonUtils e quadros de referência para calibração e ancoragem.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать элегантные и производительные веб-опыты Three.js с функциями, такими как загрузка моделей GLTF, кэширование и клонирование, используя SkeletonUtils и рамки ссылок для калибровки и якорения.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على إرسال تجارب ويب Three.js أنيقة وذات أداء عالي مع ميزات مثل تحميل نماذج GLTF وتخزينها مؤقتًا والاستنساخ، باستخدام SkeletonUtils وإطارات المرجعية للتعيين والترسيم."},"useCases":{"en":["Loading and caching 3D GLTF models for web applications","Calibrating and anchoring reference frames for axis correctness","Debugging Three.js web experiences with reference frame contracts"],"zh":["为网页应用程序加载和缓存 3D GLTF 模型","校准和固定参考帧以确保轴向正确性","使用参考帧契约调试 Three.js 网页体验"],"ja":["Web アプリケーションのために 3D GLTF モデルを読み込み、キャッシングする","軸の正確性を確保するために参照フレームを校準、固定する","参照フレーム契約を使用して Three.js Web エクスペリエンスのデバッグを行う"],"ko":["웹 애플리케이션을 위한 3D GLTF 모델 로딩 및 캐싱","축 방향 정확성을 보장하기 위한 참조 프레임의 校準 및 고정","참조 프레임 계약을 사용한 Three.js 웹 경험 디버깅"],"es":["Carga y almacenamiento en caché de modelos 3D GLTF para aplicaciones web","Calibración y anclaje de marcos de referencia para la corrección del eje","Depuración de experiencias web Three.js con contratos de marco de referencia"],"fr":["Chargement et mise en cache de modèles 3D GLTF pour les applications web","Étalonnage et ancrage des cadres de référence pour la correction de l''axe","Débogage des expériences web Three.js avec des contrats de cadre de référence"],"de":["Laden und Zwischenspeichern von 3D-GLTF-Modellen für Webanwendungen","Kalibrierung und Verankerung von Referenzrahmen für die Achsenkorrektheit","Fehlerbehebung bei Three.js-Web-Erfahrungen mit Referenzrahmenverträgen"],"pt":["Carregamento e cache de modelos 3D GLTF para aplicações web","Calibração e ancoragem de quadros de referência para correção do eixo","Depuração de experiências web Three.js com contratos de quadro de referência"],"ru":["Загрузка и кэширование 3D-моделей GLTF для веб-приложений","Калибровка и якорение рамок ссылок для правильности оси","Отладка веб-опытов Three.js с контрактами рамки ссылки"],"ar":["تحميل ونماذج 3D GLTF لتطبيقات الويب، وتخزينها مؤقتًا","تعيين وإرساء إطارات المرجعية لتصحيح المحور","تصحيح أخطاء تجارب الويب Three.js مع عقود إطار المرجعية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Codex CLI and Agent Skills integration","Specific to Three.js and modern ES modules"],"zh":["需要 Codex CLI 和 Agent Skills 集成","仅限 Three.js 和现代 ES 模块"],"ja":["Codex CLI およびエージェント スキルの統合が必要","Three.js およびモダン ES モジュールに限定される"],"ko":["Codex CLI 및 에이전트 스킬 통합이 필요함","Three.js 및 현대적인 ES 모듈에만 국한됨"],"es":["Requiere la integración de Codex CLI y Agent Skills","Específico para Three.js y módulos ES modernos"],"fr":["Nécessite l''intégration de Codex CLI et Agent Skills","Spécifique à Three.js et aux modules ES modernes"],"de":["Benötigt die Integration von Codex CLI und Agent Skills","Spezifisch für Three.js und moderne ES-Module"],"pt":["Requer integração do Codex CLI e habilidades do agente","Específico para Three.js e módulos ES modernos"],"ru":["Требует интеграции Codex CLI и навыков агента","Специфичен для Three.js и современных модулей ES"],"ar":["يتطلب تكامل Codex CLI و مهارات الوكيل","محدد ل Three.js ووحدات ES الحديثة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
