","fr":"Outil d''affinage de rythme pour les documents LaTeX qui améliore la lisibilité et le flux de la prose académique","de":"Werkzeug zum Verfeinern des Rhythmus für LaTeX-Dokumente, das die Lesbarkeit und den Fluss der akademischen Prosa verbessert","pt":"O LaTeX Rhythm Refiner é uma ferramenta para melhorar a fluidez e legibilidade de documentos acadêmicos.","ru":"Улучшение ритма LaTeX - это инструмент для улучшения потока и читаемости академических документов.","ar":"مُحسّن إيقاع LaTeX هو أداة لتحسين سهولة القراءة وفهماً للمستندات الأكاديمية.","en":"A .codex SKILL for issue-driven ML/AI arXiv review papers: scaffold LaTeX + verify BibTeX citations end-to-end."},"definition":{"en":"A .codex SKILL for issue-driven ML/AI arXiv review papers: scaffold LaTeX + verify BibTeX citations end-to-end."},"features":{"zh":["优化LaTeX文档的可读性和流畅度","保持引文的准确性和语义上下文","改善学术文档的结构和组织","支持BibTeX引文验证","提高文档的整体质量和专业性"],"ja":["LaTeX 文書の可読性と流暢性を最適化","引用の正確性とセマンティックコンテキストを保持","学術文書の構造と組織を改善","BibTeX 引用の検証をサポート","文書の全体的な品質とプロフェッショナリズムを向上"],"ko":["LaTeX 문서의 가독성과 유창성을 최적화","인용의 정확성과 의미적 문맥을 유지","학술 문서의 구조와 조직을 개선","BibTeX 인용 확인 지원","문서의 전체적인 품질과 전문성을 향상"],"es":["Mejora el flujo de la prosa académica","Mantiene intactas las citas BibTeX","Optimiza la legibilidad de los documentos","No altera el contexto semántico de las citas","Permite la verificación de citas de extremo a extremo"],"fr":["Améliore le flux de la prose académique","Préserve les citations BibTeX intactes","Optimise la lisibilité des documents","Ne modifie pas le contexte sémantique des citations","Permet la vérification des citations de bout en bout"],"de":["Verbessert den Fluss der akademischen Prosa","BibTeX-Zitate bleiben unverändert","Optimiert die Lesbarkeit von Dokumenten","Ändert den semantischen Kontext von Zitaten nicht","Ermöglicht die Überprüfung von Zitaten von Anfang bis Ende"],"pt":["Preserva as citações exatamente","Melhora a fluidez do texto","Otimiza a legibilidade dos documentos","Não altera a estrutura técnica do LaTeX","Verifica as citações BibTeX"],"ru":["Сохраняет цитаты точно","Улучшает поток текста","Оптимизирует читаемость документов","Не изменяет техническую структуру LaTeX","Проверяет цитаты BibTeX"],"ar":["تحافظ على المراجع بدقة","تحسّن تدفق النص","تحسين سهولة قراءة المستندات","لا تغير الهيكل الفني للlatex","تفحص المراجع BibTeX"]},"keywords":{"zh":["LaTeX","学术文档","可读性","流畅度","引文","BibTeX","文档优化","结构改善","专业性"],"ja":["LaTeX","学術文書","可読性","流暢性","引用","BibTeX","文書最適化","構造改善","プロフェッショナリズム"],"ko":["LaTeX","학술 문서","가독성","유창성","인용","BibTeX","문서 최적화","구조 개선","전문성"],"es":["LaTeX","refinador de ritmo","prosa académica","legibilidad","citas BibTeX","documentos académicos","verificación de citas"],"fr":["LaTeX","affineur de rythme","prose académique","lisibilité","citations BibTeX","documents académiques","vérification de citations"],"de":["LaTeX","Rhythmus Refiner","akademische Prosa","Lesbarkeit","BibTeX-Zitate","akademische Dokumente","Zitatsüberprüfung"],"pt":["LaTeX Rhythm Refiner","Otimização de texto","Legibilidade de documentos","Citações BibTeX","Estrutura de texto","Documentos acadêmicos"],"ru":["Улучшение ритма LaTeX","Оптимизация текста","Читаемость документов","Цитаты BibTeX","Структура текста","Академические документы"],"ar":["مُحسّن إيقاع LaTeX","تحسين النص","قراءة المستندات","مراجع BibTeX","هيكل النص","المستندات الأكاديمية"]}},"owner":"renocrypt","repo":"latex-arxiv-SKILL","repoPath":"renocrypt/latex-arxiv-SKILL","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.466Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"latex-rhythm-refiner","description":">","bodyPreview":"# LaTeX Rhythm Refiner\n\n## When to Use\n- After LaTeX content generation is complete\n- To improve prose flow and readability in academic documents\n- When sections feel monotonous or blocky\n\n## When NOT to Use\n- During initial content drafting\n- For citation verification or addition\n- For technical/structural LaTeX fixes\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Preserve Citations Exactly\n- Every `\\cite{...}` must remain in place\n- Citations stay attached to their original semantic context\n- Never move a citati","body":"# LaTeX Rhythm Refiner\n\n## When to Use\n- After LaTeX content generation is complete\n- To improve prose flow and readability in academic documents\n- When sections feel monotonous or blocky\n\n## When NOT to Use\n- During initial content drafting\n- For citation verification or addition\n- For technical/structural LaTeX fixes\n\n## Core Principles\n\n### 1. Preserve Citations Exactly\n- Every `\\cite{...}` must remain in place\n- Citations stay attached to their original semantic context\n- Never move a citation to a different claim or sentence meaning\n\n### 2. Vary Rhythm Stochastically\n**Sentence length**: Mix short (5-12 words), medium (13-22 words), and long (23-35 words) sentences. Avoid consecutive sentences of similar length.\n\n**Paragraph length**: Alternate between:\n- Short (2-3 sentences) for emphasis or transitions\n- Medium (4-5 sentences) for standard exposition\n- Long (6-8 sentences) for complex arguments\n\n### 3. Remove Fillers\nEliminate or replace:\n- \"in order to\" → \"to\"\n- \"it is worth noting that\" → (delete or rephrase directly)\n- \"due to the fact that\" → \"because\"\n- \"in the context of\" → \"in\" or \"for\"\n- \"a large number of\" → \"many\"\n- \"in spite of the fact that\" → \"although\"\n- \"at the present time\" → \"now\" or \"currently\"\n- \"for the purpose of\" → \"to\" or \"for\"\n\n### 4. Minimize Transitions\nRemove when structure already implies the relationship:\n- \"However,\" / \"Therefore,\" / \"Moreover,\" / \"Furthermore,\"\n- \"As mentioned above,\" / \"As previously discussed,\"\n- \"It should be noted that\" / \"In this regard,\"\n\n### 5. Tighten Prose\n- Prefer active voice; replace vague verbs (\"shows\", \"does\", \"works\") with concrete ones\n- Avoid repeated sentence openings across adjacent sentences (\"This\", \"In practice\", etc.)\n- Replace hedge stacks (\"may potentially\") with one qualifier\n- Each paragraph: one main idea, clear first sentence\n- Ensure figures/tables are referenced and explained in text\n\n## Processing Workflow\n\n### Per-Section Refinement\nProcess one section at a time:\n\n1. **Read** the section fully to understand context and argument flow\n2. **Identify** all `\\cite{...}` locations and their attached claims\n3. **Map** current sentence/paragraph lengths\n4. **Refine**:\n   - Vary sentence lengths (break long chains, combine choppy sequences)\n   - Adjust paragraph boundaries for rhythm\n   - Strip fillers and unnecessary transitions\n5. **Verify** all citations remain with their original semantic claims\n6. **Output** the refined section\n\n### Verification Checklist\nBefore finalizing each section:\n- [ ] Citation count unchanged\n- [ ] Each citation still supports its original claim\n- [ ] No 3+ consecutive sentences of similar length\n- [ ] Paragraph lengths vary\n- [ ] Filler phrases removed\n- [ ] Unnecessary transitions eliminated\n- [ ] Technical accuracy preserved\n\n## Constraints\n- **Do not** add, remove, or relocate citations\n- **Do not** change technical claims or data\n- **Do not** alter LaTeX commands, environments, or structure\n- **Do not** modify figure/table references or captions\n- **Do not** expand abbreviations or change terminology\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:25:07.322Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Academic Writing Agents requiring precise LaTeX document refinement and BibTeX citation verification.","zh":"适用于需要精确 LaTeX 文档改进和 BibTeX 引用验证的学术写作代理。","ja":"精密なLaTeX文書の改良とBibTeX引用の検証を必要とする学術文章エージェントに適しています。","ko":"정확한 LaTeX 문서 개선 및 BibTeX 인용 확인이 필요한 학술 작성 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de escritura académica que requieren un refinamiento preciso de documentos LaTeX y verificación de citas BibTeX.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''écriture académique nécessitant un affinement précis de documents LaTeX et une vérification de citations BibTeX.","de":"Ideal für akademische Schreibagenten, die eine präzise Verfeinerung von LaTeX-Dokumenten und eine BibTeX-Zitierüberprüfung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Escrita Acadêmica que exigem refinamento preciso de documentos LaTeX e verificação de citações BibTeX.","ru":"Идеально для академических агентов написания, требующих точного усовершенствования документов LaTeX и проверки цитат BibTeX.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الكتابة الأكاديمية الذي يتطلب تحسينًا دقيقًا لتوثيق LaTeX والتحقق من الاقتباسات BibTeX."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to refine LaTeX documents by improving prose flow and readability, while preserving BibTeX citations exactly, utilizing end-to-end verification and ensuring semantic context integrity.","zh":"赋予代理人通过提高文章流畅度和可读性来改进LaTeX文档的能力，同时保留BibTeX引用，并利用端到端的验证来确保语义上下文的完整性。","ja":"エージェントがLaTeX文書を改良できるようにし、文章の流れと可読性を向上させ、BibTeX引用を正確に保持し、エンドツーエンドの検証を利用して意味的コンテキストの完全性を確保します。","ko":"에이전트가 LaTeX 문서를 개선할 수 있도록하여 문장의 흐름과 가독성을 향상시키고, BibTeX 인용을 정확하게 유지하며, 끝에서 끝까지의 검증을 사용하여 의미적 문脈의 완전성을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a perfeccionar documentos LaTeX mejorando el flujo de prosa y la legibilidad, mientras se conservan las citas BibTeX exactamente, utilizando una verificación de extremo a extremo y garantizando la integridad del contexto semántico.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''affiner les documents LaTeX en améliorant le flux de prose et la lisibilité, tout en préservant les citations BibTeX exactement, en utilisant une vérification de bout en bout et en garantissant l''intégrité du contexte sémantique.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, LaTeX-Dokumente zu verfeinern, indem sie den Prosafly und die Lesbarkeit verbessern, während die BibTeX-Zitate genau beibehalten werden, unter Verwendung einer End-to-End-Überprüfung und Gewährleistung der Integrität des semantischen Kontexts.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a refinarem documentos LaTeX melhorando o fluxo de prosa e a legibilidade, preservando exatamente as citações BibTeX, utilizando verificação de ponta a ponta e garantindo a integridade do contexto semântico.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью усовершенствовать документы LaTeX, улучшая поток и читаемость текста, сохраняя при этом точность цитат BibTeX, используя проверку от начала до конца и обеспечивая целостность семантического контекста.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تحسين توثيق LaTeX عن طريق تحسين تدفق النصوص وقراءته، مع الحفاظ على دقة الاقتباسات BibTeX، باستخدام التحقق من البداية إلى النهاية وضمان سلامة السياق الدلالي."},"useCases":{"en":["Refining LaTeX documents for improved readability","Verifying BibTeX citations for accuracy and consistency","Enhancing academic paper flow by adjusting section rhythms"],"zh":["改进LaTeX文档的可读性","验证BibTeX引用的准确性和一致性","通过调整节奏来增强学术论文的流畅度"],"ja":["LaTeX文書の可読性を向上させる","BibTeX引用の正確性と一貫性を検証する","セクションのリズムを調整して学術論文の流れを向上させる"],"ko":["LaTeX 문서의 가독성을 개선한다","BibTeX 인용의 정확성과 일관성을 검증한다","절의 리듬을 조정하여 학술 논문의 흐름을 향상시킨다"],"es":["Perfeccionar documentos LaTeX para mejorar la legibilidad","Verificar citas BibTeX para precisión y coherencia","Mejorar el flujo de trabajos académicos ajustando los ritmos de sección"],"fr":["Affiner les documents LaTeX pour améliorer la lisibilité","Vérifier les citations BibTeX pour l''exactitude et la cohérence","Améliorer le flux des articles académiques en ajustant les rythmes de section"],"de":["LaTeX-Dokumente verfeinern, um die Lesbarkeit zu verbessern","BibTeX-Zitate auf Genauigkeit und Konsistenz überprüfen","Den Fluss akademischer Arbeiten verbessern, indem die Abschnittsrhythmen angepasst werden"],"pt":["Refinamento de documentos LaTeX para melhor legibilidade","Verificação de citações BibTeX para exatidão e consistência","Melhoria do fluxo de artigos acadêmicos ajustando o ritmo das seções"],"ru":["Усовершенствование документов LaTeX для улучшения читаемости","Проверка цитат BibTeX на точность и последовательность","Улучшение потока академических статей путем регулировки ритма разделов"],"ar":["تحسين توثيق LaTeX من أجل تحسين القراءة","تحقق من دقة الاقتباسات BibTeX وثباتها","تحسين تدفق الأوراق الأكاديمية bằng調整 إيقاع الأقسام"]},"limitations":{"en":["Not suitable for initial content drafting","Not intended for technical or structural LaTeX fixes","Requires completed LaTeX content generation"],"zh":["不适合初步内容草稿","不用于技术或结构上的LaTeX修复","需要完成的LaTeX内容生成"],"ja":["初期コンテンツの草案には適していない","技術的または構造的なLaTeXの修正には使用しない","完成したLaTeXコンテンツの生成が必要"],"ko":["초기 내용 초안에는 적합하지 않음","기술적 또는 구조적인 LaTeX 수정에는 사용하지 않음","완성된 LaTeX 내용 생성이 필요"],"es":["No es adecuado para la creación inicial de contenido","No está destinado a correcciones técnicas o estructurales de LaTeX","Requiere una generación de contenido LaTeX completada"],"fr":["N''est pas adapté pour la création initiale de contenu","N''est pas destiné aux corrections techniques ou structurelles de LaTeX","Nécessite une génération de contenu LaTeX complétée"],"de":["Nicht geeignet für die erste Inhaltsentwicklung","Nicht für technische oder strukturelle LaTeX-Korrekturen vorgesehen","Erfordert eine abgeschlossene LaTeX-Inhaltsgenerierung"],"pt":["Não é adequado para a criação inicial de conteúdo","Não é destinado a correções técnicas ou estruturais de LaTeX","Exige geração de conteúdo LaTeX concluída"],"ru":["Не подходит для первоначального создания контента","Не предназначен для технических или структурных исправлений LaTeX","Требует завершенной генерации контента LaTeX"],"ar":["غير مناسب لإنشاء المحتوى الأولي","غير مخطط له لإصلاحات تقنية أو هيكلية لبرنامج LaTeX","يتطلب إنشاء محتوى LaTeX مكتمل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('mufengbufeng/opence/opence-skill-creator', 'community', 'mufengbufeng', 'opence', 'mufengbufeng/opence', 'opence-skill-creator', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.467Z', '2026-02-18T08:26:14.477Z', NULL, '{"id":"mufengbufeng/opence/opence-skill-creator","name":"opence-skill-creator","description":{"zh":"OpenCE 技能创建器帮助您创建有效的项目技能，遵循 OpenCE 约定","ja":"OpenCE スキル作成者は、OpenCE 標準に従って効果的なプロジェクトスキルを作成するのに役立ちます","ko":"OpenCE 스킬 생성기는 OpenCE 규약을 따라 효과적인 프로젝트 스킬을 생성하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"El creador de habilidades opence es una guía para desarrolladores que buscan crear habilidades de proyecto efectivas. Aprende a identificar flujos de trabajo repetibles y a documentar conocimientos específicos del dominio.","fr":"Le créateur de compétences opence est un guide pour les développeurs qui cherchent à créer des compétences de projet efficaces. Apprenez à identifier les flux de travail répétitifs et à documenter les connaissances spécifiques au domaine.","de":"Der opence-Fähigkeits-creator ist ein Leitfaden für Entwickler, die effektive Projekt-Fähigkeiten erstellen möchten. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie wiederholbare Arbeitsabläufe identifizieren und domänenspezifisches Wissen dokumentieren.","pt":"O Opence Skill Creator é uma ferramenta para criar habilidades de projeto personalizadas. Aprenda a criá-las seguindo as convenções do Opence.","ru":"Opence Skill Creator — это инструмент для создания индивидуальных навыков проекта. Узнайте, как создавать их, следуя конвенциям Opence.","ar":"Opence Skill Creator هو أداة لإنشاء مهارات مشروع مخصصة. تعلم كيفية إنشائها متبعةً اتفاقيات Opence.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"OpenCE 技能创建器","ja":"OpenCE スキル作成者","ko":"OpenCE 스킬 생성기","es":"Creador de habilidades opence: Guía para desarrolladores","fr":"Créateur de compétences opence : Guide pour les développeurs","de":"Opence-Fähigkeits-creator: Leitfaden für Entwickler","pt":"Crie Habilidades de Projeto com Opence","ru":"Создание навыков проекта с Opence","ar":"إنشاء مهارات مشروع مع Opence","en":"opence-skill-creator"},"description":{"zh":"OpenCE 技能创建器帮助您创建有效的项目技能，遵循 OpenCE 约定","ja":"OpenCE スキル作成者は、OpenCE 標準に従って効果的なプロジェクトスキルを作成するのに役立ちます","ko":"OpenCE 스킬 생성기는 OpenCE 규약을 따라 효과적인 프로젝트 스킬을 생성하는 데 도움이 됩니다","es":"El creador de habilidades opence es una guía para desarrolladores que buscan crear habilidades de proyecto efectivas. Aprende a identificar flujos de trabajo...","fr":"Le créateur de compétences opence est un guide pour les développeurs qui cherchent à créer des compétences de projet efficaces. Apprenez à identifier les flu...","de":"Der opence-Fähigkeits-creator ist ein Leitfaden für Entwickler, die effektive Projekt-Fähigkeiten erstellen möchten. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie wiederholbare Arbe...","pt":"O Opence Skill Creator é uma ferramenta para criar habilidades de projeto personalizadas. Aprenda a criá-las seguindo as convenções do Opence.","ru":"Opence Skill Creator — это инструмент для создания индивидуальных навыков проекта. Узнайте, как создавать их, следуя конвенциям Opence.","ar":"Opence Skill Creator هو أداة لإنشاء مهارات مشروع مخصصة. تعلم كيفية إنشائها متبعةً اتفاقيات Opence.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["遵循 OpenCE 约定","创建有效的项目技能","提高开发效率","支持复合阶段技能创建","文档化领域特定知识"],"ja":["OpenCE 標準に従う","効果的なプロジェクトスキルを作成","開発効率を向上させる","複合ステージでのスキル作成をサポート","ドメイン固有の知識を文書化"],"ko":["OpenCE 규약을 따른다","효과적인 프로젝트 스킬을 생성한다","개발 효율성을 높인다","복합 단계에서 스킬 생성을 지원한다","도메인 특정 지식을 문서화한다"],"es":["Guía para crear habilidades de proyecto efectivas","Identificación de flujos de trabajo repetibles","Documentación de conocimientos específicos del dominio","Creación de habilidades reutilizables","Integración con las convenciones de opence"],"fr":["Guide pour créer des compétences de projet efficaces","Identification de flux de travail répétitifs","Documentation de connaissances spécifiques au domaine","Création de compétences réutilisables","Intégration avec les conventions opence"],"de":["Leitfaden für die Erstellung effektiver Projekt-Fähigkeiten","Identifizierung wiederholbarer Arbeitsabläufe","Dokumentation domänenspezifischen Wissens","Erstellung wiederverwendbarer Fähigkeiten","Integration mit den opence-Konventionen"],"pt":["Crie habilidades de projeto personalizadas","Siga as convenções do Opence","Identifique fluxos de trabalho repetíveis","Documente conhecimentos específicos de domínio","Evite soluções de um só uso","Otimização de processos de projeto"],"ru":["Создайте индивидуальные навыки проекта","Следуйте конвенциям Opence","Определите повторяющиеся рабочие процессы","Документируйте специфические знания домена","Избегайте одноразовых решений","Оптимизация процессов проекта"],"ar":["أنشئ مهارات مشروع مخصصة","اتبع اتفاقيات Opence","حدد سلاسل عمل متكررة","وثق معرفة محددة للنطاق","تجنب حلول لمرة واحدة","تحسين عمليات المشروع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenCE","技能创建器","项目技能","开发效率","复合阶段","领域特定知识"],"ja":["OpenCE","スキル作成者","プロジェクトスキル","開発効率","複合ステージ","ドメイン固有の知識"],"ko":["OpenCE","스킬 생성기","프로젝트 스킬","개발 효율성","복합 단계","도메인 특정 지식"],"es":["creador de habilidades opence","desarrollo de habilidades de proyecto","convenciones de opence","flujo de trabajo repetible","conocimiento específico del dominio","creación de habilidades reutilizables"],"fr":["créateur de compétences opence","développement de compétences de projet","conventions opence","flux de travail répétitif","connaissance spécifique au domaine","création de compétences réutilisables"],"de":["opence-Fähigkeits-creator","Entwicklung von Projekt-Fähigkeiten","opence-Konventionen","wiederholbarer Arbeitsablauf","domänenspezifisches Wissen","Erstellung wiederverwendbarer Fähigkeiten"],"pt":["Opence Skill Creator","criação de habilidades de projeto","convenções do Opence","fluxos de trabalho repetíveis","documentação de conhecimentos","otimização de processos de projeto","desenvolvimento de habilidades","ferramentas de projeto","gestão de projetos"],"ru":["Opence Skill Creator","создание навыков проекта","конвенции Opence","повторяющиеся рабочие процессы","документирование знаний","оптимизация процессов проекта","разработка навыков","инструменты проекта","управление проектами"],"ar":["Opence Skill Creator","إنشاء مهارات مشروع","اتفاقيات Opence","سلاسل عمل متكررة","توثيق معرفة","تحسين عمليات المشروع","تطوير مهارات","أدوات مشروع","إدارة مشاريع"]}},"owner":"mufengbufeng","repo":"opence","repoPath":"mufengbufeng/opence","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.467Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"opence-skill-creator","description":"Learn how to create effective project skills following opence conventions.","bodyPreview":"<!-- OPENCE:START -->\n# opence-skill-creator\n\nLearn how to create effective project skills following opence conventions.\n\n## When to Create a Skill\n\nCreate a skill during the **compound phase** when you identify:\n- Repeatable workflows that can be encoded as instructions\n- Recurring pitfalls or manual checks that need documentation\n- Domain-specific knowledge that will be useful in future changes\n\nDon''t create a skill for one-off solutions or highly specific edge cases.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nUse the","body":"<!-- OPENCE:START -->\n# opence-skill-creator\n\nLearn how to create effective project skills following opence conventions.\n\n## When to Create a Skill\n\nCreate a skill during the **compound phase** when you identify:\n- Repeatable workflows that can be encoded as instructions\n- Recurring pitfalls or manual checks that need documentation\n- Domain-specific knowledge that will be useful in future changes\n\nDon''t create a skill for one-off solutions or highly specific edge cases.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nUse the CLI to create skills (recommended):\n\n```bash\n# Create a new skill\nopence skill add api-testing --description \"Guidelines for testing API endpoints\"\n\n# List all skills\nopence skill list\n\n# Show skill details\nopence skill show api-testing\n```\n\nThe CLI automatically:\n- Creates proper directory structure\n- Generates correct frontmatter for each tool\n- Validates naming conventions\n- Creates references/ and scripts/ directories\n\n## Skill Structure\n\n```\n.claude/skills/my-skill/\n├── SKILL.md           # Concise entry point (< 200 lines)\n├── references/        # Detailed documentation\n│   └── *.md          # Extended guides, examples\n└── scripts/          # Reusable code\n    └── *.sh, *.py    # Helper scripts\n```\n\n**SKILL.md**: Keep concise. Include \"When to use\", key steps, and pointers to references/.\n\n**references/**: Put detailed docs, long examples, API references here.\n\n**scripts/**: Add reusable code that users can copy or execute.\n\n## Naming Rules\n\n- **Format**: kebab-case (e.g., `api-testing`, `deploy-prod`)\n- **Reserved**: Don''t use `opence-` prefix (reserved for native skills)\n- **Unique**: Check with `opence skill list` to avoid duplicates\n\n**Valid**: `api-testing`, `error-recovery`, `db-migration`\n**Invalid**: `api testing` (spaces), `api_testing` (underscores), `opence-custom` (reserved)\n\n## Next Steps\n\nAfter creating a skill:\n1. Edit SKILL.md to add instructions and examples\n2. Add detailed docs to references/ if needed\n3. Add helper scripts to scripts/ if applicable\n4. Test the skill in actual usage\n5. Commit to version control\n\nSee references/ for detailed guidance on:\n- Directory structure and sizing\n- Frontmatter formats for different tools\n- Best practices and anti-patterns\n<!-- OPENCE:END -->\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:26:14.477Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents needing structured workflow automation following opence conventions.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化工作流自动化的AI代理，遵循opence约定。","ja":"オープンセ規約に従った構造化されたワークフローの自動化が必要なAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"오픈스 규약을 따르는 구조화된 워크플로 자동화가 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan automatización de flujo de trabajo estructurado siguiendo convenciones de opence.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA ayant besoin d''une automatisation de workflow structurée suivant les conventions opence.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die eine strukturierte Workflow-Automatisierung nach opence-Konventionen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que necessitam de automação de fluxo de trabalho estruturada seguindo convenções opence.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, которым требуется автоматизация структурированных рабочих процессов в соответствии с открытыми конвенциями opence.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يحتاج إلى تلقيم سير العمل الهيكلي متبوعًا بإرشادات مفتوحة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to encode repeatable workflows as instructions, document recurring pitfalls, and capture domain-specific knowledge using opence skill creation protocols, facilitating efficient compound phase project management.","zh":"能够赋予代理编码可重复的工作流作为指令，记录反复出现的陷阱，并使用opence技能创建协议捕获特定领域的知识，从而实现高效的复合阶段项目管理。","ja":"エージェントに、繰り返し実行可能なワークフローを指令としてエンコードし、再発する落とし穴を文書化し、オープンセのスキル作成プロトコルを使用してドメイン固有の知識を取得できるようにし、効率的な複合段階プロジェクト管理を促進します。","ko":"에이전트가 반복 가능한 워크플ロー 를 지시로 인코딩하고 다시 발생하는 함정을 문서화하며 오픈스 스킬 생성 프로토콜을 사용하여 도메인 특정 지식을 캡처하여 효율적인 복합 단계 프로젝트 관리를 가능하게 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a codificar flujos de trabajo repetibles como instrucciones, documentar trampas recurrentes y capturar conocimientos específicos del dominio utilizando protocolos de creación de habilidades de opence, lo que facilita una gestión de proyectos de fase compuesta eficiente.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''encoder des flux de travail répétitifs en tant qu''instructions, de documenter les pièges récurrents et de capturer les connaissances spécifiques au domaine en utilisant les protocoles de création de compétences opence, ce qui facilite une gestion de projet de phase composite efficiente.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, wiederholbare Workflows als Anweisungen zu kodieren, wiederkehrende Fallstricke zu dokumentieren und domänen-spezifisches Wissen unter Verwendung von opence-Fähigkeitserstellungprotokollen zu erfassen, was eine effiziente Verwaltung von Projekten mit zusammengesetzten Phasen ermöglicht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a codificar fluxos de trabalho repetíveis como instruções, documentar armadilhas recorrentes e capturar conhecimento específico de domínio usando protocolos de criação de habilidades opence, facilitando a gestão eficiente de projetos de fases compostas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью кодировать повторяющиеся рабочие процессы в виде инструкций, документировать повторяющиеся ловушки и захватывать знания, специфичные для области, с помощью протоколов создания навыков opence, что облегчает эффективное управление проектами с составными фазами.","ar":"يمكن الوكيل من تشفير سير العمل القابل للتكرار كتعليمات وتوثيق الفخاخ المتكررة والتقاط المعرفة الخاصة بالمجال باستخدام بروتوكولات إنشاء المهارات مفتوحة، مما يسهل إدارة المراحل المعقدة للمشروع بكفاءة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating repeatable workflows","Documenting recurring pitfalls or manual checks","Capturing domain-specific knowledge for future project changes"],"zh":["自动化可重复的工作流","记录反复出现的陷阱或手动检查","捕获特定领域的知识以用于未来的项目更改"],"ja":["繰り返し実行可能なワークフローの自動化","再発する落とし穴や手動チェックの文書化","将来のプロジェクト変更のためにドメイン固有の知識を取得"],"ko":["반복 가능한 워크플로 자동화","다시 발생하는 함정 또는 수동 확인 문서화","将来의 프로젝트 변경을 위한 도메인 특정 지식 캡처"],"es":["Automatización de flujos de trabajo repetibles","Documentación de trampas recurrentes o controles manuales","Captura de conocimientos específicos del dominio para cambios de proyectos futuros"],"fr":["Automatisation de flux de travail répétitifs","Documentation de pièges récurrents ou de vérifications manuelles","Capture de connaissances spécifiques au domaine pour les changements de projets futurs"],"de":["Automatisierung von wiederholbaren Workflows","Dokumentation von wiederkehrenden Fallstricken oder manuellen Prüfungen","Erfassung von domänen-spezifischem Wissen für zukünftige Projektänderungen"],"pt":["Automatizar fluxos de trabalho repetíveis","Documentar armadilhas recorrentes ou verificações manuais","Capturar conhecimento específico de domínio para alterações futuras de projeto"],"ru":["Автоматизация повторяющихся рабочих процессов","Документирование повторяющихся ловушек или ручных проверок","Захват знаний, специфичных для области, для будущих изменений проекта"],"ar":["تلقيم سير العمل القابل للتكرار","توثيق الفخاخ المتكررة أو الفحوصات اليدوية","التقاط المعرفة الخاصة بالمجال من أجل تغييرات مستقبلية للمشروع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Not intended for one-off solutions","Not suitable for highly specific edge cases"],"zh":["不适用于一次性解决方案","不适合高度特定的边缘情况"],"ja":["一回限りのソリューションには適していない","高度に特定のエッジケースには適していない"],"ko":["일회성 솔루션에는 적합하지 않음","고도로 특정한 에지 ケース에는 적합하지 않음"],"es":["No está destinado a soluciones de un solo uso","No es adecuado para casos de borde muy específicos"],"fr":["N''est pas destiné à des solutions à usage unique","N''est pas adapté à des cas de bord très spécifiques"],"de":["Ist nicht für Einmal-Lösungen vorgesehen","Ist nicht geeignet für sehr spezifische Randfälle"],"pt":["Não destinado a soluções de uso único","Não adequado para casos de bordo altamente específicos"],"ru":["Не предназначен для одноразовых решений","Не подходит для высоко специфичных граничных случаев"],"ar":["غير مناسب للحلول المستخدمة لمرة واحدة","غير مناسب للحالات الحدية الخاصة جدا"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('chrisfrantz/nanoclaw/add-gmail', 'community', 'chrisfrantz', 'nanoclaw', 'chrisfrantz/nanoclaw', 'add-gmail', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.467Z', '2026-02-18T08:26:09.002Z', NULL, '{"id":"chrisfrantz/nanoclaw/add-gmail","name":"add-gmail","description":{"zh":"NanoClaw Gmail, IPC WhatsApp","ja":"NanoClaw Gmail, IPC WhatsApp","ko":"NanoClaw Gmail, IPC WhatsApp","es":"El skill ''add-gmail'' permite agregar capacidades de Gmail a NanoClaw, configurable en dos modos: Tool Mode y Channel Mode.","fr":"Le skill ''add-gmail'' permet d''ajouter des capacités de Gmail à NanoClaw, configurable en deux modes : Tool Mode et Channel Mode.","de":"Der Skill ''add-gmail'' ermöglicht es, Gmail-Funktionen in NanoClaw hinzuzufügen, konfigurierbar in zwei Modi: Tool Mode und Channel Mode.","pt":"O skill add-gmail adiciona capacidades de e-mail ao NanoClaw, permitindo a leitura e envio de e-mails de forma configurável","ru":"Навык add-gmail добавляет функциональность электронной почты к NanoClaw, позволяя читать и отправлять электронные письма в настраиваемом режиме","ar":"المهارة add-gmail تضيف قدرات البريد الإلكتروني إلى NanoClaw، مما يسمح بقراءة وsending البريد الإلكتروني بطريقة قابلة للتخصيص","en":"codex it"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"NanoClaw Gmail","ja":"NanoClaw Gmail","ko":"NanoClaw Gmail","es":"Integración de Gmail para NanoClaw","fr":"Intégration de Gmail pour NanoClaw","de":"Gmail-Integration für NanoClaw","pt":"Integração do Gmail: Adicione Funcionalidades de E-mail","ru":"Интеграция Gmail: добавление функциональности электронной...","ar":"دمج جيميل: إضافة ميزات البريد الإلكتروني","en":"add-gmail"},"description":{"zh":"NanoClaw Gmail, IPC WhatsApp","ja":"NanoClaw Gmail, IPC WhatsApp","ko":"NanoClaw Gmail, IPC WhatsApp","es":"El skill ''add-gmail'' permite agregar capacidades de Gmail a NanoClaw, configurable en dos modos: Tool Mode y Channel Mode.","fr":"Le skill ''add-gmail'' permet d''ajouter des capacités de Gmail à NanoClaw, configurable en deux modes : Tool Mode et Channel Mode.","de":"Der Skill ''add-gmail'' ermöglicht es, Gmail-Funktionen in NanoClaw hinzuzufügen, konfigurierbar in zwei Modi: Tool Mode und Channel Mode.","pt":"O skill add-gmail adiciona capacidades de e-mail ao NanoClaw, permitindo a leitura e envio de e-mails de forma configurável","ru":"Навык add-gmail добавляет функциональность электронной почты к NanoClaw, позволяя читать и отправлять электронные письма в настраиваемом режиме","ar":"المهارة add-gmail تضيف قدرات البريد الإلكتروني إلى NanoClaw، مما يسمح بقراءة وsending البريد الإلكتروني بطريقة قابلة للتخصيص","en":"codex it"},"definition":{"en":"codex it"},"features":{"zh":["Tool","Channel","IPC","Gmail API","WhatsApp"],"ja":["Tool","Channel","IPC","Gmail API","WhatsApp"],"ko":["Tool","Channel","IPC","Gmail API","WhatsApp"],"es":["Lectura y envío de correos electrónicos","Configuración en modo Tool o Channel","Activación mediante WhatsApp o correo electrónico","Programación de tareas","Compatibilidad con la API de Gmail"],"fr":["Lecture et envoi de courriels","Configuration en mode Tool ou Channel","Activation via WhatsApp ou courriel","Planification de tâches","Compatibilité avec l''API de Gmail"],"de":["Lesen und Senden von E-Mails","Konfiguration im Tool- oder Channel-Modus","Aktivierung über WhatsApp oder E-Mail","Terminplanung","Kompatibilität mit der Gmail-API"],"pt":["Modo Ferramenta: leitura e envio de e-mails via WhatsApp","Modo Canal: e-mails podem acionar o agente e agendar tarefas","Integração com a API do Gmail","Configuração personalizada","Suporte a envio e recebimento de e-mails"],"ru":["Режим инструмента: чтение и отправка электронных писем через WhatsApp","Режим канала: электронные письма могут запускать агента и планировать задачи","Интеграция с API Gmail","Пользовательская настройка","Поддержка отправки и получения электронной почты"],"ar":["وضع الأداة: قراءة وsending البريد الإلكتروني عبر WhatsApp","وضع القناة: يمكن للبريد الإلكتروني تشغيل العميل وتخطيط المهام","دمج مع واجهة برمجة تطبيقات جيميل","التخصيص الشخصي","دعم إرسال واستقبال البريد الإلكتروني"]},"keywords":{"zh":["NanoClaw","Gmail","IPC","WhatsApp","Gmail API","Tool","Channel"],"ja":["NanoClaw","Gmail","IPC","WhatsApp","Gmail API","Tool","Channel"],"ko":["NanoClaw","Gmail","IPC","WhatsApp","Gmail API","Tool","Channel"],"es":["integración de Gmail","NanoClaw","desarrollo de skills","API de Gmail","automatización de correo electrónico","programación de tareas"],"fr":["intégration de Gmail","NanoClaw","développement de skills","API de Gmail","automatisation de courriel","planification de tâches"],"de":["Gmail-Integration","NanoClaw","Skill-Entwicklung","Gmail-API","E-Mail-Automatisierung","Terminplanung"],"pt":["integração do gmail","nanoClaw","envio de e-mails","leitura de e-mails","api do gmail","desenvolvimento de software","tecnologia de e-mail"],"ru":["интеграция гмейла","nanoClaw","отправка электронных писем","чтение электронной почты","api гмейла","разработка программного обеспечения","технология электронной почты"],"ar":["دمج جيميل","nanoClaw","إرسال البريد الإلكتروني","قراءة البريد الإلكتروني","واجهة برمجة تطبيقات جيميل","تطوير البرمجيات","تكنولوجيا البريد الإلكتروني"]}},"owner":"chrisfrantz","repo":"nanoclaw","repoPath":"chrisfrantz/nanoclaw","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.467Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"add-gmail","description":"Add Gmail integration to NanoClaw. Can be configured as a tool (agent reads/sends emails when triggered from WhatsApp) or as a full channel (emails can trigger the agent, schedule tasks, and receive replies). Guides through GCP OAuth setup and implements the integration.","bodyPreview":"# Add Gmail Integration\n\n> **Note:** This skill is MCP-based and was written for the previous SDK-based runtime. The Codex version of NanoClaw uses IPC actions. Port by defining IPC actions + host-side Gmail API calls; treat `mcp__*` references below as legacy.\n\nThis skill adds Gmail capabilities to NanoClaw. It can be configured in two modes:\n\n1. **Tool Mode** - Agent can read/send emails, but only when triggered from WhatsApp\n2. **Channel Mode** - Emails can trigger the agent, schedule tasks,","body":"# Add Gmail Integration\n\n> **Note:** This skill is MCP-based and was written for the previous SDK-based runtime. The Codex version of NanoClaw uses IPC actions. Port by defining IPC actions + host-side Gmail API calls; treat `mcp__*` references below as legacy.\n\nThis skill adds Gmail capabilities to NanoClaw. It can be configured in two modes:\n\n1. **Tool Mode** - Agent can read/send emails, but only when triggered from WhatsApp\n2. **Channel Mode** - Emails can trigger the agent, schedule tasks, and receive email replies\n\n## Initial Questions\n\nAsk the user:\n\n> How do you want to use Gmail with NanoClaw?\n>\n> **Option 1: Tool Mode**\n> - Agent can read and send emails when you ask it to\n> - Triggered only from WhatsApp (e.g., \"@Andy check my email\" or \"@Andy send an email to...\")\n> - Simpler setup, no email polling\n>\n> **Option 2: Channel Mode**\n> - Everything in Tool Mode, plus:\n> - Emails to a specific address/label trigger the agent\n> - Agent replies via email (not WhatsApp)\n> - Can schedule tasks via email\n> - Requires email polling infrastructure\n\nStore their choice and proceed to the appropriate section.\n\n---\n\n## Prerequisites (Both Modes)\n\n### 1. Check Existing Gmail Setup\n\nFirst, check if Gmail is already configured:\n\n```bash\nls -la ~/.gmail-mcp/ 2>/dev/null || echo \"No Gmail config found\"\n```\n\nIf `credentials.json` exists, skip to \"Verify Gmail Access\" below.\n\n### 2. Create Gmail Config Directory\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p ~/.gmail-mcp\n```\n\n### 3. GCP Project Setup\n\n**USER ACTION REQUIRED**\n\nTell the user:\n\n> I need you to set up Google Cloud OAuth credentials. I''ll walk you through it:\n>\n> 1. Open https://console.cloud.google.com in your browser\n> 2. Create a new project (or select existing) - click the project dropdown at the top\n\nWait for user confirmation, then continue:\n\n> 3. Now enable the Gmail API:\n>    - In the left sidebar, go to **APIs & Services → Library**\n>    - Search for \"Gmail API\"\n>    - Click on it, then click **Enable**\n\nWait for user confirmation, then continue:\n\n> 4. Now create OAuth credentials:\n>    - Go to **APIs & Services → Credentials** (in the left sidebar)\n>    - Click **+ CREATE CREDENTIALS** at the top\n>    - Select **OAuth client ID**\n>    - If prompted for consent screen, choose \"External\", fill in app name (e.g., \"NanoClaw\"), your email, and save\n>    - For Application type, select **Desktop app**\n>    - Name it anything (e.g., \"NanoClaw Gmail\")\n>    - Click **Create**\n\nWait for user confirmation, then continue:\n\n> 5. Download the credentials:\n>    - Click **DOWNLOAD JSON** on the popup (or find it in the credentials list and click the download icon)\n>    - Save it as `gcp-oauth.keys.json`\n>\n> Where did you save the file? (Give me the full path, or just paste the file contents here)\n\nIf user provides a path, copy it:\n\n```bash\ncp \"/path/user/provided/gcp-oauth.keys.json\" ~/.gmail-mcp/gcp-oauth.keys.json\n```\n\nIf user pastes the JSON content, write it directly:\n\n```bash\ncat > ~/.gmail-mcp/gcp-oauth.keys.json << ''EOF''\n{paste the JSON here}\nEOF\n```\n\nVerify the file is valid JSON:\n\n```bash\ncat ~/.gmail-mcp/gcp-oauth.keys.json | head -5\n```\n\n### 4. OAuth Authorization\n\n**USER ACTION REQUIRED**\n\nTell the user:\n\n> I''m going to run the Gmail authorization. A browser window will open asking you to sign in to Google and grant access.\n>\n> **Important:** If you see a warning that the app isn''t verified, click \"Advanced\" then \"Go to [app name] (unsafe)\" - this is normal for personal OAuth apps.\n\nRun the authorization:\n\n```bash\nnpx -y @gongrzhe/server-gmail-autoauth-mcp auth\n```\n\nIf that doesn''t work (some versions don''t have an auth subcommand), run it and let it prompt:\n\n```bash\ntimeout 60 npx -y @gongrzhe/server-gmail-autoauth-mcp || true\n```\n\nTell user:\n> Complete the authorization in your browser. The window should close automatically when done. Let me know when you''ve authorized.\n\n### 5. Verify Gmail Access\n\nCheck that credentials were saved:\n\n```bash\nif [ -f ~/.gmail-mcp/credentials.json ]; then\n  echo \"Gmail authorization successful!\"\n  ls -la ~/.gmail-mcp/\nelse\n  echo \"ERROR: credentials.json not found - authorization may have failed\"\nfi\n```\n\nTest the connection by listing labels (quick sanity check):\n\n```bash\necho ''{\"method\": \"tools/list\"}'' | timeout 10 npx -y @gongrzhe/server-gmail-autoauth-mcp 2>/dev/null | head -20 || echo \"MCP responded (check output above)\"\n```\n\nIf everything works, proceed to implementation.\n\n---\n\n## Tool Mode Implementation\n\nFor Tool Mode, integrate Gmail MCP into the agent runner. Execute these changes directly.\n\n### Step 1: Add Gmail MCP to Agent Runner\n\nRead `container/agent-runner/src/index.ts` and find the `mcpServers` config in the `query()` call.\n\nAdd `gmail` to the `mcpServers` object:\n\n```typescript\ngmail: { command: ''npx'', args: [''-y'', ''@gongrzhe/server-gmail-autoauth-mcp''] }\n```\n\nFind the `allowedTools` array and add Gmail tools:\n\n```typescript\n''mcp__gmail__*''\n```\n\nThe result should look like:\n\n```typescript\nmcpServers: {\n  nanoclaw: ipcMcp,\n  gmail: { command: ''npx'', args: [''-y'', ''@gongrzhe/server-gmail-autoauth-mcp''] }\n},\nallowedTools: [\n  ''Bash'',\n  ''Read'', ''Write'', ''Edit'', ''Glob'', ''Grep'',\n  ''WebSearch'', ''WebFetch'',\n  ''mcp__nanoclaw__*'',\n  ''mcp__gmail__*''\n],\n```\n\n### Step 2: Mount Gmail Credentials in Container\n\nRead `src/container-runner.ts` and find the `buildVolumeMounts` function.\n\nAdd this mount block (after the `.codex` mount is a good location):\n\n```typescript\n// Gmail credentials directory\nconst gmailDir = path.join(homeDir, ''.gmail-mcp'');\nif (fs.existsSync(gmailDir)) {\n  mounts.push({\n    hostPath: gmailDir,\n    containerPath: ''/home/node/.gmail-mcp'',\n    readonly: false  // MCP may need to refresh tokens\n  });\n}\n```\n\n### Step 3: Update Group Memory\n\nAppend to `groups/MEMORY.md` (the global memory file):\n\n```markdown\n\n## Email (Gmail)\n\nYou have access to Gmail via MCP tools:\n- `mcp__gmail__search_emails` - Search emails with query\n- `mcp__gmail__get_email` - Get full email content by ID\n- `mcp__gmail__send_email` - Send an email\n- `mcp__gmail__draft_email` - Create a draft\n- `mcp__gmail__list_labels` - List available labels\n\nExample: \"Check my unread emails from today\" or \"Send an email to john@example.com about the meeting\"\n```\n\nAlso append the same section to `groups/main/MEMORY.md`.\n\n### Step 4: Rebuild and Restart\n\nRun these commands:\n\n```bash\ncd container && ./build.sh\n```\n\nWait for container build to complete, then:\n\n```bash\ncd .. && npm run build\n```\n\nWait for TypeScript compilation, then restart the service:\n\n```bash\nlaunchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.nanoclaw\n```\n\nCheck that it started:\n\n```bash\nsleep 2 && launchctl list | grep nanoclaw\n```\n\n### Step 5: Test Gmail Integration\n\nTell the user:\n\n> Gmail integration is set up! Test it by sending this message in your WhatsApp main channel:\n>\n> `@Andy check my recent emails`\n>\n> Or:\n>\n> `@Andy list my Gmail labels`\n\nWatch the logs for any errors:\n\n```bash\ntail -f logs/nanoclaw.log\n```\n\n---\n\n## Channel Mode Implementation\n\nChannel Mode includes everything from Tool Mode, plus email polling and routing.\n\n### Additional Questions for Channel Mode\n\nAsk the user:\n\n> How should the agent be triggered from email?\n>\n> **Option A: Specific Label**\n> - Create a Gmail label (e.g., \"NanoClaw\")\n> - Emails with this label trigger the agent\n> - You manually label emails or set up Gmail filters\n>\n> **Option B: Email Address Pattern**\n> - Emails to a specific address pattern (e.g., andy+task@gmail.com)\n> - Uses Gmail''s plus-addressing feature\n>\n> **Option C: Subject Prefix**\n> - Emails with a subject starting with a keyword (e.g., \"[Andy]\")\n> - Anyone can trigger the agent by using the prefix\n\nAlso ask:\n\n> How should email conversations be grouped?\n>\n> **Option A: Per Email Thread**\n> - Each email thread gets its own conversation context\n> - Agent remembers the thread history\n>\n> **Option B: Per Sender**\n> - All emails from the same sender share context\n> - Agent remembers all interactions with that person\n>\n> **Option C: Single Context**\n> - All emails share the main group context\n> - Like an additional input to the main channel\n\nStore their choices for implementation.\n\n### Step 1: Complete Tool Mode First\n\nComplete all Tool Mode steps above before continuing. Verify Gmail tools work by having the user test `@Andy check my recent emails`.\n\n### Step 2: Add Email Polling Configuration\n\nRead `src/types.ts` and add this interface:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface EmailChannelConfig {\n  enabled: boolean;\n  triggerMode: ''label'' | ''address'' | ''subject'';\n  triggerValue: string;  // Label name, address pattern, or subject prefix\n  contextMode: ''thread'' | ''sender'' | ''single'';\n  pollIntervalMs: number;\n  replyPrefix?: string;  // Optional prefix for replies\n}\n```\n\nRead `src/config.ts` and add this configuration (customize values based on user''s earlier answers):\n\n```typescript\nexport const EMAIL_CHANNEL: EmailChannelConfig = {\n  enabled: true,\n  triggerMode: ''label'',  // or ''address'' or ''subject''\n  triggerValue: ''NanoClaw'',  // the label name, address pattern, or prefix\n  contextMode: ''thread'',\n  pollIntervalMs: 60000,  // Check every minute\n  replyPrefix: ''[Andy] ''\n};\n```\n\n### Step 3: Add Email State Tracking\n\nRead `src/db.ts` and add these functions for tracking processed emails:\n\n```typescript\n// Track processed emails to avoid duplicates\nexport function initEmailTable(): void {\n  db.exec(`\n    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS processed_emails (\n      message_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n      thread_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n      sender TEXT NOT NULL,\n      subject TEXT,\n      processed_at TEXT NOT NULL,\n      response_sent INTEGER DEFAULT 0\n    )\n  `);\n}\n\nexport function isEmailProcessed(messageId: string): boolean {\n  const row = db.prepare(''SELECT 1 FROM processed_emails WHERE message_id = ?'').get(messageId);\n  return !!row;\n}\n\nexport function markEmailProcessed(messageId: string, threadId: string, sender: string, subject: string): void {\n  db.prepare(`\n    INSERT OR REPLACE INTO processed_emails (message_id, thread_id, sender, subject, processed_at)\n    VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)\n  `).run(messageId, threadId, sender, subject, new Date().toISOString());\n}\n\nexport function markEmailResponded(messageId: string): void {\n  db.prepare(''UPDATE processed_emails SET response_sent = 1 WHERE message_id = ?'').run(messageId);\n}\n```\n\nAlso find the `initDatabase()` function in `src/db.ts` and add a call to `initEmailTable()`.\n\n### Step 4: Create Email Channel Module\n\nCreate a new file `src/email-channel.ts` with this content:\n\n```typescript\nimport { EMAIL_CHANNEL } from ''./config.js'';\nimport { isEmailProcessed, markEmailProcessed, markEmailResponded } from ''./db.js'';\nimport pino from ''pino'';\n\nconst logger = pino({\n  level: process.env.LOG_LEVEL || ''info'',\n  transport: { target: ''pino-pretty'', options: { colorize: true } }\n});\n\ninterface EmailMessage {\n  id: string;\n  threadId: string;\n  from: string;\n  subject: string;\n  body: string;\n  date: string;\n}\n\n// Gmail MCP client functions (call via subprocess or import the MCP directly)\n// These would invoke the Gmail MCP tools\n\nexport async function checkForNewEmails(): Promise<EmailMessage[]> {\n  // Build query based on trigger mode\n  let query: string;\n  switch (EMAIL_CHANNEL.triggerMode) {\n    case ''label'':\n      query = `label:${EMAIL_CHANNEL.triggerValue} is:unread`;\n      break;\n    case ''address'':\n      query = `to:${EMAIL_CHANNEL.triggerValue} is:unread`;\n      break;\n    case ''subject'':\n      query = `subject:${EMAIL_CHANNEL.triggerValue} is:unread`;\n      break;\n  }\n\n  // This requires calling Gmail MCP''s search_emails tool\n  // Implementation depends on how you want to invoke MCP from Node\n  // Option 1: Use legacy SDK with just gmail MCP\n  // Option 2: Run npx gmail MCP as subprocess and parse output\n  // Option 3: Import gmail-autoauth-mcp directly\n\n  // Placeholder - implement based on preference\n  return [];\n}\n\nexport async function sendEmailReply(\n  threadId: string,\n  to: string,\n  subject: string,\n  body: string\n): Promise<void> {\n  // Call Gmail MCP''s send_email tool with in_reply_to for threading\n  // Prefix subject with replyPrefix if configured\n  const replySubject = subject.startsWith(''Re:'')\n    ? subject\n    : `Re: ${subject}`;\n\n  const prefixedBody = EMAIL_CHANNEL.replyPrefix\n    ? `${EMAIL_CHANNEL.replyPrefix}${body}`\n    : body;\n\n  // Implementation: invoke Gmail MCP send_email\n}\n\nexport function getContextKey(email: EmailMessage): string {\n  switch (EMAIL_CHANNEL.contextMode) {\n    case ''thread'':\n      return `email-thread-${email.threadId}`;\n    case ''sender'':\n      return `email-sender-${email.from.toLowerCase()}`;\n    case ''single'':\n      return ''email-main'';\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Step 5: Add Email Polling to Main Loop\n\nRead `src/index.ts` and add the email polling infrastructure. First, add these imports at the top:\n\n```typescript\nimport { checkForNewEmails, sendEmailReply, getContextKey } from ''./email-channel.js'';\nimport { EMAIL_CHANNEL } from ''./config.js'';\nimport { isEmailProcessed, markEmailProcessed, markEmailResponded } from ''./db.js'';\n\nasync function startEmailLoop(): Promise<void> {\n  if (!EMAIL_CHANNEL.enabled) {\n    logger.info(''Email channel disabled'');\n    return;\n  }\n\n  logger.info(`Email channel running (trigger: ${EMAIL_CHANNEL.triggerMode}:${EMAIL_CHANNEL.triggerValue})`);\n\n  while (true) {\n    try {\n      const emails = await checkForNewEmails();\n\n      for (const email of emails) {\n        if (isEmailProcessed(email.id)) continue;\n\n        logger.info({ from: email.from, subject: email.subject }, ''Processing email'');\n        markEmailProcessed(email.id, email.threadId, email.from, email.subject);\n\n        // Determine which group/context to use\n        const contextKey = getContextKey(email);\n\n        // Build prompt with email content\n        const prompt = `<email>\n<from>${email.from}</from>\n<subject>${email.subject}</subject>\n<body>${email.body}</body>\n</email>\n\nRespond to this email. Your response will be sent as an email reply.`;\n\n        // Run agent with email context\n        // You''ll need to create a registered group for email or use a special handler\n        const response = await runEmailAgent(contextKey, prompt, email);\n\n        if (response) {\n          await sendEmailReply(email.threadId, email.from, email.subject, response);\n          markEmailResponded(email.id);\n          logger.info({ to: email.from }, ''Email reply sent'');\n        }\n      }\n    } catch (err) {\n      logger.error({ err }, ''Error in email loop'');\n    }\n\n    await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, EMAIL_CHANNEL.pollIntervalMs));\n  }\n}\n\nThen find the `connectWhatsApp` function and add `startEmailLoop()` call after `startMessageLoop()`:\n\n```typescript\n// In the connection === ''open'' block, after startMessageLoop():\nstartEmailLoop();\n```\n\n### Step 6: Implement Email Agent Runner\n\nAdd this function to `src/index.ts` (or create a separate `src/email-agent.ts` if preferred):\n\n```typescript\nasync function runEmailAgent(\n  contextKey: string,\n  prompt: string,\n  email: EmailMessage\n): Promise<string | null> {\n  // Email uses either:\n  // 1. A dedicated \"email\" group folder\n  // 2. Or dynamic folders per thread/sender\n\n  const groupFolder = EMAIL_CHANNEL.contextMode === ''single''\n    ? ''main''  // Use main group context\n    : `email/${contextKey}`;  // Isolated email context\n\n  // Ensure folder exists\n  const groupDir = path.join(GROUPS_DIR, groupFolder);\n  fs.mkdirSync(groupDir, { recursive: true });\n\n  // Create minimal registered group for email\n  const emailGroup: RegisteredGroup = {\n    name: contextKey,\n    folder: groupFolder,\n    trigger: '''',  // No trigger for email\n    added_at: new Date().toISOString()\n  };\n\n  // Use existing runContainerAgent\n  const output = await runContainerAgent(emailGroup, {\n    prompt,\n    sessionId: sessions[groupFolder],\n    groupFolder,\n    chatJid: `email:${email.from}`,  // Use email: prefix for JID\n    isMain: false,\n    isScheduledTask: false\n  });\n\n  if (output.newSessionId) {\n    sessions[groupFolder] = output.newSessionId;\n    saveJson(path.join(DATA_DIR, ''sessions.json''), sessions);\n  }\n\n  return output.status === ''success'' ? output.result : null;\n}\n```\n\n### Step 7: Update IPC for Email Responses (Optional)\n\nIf you want the agent to be able to send emails proactively from within a session, read `container/agent-runner/src/ipc-mcp.ts` and add this tool:\n\n```typescript\n// Add to the MCP tools\n{\n  name: ''send_email_reply'',\n  description: ''Send an email reply in the current thread'',\n  inputSchema: {\n    type: ''object'',\n    properties: {\n      body: { type: ''string'', description: ''Email body content'' }\n    },\n    required: [''body'']\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThen add handling in `src/index.ts` in the `processTaskIpc` function or create a new IPC handler for email actions.\n\n### Step 8: Create Email Group Memory\n\nCreate the email group directory and memory file:\n\n```bash\nmkdir -p groups/email\n```\n\nWrite `groups/email/MEMORY.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Email Channel\n\nYou are responding to emails. Your responses will be sent as email replies.\n\n## Guidelines\n\n- Be professional and clear\n- Keep responses concise but complete\n- Use proper email formatting (greetings, sign-off)\n- If the email requires action you can''t take, explain what the user should do\n\n## Context\n\nEach email thread or sender (depending on configuration) has its own conversation history.\n```\n\n### Step 9: Rebuild and Test\n\nRebuild the container (required since agent-runner changed):\n\n```bash\ncd container && ./build.sh\n```\n\nWait for build to complete, then compile TypeScript:\n\n```bash\ncd .. && npm run build\n```\n\nRestart the service:\n\n```bash\nlaunchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.nanoclaw\n```\n\nVerify it started and check for email channel startup message:\n\n```bash\nsleep 3 && tail -20 logs/nanoclaw.log | grep -i email\n```\n\nTell the user:\n\n> Email channel is now active! Test it by sending an email that matches your trigger:\n> - **Label mode:** Apply the \"${triggerValue}\" label to any email\n> - **Address mode:** Send an email to ${triggerValue}\n> - **Subject mode:** Send an email with subject starting with \"${triggerValue}\"\n>\n> The agent should process it within a minute and send a reply.\n\nMonitor for the test:\n\n```bash\ntail -f logs/nanoclaw.log | grep -E \"(email|Email)\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Gmail MCP not responding\n```bash\n# Test Gmail MCP directly\nnpx -y @gongrzhe/server-gmail-autoauth-mcp\n```\n\n### OAuth token expired\n```bash\n# Re-authorize\nrm ~/.gmail-mcp/credentials.json\nnpx -y @gongrzhe/server-gmail-autoauth-mcp\n```\n\n### Emails not being detected\n- Check the trigger configuration matches your test email\n- Verify the label exists (for label mode)\n- Check `processed_emails` table for already-processed emails\n\n### Container can''t access Gmail\n- Verify `~/.gmail-mcp` is mounted in container\n- Check container logs: `cat groups/main/logs/container-*.log | tail -50`\n\n---\n\n## Removing Gmail Integration\n\nTo remove Gmail entirely:\n\n1. Remove from `container/agent-runner/src/index.ts`:\n   - Delete `gmail` from `mcpServers`\n   - Remove `mcp__gmail__*` from `allowedTools`\n\n2. Remove from `src/container-runner.ts`:\n   - Delete the `~/.gmail-mcp` mount block\n\n3. Remove from `src/index.ts` (Channel Mode only):\n   - Delete `startEmailLoop()` call\n   - Delete email-related imports\n\n4. Delete `src/email-channel.ts` (if created)\n\n5. Remove Gmail sections from `groups/*/MEMORY.md`\n\n6. Rebuild:\n   ```bash\n   cd container && ./build.sh && cd ..\n   npm run build\n   launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.nanoclaw\n   ```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:26:09.002Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Virtual Assistant Agents needing integrated email capabilities via Gmail API","zh":"非常适合需要通过Gmail API集成电子邮件功能的虚拟助手代理","ja":"Gmail APIを介して統合された電子メール機能を必要とする仮想アシスタントエージェントに最適","ko":"Gmail API를 통해 통합된 이메일 기능을 필요로 하는 가상 어시스턴트 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de asistente virtual que necesitan capacidades integradas de correo electrónico a través de la API de Gmail","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''assistant virtuel nécessitant des capacités de messagerie intégrées via l''API Gmail","de":"Ideal für virtuelle Assistenten-Agents, die integrierte E-Mail-Funktionen über die Gmail API benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Assistente Virtual que precisam de capacidades de e-mail integradas via Gmail API","ru":"Идеально для виртуальных агентов помощников, которым необходимы интегрированные возможности электронной почты через Gmail API","ar":"مثالي لعميل المساعد الافتراضي الذي يحتاج إلى إمكانيات البريد الإلكتروني المتكاملة عبر واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Gmail"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to read and send emails using IPC actions and host-side Gmail API calls, enabling seamless communication in both Tool Mode and Channel Mode, leveraging protocols like WhatsApp for triggered actions","zh":"赋予代理读取和发送电子邮件的能力，使用IPC操作和主机端Gmail API调用，在工具模式和渠道模式下实现无缝通信，利用WhatsApp等协议触发操作","ja":"IPCアクションとホスト側のGmail API呼び出しを使用して、エージェントが電子メールを読み書きする能力を付与し、Tool ModeとChannel Modeの両方で無停滞の通信を可能にし、WhatsAppなどのプロトコルを使用してトリガーされたアクションを実現する","ko":"IPC 동작과 호스트 측 Gmail API 호출을 사용하여 에이전트가 이메일을 읽고 쓰는 기능을 부여하여, 툴 모드와 채널 모드 모두에서 무정지 통신을 가능하게 하며, WhatsApp 등의 프로토콜을 사용하여 트리거된 동작을 구현","es":"Permite a los agentes leer y enviar correos electrónicos utilizando acciones IPC y llamadas a la API de Gmail del lado del host, lo que permite una comunicación fluida tanto en el Modo Herramienta como en el Modo Canal, aprovechando protocolos como WhatsApp para acciones activadas","fr":"Permet aux agents de lire et d''envoyer des e-mails en utilisant des actions IPC et des appels d''API Gmail côté hôte, permettant une communication transparente à la fois en Mode Outil et en Mode Canal, en tirant parti de protocoles comme WhatsApp pour les actions déclenchées","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, E-Mails über IPC-Aktionen und hostseitige Gmail API-Aufrufe zu lesen und zu senden, was eine nahtlose Kommunikation sowohl im Tool-Modus als auch im Kanal-Modus ermöglicht, unter Nutzung von Protokollen wie WhatsApp für ausgelöste Aktionen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a lerem e enviarem e-mails usando ações IPC e chamadas de API do Gmail no lado do host, permitindo uma comunicação sem problemas em ambos os modos, Ferramenta e Canal, aproveitando protocolos como o WhatsApp para ações acionadas","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью читать и отправлять электронные письма, используя действия IPC и вызовы API Gmail на стороне хоста, обеспечивая бесперебойную связь как в режиме инструмента, так и в режиме канала, используя протоколы типа WhatsApp для вызванных действий","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من قراءة و إرسال البريد الإلكتروني باستخدام إجراءات IPC و呼وف واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Gmail على جانب المضيف، و مما يتيح اتصالا سلسا في كل من وضع الأداة و وضع القناة، و باستخدام بروتوكولات مثل WhatsApp للعمل المفعّل"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating email responses using Gmail integration","Triggering agent tasks via incoming emails in Channel Mode","Sending emails directly from the agent in Tool Mode"],"zh":["使用Gmail集成自动回复电子邮件","在渠道模式下通过收到的电子邮件触发代理任务","在工具模式下直接从代理发送电子邮件"],"ja":["Gmail統合を使用して電子メールの自動応答","チャネルモードでの受信電子メールによるエージェントタスクのトリガー","ツールモードでのエージェントからの直接電子メール送信"],"ko":["Gmail 통합을 사용하여 이메일 자동 응답","채널 모드에서 수신 이메일을 통한 에이전트 작업 트리거","툴 모드에서 에이전트로부터 직접 이메일 전송"],"es":["Automatización de respuestas por correo electrónico utilizando la integración con Gmail","Activación de tareas del agente mediante correos electrónicos entrantes en el Modo Canal","Envío de correos electrónicos directamente desde el agente en el Modo Herramienta"],"fr":["Automatisation des réponses par e-mail en utilisant l''intégration Gmail","Déclenchement des tâches de l''agent via des e-mails entrants en Mode Canal","Envoi d''e-mails directement depuis l''agent en Mode Outil"],"de":["Automatisierung von E-Mail-Antworten mithilfe der Gmail-Integration","Auslösen von Agentenaufgaben über eingehende E-Mails im Kanal-Modus","Direktes Senden von E-Mails vom Agenten im Tool-Modus"],"pt":["Automatizar respostas de e-mail usando integração do Gmail","Acionar tarefas de agente via e-mails recebidos no Modo Canal","Enviar e-mails diretamente do agente no Modo Ferramenta"],"ru":["Автоматизировать ответы на электронные письма, используя интеграцию с Gmail","Вызывать задачи агента через входящие электронные письма в режиме канала","Отправлять электронные письма直接 из агента в режиме инструмента"],"ar":["توفير استجابات البريد الإلكتروني آليا باستخدام التكامل مع Gmail","تشغيل مهام الوكيل عبر البريد الإلكتروني الوارد في وضع القناة","إرسال البريد الإلكتروني مباشرة من الوكيل في وضع الأداة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Gmail API setup","Legacy MCP references need conversion to IPC actions","Compatibility issues may arise from SDK-based runtime differences"],"zh":["需要Gmail API设置","传统MCP引用需要转换为IPC操作","可能由于SDK基准的运行时差异引起兼容性问题"],"ja":["Gmail APIの設定が必要","レガシMCP参照はIPCアクションへの変換が必要","SDKベースのランタイムの差異により互換性の問題が発生する可能性"],"ko":["Gmail API 설정이 필요","레거시 MCP 참조는 IPC 동작으로 변환해야 함","SDK 기반의 런타임 차이로 인해 호환성 문제가 발생할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere la configuración de la API de Gmail","Las referencias heredadas de MCP necesitan conversión a acciones IPC","Pueden surgir problemas de compatibilidad debido a diferencias en el runtime basado en SDK"],"fr":["Nécessite la configuration de l''API Gmail","Les références héritées MCP doivent être converties en actions IPC","Des problèmes de compatibilité peuvent survenir en raison des différences de runtime basé sur SDK"],"de":["Erfordert die Einrichtung der Gmail API","Veraltete MCP-Referenzen müssen in IPC-Aktionen umgewandelt werden","Kompatibilitätsprobleme können aufgrund von Laufzeitunterschieden auf SDK-Basis auftreten"],"pt":["Exige configuração da API do Gmail","Referências legadas do MCP precisam ser convertidas para ações IPC","Pode haver problemas de compatibilidade devido às diferenças de tempo de execução baseadas em SDK"],"ru":["Требует настройки API Gmail","Наследственные ссылки MCP необходимы для преобразования в действия IPC","Могут возникнуть проблемы совместимости из-за различий в времени выполнения на основе SDK"],"ar":["يتطلب إعداد واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Gmail","REFERENCES الإرث MCP تحتاج إلى التحويل إلى إجراءات IPC","قد تنشأ مشاكل في التوافق بسبب الفروقات في وقت التشغيل المعتمد على SDK"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
