"ja":"Git Commit は Conventional Commits フォーマットに基づいて Git コミットを作成する方法です","ko":"Git Commit은 Conventional Commits 형식에 따라 Git提交을 생성하는 방법입니다","es":"El commit es una habilidad que crea commits de Git siguiendo el formato Conventional Commits con tipo, alcance y asunto adecuados.","fr":"Le commit est une compétence qui crée des commits Git suivant le format Conventional Commits avec type, portée et sujet appropriés.","de":"Der Commit ist eine Fähigkeit, die Git-Commits im Conventional-Commits-Format mit geeignetem Typ, Umfang und Betreff erstellt.","pt":"O commit Git é uma ferramenta para criar commits padrão com tipo, escopo e assunto. Isso ajuda a manter o código organizado e fácil de entender.","ru":"Коммит Git - это инструмент для создания стандартизированных коммитов с типом, областью и темой. Это помогает поддерживать код организованным и легко понимае...","ar":"التزام Git هو أداة لإنشاء التزامات قياسية مع النوع والنطاق والموضوع. هذا يساعد في الحفاظ على код منظم وسهل الفهم","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持 Conventional Commits 格式","包括类型、范围和主题","提高代码提交质量","易于使用和理解","符合开发团队规范"],"ja":["Conventional Commits フォーマットをサポート","タイプ、スコープ、サブジェクトを含む","コードの品質を向上させる","使用しやすく理解容易","開発チームの規約に適合"],"ko":["Conventional Commits 형식 지원","타입, 범위, 주제 포함","코드 제출 품질 향상","사용하기 쉽고 이해하기 쉬움","개발 팀 규약에 부합"],"es":["Creación de commits con formato Conventional Commits","Tipos de commit personalizables (feat, fix, etc.)","Alcance y asunto claros y significativos","Compatibilidad con Git","Mejora del flujo de trabajo con commits claros"],"fr":["Création de commits avec le format Conventional Commits","Types de commit personnalisables (feat, fix, etc.)","Portée et sujet clairs et significatifs","Compatibilité avec Git","Amélioration du flux de travail avec des commits clairs"],"de":["Erstellung von Commits im Conventional-Commits-Format","Anpassbare Commit-Typen (feat, fix usw.)","Klarer und aussagekräftiger Umfang und Betreff","Kompatibilität mit Git","Verbesserung des Arbeitsablaufs mit klaren Commits"],"pt":["Criação de commits padrão","Tipos de commits (feat, fix, etc.)","Escopo e assunto personalizados","Corpo do commit para explicar mudanças","Referência a tarefas e requisitos"],"ru":["Создание стандартизированных коммитов","Типы коммитов (feat, fix и т. д.)","Пользовательский область и тема","Тело коммита для объяснения изменений","Ссылка на задачи и требования"],"ar":["إنشاء التزامات قياسية","أنواع التزامات (feat, fix, etc.)","نطاق وموضوع مخصص","جسم الالتزام لشرح التغييرات","مرجع إلى المهام والمتطلبات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Git Commit","Conventional Commits","代码提交","代码质量","开发团队","代码规范"],"ja":["Git Commit","Conventional Commits","コード提交","コード品質","開発チーム","コード規約"],"ko":["Git Commit","Conventional Commits","코드 제출","코드 품질","개발 팀","코드 규약"],"es":["commit","Conventional Commits","Git","desarrollo de software","flujo de trabajo","control de versiones"],"fr":["commit","Conventional Commits","Git","développement de logiciels","flux de travail","contrôle de version"],"de":["Commit","Conventional Commits","Git","Softwareentwicklung","Arbeitsablauf","Versionskontrolle"],"pt":["commit git","commits padrão","tipo de commit","escopo de commit","assunto de commit","corpo de commit","referência de commit"],"ru":["коммит гит","стандартизированные коммиты","тип коммита","область коммита","тема коммита","тело коммита","ссылка на коммит"],"ar":["التزام جيت","التزامات قياسية","نوع الالتزام","نطاق الالتزام","موضوع الالتزام","جسم الالتزام","مرجع إلى الالتزام"]}},"owner":"reety11","repo":"Hospitality-OS","repoPath":"reety11/Hospitality-OS","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.467Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"commit","description":"Write conventional commit messages with type, scope, and subject when the user wants to commit changes or save work.","bodyPreview":"# Git Commit\n\nCreates git commits following Conventional Commits format with proper type, scope, and subject.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n# 1. Stage changes\ngit add <files>  # or: git add -A\n\n# 2. Create commit (branch commit format)\ngit commit -m \"type(scope): subject\n\nBody explaining HOW and WHY.\nReference: Task X.Y, Req N\"\n```\n\n## Commit Types\n\n### Regular Branch Commits (During Development)\n\n**Format**: `type(scope): subject`\n\n| Type | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `feat` | New feature or func","body":"# Git Commit\n\nCreates git commits following Conventional Commits format with proper type, scope, and subject.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n# 1. Stage changes\ngit add <files>  # or: git add -A\n\n# 2. Create commit (branch commit format)\ngit commit -m \"type(scope): subject\n\nBody explaining HOW and WHY.\nReference: Task X.Y, Req N\"\n```\n\n## Commit Types\n\n### Regular Branch Commits (During Development)\n\n**Format**: `type(scope): subject`\n\n| Type | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `feat` | New feature or functionality |\n| `fix` | Bug fix or issue resolution |\n| `refactor` | Code refactoring without behavior change |\n| `perf` | Performance improvements |\n| `test` | Test additions or modifications |\n| `ci` | CI/CD configuration changes |\n| `docs` | Documentation updates |\n| `chore` | Maintenance, dependencies, tooling |\n| `style` | Code formatting, linting (non-functional) |\n| `security` | Security vulnerability fixes or hardening |\n\n### Scope (Required, kebab-case)\n\nExamples: `validation`, `auth`, `cookie-service`, `template`, `config`, `tests`, `api`\n\n### Subject Line Rules\n\n- Max 50 characters after colon\n- Present tense imperative: add, implement, fix, improve, enhance, refactor, remove, prevent\n- NO period at the end\n- Specific and descriptive - state WHAT, not WHY\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n### 1. Review Changes\n\n```bash\ngit status\ngit diff --staged  # if already staged\ngit diff           # if not staged\n```\n\n### 2. Stage Files\n\n```bash\ngit add <specific-files>  # preferred\n# or\ngit add -A  # all changes\n```\n\n**NEVER commit**:\n- `.env`, `credentials.json`, secrets\n- `node_modules/`, `__pycache__/`, `.venv/`\n- Large binary files without explicit approval\n\n### 3. Create Commit\n\n**Simple change**:\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"fix(auth): use hmac.compare_digest for secure comparison\"\n```\n\n**Complex change (with body)**:\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\nfeat(validation): add URLValidator with domain whitelist\n\nImplement URLValidator class supporting:\n- Domain whitelist enforcement (youtube.com, youtu.be)\n- Dangerous scheme blocking (javascript, data, file)\n- URL parsing with embedded credentials handling\n\nAddresses Requirement 31: Input validation\nPart of Task 5.1: Input Validation Utilities\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n### 4. Verify Commit\n\n```bash\ngit log -1 --format=\"%h %s\"\ngit show --stat HEAD\n```\n\n## Body Format (Recommended for Complex Changes)\n\n```\n<blank line>\nExplain HOW and WHY the change was made.\n- Use bullet points for multiple items\n- Wrap at 72 characters\n\nReference: Task X.Y\nAddresses: Req N\n```\n\n## Git Trailers\n\n| Trailer | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `Fixes #N` | Links and closes issue on merge |\n| `Closes #N` | Same as Fixes |\n| `Co-authored-by: Name <email>` | Credit co-contributors |\n\nPlace trailers at end of body after blank line. See `references/commit_examples.md` for examples.\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\nFor incompatible API/behavior changes, use `!` after scope OR `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer:\n\n```\nfeat(api)!: change response format to JSON:API\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Response envelope changed from `{ data }` to `{ data: { type, id, attributes } }`.\n```\n\nTriggers major version bump in semantic-release.\n\n## Merge Commits (PR Closure)\n\nFor PRs, use extended description with sections:\n\n```bash\ngh pr create --title \"feat(security): implement input validation (Task 5)\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\n- Input validation utilities (URLValidator, FormatValidator)\n- Secure template processor with path traversal prevention\n- API key authentication middleware\n\n## Task Breakdown\nTask 5.1: Input Validation - URLValidator, FormatValidator\nTask 5.2: Template Processing - Path traversal prevention\nTask 5.3: API Key Auth - Multi-key support, excluded paths\nTask 5.4: Security Tests - 102 path traversal tests\n\n## Requirements Covered\nReq 7, Req 9, Req 31, Req 33\n\n## Test Coverage\n- All 473 tests passing\n- Coverage: 93%\n- Pre-commit checks: passing\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n### From github-pr-review\n\nWhen fixing review comments, use this format:\n\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"fix(scope): address review comment #ID\n\nBrief explanation of what was wrong and how it''s fixed.\nAddresses review comment #123456789.\"\n```\n\n### From github-pr-creation\n\nBefore creating PR, ensure all commits follow this format. The PR skill will:\n1. Analyze commits for proper format\n2. Extract types for PR labels\n3. Build PR description from commit bodies\n\n## Important Rules\n\n- **ALWAYS** include scope in parentheses\n- **ALWAYS** use present tense imperative verb\n- **NEVER** end subject with period\n- **NEVER** commit secrets or credentials\n- **NEVER** use generic messages (\"update code\", \"fix bug\", \"changes\")\n- **NEVER** exceed 50 chars in subject line\n- Group related changes -> single focused commit\n\n## Examples\n\n**Good**:\n```\nfeat(validation): add URLValidator with domain whitelist\nfix(auth): use hmac.compare_digest for secure key comparison\nrefactor(template): consolidate filename sanitization logic\ntest(security): add 102 path traversal prevention tests\n```\n\n**Bad**:\n```\nupdate validation code           # no type, no scope, vague\nfeat: add stuff                  # missing scope, too vague\nfix(auth): fix bug               # circular, not specific\nchore: make changes              # missing scope, vague\nfeat(security): improve things.  # has period, vague\n```\n\n## References\n\n- `references/commit_examples.md` - Extended examples by type\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:27:02.401Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing standardized Git commit management with Conventional Commits format support.","zh":"非常适合需要标准化 Git 提交管理的开发代理，支持 Conventional Commits 格式。","ja":"Conventional Commits 形式の標準的な Git コミット管理が必要な開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"표준화된 Git 커밋 관리가 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합하며 Conventional Commits 형식을 지원합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una gestión de commits de Git estandarizada con soporte para el formato de Commits Convencionales.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une gestion de commits Git standardisée avec une prise en charge du format de Commits Conventionnels.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine standardisierte Git-Commit-Verwaltung mit Unterstützung für das Conventional Commits-Format benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de gerenciamento de commit do Git padronizado com suporte ao formato de Commits Convencionais.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым необходима стандартизированная система управления коммитами Git с поддержкой формата Conventional Commits.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة التزامات جيت قياسية مع دعم تنسيق التعهدات التقليدية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create properly formatted Git commits with type, scope, and subject, following the Conventional Commits specification, utilizing git add and git commit commands with formatted commit messages.","zh":"赋予代理创建格式正确的 Git 提交的能力，包括类型、范围和主题，遵循 Conventional Commits 规范，利用 git add 和 git commit 命令以格式化的提交消息。","ja":"Conventional Commits の仕様に従って、タイプ、スコープ、サブジェクトを含む適切にフォーマットされた Git コミットを作成するエージェントの能力を与えます。git add および git commit コマンドを使用して、フォーマットされたコミット メッセージでコミットを作成します。","ko":"에이전트가 Conventional Commits 사양을 따라 유형, 범위 및 주제를 포함하여 올바르게 형식화된 Git 커밋을 생성하는 능력을 부여합니다. git add 및 git commit 명령을 사용하여 형식화된 커밋 메시지로 커밋을 생성합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear commits de Git debidamente formateados con tipo, alcance y asunto, siguiendo la especificación de Commits Convencionales, utilizando los comandos git add y git commit con mensajes de commit formateados.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des commits Git correctement formatés avec un type, une portée et un sujet, en suivant la spécification des Commits Conventionnels, en utilisant les commandes git add et git commit avec des messages de commit formatés.","de":"Ermächtigt die Mittel, ordnungsgemäß formatierte Git-Commits mit Typ, Umfang und Betreff zu erstellen, die den Conventional Commits-Spezifikationen entsprechen, indem die Befehle git add und git commit mit formatierten Commit-Meldungen verwendet werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes criem commits do Git formatados corretamente com tipo, escopo e assunto, seguindo a especificação Conventional Commits, utilizando os comandos git add e git commit com mensagens de commit formatadas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать правильно отформатированные коммиты Git с типом, областью и темой, следуя спецификации Conventional Commits, используя команды git add и git commit с отформатированными сообщениями о коммитах.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إنشاء التزامات جيت مع التنسيق الصحيح مع النوع والنطاق والموضوع، اتباعا لمواصفات التعهدات التقليدية، باستخدام أوامر جيت أضف وجيت التزام مع رسائل التزام معدة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating commit messages for new features","Generating commit history reports with proper type and scope","Standardizing commit formats across development teams"],"zh":["自动为新功能生成提交消息","使用正确的类型和范围生成提交历史报告","在开发团队中标准化提交格式"],"ja":["新機能のコミット メッセージを自動生成する","適切なタイプとスコープを使用してコミット履歴レポートを生成する","開発チーム全体でコミット形式を標準化する"],"ko":["새로운 기능에 대한 커밋 메시지를 자동 생성하는こと","적절한 유형과 범위를 사용하여 커밋 기록 보고서를 생성하는 것","개발 팀 전체에서 커밋 형식을 표준화하는 것"],"es":["Automatización de mensajes de commit para nuevas características","Generación de informes de historial de commit con tipo y alcance adecuados","Estandarización de formatos de commit en equipos de desarrollo"],"fr":["Automatisation des messages de commit pour les nouvelles fonctionnalités","Génération de rapports d''historique de commit avec type et portée appropriés","Standardisation des formats de commit dans les équipes de développement"],"de":["Automatisierung von Commit-Meldungen für neue Funktionen","Erstellung von Commit-Historienberichten mit ordnungsgemäßen Typ und Umfang","Standardisierung von Commit-Formaten in Entwicklungsteams"],"pt":["Automatizar mensagens de commit para recursos novos","Gerar relatórios de histórico de commit com tipo e escopo apropriados","Padronizar formatos de commit em equipes de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Автоматизация сообщений о коммитах для новых функций","Генерация отчетов об истории коммитов с правильным типом и областью","Стандартизация форматов коммитов в командах разработки"],"ar":["تأتمتات رسائل الالتزام لخصائص جديدة","توليد تقارير بتاريخ الالتزام مع النوع والمدى المناسبين","توحيد تنسيقات الالتزام عبر فرق التطوير"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git installation and configuration","Limited to Conventional Commits format"],"zh":["需要 Git 安装和配置","仅限于 Conventional Commits 格式"],"ja":["Git のインストールと構成が必要","Conventional Commits 形式のみをサポート"],"ko":["Git 설치 및 구성이 필요함","Conventional Commits 형식만 지원"],"es":["Requiere la instalación y configuración de Git","Limitado al formato de Commits Convencionales"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de Git","Limité au format de Commits Conventionnels"],"de":["Erfordert die Installation und Konfiguration von Git","Begrenzt auf das Conventional Commits-Format"],"pt":["Requer instalação e configuração do Git","Limitado ao formato de Commits Convencionais"],"ru":["Требуется установка и конфигурация Git","Ограничен форматом Conventional Commits"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت جيت وتفصيله","محدود بتنسيق التعهدات التقليدية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('narumiruna/telegram-bot/python-packaging-uv', 'community', 'narumiruna', 'telegram-bot', 'narumiruna/telegram-bot', 'python-packaging-uv', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.467Z', '2026-02-18T08:27:49.632Z', NULL, '{"id":"narumiruna/telegram-bot/python-packaging-uv","name":"python-packaging-uv","description":{"es":"El empaquetado de Python con uv permite construir y publicar paquetes de manera eficiente.","fr":"Le packaging Python avec uv permet de construire et de publier des packages de manière efficace.","de":"Das Python-Packaging mit uv ermöglicht die effiziente Erstellung und Veröffentlichung von Paketen.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Empaquetado de Python con uv","fr":"Packaging Python avec uv","de":"Python-Packaging mit uv","en":"python-packaging-uv"},"description":{"es":"El empaquetado de Python con uv permite construir y publicar paquetes de manera eficiente.","fr":"Le packaging Python avec uv permet de construire et de publier des packages de manière efficace.","de":"Das Python-Packaging mit uv ermöglicht die effiziente Erstellung und Veröffentlichung von Paketen.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"es":["Construcción de wheels y sdists","Publicación en PyPI","Soporte para Test PyPI","Comandos personalizables","Flujos de trabajo automatizados"],"fr":["Construction de wheels et sdists","Publication sur PyPI","Prise en charge de Test PyPI","Commandes personnalisables","Workflows automatisés"],"de":["Erstellung von Wheels und Sdist","Veröffentlichung auf PyPI","Unterstützung für Test PyPI","Anpassbare Befehle","Automatisierte Workflows"]},"keywords":{"es":["empaquetado de python","uv","pyPI","wheels","sdists","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo"],"fr":["packaging python","uv","pyPI","wheels","sdists","développement de logiciels","outils de développement"],"de":["python-packaging","uv","pyPI","wheels","sdists","software-entwicklung","entwicklungstools"]}},"owner":"narumiruna","repo":"telegram-bot","repoPath":"narumiruna/telegram-bot","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.467Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"python-packaging-uv","description":"Use when building or publishing Python packages with uv, including dist artifacts and pre-publish checks.","bodyPreview":"# Python Packaging with uv\n\n## Overview\n\nUse uv build and publish commands to produce wheels/sdists and ship to PyPI. Core principle: build, verify, then publish.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Command |\n| --- | --- |\n| Build wheel+sdist | `uv build` |\n| Build wheel only | `uv build --no-sources` |\n| Publish to PyPI | `uv publish --token $PYPI_TOKEN` |\n| Publish to Test PyPI | `uv publish --publish-url https://test.pypi.org/legacy/ --token $TEST_PYPI_TOKEN` |\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Build artifacts in `","body":"# Python Packaging with uv\n\n## Overview\n\nUse uv build and publish commands to produce wheels/sdists and ship to PyPI. Core principle: build, verify, then publish.\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Task | Command |\n| --- | --- |\n| Build wheel+sdist | `uv build` |\n| Build wheel only | `uv build --no-sources` |\n| Publish to PyPI | `uv publish --token $PYPI_TOKEN` |\n| Publish to Test PyPI | `uv publish --publish-url https://test.pypi.org/legacy/ --token $TEST_PYPI_TOKEN` |\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Build artifacts in `dist/`.\n2. Test install from wheel.\n3. Publish to Test PyPI, validate, then publish to PyPI.\n\n## Example\n\n```bash\nuv build --no-sources\nuv pip install dist/my_package-1.0.0-py3-none-any.whl\nuv publish --publish-url https://test.pypi.org/legacy/ --token $TEST_PYPI_TOKEN\n```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n- Publishing before verifying wheel contents.\n- Skipping Test PyPI for first release.\n\n## Red Flags\n\n- Packaging guidance that ignores uv build/publish.\n\n## References\n\n- `references/packaging.md` - Build and publish details\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:27:49.632Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Python Development Agents needing streamlined package building and publishing to PyPI.","zh":"非常适合需要简化包构建和发布到PyPI的Python开发代理。","ja":"PyPIへのパッケージの構築と公開を簡素化する必要があるPython開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"PyPI에 패키지를 구축하고 게시하기 위한 패키지를 단순화해야 하는 Python 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo de Python que necesitan una compilación y publicación de paquetes simplificadas en PyPI.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement Python qui ont besoin d''une construction et de publication de paquets simplifiées sur PyPI.","de":"Perfekt für Python-Entwicklungsagenten, die eine vereinfachte Paketbildung und -veröffentlichung auf PyPI benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Python que necessitam de compilação e publicação de pacotes simplificadas para o PyPI.","ru":"Идеально для агентов разработки Python, которым необходима упрощенная сборка и публикация пакетов в PyPI.","ar":"เหมาะ لعميل تطوير بايثون الذي يحتاج إلى بناء حزمة وبناء متدفق إلى PyPI."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build and publish Python packages using uv, supporting wheel and sdist formats, with secure publishing to PyPI and Test PyPI using tokens.","zh":"赋予代理构建和发布Python包的能力，支持wheel和sdist格式，并使用令牌安全地将其发布到PyPI和Test PyPI。","ja":"エージェントがuvを使用してPythonパッケージを構築および公開する機能を提供し、wheelおよびsdist形式をサポートし、トークンを使用してPyPIおよびTest PyPIへの公開を安全に行います。","ko":"uv를 사용하여 Python 패키지를 구축 및 게시하는 에이전트의 능력을 강화하여 wheel 및 sdist 형식을 지원하며 토큰을 사용하여 PyPI 및 Test PyPI로 안전하게 게시합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a compilar y publicar paquetes de Python utilizando uv, que admite los formatos wheel y sdist, con publicación segura en PyPI y Test PyPI utilizando tokens.","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire et de publier des paquets Python en utilisant uv, en prenant en charge les formats wheel et sdist, avec une publication sécurisée sur PyPI et Test PyPI à l''aide de jetons.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, P