 기술 평가가 필요합니다","es":"La revisión de código es crucial para garantizar la calidad del software. Aprende a recibir revisiones de código de manera efectiva","fr":"La révision de code est cruciale pour garantir la qualité du logiciel. Apprenez à recevoir des révisions de code de manière efficace","de":"Die Code-Review ist entscheidend für die Qualität der Software. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Code-Reviews effektiv erhalten","pt":"Revisão de código é uma etapa crucial no desenvolvimento de software, garantindo a qualidade e a segurança do código","ru":"Код-ревью является важным этапом в разработке программного обеспечения, обеспечивающим качество и безопасность кода","ar":"مراجعة الكود هي خطوة حاسمة في تطوير البرمجيات، وتضمن جودة وأمان الكود","en":" question your logs | AI Observability Platform for GenAI/LLM workloads. OTLP ingestion, DuckDB storage, semantic conventions for AI telemetry."},"definition":{"en":" question your logs | AI Observability Platform for GenAI/LLM workloads. OTLP ingestion, DuckDB storage, semantic conventions for AI telemetry."},"features":{"zh":["技术评估","验证和实施","协作模式","代码质量保证"],"ja":["技術評価","検証と実装","コラボレーションパターン","コード品質保証"],"ko":["기술 평가","검증 및 구현","협업 패턴","코드 품질 보장"],"es":["Principios de revisión de código","Mejores prácticas para la colaboración","Evaluación técnica del código","Verificación antes de implementación","Preguntar antes de asumir"],"fr":["Principes de révision de code","Meilleures pratiques pour la collaboration","Évaluation technique du code","Vérification avant mise en œuvre","Demander avant de supposer"],"de":["Prinzipien der Code-Review","Best Practices für die Zusammenarbeit","Technische Bewertung des Codes","Verifizierung vor Implementierung","Fragen vor Annahme"],"pt":["Verificação técnica do código","Colaboração em equipe","Melhoria da qualidade do código","Garantia de segurança","Otimização do desempenho","Integração contínua"],"ru":["Техническая проверка кода","Командная работа","Улучшение качества кода","Обеспечение безопасности","Оптимизация производительности","Непрерывная интеграция"],"ar":["التحقق الفني للكود","التعاون الفريق","تحسين جودة الكود","ضمان الأمان","تحسين الأداء","التكامل المستمر"]},"keywords":{"zh":["代码审查","技术评估","代码质量","开发过程","协作模式","代码管理"],"ja":["コードレビュー","技術評価","コード品質","開発プロセス","コラボレーションパターン","コード管理"],"ko":["코드 리뷰","기술 평가","코드 품질","개발 프로세스","협업 패턴","코드 관리"],"es":["revisión de código","principios de revisión de código","mejores prácticas de colaboración","evaluación técnica del código","verificación antes de implementación","preguntar antes de asumir","desarrollo de software","calidad del código"],"fr":["révision de code","principes de révision de code","meilleures pratiques de collaboration","évaluation technique du code","vérification avant mise en œuvre","demander avant de supposer","développement de logiciels","qualité du code"],"de":["Code-Review","Prinzipien der Code-Review","Best Practices für die Zusammenarbeit","technische Bewertung des Codes","Verifizierung vor Implementierung","Fragen vor Annahme","Software-Entwicklung","Code-Qualität"],"pt":["revisão de código","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade do código","segurança do código","colaboração em equipe","melhoria da qualidade","otimização do desempenho","integração contínua"],"ru":["код-ревью","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода","безопасность кода","командная работа","улучшение качества","оптимизация производительности","непрерывная интеграция"],"ar":["مراجعة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة الكود","أمان الكود","التعاون الفريق","تحسين الجودة","تحسين الأداء","التكامل المستمر"]}},"owner":"ANcpLua","repo":"qyl","repoPath":"ANcpLua/qyl","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.468Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"receiving-code-review","description":"|","bodyPreview":"## Source Metadata\n\n```yaml\nplugin:\n  name: \"superpowers\"\n  version: \"4.1.1\"\n  description: \"Core skills library for Claude Code: TDD, debugging, collaboration patterns, and proven techniques\"\n  author:\n    name: \"Jesse Vincent\"\n    email: \"jesse@fsck.com\"\n```\n\n\n# Code Review Reception\n\n## Overview\n\nCode review requires technical evaluation, not emotional performance.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify before implementing. Ask before assuming. Technical correctness over social comfort.\n\n## The Response","body":"## Source Metadata\n\n```yaml\nplugin:\n  name: \"superpowers\"\n  version: \"4.1.1\"\n  description: \"Core skills library for Claude Code: TDD, debugging, collaboration patterns, and proven techniques\"\n  author:\n    name: \"Jesse Vincent\"\n    email: \"jesse@fsck.com\"\n```\n\n\n# Code Review Reception\n\n## Overview\n\nCode review requires technical evaluation, not emotional performance.\n\n**Core principle:** Verify before implementing. Ask before assuming. Technical correctness over social comfort.\n\n## The Response Pattern\n\n```\nWHEN receiving code review feedback:\n\n1. READ: Complete feedback without reacting\n2. UNDERSTAND: Restate requirement in own words (or ask)\n3. VERIFY: Check against codebase reality\n4. EVALUATE: Technically sound for THIS codebase?\n5. RESPOND: Technical acknowledgment or reasoned pushback\n6. IMPLEMENT: One item at a time, test each\n```\n\n## Forbidden Responses\n\n**NEVER:**\n- \"You''re absolutely right!\" (explicit CLAUDE.md violation)\n- \"Great point!\" / \"Excellent feedback!\" (performative)\n- \"Let me implement that now\" (before verification)\n\n**INSTEAD:**\n- Restate the technical requirement\n- Ask clarifying questions\n- Push back with technical reasoning if wrong\n- Just start working (actions > words)\n\n## Handling Unclear Feedback\n\n```\nIF any item is unclear:\n  STOP - do not implement anything yet\n  ASK for clarification on unclear items\n\nWHY: Items may be related. Partial understanding = wrong implementation.\n```\n\n**Example:**\n```\nyour human partner: \"Fix 1-6\"\nYou understand 1,2,3,6. Unclear on 4,5.\n\n❌ WRONG: Implement 1,2,3,6 now, ask about 4,5 later\n✅ RIGHT: \"I understand items 1,2,3,6. Need clarification on 4 and 5 before proceeding.\"\n```\n\n## Source-Specific Handling\n\n### From your human partner\n- **Trusted** - implement after understanding\n- **Still ask** if scope unclear\n- **No performative agreement**\n- **Skip to action** or technical acknowledgment\n\n### From External Reviewers\n```\nBEFORE implementing:\n  1. Check: Technically correct for THIS codebase?\n  2. Check: Breaks existing functionality?\n  3. Check: Reason for current implementation?\n  4. Check: Works on all platforms/versions?\n  5. Check: Does reviewer understand full context?\n\nIF suggestion seems wrong:\n  Push back with technical reasoning\n\nIF can''t easily verify:\n  Say so: \"I can''t verify this without [X]. Should I [investigate/ask/proceed]?\"\n\nIF conflicts with your human partner''s prior decisions:\n  Stop and discuss with your human partner first\n```\n\n**your human partner''s rule:** \"External feedback - be skeptical, but check carefully\"\n\n## YAGNI Check for \"Professional\" Features\n\n```\nIF reviewer suggests \"implementing properly\":\n  grep codebase for actual usage\n\n  IF unused: \"This endpoint isn''t called. Remove it (YAGNI)?\"\n  IF used: Then implement properly\n```\n\n**your human partner''s rule:** \"You and reviewer both report to me. If we don''t need this feature, don''t add it.\"\n\n## Implementation Order\n\n```\nFOR multi-item feedback:\n  1. Clarify anything unclear FIRST\n  2. Then implement in this order:\n     - Blocking issues (breaks, security)\n     - Simple fixes (typos, imports)\n     - Complex fixes (refactoring, logic)\n  3. Test each fix individually\n  4. Verify no regressions\n```\n\n## When To Push Back\n\nPush back when:\n- Suggestion breaks existing functionality\n- Reviewer lacks full context\n- Violates YAGNI (unused feature)\n- Technically incorrect for this stack\n- Legacy/compatibility reasons exist\n- Conflicts with your human partner''s architectural decisions\n\n**How to push back:**\n- Use technical reasoning, not defensiveness\n- Ask specific questions\n- Reference working tests/code\n- Involve your human partner if architectural\n\n**Signal if uncomfortable pushing back out loud:** \"Strange things are afoot at the Circle K\"\n\n## Acknowledging Correct Feedback\n\nWhen feedback IS correct:\n```\n✅ \"Fixed. [Brief description of what changed]\"\n✅ \"Good catch - [specific issue]. Fixed in [location].\"\n✅ [Just fix it and show in the code]\n\n❌ \"You''re absolutely right!\"\n❌ \"Great point!\"\n❌ \"Thanks for catching that!\"\n❌ \"Thanks for [anything]\"\n❌ ANY gratitude expression\n```\n\n**Why no thanks:** Actions speak. Just fix it. The code itself shows you heard the feedback.\n\n**If you catch yourself about to write \"Thanks\":** DELETE IT. State the fix instead.\n\n## Gracefully Correcting Your Pushback\n\nIf you pushed back and were wrong:\n```\n✅ \"You were right - I checked [X] and it does [Y]. Implementing now.\"\n✅ \"Verified this and you''re correct. My initial understanding was wrong because [reason]. Fixing.\"\n\n❌ Long apology\n❌ Defending why you pushed back\n❌ Over-explaining\n```\n\nState the correction factually and move on.\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Fix |\n|---------|-----|\n| Performative agreement | State requirement or just act |\n| Blind implementation | Verify against codebase first |\n| Batch without testing | One at a time, test each |\n| Assuming reviewer is right | Check if breaks things |\n| Avoiding pushback | Technical correctness > comfort |\n| Partial implementation | Clarify all items first |\n| Can''t verify, proceed anyway | State limitation, ask for direction |\n\n## Real Examples\n\n**Performative Agreement (Bad):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Remove legacy code\"\n❌ \"You''re absolutely right! Let me remove that...\"\n```\n\n**Technical Verification (Good):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Remove legacy code\"\n✅ \"Checking... build target is 10.15+, this API needs 13+. Need legacy for backward compat. Current impl has wrong bundle ID - fix it or drop pre-13 support?\"\n```\n\n**YAGNI (Good):**\n```\nReviewer: \"Implement proper metrics tracking with database, date filters, CSV export\"\n✅ \"Grepped codebase - nothing calls this endpoint. Remove it (YAGNI)? Or is there usage I''m missing?\"\n```\n\n**Unclear Item (Good):**\n```\nyour human partner: \"Fix items 1-6\"\nYou understand 1,2,3,6. Unclear on 4,5.\n✅ \"Understand 1,2,3,6. Need clarification on 4 and 5 before implementing.\"\n```\n\n## GitHub Thread Replies\n\nWhen replying to inline review comments on GitHub, reply in the comment thread (`gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{pr}/comments/{id}/replies`), not as a top-level PR comment.\n\n## The Bottom Line\n\n**External feedback = suggestions to evaluate, not orders to follow.**\n\nVerify. Question. Then implement.\n\nNo performative agreement. Technical rigor always.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:31:38.262Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Essential for AI Observability Agents specializing in LLM workload telemetry analysis and code review validation.","zh":"适用于专门从事大语言模型工作量遥测分析和代码审查验证的AI可观察性代理。","ja":"LLMワークロードのテレメトリ分析およびコードレビューの検証を専門とするAIオブザーバビリティエージェントに不可欠。","ko":"대규모 언어 모델 작업량 텔레메트리 분석 및 코드 리뷰 유효성 검사를 전문으로 하는 AI 관측 가능성 에이전트에 필수적입니다.","es":"Esencial para los agentes de observabilidad de IA que se especializan en el análisis de telemetría de carga de trabajo de LLM y la validación de revisión de código.","fr":"Essentiel pour les agents d''observabilité de l''IA spécialisés dans l''analyse de la télémétrie de charge de travail LLM et la validation de la révision de code.","de":"Wesentlich für AI-Beobachtungsagenten, die sich auf die Analyse der Telemetrie von LLM-Workloads und die Überprüfung der Code-Validierung spezialisieren.","pt":"Essencial para Agentes de Observabilidade de IA especializados em análise de telemetria de carga de trabalho LLM e validação de revisão de código.","ru":"Необходимо для агентов наблюдения за ИИ, специализирующихся на анализе телеметрии рабочей нагрузки LLM и проверке кода.","ar":"ضروري للوكلاء المراقبين للذكاء الاصطناعي المتخصصين في تحليل بيانات المراقبة للحمل الزائد LLM وتأكيد مراجعة الكود."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables OTLP ingestion and DuckDB storage for AI telemetry with semantic conventions, providing technical evaluation capabilities for code review reception without emotional bias.","zh":"启用OTLP摄取和DuckDB存储，用于具有语义约定的AI遥测，提供技术评估能力，用于没有情感偏见的代码审查接收。","ja":"OTLPの取り込みとDuckDBのストレージを有効にし、セマンティック規約を使用したAIテレメトリを提供し、感情的偏見のないコードレビューの受信に対して技術評価機能を提供します。","ko":"OTLP摄取 및 DuckDB 저장소를 활성화하여语义约定을 사용한 AI 텔레메트리를 제공하고 감정적 편향이 없는 코드 리뷰 수신에 대한 기술 평가 기능을 제공합니다.","es":"Permite la ingesta de OTLP y el almacenamiento de DuckDB para la telemetría de IA con convenciones semánticas, proporcionando capacidades de evaluación técnica para la recepción de revisiones de código sin sesgo emocional.","fr":"Permet l''ingestion OTLP et le stockage DuckDB pour la télémétrie de l''IA avec des conventions sémantiques, fournissant des capacités d''évaluation technique pour la réception de révision de code sans biais émotionnel.","de":"Ermöglicht die OTLP-Einbeziehung und den DuckDB-Speicher für die AI-Telemetrie mit semantischen Konventionen, die technische Bewertungsfähigkeiten für die Code-Überprüfungseingabe ohne emotionale Voreingenommenheit bereitstellen.","pt":"Permite a ingestão de OTLP e o armazenamento DuckDB para telemetria de IA com convenções semânticas, fornecendo capacidades de avaliação técnica para a recepção de revisão de código sem viés emocional.","ru":"Позволяет использовать приемку OTLP и хранение DuckDB для телеметрии ИИ с семантическими соглашениями, обеспечивая технические возможности оценки для приема проверки кода без эмоционального предубеждения.","ar":"يسمح بالاستهلاك OTLP وتخزين DuckDB لمعاينة الذكاء الاصطناعي بالاتفاقات الدلالية، وتوفير القدرات التقنية لتقييم استقبال مراجعة الكود بدون تحيز عاطفي."},"useCases":{"en":["Processing OTLP telemetry data from GenAI workloads","Storing and querying AI observability data in DuckDB","Applying semantic conventions to AI telemetry analysis","Conducting technical code review evaluations"],"zh":["处理来自GenAI工作量的OTLP遥测数据","在DuckDB中存储和查询AI可观察性数据","将语义约定应用于AI遥测分析","进行技术代码审查评估"],"ja":["GenAIワークロードからのOTLPテレメトリデータを処理する","DuckDBにAIオブザーバビリティデータを保存して照会する","AIテレメトリ分析にセマンティック規約を適用する","技術的なコードレビュー評価を実施する"],"ko":["GenAI 작업량에서来的 OTLP 텔레메트리 데이터를 처리","DuckDB에 AI 관측 가능성 데이터를 저장하고 쿼리","AI 텔레메트리 분석에语义约定을 적용","기술적인 코드 리뷰 평가를 수행"],"es":["Procesamiento de datos de telemetría OTLP desde cargas de trabajo de GenAI","Almacenamiento y consulta de datos de observabilidad de IA en DuckDB","Aplicación de convenciones semánticas al análisis de telemetría de IA","Realización de evaluaciones técnicas de revisión de código"],"fr":["Traitement des données de télémétrie OTLP à partir de charges de travail GenAI","Stockage et interrogation des données d''observabilité de l''IA dans DuckDB","Application de conventions sémantiques à l''analyse de la télémétrie de l''IA","Réalisations d''évaluations techniques de révision de code"],"de":["Verarbeitung von OTLP-Telemetriedaten aus GenAI-Workloads","Speicherung und Abfrage von AI-Beobachtungsdaten in DuckDB","Anwendung von semantischen Konventionen auf die AI-Telemetrie-Analyse","Durchführung von technischen Code-Überprüfungsbewertungen"],"pt":["Processamento de dados de telemetria OTLP de cargas de trabalho GenAI","Armazenamento e consulta de dados de observabilidade de IA no DuckDB","Aplicação de convenções semânticas à análise de telemetria de IA","Realização de avaliações técnicas de revisão de código"],"ru":["Обработка данных телеметрии OTLP рабочих нагрузок GenAI","Хранение и запрос данных наблюдения за ИИ в DuckDB","Применение семантических соглашений к анализу телеметрии ИИ","Проведение технических оценок проверки кода"],"ar":["معالجة بيانات المراقبة OTLP للحمل الزائد GenAI","تخزين واستعلام بيانات المراقبة للذكاء الاصطناعي في DuckDB","تطبيق الاتفاقات الدلالية على تحليل بيانات المراقبة للذكاء الاصطناعي","إجراء تقييمات تقنية لمراجعة الكود"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OTLP-compatible telemetry sources","DuckDB storage dependency","Limited to AI/LLM semantic conventions"],"zh":["需要OTLP兼容的遥测源","依赖DuckDB存储","仅限AI/LLM语义约定"],"ja":["OTLP互換のテレメトリソースが必要","DuckDBストレージに依存","AI/LLMセマンティック規約のみ"],"ko":["OTLP 호환 텔레메트리 소스가 필요","DuckDB 저장소 의존","AI/LLM语义约定만"],"es":["Requiere fuentes de telemetría compatibles con OTLP","Dependencia de almacenamiento de DuckDB","Limitado a convenciones semánticas de IA/LLM"],"fr":["Nécessite des sources de télémétrie compatibles OTLP","Dépendance de stockage DuckDB","Limité aux conventions sémantiques de l''IA/LLM"],"de":["Benötigt OTLP-kompatible Telemetriequellen","DuckDB-Speicherabhängigkeit","Begrenzt auf semantische Konventionen von AI/LLM"],"pt":["Exige fontes de telemetria compatíveis com OTLP","Dependência de armazenamento DuckDB","Limitado a convenções semânticas de IA/LLM"],"ru":["Требует источников телеметрии, совместимых с OTLP","Зависимость от хранилища DuckDB","Ограничен семантическими соглашениями ИИ/LLM"],"ar":["يتطلب مصادر مراقبة متوافقة مع OTLP","اعتماد على تخزين DuckDB","محدود بالاتفاقات الدلالية للذكاء الاصطناعي/LLM"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
