 aplicación de escritorio Spellbook con Playwright y utilidades personalizadas","fr":"Guide spécialisé pour écrire des tests E2E pour l''application de bureau Spellbook avec Playwright et utilitaires personnalisés","de":"Spezialisierte Anleitung zum Schreiben von E2E-Tests für die Spellbook-Desktop-Anwendung mit Playwright und benutzerdefinierten Utilities","pt":"O playwright-e2e-spellbook fornece orientação especializada para testes E2E do aplicativo de desktop Spellbook usando Playwright.","ru":"Playwright-e2e-spellbook предоставляет специализированное руководство для тестирования E2E настольного приложения Spellbook с использованием Playwright.","ar":"يوفر playwright-e2e-spellbook إرشادات متخصصة لاختبارات E2E لتطبيق Spellbook على سطح المكتب باستخدام Playwright.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["Playwright E2E","Tauri","","MIGRATION.md",""],"ja":["Playwright E2E","Tauri","","MIGRATION.md",""],"ko":["Playwright E2E","Tauri","","MIGRATION.md",""],"es":["Pruebas E2E personalizadas para Spellbook","Utilidades y fixtures personalizados para Playwright","Migración de pruebas existentes a infraestructura moderna","Mejora de la infraestructura de prueba","Guía paso a paso para la migración"],"fr":["Tests E2E personnalisés pour Spellbook","Utilitaires et fixtures personnalisés pour Playwright","Migration de tests existants vers une infrastructure moderne","Amélioration de l''infrastructure de test","Guide étape par étape pour la migration"],"de":["Benutzerdefinierte E2E-Tests für Spellbook","Benutzerdefinierte Utilities und Fixtures für Playwright","Migration von bestehenden Tests zu moderner Infrastruktur","Verbesserung der Testinfrastruktur","Schritt-für-Schritt-Anleitung für die Migration"],"pt":["Testes E2E personalizados para Spellbook","Fixtures e utilitários personalizados","Migração de testes existentes","Lista de verificação para revisão de PR","Exemplos de antes e depois"],"ru":["Пользовательские тесты E2E для Spellbook","Настраиваемые фикстуры и утилиты","Миграция существующих тестов","Чек-лист для проверки PR","Примеры до и после"],"ar":["اختبارات E2E مخصصة لسبل بوك","إصلاحات و أدوات مخصصة","هجرة الاختبارات الحالية","قائمة التحقق لمراجعة PR","أمثلة قبل وبعد"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Playwright E2E","Tauri","E2E","","MIGRATION.md","PR",""],"ja":["Playwright E2E","Tauri","E2E","","MIGRATION.md","PR",""],"ko":["Playwright E2E","Tauri","E2E","","MIGRATION.md","PR",""],"es":["pruebas E2E","Playwright","Spellbook","tests de extremo a extremo","infraestructura de prueba","migración de pruebas","utilidades personalizadas","fixtures personalizados"],"fr":["tests E2E","Playwright","Spellbook","tests de bout en bout","infrastructure de test","migration de tests","utilitaires personnalisés","fixtures personnalisés"],"de":["E2E-Tests","Playwright","Spellbook","End-to-End-Tests","Testinfrastruktur","Testmigration","benutzerdefinierte Utilities","benutzerdefinierte Fixtures"],"pt":["testes E2E","playwright","spellbook","testes automatizados","desenvolvimento de software","aplicativos de desktop"],"ru":["тесты E2E","playwright","spellbook","автоматизированное тестирование","разработка программного обеспечения","настольные приложения"],"ar":["اختبارات E2E","playwright","سبل بوك","اختبارات آلية","تطوير البرمجيات","برامج سطح المكتب"]}},"owner":"runecalico-ai","repo":"second_edition_spellbook","repoPath":"runecalico-ai/second_edition_spellbook","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.468Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"playwright-e2e-spellbook","description":"Playwright E2E testing for the Spellbook Tauri desktop application with shared fixtures, page objects, and test utilities. Use when writing or modifying E2E tests for the Spellbook app, debugging test failures, or setting up new test infrastructure. Includes automatic app lifecycle management, file tracking, and common test patterns.","bodyPreview":"# Playwright E2E Testing for Spellbook\n\nSpecialized guidance for writing E2E tests for the Spellbook Tauri desktop application using Playwright with custom fixtures and utilities.\n\n## Migrating Existing Tests\n\n**Updating old tests to use modern infrastructure?** See [references/MIGRATION.md](references/MIGRATION.md) for:\n- Step-by-step migration checklist\n- Quick wins (low effort, high value changes)\n- Complete before/after examples\n- PR review checklist\n- Common migration pitfalls\n\n## Build Req","body":"# Playwright E2E Testing for Spellbook\n\nSpecialized guidance for writing E2E tests for the Spellbook Tauri desktop application using Playwright with custom fixtures and utilities.\n\n## Migrating Existing Tests\n\n**Updating old tests to use modern infrastructure?** See [references/MIGRATION.md](references/MIGRATION.md) for:\n- Step-by-step migration checklist\n- Quick wins (low effort, high value changes)\n- Complete before/after examples\n- PR review checklist\n- Common migration pitfalls\n\n## Build Requirements Before Testing\n\n> [!CRITICAL]\n> **ALWAYS rebuild the application** before running tests after code changes. Playwright tests launch the compiled application, not source code.\n\n### Backend Changes (Rust)\n\nIf you modified files in `src-tauri/src/` or `Cargo.toml`:\n\n```powershell\ncd apps/desktop\npnpm tauri:build --debug\n```\n\nThis rebuilds the Rust backend and bundles the frontend (30-90 seconds full, 5-15 incremental).\n\n### Frontend Changes (TypeScript/React)\n\nIf you only modified files in `src/`:\n\n```powershell\ncd apps/desktop\npnpm build\n```\n\nThis creates the production bundle in `dist/` (5-20 seconds).\n\n### Both or Unsure\n\nWhen in doubt, perform a full rebuild:\n\n```powershell\ncd apps/desktop\npnpm tauri:build --debug\n```\n\n**See `/test-workflow` for the complete rebuild and test workflow.**\n\n## Quick Start Template\n\n```typescript\nimport { expect, test } from \"./fixtures/test-fixtures\";\nimport { TIMEOUTS } from \"./fixtures/constants\";\nimport { createTmpFilePath, generateRunId, getTestDirname } from \"./fixtures/test-utils\";\nimport { SpellbookApp } from \"./page-objects/SpellbookApp\";\n\nconst __dirname = getTestDirname(import.meta.url);\n\ntest.describe(\"My Feature\", () => {\n  test(\"my test case\", async ({ appContext, fileTracker }) => {\n    const { page } = appContext;\n    const app = new SpellbookApp(page);\n    const runId = generateRunId();\n\n    // Your test code here\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## Visual Debugging with Screenshots\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **CDP Trace Limitation**: When using `connectOverCDP` to test Tauri apps, Playwright traces **cannot capture screenshots automatically**. The trace viewer will show `about:blank` instead of visual snapshots. This is a fundamental limitation of CDP connections, not a configuration issue.\n\n**What still works in traces:**\n- ✅ DOM snapshots (inspect page structure)\n- ✅ Network activity\n- ✅ Console logs\n- ✅ Test actions and timing\n\n**Workaround**: Use manual screenshot capture for visual debugging.\n\n### Manual Screenshot Capture\n\nUse the `captureDebugScreenshot()` helper to capture and attach screenshots to test reports:\n\n```typescript\nimport { captureDebugScreenshot, expect, test } from \"./fixtures/test-fixtures\";\n\ntest(\"my test\", async ({ appContext }) => {\n  const { page } = appContext;\n\n  // Capture screenshot at key points\n  await captureDebugScreenshot(page, \"before-action\");\n\n  // Perform action\n  await page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Delete\" }).click();\n\n  // Capture result\n  await captureDebugScreenshot(page, \"after-action\", { fullPage: true });\n});\n```\n\nScreenshots appear in the HTML report under the \"Attachments\" section.\n\n### Automatic Failure Screenshots\n\nThe `appContext` fixture **automatically captures a full-page screenshot** when tests fail. No manual action needed - just check the \"Attachments\" section in the HTML report after a test failure.\n\n## Core Infrastructure\n\n\n### Playwright Fixtures (Automatic Lifecycle)\n\nImport custom fixtures instead of base Playwright test:\n\n```typescript\nimport { expect, test } from \"./fixtures/test-fixtures\";\n```\n\n**Available fixtures:**\n- `appContext`: Tauri app with browser, page, and process handles (auto cleanup)\n- `fileTracker`: File tracker for temporary files (auto cleanup)\n\n**Benefits:**\n- No manual `beforeAll`/`afterAll` hooks\n- Automatic cleanup even on test failure\n- Type-safe fixture access\n\n### Test Utilities\n\n```typescript\nimport { createTmpFilePath, generateRunId, getTestDirname } from \"./fixtures/test-utils\";\n\n// Get __dirname\nconst __dirname = getTestDirname(import.meta.url);\n\n// Generate unique IDs\nconst runId = generateRunId();\nconst name = `Test Item ${runId}`;\n\n// Create temp files with auto-tracking\nconst filePath = createTmpFilePath(__dirname, \"backup.zip\", fileTracker);\n```\n\n### Standard Timeouts\n\n```typescript\nimport { TIMEOUTS } from \"./fixtures/constants\";\n\nawait expect(element).toBeVisible({ timeout: TIMEOUTS.medium });\n```\n\n| Constant | Value | Use Case |\n|----------|-------|----------|\n| `TIMEOUTS.short` | 5000ms | Quick UI updates |\n| `TIMEOUTS.medium` | 15000ms | Form submissions, navigation |\n| `TIMEOUTS.long` | 30000ms | App startup, complex operations |\n| `TIMEOUTS.batch` | 120000ms | Batch imports, file processing |\n\n## SpellbookApp Page Object\n\nAlways use the page object for common interactions:\n\n```typescript\nconst app = new SpellbookApp(page);\n\n// Navigation\nawait app.navigate(\"Library\" | \"Characters\" | \"Import\" | \"Add Spell\");\n\n// Spell management\nawait app.createSpell({ name, level, description, ... });\nawait app.openSpell(name);\nawait app.importFile(path, allowOverwrite?);\n\n// Character management\nawait app.createCharacter(name);\nawait app.selectCharacter(name);\nawait app.openCharacterEditor(name);\nawait app.addClass(className);\nawait app.addSpellToClass(className, spellName, \"KNOWN\" | \"PREPARED\");\n```\n\n## Dialog Handling\n\n### Custom Modals (React-based)\n\n```typescript\nimport { handleCustomModal } from \"./utils/dialog-handler\";\n\nawait page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Save\" }).click();\nawait handleCustomModal(page, \"OK\");\n\nawait page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Delete\" }).click();\nawait handleCustomModal(page, \"Confirm\");\n```\n\n### Native Browser Dialogs\n\n```typescript\nimport { setupDialogHandler } from \"./utils/dialog-handler\";\n\nconst cleanup = setupDialogHandler(page, {\n  acceptDelete: true,\n  dismissValidation: true,\n  debug: true,\n});\n\n// Trigger action that shows dialog\nawait page.getByRole(\"button\", { name: \"Reset\" }).click();\n\ncleanup(); // CRITICAL: Stop listening after action\n```\n\n## Test Organization\n\nUse `test.step()` for logical phases:\n\n```typescript\ntest(\"Feature Test\", async ({ appContext }) => {\n  await test.step(\"Setup: Create test data\", async () => {\n    // setup\n  });\n\n  await test.step(\"Action: Perform operation\", async () => {\n    // main test action\n  });\n\n  await test.step(\"Verify: Check results\", async () => {\n    // assertions\n  });\n});\n```\n\n## Locator Strategy\n\nUse the most user-facing, semantic locators available. Follow this priority hierarchy:\n\n| Priority | Locator Method | Use Case | Example |\n|----------|---------------|----------|---------|\n| **1** | `getByTestId()` | Interactive elements, dynamic content | `page.getByTestId(''save-button'')` |\n| **2** | `getByRole()` | Semantic HTML elements | `page.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''Save'' })` |\n| **3** | `getByLabel()` | Form fields with labels | `page.getByLabel(''Character Name'')` |\n| **4** | `getByPlaceholder()` | Inputs with placeholders | `page.getByPlaceholder(''Search spells...'')` |\n| **5** | `getByText()` | Static text content | `page.getByText(''Fireball'')` |\n| **6** | `locator()` with CSS | Last resort only | `page.locator(''.btn-primary'')` |\n\n### When New UI Elements Are Added\n\nBefore writing tests for new UI components:\n\n1. **Verify the element has a `data-testid`**:\n   ```typescript\n   const count = await page.getByTestId(''new-element-id'').count();\n   console.log(`Found ${count} elements`); // Should be 1\n   ```\n\n2. **If `data-testid` is missing**, check if semantic locators work:\n   ```typescript\n   await page.getByRole(''button'', { name: ''New Button'' }).click();\n   ```\n\n3. **If neither works**, request the UI developer add `data-testid` to the component (see `src/AGENTS.md` for guidelines).\n\n### Debugging Locators\n\nIf you can''t find an element:\n\n```typescript\n// List all available data-testid attributes\nconst testIds = await page.locator(''[data-testid]'').evaluateAll(\n  nodes => nodes.map(n => n.getAttribute(''data-testid''))\n);\nconsole.log(''Available testids:'', testIds);\n\n// Check if element exists anywhere\nconst exists = await page.locator(''text=My Element'').count();\nconsole.log(`Element exists: ${exists > 0}`);\n```\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### Creating Unique Test Data\n\n```typescript\nconst runId = generateRunId();\nconst spellName = `Test Spell ${runId}`;\nconst tmpFile = createTmpFilePath(__dirname, \"data.json\", fileTracker);\n```\n\n### Working with Temporary Files\n\n```typescript\ntest(\"backup flow\", async ({ fileTracker }) => {\n  const backupPath = createTmpFilePath(__dirname, \"backup.zip\", fileTracker);\n\n  // Use the file\n  fs.writeFileSync(backupPath, data);\n\n  // Cleanup is automatic!\n});\n```\n\n### Settlement Waits\n\nAfter navigation or complex UI switches:\n\n```typescript\nawait app.navigate(\"Library\");\nawait page.waitForTimeout(500); // Standard settlement wait\n```\n\n## Running Tests\n\n```powershell\n# Run all tests\nnpx playwright test\n\n# Run specific test file\nnpx playwright test vault.spec.ts\n\n# Run with UI mode\nnpx playwright test --ui\n\n# Show HTML report\nnpx playwright show-report\n```\n\n## Debugging Test Failures\n\nWhen tests fail, follow this systematic approach to gather useful debug information:\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **CDP Trace Limitation**: Playwright traces cannot capture screenshots when using CDP connections (required for Tauri). Use manual screenshot capture instead.\n\n### 1. Capture Screenshots Manually\n\nAdd screenshots at key points in your test to visualize what''s happening:\n\n```typescript\nimport { captureDebugScreenshot } from \"./fixtures/test-fixtures\";\n\n// Before the failing assertion\nawait captureDebugScreenshot(page, \"before-assertion\");\n\n// Then the assertion\nawait expect(element).toBeVisible();\n```\n\n**Automatic failure screenshots**: The `appContext` fixture automatically captures a full-page screenshot when tests fail. Check the \"Attachments\" section in the HTML report.\n\n### 2. View the HTML Report\n\n```powershell\nnpx playwright show-report\n```\n\nThe report provides:\n- Failed test details with stack traces\n- Screenshots at the point of failure\n- Full execution traces with DOM snapshots\n- Network activity and console logs\n\n### 2. Analyze the Trace\n\nIn the HTML report:\n1. Click on the failed test\n2. Select the **Trace** tab\n3. Review:\n   - **DOM snapshots** at each test step\n   - **Network requests** (look for failed API calls)\n   - **Console logs** (check for JavaScript errors)\n   - **The exact line** where the test failed\n\n### 3. Capture Debug Screenshots\n\nAdd a screenshot immediately before the failing assertion:\n\n```typescript\n// Add this before the assertion that''s failing\nawait page.screenshot({ path: ''tests/screenshots/debug.png'', fullPage: true });\n\n// Then the assertion\nawait expect(element).toBeVisible();\n```\n\nThe screenshot will be saved to `apps/desktop/tests/screenshots/debug.png`.\n\n### 4. Extract Error Context\n\nWhen reporting or analyzing failures, include:\n- **The assertion that failed** (exact line and message)\n- **DOM state** at failure (from trace or screenshot)\n- **Console errors** (check browser console in trace)\n- **Network failures** (failed requests in trace)\n- **Recent code changes** that might have affected the test\n\n### 5. Common Failure Patterns\n\n| Error Pattern | Likely Cause | Solution |\n|---------------|--------------|----------|\n| `Timeout: element not found` | Missing `data-testid` or element doesn''t exist | Check UI code, add `data-testid`, or use semantic locators |\n| `Strict mode violation` | Multiple elements match locator | Make locator more specific with filters |\n| `Navigation timeout` | App startup too slow or crashed | Check app logs, increase timeout, verify build |\n| `Database is locked` | Previous test didn''t clean up | Kill orphaned processes, check data isolation |\n\n### 6. Use Playwright Inspector\n\nFor interactive debugging:\n\n```powershell\nnpx playwright test --debug\n```\n\nThis opens the Playwright Inspector where you can:\n- Step through the test line-by-line\n- Inspect the DOM at each step\n- Try different locators interactively\n- See live screenshots\n\n### 7. Verify Element Exists\n\nBefore writing assertions, verify the element can be found:\n\n```typescript\n// Debug: Check element count\nconst count = await page.getByTestId(''new-element'').count();\nconsole.log(`Found ${count} elements with testid ''new-element''`);\n\n// Debug: List all testids\nconst allTestIds = await page.locator(''[data-testid]'').allTextContents();\nconsole.log(''Available testids:'', allTestIds);\n```\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Port Collisions\n\nTests use isolated ports per worker. If \"Address already in use\" errors occur:\n\n1. Ensure no other app instances are running\n2. Check for orphaned processes: `Get-Process | Where-Object {$_.ProcessName -match \"spellbook\"} | Stop-Process`\n\n### WebView2 State Pollution\n\nTests use isolated data directories. If state leaks between runs:\n\n- Check `tests/tmp/data-w*` directories\n- Cleanup happens automatically but may fail if processes don''t terminate cleanly\n\n### Blank Screen on Launch\n\nDebug builds expect Vite dev server at `http://127.0.0.1:5173`. The test infrastructure handles this automatically.\n\n## Advanced: Manual Lifecycle\n\nFor test suites sharing app state across multiple tests:\n\n```typescript\nimport { type TauriAppContext, cleanupTauriApp, createFileTracker, launchTauriApp } from \"./fixtures/tauri-fixture\";\n\nlet appContext: TauriAppContext | null = null;\nconst fileTracker = createFileTracker();\n\ntest.beforeAll(async () => {\n  appContext = await launchTauriApp();\n});\n\ntest.afterAll(async () => {\n  if (appContext) {\n    await cleanupTauriApp(appContext);\n  }\n  fileTracker.cleanup();\n});\n\ntest(\"my test\", async () => {\n  if (!appContext) throw new Error(\"App context not initialized\");\n  const { page } = appContext;\n  // test code\n});\n```\n\n**Use manual lifecycle when:**\n- Sharing app state across multiple tests\n- Running large test suites (minimize app launches)\n- Need fine-grained control over lifecycle\n\n## Key Constraints\n\n- **Windows only**: Tests require WebView2 (Windows-only)\n- **Workers**: Configured for `workers: 1` to avoid port collisions\n- **Timeout**: Default test timeout is 120000ms (2 minutes)\n- **Data isolation**: Each test run uses unique data directory\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:35:52.988Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Test Automation Agents requiring advanced End-to-End testing capabilities for desktop applications like Spellbook using Playwright","zh":"适用于需要为桌面应用程序（如使用Playwright的Spellbook）提供高级端到端测试功能的测试自动化代理的理想选择","ja":"Playwrightを使用したSpellbookのようなデスクトップアプリケーション向けの高度なエンドツーエンドテスト機能を必要とするテスト自動化エージェントに最適","ko":"Playwright를 사용하는 Spellbookのような 데스크탑 애플리케이션을 위한 고급 엔드 투 엔드 테스트 기능을 필요로 하는 테스트 자동화 에이전트에게 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de automatización de pruebas que requieren capacidades de prueba de extremo a extremo avanzadas para aplicaciones de escritorio como Spellbook utilizando Playwright","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''automatisation de tests nécessitant des capacités de test de bout en bout avancées pour des applications de bureau comme Spellbook en utilisant Playwright","de":"Ideal für Testautomatisierungsagenten, die erweiterte End-to-End-Testfunktionen für Desktop-Anwendungen wie Spellbook mit Playwright benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Automação de Testes que exigem capacidades de teste de ponta a ponta avançadas para aplicações de desktop como Spellbook usando Playwright","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автоматизации тестирования, требующих расширенных возможностей тестирования от начала до конца для настольных приложений, таких как Spellbook, с использованием Playwright","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء اختبار التطبيق الآلي الذين يتطلبون إمكانيات اختبار من النهاية إلى النهاية متقدمة للتطبيقات المكتبية مثل Spellbook باستخدام Playwright"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write and migrate E2E tests for the Spellbook Tauri desktop application using custom fixtures and utilities with Playwright, streamlining test infrastructure updates and leveraging step-by-step migration checklists and before/after examples","zh":"赋予代理编写和迁移Spellbook Tauri桌面应用程序的端到端测试的能力，使用自定义的固定装置和工具与Playwright，简化测试基础设施更新，并利用步骤式迁移检查清单和前后示例","ja":"Playwrightとカスタムフィクスチャおよびユーティリティを使用して、Spellbook Tauriデスクトップアプリケーションのエンドツーエンドテストを書き込み、移行するエージェントの能力を提供し、テストインフラストラクチャの更新を簡素化し、ステップバイステップの移行チェックリストおよび前後例を利用","ko":"Playwright와 사용자 정의된 고정 장치 및 유틸리티를 사용하여 Spellbook Tauri 데스크탑 애플리케이션의 엔드 투 엔드 테스트를 작성하고 이전하는 에이전트의 능력을 제공하며, 테스트 인프라의 업데이트를 간소화하고, 단계별 이전 체크리스트 및 이전/이후 예제를 활용","es":"Permite a los agentes escribir y migrar pruebas de extremo a extremo para la aplicación de escritorio Spellbook Tauri utilizando fixtures y utilidades personalizadas con Playwright, simplificando las actualizaciones de la infraestructura de pruebas y aprovechando listas de verificación de migración paso a paso y ejemplos antes y después","fr":"Permet aux agents d''écrire et de migrer des tests de bout en bout pour l''application de bureau Spellbook Tauri en utilisant des fixtures et des utilités personnalisées avec Playwright, simplifiant les mises à jour de l''infrastructure de test et exploitant des listes de vérification de migration étape par étape et des exemples avant et après","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, End-to-End-Tests für die Spellbook-Tauri-Desktop-Anwendung mit benutzerdefinierten Fixtures und Utilities mit Playwright zu schreiben und zu migrieren, wodurch die Aktualisierung der Testinfrastruktur vereinfacht und die Schritt-für-Schritt-Migrationsprüflisten und Beispiele vor und nach der Migration genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a escrever e migrar testes de ponta a ponta para o aplicativo de desktop Spellbook Tauri usando fixtures e utilitários personalizados com Playwright, simplificando atualizações de infraestrutura de teste e utilizando listas de verificação de migração passo a passo e exemplos antes e depois","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью писать и переносить тесты от начала до конца для настольного приложения Spellbook Tauri, используя пользовательские фикстуры и утилиты с Playwright, упрощая обновления тестовой инфраструктуры и используя пошаговые списки проверки миграции и примеры до и после","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من كتابة وتنقل الاختبارات من النهاية إلى النهاية لتطبيق Spellbook Tauri المكتبية باستخدام إصلاحات وبرامج مساعدة مخصصة مع Playwright، وبذلك يُبسط تحديثات بنية الاختبار ويتوفر قائمة تدقيق هجرة خطوة بخطوة وأمثلة قبل وبعد"},"useCases":{"en":["Migrating existing tests to modern infrastructure","Writing E2E tests for Spellbook with custom fixtures","Debugging test failures using Playwright utilities"],"zh":["将现有测试迁移到现代基础设施","使用自定义固定装置为Spellbook编写端到端测试","使用Playwright工具调试测试失败"],"ja":["既存のテストを最新のインフラストラクチャに移行","カスタムフィクスチャを使用してSpellbookのエンドツーエンドテストを書き込む","Playwrightユーティリティを使用してテストの失敗をデバッグ"],"ko":["기존 테스트를 현대적인 인프라로 이전","사용자 정의된 고정 장치를 사용하여 Spellbook의 엔드 투 엔드 테스트를 작성","Playwright 유틸리티를 사용하여 테스트 실패를 디버깅"],"es":["Migrar pruebas existentes a infraestructura moderna","Escribir pruebas de extremo a extremo para Spellbook con fixtures personalizadas","Depurar fallos de pruebas utilizando utilidades de Playwright"],"fr":["Migrer des tests existants vers une infrastructure moderne","Écrire des tests de bout en bout pour Spellbook avec des fixtures personnalisées","Déboguer les défaillances de test en utilisant les utilités de Playwright"],"de":["Vorhandene Tests auf moderne Infrastruktur migrieren","End-to-End-Tests für Spellbook mit benutzerdefinierten Fixtures schreiben","Testfehler mit Playwright-Utilities debuggen"],"pt":["Migrar testes existentes para infraestrutura moderna","Escrever testes de ponta a ponta para Spellbook com fixtures personalizados","Depurar falhas de teste usando utilitários Playwright"],"ru":["Перенос существующих тестов на современную инфраструктуру","Написание тестов от начала до конца для Spellbook с пользовательскими фикстурами","Отладка сбоев тестирования с помощью утилит Playwright"],"ar":["نقل الاختبارات الحالية إلى بنية حديثة","كتابة اختبارات من النهاية إلى النهاية لبرنامج Spellbook مع إصلاحات مخصصة","تصحيح أعطال الاختبار باستخدام أدوات Playwright"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Playwright installation","Spellbook Tauri desktop application specific","Custom fixtures and utilities required for optimal use"],"zh":["需要Playwright安装","特定于Spellbook Tauri桌面应用程序","需要自定义固定装置和工具以实现最佳使用"],"ja":["Playwrightのインストールが必要","Spellbook Tauriデスクトップアプリケーションに特有","カスタムフィクスチャおよびユーティリティが最適な使用のために必要"],"ko":["Playwright 설치가 필요","Spellbook Tauri 데스크탑 애플리케이션에 특화","사용자 정의된 고정 장치 및 유틸리티가 최적의 사용을 위해 필요"],"es":["Requiere instalación de Playwright","Específico de la aplicación de escritorio Spellbook Tauri","Se requieren fixtures y utilidades personalizadas para un uso óptimo"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation de Playwright","Spécifique à l''application de bureau Spellbook Tauri","Des fixtures et des utilités personnalisées sont requises pour une utilisation optimale"],"de":["Benötigt Playwright-Installation","Spezifisch für die Spellbook-Tauri-Desktop-Anwendung","Benutzerdefinierte Fixtures und Utilities erforderlich für optimalen Einsatz"],"pt":["Exige instalação do Playwright","Especificamente para aplicativo de desktop Spellbook Tauri","Exige fixtures e utilitários personalizados para uso ótimo"],"ru":["Требует установки Playwright","Конкретно для настольного приложения Spellbook Tauri","Требует пользовательских фикстур и утилит для оптимального использования"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت Playwright","نظام مکتبي Spellbook Tauri محدد","يتطلب إصلاحات وبرامج مساعدة مخصصة للاستخدام الأمثل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('willyu1007/Skill_Template_Module/project-sync-lint', 'community', 'willyu1007', 'Skill_Template_Module', 'willyu1007/Skill_Template_Module', 'project-sync-lint', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.468Z', '2026-02-18T08:35:58.118Z', NULL, '{"id":"willyu1007/Skill_Template_Module/project-sync-lint","name":"project-sync-lint","description":{"zh":"project-sync-lint是一个基于模块化方法的技能模板，具有基本版本的功能，并默认启用大多数插件","ja":"project-sync-lintはモジュラーなアプローチに基づくスキルテンプレートであり、基本的なバージョンの機能を備え、多くのプラグインをデフォルトで有効にします","ko":"project-sync-lint는 모듈화된 접근 방식에 기반한 스킬 템플릿으로, 기본 버전의 기능을 가지고 있으며 대부분의 플러그인을 기본적으로 활성화합니다","es":"Project Sync Lint es una herramienta de sincronización de proyectos basada en un enfoque modular con funcionalidad básica completa","fr":"Project Sync Lint est un outil de synchronisation de projets basé sur une approche modulaire avec une fonctionnalité de base complète","de":"Project Sync Lint ist ein Projekt-Synchronisierungstool basierend auf einem modularen Ansatz mit vollständiger Basisfunktionalität","pt":"O project-sync-lint é uma habilidade de sincronização de projetos que oferece funcionalidades básicas e permite a ativação de add-ons por padrão.","ru":"Project-sync-lint — это навык синхронизации проектов, который обеспечивает базовые функции и позволяет активировать дополнения по умолчанию.","ar":"project-sync-lint هي مهارة مزامنة المشاريع التي توفر وظائف أساسية وتسمح بتفعيل الإضافات افتراضيًا.","en":"Skill template based on a modular approach, has complete basic version functionality and enables most add-ons by default."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"项目同步检查模板 - project-sync-lint","ja":"プロジェクト同期Lintテンプレート - project-sync-lint","ko":"프로젝트 동기화 린트 템플릿 - project-sync-lint","es":"Project Sync Lint: Herramienta de sincronización de proye...","fr":"Project Sync Lint : Outil de synchronisation de projets","de":"Project Sync Lint: Proj