Git"],"ar":["إلغاء المسارات الكاملة","إلغاء المراحل المحددة","إلغاء المهام الفردية","تحقق ما قبل الطيران من Conductor","تحقق من مستودع Git"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Git 逻辑工作单元还原","Revert 功能","Conductor 初始化","跟踪还原","阶段还原","任务还原","Git 感知"],"ja":["Git 論理ワークユニットの復元","Revert 機能","Conductor 初期化","トラックの還元","フェーズの還元","タスクの還元","Git 感知"],"ko":["Git 논리 작업 단위 되돌리기","Revert 기능","Conductor 초기화","추적 되돌리기","단계 되돌리기","작업 되돌리기","Git 인식"],"es":["revertir cambios","conciencia de Git","unidad de trabajo lógica","reversión de pistas","reversión de fases","reversión de tareas","desarrollo de software","control de versiones"],"fr":["annuler des modifications","conscience Git","unité de travail logique","annulation de pistes","annulation de phases","annulation de tâches","développement de logiciels","contrôle de version"],"de":["änderungen rückgängig machen","Git-Bewusstsein","logische ArbeitsEinheit","Rückgängig-Machen von Tracks","Rückgängig-Machen von Phasen","Rückgängig-Machen von Aufgaben","Software-Entwicklung","Versionskontrolle"],"pt":["reverter alterações","conhecimento Git","unidade de trabalho lógica","faixas","fases","tarefas","Conductor","repositório Git"],"ru":["отмена изменений","осведомленность о Git","логическая единица работы","треки","фазы","задачи","Conductor","репозиторий Git"],"ar":["إلغاء التغييرات","إدراك Git","وحدة عمل منطقية","مسارات","مراحل","مهام","Conductor","مستودع Git"]}},"owner":"itsimonfredlingjack","repo":"codex-dev-plugin","repoPath":"itsimonfredlingjack/codex-dev-plugin","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.468Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"revert","description":"Git-aware undo by logical work unit (track, phase, or task)","bodyPreview":"---\ndescription: \"Git-aware undo by logical work unit (track, phase, or task)\"\nargument-hint: \"[track-id | track-id:phase | track-id:task]\"\n---\n\n# Revert Track\n\nRevert changes by logical work unit with full git awareness. Supports reverting entire tracks, specific phases, or individual tasks.\n\n## Pre-flight Checks\n\n1. Verify Conductor is initialized:\n   - Check `conductor/tracks.md` exists\n   - If missing: Display error and suggest running `/conductor:setup` first\n\n2. Verify git repository:\n   -","body":"---\ndescription: \"Git-aware undo by logical work unit (track, phase, or task)\"\nargument-hint: \"[track-id | track-id:phase | track-id:task]\"\n---\n\n# Revert Track\n\nRevert changes by logical work unit with full git awareness. Supports reverting entire tracks, specific phases, or individual tasks.\n\n## Pre-flight Checks\n\n1. Verify Conductor is initialized:\n   - Check `conductor/tracks.md` exists\n   - If missing: Display error and suggest running `/conductor:setup` first\n\n2. Verify git repository:\n   - Run `git status` to confirm git repo\n   - Check for uncommitted changes\n   - If uncommitted changes exist:\n\n     ```\n     WARNING: Uncommitted changes detected\n\n     Files with changes:\n     {list of files}\n\n     Options:\n     1. Stash changes and continue\n     2. Commit changes first\n     3. Cancel revert\n     ```\n\n3. Verify git is clean enough to revert:\n   - No merge in progress\n   - No rebase in progress\n   - If issues found: Halt and explain resolution steps\n\n## Target Selection\n\n### If argument provided:\n\nParse the argument format:\n\n**Full track:** `{trackId}`\n\n- Example: `auth_20250115`\n- Reverts all commits for the entire track\n\n**Specific phase:** `{trackId}:phase{N}`\n\n- Example: `auth_20250115:phase2`\n- Reverts commits for phase N and all subsequent phases\n\n**Specific task:** `{trackId}:task{X.Y}`\n\n- Example: `auth_20250115:task2.3`\n- Reverts commits for task X.Y only\n\n### If no argument:\n\nDisplay guided selection menu:\n\n```\nWhat would you like to revert?\n\nCurrently In Progress:\n1. [~] Task 2.3 in dashboard_20250112 (most recent)\n\nRecently Completed:\n2. [x] Task 2.2 in dashboard_20250112 (1 hour ago)\n3. [x] Phase 1 in dashboard_20250112 (3 hours ago)\n4. [x] Full track: auth_20250115 (yesterday)\n\nOptions:\n5. Enter specific reference (track:phase or track:task)\n6. Cancel\n\nSelect option:\n```\n\n## Commit Discovery\n\n### For Task Revert\n\n1. Search git log for task-specific commits:\n\n   ```bash\n   git log --oneline --grep=\"{trackId}\" --grep=\"Task {X.Y}\" --all-match\n   ```\n\n2. Also find the plan.md update commit:\n\n   ```bash\n   git log --oneline --grep=\"mark task {X.Y} complete\" --grep=\"{trackId}\" --all-match\n   ```\n\n3. Collect all matching commit SHAs\n\n### For Phase Revert\n\n1. Determine task range for the phase by reading plan.md\n2. Search for all task commits in that phase:\n\n   ```bash\n   git log --oneline --grep=\"{trackId}\" | grep -E \"Task {N}\\.[0-9]\"\n   ```\n\n3. Find phase verification commit if exists\n4. Find all plan.md update commits for phase tasks\n5. Collect all matching commit SHAs in chronological order\n\n### For Full Track Revert\n\n1. Find ALL commits mentioning the track:\n\n   ```bash\n   git log --oneline --grep=\"{trackId}\"\n   ```\n\n2. Find track creation commits:\n\n   ```bash\n   git log --oneline -- \"conductor/tracks/{trackId}/\"\n   ```\n\n3. Collect all matching commit SHAs in chronological order\n\n## Execution Plan Display\n\nBefore any revert operations, display full plan:\n\n```\n================================================================================\n                           REVERT EXECUTION PLAN\n================================================================================\n\nTarget: {description of what''s being reverted}\n\nCommits to revert (in reverse chronological order):\n  1. abc1234 - feat: add chart rendering (dashboard_20250112)\n  2. def5678 - chore: mark task 2.3 complete (dashboard_20250112)\n  3. ghi9012 - feat: add data hooks (dashboard_20250112)\n  4. jkl3456 - chore: mark task 2.2 complete (dashboard_20250112)\n\nFiles that will be affected:\n  - src/components/Dashboard.tsx (modified)\n  - src/hooks/useData.ts (will be deleted - was created in these commits)\n  - conductor/tracks/dashboard_20250112/plan.md (modified)\n\nPlan updates:\n  - Task 2.2: [x] -> [ ]\n  - Task 2.3: [~] -> [ ]\n\n================================================================================\n                              !! WARNING !!\n================================================================================\n\nThis operation will:\n- Create {N} revert commits\n- Modify {M} files\n- Reset {P} tasks to pending status\n\nThis CANNOT be easily undone without manual intervention.\n\n================================================================================\n\nType ''YES'' to proceed, or anything else to cancel:\n```\n\n**CRITICAL: Require explicit ''YES'' confirmation. Do not proceed on ''y'', ''yes'', or enter.**\n\n## Revert Execution\n\nExecute reverts in reverse chronological order (newest first):\n\n```\nExecuting revert plan...\n\n[1/4] Reverting abc1234...\n      git revert --no-edit abc1234\n      ✓ Success\n\n[2/4] Reverting def5678...\n      git revert --no-edit def5678\n      ✓ Success\n\n[3/4] Reverting ghi9012...\n      git revert --no-edit ghi9012\n      ✓ Success\n\n[4/4] Reverting jkl3456...\n      git revert --no-edit jkl3456\n      ✓ Success\n```\n\n### On Merge Conflict\n\nIf any revert produces a merge conflict:\n\n```\n================================================================================\n                           MERGE CONFLICT DETECTED\n================================================================================\n\nConflict occurred while reverting: {sha} - {message}\n\nConflicted files:\n  - src/components/Dashboard.tsx\n\nOptions:\n1. Show conflict details\n2. Abort revert sequence (keeps completed reverts)\n3. Open manual resolution guide\n\nIMPORTANT: Reverts 1-{N} have been completed. You may need to manually\nresolve this conflict before continuing or fully undo the revert sequence.\n\nSelect option:\n```\n\n**HALT immediately on any conflict. Do not attempt automatic resolution.**\n\n## Plan.md Updates\n\nAfter successful git reverts, update plan.md:\n\n1. Read current plan.md\n2. For each reverted task, change marker:\n   - `[x]` -> `[ ]`\n   - `[~]` -> `[ ]`\n3. Write updated plan.md\n4. Update metadata.json:\n   - Decrement `tasks.completed`\n   - Update `status` if needed\n   - Update `updated` timestamp\n\n**Do NOT commit plan.md changes** - they are part of the revert operation\n\n## Track Status Updates\n\n### If reverting entire track:\n\n- In tracks.md: Change `[x]` or `[~]` to `[ ]`\n- Consider offering to delete the track directory entirely\n\n### If reverting to incomplete state:\n\n- In tracks.md: Ensure marked as `[~]` if partially complete, `[ ]` if fully reverted\n\n## Verification\n\nAfter revert completion:\n\n```\n================================================================================\n                           REVERT COMPLETE\n================================================================================\n\nSummary:\n  - Reverted {N} commits\n  - Reset {P} tasks to pending\n  - {M} files affected\n\nGit log now shows:\n  {recent commit history}\n\nPlan.md status:\n  - Task 2.2: [ ] Pending\n  - Task 2.3: [ ] Pending\n\n================================================================================\n\nVerify the revert was successful:\n  1. Run tests: {test command}\n  2. Check application: {relevant check}\n\nIf issues are found, you may need to:\n  - Fix conflicts manually\n  - Re-implement the reverted tasks\n  - Use ''git revert HEAD~{N}..HEAD'' to undo the reverts\n\n================================================================================\n```\n\n## Safety Rules\n\n1. **NEVER use `git reset --hard`** - Only use `git revert`\n2. **NEVER use `git push --force`** - Only safe push operations\n3. **NEVER auto-resolve conflicts** - Always halt for human intervention\n4. **ALWAYS show full plan** - User must see exactly what will happen\n5. **REQUIRE explicit ''YES''** - Not ''y'', not enter, only ''YES''\n6. **HALT on ANY error** - Do not attempt to continue past failures\n7. **PRESERVE history** - Revert commits are preferred over history rewriting\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n### Track Never Committed\n\n```\nNo commits found for track: {trackId}\n\nThe track exists but has no associated commits. This may mean:\n- Implementation never started\n- Commits used different format\n\nOptions:\n1. Delete track directory only\n2. Cancel\n```\n\n### Commits Already Reverted\n\n```\nSome commits appear to already be reverted:\n  - abc1234 was reverted by xyz9876\n\nOptions:\n1. Skip already-reverted commits\n2. Cancel and investigate\n```\n\n### Remote Already Pushed\n\n```\nWARNING: Some commits have been pushed to remote\n\nCommits on remote:\n  - abc1234 (origin/main)\n  - def5678 (origin/main)\n\nReverting will create new revert commits that you''ll need to push.\nThis is the safe approach (no force push required).\n\nContinue with revert? (YES/no):\n```\n\n## Undo the Revert\n\nIf user needs to undo the revert itself:\n\n```\nTo undo this revert operation:\n\n  git revert HEAD~{N}..HEAD\n\nThis will create new commits that restore the reverted changes.\n\nAlternatively, if not yet pushed:\n  git reset --soft HEAD~{N}\n  git checkout -- .\n\n(Use with caution - this discards the revert commits)\n```\n## Output Format\n\n```xml\n<result>\n  <analysis>Brief analysis</analysis>\n  <solution>Implementation</solution>\n  <considerations>Trade-offs and notes</considerations>\n</result>\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:36:42.238Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing Git-aware undo capabilities for tracks, phases, or tasks","zh":"非常适合需要 Git 感知撤消功能的开发代理，适用于跟踪、阶段或任务","ja":"Git に対応したトラック、フェーズ、またはタスクのためのUndo機能を必要とする開発エージェントに最適","ko":"Git 인식 취소 기능이 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합하며 트랙, 단계 또는 작업에 사용할 수 있습니다","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan capacidades de deshacer conscientes de Git para pistas, fases o tareas","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin de capacités d''annulation conscientes de Git pour les pistes, les phases ou les tâches","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die Git-bewusste Undo-Funktionen für Tracks, Phasen oder Aufgaben benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de capacidades de desfazer cientes do Git para faixas, fases ou tarefas","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым требуются возможности отмены, осведомленные о Git, для треков, фаз или задач","ar":"مثالي ل와كلاء التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى возможности إلغاء تمكين Git لتحديد المسارات أو المراحل أو المهام"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to revert changes by logical work unit with full Git awareness, supporting reverting entire tracks, specific phases, or individual tasks using track-id, track-id:phase, or track-id:task arguments","zh":"赋予代理以逻辑工作单元撤消更改的能力，具有完全的 Git 感知，支持撤消整个跟踪、特定阶段或单个任务，使用 track-id、track-id:phase 或 track-id:task 参数","ja":"エージェントに論理的な作業単位で変更を元に戻す能力を付与し、完全なGit認識をサポートし、トラックID、トラックID:フェーズ、またはトラックID:タスクの引数を使用して、トラック全体、特定のフェーズ、または個々のタスクを元に戻します","ko":"에이전트에게 논리적인 작업 단위로 변경을 되돌릴 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, 전체 Git 인식을 지원하여 트랙 ID, 트랙 ID: 단계 또는 트랙 ID: 작업 인수를 사용하여 전체 트랙, 특정 단계 또는 개별 작업을 되돌릴 수 있습니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a revertir cambios por unidad de trabajo lógica con plena conciencia de Git, lo que admite la reversión de pistas completas, fases específicas o tareas individuales utilizando argumentos de track-id, track-id:phase o track-id:task","fr":"Autonomise les agents pour annuler les modifications par unité de travail logique avec une pleine conscience de Git, ce qui prend en charge l''annulation de pistes entières, de phases spécifiques ou de tâches individuelles à l''aide d''arguments track-id, track-id:phase ou track-id:task","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Änderungen durch logische Arbeitseinheiten mit voller Git-Kenntnis rückgängig zu machen, was das Rückgängig machen ganzer Tracks, spezifischer Phasen oder einzelner Aufgaben unter Verwendung von track-id-, track-id:phase- oder track-id:task-Argumenten unterstützt","pt":"Habilita os agentes a reverter alterações por unidade lógica de trabalho com total conscientização do Git, suportando reverter faixas inteiras, fases específicas ou tarefas individuais usando argumentos de track-id, track-id: fase ou track-id: tarefa","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью отменить изменения по логической единице работы с полной осведомленностью о Git, поддерживая отмену целых треков, конкретных фаз или отдельных задач с использованием аргументов track-id, track-id: фаза или track-id: задача","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من إعادة التغييرات بواسطة وحدة عمل منطقية مع إدراك كامل ل Git ، تدعم إعادة التغييرات المسارات الكاملة أو المراحل المحددة أو المهام الفردية باستخدام حجج track-id ، track-id: phase أو track-id: task"},"useCases":{"en":["Reverting entire tracks to previous states","Undoing changes in specific phases of a project","Canceling individual tasks within a track"],"zh":["将整个跟踪恢复到以前的状态","撤消项目特定阶段中的更改","取消跟踪内的单个任务"],"ja":["トラック全体を以前の状態に戻す","プロジェクトの特定のフェーズでの変更を元に戻す","トラック内の個々のタスクをキャンセルする"],"ko":["전체 트랙을 이전 상태로 되돌리기","프로젝트의 특정 단계에서 변경을 취소하기","트랙 내의 개별 작업을 취소하기"],"es":["Revertir pistas completas a estados anteriores","Deshacer cambios en fases específicas de un proyecto","Cancelar tareas individuales dentro de una pista"],"fr":["Rétablir des pistes entières à des états antérieurs","Annuler les modifications dans des phases spécifiques d''un projet","Annuler des tâches individuelles au sein d''une piste"],"de":["Ganze Tracks auf vorherige Zustände zurücksetzen","Änderungen in bestimmten Phasen eines Projekts rückgängig machen","Einzelne Aufgaben innerhalb eines Tracks abbrechen"],"pt":["Reverter faixas inteiras para estados anteriores","Desfazer alterações em fases específicas de um projeto","Cancelar tarefas individuais dentro de uma faixa"],"ru":["Отмена целых треков до предыдущих состояний","Отмена изменений в конкретных фазах проекта","Отмена отдельных задач внутри трека"],"ar":["إعادة المسارات الكاملة إلى الحالات السابقة","إلغاء التغييرات في مراحل معينة من المشروع","إلغاء المهام الفردية داخل المسار"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Conductor initialization with conductor/tracks.md","Needs a verified Git repository"],"zh":["需要使用 conductor/tracks.md 初始化 Conductor","需要验证的 Git 仓库"],"ja":["conductor/tracks.md で Conductor を初期化する必要があります","検証された Git リポジトリが必要です"],"ko":["conductor/tracks.md를 사용하여 Conductor를 초기화해야 함","검증된 Git 저장소가 필요함"],"es":["Requiere la inicialización del Conductor con conductor/tracks.md","Necesita un repositorio Git verificado"],"fr":["Nécessite l''initialisation du Conductor avec conductor/tracks.md","Nécessite un référentiel Git vérifié"],"de":["Erfordert die Initialisierung des Conductors mit conductor/tracks.md","Benötigt ein verifiziertes Git-Repository"],"pt":["Requer inicialização do Conductor com conductor/tracks.md","Necessita de um repositório Git verificado"],"ru":["Требует инициализации Conductor с conductor/tracks.md","Требует проверенного репозитория Git"],"ar":["يتطلب تهيئة Conductor مع conductor/tracks.md","يحتاج إلى مستودع Git تم التحقق منه"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Sologa/codex-pipeline/anndata', 'community', 'Sologa', 'codex-pipeline', 'Sologa/codex-pipeline', 'anndata', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z', '2026-02-18T08:36:41.249Z', NULL, '{"id":"Sologa/codex-pipeline/anndata","name":"anndata","description":{"zh":"AnnData是一个Python包，用于处理注释数据矩阵，能够高效存储、操作和分析实验测量数据和元数据","ja":"AnnDataは注釈付きデータマトリックスを処理するためのPythonパッケージであり、実験測定データとメタデータを効率的にストレージ、操作、分析できる","ko":"AnnData는 주석 데이터 행렬을 처리하는 Python 패키지로 효율적으로 실험 측정 데이터와 메타데이터를 저장, 조작, 분석할 수 있다","es":"AnnData es un paquete de Python para el manejo de matrices de datos anotados, ideal para el análisis de datos de genómica de células individuales y otros datos anotados","fr":"AnnData est un package Python pour la manipulation de matrices de données annotées, conçu pour l''analyse de données de génomique à cellule unique et d''autres données annotées","de":"AnnData ist ein Python-Paket für die Verwaltung von annotierten Datenmatrizen, geeignet für die Analyse von Daten der Einzelzellegenomik und anderen annotierten Daten","pt":"Anndata é uma biblioteca Python para manipulação de matrizes de dados anotados, projetada para análise de genômica de célula única.","ru":"Anndata - это библиотека Python для работы с аннотированными матрицами данных, предназначенная для анализа геномики отдельных клеток.","ar":"Anndata هي مكتبة بايثون لمعالجة مصفوفات البيانات المُحَدّدة، مصممة للتحليل الجينومي لخلايا واحدة.","en":"研究 codex 使用 skill 生成 survey 這件事"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"AnnData技能：高效处理注释数据矩阵","ja":"AnnDataスキル：注釈付きデータマトリックスの効率的な処理","ko":"AnnData 스킬: 효율적인 주석 데이터 행렬 처리","es":"AnnData: Análisis de Datos Anotados","fr":"AnnData: Analyse de Données Annotées","de":"AnnData: Analyse von Annotierten Daten","pt":"Anndata: Trabalhando com Matrizes de Dados Anotados","ru":"Anndata: Работа с аннотированными матрицами данных","ar":"Anndata: معالجة مصفوفا