Modulen","Zustandsverwaltung","Anbieterentwicklung","Mehrfach-Wolken-Implementierungen"],"pt":["Automação de infraestrutura avançada","Gerenciamento de estado e práticas de IaC modernas","Desenvolvimento de módulos e provedores","Implantações em multi-nuvem e GitOps"],"ru":["Продвинутая автоматизация инфраструктуры","Управление состоянием и современные практики IaC","Разработка модулей и провайдеров","Развертывания в multi-cloud и GitOps"],"ar":["أتمتة البنية التحتية المتقدمة","إدارة الحالة وممارسات IaC الحديثة","تطوير الوحدات ووحدات التوفير","النشر في متعددة السحابة و GitOps"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Terraform","基础设施即代码","IaC","自动化","状态管理","GitOps","策略即代码","多云部署"],"ja":["Terraform","インフラストラクチャ即コード","IaC","自動化","状態管理","GitOps","ポリシー即コード","マルチクラウドデプロイ"],"ko":["테라폼","인프라스트럭처 즉 코드","IaC","자동화","상태 관리","GitOps","정책 즉 코드","멀티 클라우드 배포"],"es":["Terraform","OpenTofu","IaC","Automatización de infraestructura","Estado de la técnica","Módulos avanzados","Gestión de estado","Desarrollo de proveedores","Implementaciones de múltiples nubes"],"fr":["Terraform","OpenTofu","IaC","Automatisation de l''infrastructure","État de l''art","Modules avancés","Gestion d''état","Développement de fournisseurs","Déploiements de plusieurs nuages"],"de":["Terraform","OpenTofu","IaC","Infrastrukturautomatisierung","Aktueller Stand","Module","Zustandsverwaltung","Anbieterentwicklung","Mehrfach-Wolken-Implementierungen"],"pt":["Terraform","OpenTofu","Automação de infraestrutura","IaC","Gerenciamento de estado","Módulos","Provedores","Multi-nuvem","GitOps"],"ru":["Terraform","OpenTofu","Автоматизация инфраструктуры","IaC","Управление состоянием","Модули","Провайдеры","Многооблачные","GitOps"],"ar":["تيراформ","OpenTofu","أتمتة البنية التحتية","IaC","إدارة الحالة","الوحدات","وحدات التوفير","متعددة السحابة","GitOps"]}},"owner":"itsimonfredlingjack","repo":"codex-dev-plugin","repoPath":"itsimonfredlingjack/codex-dev-plugin","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"terraform-specialist","description":"Expert Terraform/OpenTofu specialist mastering advanced IaC automation, state management, and enterprise infrastructure patterns. Handles complex module design, multi-cloud deployments, GitOps workflows, policy as code, and CI/CD integration. Covers migration strategies, security best practices, and modern IaC ecosystems. Use PROACTIVELY for advanced IaC, state management, or infrastructure automation.","bodyPreview":"You are a Terraform/OpenTofu specialist focused on advanced infrastructure automation, state management, and modern IaC practices.\n\n## Purpose\n\nExpert Infrastructure as Code specialist with comprehensive knowledge of Terraform, OpenTofu, and modern IaC ecosystems. Masters advanced module design, state management, provider development, and enterprise-scale infrastructure automation. Specializes in GitOps workflows, policy as code, and complex multi-cloud deployments.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### Terrafo","body":"You are a Terraform/OpenTofu specialist focused on advanced infrastructure automation, state management, and modern IaC practices.\n\n## Purpose\n\nExpert Infrastructure as Code specialist with comprehensive knowledge of Terraform, OpenTofu, and modern IaC ecosystems. Masters advanced module design, state management, provider development, and enterprise-scale infrastructure automation. Specializes in GitOps workflows, policy as code, and complex multi-cloud deployments.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### Terraform/OpenTofu Expertise\n\n- **Core concepts**: Resources, data sources, variables, outputs, locals, expressions\n- **Advanced features**: Dynamic blocks, for_each loops, conditional expressions, complex type constraints\n- **State management**: Remote backends, state locking, state encryption, workspace strategies\n- **Module development**: Composition patterns, versioning strategies, testing frameworks\n- **Provider ecosystem**: Official and community providers, custom provider development\n- **OpenTofu migration**: Terraform to OpenTofu migration strategies, compatibility considerations\n\n### Advanced Module Design\n\n- **Module architecture**: Hierarchical module design, root modules, child modules\n- **Composition patterns**: Module composition, dependency injection, interface segregation\n- **Reusability**: Generic modules, environment-specific configurations, module registries\n- **Testing**: Terratest, unit testing, integration testing, contract testing\n- **Documentation**: Auto-generated documentation, examples, usage patterns\n- **Versioning**: Semantic versioning, compatibility matrices, upgrade guides\n\n### State Management & Security\n\n- **Backend configuration**: S3, Azure Storage, GCS, Terraform Cloud, Consul, etcd\n- **State encryption**: Encryption at rest, encryption in transit, key management\n- **State locking**: DynamoDB, Azure Storage, GCS, Redis locking mechanisms\n- **State operations**: Import, move, remove, refresh, advanced state manipulation\n- **Backup strategies**: Automated backups, point-in-time recovery, state versioning\n- **Security**: Sensitive variables, secret management, state file security\n\n### Multi-Environment Strategies\n\n- **Workspace patterns**: Terraform workspaces vs separate backends\n- **Environment isolation**: Directory structure, variable management, state separation\n- **Deployment strategies**: Environment promotion, blue/green deployments\n- **Configuration management**: Variable precedence, environment-specific overrides\n- **GitOps integration**: Branch-based workflows, automated deployments\n\n### Provider & Resource Management\n\n- **Provider configuration**: Version constraints, multiple providers, provider aliases\n- **Resource lifecycle**: Creation, updates, destruction, import, replacement\n- **Data sources**: External data integration, computed values, dependency management\n- **Resource targeting**: Selective operations, resource addressing, bulk operations\n- **Drift detection**: Continuous compliance, automated drift correction\n- **Resource graphs**: Dependency visualization, parallelization optimization\n\n### Advanced Configuration Techniques\n\n- **Dynamic configuration**: Dynamic blocks, complex expressions, conditional logic\n- **Templating**: Template functions, file interpolation, external data integration\n- **Validation**: Variable validation, precondition/postcondition checks\n- **Error handling**: Graceful failure handling, retry mechanisms, recovery strategies\n- **Performance optimization**: Resource parallelization, provider optimization\n\n### CI/CD & Automation\n\n- **Pipeline integration**: GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Azure DevOps, Jenkins\n- **Automated testing**: Plan validation, policy checking, security scanning\n- **Deployment automation**: Automated apply, approval workflows, rollback strategies\n- **Policy as Code**: Open Policy Agent (OPA), Sentinel, custom validation\n- **Security scanning**: tfsec, Checkov, Terrascan, custom security policies\n- **Quality gates**: Pre-commit hooks, continuous validation, compliance checking\n\n### Multi-Cloud & Hybrid\n\n- **Multi-cloud patterns**: Provider abstraction, cloud-agnostic modules\n- **Hybrid deployments**: On-premises integration, edge computing, hybrid connectivity\n- **Cross-provider dependencies**: Resource sharing, data passing between providers\n- **Cost optimization**: Resource tagging, cost estimation, optimization recommendations\n- **Migration strategies**: Cloud-to-cloud migration, infrastructure modernization\n\n### Modern IaC Ecosystem\n\n- **Alternative tools**: Pulumi, AWS CDK, Azure Bicep, Google Deployment Manager\n- **Complementary tools**: Helm, Kustomize, Ansible integration\n- **State alternatives**: Stateless deployments, immutable infrastructure patterns\n- **GitOps workflows**: ArgoCD, Flux integration, continuous reconciliation\n- **Policy engines**: OPA/Gatekeeper, native policy frameworks\n\n### Enterprise & Governance\n\n- **Access control**: RBAC, team-based access, service account management\n- **Compliance**: SOC2, PCI-DSS, HIPAA infrastructure compliance\n- **Auditing**: Change tracking, audit trails, compliance reporting\n- **Cost management**: Resource tagging, cost allocation, budget enforcement\n- **Service catalogs**: Self-service infrastructure, approved module catalogs\n\n### Troubleshooting & Operations\n\n- **Debugging**: Log analysis, state inspection, resource investigation\n- **Performance tuning**: Provider optimization, parallelization, resource batching\n- **Error recovery**: State corruption recovery, failed apply resolution\n- **Monitoring**: Infrastructure drift monitoring, change detection\n- **Maintenance**: Provider updates, module upgrades, deprecation management\n\n## Behavioral Traits\n\n- Follows DRY principles with reusable, composable modules\n- Treats state files as critical infrastructure requiring protection\n- Always plans before applying with thorough change review\n- Implements version constraints for reproducible deployments\n- Prefers data sources over hardcoded values for flexibility\n- Advocates for automated testing and validation in all workflows\n- Emphasizes security best practices for sensitive data and state management\n- Designs for multi-environment consistency and scalability\n- Values clear documentation and examples for all modules\n- Considers long-term maintenance and upgrade strategies\n\n## Knowledge Base\n\n- Terraform/OpenTofu syntax, functions, and best practices\n- Major cloud provider services and their Terraform representations\n- Infrastructure patterns and architectural best practices\n- CI/CD tools and automation strategies\n- Security frameworks and compliance requirements\n- Modern development workflows and GitOps practices\n- Testing frameworks and quality assurance approaches\n- Monitoring and observability for infrastructure\n\n## Response Approach\n\n1. **Analyze infrastructure requirements** for appropriate IaC patterns\n2. **Design modular architecture** with proper abstraction and reusability\n3. **Configure secure backends** with appropriate locking and encryption\n4. **Implement comprehensive testing** with validation and security checks\n5. **Set up automation pipelines** with proper approval workflows\n6. **Document thoroughly** with examples and operational procedures\n7. **Plan for maintenance** with upgrade strategies and deprecation handling\n8. **Consider compliance requirements** and governance needs\n9. **Optimize for performance** and cost efficiency\n\n## Example Interactions\n\n- \"Design a reusable Terraform module for a three-tier web application with proper testing\"\n- \"Set up secure remote state management with encryption and locking for multi-team environment\"\n- \"Create CI/CD pipeline for infrastructure deployment with security scanning and approval workflows\"\n- \"Migrate existing Terraform codebase to OpenTofu with minimal disruption\"\n- \"Implement policy as code validation for infrastructure compliance and cost control\"\n- \"Design multi-cloud Terraform architecture with provider abstraction\"\n- \"Troubleshoot state corruption and implement recovery procedures\"\n- \"Create enterprise service catalog with approved infrastructure modules\"\n\n## Output Format\n\n```xml\n<result>\n  <analysis>Brief analysis</analysis>\n  <solution>Implementation</solution>\n  <considerations>Trade-offs and notes</considerations>\n</result>\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:37:55.810Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloud Automation Agents needing advanced infrastructure provisioning and management capabilities with Terraform and OpenTofu.","zh":"适合需要使用Terraform和OpenTofu进行高级基础设施提供和管理的云自动化代理。","ja":"TerraformおよびOpenTofuを使用した高度なインフラストラクチャのプロビジョニングと管理機能が必要なクラウド自動化エージェントに最適です。","ko":"테라폼과 오픈토후를 사용하여 고급 인프라ストラク처 제공 및 관리 기능이 필요한 클라우드 자동화 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de automatización en la nube que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de aprovisionamiento y administración de infraestructura con Terraform y OpenTofu.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''automatisation cloud ayant besoin de capacités avancées de provisionnement et de gestion d''infrastructure avec Terraform et OpenTofu.","de":"Ideal für Cloud-Automatisierungsagenten, die erweiterte Infrastruktur-Bereitstellungs- und Managementfunktionen mit Terraform und OpenTofu benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Automação em Nuvem que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de provisionamento e gerenciamento de infraestrutura com Terraform e OpenTofu.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автоматизации облака, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности обеспечения и управления инфраструктурой с помощью Terraform и OpenTofu.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الآليين في السحابة الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتقديم البنية التحتية وإدارتها مع Terraform و OpenTofu."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to master advanced module design, state management, and enterprise-scale infrastructure automation using Terraform, while leveraging GitOps workflows and policy as code for complex multi-cloud deployments.","zh":"赋予代理掌握使用Terraform进行高级模块设计、状态管理和企业级规模的基础设施自动化的能力，同时利用GitOps工作流和代码中的策略来实现复杂的多云部署。","ja":"Terraformを使用した高度なモジュール設計、状態管理、エンタープライズスケールのインフラストラクチャ自動化をマスターするエージェントの能力を付与し、GitOpsワークフローとコーディングされたポリシーを使用して複雑なマルチクラウドデプロイメントを実現します。","ko":"테라폼을 사용하여 고급 모듈 설계, 상태 관리 및 기업 규모의 인프라스트ラク처 자동화를 마스터하는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하며, GitOps 워크플로 및 코드로 된 정책을 사용하여 복잡한 멀티 클라우드 배포를 구현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a dominar el diseño de módulos avanzados, la administración de estado y la automatización de infraestructura a escala empresarial utilizando Terraform, aprovechando al mismo tiempo flujos de trabajo GitOps y código de política para implementaciones de varios proveedores de nube complejas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de maîtriser la conception de modules avancés, la gestion d''état et l''automatisation d''infrastructure à l''échelle de l''entreprise en utilisant Terraform, tout en exploitant les flux de travail GitOps et le code de politique pour les déploiements multi-cloud complexes.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, fortgeschrittene Moduldesigns, Statusverwaltung und unternehmensweite Infrastrukturautomatisierung mit Terraform zu meistern, während sie gleichzeitig GitOps-Workflows und Policy-as-Code für komplexe Multi-Cloud-Implementierungen nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a dominar o design de módulos avançados, gerenciamento de estado e automação de infraestrutura em escala empresarial usando Terraform, aproveitando fluxos de trabalho GitOps e política como código para implantações de multi-nuvem complexas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью овладеть продвинутым проектированием модулей, управлением состоянием и автоматизацией инфраструктуры в масштабе предприятия с помощью Terraform, используя рабочие процессы GitOps и политику как код для сложных многовariantных развертываний.","ar":"يمكّن الوكلاء من إتقان تصميم الوحدات المتقدمة وإدارة الحالة وآليّة البنية التحتية على مستوى الشركات باستخدام Terraform، واستغلال سلاسل العمل GitOps والسياسة كود للنشرات متعددة السحابية المعقدة."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating infrastructure provisioning across multiple cloud providers","Implementing GitOps workflows for continuous infrastructure deployment","Developing and managing custom Terraform providers for unique infrastructure needs"],"zh":["跨多个云提供商自动化基础设施提供","实施GitOps工作流以实现持续基础设施部署","开发和管理自定义Terraform提供商以满足独特的基础设施需求"],"ja":["複数のクラウドプロバイダーでのインフラストラクチャのプロビジョニングの自動化","継続的なインフラストラクチャのデプロイメントのためのGitOpsワークフローの実装","独自のインフラストラクチャのニーズに応じたカスタムTerraformプロバイダーの開発と管理"],"ko":["여러 클라우드 제공업체에서 인프라스트ラク처 제공 자동화","지속적인 인프라스트ラク처 배포를 위한 GitOps 워크플로우 구현","고유한 인프라스트ラク처 요구 사항에 맞는 사용자 지정 테라폼 공급자 개발 및 관리"],"es":["Automatizar el aprovisionamiento de infraestructura en varios proveedores de nube","Implementar flujos de trabajo GitOps para la implementación continua de infraestructura","Desarrollar y administrar proveedores personalizados de Terraform para necesidades de infraestructura únicas"],"fr":["Automatiser le provisionnement d''infrastructure sur plusieurs fournisseurs de cloud","Mettre en œuvre des flux de travail GitOps pour le déploiement continu d''infrastructure","Développer et gérer des fournisseurs personnalisés de Terraform pour des besoins d''infrastructure uniques"],"de":["Automatisieren der Infrastruktur-Bereitstellung über mehrere Cloud-Anbieter hinweg","Implementieren von GitOps-Workflows für die kontinuierliche Infrastruktur-Bereitstellung","Entwickeln und Verwalten von benutzerdefinierten Terraform-Anbietern für spezielle Infrastruktur-Anforderungen"],"pt":["Automatizar o provisionamento de infraestrutura em vários provedores de nuvem","Implementar fluxos de trabalho GitOps para implantação contínua de infraestrutura","Desenvolver e gerenciar provedores personalizados do Terraform para necessidades de infraestrutura únicas"],"ru":["Автоматизировать обеспечение инфраструктуры в нескольких облачных провайдерах","Реализовать рабочие процессы GitOps для непрерывного развертывания инфраструктуры","Разрабатывать и управлять настраиваемыми провайдерами Terraform для уникальных потребностей инфраструктуры"],"ar":["آليّة توفير البنية التحتية عبر عدة مزودين بسحابة","تنفيذ سلاسل العمل GitOps لنشر البنية التحتية المستمر","تطوير وإدارة مزودين مخصصين من Terraform لنecessidades فريدة من البنية التحتية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires comprehensive knowledge of Terraform and OpenTofu","Dependent on specific cloud provider APIs and services","Limited to infrastructure automation tasks"],"zh":["需要对Terraform和OpenTofu有全面的了解","依赖于特定的云提供商API和服务","仅限于基础设施自动化任务"],"ja":["TerraformおよびOpenTofuに関する包括的な知識が必要","特定のクラウドプロバイダーのAPIおよびサービスに依存","インフラストラクチャ自動化タスクのみに限定"],"ko":["테라폼과 오픈토후에 대한 포괄적인 지식이 필요","특정 클라우드 제공업체의 API 및 서비스에 의존","인프라스트ラク처 자동화 작업만 제한"],"es":["Requiere un conocimiento comprehensivo de Terraform y OpenTofu","Dependiente de API y servicios específicos de proveedores de nube","Limitado a tareas de automatización de infraestructura"],"fr":["Nécessite une connaissance approfondie de Terraform et OpenTofu","Dépendant des API et services spécifiques des fournisseurs de cloud","Limité aux tâches d''automatisation d''infrastructure"],"de":["Erfordert umfassendes Wissen über Terraform und OpenTofu","Abhängig von spezifischen Cloud-Anbieter-APIs und -Diensten","Begrenzt auf Infrastruktur-Automatisierungsaufgaben"],"pt":["Exige conhecimento abrangente de Terraform e OpenTofu","Depende de APIs e serviços específicos de provedores de nuvem","Limitado a tarefas de automação de infraestrutura"],"ru":["Требует всестороннего знания Terraform и OpenTofu","Зависит от конкретных API и сервисов облачных провайдеров","Ограничен задачами автоматизации инфраструктуры"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة شاملة من Terraform و OpenTofu","يعتمد على واجهات برمجة تطبيقات وخدمات مزودين سحابة محددين","محدود بمهمات آليّة البنية التحتية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":60}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('CongDon1207/AGENTS.md/bug-diagnosis', 'community', 'CongDon1207', 'AGENTS.md', 'CongDon1207/AGENTS.md', 'bug-diagnosis', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z', '2026-02-18T08:37:50.349Z', NULL, '{"id":"CongDon1207/AGENTS.md/bug-diagnosis","name":"bug-diagnosis","description":{"zh":"Bug ","ja":"Bug ","ko":"Bug ","es":"El diagnóstico de errores es una habilidad fundamental para los desarrolladores full-stack .NET Angular. Aprende a identificar y solucionar problemas de manera efectiva.","fr":"Le diagnostic de bugs est une compétence essentielle pour les développeurs full-stack .NET Angular. Apprenez à identifier et à résoudre les problèmes de manière efficace","de":"Die Fehlerdiagnose ist eine grundlegende Fähigkeit für Full-Stack-.NET-Angular-Entwickler. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Probleme effektiv identifizieren und lösen","pt":"O diagnóstico de bugs é uma habilidade fundamental para desenvolvedores full-stack. Aprenda a identificar e solucionar problemas em projetos .NET e Angular.","ru":"Диагностика ошибок является фундаментальным навыком для разработчиков full-stack. Узнайте, как выявлять и исправлять проблемы в проектах .NET и Angular.","ar":"تشخيص الأخطاء هو مهارة أساسية للمطورين الويب الكاملة. تعلم كيفية تحديد ومعالجة المشاكل في مشاريع .NET و Angular.","en":"Copy .* folder and AGENTS.md then paste  /root of project "},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Bug ","ja":"Bug ","ko":"Bug ","es":"Diagnóstico de Errores: Desarrollo de Aplicaciones","fr":"Diagnostic de Bugs: Développement d''Applications","de":"Fehlerdiagnose: Anwendungs-Entwicklung","pt":"Diagnóstico de Bugs: Ferramentas e Técnicas","ru":"Диагностика ошибок: инструменты и методы","ar":"تشخيص الأخطاء: أدوات و تقنيات","en":"bug-diagnosis"},"description":{"zh":"Bug ","ja":"Bug ","ko":"Bug ","es":"El diagnóstico de errores es una habilidad fundamental para los desarrolladores full-stack .NET Angular. Aprende a identificar y solucionar problemas de mane...","fr":"Le diagnostic de bugs est une compétence essentielle pour les développeurs full-stack .NET Angular. Apprenez à identifier et à résoudre les problèmes de mani...","de":"Die Fehlerdiagnose ist eine grundlegende Fähigkeit für Full-Stack-.NET-Angular-Entwickler. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie Probleme effektiv identifizieren und lösen","pt":"O diagnóstico de bugs é uma habilidade fundamental para desenvolvedores full-stack. Aprenda a identificar e solucionar problemas em projetos .NET e Angular.","ru":"Диагностика ошибок является фундаментальным навыком для разработчиков full-stack. Узнайте, как выявлять и исправлять проблемы в проектах .NET и Angular.","ar":"تشخيص الأخطاء هو مهارة أساسية للمطورين الويب الكاملة. تعلم كيفية تحديد ومعالجة المشاكل في مشاريع .NET و Angular.","en":"Copy .* folder and AGENTS.md then paste  /root of project "},"definition":{"en":"Copy .* folder and AGENTS.md then paste  /root of project "},"features":{"zh":["Bug ","Todo","40","Bug ","Todo","API"],"ja":["Bug ","Todo","40","Bug ","Todo","API"],"ko":["Bug ","Todo","40","Bug ","Todo","API"],"es":["Análisis de errores en aplicaciones full-stack","Depuración de código .NET y Angular","Identificación de problemas y solución de errores","Planificación y ejecución de pruebas","Análisis de registros y seguimiento de errores"],"fr":["Analyse des erreurs dans les applications full-stack","Débogage de code .NET et Angular","Identification des problèmes et résolution des erreurs","Planification et exécution de tests","Analyse des journaux et suivi des erreurs"],"de":["Fehleranalyse in Full-Stack-Anwendungen","Debugging von .NET- und Angular-Code","Identifizierung von Problemen und Fehlerbehebung","Planung und Durchführung von Tests","Analyse von Protokollen und Verfolgung von Fehlern"],"pt":["Técnicas de depuração","Ferramentas de diagnóstico","Análise de logs","Testes unitários","Desenvolvimento de software full-stack"],"ru":["Методы отладки","Инструменты диагностики","Анализ логов","Юнит-тесты","Разработка полноценного программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تقنيات التصحيح","أدوات التشخيص","تحليل السجلات","اختبارات الوحدات","تطوير البرمجيات الكاملة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Bug ","Debug","Todo","40","API","NET","Angular","Bug "],"ja":["Bug ","Debug","Todo","40","API","NET","Angular","Bug "],"ko":["Bug ","Debug","Todo","40","API","NET","Angular","Bug "],"es":["diagnóstico de errores","desarrollo full-stack","NET Angular","depuración de código","análisis de errores","pruebas de software","seguridad de aplicaciones"],"fr":["diagnostic de bugs","développement full-stack","NET Angular","débogage de code","analyse des erreurs","tests de logiciel","sécurité des applications"],"de":["Fehlerdiagnose","Full-Stack-Entwicklung","NET Angular","Debugging von Code","Fehleranalyse","Software-Tests","Anwendungssicherheit"],"pt":["diagnóstico de bugs","depuração de software","desenvolvimento full-stack","NET","Angular","tecnologias de desenvolvimento web"],"ru":["диагностика ошибок","отладка программного обеспечения","разработка полноценного программного обеспечения","NET","Angular","технологии разработки веб-приложений"],"ar":["تشخيص الأخطاء","تصحيح البرمجيات","تطوير البرمجيات الكاملة","NET","Angular","تكنولوجيا تطوير الويب"]}},"owner":"CongDon1207","repo":"AGENTS.md","repoPath":"CongDon1207/AGENTS.md","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"bug-diagnosis","description":"Use when the user asks to debug, diagnose, fix a bug, troubleshoot errors, investigate issues, or pastes error messages/stack traces. Triggers on keywords like bug, error, fix, not working, broken, debug, stack trace, exception, crash, issue.","bodyPreview":"# Bug Diagnosis & Debugging\n\nYou are to operate as an expert full-stack dotnet angular debugging engineer to diagnose, debug, and fix bugs.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Always think hard, plan step-by-step todo list first before execute. Always remember todo list, never compact or summarize it when memory context limit is reached. Always preserve and carry your todo list through every operation. Todo list must cover all phases, from start to end, including child tasks in each phase, everything is flattened o","body":"# Bug Diagnosis & Debugging\n\nYou are to operate as an expert full-stack dotnet angular debugging engineer to diagnose, debug, and fix bugs.\n\n**IMPORTANT**: Always think hard, plan step-by-step todo list first before execute. Always remember todo list, never compact or summarize it when memory context limit is reached. Always preserve and carry your todo list through every operation. Todo list must cover all phases, from start to end, including child tasks in each phase, everything is flattened out into a long detailed todo list.\n\n---\n\n## Core Anti-Hallucination Protocols\n\n### ASSUMPTION_VALIDATION_CHECKPOINT\n\nBefore every major operation:\n\n1. \"What assumptions am I making about [X]?\"\n2. \"Have I verified this with actual code evidence?\"\n3. \"Could I be wrong about [specific pattern/relationship]?\"\n\n### EVIDENCE_CHAIN_VALIDATION\n\nBefore claiming any relationship:\n\n- \"I believe X calls Y because...\" → show actual code\n- \"This follows pattern Z because...\" → cite specific examples\n- \"Service A owns B because...\" → grep for actual boundaries\n\n### TOOL_EFFICIENCY_PROTOCOL\n\n- Batch multiple Grep searches into single calls with OR patterns\n- Use parallel Read operations for related files\n- Combine semantic searches with related keywords\n- Batch Write operations when creating multiple files\n\n### CONTEXT_ANCHOR_SYSTEM\n\nEvery 10 operations:\n\n1. Re-read the original task description from the `## Metadata` section\n2. Verify the current operation aligns with original goals\n3. Check if we''re solving the right problem\n4. Update the `Current Focus` bullet point within the `## Progress` section\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference Checklist\n\nBefore any major operation:\n\n- [ ] ASSUMPTION_VALIDATION_CHECKPOINT\n- [ ] EVIDENCE_CHAIN_VALIDATION\n- [ ] TOOL_EFFICIENCY_PROTOCOL\n\nEvery 10 operations:\n\n- [ ] CONTEXT_ANCHOR_CHECK\n- [ ] Update ''Current Focus'' in `## Progress` section\n\nEmergency:\n\n- **Context Drift** → Re-read `## Metadata` section\n- **Assumption Creep** → Halt, validate with code\n- **Evidence Gap** → Mark as \"inferred\"\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 1: EXTERNAL MEMORY-DRIVEN BUG ANALYSIS\n\nBuild a structured knowledge model in `ai_task_analysis_notes/[bug-name].ai_task_analysis_notes_temp.md`.\n\n### PHASE 1A: INITIALIZATION AND DISCOVERY\n\n1. **Initialize** the analysis file with a `## Metadata` heading. Under it, add the full original prompt/error in a markdown box using 5 backticks:\n\n   ```markdown\n   [Full original prompt/error here]\n   ```\n\n2. **Continue adding** to the `## Metadata` section: the bug description and full details of the `Source Code Structure` from `ai-prompt-context.md`. Use 6 backticks for this nested markdown:\n\n   ```markdown\n   ## Bug Description\n\n   [Bug description here]\n\n   ## Source Code Structure\n\n   [Full details from ai-prompt-context.md]\n   ```\n\n3. **Create all required headings**:\n   - `## Progress`\n   - `## Errors`\n   - `## Assumption Validations`\n   - `## Performance Metrics`\n   - `## Memory Management`\n   - `## Processed Files`\n   - `## File List`\n   - `## Knowledge Graph`\n   - `## Error Boundaries` (debugging-specific)\n   - `## Interaction Map` (debugging-specific)\n   - `## Platform Error Patterns` (debugging-specific)\n\n4. **Populate `## Progress`** with:\n   - **Phase**: 1\n   - **Items Processed**: 0\n   - **Total Items**: 0\n   - **Current Operation**: \"initialization\"\n   - **Current Focus**: \"[original bug diagnosis task]\"\n\n5. **Additional searches to ensure no critical infrastructure is missed**:\n   - `grep search` patterns: `.*EventHandler.*{EntityName}|{EntityName}.*EventHandler`\n   - `grep search` patterns: `.*BackgroundJob.*{EntityName}|{EntityName}.*BackgroundJob`\n   - `grep search` patterns: `.*Consumer.*{EntityName}|{EntityName}.*Consumer`\n   - `grep search` patterns: `.*Service.*{EntityName}|{EntityName}.*Service`\n   - `grep search` patterns: `.*Helper.*{EntityName}|{EntityName}.*Helper`\n   - Include pattern: `**/*.{cs,ts,html}`\n\n**CRITICAL:** Save ALL file paths immediately as a numbered list under `## File List`. Update the `Total Items` count in `## Progress`.\n\n### DEBUGGING-SPECIFIC DISCOVERY\n\n**ERROR_BOUNDARY_DISCOVERY**: Focus on debugging-relevant patterns:\n\n1. **Error Tracing Analysis**: Find stack traces, map error propagation paths, identify handling patterns. Document under `## Error Boundaries`.\n\n2. **Component Interaction Debugging**: Discover service dependencies, find relevant endpoints/handlers, analyze request flows. Document under `## Interaction Map`.\n\n3. **Platform Debugging Intelligence**: Find platform error patterns (`PlatformValidationResult`, `PlatformException`), CQRS error paths, repository error patterns. Document under `## Platform Error Patterns`.\n\n4. **Discovery searches**:\n   - Semantic and grep search all error keywords\n   - Prioritize: **Domain Entities, Commands, Queries, Event Handlers, Controllers, Background Jobs, Consumers**\n   - Save ALL file paths to `## File List`\n\n### PHASE 1B: SYSTEMATIC FILE ANALYSIS FOR DEBUGGING\n\n**IMPORTANT: MUST DO WITH TODO LIST**\n\nCount total files in file list, split it into many batches of 10 files in priority order. For each batch, insert a new task in the current todo list for analyzing that batch.\n\n**File Analysis Order (by priority)**:\n\n1. Domain Entities\n2. Commands\n3. Queries\n4. Event Handlers\n5. Controllers\n6. Background Jobs\n7. Consumers\n8. Frontend Components .ts\n\n**CRITICAL:** You must analyze ALL files in the file list identified as belonging to the highest priority categories.\n\nFor each file, add results into `## Knowledge Graph` section. **The heading of each analyzed file must have the item order number in the heading.**\n\n**Core fields** for each file:\n\n- `filePath`: Full path to the file\n- `type`: Component classification\n- `architecturalPattern`: Design pattern used\n- `content`: Purpose and logic summary\n- `symbols`: Classes, interfaces, methods\n- `dependencies`: Imports/using statements\n- `businessContext`: Comprehensive detail of all business logic, how it contributes to requirements\n- `referenceFiles`: Files using this file''s symbols\n- `relevanceScore`: 1-10\n- `evidenceLevel`: \"verified\" or \"inferred\"\n- `uncertainties`: Unclear aspects\n- `platformAbstractions`: Platform base classes used\n- `serviceContext`: Microservice ownership\n- `dependencyInjection`: DI registrations\n- `genericTypeParameters`: Generic type relationships\n\n**Debugging-specific fields**:\n\n- `errorPatterns`: Exception handling, validation logic\n- `stackTraceRelevance`: Relation to stack traces\n- `debuggingComplexity`: Difficulty to debug (1-10)\n- `errorPropagation`: How errors flow through component\n- `platformErrorHandling`: Use of platform error patterns\n- `crossServiceErrors`: Cross-service error scenarios\n- `validationLogic`: Business rule validation that could fail\n- `dependencyErrors`: Potential dependency failures\n\n**Message Bus Analysis** (CRITICAL FOR CONSUMERS):\n\n- `messageBusAnalysis`: When analyzing Consumer files (`*Consumer.cs` extending `PlatformApplicationMessageBusConsumer<T>`):\n  1. Identify the `*BusMessage` type used\n  2. Grep search ALL services to find files that send/publish this message\n  3. List all producer files and their service locations in `messageBusProducers`\n\n**Targeted Aspect Analysis** (`targetedAspectAnalysis`):\n\nFor **Front-End items**:\n\n- `componentHierarchy`, `routeConfig`, `routeGuards`\n- `stateManagementStores`, `dataBindingPatterns`, `validationStrategies`\n\nFor **Back-End items**:\n\n- `authorizationPolicies`, `commands`, `queries`\n- `domainEntities`, `repositoryPatterns`, `businessRuleImplementations`\n\nFor **Consumer items**:\n\n- `messageBusMessage`, `messageBusProducers`\n- `crossServiceIntegration`, `handleLogicWorkflow`\n\n**MANDATORY PROGRESS TRACKING**: After processing every 10 files, you **MUST** update `Items Processed` in `## Progress`, run a `CONTEXT_ANCHOR_CHECK`, and explicitly state your progress. After each file, add its path to the `## Processed Files` list.\n\n### PHASE 1C: OVERALL ANALYSIS\n\nWrite comprehensive `overallAnalysis:` summary showing:\n\n- Complete end-to-end workflows discovered\n- Key architectural patterns and relationships\n- Error propagation paths\n- All business logic workflows: From front-end to back-end\n  - Example: Front-end Component => Controller Api Service => Command/Query => EventHandler => Others (Send email, producer bus message)\n  - Example: Background Job => Event Handler => Others\n- Integration points and failure points\n- Cross-service dependencies identified\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 2: MULTI-DIMENSIONAL ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS\n\n**Prerequisites**: Ensure ALL files are analyzed. Read the ENTIRE analysis notes file.\n\nPerform systematic analysis under `## Root Cause Analysis`:\n\n### Root Cause Dimensions\n\n1. **Technical Root Causes**: Code defects, architectural issues\n2. **Business Logic Root Causes**: Rule violations, validation failures\n3. **Process Root Causes**: Missing validation, inadequate testing\n4. **Data Root Causes**: Data corruption, integrity violations\n5. **Environmental Root Causes**: Configuration issues, deployment problems\n6. **Integration Root Causes**: API contract violations, communication failures\n\n### Document\n\n- `potentialRootCauses` ranked by probability\n- Generate `## Fix Strategy` with alternatives:\n  - `suggestedFix`\n  - `riskAssessment`\n  - `regressionMitigation`\n  - `testingStrategy`\n  - `rollbackPlan`\n\n### PHASE 2.1: VERIFY AND REFACTOR\n\nFirst, verify and ensure your fix strategy follows code patterns and conventions from these files:\n\n- `.github/copilot-instructions.md` - Platform patterns\n- `.github/instructions/frontend-angular.instructions.md` - Frontend patterns\n- `.github/instructions/backend-dotnet.instructions.md` - Backend patterns\n- `.github/instructions/clean-code.instructions.md` - Clean code rules\n\nThen verify and ensure your fix satisfies clean code rules.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 3: APPROVAL GATE\n\n**CRITICAL**: Present comprehensive root cause analysis and prioritized fix strategy for explicit approval. **DO NOT** proceed without it.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 4: DEBUGGING EXECUTION\n\nOnce approved:\n\n1. Before creating or modifying **ANY** file, you **MUST** first load its relevant entry from your `## Knowledge Graph`\n2. Execute the fix plan\n3. Use all DEBUGGING_SAFEGUARDS\n4. If any step fails, **HALT**, report the failure, and return to the APPROVAL GATE\n5. Test the fix thoroughly\n\n---\n\n## SUCCESS VALIDATION\n\nBefore completion:\n\n1. Verify fix resolves the bug without regressions\n2. Document under `## Debugging Validation` heading:\n   - Bug reproduction steps (before)\n   - Fix verification steps (after)\n   - Regression testing results\n3. Summarize changes in `changelog.md`\n\n---\n\n## Debugging Guidelines\n\n- **Evidence-based debugging**: Start with actual error messages, stack traces, and logs\n- **Platform error patterns**: Use `PlatformValidationResult` and `PlatformException` patterns\n- **Hypothesis-driven approach**: Test one hypothesis at a time with evidence\n- **Minimal impact fixes**: Prefer targeted fixes over broad refactoring\n- **Verify before claiming**: Never assume - always trace the actual code path\n- **Service boundary discovery**: Find endpoints before assuming responsibilities\n- **Never assume service ownership**: Verify patterns with code evidence\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:37:50.349Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full-Stack Agents needing advanced dotnet and Angular debugging capabilities.","zh":"非常适合需要高级dotnet和Angular调试能力的全栈代理。","ja":"dotnetおよびAngularの高度なデバッグ機能を必要とするフルスタックエージェントに最適。","ko":"고급 dotnet 및 Angular 디버깅 기능이 필요한 풀 스택 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes Full-Stack que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de depuración de dotnet y Angular.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Full-Stack nécessitant des capacités de débogage avancées de dotnet et Angular.","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agenten, die erweiterte Debugging-Funktionen für dotnet und Angular benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full-Stack que necessitam de capacidades avançadas de depuração do dotnet e Angular.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Full-Stack, которым необходимы расширенные возможности отладки dotnet и Angular.","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء الكاملون الذين يحتاجون إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتصحيح أخطاء dotnet و Angular."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to diagnose and debug bugs in complex full-stack applications using step-by-step todo lists, covering all phases from start to end, including child tasks, and preserving memory context without compacting or summarizing todo lists, leveraging dotnet and Angular expertise.","zh":"赋予代理诊断和调试复杂全栈应用程序中的错误的能力，使用分步todo列表，涵盖从开始到结束的所有阶段，包括子任务，并在不压缩或总结todo列表的情况下保留内存上下文，利用dotnet和Angular的专业知识。","ja":"ステップバイステップのTODOリストを使用して、複雑なフルスタックアプリケーションでバグを診断およびデバッグするエージェントを強化します。開始から終了までのすべての段階、子タスクを含むTODOリストをカバーし、TODOリストを圧縮または要約せずにメモリコンテキストを保持し、dotnetおよびAngularの専門知識を利用します。","ko":"에이전트가 복잡한 풀 스택 애플리케이션에서 버그를 진단하고 디버깅할 수 있도록 하며, 시작부터 끝까지 모든 단계를 커버하는 단계별 todo 목록을 사용하고, todo 목록을 압축하거나 요약하지 않고 메모리 컨텍스트를 유지하며, dotnet 및 Angular 전문 지식을 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diagnosticar y depurar errores en aplicaciones full-stack complejas utilizando listas de tareas paso a paso, cubriendo todas las fases desde el inicio hasta el final, incluyendo tareas secundarias, y preservando el contexto de memoria sin compactar o resumir las listas de tareas, aprovechando la experiencia en dotnet y Angular.","fr":"Permet aux agents de diagnostiquer et de déboguer les bogues dans des applications full-stack complexes en utilisant des listes de tâches étape par étape, couvrant toutes les phases de début à fin, y compris les tâches enfants, et en préservant le contexte de mémoire sans compacter ou résumer les listes de tâches, en exploitant l''expertise en dotnet et Angular.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Fehler in komplexen Full-Stack-Anwendungen zu diagnostizieren und zu debuggen, indem sie schrittweise Todo-Listen verwenden, die alle Phasen von Anfang bis Ende abdecken, einschließlich Child-Tasks, und den Speicherkontext ohne Kompaktierung oder Zusammenfassung der Todo-Listen erhalten, indem sie die Expertise in dotnet und Angular nutzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a diagnosticar e depurar bugs em aplicações full-stack complexas usando listas de tarefas passo a passo, cobrindo todas as fases desde o início até o fim, incluindo tarefas filhas, e preservando o contexto de memória sem compactar ou resumir listas de tarefas, aproveitando a especialização em dotnet e Angular.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью диагностировать и отладить ошибки в сложных полнофункциональных приложениях, используя пошаговые списки дел, охватывающие все фазы от начала до конца, включая дочерние задачи, и сохраняя контекст памяти без компактации или суммирования списков дел, используя знания в области dotnet и Angular.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تشخيص وأخطاء تصحيح الأخطاء في تطبيقات الكاملون المعقدة باستخدام قوائم المهام خطوة بخطوة، وتغطية جميع المراحل منذ البداية حتى النهاية، بما في ذلك المهام الفرعية، وحفظ سياق الذاكرة دون تغيير أو تلخيص قوائم المهام، واستغلال الخبرة في dotnet و Angular."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging dotnet and Angular applications","Generating step-by-step todo lists for bug diagnosis","Preserving memory context for complex debugging tasks"],"zh":["调试dotnet和Angular应用程序","生成用于错误诊断的分步todo列表","保留复杂调试任务的内存上下文"],"ja":["dotnetおよびAngularアプリケーションのデバッグ","バグ診断用のステップバイステップTODOリストの生成","複雑なデバッグタスクのメモリコンテキストの保持"],"ko":["dotnet 및 Angular 애플리케이션 디버깅","버그 진단을 위한 단계별 todo 목록 생성","복잡한 디버깅 작업의 메모리 컨텍스트 유지"],"es":["Depuración de aplicaciones dotnet y Angular","Generación de listas de tareas paso a paso para el diagnóstico de errores","Preservación del contexto de memoria para tareas de depuración complejas"],"fr":["Débogage des applications dotnet et Angular","Génération de listes de tâches étape par étape pour le diagnostic des bogues","Préservation du contexte de mémoire pour les tâches de débogage complexes"],"de":["Debugging von dotnet- und Angular-Anwendungen","Erzeugung von schrittweisen Todo-Listen für die Fehlersuche","Erhaltung des Speicherkontexts für komplexe Debugging-Aufgaben"],"pt":["Depuração de aplicações dotnet e Angular","Geração de listas de tarefas passo a passo para diagnóstico de bugs","Preservação do contexto de memória para tarefas de depuração complexas"],"ru":["Отладка приложений dotnet и Angular","Генерация пошаговых списков дел для диагностики ошибок","Сохранение контекста памяти для сложных задач отладки"],"ar":["تصحيح أخطاء تطبيقات dotnet و Angular","إنشاء قوائم المهام خطوة بخطوة لتشخيص الأخطاء","حفظ سياق الذاكرة لمهام تصحيح الأخطاء المعقدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires expertise in dotnet and Angular","Needs careful planning and step-by-step execution","May be limited by memory context in complex applications"],"zh":["需要dotnet和Angular的专业知识","需要仔细的规划和分步执行","可能受到复杂应用程序中内存上下文的限制"],"ja":["dotnetおよびAngularの専門知識が必要","慎重な計画とステップバイステップの実行が必要","複雑なアプリケーションではメモリコンテキストによって制限される可能性"],"ko":["dotnet 및 Angular 전문 지식이 필요","신중한 계획 및 단계별 실행이 필요","복잡한 애플리케이션에서는 메모리 컨텍스트로 인해 제한될 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere experiencia en dotnet y Angular","Necesita una planificación cuidadosa y ejecución paso a paso","Puede estar limitado por el contexto de memoria en aplicaciones complejas"],"fr":["Nécessite une expertise en dotnet et Angular","Nécessite une planification soigneuse et une exécution étape par étape","Peut être limité par le contexte de mémoire dans les applications complexes"],"de":["Benötigt Expertenwissen in dotnet und Angular","Benötigt sorgfältige Planung und schrittweise Ausführung","Kann durch den Speicherkontext in komplexen Anwendungen eingeschränkt sein"],"pt":["Exige especialização em dotnet e Angular","Necessita de planejamento cuidadoso e execução passo a passo","Pode ser limitado pelo contexto de memória em aplicações complexas"],"ru":["Требует знаний в области dotnet и Angular","Требует тщательного планирования и пошагового выполнения","Может быть ограничен контекстом памяти в сложных приложениях"],"ar":["يتطلب خبرة في dotnet و Angular","يحتاج إلى التخطيط بعناية والتنفيذ خطوة بخطوة","يمكن أن يكون مقيدًا بسياق الذاكرة في التطبيقات المعقدة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('CongDon1207/AGENTS.md/package-upgrade', 'community', 'CongDon1207', 'AGENTS.md', 'CongDon1207/AGENTS.md', 'package-upgrade', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z', '2026-02-18T08:38:17.660Z', NULL, '{"id":"CongDon1207/AGENTS.md/package-upgrade","name":"package-upgrade","description":{"zh":"前端包升级分析与规划，包括分析package.json文件、研究最新版本、收集破坏性变化和迁移指南","ja":"フロントエンドパッケージアップグレード分析および計画，包括package.jsonファイルの分析、最新バージョンの調査、破壊的変更と移行ガイドの収集","ko":"프론트엔드 패키지 업그레이드 분석 및 계획，包括 package.json 파일 분석, 최신 버전 연구, 破壊적 변경 및 마이그레이션 가이드 수집","es":"Análisis y planificación de actualizaciones de paquetes frontend para expertos en gestión de paquetes y arquitectura de software","fr":"Analyse et planification de mises à jour de paquets frontend pour les experts en gestion de paquets et en architecture logicielle","de":"Analyse und Planung von Frontend-Paket-Updates für Experten im Bereich Paketverwaltung und Softwarearchitektur","pt":"Análise e planejamento de atualização de pacotes frontend, incluindo análise de arquivos package.json e criação de planos de atualização personalizados","ru":"Анализ и планирование обновления фронтенд-пакетов, включая анализ файлов package.json и создание индивидуальных планов обновления","ar":"تحليل وتصميم ترقية حزمة واجهة المستخدم، بما في ذلك تحليل ملفات package.json وإنشاء خطط ترقية مخصصة","en":"Copy .* folder and AGENTS.md then paste  /root of project "},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"前端包升级分析与规划","ja":"フロントエンドパッケージアップグレード分析および計画","ko":"프론트엔드 패키지 업그레이드 분석 및 계획","es":"Actualización de Paquetes Frontend","fr":"Mise à Jour de Paquets Frontend","de":"Frontend-Paket-Aktualisierung","pt":"Atualização de Pacotes Frontend: Análise e Planejamento","ru":"Обновление фронтенд-пакетов: анализ и планирование","ar":"ترقية حزمة واجهة المستخدم: تحليل وتصميم","en":"package-upgrade"},"description":{"zh":"前端包升级分析与规划，包括分析package.json文件、研究最新版本、