zberg is a fast, polyglot document intelligence engine with a Rust core. It extracts structured data from 56+ document formats using streaming parsers and built-in OCR."},"features":{"zh":["模块结构原则","根模块和特性模块","使用 pub 和 pub(crate) 控制可见性","组织代码以提高可维护性","设计公共 API 以提高代码重用性"],"ja":["モジュール構造の原則","ルートモジュールと機能モジュール","pub と pub(crate) を使用して可視性を制御する","コードを組織して保守性を向上させる","パブリック API を設計してコードの再利用性を向上させる"],"ko":["모듈 구조 원칙","루트 모듈과 기능 모듈","pub과 pub(crate)을 사용하여 가시성을 제어","코드를 구성하여 유지 보수성을 향상","공개 API를 설계하여 코드 재사용성을 향상"],"es":["Diseño de API pública","Organización de módulos","Mejora del rendimiento","Escalabilidad","Legibilidad del código","Integración con Kreuzberg"],"fr":["Conception d''API publique","Organisation de modules","Amélioration des performances","Scalabilité","Lisibilité du code","Intégration avec Kreuzberg"],"de":["Öffentliches API-Design","Modulorganisation","Leistungsverbesserung","Skalierbarkeit","Lesbarkeit des Codes","Integration mit Kreuzberg"],"pt":["Módulos organizados por domínio","Controle de visibilidade explícito com `pub` e `pub(crate)`","Re-exportação de itens públicos no módulo raiz","Estrutura de módulos flexível e escalável","Melhoria da manutenção e reutilização do código"],"ru":["Модули, организованные по доменам","Явный контроль видимости с помощью `pub` и `pub(crate)`","Перекрестная ссылка на публичные элементы в корневом модуле","Гибкая и масштабируемая структура модулей","Улучшение обслуживания и повторного использования кода"],"ar":["الوحدات النمطية المنظمة حسب المجال","التحكم الصريح في الرؤية باستخدام `pub` و `pub(crate)`","إعادة التصدير للأجزاء العامة في وحدة الرأس","هيكل الوحدات المرنة و القابلة للتوسيع","تحسين الصيانة و إعادة الاستخدام للرمز"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Rust 模块组织","公共 API 设计","Rust 编程","代码可维护性","代码重用性","模块结构","可见性控制","保守性"],"ja":["Rust モジュール組織","パブリック API デザイン","Rust プログラミング","コードの保守性","コードの再利用性","モジュール構造","可視性制御","保守性"],"ko":["러스트 모듈 구성","공개 API 설계","러스트 프로그래밍","코드 유지 보수성","코드 재사용성","모듈 구조","가시성 제어","유지 보수성"],"es":["Rust","diseño de API","organización de módulos","alto rendimiento","escalabilidad","Kreuzberg","desarrollo de aplicaciones","programación en Rust","mejora del rendimiento"],"fr":["Rust","conception d''API","organisation de modules","haute performance","scalabilité","Kreuzberg","développement d''applications","programmation en Rust","amélioration des performances"],"de":["Rust","öffentliches API-Design","Modulorganisation","Hochleistung","Skalierbarkeit","Kreuzberg","Anwendungsentwicklung","Rust-Programmierung","Leistungsverbesserung"],"pt":["desenvolvimento de módulos rust","organização de módulos","design de api pública","controle de visibilidade","reutilização de código","manutenção de código"],"ru":["разработка модулей rust","организация модулей","проектирование публичного api","контроль видимости","повторное использование кода","обслуживание кода"],"ar":["تنمية الوحدات النمطية في rust","تنظيم الوحدات النمطية","تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات العامة","التحكم في الرؤية","إعادة الاستخدام للرمز","صيانة الرمز"]}},"owner":"kreuzberg-dev","repo":"html-to-markdown","repoPath":"kreuzberg-dev/html-to-markdown","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rust-module-organization-public-api-design","description":"","bodyPreview":"______________________________________________________________________\n\n## priority: high\n\n# Rust Module Organization & Public API Design\n\n## Module Structure Principles\n\n**Modules are organizational units, not visibility boundaries**. Use `pub` / `pub(crate)` / `pub(super)` to control visibility explicitly.\n\n1. **Root crate module**: `src/lib.rs` or `src/main.rs` re-exports public items\n1. **Feature-specific modules**: `src/parsing/`, `src/conversion/`, `src/utils/` organize by domain\n1. **Inte","body":"______________________________________________________________________\n\n## priority: high\n\n# Rust Module Organization & Public API Design\n\n## Module Structure Principles\n\n**Modules are organizational units, not visibility boundaries**. Use `pub` / `pub(crate)` / `pub(super)` to control visibility explicitly.\n\n1. **Root crate module**: `src/lib.rs` or `src/main.rs` re-exports public items\n1. **Feature-specific modules**: `src/parsing/`, `src/conversion/`, `src/utils/` organize by domain\n1. **Internal vs. public**: Mark private modules with `pub(crate)` if they''re internal infrastructure\n1. **Re-exports**: Use `pub use` in `lib.rs` to define the public API surface\n\n## Module Hierarchy Example\n\n```\nsrc/\n├── lib.rs                    # Root: re-exports public API\n├── parsing/                  # Feature module\n│   ├── mod.rs               # Module interface, re-exports\n│   ├── html_parser.rs       # Internal implementation\n│   ├── sanitizer.rs         # Internal implementation\n│   └── error.rs             # Domain-specific errors\n├── conversion/              # Feature module\n│   ├── mod.rs               # Module interface\n│   ├── node_visitor.rs      # Implementation\n│   └── formatters/          # Submodule\n│       ├── mod.rs\n│       ├── markdown.rs\n│       └── text.rs\n├── error.rs                 # Crate-wide error types\n└── config.rs                # Configuration\n```\n\n## Public API Design\n\n**Golden Rule**: Your `src/lib.rs` should read like a user guide.\n\n````rust\n//! html-to-markdown: Convert HTML to Markdown with safety & performance\n//!\n//! # Quick Start\n//! ```\n//! use html_to_markdown::HtmlConverter;\n//! let converter = HtmlConverter::new();\n//! let markdown = converter.convert(\"<h1>Hello</h1>\")?;\n//! ```\n\n// Public types\npub use crate::conversion::{HtmlConverter, ConversionConfig};\npub use crate::parsing::ParseError;\npub use crate::error::Error;\n\n// Public type aliases for convenience\npub type Result<T> = std::result::Result<T, Error>;\n\n// Don''t re-export implementation details\n// pub use crate::parsing::html_parser;  // BAD\n````\n\n## Pub/Private Boundaries\n\n**Public** (`pub`): Part of stable API contract\n\n- Main types: `HtmlConverter`, `ConversionConfig`\n- Error types: `ParseError`, `ConversionError`\n- Common utility functions\n- Config builders\n\n**Pub(crate)** (`pub(crate)`): Internal infrastructure, not for external users\n\n```rust\npub(crate) struct InternalParser { ... }\npub(crate) fn internal_helper() { ... }\n```\n\n**Private** (no visibility keyword): Never exposed\n\n```rust\nfn internal_detail() { ... }\nstruct InternalState { ... }\n```\n\n## Feature Gates\n\nUse Cargo features to conditionally expose API surface:\n\n```toml\n[features]\ndefault = [\"parsing\"]\nparsing = []\nasync-runtime = [\"tokio\"]\nffi = [\"libffi\"]\n\n[[example]]\nname = \"async_convert\"\nrequired-features = [\"async-runtime\"]\n```\n\n```rust\n// Conditional re-export\n#[cfg(feature = \"async-runtime\")]\npub use crate::async_convert::AsyncConverter;\n\n#[cfg(feature = \"ffi\")]\npub use crate::ffi::ExportedAPI;\n```\n\n## Module Re-exports Pattern\n\n**Module interface** (`src/parsing/mod.rs`):\n\n```rust\n//! HTML parsing module with robust error handling\n\nmod html_parser;\nmod sanitizer;\npub mod error;\n\npub use self::html_parser::{Parser, ParseConfig};\npub use self::sanitizer::Sanitizer;\n\n// Internal utilities not re-exported\nuse self::html_parser::HtmlToken;\n```\n\n**Root re-export** (`src/lib.rs`):\n\n```rust\npub use crate::parsing::{Parser, ParseConfig};\npub use crate::parsing::error::{ParseError, SyntaxError};\npub use crate::conversion::HtmlConverter;\n\n// Don''t expose internal modules\n// Bad: pub mod parsing;\n```\n\n## Cargo Public API Validation\n\nUse `cargo-public-api` to track breaking changes:\n\n```bash\n# Generate baseline\ncargo public-api --baseline > baseline.txt\n\n# Check for breaking changes in PRs\ncargo public-api --diff baseline.txt\n\n# Track additions\ncargo public-api > current.txt\n```\n\nAdd to CI:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Check public API\n  run: |\n    cargo install cargo-public-api\n    cargo public-api --diff baseline.txt\n```\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n1. **Exposing implementation details**:\n\n   ```rust\n   // BAD: Leaks internal parser state\n   pub use crate::parsing::internal::ParserState;\n\n   // GOOD: Expose stable interface\n   pub fn parse(input: &str) -> Result<Document> { ... }\n   ```\n\n1. **Deeply nested modules in public API**:\n\n   ```rust\n   // BAD: Public `mod parsing { mod html_parser { ... } }`\n   // Users write: html_to_markdown::parsing::html_parser::Parser\n\n   // GOOD: Flatten in re-export\n   // Users write: html_to_markdown::Parser\n   ```\n\n1. **Mixed public/private in single module**:\n\n   ```rust\n   // BAD: Confusing what''s stable\n   pub fn stable_api() { ... }\n   pub fn internal_detail() { ... }\n\n   // GOOD: Separate concerns\n   pub mod api { pub fn stable() { ... } }\n   mod internal { pub(crate) fn detail() { ... } }\n   ```\n\n1. **Not documenting API stability**:\n\n   ```rust\n   // BAD: Users don''t know if this might change\n   pub struct Config { ... }\n\n   // GOOD: Clear stability guarantees\n   /// Configuration for HTML conversion (part of stable 1.x API)\n   pub struct Config { ... }\n   ```\n\n## Documentation Best Practices\n\n- **Module docs**: Explain purpose and common patterns\n- **Type docs**: Document public invariants\n- **Example code**: Show real usage patterns\n- **Error docs**: Document error conditions\n\n````rust\n/// Converts HTML to Markdown\n///\n/// # Examples\n/// ```\n/// use html_to_markdown::HtmlConverter;\n/// let converter = HtmlConverter::new();\n/// let md = converter.convert(\"<h1>Title</h1><p>Content</p>\")?;\n/// assert!(md.contains(\"# Title\"));\n/// ```\n///\n/// # Errors\n/// Returns `ParseError` if HTML is malformed beyond recovery.\npub fn convert(html: &str) -> Result<String> { ... }\n````\n\n## Stability Markers\n\nDocument API stability intentions:\n\n```rust\n// Stable in 1.x API\n/// Configuration builder (stable API)\npub struct ConfigBuilder { ... }\n\n// Experimental, may change\n/// Experimental: May change in minor versions\n#[doc(alias = \"deprecated\")]\npub struct ExperimentalFeature { ... }\n\n// Deprecated\n/// Deprecated: Use `convert_v2()` instead\n#[deprecated(since = \"0.5.0\", note = \"use convert_v2\")]\npub fn convert_old(input: &str) -> Result<String> { ... }\n```\n\n## Cross-references to Related Skills\n\n- **workspace-dependency-management**: Coordinating public API across crates\n- **error-handling-strategy**: Designing error types as part of public API\n- **testing-philosophy-coverage**: Testing public API surface\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:38:17.942Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Rust-based AI Agents needing high-performance module organization and public API design principles.","zh":"非常适合需要高性能模块组织和公共 API 设计原则的 Rust 基础 AI 代理。","ja":"Rust ベースの AI エージェントが高性能なモジュールの組織化とパブリック API の設計原則を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고성능 모듈 구성 및 공개 API 설계 원칙이 필요한 러스트 기반 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfect for Rust-based AI Agents needing high-performance module organization and public API design principles.","fr":"Perfect for Rust-based AI Agents needing high-performance module organization and public API design principles.","de":"Perfect for Rust-based AI Agents needing high-performance module organization and public API design principles.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de IA baseados em Rust que precisam de organização de módulos de alto desempenho e princípios de design de API pública.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ на основе Rust, которым необходима организация модулей с высокими производительными характеристиками и принципами проектирования публичного API.","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي المبني على روست والذي يحتاج إلى تنظيم وحدة عالية الأداء ومبادئ تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات العامة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to structure Rust codebases efficiently using explicit visibility control with `pub`, `pub(crate)`, and `pub(super)`, and organize modules by domain for optimal performance and readability, leveraging Rust''s module structure principles.","zh":"赋予代理结构 Rust 代码库的能力，使用显式的可见性控制和 `pub`、`pub(crate)`、`pub(super)`，并按照领域组织模块，以实现最佳的性能和可读性，利用 Rust 的模块结构原则。","ja":"エージェントが Rust コードベースを効率的に構造化できるようにし、`pub`、`pub(crate)`、`pub(super)` を使用した明示的な可視性制御と、パフォーマンスと可読性の最適化のためにドメイン別にモジュールを組織することで、Rust のモジュール構造原則を活用します。","ko":"에이전트가 러스트 코드베이스를 효율적으로 구조화할 수 있도록 해주고, `pub`, `pub(crate)`, `pub(super)`를 사용한 명시적인 가시성 제어 및 최적의 성능과 가독성을 위한 도메인별 모듈 구성으로 러스트의 모듈 구조 원리를 활용합니다.","es":"Empowers agents to structure Rust codebases efficiently using explicit visibility control with `pub`, `pub(crate)`, and `pub(super)`, and organize modules by domain for optimal performance and readability, leveraging Rust''s module structure principles.","fr":"Empowers agents to structure Rust codebases efficiently using explicit visibility control with `pub`, `pub(crate)`, and `pub(super)`, and organize modules by domain for optimal performance and readability, leveraging Rust''s module structure principles.","de":"Empowers agents to structure Rust codebases efficiently using explicit visibility control with `pub`, `pub(crate)`, and `pub(super)`, and organize modules by domain for optimal performance and readability, leveraging Rust''s module structure principles.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a estruturarem bases de código Rust de forma eficiente, utilizando controle de visibilidade explícito com `pub`, `pub(crate)` e `pub(super)`, e organizam módulos por domínio para otimizar o desempenho e a legibilidade, aproveitando os princípios da estrutura de módulos do Rust.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью структурировать базы кода Rust эффективно, используя явный контроль видимости с `pub`, `pub(crate)` и `pub(super)`, и организовывать модули по доменам для оптимальной производительности и читаемости, используя принципы структуры модулей Rust.","ar":"يمكن العميل من هيكلة قواعد بيانات روست بطريقة فعالة باستخدام التحكم الصريح في الرؤية باستخدام `pub` و `pub(crate)` و `pub(super)` ، وتنظيم الوحدات حسب المجال من أجل أداء وقراءة أمثالية ، واستخدام مبادئ هيكلة الوحدات في روست."},"useCases":{"en":["Organizing large Rust codebases for improved maintainability","Designing public APIs for Rust modules with controlled visibility","Streamlining Rust project structures for better collaboration"],"zh":["组织大型 Rust 代码库以提高可维护性","设计具有受控可见性的 Rust 模块的公共 API","优化 Rust 项目结构以提高协作效率"],"ja":["メンテナンス性の向上のために大規模な Rust コードベースを組織する","制御された可視性を持つ Rust モジュールのパブリック API を設計する","コラボレーションの効率化のために Rust プロジェクト構造を最適化する"],"ko":["유지 보수성을 향상하기 위해 대형 러스트 코드베이스를 구성하기","제어된 가시성을 갖는 러스트 모듈의 공개 API 설계하기","협업 효율성을 높이기 위해 러스트 프로젝트 구조 최적화하기"],"es":["Organizing large Rust codebases for improved maintainability","Designing public APIs for Rust modules with controlled visibility","Streamlining Rust project structures for better collaboration"],"fr":["Organizing large Rust codebases for improved maintainability","Designing public APIs for Rust modules with controlled visibility","Streamlining Rust project structures for better collaboration"],"de":["Organizing large Rust codebases for improved maintainability","Designing public APIs for Rust modules with controlled visibility","Streamlining Rust project structures for better collaboration"],"pt":["Organizar grandes bases de código Rust para melhor manutenção","Projetar APIs públicas para módulos Rust com visibilidade controlada","Otimizar estruturas de projetos Rust para melhor colaboração"],"ru":["Организация больших баз кода Rust для улучшения поддержки","Проектирование публичных API для модулей Rust с контролируемой видимостью","Оптимизация структур проектов Rust для лучшего сотрудничества"],"ar":["تنظيم قواعد بيانات روست الكبيرة لتحسين الصيانة","تصميم واجهات برمجة تطبيقات عامة لمكونات روست مع رؤية خاضعة للرقابة","تحسين هياكل مشاريع روست من أجل تعاون أفضل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Rust programming language","Specific to Rust module organization and public API design"],"zh":["需要了解 Rust 编程语言","特定于 Rust 模块组织和公共 API 设计"],"ja":