wurfsbearbeitung","pt":"Draft Polisher: Edição de Textos Técnicos","ru":"Draft Polisher: Техническое редактирование текстов","ar":"_draft Polisher: تعديل نصوص تقنية","en":"draft-polisher"},"description":{"zh":"draft-polisher 技术是一种通过语义执行单元和循证方法来提高初稿质量的技术，能够有效地提高写作效率","ja":"draft-polisher 技術は、初稿の品質を向上させるために、セマンティック実行ユニットとエビデンスファーストの方法を使用する技術です","ko":"draft-polisher 기술은 초안의 품질을 향상시키기 위해 의미 실행 단위와 증거 우선 방법을 사용하는 기술입니다","es":"Draft Polisher es una herramienta de edición de borradores técnicos que mejora la legibilidad y coherencia del texto.","fr":"Draft Polisher est un outil d''édition de brouillons techniques qui améliore la lisibilité et la cohérence du texte.","de":"Draft Polisher ist ein Werkzeug zur Bearbeitung von technischen Entwürfen, das die Lesbarkeit und Kohärenz des Textes verbessert.","pt":"O Draft Polisher é uma ferramenta de edição que ajuda a melhorar a qualidade dos textos técnicos, tornando-os mais claros e concisos.","ru":"Draft Polisher - это инструмент редактирования, который помогает улучшить качество технических текстов, делая их более ясными и лаконичными.","ar":"Draft Polisher هو أداة تحرير تساعد على تحسين جودة النصوص التقنية، تجعلها أكثر وضوحًا وملاءمة.","en":"Research pipelines as semantic execution units: each skill declares inputs/outputs, acceptance criteria, and guardrails. Evidence-first methodology prevents ..."},"definition":{"en":"Research pipelines as semantic execution units: each skill declares inputs/outputs, acceptance criteria, and guardrails. Evidence-first methodology prevents hollow writing through structured intermediate artifacts."},"features":{"zh":["语义执行单元","循证方法","提高初稿质量","提高写作效率","结构化中间件件"],"ja":["セマンティック実行ユニット","エビデンスファーストの方法","初稿の品質向上","書き込み効率の向上","構造化中間アーティファクト"],"ko":["의미 실행 단위","증거 우선 방법","초안의 품질 향상","작성 효율 향상","구조화된 중간 아티팩트"],"es":["Edición de auditoría para mejorar la legibilidad","Eliminación de redundancias y términos innecesarios","Mejora de la coherencia y la estructura del texto","Corrección de errores de estilo y gramática","Optimización para crear prosa de encuesta legible"],"fr":["Édition d''audit pour améliorer la lisibilité","Élimination des redondances et des termes inutiles","Amélioration de la cohérence et de la structure du texte","Correction des erreurs de style et de grammaire","Optimisation pour créer une prose de sondage lisible"],"de":["Audit-Style-Editing für verbesserte Lesbarkeit","Entfernung von Redundanz und überflüssigen Begriffen","Verbesserung der Kohärenz und Struktur des Textes","Korrektur von Stil- und Grammatikfehlern","Optimierung für lesbare Umfrageprosa"],"pt":["Edição de texto técnico","Melhoria da clareza e concisão","Remoção de redundâncias","Otimização de terminologia","Verificação de coerência"],"ru":["Техническое редактирование текстов","Улучшение ясности и лаконичности","Удаление повторений","Оптимизация терминологии","Проверка коherencia"],"ar":["تحرير نصوص تقنية","تحسين الوضوح والملاءمة","إزالة التكرارات","تحسين المصطلحات","فحص الاتساق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["draft-polisher","语义执行单元","循证方法","初稿质量","写作效率","结构化中间件件","技术写作"],"ja":["draft-polisher","セマンティック実行ユニット","エビデンスファーストの方法","初稿の品質","書き込み効率","構造化中間アーティファクト","テクニカルライティング"],"ko":["draft-polisher","의미 실행 단위","증거 우선 방법","초안 품질","작성 효율","구조화된 중간 아티팩트","기술 글쓰기"],"es":["edición de borradores técnicos"," Draft Polisher","edición de auditoría","mejora de la legibilidad","eliminación de redundancias","coherencia del texto","estilo y gramática","prosa de encuesta"],"fr":["édition de brouillons techniques","Draft Polisher","édition d''audit","amélioration de la lisibilité","élimination des redondances","cohérence du texte","style et grammaire","prose de sondage"],"de":["Bearbeitung von technischen Entwürfen","Draft Polisher","Audit-Style-Editing","Verbesserung der Lesbarkeit","Entfernung von Redundanz","Kohärenz des Textes","Stil und Grammatik","Umfrageprosa"],"pt":["edição de texto técnico","melhoria de texto","ferramenta de edição","texto claro","texto conciso","revisão de texto","otimização de texto"],"ru":["техническое редактирование текстов","улучшение текста","инструмент редактирования","ясный текст","лаконичный текст","ревизия текста","оптимизация текста"],"ar":["تحرير نصوص تقنية","تحسين النص","أداة تحرير","نص واضح","نص ملائم","مراجعة النص","تحسين النص"]}},"owner":"WILLOSCAR","repo":"research-units-pipeline-skills","repoPath":"WILLOSCAR/research-units-pipeline-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"draft-polisher","description":"|","bodyPreview":"# Draft Polisher (Audit-style editing)\n\nGoal: turn a first-pass draft into readable survey prose **without breaking the evidence contract**.\n\nThis is a local polish pass: de-template + coherence + terminology + redundancy pruning.\n\nNote: if the main issue is structural redundancy from section accumulation, push the change upstream to `sections/` and use `paragraph-curator` before merge. `draft-polisher` should not be the primary place where you decide which paragraphs to keep.\n\n\n\n## Role cards (","body":"# Draft Polisher (Audit-style editing)\n\nGoal: turn a first-pass draft into readable survey prose **without breaking the evidence contract**.\n\nThis is a local polish pass: de-template + coherence + terminology + redundancy pruning.\n\nNote: if the main issue is structural redundancy from section accumulation, push the change upstream to `sections/` and use `paragraph-curator` before merge. `draft-polisher` should not be the primary place where you decide which paragraphs to keep.\n\n\n\n## Role cards (use explicitly)\n\n### Style Harmonizer (editor)\n\nMission: remove generator voice and make prose read like one author wrote it.\n\nDo:\n- Delete narration openers and slide navigation; replace with argument bridges.\n- Vary rhythm; remove repeated template stems.\n- Collapse repeated disclaimers into one front-matter methodology paragraph.\n\nAvoid:\n- Adding or removing citation keys.\n- Moving citations across subsections.\n\n### Evidence Contract Guard (skeptic)\n\nMission: prevent polishing from inflating claims beyond evidence.\n\nDo:\n- Keep quantitative statements scoped (task/metric/constraint) or weaken them.\n- Treat missing evidence as a failure signal; route upstream rather than rewriting around gaps.\n\nAvoid:\n- Overconfident language when evidence is abstract-only.\n\n\n## Role prompt: Style Harmonizer (editor expert)\n\n```text\nYou are the style and coherence editor for a technical survey.\n\nYour goal is to make the draft read like one careful author wrote it, without changing the evidence contract.\n\nHard constraints:\n- do not add/remove citation keys\n- do not move citations across ### subsections\n- do not strengthen claims beyond what existing citations support\n\nHigh-leverage edits:\n- delete generator voice (This subsection..., Next we move..., We now turn...)\n- replace navigation with argument bridges (content-bearing handoffs)\n- collapse repeated disclaimers into one methodology paragraph in front matter\n- keep quantitative statements well-scoped (task/metric/constraint in the same sentence)\n\nWorking style:\n- rewrite sentences so they carry content, not process\n- vary rhythm, but avoid “template stems” repeating across H3s\n```\n\n## Inputs\n\n- `output/DRAFT.md`\n- Optional context (read-only; helps avoid “polish drift”):\n  - `outline/outline.yml`\n  - `outline/subsection_briefs.jsonl`\n  - `outline/evidence_drafts.jsonl`\n  - `citations/ref.bib`\n\n## Outputs\n\n- `output/DRAFT.md` (in-place refinement)\n- `output/citation_anchors.prepolish.jsonl` (baseline, generated on first run by the script)\n\n## Non-negotiables (hard rules)\n\n1) **Citation keys are immutable**\n- Do not add new `[@BibKey]` keys.\n- Do not delete citation markers.\n- If `citations/ref.bib` exists, do not introduce any key that is not defined there.\n\n2) **Citation anchoring is immutable**\n- Do not move citations across `###` subsections.\n- If you must restructure across subsections, stop and push the change upstream (outline/briefs/evidence), then regenerate.\n\n3) **No evidence inflation**\n- If a sentence sounds stronger than the evidence level (abstract-only), rewrite it into a qualified statement.\n- When in doubt, check the subsection’s evidence pack in `outline/evidence_drafts.jsonl` and keep claims aligned to snippets.\n\n4) **Citation shape normalization**\n- Merge adjacent citation blocks in the same sentence (avoid `[@a] [@b]`).\n- Deduplicate keys inside one block (avoid `[@a; @a]`).\n- Avoid tail-only citation dumps: keep some citations in the claim sentence itself (mid-sentence), not only paragraph end.\n\n5) **Quantitative claim hygiene**\n- If you keep a number, ensure the sentence also states (without guessing): task type + metric definition + relevant constraint (budget/cost/tool access), and the citation is embedded in that sentence.\n- Avoid ambiguous model naming (e.g., “GPT-5”) unless the cited paper uses that exact label; otherwise use the paper’s naming or a neutral description.\n\n6) **No pipeline voice**\n- Remove scaffolding phrases like:\n  - “We use the following working claim …”\n  - “The main axes we track are …”\n  - “abstracts are treated as verification targets …”\n  - “Method note (evidence policy): …” (avoid labels; rewrite as plain survey methodology)\n  - “this run is …” (rewrite as survey methodology: “This survey is …”)\n  - “Scope and definitions / Design space / Evaluation practice …”\n  - “Next, we move from …”\n  - “We now turn to …”\n  - “From <X> to <Y>, ...” (title narration; rewrite as an argument bridge)\n  - “In the next section/subsection …”\n  - “Therefore/As a result, survey synthesis/comparisons should …” (rewrite as literature-facing observation)\n- Also remove generator-like thesis openers that read like outline narration:\n  - “This subsection surveys …”\n  - “This subsection argues …”\n\n## Three passes (recommended)\n\n### Pass 1 — Subsection polish (structure + de-template)\n\nBest-of-2 micro-polish (recommended):\n- For any sentence/paragraph you touch, draft 2 candidate rewrites, then keep the better one.\n- Choose with a simple rubric: move clarity, no template stem, citations stay anchored, and citation shape stays reader-facing (no adjacent cite blocks / dup keys).\n- Do not keep both candidates. Pick one and move on (the goal is convergence, not endless rewriting).\n\nRole split:\n- **Editor**: rewrite sentences for clarity and flow.\n- **Skeptic**: deletes any generic/template sentence.\n\nTargets:\n- Each H3 reads like: tension → contrast → evidence → limitation.\n- Remove repeated “disclaimer paragraphs”; keep evidence-policy in **one** place (prefer a single paragraph in Introduction or Related Work phrased as survey methodology, not as pipeline/execution logs).\n- Use `outline/outline.yml` (if present) to avoid heading drift during edits.\n- If present, use `outline/subsection_briefs.jsonl` to keep each H3’s scope/RQ consistent while improving flow.\n- Do a quick “pattern sweep” (semantic, not mechanical):\n   - delete outline narration: `This subsection ...`, `In this subsection ...`\n   - delete slide navigation: `Next, we move from ...`, `We now turn to ...`, `In the next section ...`\n   - delete title narration: `From <X> to <Y>, ...`\n   - replace with: content claims + argument bridges + organization sentences (no new facts/citations)\n- If `citation-injector` was used, smooth any budget-injection sentences so they read paper-like:\n  - Keep the citation keys unchanged.\n  - Avoid list-injection stems (e.g., “A few representative references include …”, “Notable lines of work include …”, “Concrete examples ... include ...”).\n  - Prefer integrating the added citations into an existing argument sentence, or rewrite as a short parenthetical `e.g., ...` clause tied to the subsection’s lens (no new facts).\n  - Vary phrasing; avoid repeating the same opener stem across many H3s.\n- Tone: keep it calm and academic; remove hype words and repeated opener labels (e.g., literal `Key takeaway:` across many H3s).\n- **Reduce repeated synthesis stems** (e.g., many paragraphs starting with `Taken together, ...`); vary synthesis phrasing and keep it content-bearing.\n  - Treat repeated \"Taken together,\" as a generator-voice smell. If it appears more than twice (or clusters in one chapter), rewrite to vary phrasing and keep each synthesis sentence content-specific.\n  - Vary synthesis openings: \"In summary,\" \"Across these studies,\" \"The pattern that emerges,\" \"A key insight,\" \"Collectively,\" \"The evidence suggests,\" or directly state the conclusion without a synthesis marker.\n  - Each synthesis opening should be content-specific, not a template label.\n\nRewrite recipe for subsection openers (paper voice, no new facts):\n- Delete: `This subsection surveys/argues...` / `In this subsection, we...`\n- Replace with a compact opener that does 2–3 of these (no labels; vary across subsections):\n  - **Content claim**: the subsection-specific tension/trade-off (optionally with 1–2 embedded citations)\n  - **Why it matters**: link the claim to evaluation/engineering constraints (benchmark/protocol/cost/tool access)\n  - **Preview**: what you will contrast next and on what lens (A vs B; then evaluation anchors; then limitations)\n- Example skeletons (paraphrase; don’t reuse verbatim):\n  - Tension-first: `A central tension is ...; ...; we contrast ...`\n  - Decision-first: `For builders, the crux is ...; ...`\n  - Lens-first: `Seen through the lens of ..., ...`\n\n### Pass 2 — Terminology normalization\n\nRole split:\n- **Taxonomist**: chooses canonical terms and synonym policy.\n- **Integrator**: applies consistent replacements across the draft.\n\nTargets:\n- One concept = one name across sections.\n- Headings, tables, and prose use the same canonical terms.\n\n### Pass 3 — Redundancy pruning (global repetition)\n\nRole split:\n- **Compressor**: collapses repeated boilerplate.\n- **Narrative keeper**: ensures removing repetition does not break the argument chain.\n\nTargets:\n- Cross-section repeated intros/outros are removed.\n- Only subsection-specific content remains inside subsections.\n\n## Script\n\n### Quick Start\n\n- `python .codex/skills/draft-polisher/scripts/run.py --help`\n- `python .codex/skills/draft-polisher/scripts/run.py --workspace workspaces/<ws>`\n\n### All Options\n\n- `--workspace <dir>`: workspace root\n- `--unit-id <U###>`: unit id (optional; for logs)\n- `--inputs <semicolon-separated>`: override inputs (rare; prefer defaults)\n- `--outputs <semicolon-separated>`: override outputs (rare; prefer defaults)\n- `--checkpoint <C#>`: checkpoint id (optional; for logs)\n\n### Examples\n\n- First polish pass (creates anchoring baseline `output/citation_anchors.prepolish.jsonl`):\n  - `python .codex/skills/draft-polisher/scripts/run.py --workspace workspaces/<ws>`\n\n- Reset the anchoring baseline (only if you intentionally accept citation drift):\n  - Delete `output/citation_anchors.prepolish.jsonl`, then rerun the polisher.\n\n## Acceptance checklist\n\n- [ ] No `TODO/TBD/FIXME/(placeholder)`.\n- [ ] No `…` or `...` truncation.\n- [ ] No repeated boilerplate sentence across many subsections.\n- [ ] Citation anchoring passes (no cross-subsection drift).\n- [ ] Each H3 has at least one cross-paper synthesis paragraph (>=2 citations).\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Issue: polishing causes citation drift across subsections\n\n**Fix**:\n- Keep citations inside the same `###` subsection; if restructuring is intentional, delete `output/citation_anchors.prepolish.jsonl` and regenerate a new baseline.\n\n### Issue: draft polishing is requested before writing approval\n\n**Fix**:\n- Record the relevant approval in `DECISIONS.md` (typically `Approve C2`) before doing prose-level edits.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:38:29.510Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Language Agents needing advanced text refinement and editing capabilities to ensure evidence-based writing.","zh":"非常适合需要高级文本精炼和编辑功能的语言代理，以确保基于证据的写作。","ja":"高度なテキストの洗練と編集機能を必要とする言語エージェントに最適で、エビデンスベースのライティングを保証する。","ko":"고급 텍스트 정련 및 편집 기능이 필요한 언어 에이전트에게 적합하여 증거 기반 작성 보장을 제공한다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Lenguaje que necesitan capacidades de refinamiento y edición de texto avanzadas para garantizar una escritura basada en evidencia.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Langage ayant besoin de capacités de raffinement et d''édition de texte avancées pour assurer une rédaction basée sur des preuves.","de":"Perfekt für Sprachagenten, die erweiterte Textverfeinerungs- und Bearbeitungsfunktionen benötigen, um evidencebasiertes Schreiben zu gewährleisten.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Linguagem que precisam de recursos avançados de refinamento e edição de texto para garantir escrita baseada em evidências.","ru":"Идеально для языковых агентов, которым требуются передовые возможности доработки и редактирования текста для обеспечения доказательной письменной речи.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل اللغوي التي تحتاج إلى إمكانيات متقدمة لتنقية النص وتحريره لضمان الكتابة القائمة على الأدلة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to perform audit-style editing, refining drafts into readable survey prose without breaking the evidence contract, utilizing techniques such as de-templating, coherence enhancement, terminology standardization, and redundancy pruning through structured intermediate artifacts.","zh":"赋予代理商进行审计式编辑的能力，将草稿精炼为可读的调查散文，而不违反证据合同，利用诸如去模板化、连贯性增强、术语标准化和结构化中间文物的冗余修剪等技术。","ja":"エージェントに監査スタイルの編集を実行する能力を与え、草稿を証拠契約を破壊せずに読みやすい調査散文に洗練させることができる。デテンプレート化、連貫性の強化、用語の標準化、構造化された中間アーティファクトによる冗長性のカットなどの技術を利用する。","ko":"에이전트가 감사 스타일의 편집을 수행할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 초안을 증거 계약을 깨지 않고 읽기 쉬운 조사散文으로 정련할 수 있다. 템플릿 제거, 일관성 향상, 용어 표준화, 구조화된 중간 아티팩트를 통한 중복성 절단 등의 기술을 활용한다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a realizar ediciones de estilo de auditoría, perfeccionando borradores en prosa de encuesta legible sin romper el contrato de evidencia, utilizando técnicas como des-plantillado, mejora de coherencia, estandarización de terminología y poda de redundancia a través de artefactos intermedios estructurados.","fr":"Habilite les agents à effectuer des éditions de style d''audit, affinant les brouillons en prose de sondage lisible sans rompre le contrat de preuve, en utilisant des techniques telles que le dé-templating, l''amélioration de la cohérence, la normalisation de la terminologie et l''élagage des redondances via des artefacts intermédiaires structurés.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Audit-Stil-Edits durchzuführen, Entwürfe in lesbare Umfrage-Prosa zu verfeinern, ohne den Evidenzvertrag zu brechen, unter Verwendung von Techniken wie Entschablonisierung, Kohärenzverbesserung, Terminologiestandardisierung und Redundanzbeschneidung durch strukturierte Zwischenartefakte.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a realizar edição no estilo de auditoria, refinando rascunhos em prosa de inquérito legível sem violar o contrato de evidências, utilizando técnicas como desmodelagem, melhoria da coerência, padronização de terminologia e poda de redundâncias por meio de artefatos intermediários estruturados.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять редактирование в стиле аудита, дорабатывая черновики в читаемую прозу опроса без нарушения договора о доказательствах, используя такие техники, как удаление шаблонов, повышение связности, стандартизация терминологии и удаление избыточности посредством структурированных промежуточных артефактов.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من أداء تحرير على طريقة التدقيق، وتنقيح المسودات إلى نصوص استطلاعية قابلة للقراءة دون كسر عقد الأدلة، باستخدام تقنيات مثل إزالة القوالب، وتحسين الانسجام، وتنمية المصطلحات، وقص الفائض من خلال هياكل وسيطة منظمة."},"useCases":{"en":["Refining first-pass drafts into publishable content","Ensuring consistency and coherence in long-form texts","Pruning redundant information to enhance readability"],"zh":["将初步草稿精炼为可发布的内容","确保长篇文本的一致性和连贯性","修剪冗余信息以提高可读性"],"ja":["初期草稿を公開可能なコンテンツに洗練する","長文の的一貫性と連貫性を確保する","冗長な情報をカットして可読性を高める"],"ko":["초기 초안을 게시 가능한 콘텐츠로 정련한다","장문 텍스트의 일관성과 일관성을 보장한다","중복된 정보를 修剪하여 가독성을 향상한다"],"es":["Perfeccionar los borradores de primera pasada en contenido publicable","Garantizar la coherencia y la cohesión en textos de largo formato","Podar la información redundante para mejorar la legibilidad"],"fr":["Affiner les brouillons de première passe en contenu publiable","Assurer la cohérence et la cohésion dans les textes de long format","Élaguer les informations redondantes pour améliorer la lisibilité"],"de":["Erste-Entwürfe in veröffentlichbares Inhaltsmaterial verfeinern","Konsistenz und Kohärenz in Langtexten sicherstellen","Redundante Informationen beschneiden, um die Lesbarkeit zu verbessern"],"pt":["Refinamento de rascunhos iniciais em conteúdo publicável","Garantia de consistência e coerência em textos longos","Poda de informações redundantes para melhorar a legibilidade"],"ru":["Уточнение первых черновиков в публикуемый контент","Обеспечение согласованности и связности в длинных текстах","Обрезка избыточной информации для улучшения читаемости"],"ar":["تنقيح المسودات الأولية إلى محتوى منشور","ضمان الاتساق والانسجام في النصوص الطويلة","قص المعلومات الزائدة لتحسين القابلية للقراءة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Not intended for structural changes, use ''paragraph-curator'' for section-level edits","Requires input drafts with clear evidence contracts"],"zh":["不适用于结构性变化，请使用''段落策展人''进行节级编辑","需要具有明确证据合同的输入草稿"],"ja":["構造的な変更には適さない。節レベルの編集には''パラグラフキュレーター''を使用してください","明確な証拠契約を持つ入力草稿が必要"],"ko":["구조적인 변경에는 적합하지 않음. 절 수준의 편집에는 ''段落 큐레이터''를 사용하십시오","명확한 증거 계약을 갖춘 입력 초안이 필요"],"es":["No está destinado a cambios estructurales, use ''paragraph-curator'' para ediciones a nivel de sección","Requiere borradores de entrada con contratos de evidencia claros"],"fr":["N''est pas destiné aux modifications structurelles, utilisez ''paragraph-curator'' pour les éditions au niveau de la section","Nécessite des brouillons d''entrée avec des contrats de preuve clairs"],"de":["Ist nicht für strukturelle Änderungen bestimmt, verwenden Sie ''paragraph-curator'' für Abschnitts-Edits","Benötigt Eingabeborratore mit klaren Evidenzverträgen"],"pt":["Não destinado a alterações estruturais, use ''paragraph-curator'' para edições de nível de seção","Requer rascunhos de entrada com contratos de evidências claros"],"ru":["Не предназначен для структурных изменений, используйте ''paragraph-curator'' для редактирования на уровне раздела","Требует входных черновиков с ясными договорами о доказательствах"],"ar":["غير مخصص للتغييرات الهيكلية، استخدم ''paragraph-curator'' لتعديلات مستوى الفقرة","يتطلب مسودات إدخال ذات عقود أدلة واضحة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('kreuzberg-dev/html-to-markdown/typescript-bindings-patterns', 'community', 'kreuzberg-dev', 'html-to-markdown', 'kreuzberg-dev/html-to-markdown', 'typescript-bindings-patterns', 0, 0, 30, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z', '2026-02-18T08:38:32.232Z', NULL, '{"id":"kreuzberg-dev/html-to-markdown/typescript-bindings-patterns","name":"typescript-bindings-patterns","description":{"zh":"TypeScript 绑定模式为 Kreuzberg 文档智能引擎的 Rust 核心提供了高性能的绑定解决方案","ja":"TypeScript バインディング パターンは、Kreuzberg ドキュメント インテリジェンス エンジンの Rust コアに高パフォーマンスなバインディング ソリューションを提供します","ko":"타입스크립트 바인딩 패턴은 Kreuzberg 문서 지능 엔진의 Rust 핵심을 위한 고성능 바인딩 솔루션을 제공합니다","es":"Los patrones de enlaces de TypeScript para Rust permiten una integración eficiente entre los dos lenguajes","fr":"Les modèles de liaison TypeScript pour Rust permettent une intégration efficace entre les deux langages","de":"Die TypeScript-Bindungsmuster für Rust ermöglichen eine effiziente Integration zwischen den beiden Sprachen","pt":"Os padrões de ligação TypeScript permitem uma integração transparente com o núcleo Rust, proporcionando uma experiência de desenvolvimento eficiente","ru":"Шаблоны привязки TypeScript позволяют прозрачно интегрироваться с ядром Rust, обеспечивая эффективный опыт разработки","ar":"نماذج ربط TypeScript تسمح بالتكامل الشفاف مع النواة روست، وتوفر تجربة تطوير فعالة","en":"High performance and CommonMark compliant HTML to Markdown converter. Maintained by the Kreuzberg team. Kreuzberg is a fast, polyglot document intelligence engine with a Rust core. It extracts structured data from 56+ document formats using streaming parsers and built-in OCR."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"TypeScript 绑定模式","ja":"TypeScript バインディング パターン","ko":"타입스크립트 바인딩 패턴","es":"Patrones de enlaces de TypeScript para Rust","fr":"Modèles de liaison TypeScript pour Rust","de":"TypeScript-Bindungsmuster für Rust","pt":"Padrões de Ligação TypeScript para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Шаблоны привязки TypeScript для разработчиков","ar":"نماذج ربط TypeScript للمطورين","en":"typescript-bindings-patterns"},"description":{"zh":"TypeScript 绑定模式为 Kreuzberg 文档智能引擎的 Rust 核心提供了高性能的绑定解决方案","ja":"TypeScript バインディング パターンは、Kreuzberg ドキュメント インテリジェンス エンジンの Rust コアに高パフォーマンスなバインディング ソリューションを提供します","ko":"타입스크립트 바인딩 패턴은 Kreuzberg 문서 지능 엔진의 Rust 핵심을 위한 고성능 바인딩 솔루션을 제공합니다","es":"Los patrones de enlaces de TypeScript para Rust permiten una integración eficiente entre los dos lenguajes","fr":"Les modèles de liaison TypeScript pour Rust permettent une intégration efficace entre les deux langages","de":"Die TypeScript-Bindungsmuster für Rust ermöglichen eine effiziente Integration zwischen den beiden Sprachen","pt":"Os padrões de ligação TypeScript permitem uma integração transparente com o núcleo Rust, proporcionando uma experiência de desenvolvimento eficiente","ru":"Шаблоны привязки TypeScript позволяют прозрачно интегрироваться с ядром Rust, обеспечивая эффективный опыт разработки","ar":"نماذج ربط TypeScript تسمح بالتكامل الشفاف مع النواة روست، وتوفر تجربة تطوير فعالة","en":"High performance and CommonMark compliant HTML to Markdown converter. Maintained by the Kreuzberg team. Kreuzberg is a fast, polyglot document intelligence e..."},"definition":{"en":"High performance and CommonMark compliant HTML to Markdown converter. Maintained by the Kreuzberg team. Kreuzberg is a fast, polyglot document intelligence engine with a Rust core. It extracts structured data from 56+ document formats using streaming parsers and built-in OCR."},"features":{"zh":["高性能的 TypeScript 绑定","支持 Kreuzberg 文档智能引擎的 Rust 核心","使用 NAPI-RS 桥接和 TypeScript SDK 包","提供类型定义和 JSDoc 文档","支持 pnpm 安装、构建、测试和 lint"],"ja":["高パフォーマンスな TypeScript バインディング","Kreuzberg ドキュメント インテリジェンス エンジンの Rust コアをサポート","NAPI-RS ブリッジと TypeScript SDK パッケージを使用","型定義と JSDoc ドキュメントを提供","pnpm インストール、ビルド、テスト、lint をサポート"],"ko":["고성능의 타입스크립트 바인딩","Kreuzberg 문서 지능 엔진의 Rust 핵심을 지원","NAPI-RS 브리지와 타입스크립트 SDK 패키지를 사용","타입 정의와 JSDoc 문서를 제공","pnpm 설치, 빌드, 테스트, lint를 지원"],"es":["Integración de TypeScript con Rust","Mejora del rendimiento de la aplicación","Uso de NAPI-RS para la comunicación entre lenguajes","Creación de SDK de TypeScript para Rust","Generación de definiciones de tipo y documentación JSDoc"],"fr":["Intégration de TypeScript avec Rust","Amélioration des performances de l''application","Utilisation de NAPI-RS pour la communication entre langages","Création d''un SDK TypeScript pour Rust","Génération de définitions de type et de documentation JSDoc"],"de":["Integration von TypeScript mit Rust","Leistungsverbesserung der Anwendung","Verwendung von NAPI-RS für die Kommunikation zwischen Sprachen","Erstellung eines TypeScript-SDK für Rust","Generierung von Typdefinitionen und JSDoc-Dokumentation"],"pt":["Integração com NAPI-RS","API idiomática para TypeScript","Definições de tipo para melhor suporte","Documentação JSDoc para exports","Suporte a streaming parsers e OCR"],"ru":["Интеграция с NAPI-RS","Идиоматический API для TypeScript","Определения типов для лучшей поддержки","Документация JSDoc для экспортов","Поддержка потоковых парсеров и OCR"],"ar":["التكامل مع NAPI-RS","واجهة برمجة تطبيقات معيارية لTypeScript","تعريفات النوع لافضل دعم","وثائق JSDoc للتصدير","دعم معالجات الفيديو و OCR"]},"keywords":{"zh":["TypeScript 绑定","Kreuzberg 文档智能引擎","Rust 核心","NAPI-RS","TypeScript SDK","高性能绑定","文档智能","Rust","TypeScript"],"ja":["TypeScript バインディング","Kreuzberg ドキュメント インテリジェンス エンジン","Rust コア","NAPI-RS","TypeScript SDK","高パフォーマンス バインディング","ドキュメント インテリジェンス","Rust","TypeScript"],"ko":["타입스크립트 바인딩","Kreuzberg 문서 지능 엔진","Rust 핵심","NAPI-RS","타입스크립트 SDK","고성능 바인딩","문서 지능","Rust","타입스크립트"],"es":["TypeScript","Rust","NAPI-RS","bindings","patrones de enlace","integración de lenguajes","mejora del rendimiento","desarrollo de aplicaciones"],"fr":["TypeScript","Rust","NAPI-RS","liaisons","modèles de liaison","intégration de langages","amélioration des performances","développement d''applications"],"de":["TypeScript","Rust","NAPI-RS","Bindungen","Bindungsmuster","Sprachintegration","Leistungsverbesserung","Anwendungsentwicklung"],"pt":["TypeScript","Rust","NAPI-RS","Desenvolvimento de software","Integração de linguagens","Programação de sistemas","TypeScript bindings","Rust core","Desenvolvedores"],"ru":["TypeScript","Rust","NAPI-RS","Разработка программного обеспечения","Интеграция языков","Программирование систем","Привязки TypeScript","Ядро Rust","Разработчики"],"ar":["TypeScript","روست","NAPI-RS","تطوير البرمجيات","التكامل اللغوي","برمجة الأنظمة","ربطات TypeScript","النواة روست","المطورون"]}},"owner":"kreuzberg-dev","repo":"html-to-markdown","repoPath":"kreuzberg-dev/html-to-markdown","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"typescript-bindings-patterns","description":"","bodyPreview":"______________________________________________________________________\n\n## priority: critical\n\n# TypeScript Bindings Patterns\n\n**Role**: TypeScript bindings for Rust core. Work on NAPI-RS bridge and TypeScript SDK packages.\n\n**Scope**: NAPI-RS FFI, TypeScript-idiomatic API, type definitions, JSDoc for all exports with @param/@returns/@example.\n\n**Commands**: pnpm install/build/test/lint.\n\n**Critical**: Core logic lives in Rust. TypeScript only for bindings/wrappers. If core logic needed, coordin","body":"______________________________________________________________________\n\n## priority: critical\n\n# TypeScript Bindings Patterns\n\n**Role**: TypeScript bindings for Rust core. Work on NAPI-RS bridge and TypeScript SDK packages.\n\n**Scope**: NAPI-RS FFI, TypeScript-idiomatic API, type definitions, JSDoc for all exports with @param/@returns/@example.\n\n**Commands**: pnpm install/build/test/lint.\n\n**Critical**: Core logic lives in Rust. TypeScript only for bindings/wrappers. If core logic needed, coordinate with Rust team.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:38:32.232Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, or Claude Code that require seamless interaction between TypeScript and Rust for high-performance document processing.","zh":"非常适合像Cursor、Windsurf或Claude Code这样的AI代理，它们需要TypeScript和Rust之间的无缝交互以进行高性能文档处理。","ja":"TypeScriptとRustのシームレスな相互作用を必要とするCursor、Windsurf、またはClaude CodeのようなAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"커서, 윈드서핑 또는 클로드 코드와 같은 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 이러한 에이전트는 고성능 문서 처리를 위해 TypeScript와 Rust 간의 무결점 상호 작용을 필요로 합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf o Claude Code que requieren una interacción sin problemas entre TypeScript y Rust para el procesamiento de documentos de alto rendimiento.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code qui nécessitent une interaction transparente entre TypeScript et Rust pour le traitement de documents haute performance.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Cursor, Windsurf oder Claude Code, die eine nahtlose Interaktion zwischen TypeScript und Rust für die Verarbeitung von Dokumenten mit hoher Leistung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf ou Claude Code que exigem interação perfeita entre TypeScript e Rust para processamento de documentos de alto desempenho.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf или Claude Code, которые требуют бесшовного взаимодействия между TypeScript и Rust для высокопроизводительной обработки документов.","ar":"مثالية لعمليات الوكيل الذكي مثل Cursor و Windsurf أو Claude Code التي تتطلب تفاعلاً سلسًا بين TypeScript و Rust لمعالجة المستندات عالية الأداء."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage the Kreuzberg document intelligence engine''s Rust core through TypeScript bindings, utilizing NAPI-RS for efficient FFI and generating type definitions with JSDoc documentation for clear API usage, including @param, @returns, and @example tags.","zh":"通过使用NAPI-RS进行高效的FFI，并使用JSDoc文档生成类型定义，包括@param、@returns和@example标签，赋予代理使用Kreuzberg文档智能引擎的Rust核心并通过TypeScript绑定进行利用的能力。","ja":"NAPI-RSを使用した効率的なFFIと、@param、@returns、@exampleタグを含むJSDocドキュメントを使用した型定義の生成により、KreuzbergドキュメントインテリジェンスエンジンのRustコアをTypeScriptバインディングを介して利用できるようにエージェントに権限を与えます。","ko":"NAPI-RS를 사용한 효율적인 FFI와 @param, @returns 및 @example 태그를 포함한 JSDoc 문서를 사용한 형식 정의 생성으로 Kreuzberg 문서 지능 엔진의 Rust 코어를 TypeScript 바인딩을 통해 활용할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar el motor de inteligencia de documentos Kreuzberg con núcleo Rust a través de enlaces TypeScript, utilizando NAPI-RS para FFI eficiente y generando definiciones de tipo con documentación JSDoc para una clara utilización de la API, incluyendo etiquetas @param, @returns y @example.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter le moteur d''intelligence de documents Kreuzberg à base Rust via des liaisons TypeScript, en utilisant NAPI-RS pour un FFI efficace et en générant des définitions de type avec une documentation JSDoc pour une utilisation claire de l''API, y compris les balises @param, @returns et @example.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, den Kreuzberg-Dokumenten-Intelligenz-Motor mit Rust-Kern über TypeScript-Bindings zu nutzen, indem NAPI-RS für effizientes FFI verwendet wird und Typdefinitionen mit JSDoc-Dokumentation für eine klare API-Nutzung generiert werden, einschließlich @param-, @returns- und @example-Tags.","pt":"Habilita agentes a aproveitarem o motor de inteligência de documentos Kreuzberg com core em Rust por meio de vinculações TypeScript, utilizando NAPI-RS para FFI eficiente e gerando definições de tipo com documentação JSDoc para uso de API claro, incluindo tags @param, @returns e @example.","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать движок интеллекта документов Kreuzberg с ядром на Rust через привязки TypeScript, используя NAPI-RS для эффективного FFI и генерируя определения типов с документацией JSDoc для ясного использования API, включая теги @param, @returns и @example.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من الاستفادة من محرك ذكاء المستندات Kreuzberg ذي النواة الرستية من خلال ربطات TypeScript، وذلك باستخدام NAPI-RS للواجهة الخارجية الفعالة وتوليد تعريفات النوع مع توثيق JSDoc لاستخدام واجهة برمجة التطبيقات الواضح، بما في ذلك علامات @param و @returns و @example."},"useCases":{"en":["Developing high-performance HTML to Markdown converters with CommonMark compliance","Creating TypeScript-idiomatic APIs for document intelligence tasks","Building and testing TypeScript SDK packages with pnpm for streamlined development"],"zh":["开发符合CommonMark标准的高性能HTML到Markdown转换器","为文档智能任务创建TypeScript风格的API","使用pnpm进行流畅开发的TypeScript SDK包的构建和测试"],"ja":["CommonMark準拠の高性能HTMLからMarkdownへのコンバータを開発する","ドキュメントインテリジェンスタスク用のTypeScriptスタイルのAPIを作成する","スムーズな開発のためのpnpmを使用したTypeScript SDKパッケージの構築とテスト"],"ko":["공통 마크 규약을 준수하는 고성능 HTML에서 마크다운으로의 변환기를 개발합니다.","문서 지능 작업을 위한 TypeScript 스타일의 API를 생성합니다.","pnpm을 사용하여 원활한 개발을 위한 TypeScript SDK 패키지의 구축 및 테스트"],"es":["Desarrollar convertidores de HTML a Markdown de alto rendimiento con cumplimiento de CommonMark","Crear APIs idiomáticas de TypeScript para tareas de inteligencia de documentos","Crear y probar paquetes de SDK de TypeScript con pnpm para un desarrollo fluido"],"fr":["Développer des convertisseurs HTML vers Markdown haute performance avec conformité CommonMark","Créer des API idiomatiques TypeScript pour les tâches d''intelligence de documents","Construire et tester des packages de SDK TypeScript avec pnpm pour un développement fluide"],"de":["Entwicklung von Hochleistungs-HTML-zu-Markdown-Konvertern mit CommonMark-Konformität","Erstellen von typsicheren TypeScript-APIs für Dokumenten-Intelligenzaufgaben","Erstellen und Testen von TypeScript-SDK-Paketen mit pnpm für ein reibungsloses Entwicklungserlebnis"],"pt":["Desenvolver conversores HTML para Markdown de alto desempenho com conformidade CommonMark","Criar APIs idiomáticas TypeScript para tarefas de inteligência de documentos","Construir e testar pacotes SDK TypeScript com pnpm para desenvolvimento simplificado"],"ru":["Разработка высокопроизводительных конвертеров HTML в Markdown с соблюдением CommonMark","Создание идiomатических API TypeScript для задач интеллекта документов","Создание и тестирование пакетов SDK TypeScript с pnpm для упрощенного развития"],"ar":["تطوير محولات HTML إلى Markdown عالية الأداء مع امتثال CommonMark","إنشاء واجهات برمجة التطبيقات المتماثلة مع TypeScript لأعمال ذكاء المستندات","بناء وتجريب حزم SDK TypeScript مع pnpm من أجل التطوير المبسّط"]},"limitations":{"en":["Core logic must reside in Rust, with TypeScript used only for bindings and wrappers","Requires coordination for core logic modifications"],"zh":["核心逻辑必须居住在Rust中，仅使用TypeScript进行绑定和包装","需要协调核心逻辑的修改"],"ja":["コアロジックはRustに住まなければならず、TypeScriptはバインディングとラッパーのみに使用される","コアロジックの変更に調整が必要"],"ko":["코어 로직은 러스트에만 존재해야 하며, TypeScript는 바인딩과 래퍼에만 사용됩니다.","코어 로직의 수정에는 조정이 필요합니다."],"es":["La lógica central debe residir en Rust, con TypeScript utilizado solo para enlaces y envolturas","Requiere coordinación para modificaciones de la lógica central"],"fr":["La logique centrale doit résider dans Rust, avec TypeScript utilisé uniquement pour les liaisons et les enveloppes","Nécessite une coordination pour les modifications de la logique centrale"],"de":["Die Kernlogik muss in Rust residieren, wobei TypeScript nur für Bindings und Wrapper verwendet wird","Erfordert Koordination für Änderungen an der Kernlogik"],"pt":["A lógica central deve residir em Rust, com TypeScript usado apenas para vinculações e invólucros","Exige coordenação para modificações da lógica central"],"ru":["Центральная логика должна находиться в Rust, с использованием TypeScript только для привязок и оберток","Требует координации для изменений центральной логики"],"ar":["يجب أن تقع المنطق المركزية في Rust، مع استخدام TypeScript فقط للربطات والغلاف","يتطلب تنسيقًا لتحديثات المنطق المركزية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":30}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('SidU/GoodDocs-Sample4/init-repo', 'community', 'SidU', 'GoodDocs-Sample4', 'SidU/GoodDocs-Sample4', 'init-repo', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z', '2026-02-18T08:38:53.310Z', NULL, '{"id":"SidU/GoodDocs-Sample4/init-repo","name":"init-repo","description":{"zh":"init-repo 技能用于初始化 GoodDocs Fork 并设置自定义文档类型。它会提示用户输入仓库名称、文档类型显示名称、文档类型键等信息","ja":"init-repo スキルは GoodDocs フォークを初期化し、カスタム ドキュメントの種類を設定するために使用されます。ユーザーはリポジトリ名、ドキュメントの種類の表示名、ドキュメントの種類キーの入力を求められます","ko":"init-repo 스킬은 GoodDocs Fork를 초기화하고 사용자 지정 문서 유형을 설정하는 데 사용됩니다. 사용자는 저장소 이름, 문서 유형 표시 이름, 문서 유형 키 등의 정보를 입력하도록 요청받습니다","es":"El skill init-repo permite a los desarrolladores inicializar un fork de GoodDocs con configuraciones personalizadas","fr":"Le skill init-repo permet aux développeurs d''initialiser un fork de GoodDocs avec des configurations personnalisées","de":"Das Skill init-repo ermöglicht es Entwicklern, einen Fork von GoodDocs mit benutzerdefinierten Einstellungen zu initialisieren","pt":"A habilidade init-repo inicializa um fork de GoodDocs com configurações personalizadas e tipo de documento. Ela cria um arquivo repo.config.json com as configurações fornecidas","ru":"Навык init-repo инициализирует форк GoodDocs с настраиваемыми параметрами и типом документа. Он создает файл repo.config.json с заданными настройками","ar":"تflater مهارة init-repo المستودع مع إعدادات مخصصة ونوع مستند. إنها تضع ملف repo.config.json مع الإعدادات المحددة","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"初始化仓库：init-repo 技能","ja":"リポジトリの初期化：init-repo スキル","ko":"저장소 초기화: init-repo 스킬","es":"Inicializa repo con init-repo","fr":"Initialiser un dépôt avec init-repo","de":"Repo initialisieren mit init-repo","pt":"Inicializar Repositório com init-repo","ru":"Инициализация репозитория с помощью init-repo","ar":"تflater المستودع باستخدام init-repo","en":"init-repo"},"description":{"zh":"init-repo 技能用于初始化 GoodDocs Fork 并设置自定义文档类型。它会提示用户输入仓库名称、文档类型显示名称、文档类型键等信息","ja":"init-repo スキルは GoodDocs フォークを初期化し、カスタム ドキュメントの種類を設定するために使用されます。ユーザーはリポジトリ名、ドキュメントの種類の表示名、ドキュメントの種類キーの入力を求められます","ko":"init-repo 스킬은 GoodDocs Fork를 초기화하고 사용자 지정 문서 유형을 설정하는 데 사용됩니다. 사용자는 저장소 이름, 문서 유형 표시 이름, 문서 유형 키 등의 정보를 입력하도록 요청받습니다","es":"El skill init-repo permite a los desarrolladores inicializar un fork de GoodDocs con configuraciones personalizadas","fr":"Le skill init-repo permet aux développeurs d''initialiser un fork de GoodDocs avec des configurations personnalisées","de":"Das Skill init-repo ermöglicht es Entwicklern, einen Fork von GoodDocs mit benutzerdefinierten Einstellungen zu initialisieren","pt":"A habilidade init-repo inicializa um fork de GoodDocs com configurações personalizadas e tipo de documento. Ela cria um arquivo repo.config.json com as confi...","ru":"Навык init-repo инициализирует форк GoodDocs с настраиваемыми параметрами и типом документа. Он создает файл repo.config.json с заданными настройками","ar":"تflater مهارة init-repo المستودع مع إعدادات مخصصة ونوع مستند. إنها تضع ملف repo.config.json مع الإعدادات المحددة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["初始化 GoodDocs Fork","设置自定义文档类型","提示用户输入仓库名称和文档类型信息","创建 repo.config.json 文件","设置默认所有者和创建时间"],"ja":["GoodDocs フォークの初期化","カスタム ドキュメントの種類の設定","ユーザーにリポジトリ名とドキュメントの種類の情報の入力を求める","repo.config.json ファイルの作成","デフォルト所有者と作成日の設定"],"ko":["GoodDocs Fork 초기화","사용자 지정 문서 유형 설정","사용자에게 저장소 이름과 문서 유형 정보 입력 요청","repo.config.json 파일 생성","기본 소유자 및 생성일 설정"],"es":["Inicializa un fork de GoodDocs","Configura el tipo de documento por defecto","Establece los propietarios predeterminados","Crea un archivo de configuración del repositorio","Permite la personalización del nombre del repositorio"],"fr":["Initialise un fork de GoodDocs","Configure le type de document par défaut","Définit les propriétaires par défaut","Crée un fichier de configuration du dépôt","Permet la personnalisation du nom du dépôt"],"de":["Initialisiert einen Fork von GoodDocs","Konfiguriert den Standard-Dokumententyp","Legt die Standard-Besitzer fest","Erstellt eine Repository-Konfigurationsdatei","Ermöglicht die Anpassung des Repository-Namens"],"pt":["Inicializa um fork de GoodDocs","Cria um arquivo repo.config.json","Permite configurações personalizadas","Suporta vários tipos de documentos","Aceita proprietários padrão","Define a data de criação do repositório"],"ru":["Инициализирует форк GoodDocs","Создает файл repo.config.json","Позволяет настраивать параметры","Поддерживает несколько типов документов","Принимает владельцев по умолчанию","Определяет дату создания репозитория"],"ar":["تflater المستودع","تضع ملف repo.config.json","تسمح بالإعدادات المخصصة","تدعم أنواع مستندات متعددة","تقبل المالكين الإفتراضيين","تحدد تاريخ إنشاء المستودع"]},"keywords":{"zh":["init-repo","GoodDocs","仓库初始化","文档类型","repo.config.json","默认所有者","创建时间"],"ja":["init-repo","GoodDocs","リポジトリの初期化","ドキュメントの種類","repo.config.json","デフォルト所有者","作成日"],"ko":["init-repo","GoodDocs","저장소 초기화","문서 유형","repo.config.json","기본 소유자","생성일"],"es":["init-repo","GoodDocs","inicializar repositorio","configuración de repositorio","desarrollo de software","herramientas de desarrollo","configuración de documento","propietarios de repositorio"],"fr":["init-repo","GoodDocs","initialiser dépôt","configuration de dépôt","développement de logiciels","outils de développement","configuration de document","propriétaires de dépôt"],"de":["init-repo","GoodDocs","Repository initialisieren","Repository-Konfiguration","Software-Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools","Dokumenten-Konfiguration","Repository-Besitzer"],"pt":["inicializar repositório","init-repo","GoodDocs","configurações personalizadas","tipo de documento","repo.config.json","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["инициализировать репозиторий","init-repo","GoodDocs","настраиваемые параметры","тип документа","repo.config.json","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["تflater المستودع","init-repo","GoodDocs","إعدادات مخصصة","نوع المستند","repo.config.json","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"SidU","repo":"GoodDocs-Sample4","repoPath":"SidU/GoodDocs-Sample4","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"init-repo","description":"Initialize a fork of GoodDocs with fork-specific defaults and a customized doc type.","bodyPreview":"# Skill: init-repo\n\n## Purpose\nInitialize a fork of GoodDocs with fork-specific defaults and a customized doc type.\n\n## Behavior\n1. Prompt the user for:\n   - `repoName`\n   - `docTypeDisplayName` (default: Design Docs)\n   - `docTypeKey` (default: design-docs)\n   - `docRoot` folder name under `docs/` (default derived from docTypeKey)\n   - `defaultOwners` (comma-separated)\n2. Create `repo.config.json` with:\n   - `repoName`, `defaultDocTypeKey`, `defaultOwners` (array), and `createdAt` (YYYY-MM-DD).","body":"# Skill: init-repo\n\n## Purpose\nInitialize a fork of GoodDocs with fork-specific defaults and a customized doc type.\n\n## Behavior\n1. Prompt the user for:\n   - `repoName`\n   - `docTypeDisplayName` (default: Design Docs)\n   - `docTypeKey` (default: design-docs)\n   - `docRoot` folder name under `docs/` (default derived from docTypeKey)\n   - `defaultOwners` (comma-separated)\n2. Create `repo.config.json` with:\n   - `repoName`, `defaultDocTypeKey`, `defaultOwners` (array), and `createdAt` (YYYY-MM-DD).\n3. Update `schema/doc_rules.json` so `docTypes[0]` matches the new doc type key, display name, and doc root.\n4. If `docs/example` exists and the chosen doc root differs, rename it and update links in `docs/README.md`.\n5. Run `python3 scripts/validate_docs.py` and fix issues before finishing.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:38:53.310Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring automated repository initialization with customized doc types and fork-specific defaults.","zh":"适用于需要自动化仓库初始化的开发代理，具有自定义文档类型和fork特定默认值。","ja":"自動化されたリポジトリ初期化が必要な開発エージェントに適しています。カスタムドキュメントタイプとフォーク固有のデフォルト値を備えています。","ko":"자동화된 저장소 초기화가 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 사용자 정의 문서 유형과 포크별 기본값을 제공합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren la inicialización automática del repositorio con tipos de documentos personalizados y valores predeterminados específicos de fork.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une initialisation automatique du référentiel avec des types de documents personnalisés et des valeurs par défaut spécifiques à la fourche.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine automatisierte Initialisierung des Repository mit benutzerdefinierten Dokumenttypen und fork-spezifischen Standardwerten erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que exigem inicialização automática de repositório com tipos de documentos personalizados e padrões específicos de bifurcação.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, требующих автоматизированной инициализации репозитория с настраиваемыми типами документов и настройками по умолчанию, специфичными для форка.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء النموزجيون الذين يتطلبون تهيئة مستودع автоматية مع أنواع وثائق مخصصة وافتراضيات محددة للفرع."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create repository configurations with customized doc types, utilizing JSON files like ''repo.config.json'', and specifying details such as ''repoName'', ''docTypeKey'', and ''defaultOwners'', all while managing folder structures under ''docs/'' with ease.","zh":"赋予代理创建具有自定义文档类型的仓库配置的能力，利用如''repo.config.json''的JSON文件，指定诸如''repoName''、''docTypeKey''和''defaultOwners''的详细信息，并轻松管理''docs/''下的文件夹结构。","ja":"エージェントがカスタムドキュメントタイプを備えたリポジトリ構成を作成できるようにします。''repo.config.json''などのJSONファイルを利用し、''repoName''、''docTypeKey''、''defaultOwners''などの詳細を指定し、''docs/''以下のフォルダ構造を簡単に管理します。","ko":"에이전트가 사용자 정의 문서 유형을 갖춘 저장소 구성 만들 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다. ''repo.config.json''과 같은 JSON 파일을 사용하여 ''repoName'', ''docTypeKey'', ''defaultOwners''와 같은 세부 정보를 지정하고 ''docs/''下的 폴더 구조를 쉽게 관리합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes crear configuraciones de repositorio con tipos de documentos personalizados, utilizando archivos JSON como ''repo.config.json'', y especificar detalles como ''repoName'', ''docTypeKey'' y ''defaultOwners'', todo mientras gestiona estructuras de carpetas bajo ''docs/'' con facilidad.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des configurations de référentiel avec des types de documents personnalisés, en utilisant des fichiers JSON tels que ''repo.config.json'', et en spécifiant des détails tels que ''repoName'', ''docTypeKey'' et ''defaultOwners'', le tout en gérant les structures de dossiers sous ''docs/'' avec facilité.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Repository-Konfigurationen mit benutzerdefinierten Dokumenttypen zu erstellen, indem JSON-Dateien wie ''repo.config.json'' verwendet werden, und Details wie ''repoName'', ''docTypeKey'' und ''defaultOwners'' anzugeben, während Ordnerstrukturen unter ''docs/'' leicht verwaltet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar configurações de repositório com tipos de documentos personalizados, utilizando arquivos JSON como ''repo.config.json'', e especificando detalhes como ''repoName'', ''docTypeKey'' e ''defaultOwners'', tudo isso enquanto gerencia estruturas de pastas em ''docs/'' com facilidade.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать конфигурации репозитория с настраиваемыми типами документов, используя файлы JSON, такие как ''repo.config.json'', и указывая детали, такие как ''repoName'', ''docTypeKey'' и ''defaultOwners'', все это при легком управлении структурами папок под ''docs/''.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية إنشاء تكوينات مستودع مع أنواع وثائق مخصصة، باستخدام ملفات JSON مثل ''repo.config.json''، وتحديد تفاصيل مثل ''repoName'' و ''docTypeKey'' و ''defaultOwners''، كل ذلك مع إدارة هيكل المجلدات في ''docs/'' بسهولة."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing repositories with customized documentation types","Automating the creation of ''repo.config.json'' files with specific metadata","Setting up default owners and document roots for new repositories"],"zh":["使用自定义文档类型初始化仓库","自动创建带有特定元数据的''repo.config.json''文件","为新仓库设置默认所有者和文档根目录"],"ja":["カスタムドキュメントタイプでリポジトリを初期化する","特定のメタデータを持つ''repo.config.json''ファイルを作成自動化する","新しいリポジトリのデフォルト所有者とドキュメントルートを設定する"],"ko":["사용자 정의 문서 유형으로 저장소를 초기화하는 경우","특정 메타데이터를 가진 ''repo.config.json'' 파일 생성 자동화","새로운 저장소에 대한 기본 소유자 및 문서 루트 설정"],"es":["Inicialización de repositorios con tipos de documentación personalizados","Automatización de la creación de archivos ''repo.config.json'' con metadatos específicos","Configuración de propietarios predeterminados y raíces de documentos para nuevos repositorios"],"fr":["Initialisation de référentiels avec des types de documentation personnalisés","Automatisation de la création de fichiers ''repo.config.json'' avec des métadonnées spécifiques","Configuration des propriétaires par défaut et des racines de documents pour les nouveaux référentiels"],"de":["Initialisierung von Repositorys mit benutzerdefinierten Dokumenttypen","Automatisierung der Erstellung von ''repo.config.json''-Dateien mit spezifischen Metadaten","Einrichtung von Standardbesitzern und Dokumentenwurzeln für neue Repositorys"],"pt":["Inicialização de repositórios com tipos de documentação personalizados","Automatização da criação de arquivos ''repo.config.json'' com metadados específicos","Configuração de proprietários padrão e raízes de documento para novos repositórios"],"ru":["Инициализация репозиториев с настраиваемыми типами документации","Автоматизация создания файлов ''repo.config.json'' с конкретными метаданными","Настройка владельцев по умолчанию и корней документов для новых репозиториев"],"ar":["تهيئة المستودعات مع أنواع وثائق مخصصة","الautomatización من إنشاء ملفات ''repo.config.json'' مع بيانات وصفية محددة","ضبط الملاك الافتراضيين وأصول الوثائق للمستودعات الجديدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires user input for repository name, doc type, and default owners","Limited to creating configurations for GoodDocs forks"],"zh":["需要用户输入仓库名称、文档类型和默认所有者","仅限于为GoodDocs分支创建配置"],"ja":["リポジトリ名、ドキュメントタイプ、デフォルト所有者のユーザー入力が必要","GoodDocsフォークの構成を作成することのみに限定される"],"ko":["저장소 이름, 문서 유형, 기본 소유자의 사용자 입력이 필요","GoodDocs 포크에 대한 구성 생성만으로 제한"],"es":["Requiere la entrada del usuario para el nombre del repositorio, el tipo de documento y los propietarios predeterminados","Limitado a la creación de configuraciones para bifurcaciones de GoodDocs"],"fr":["Nécessite une entrée utilisateur pour le nom du référentiel, le type de document et les propriétaires par défaut","Limité à la création de configurations pour les fourches de GoodDocs"],"de":["Benutzereingabe für Repository-Namen, Dokumenttyp und Standardbesitzer erforderlich","Begrenzt auf die Erstellung von Konfigurationen für GoodDocs-Forks"],"pt":["Exige entrada do usuário para o nome do repositório, tipo de documento e proprietários padrão","Limitado à criação de configurações para bifurcações do GoodDocs"],"ru":["Требует ввода пользователя для имени репозитория, типа документа и владельцев по умолчанию","Ограничен созданием конфигураций только для форков GoodDocs"],"ar":["يتطلب إدخال المستخدم لاسم المستودع ونوع الوثيقة والملّاك الافتراضيين","محدود بإنشاء التكوينات لمفروقات GoodDocs"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('alexey1312/swift-index/openspec-bulk-archive-change', 'community', 'alexey1312', 'swift-index', 'alexey1312/swift-index', 'openspec-bulk-archive-change', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z', '2026-02-18T08:38:55.092Z', NULL, '{"id":"alexey1312/swift-index/openspec-bulk-archive-change","name":"openspec-bulk-archive-change","description":{"zh":"openspec-bulk-archive-change 技术允许您批量存档更改，智能处理规格冲突","ja":"openspec-bulk-archive-change スキルは、複数の変更を一括でアーカイブし、コードベースをチェックして実装されているものを決定","ko":"openspec-bulk-archive-change 기능은 여러 변경을 일괄적으로 아카이브하고 코드베이스를 확인하여 실제 구현된 항목을 결정","es":"La habilidad openspec-bulk-archive-change permite archivar múltiples cambios completados en una sola operación, manejando conflictos de especificaciones de forma inteligente","fr":"La compétence openspec-bulk-archive-change permet d''archiver plusieurs modifications terminées en une seule opération, en gérant de manière intelligente les conflits de spécifications","de":"Die Fähigkeit openspec-bulk-archive-change ermöglicht das Archivieren mehrerer abgeschlossener Änderungen in einer einzigen Operation, wobei Konflikte intelligenterweise gehandhabt werden","pt":"O Openspec permite arquivar múltiplas alterações em uma operação, lidando com conflitos de especificação de forma inteligente.","ru":"Openspec позволяет архивировать несколько изменений в одной операции, умно справляясь с конфликтами спецификаций.","ar":"أوبنسبك يسمح بأرشفة التغييرات المتعددة في عملية واحدة، ويتعامل مع تضارب المواصفات بذكاء.","en":"SwiftIndex — Swift-native semantic code search"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"openspec-bulk-archive-change 技术","ja":"openspec-bulk-archive-change スキル","ko":"openspec-bulk-archive-change 기능","es":"Archivar cambios masivos con openspec-bulk-archive-change","fr":"Archivage massif de modifications avec openspec-bulk-arch...","de":"Massen-Archivierung von Änderungen mit openspec-bulk-arch...","pt":"Openspec: Arquivamento em Massa de Alterações","ru":"Openspec: Пакетное архивирование изменений","ar":"أوبنسبك: أرشفة تغييرات بالجملة","en":"openspec-bulk-archive-change"},"description":{"zh":"openspec-bulk-archive-change 技术允许您批量存档更改，智能处理规格冲突","ja":"openspec-bulk-archive-change スキルは、複数の変更を一括でアーカイブし、コードベースをチェックして実装されているものを決定","ko":"openspec-bulk-archive-change 기능은 여러 변경을 일괄적으로 아카이브하고 코드베이스를 확인하여 실제 구현된 항목을 결정","es":"La habilidad openspec-bulk-archive-change permite archivar múltiples cambios completados en una sola operación, manejando conflictos de especificaciones de f...","fr":"La compétence openspec-bulk-archive-change permet d''archiver plusieurs modifications terminées en une seule opération, en gérant de manière intelligente les ...","de":"Die Fähigkeit openspec-bulk-archive-change ermöglicht das Archivieren mehrerer abgeschlossener Änderungen in einer einzigen Operation, wobei Konflikte intell...","pt":"O Openspec permite arquivar múltiplas alterações em uma operação, lidando com conflitos de especificação de forma inteligente.","ru":"Openspec позволяет архивировать несколько изменений в одной операции, умно справляясь с конфликтами спецификаций.","ar":"أوبنسبك يسمح بأرشفة التغييرات المتعددة في عملية واحدة، ويتعامل مع تضارب المواصفات بذكاء.","en":"SwiftIndex — Swift-native semantic code search"},"definition":{"en":"SwiftIndex — Swift-native semantic code search"},"features":{"zh":["批量存档更改","智能处理规格冲突","检查代码库以确定实际实现","支持多选","无需输入即可运行"],"ja":["複数の変更を一括でアーカイブ","規格の衝突を智能的に処理","コードベースをチェックして実装されているものを決定","複数選択に対応","入力不要で実行可能"],"ko":["여러 변경을 일괄적으로 아카이브","규격 충돌을智能적으로 처리","코드베이스를 확인하여 실제 구현된 항목을 결정","다중 선택 지원","입력 없이 실행 가능"],"es":["Archivado masivo de cambios","Manejo inteligente de conflictos de especificaciones","Selección de cambios mediante la herramienta AskUserQuestion","Obtención de cambios activos con openspec list --json","Información al usuario en caso de no haber cambios activos"],"fr":["Archivage massif de modifications","Gestion intelligente des conflits de spécifications","Sélection de modifications via l''outil AskUserQuestion","Obtention des modifications actives avec openspec list --json","Information de l''utilisateur en cas d''absence de modifications actives"],"de":["Massen-Archivierung von Änderungen","Intelligente Handhabung von Konflikten","Auswahl von Änderungen über das Tool AskUserQuestion","Abruf von aktiven Änderungen mit openspec list --json","Benachrichtigung des Benutzers bei fehlenden aktiven Änderungen"],"pt":["Arquivamento em massa de alterações","Lidando com conflitos de especificação de forma inteligente","Utiliza o comando ''openspec list --json'' para obter alterações ativas","Permite seleção de alterações para arquivamento","Executa arquivamento em uma operação única"],"ru":["Пакетное архивирование изменений","Умное решение конфликтов спецификаций","Использует команду ''openspec list --json'' для получения активных изменений","Позволяет выбирать изменения для архивирования","Выполняет архивирование в одной операции"],"ar":["أرشفة التغييرات بالجملة","التعامل مع تضارب المواصفات بذكاء","استخدام الأمر ''openspec list --json'' لاسترداد التغييرات النشطة","السماح باختيار التغييرات لأرشفتها","تنفيذ الأرشفة في عملية واحدة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["openspec-bulk-archive-change","批量存档","规格冲突","代码库","智能处理","多选","SwiftIndex","semantic code search"],"ja":["openspec-bulk-archive-change","一括アーカイブ","規格の衝突","コードベース","智能的な処理","複数選択","SwiftIndex","セマンティックコード検索"],"ko":["openspec-bulk-archive-change","일괄 아카이브","규격 충돌","코드베이스","智能적인 처리","다중 선택","SwiftIndex","세맨틱 코드 검색"],"es":["archivado masivo de cambios","openspec-bulk-archive-change","desarrollo de software","gestión de cambios","conflictos de especificaciones","AskUserQuestion","openspec list --json"],"fr":["archivage massif de modifications","openspec-bulk-archive-change","développement de logiciels","gestion de modifications","conflits de spécifications","AskUserQuestion","openspec list --json"],"de":["Massen-Archivierung von Änderungen","openspec-bulk-archive-change","Software-Entwicklung","Änderungsmanagement","Konflikte","AskUserQuestion","openspec list --json"],"pt":["Openspec","arquivamento em massa","alterações","conflitos de especificação","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Openspec","пакетное архивирование","изменения","конфликты спецификаций","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["أوبنسبك","أرشفة بالجملة","التغييرات","تضارب المواصفات","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"alexey1312","repo":"swift-index","repoPath":"alexey1312/swift-index","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-bulk-archive-change","description":"Archive multiple completed changes at once. Use when archiving several parallel changes.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Archive multiple completed changes in a single operation.\n\nThis skill allows you to batch-archive changes, handling spec conflicts intelligently by checking the codebase to determine what''s actually implemented.\n\n**Input**: None required (prompts for selection)\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **Get active changes**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get all active changes.\n\n   If no active changes exist, inform user and stop.\n\n2. **Prompt for change selection**\n\n   Use **AskUserQuestion tool** with multi-select t","body":"Archive multiple completed changes in a single operation.\n\nThis skill allows you to batch-archive changes, handling spec conflicts intelligently by checking the codebase to determine what''s actually implemented.\n\n**Input**: None required (prompts for selection)\n\n**Steps**\n\n1. **Get active changes**\n\n   Run `openspec list --json` to get all active changes.\n\n   If no active changes exist, inform user and stop.\n\n2. **Prompt for change selection**\n\n   Use **AskUserQuestion tool** with multi-select to let user choose changes:\n   - Show each change with its schema\n   - Include an option for \"All changes\"\n   - Allow any number of selections (1+ works, 2+ is the typical use case)\n\n   **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT auto-select. Always let the user choose.\n\n3. **Batch validation - gather status for all selected changes**\n\n   For each selected change, collect:\n\n   a. **Artifact status** - Run `openspec status --change \"<name>\" --json`\n   - Parse `schemaName` and `artifacts` list\n   - Note which artifacts are `done` vs other states\n\n   b. **Task completion** - Read `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`\n   - Count `- [ ]` (incomplete) vs `- [x]` (complete)\n   - If no tasks file exists, note as \"No tasks\"\n\n   c. **Delta specs** - Check `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/` directory\n   - List which capability specs exist\n   - For each, extract requirement names (lines matching `### Requirement: <name>`)\n\n4. **Detect spec conflicts**\n\n   Build a map of `capability -> [changes that touch it]`:\n\n   ```\n   auth -> [change-a, change-b]  <- CONFLICT (2+ changes)\n   api  -> [change-c]            <- OK (only 1 change)\n   ```\n\n   A conflict exists when 2+ selected changes have delta specs for the same capability.\n\n5. **Resolve conflicts agentically**\n\n   **For each conflict**, investigate the codebase:\n\n   a. **Read the delta specs** from each conflicting change to understand what each claims to add/modify\n\n   b. **Search the codebase** for implementation evidence:\n   - Look for code implementing requirements from each delta spec\n   - Check for related files, functions, or tests\n\n   c. **Determine resolution**:\n   - If only one change is actually implemented -> sync that one''s specs\n   - If both implemented -> apply in chronological order (older first, newer overwrites)\n   - If neither implemented -> skip spec sync, warn user\n\n   d. **Record resolution** for each conflict:\n   - Which change''s specs to apply\n   - In what order (if both)\n   - Rationale (what was found in codebase)\n\n6. **Show consolidated status table**\n\n   Display a table summarizing all changes:\n\n   ```\n   | Change               | Artifacts | Tasks | Specs   | Conflicts | Status |\n   |---------------------|-----------|-------|---------|-----------|--------|\n   | schema-management   | Done      | 5/5   | 2 delta | None      | Ready  |\n   | project-config      | Done      | 3/3   | 1 delta | None      | Ready  |\n   | add-oauth           | Done      | 4/4   | 1 delta | auth (!)  | Ready* |\n   | add-verify-skill    | 1 left    | 2/5   | None    | None      | Warn   |\n   ```\n\n   For conflicts, show the resolution:\n   ```\n   * Conflict resolution:\n     - auth spec: Will apply add-oauth then add-jwt (both implemented, chronological order)\n   ```\n\n   For incomplete changes, show warnings:\n   ```\n   Warnings:\n   - add-verify-skill: 1 incomplete artifact, 3 incomplete tasks\n   ```\n\n7. **Confirm batch operation**\n\n   Use **AskUserQuestion tool** with a single confirmation:\n\n   - \"Archive N changes?\" with options based on status\n   - Options might include:\n     - \"Archive all N changes\"\n     - \"Archive only N ready changes (skip incomplete)\"\n     - \"Cancel\"\n\n   If there are incomplete changes, make clear they''ll be archived with warnings.\n\n8. **Execute archive for each confirmed change**\n\n   Process changes in the determined order (respecting conflict resolution):\n\n   a. **Sync specs** if delta specs exist:\n   - Use the openspec-sync-specs approach (agent-driven intelligent merge)\n   - For conflicts, apply in resolved order\n   - Track if sync was done\n\n   b. **Perform the archive**:\n   ```bash\n   mkdir -p openspec/changes/archive\n   mv openspec/changes/<name> openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>\n   ```\n\n   c. **Track outcome** for each change:\n   - Success: archived successfully\n   - Failed: error during archive (record error)\n   - Skipped: user chose not to archive (if applicable)\n\n9. **Display summary**\n\n   Show final results:\n\n   ```\n   ## Bulk Archive Complete\n\n   Archived 3 changes:\n   - schema-management-cli -> archive/2026-01-19-schema-management-cli/\n   - project-config -> archive/2026-01-19-project-config/\n   - add-oauth -> archive/2026-01-19-add-oauth/\n\n   Skipped 1 change:\n   - add-verify-skill (user chose not to archive incomplete)\n\n   Spec sync summary:\n   - 4 delta specs synced to main specs\n   - 1 conflict resolved (auth: applied both in chronological order)\n   ```\n\n   If any failures:\n   ```\n   Failed 1 change:\n   - some-change: Archive directory already exists\n   ```\n\n**Conflict Resolution Examples**\n\nExample 1: Only one implemented\n\n```\nConflict: specs/auth/spec.md touched by [add-oauth, add-jwt]\n\nChecking add-oauth:\n- Delta adds \"OAuth Provider Integration\" requirement\n- Searching codebase... found src/auth/oauth.ts implementing OAuth flow\n\nChecking add-jwt:\n- Delta adds \"JWT Token Handling\" requirement\n- Searching codebase... no JWT implementation found\n\nResolution: Only add-oauth is implemented. Will sync add-oauth specs only.\n```\n\nExample 2: Both implemented\n\n```\nConflict: specs/api/spec.md touched by [add-rest-api, add-graphql]\n\nChecking add-rest-api (created 2026-01-10):\n- Delta adds \"REST Endpoints\" requirement\n- Searching codebase... found src/api/rest.ts\n\nChecking add-graphql (created 2026-01-15):\n- Delta adds \"GraphQL Schema\" requirement\n- Searching codebase... found src/api/graphql.ts\n\nResolution: Both implemented. Will apply add-rest-api specs first,\nthen add-graphql specs (chronological order, newer takes precedence).\n```\n\n**Output On Success**\n\n```\n## Bulk Archive Complete\n\nArchived N changes:\n- <change-1> -> archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<change-1>/\n- <change-2> -> archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<change-2>/\n\nSpec sync summary:\n- N delta specs synced to main specs\n- No conflicts (or: M conflicts resolved)\n```\n\n**Output On Partial Success**\n\n```\n## Bulk Archive Complete (partial)\n\nArchived N changes:\n- <change-1> -> archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<change-1>/\n\nSkipped M changes:\n- <change-2> (user chose not to archive incomplete)\n\nFailed K changes:\n- <change-3>: Archive directory already exists\n```\n\n**Output When No Changes**\n\n```\n## No Changes to Archive\n\nNo active changes found. Use `/opsx:new` to create a new change.\n```\n\n**Guardrails**\n\n- Allow any number of changes (1+ is fine, 2+ is the typical use case)\n- Always prompt for selection, never auto-select\n- Detect spec conflicts early and resolve by checking codebase\n- When both changes are implemented, apply specs in chronological order\n- Skip spec sync only when implementation is missing (warn user)\n- Show clear per-change status before confirming\n- Use single confirmation for entire batch\n- Track and report all outcomes (success/skip/fail)\n- Preserve .openspec.yaml when moving to archive\n- Archive directory target uses current date: YYYY-MM-DD-<name>\n- If archive target exists, fail that change but continue with others\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:38:55.092Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Management Agents needing efficient bulk archiving of completed changes with intelligent spec conflict resolution.","zh":"Perfect for Code Management Agents needing efficient bulk archiving of completed changes with intelligent spec conflict resolution.","ja":"Perfect for Code Management Agents needing efficient bulk archiving of completed changes with intelligent spec conflict resolution.","ko":"Perfect for Code Management Agents needing efficient bulk archiving of completed changes with intelligent spec conflict resolution.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de gestión de código que necesitan un archivado en bloque eficiente de cambios completados con resolución inteligente de conflictos de especificaciones.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de gestion de code nécessitant un archivage en bloc efficace des modifications terminées avec une résolution intelligente des conflits de spécifications.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Management-Agents, die ein effizientes Massenarchivieren abgeschlossener Änderungen mit intelligenter Spezifikationskonfliktlösung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Código que necessitam de arquivamento em massa eficiente de alterações concluídas com resolução inteligente de conflitos de especificação.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов управления кодом, которым требуется эффективное массовое архивирование завершенных изменений с интеллектуальным разрешением конфликтов спецификаций.","ar":"مثالي لوجوهات إدارة الشفرة التي تحتاج إلى أرشفة大量 تغييرات كاملة مع حل ذكي لنزاعات المواصفات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to batch-archive changes using SwiftIndex, handling spec conflicts by checking the codebase to determine implemented changes, utilizing the `openspec list --json` command for active change retrieval and the AskUserQuestion tool for multi-select prompts.","zh":"Empowers agents to batch-archive changes using SwiftIndex, handling spec conflicts by checking the codebase to determine implemented changes, utilizing the `openspec list --json` command for active change retrieval and the AskUserQuestion tool for multi-select prompts.","ja":"Empowers agents to batch-archive changes using SwiftIndex, handling spec conflicts by checking the codebase to determine implemented changes, utilizing the `openspec list --json` command for active change retrieval and the AskUserQuestion tool for multi-select prompts.","ko":"Empowers agents to batch-archive changes using SwiftIndex, handling spec conflicts by checking the codebase to determine implemented changes, utilizing the `openspec list --json` command for active change retrieval and the AskUserQuestion tool for multi-select prompts.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a archivar por lotes las modificaciones utilizando SwiftIndex, manejando conflictos de especificaciones mediante la verificación de la base de código para determinar los cambios implementados, utilizando el comando `openspec list --json` para la recuperación de cambios activos y la herramienta AskUserQuestion para solicitudes de selección múltiple.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''archiver par lots les modifications à l''aide de SwiftIndex, en gérant les conflits de spécifications en vérifiant la base de code pour déterminer les modifications mises en œuvre, en utilisant la commande `openspec list --json` pour la récupération des modifications actives et l''outil AskUserQuestion pour les invites de sélection multiple.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Änderungen in Batches zu archivieren, indem SwiftIndex verwendet wird, Spezifikationskonflikte durch Überprüfung des Codebasis zur Bestimmung der implementierten Änderungen gehandhabt werden, unter Verwendung des Befehls `openspec list --json` für die Abrufung von aktiven Änderungen und des Tools AskUserQuestion für multiple Auswahlhinweise.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a arquivar em massa alterações usando o SwiftIndex, lidando com conflitos de especificação verificando a base de código para determinar as alterações implementadas, utilizando o comando `openspec list --json` para recuperação de alterações ativas e a ferramenta AskUserQuestion para prompts de seleção múltipla.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью пакетного архивирования изменений с помощью SwiftIndex, обрабатывая конфликты спецификаций путем проверки кодовой базы для определения реализованных изменений, используя команду `openspec list --json` для извлечения активных изменений и инструмент AskUserQuestion для многоселекторных запросов.","ar":"تمكين الوكالات من أرشفة التغييرات بالجملة باستخدام SwiftIndex، والتعامل مع نزاعات المواصفات من خلال التحقق من قاعدة الشفرة لتحديد التغييرات المطبقة، باستخدام الأمر `openspec list --json` لاسترجاع التغييرات النشطة وأداة AskUserQuestion لمطالبات التحديد المتعدد."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating bulk archiving of completed changes","Resolving spec conflicts intelligently across the codebase","Streamlining code management workflows with SwiftIndex"],"zh":["Automating bulk archiving of completed changes","Resolving spec conflicts intelligently across the codebase","Streamlining code management workflows with SwiftIndex"],"ja":["Automating bulk archiving of completed changes","Resolving spec conflicts intelligently across the codebase","Streamlining code management workflows with SwiftIndex"],"ko":["Automating bulk archiving of completed changes","Resolving spec conflicts intelligently across the codebase","Streamlining code management workflows with SwiftIndex"],"es":["Automatización del archivado en bloque de cambios completados","Resolución inteligente de conflictos de especificaciones en toda la base de código","Optimización de flujos de trabajo de gestión de código con SwiftIndex"],"fr":["Automatisation de l''archivage en bloc des modifications terminées","Résolution intelligente des conflits de spécifications dans l''ensemble de la base de code","Optimisation des flux de travail de gestion de code avec SwiftIndex"],"de":["Automatisierung des Massenarchivierens abgeschlossener Änderungen","Intelligente Auflösung von Spezifikationskonflikten im gesamten Codebasis","Optimierung von Code-Management-Workflows mit SwiftIndex"],"pt":["Automatizar a arquivamento em massa de alterações concluídas","Resolver conflitos de especificação de forma inteligente em toda a base de código","Otimizar fluxos de trabalho de gerenciamento de código com o SwiftIndex"],"ru":["Автоматизировать массовое архивирование завершенных изменений","Интеллектуально разрешать конфликты спецификаций на протяжении всей кодовой базы","Оптимизировать рабочие процессы управления кодом с помощью SwiftIndex"],"ar":["أتمتة أرشفة التغييرات الكاملة بالجملة","حل نزاعات المواصفات بذكاء عبر قاعدة الشفرة","تبسيط سير عمل إدارة الشفرة مع SwiftIndex"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires SwiftIndex and openspec tooling","No active changes results in termination"],"zh":["Requires SwiftIndex and openspec tooling","No active changes results in termination"],"ja":["Requires SwiftIndex and openspec tooling","No active changes results in termination"],"ko":["Requires SwiftIndex and openspec tooling","No active changes results in termination"],"es":["Requiere SwiftIndex y herramientas openspec","No se producen resultados de cambios activos en la terminación"],"fr":["Nécessite SwiftIndex et les outils openspec","Aucun résultat de modifications actives n''est généré lors de la termination"],"de":["Benötigt SwiftIndex und openspec-Tooling","Keine aktiven Änderungen resultieren in Beendigung"],"pt":["Requer SwiftIndex e ferramentas openspec","Nenhum resultado de alterações ativas resulta em terminação"],"ru":["Требует SwiftIndex и инструментов openspec","Отсутствие результатов активных изменений приводит к завершению"],"ar":["يتطلب SwiftIndex وأدوات openspec","عدم وجود نتائج للتغييرات النشطة يؤدي إلى الإنهاء"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
