"commit"},"description":{"zh":"Git Commit 是一种使用 Conventional Commits 格式创建 Git 提交的方法，包括类型、范围和主题","ja":"Git Commit は Conventional Commits 形式を使用して Git コミットを作成する方法です","ko":"Git Commit은 Conventional Commits 형식을 사용하여 Git 커밋을 생성하는 방법입니다","es":"El commit es una habilidad que te permite crear commits de Git siguiendo el formato Conventional Commits con tipo, alcance y asunto adecuados.","fr":"Le commit est une compétence qui vous permet de créer des commits Git suivant le format Conventional Commits avec type, portée et sujet appropriés.","de":"Der Commit ist eine Fähigkeit, die es Ihnen ermöglicht, Git-Commits im Conventional-Commits-Format mit geeigneten Typ, Umfang und Betreff zu erstellen.","pt":"O commit Git é uma ferramenta para criar commits no formato Conventional Commits com tipo, escopo e assunto. Ele ajuda a manter um histórico de alterações cl...","ru":"Коммит Git — это инструмент для создания коммитов в формате Conventional Commits с типом, областью и темой. Он помогает поддерживать чистую и организованную ...","ar":"التزام Git هو أداة لإنشاء التزامات بتنسيق التزامات التقليدية مع النوع والنطاق والموضوع. يساعد على الحفاظ على سجل تغييرات واضح ومنظم","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持 Conventional Commits 格式","包括类型、范围和主题","快速创建 Git 提交","支持多种 Git 操作"],"ja":["Conventional Commits 形式をサポート","タイプ、スコープ、サブジェクトを含む","Git コミットの迅速な作成","多種多様な Git 操作をサポート"],"ko":["Conventional Commits 형식 지원","유형, 범위, 주제 포함","Git 커밋 빠른 생성","다양한 Git 작업 지원"],"es":["Creación de commits de Git con formato Conventional Commits","Soporte para commits regulares y de características","Opción para incluir un cuerpo descriptivo en el commit","Compatibilidad con diferentes tipos de commits","Facilidad de uso con la línea de comandos"],"fr":["Création de commits Git avec format Conventional Commits","Prise en charge des commits réguliers et de fonctionnalités","Option pour inclure un corps descriptif dans le commit","Compatibilité avec différents types de commits","Facilité d''utilisation avec la ligne de commande"],"de":["Erstellung von Git-Commits im Conventional-Commits-Format","Unterstützung für reguläre und Funktions-Commits","Option, einen beschreibenden Text im Commit zu includieren","Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen Commit-Typen","Einfache Verwendung über die Kommandozeile"],"pt":["Cria commits no formato Conventional Commits","Suporta tipo, escopo e assunto","Ajuda a manter um histórico de alterações claro","Permite referenciar tarefas e requisitos","Segue as melhores práticas de commit"],"ru":["Создает коммиты в формате Conventional Commits","Поддерживает тип, область и тему","Помогает поддерживать чистую историю изменений","Позволяет ссылаться на задачи и требования","Следует лучшим практикам коммитов"],"ar":["ينشئ التزامات بتنسيق التزامات التقليدية","يدعم النوع والنطاق والموضوع","يساعد على الحفاظ على سجل تغييرات واضح","يسمح بالرجوع إلى المهام والمتطلبات","يتبع أفضل الممارسات للازمات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Git Commit","Conventional Commits","Git 提交格式","类型","范围","主题"],"ja":["Git Commit","Conventional Commits","Git コミット形式","タイプ","スコープ","サブジェクト"],"ko":["Git Commit","Conventional Commits","Git 커밋 형식","유형","범위","주제"],"es":["commit","git commit","conventional commits","formato de commit","tipo de commit","desarrollo de software","control de versiones"],"fr":["commit","git commit","conventional commits","format de commit","type de commit","développement de logiciels","contrôle de version"],"de":["commit","git commit","conventional commits","commit-format","commit-typ","software-entwicklung","versionskontrolle"],"pt":["commit git","conventional commits","git commit","tipo de commit","escopo de commit","assunto de commit","histórico de alterações","desenvolvimento de software"],"ru":["коммит гит","конвенциональные коммиты","гит коммит","тип коммита","область коммита","тема коммита","история изменений","разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["التزام جيت","التزامات تقليدية","التزام جيت","نوع التزام","نطاق التزام","موضوع التزام","سجل التغييرات","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"DJJones66","repo":"Library-Service","repoPath":"DJJones66/Library-Service","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"commit","description":"Write conventional commit messages with type, scope, and subject when the user wants to commit changes or save work.","bodyPreview":"# Git Commit\n\nCreates git commits following Conventional Commits format with proper type, scope, and subject.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n# 1. Stage changes\ngit add <files>  # or: git add -A\n\n# 2. Create commit (branch commit format)\ngit commit -m \"type(scope): subject\n\nBody explaining HOW and WHY.\nReference: Task X.Y, Req N\"\n```\n\n## Commit Types\n\n### Regular Branch Commits (During Development)\n\n**Format**: `type(scope): subject`\n\n| Type | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `feat` | New feature or func","body":"# Git Commit\n\nCreates git commits following Conventional Commits format with proper type, scope, and subject.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n# 1. Stage changes\ngit add <files>  # or: git add -A\n\n# 2. Create commit (branch commit format)\ngit commit -m \"type(scope): subject\n\nBody explaining HOW and WHY.\nReference: Task X.Y, Req N\"\n```\n\n## Commit Types\n\n### Regular Branch Commits (During Development)\n\n**Format**: `type(scope): subject`\n\n| Type | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `feat` | New feature or functionality |\n| `fix` | Bug fix or issue resolution |\n| `refactor` | Code refactoring without behavior change |\n| `perf` | Performance improvements |\n| `test` | Test additions or modifications |\n| `ci` | CI/CD configuration changes |\n| `docs` | Documentation updates |\n| `chore` | Maintenance, dependencies, tooling |\n| `style` | Code formatting, linting (non-functional) |\n| `security` | Security vulnerability fixes or hardening |\n\n### Scope (Required, kebab-case)\n\nExamples: `validation`, `auth`, `cookie-service`, `template`, `config`, `tests`, `api`\n\n### Subject Line Rules\n\n- Max 50 characters after colon\n- Present tense imperative: add, implement, fix, improve, enhance, refactor, remove, prevent\n- NO period at the end\n- Specific and descriptive - state WHAT, not WHY\n\n## Core Workflow\n\n### 1. Review Changes\n\n```bash\ngit status\ngit diff --staged  # if already staged\ngit diff           # if not staged\n```\n\n### 2. Stage Files\n\n```bash\ngit add <specific-files>  # preferred\n# or\ngit add -A  # all changes\n```\n\n**NEVER commit**:\n- `.env`, `credentials.json`, secrets\n- `node_modules/`, `__pycache__/`, `.venv/`\n- Large binary files without explicit approval\n\n### 3. Create Commit\n\n**Simple change**:\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"fix(auth): use hmac.compare_digest for secure comparison\"\n```\n\n**Complex change (with body)**:\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<''EOF''\nfeat(validation): add URLValidator with domain whitelist\n\nImplement URLValidator class supporting:\n- Domain whitelist enforcement (youtube.com, youtu.be)\n- Dangerous scheme blocking (javascript, data, file)\n- URL parsing with embedded credentials handling\n\nAddresses Requirement 31: Input validation\nPart of Task 5.1: Input Validation Utilities\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n### 4. Verify Commit\n\n```bash\ngit log -1 --format=\"%h %s\"\ngit show --stat HEAD\n```\n\n## Body Format (Recommended for Complex Changes)\n\n```\n<blank line>\nExplain HOW and WHY the change was made.\n- Use bullet points for multiple items\n- Wrap at 72 characters\n\nReference: Task X.Y\nAddresses: Req N\n```\n\n## Git Trailers\n\n| Trailer | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `Fixes #N` | Links and closes issue on merge |\n| `Closes #N` | Same as Fixes |\n| `Co-authored-by: Name <email>` | Credit co-contributors |\n\nPlace trailers at end of body after blank line. See `references/commit_examples.md` for examples.\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\nFor incompatible API/behavior changes, use `!` after scope OR `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer:\n\n```\nfeat(api)!: change response format to JSON:API\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: Response envelope changed from `{ data }` to `{ data: { type, id, attributes } }`.\n```\n\nTriggers major version bump in semantic-release.\n\n## Merge Commits (PR Closure)\n\nFor PRs, use extended description with sections:\n\n```bash\ngh pr create --title \"feat(security): implement input validation (Task 5)\" --body \"$(cat <<''EOF''\n## Summary\n- Input validation utilities (URLValidator, FormatValidator)\n- Secure template processor with path traversal prevention\n- API key authentication middleware\n\n## Task Breakdown\nTask 5.1: Input Validation - URLValidator, FormatValidator\nTask 5.2: Template Processing - Path traversal prevention\nTask 5.3: API Key Auth - Multi-key support, excluded paths\nTask 5.4: Security Tests - 102 path traversal tests\n\n## Requirements Covered\nReq 7, Req 9, Req 31, Req 33\n\n## Test Coverage\n- All 473 tests passing\n- Coverage: 93%\n- Pre-commit checks: passing\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n### From github-pr-review\n\nWhen fixing review comments, use this format:\n\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"fix(scope): address review comment #ID\n\nBrief explanation of what was wrong and how it''s fixed.\nAddresses review comment #123456789.\"\n```\n\n### From github-pr-creation\n\nBefore creating PR, ensure all commits follow this format. The PR skill will:\n1. Analyze commits for proper format\n2. Extract types for PR labels\n3. Build PR description from commit bodies\n\n## Important Rules\n\n- **ALWAYS** include scope in parentheses\n- **ALWAYS** use present tense imperative verb\n- **NEVER** end subject with period\n- **NEVER** commit secrets or credentials\n- **NEVER** use generic messages (\"update code\", \"fix bug\", \"changes\")\n- **NEVER** exceed 50 chars in subject line\n- Group related changes -> single focused commit\n\n## Examples\n\n**Good**:\n```\nfeat(validation): add URLValidator with domain whitelist\nfix(auth): use hmac.compare_digest for secure key comparison\nrefactor(template): consolidate filename sanitization logic\ntest(security): add 102 path traversal prevention tests\n```\n\n**Bad**:\n```\nupdate validation code           # no type, no scope, vague\nfeat: add stuff                  # missing scope, too vague\nfix(auth): fix bug               # circular, not specific\nchore: make changes              # missing scope, vague\nfeat(security): improve things.  # has period, vague\n```\n\n## References\n\n- `references/commit_examples.md` - Extended examples by type\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:39:29.207Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing standardized git commit management with Conventional Commits format.","zh":"适用于需要标准化 git 提交管理的开发代理，采用 Conventional Commits 格式。","ja":"Conventional Commits 形式の標準化された git コミット管理を必要とする開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Conventional Commits 형식의 표준화된 git 커밋 관리가 필요한 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan una gestión de commits de git estandarizada con formato Conventional Commits.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement qui ont besoin d''une gestion de commits git standardisée avec le format Conventional Commits.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine standardisierte Git-Commit-Verwaltung mit Conventional-Commits-Format benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que necessitam de gerenciamento de commits git padronizado com formato Conventional Commits.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым требуется стандартизированное управление коммитами git в формате Conventional Commits.","ar":"مثالي لعميل التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى إدارة ملحقات غيت الموحدة مع تنسيق التزامات التقليدية."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create git commits with proper type, scope, and subject, following the Conventional Commits format, utilizing git commands like ''git add'' and ''git commit -m'' to manage repository changes.","zh":"赋予代理创建 git 提交的能力，具有适当的类型、范围和主题，遵循 Conventional Commits 格式，利用 git 命令如 ''git add'' 和 ''git commit -m'' 来管理仓库更改。","ja":"Conventional Commits 形式に従って、適切なタイプ、スコープ、サブジェクトを持つ git コミットを作成するエージェントを可能にします。git コマンド seperti ''git add'' および ''git commit -m'' を使用してリポジトリの変更を管理します。","ko":"Conventional Commits 형식을 따르며, 적절한 유형, 범위 및 주제를 갖는 git 커밋을 만들 수 있는 에이전트를 가능하게 합니다. git 명령어인 ''git add'' 및 ''git commit -m''를 사용하여 리포지토리의 변경 사항을 관리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear commits de git con el tipo, alcance y asunto adecuados, siguiendo el formato Conventional Commits, utilizando comandos de git como ''git add'' y ''git commit -m'' para gestionar los cambios del repositorio.","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des commits git avec le type, la portée et l''objet appropriés, en suivant le format Conventional Commits, en utilisant des commandes git comme ''git add'' et ''git commit -m'' pour gérer les modifications du référentiel.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Git-Commits mit geeigneter Art, Umfang und Betreff zu erstellen, indem sie dem Conventional-Commits-Format folgen und Git-Befehle wie ''git add'' und ''git commit -m'' zur Verwaltung von Repository-Änderungen verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar commits git com tipo, escopo e assunto apropriados, seguindo o formato Conventional Commits, utilizando comandos git como ''git add'' e ''git commit -m'' para gerenciar alterações no repositório.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать коммиты git с правильным типом, областью и предметом, следуя формату Conventional Commits, используя команды git, такие как ''git add'' и ''git commit -m'', для управления изменениями в репозитории.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية إنشاء ملحقات غيت مع نوع ومدى وموضوع مناسب، اتباعًا لتنسيق التزامات التقليدية، باستخدام أوامر غيت مثل ''git add'' و ''git commit -m'' لإدارة التغييرات في المستودع."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating commit creation with feat, fix, or docs types","Generating commit messages with scope and subject details","Standardizing commit formats for team collaboration"],"zh":["使用 feat、fix 或 docs 类型自动创建提交","生成包含范围和主题详细信息的提交消息","标准化提交格式以便团队合作"],"ja":["feat、fix、または docs タイプを使用したコミットの自動作成","スコープとサブジェクトの詳細を含むコミットメッセージの生成","チームコラボレーションのためのコミット形式の標準化"],"ko":["feat, fix 또는 docs 유형을 사용한 커밋 자동 생성","범위 및 주제 세부 정보를 포함한 커밋 메시지 생성","팀 협력을 위한 커밋 형식 표준화"],"es":["Automatización de la creación de commits con tipos feat, fix o docs","Generación de mensajes de commit con detalles de alcance y asunto","Estandarización de formatos de commit para la colaboración en equipo"],"fr":["Automation de la création de commits avec des types feat, fix ou docs","Génération de messages de commit avec des détails de portée et d''objet","Standardisation des formats de commit pour la collaboration d''équipe"],"de":["Automatisierung der Commit-Erstellung mit Typen feat, fix oder docs","Erzeugung von Commit-Nachrichten mit Umfangs- und Betreffdetails","Standardisierung von Commit-Formaten für die Teamzusammenarbeit"],"pt":["Automatizar a criação de commits com tipos feat, fix ou docs","Gerar mensagens de commit com detalhes de escopo e assunto","Padronizar formatos de commit para colaboração em equipe"],"ru":["Автоматизация создания коммитов с типами feat, fix или docs","Генерация сообщений коммитов с деталями области и предмета","Стандартизация форматов коммитов для командной работы"],"ar":["توفير إنشاء التزامات автомاتيكيًا مع أنواع feat أو fix أو docs","توليد رسائل التزام مع تفاصيل النطاق والموضوع","توحيد تنسيقات التزامات للتعاون الفريقي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires git installation and configuration","Limited to Conventional Commits format"],"zh":["需要 git 安装和配置","仅限于 Conventional Commits 格式"],"ja":["git のインストールと設定が必要","Conventional Commits 形式に限定される"],"ko":["git 설치 및 구성이 필요함","Conventional Commits 형식으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere instalación y configuración de git","Limitado al formato Conventional Commits"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation et la configuration de git","Limité au format Conventional Commits"],"de":["Benötigt Git-Installation und -Konfiguration","Begrenzt auf das Conventional-Commits-Format"],"pt":["Requer instalação e configuração do git","Limitado ao formato Conventional Commits"],"ru":["Требует установки и конфигурации git","Ограничен форматом Conventional Commits"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت وتكوين غيت","محدود بتنسيق التزامات التقليدية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Treytucker05/pt-study-sop/planning-with-files', 'community', 'Treytucker05', 'pt-study-sop', 'Treytucker05/pt-study-sop', 'planning-with-files', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z', '2026-02-18T08:39:28.238Z', NULL, '{"id":"Treytucker05/pt-study-sop/planning-with-files","name":"planning-with-files","description":{"zh":"文件规划是一种使用持久的markdown文件作为工作内存的工作流程，帮助开发者高效工作","ja":"ファイル計画は、永続的なMarkdownファイルを使用して作業メモリを実現するワークフローです","ko":"파일 계획은 지속적인 markdown 파일을 사용하여 작업 메모리를 구현하는 작업 흐름입니다","es":"Planificación con archivos es una técnica que utiliza archivos markdown persistentes para mejorar la productividad","fr":"La planification avec des fichiers est une technique qui utilise des fichiers markdown persistants pour améliorer la productivité","de":"Die Planung mit Dateien ist eine Technik, die persistente Markdown-Dateien verwendet, um die Produktivität zu steigern","pt":"O skill de planejamento com arquivos permite usar arquivos markdown persistentes como memória de trabalho em disco","ru":"Навык планирования с файлами позволяет использовать постоянные файлы markdown как рабочую память на диске","ar":"مهارة التخطيط مع الملفات تسمح باستخدام ملفات markdown المستدامة كذاكرة عمل على القرص","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"文件规划：高效工作流程","ja":"ファイル計画：効率的なワークフロー","ko":"파일 계획: 효율적인 작업 흐름","es":"Planificación con archivos: aumenta la productividad","fr":"Planification avec des fichiers: boostez votre productivité","de":"Planung mit Dateien: steigern Sie Ihre Produktivität","pt":"Planejamento com Arquivos: Trabalhe como Manus","ru":"Планирование с файлами: Работа как Manus","ar":"التخطيط مع الملفات: عمل مثل Manus","en":"planning-with-files"},"description":{"zh":"文件规划是一种使用持久的markdown文件作为工作内存的工作流程，帮助开发者高效工作","ja":"ファイル計画は、永続的なMarkdownファイルを使用して作業メモリを実現するワークフローです","ko":"파일 계획은 지속적인 markdown 파일을 사용하여 작업 메모리를 구현하는 작업 흐름입니다","es":"Planificación con archivos es una técnica que utiliza archivos markdown persistentes para mejorar la productividad","fr":"La planification avec des fichiers est une technique qui utilise des fichiers markdown persistants pour améliorer la productivité","de":"Die Planung mit Dateien ist eine Technik, die persistente Markdown-Dateien verwendet, um die Produktivität zu steigern","pt":"O skill de planejamento com arquivos permite usar arquivos markdown persistentes como memória de trabalho em disco","ru":"Навык планирования с файлами позволяет использовать постоянные файлы markdown как рабочую память на диске","ar":"مهارة التخطيط مع الملفات تسمح باستخدام ملفات markdown المستدامة كذاكرة عمل على القرص","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["使用持久的markdown文件作为工作内存","高效工作流程","支持多平台","自动检测python版本","支持命令行操作"],"ja":["永続的なMarkdownファイルを使用して作業メモリを実現","効率的なワークフロー","複数プラットフォームをサポート","Pythonバージョン自動検出","コマンドライン操作をサポート"],"ko":["지속적인 markdown 파일을 사용하여 작업 메모리를 구현","효율적인 작업 흐름","다중 플랫폼 지원","python 버전 자동 탐지","명령줄操作 지원"],"es":["Utiliza archivos markdown persistentes como memoria de trabajo en disco","Permite la planificación y organización de tareas de manera efectiva","Compatible con Linux, macOS y Windows","Script de detección de sesión anterior para evitar pérdida de datos","Integración con Python para una mayor flexibilidad"],"fr":["Utilise des fichiers markdown persistants comme mémoire de travail sur disque","Permet la planification et l''organisation de tâches de manière efficace","Compatible avec Linux, macOS et Windows","Script de détection de session précédente pour éviter la perte de données","Intégration avec Python pour une plus grande flexibilité"],"de":["Verwenden Sie persistente Markdown-Dateien als Arbeitsgedächtnis auf Disk","Ermöglicht die Planung und Organisation von Aufgaben auf effektive Weise","Kompatibel mit Linux, macOS und Windows","Skript zur Erkennung der vorherigen Sitzung, um Datenverlust zu vermeiden","Integration mit Python für eine größere Flexibilität"],"pt":["Uso de arquivos markdown persistentes","Verificação de sessões anteriores","Compatibilidade com Linux, macOS e Windows","Script de catch-up de sessão","Integração com Claude Plugin"],"ru":["Использование постоянных файлов markdown","Проверка предыдущих сессий","Совместимость с Linux, macOS и Windows","Сценарий catch-up сессии","Интеграция с Claude Plugin"],"ar":["استخدام ملفات markdown المستدامة","التحقق من Sessions السابقة","توافق مع Linux و macOS و Windows","سكربت catch-up Session","التكامل مع Claude Plugin"]},"keywords":{"zh":["文件规划","工作流程","持久的markdown文件","高效工作","开发者工具","命令行操作"],"ja":["ファイル計画","ワークフロー","永続的なMarkdownファイル","効率的なワークフロー","開発者ツール","コマンドライン操作"],"ko":["파일 계획","작업 흐름","지속적인 markdown 파일","효율적인 작업","개발자 도구","명령줄操作"],"es":["planificación con archivos","productividad","archivos markdown","memoria de trabajo en disco","python","linux","macos","windows"],"fr":["planification avec des fichiers","productivité","fichiers markdown","mémoire de travail sur disque","python","linux","macos","windows"],"de":["Planung mit Dateien","Produktivität","Markdown-Dateien","Arbeitsgedächtnis auf Disk","python","linux","macos","windows"],"pt":["planejamento com arquivos","arquivos markdown","memória de trabalho em disco","produtividade","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["планирование с файлами","файлы markdown","рабочая память на диске","производительность","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["التخطيط مع الملفات","ملفات markdown","ذاكرة عمل على القرص","إنتاجية","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"Treytucker05","repo":"pt-study-sop","repoPath":"Treytucker05/pt-study-sop","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"planning-with-files","description":"Implements Manus-style file-based planning for complex tasks. Creates task_plan.md, findings.md, and progress.md. Use when starting complex multi-step tasks, research projects, or any task requiring >5 tool calls. Now with automatic session recovery after /clear.","version":"2.4.1","bodyPreview":"# Planning with Files\n\nWork like Manus: Use persistent markdown files as your \"working memory on disk.\"\n\n## FIRST: Check for Previous Session (v2.2.0)\n\n**Before starting work**, check for unsynced context from a previous session:\n\n```bash\n# Linux/macOS (auto-detects python3 or python)\n$(command -v python3 || command -v python) ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/session-catchup.py \"$(pwd)\"\n```\n\n```powershell\n# Windows PowerShell\npython \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.codex\\skills\\planning-with-files\\scripts\\sessio","body":"# Planning with Files\n\nWork like Manus: Use persistent markdown files as your \"working memory on disk.\"\n\n## FIRST: Check for Previous Session (v2.2.0)\n\n**Before starting work**, check for unsynced context from a previous session:\n\n```bash\n# Linux/macOS (auto-detects python3 or python)\n$(command -v python3 || command -v python) ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/session-catchup.py \"$(pwd)\"\n```\n\n```powershell\n# Windows PowerShell\npython \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.codex\\skills\\planning-with-files\\scripts\\session-catchup.py\" (Get-Location)\n```\n\nIf catchup report shows unsynced context:\n1. Run `git diff --stat` to see actual code changes\n2. Read current planning files\n3. Update planning files based on catchup + git diff\n4. Then proceed with task\n\n## Important: Where Files Go\n\n- **Templates** are in `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/templates/`\n- **Your planning files** go in **your project directory**\n\n| Location | What Goes There |\n|----------|-----------------|\n| Skill directory (`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/`) | Templates, scripts, reference docs |\n| Your project directory | `task_plan.md`, `findings.md`, `progress.md` |\n\n## Quick Start\n\nBefore ANY complex task:\n\n1. **Create `task_plan.md`** — Use [templates/task_plan.md](templates/task_plan.md) as reference\n2. **Create `findings.md`** — Use [templates/findings.md](templates/findings.md) as reference\n3. **Create `progress.md`** — Use [templates/progress.md](templates/progress.md) as reference\n4. **Re-read plan before decisions** — Refreshes goals in attention window\n5. **Update after each phase** — Mark complete, log errors\n\n> **Note:** Planning files go in your project root, not the skill installation folder.\n\n## The Core Pattern\n\n```\nContext Window = RAM (volatile, limited)\nFilesystem = Disk (persistent, unlimited)\n\n→ Anything important gets written to disk.\n```\n\n## File Purposes\n\n| File | Purpose | When to Update |\n|------|---------|----------------|\n| `task_plan.md` | Phases, progress, decisions | After each phase |\n| `findings.md` | Research, discoveries | After ANY discovery |\n| `progress.md` | Session log, test results | Throughout session |\n\n## Critical Rules\n\n### 1. Create Plan First\nNever start a complex task without `task_plan.md`. Non-negotiable.\n\n### 2. The 2-Action Rule\n> \"After every 2 view/browser/search operations, IMMEDIATELY save key findings to text files.\"\n\nThis prevents visual/multimodal information from being lost.\n\n### 3. Read Before Decide\nBefore major decisions, read the plan file. This keeps goals in your attention window.\n\n### 4. Update After Act\nAfter completing any phase:\n- Mark phase status: `in_progress` → `complete`\n- Log any errors encountered\n- Note files created/modified\n\n### 5. Log ALL Errors\nEvery error goes in the plan file. This builds knowledge and prevents repetition.\n\n```markdown\n## Errors Encountered\n| Error | Attempt | Resolution |\n|-------|---------|------------|\n| FileNotFoundError | 1 | Created default config |\n| API timeout | 2 | Added retry logic |\n```\n\n### 6. Never Repeat Failures\n```\nif action_failed:\n    next_action != same_action\n```\nTrack what you tried. Mutate the approach.\n\n## The 3-Strike Error Protocol\n\n```\nATTEMPT 1: Diagnose & Fix\n  → Read error carefully\n  → Identify root cause\n  → Apply targeted fix\n\nATTEMPT 2: Alternative Approach\n  → Same error? Try different method\n  → Different tool? Different library?\n  → NEVER repeat exact same failing action\n\nATTEMPT 3: Broader Rethink\n  → Question assumptions\n  → Search for solutions\n  → Consider updating the plan\n\nAFTER 3 FAILURES: Escalate to User\n  → Explain what you tried\n  → Share the specific error\n  → Ask for guidance\n```\n\n## Read vs Write Decision Matrix\n\n| Situation | Action | Reason |\n|-----------|--------|--------|\n| Just wrote a file | DON''T read | Content still in context |\n| Viewed image/PDF | Write findings NOW | Multimodal → text before lost |\n| Browser returned data | Write to file | Screenshots don''t persist |\n| Starting new phase | Read plan/findings | Re-orient if context stale |\n| Error occurred | Read relevant file | Need current state to fix |\n| Resuming after gap | Read all planning files | Recover state |\n\n## The 5-Question Reboot Test\n\nIf you can answer these, your context management is solid:\n\n| Question | Answer Source |\n|----------|---------------|\n| Where am I? | Current phase in task_plan.md |\n| Where am I going? | Remaining phases |\n| What''s the goal? | Goal statement in plan |\n| What have I learned? | findings.md |\n| What have I done? | progress.md |\n\n## When to Use This Pattern\n\n**Use for:**\n- Multi-step tasks (3+ steps)\n- Research tasks\n- Building/creating projects\n- Tasks spanning many tool calls\n- Anything requiring organization\n\n**Skip for:**\n- Simple questions\n- Single-file edits\n- Quick lookups\n\n## Templates\n\nCopy these templates to start:\n\n- [templates/task_plan.md](templates/task_plan.md) — Phase tracking\n- [templates/findings.md](templates/findings.md) — Research storage\n- [templates/progress.md](templates/progress.md) — Session logging\n\n## Scripts\n\nHelper scripts for automation:\n\n- `scripts/init-session.sh` — Initialize all planning files\n- `scripts/check-complete.sh` — Verify all phases complete\n- `scripts/session-catchup.py` — Recover context from previous session (v2.2.0)\n\n## Advanced Topics\n\n- **Manus Principles:** See [reference.md](reference.md)\n- **Real Examples:** See [examples.md](examples.md)\n\n## Anti-Patterns\n\n| Don''t | Do Instead |\n|-------|------------|\n| Use TodoWrite for persistence | Create task_plan.md file |\n| State goals once and forget | Re-read plan before decisions |\n| Hide errors and retry silently | Log errors to plan file |\n| Stuff everything in context | Store large content in files |\n| Start executing immediately | Create plan file FIRST |\n| Repeat failed actions | Track attempts, mutate approach |\n| Create files in skill directory | Create files in your project |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:39:28.238Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude, AutoGPT, and LangChain that require persistent working memory and session management using markdown files.","zh":"适用于 Claude、AutoGPT 和 LangChain 等需要持久工作内存和使用 Markdown 文件进行会话管理的 AI 代理。","ja":"Claude、AutoGPT、LangChain などの持続的なワーキングメモリとセッション管理に Markdown ファイルを使用する必要がある AI エージェントに最適です。","ko":"클로드, 오토GPT, 랭체인 등 지속적인 작업 메모리와 마크다운 파일을 사용한 세션 관리가 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude, AutoGPT, and LangChain that require persistent working memory and session management using markdown files.","fr":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude, AutoGPT, and LangChain that require persistent working memory and session management using markdown files.","de":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude, AutoGPT, and LangChain that require persistent working memory and session management using markdown files.","pt":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude, AutoGPT, and LangChain that require persistent working memory and session management using markdown files.","ru":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude, AutoGPT, and LangChain that require persistent working memory and session management using markdown files.","ar":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude, AutoGPT, and LangChain that require persistent working memory and session management using markdown files."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to utilize markdown files as a ''working memory on disk'', enabling features like session catch-up using Python scripts and persistent context storage, leveraging protocols like bash and PowerShell for seamless integration.","zh":"赋予代理使用 Markdown 文件作为“磁盘上的工作内存”，启用使用 Python 脚本进行会话捕获和持久上下文存储等功能，并利用 bash 和 PowerShell 等协议实现无缝集成。","ja":"エージェントが Markdown ファイルを「ディスク上のワーキングメモリ」として使用できるようにし、Python スクリプトを使用したセッションのキャッチアップや永続的なコンテキストストレージなどの機能を可能にし、bash や PowerShell などのプロトコルを使用したシームレスな統合を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 마크다운 파일을 ''디스크상의 작업 메모리''로 사용할 수 있도록 하여 파이썬 스크립트를 사용한 세션 복구와 영속적인 컨텍스트 저장소 등의 기능을 가능하게 하고, bash와 PowerShell 등의 프로토콜을 사용한 무결점 통합을实现합니다.","es":"Empowers agents to utilize markdown files as a ''working memory on disk'', enabling features like session catch-up using Python scripts and persistent context storage, leveraging protocols like bash and PowerShell for seamless integration.","fr":"Empowers agents to utilize markdown files as a ''working memory on disk'', enabling features like session catch-up using Python scripts and persistent context storage, leveraging protocols like bash and PowerShell for seamless integration.","de":"Empowers agents to utilize markdown files as a ''working memory on disk'', enabling features like session catch-up using Python scripts and persistent context storage, leveraging protocols like bash and PowerShell for seamless integration.","pt":"Empowers agents to utilize markdown files as a ''working memory on disk'', enabling features like session catch-up using Python scripts and persistent context storage, leveraging protocols like bash and PowerShell for seamless integration.","ru":"Empowers agents to utilize markdown files as a ''working memory on disk'', enabling features like session catch-up using Python scripts and persistent context storage, leveraging protocols like bash and PowerShell for seamless integration.","ar":"Empowers agents to utilize markdown files as a ''working memory on disk'', enabling features like session catch-up using Python scripts and persistent context storage, leveraging protocols like bash and PowerShell for seamless integration."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating session recovery with Python scripts","Generating and managing persistent markdown files for context storage","Debugging unsynced context from previous sessions using session-catchup.py"],"zh":["使用 Python 脚本自动化会话恢复","生成和管理持久的 Markdown 文件用于上下文存储","使用 session-catchup.py 调试来自之前会话的非同步上下文"],"ja":["Python スクリプトを使用したセッションの自動復旧","永続的な Markdown ファイルの生成と管理を使用したコンテキストストレージ","session-catchup.py を使用した前のセッションからの非同期コンテキストのデバッグ"],"ko":["파이썬 스크립트를 사용한 세션 자동 복구","영속적인 마크다운 파일의 생성 및 관리를 사용한 컨텍스트 저장소","session-catchup.py를 사용한 이전 세션의 비동기 컨텍스트 디버깅"],"es":["Automating session recovery with Python scripts","Generating and managing persistent markdown files for context storage","Debugging unsynced context from previous sessions using session-catchup.py"],"fr":["Automating session recovery with Python scripts","Generating and managing persistent markdown files for context storage","Debugging unsynced context from previous sessions using session-catchup.py"],"de":["Automating session recovery with Python scripts","Generating and managing persistent markdown files for context storage","Debugging unsynced context from previous sessions using session-catchup.py"],"pt":["Automating session recovery with Python scripts","Generating and managing persistent markdown files for context storage","Debugging unsynced context from previous sessions using session-catchup.py"],"ru":["Automating session recovery with Python scripts","Generating and managing persistent markdown files for context storage","Debugging unsynced context from previous sessions using session-catchup.py"],"ar":["Automating session recovery with Python scripts","Generating and managing persistent markdown files for context storage","Debugging unsynced context from previous sessions using session-catchup.py"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Python 3.x installation","Needs filesystem access for reading and writing markdown files","Dependent on specific script execution (e.g., session-catchup.py) for full functionality"],"zh":["需要 Python 3.x 的安装","需要文件系统访问以读写 Markdown 文件","依赖于特定的脚本执行（例如 session-catchup.py）以实现全部功能"],"ja":["Python 3.x のインストールが必要","Markdown ファイルの読み書きのためにファイルシステムへのアクセスが必要","特定のスクリプトの実行（例：session-catchup.py）に依存して完全な機能を実現する"],"ko":["파이썬 3.x 설치가 필요","마크다운 파일의 읽기 및 쓰기 위해 파일 시스템 접근이 필요","전체 기능을 구현하기 위해 특정 스크립트 실행(예: session-catchup.py)에 의존"],"es":["Requires Python 3.x installation","Needs filesystem access for reading and writing markdown files","Dependent on specific script execution (e.g., session-catchup.py) for full functionality"],"fr":["Requires Python 3.x installation","Needs filesystem access for reading and writing markdown files","Dependent on specific script execution (e.g., session-catchup.py) for full functionality"],"de":["Requires Python 3.x installation","Needs filesystem access for reading and writing markdown files","Dependent on specific script execution (e.g., session-catchup.py) for full functionality"],"pt":["Requires Python 3.x installation","Needs filesystem access for reading and writing markdown files","Dependent on specific script execution (e.g., session-catchup.py) for full functionality"],"ru":["Requires Python 3.x installation","Needs filesystem access for reading and writing markdown files","Dependent on specific script execution (e.g., session-catchup.py) for full functionality"],"ar":["Requires Python 3.x installation","Needs filesystem access for reading and writing markdown files","Dependent on specific script execution (e.g., session-catchup.py) for full functionality"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('blahami2/event-manager/qa-write-tests', 'community', 'blahami2', 'event-manager', 'blahami2/event-manager', 'qa-write-tests', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.469Z', '2026-02-18T08:38:38.791Z', NULL, '{"id":"blahami2/event-manager/qa-write-tests","name":"qa-write-tests","description":{"zh":"qa-write-tests技能可以为给定代码生成全面的单元测试，涵盖正常路径、边界情况和错误条件","ja":"qa-write-testsスキルは、指定されたコードのための包括的なユニットテストを生成し、正常なパス、境界状況、エラーコンディションをカバーする","ko":"qa-write-tests 스킬은 주어진 코드에 대한 포괄적인 유닛 테스트를 생성하여 정상 경로, 경계 상황 및 오류 조건을 다룹니다","es":"qa-write-tests genera pruebas unitarias comprehensivas para el código dado, cubriendo caminos felices, casos límite y condiciones de error","fr":"qa-write-tests génère des tests unitaires complets pour le code donné, couvrant les chemins heureux, les cas limites et les conditions d''erreur","de":"qa-write-tests erzeugt umfassende Einheitstests für den gegebenen Code, einschließlich glücklicher Pfade, Grenzfälle und Fehlerbedingungen","pt":"A habilidade qa-write-tests gera testes de unidade completos para o código fornecido, cobrindo caminhos felizes, casos de bordo e condições de erro.","ru":"Навык qa-write-tests генерирует комплексные юнит-тесты для заданного кода, покрывая счастливые пути, граничные случаи и условия ошибок.","ar":"توليد مهارة qa-write-tests اختبارات وحدة شاملة للكود المحدد، تغطي المسارات السعيدة، وحالات الحدود والشروط الخطأ.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"自动化单元测试生成 - qa-write-tests","ja":"自動化ユニットテスト生成 - qa-write-tests","ko":"자동화 유닛 테스트 생성 - qa-write-tests","es":"Generar pruebas unitarias con qa-write-tests","fr":"Générer des tests unitaires avec qa-write-tests","de":"Erstellen von Einheitstests mit qa-write-tests","pt":"Gere Testes de Unidade Completos com qa-write-tests","ru":"Генерация комплексных юнит-тестов с помощью qa-write-tests","ar":"إنشاء اختبارات وحدة شاملة مع qa-write-tests"