es Applications Asynchrones","de":"Rust-Ökosystem: Optimierung von asynchronen Anwendungen","pt":"Rust Ecosystem: Otimizando Práticas de Engenharia","ru":"Экосистема Rust: оптимизация инженерных практик","ar":"بيئة راست: تحسين ممارسات الهندسة","en":"rust-ecosystem"},"description":{"zh":"Rust 生态系统提供异步运行时和模块化技能编排，帮助开发者提高开发效率","ja":"Rust エコシステムは非同期ランタイムとモジュラー スキル オーケストレーションを提供し、開発者の開発効率を向上させる","ko":"Rust 생태계는 비동기 런타임 및 모듈화된 스킬 오케스트레이션을 제공하여 개발자의 개발 효율성을 높여줍니다","es":"El ecosistema Rust ofrece capacidades de ingeniería avanzadas para aplicaciones asíncronas, con runtimes como Tokio y async-std","fr":"L''écosystème Rust offre des capacités d''ingénierie avancées pour les applications asynchrones, avec des runtimes tels que Tokio et async-std","de":"Das Rust-Ökosystem bietet erweiterte Ingenieursfähigkeiten für asynchrone Anwendungen, mit Laufzeiten wie Tokio und async-std","pt":"A camada de capacidade de especialista em IA para práticas de engenharia Rust, centrada na orquestração de habilidades modulares e cadeias de execução colabo...","ru":"Экспертная возможность ИИ для инженерных практик Rust, ориентированная на модульную оркестрацию навыков и совместные цепочки выполнения","ar":"طبقة الخبرة الإصطناعية للغة راست، مركزة على أوركسترا المهارات المتنقلة والسلاسل التنفيذية التعاونية","en":"An AI expert capability layer for Rust engineering practices, centered on modular skill orchestration and collaborative execution chains. It turns Rust’s cor..."},"definition":{"en":"An AI expert capability layer for Rust engineering practices, centered on modular skill orchestration and collaborative execution chains. It turns Rust’s core knowledge structures into callable reasoning and decision units, enabling diagnosis, design, and optimization in complex real-world scenarios."},"features":{"zh":["异步运行时支持","模块化技能编排","tokio、async-std、smol 和 async-executors 支持","提高开发效率","适用于复杂的实时场景"],"ja":["非同期ランタイムのサポート","モジュラー スキル オーケストレーション","tokio、async-std、smol、async-executors のサポート","開発効率の向上","複雑なリアルタイム シナリオに適している"],"ko":["비동기 런타임 지원","모듈화된 스킬 오케스트레이션","tokio、async-std、smol 및 async-executors 지원","개발 효율성 향상","복잡한 실시간 시나리오에 적합"],"es":["Orquestación de habilidades modulares","Cadenas de ejecución colaborativas","Compatibilidad con runtimes como Tokio y async-std","Unificada interfaz para runtimes","Aplicaciones asíncronas de alto rendimiento"],"fr":["Orchestration de compétences modulaires","Chaînes d''exécution collaboratives","Compatibilité avec des runtimes tels que Tokio et async-std","Interface unifiée pour les runtimes","Applications asynchrones à haute performance"],"de":["Modulare Fähigkeitsorchestrierung","Kollaborative Ausführungsketten","Kompatibilität mit Laufzeiten wie Tokio und async-std","Einheitliche Schnittstelle für Laufzeiten","Asynchrone Anwendungen mit hoher Leistung"],"pt":["Tempo de execução assíncrono","Orquestração de habilidades modulares","Cadeias de execução colaborativas","Diagnóstico e design de sistemas complexos","Otimização de desempenho"],"ru":["Асинхронный режим выполнения","Модульная оркестрация навыков","Совместные цепочки выполнения","Диагностика и проектирование сложных систем","Оптимизация производительности"],"ar":["زمن تشغيل غير متزامن","أوركسترا مهارات متنقلة","سلاسل تنفيذ تعاونية","تشخيص وتصميم أنظمة معقدة","تحسين الأداء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Rust 生态系统","异步运行时","模块化技能编排","tokio","async-std","smol","async-executors","Rust 开发"],"ja":["Rust エコシステム","非同期ランタイム","モジュラー スキル オーケストレーション","tokio","async-std","smol","async-executors","Rust 開発"],"ko":["Rust 생태계","비동기 런타임","모듈화된 스킬 오케스트레이션","tokio","async-std","smol","async-executors","Rust 개발"],"es":["Rust ecosistema","aplicaciones asíncronas","runtimes","Tokio","async-std","ingeniería de software","desarrollo de aplicaciones","optimización de rendimiento"],"fr":["Écosystème Rust","applications asynchrones","runtimes","Tokio","async-std","ingénierie logicielle","développement d''applications","optimisation des performances"],"de":["Rust-Ökosystem","asynchrone Anwendungen","Laufzeiten","Tokio","async-std","Software-Entwicklung","Anwendungs-Entwicklung","Leistungs-Optimierung"],"pt":["Rust Ecosystem","Tempo de execução assíncrono","Orquestração de habilidades","Desenvolvimento de software","Engenharia de software","Linguagem de programação Rust"],"ru":["Экосистема Rust","Асинхронный режим выполнения","Модульная оркестрация навыков","Разработка программного обеспечения","Инженерия программного обеспечения","Язык программирования Rust"],"ar":["بيئة راست","زمن تشغيل غير متزامن","أوركسترا مهارات","تطوير البرمجيات","هندسة البرمجيات","لغة برمجة راست"]}},"owner":"huiali","repo":"rust-skills","repoPath":"huiali/rust-skills","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rust-ecosystem","description":"Rust ecosystem expert covering crate selection, library recommendations, framework comparisons, async runtime choices (tokio, async-std), and common tools.","bodyPreview":"## Async Runtimes\n\n| Runtime | Characteristics | Use Case |\n|---------|----------------|----------|\n| **tokio** | Most popular, feature-rich | General async applications |\n| **async-std** | std-like API | Prefer std-style APIs |\n| **smol** | Minimal, embeddable | Lightweight applications |\n| **async-executors** | Unified interface | Need runtime portability |\n\n```toml\n# Web services\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\"] }\naxum = \"0.7\"\n\n# Lightweight\nasync-std = \"1\"\n\n# Minimal\nsmol = \"2\"\n`","body":"## Async Runtimes\n\n| Runtime | Characteristics | Use Case |\n|---------|----------------|----------|\n| **tokio** | Most popular, feature-rich | General async applications |\n| **async-std** | std-like API | Prefer std-style APIs |\n| **smol** | Minimal, embeddable | Lightweight applications |\n| **async-executors** | Unified interface | Need runtime portability |\n\n```toml\n# Web services\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\"] }\naxum = \"0.7\"\n\n# Lightweight\nasync-std = \"1\"\n\n# Minimal\nsmol = \"2\"\n```\n\n\n## Solution Patterns\n\n### Pattern 1: Web Service Stack\n\n```toml\n[dependencies]\n# Async runtime\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\"] }\n\n# Web framework\naxum = \"0.7\"\n\n# Database\nsqlx = { version = \"0.7\", features = [\"runtime-tokio\", \"postgres\"] }\n\n# Serialization\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = \"1\"\n\n# Error handling\nanyhow = \"1\"\nthiserror = \"1\"\n\n# Tracing\ntracing = \"0.1\"\ntracing-subscriber = \"0.3\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 2: CLI Tool Stack\n\n```toml\n[dependencies]\n# Argument parsing\nclap = { version = \"4\", features = [\"derive\"] }\n\n# Error handling\nanyhow = \"1\"\n\n# Config\nconfig = \"0.13\"\ndotenvy = \"0.15\"\n\n# Progress\nindicatif = \"0.17\"\n\n# Terminal colors\ncolored = \"2\"\n```\n\n### Pattern 3: Data Processing\n\n```toml\n[dependencies]\n# Parallelism\nrayon = \"1\"\n\n# CSV\ncsv = \"1\"\n\n# Serialization\nserde = { version = \"1\", features = [\"derive\"] }\nserde_json = \"1\"\n\n# HTTP client\nreqwest = { version = \"0.11\", features = [\"json\", \"blocking\"] }\n```\n\n\n## Web Frameworks\n\n| Framework | Characteristics | Performance |\n|-----------|----------------|-------------|\n| **axum** | Tower middleware, type-safe | High |\n| **actix-web** | Highest performance | Highest |\n| **rocket** | Developer-friendly | Medium |\n| **warp** | Compositional, filters | High |\n\n```rust\n// axum example\nuse axum::{Router, routing::get, Json};\nuse serde::Serialize;\n\n#[derive(Serialize)]\nstruct User {\n    id: u64,\n    name: String,\n}\n\nasync fn get_user() -> Json<User> {\n    Json(User {\n        id: 1,\n        name: \"Alice\".to_string(),\n    })\n}\n\nlet app = Router::new()\n    .route(\"/user\", get(get_user));\n```\n\n\n## Serialization\n\n| Library | Characteristics | Performance |\n|---------|----------------|-------------|\n| **serde** | Standard choice | High |\n| **bincode** | Binary, compact | Highest |\n| **postcard** | no_std, embedded | High |\n| **ron** | Readable format | Medium |\n\n```rust\nuse serde::{Serialize, Deserialize};\n\n#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]\nstruct User {\n    id: u64,\n    name: String,\n}\n\n// JSON\nlet json = serde_json::to_string(&user)?;\nlet user: User = serde_json::from_str(&json)?;\n\n// Binary (more efficient)\nlet bytes = bincode::serialize(&user)?;\nlet user: User = bincode::deserialize(&bytes)?;\n```\n\n\n## HTTP Clients\n\n| Library | Characteristics |\n|---------|----------------|\n| **reqwest** | Most popular, easy to use |\n| **ureq** | Sync, simple |\n| **surf** | Async, modern |\n| **hyper** | Low-level, flexible |\n\n```rust\n// reqwest - async\nlet response = reqwest::Client::new()\n    .post(\"https://api.example.com\")\n    .json(&payload)\n    .send()\n    .await?\n    .json::<Response>()\n    .await?;\n\n// ureq - sync (no async runtime needed)\nlet response: Response = ureq::post(\"https://api.example.com\")\n    .send_json(&payload)?\n    .into_json()?;\n```\n\n\n## Databases\n\n| Type | Library |\n|------|---------|\n| ORM | **sqlx**, diesel, sea-orm |\n| Raw SQL | **sqlx**, tokio-postgres |\n| NoSQL | mongodb, redis |\n| Connection pool | **sqlx**, deadpool, r2d2 |\n\n```rust\n// sqlx with compile-time checked queries\nuse sqlx::PgPool;\n\nlet pool = PgPool::connect(&database_url).await?;\n\nlet user = sqlx::query_as!(\n    User,\n    \"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE id = $1\",\n    user_id\n)\n.fetch_one(&pool)\n.await?;\n```\n\n\n## Concurrency & Parallelism\n\n| Scenario | Recommendation |\n|----------|---------------|\n| Data parallelism | **rayon** |\n| Work stealing | **crossbeam**, tokio |\n| Channels | **tokio::sync**, crossbeam, flume |\n| Atomics | **std::sync::atomic** |\n\n```rust\n// rayon - easy parallelism\nuse rayon::prelude::*;\n\nlet sum: i32 = data\n    .par_iter()\n    .map(|x| expensive_computation(x))\n    .sum();\n```\n\n\n## Error Handling\n\n| Library | Use Case |\n|---------|----------|\n| **thiserror** | Library error types |\n| **anyhow** | Application error propagation |\n| **snafu** | Structured errors |\n\n```rust\n// thiserror - for libraries\nuse thiserror::Error;\n\n#[derive(Error, Debug)]\npub enum MyError {\n    #[error(\"I/O error: {0}\")]\n    Io(#[from] std::io::Error),\n\n    #[error(\"Invalid data: {msg}\")]\n    Invalid { msg: String },\n}\n\n// anyhow - for applications\nuse anyhow::{Context, Result};\n\nfn load_config() -> Result<Config> {\n    let content = std::fs::read_to_string(\"config.toml\")\n        .context(\"failed to read config file\")?;\n\n    toml::from_str(&content)\n        .context(\"failed to parse config\")\n}\n```\n\n\n## Common Tools\n\n| Scenario | Library |\n|----------|---------|\n| CLI parsing | **clap** (v4), structopt |\n| Logging | **tracing**, log |\n| Config | **config**, dotenvy |\n| Testing | **tempfile**, rstest, proptest |\n| Time | **chrono**, time |\n| Random | **rand** |\n| Regex | **regex** |\n\n\n## Crate Selection Principles\n\n1. **Active maintenance**: Check GitHub activity, recent updates\n2. **Download count**: Reference crates.io downloads\n3. **MSRV**: Minimum Supported Rust Version compatibility\n4. **Dependencies**: Number and security of dependencies\n5. **Documentation**: Complete docs and examples\n6. **License**: MIT/Apache2 compatibility\n\n```bash\n# Check crate info\ncargo info <crate-name>\n\n# Check dependencies\ncargo tree\n\n# Security audit\ncargo audit\n\n# License check\ncargo deny check licenses\n```\n\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Identify Need\n\n```\nWhat problem to solve?\n  → Web service? Choose framework (axum/actix)\n  → CLI tool? Use clap + anyhow\n  → Data processing? Use rayon\n  → Database access? Use sqlx\n```\n\n### Step 2: Evaluate Options\n\n```\nCheck:\n  → crates.io download count\n  → GitHub stars and activity\n  → Documentation quality\n  → Recent releases\n  → Community support\n```\n\n### Step 3: Verify Safety\n\n```bash\n# Security audit\ncargo audit\n\n# License compatibility\ncargo deny check\n\n# Dependency tree\ncargo tree -i <crate>\n```\n\n\n## Deprecated Patterns → Modern\n\n| Deprecated | Modern | Reason |\n|-----------|--------|--------|\n| `lazy_static` | `std::sync::OnceLock` | std built-in |\n| `rand::thread_rng` | `rand::rng()` | New API |\n| `failure` | `thiserror` + `anyhow` | More popular |\n| `serde_derive` | `serde` (unified) | Simpler imports |\n\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| Scenario | Recommended Stack |\n|----------|------------------|\n| Web service | axum + tokio + sqlx + serde |\n| CLI tool | clap + anyhow + config |\n| Serialization | serde + (json/bincode/postcard) |\n| Parallel compute | rayon |\n| Config management | config + dotenvy |\n| Logging | tracing + tracing-subscriber |\n| Testing | tempfile + rstest + proptest |\n| Date/time | chrono or time |\n\n\n## Review Checklist\n\nWhen selecting crates:\n\n- [ ] Crate is actively maintained (updated within 6 months)\n- [ ] Good documentation and examples\n- [ ] Reasonable dependency count\n- [ ] No known security issues (cargo audit)\n- [ ] Compatible license (MIT/Apache2)\n- [ ] MSRV compatible with project\n- [ ] High download count and community usage\n- [ ] Stable API (1.0+ or widely used)\n\n\n## Verification Commands\n\n```bash\n# Search crates\ncargo search <keyword>\n\n# Get crate info\ncargo info <crate-name>\n\n# Check dependencies\ncargo tree\n\n# Security audit\ncargo audit\n\n# License check\ncargo deny check\n\n# Check for updates\ncargo outdated\n```\n\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n### 1. Too Many Dependencies\n\n**Symptom**: Long compile times, dependency conflicts\n\n```toml\n# ❌ Avoid: unnecessary dependencies\n[dependencies]\n# Don''t need full tokio if only using channels\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\"] }\n\n# ✅ Better: minimal features\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"sync\"] }\n```\n\n### 2. Unmaintained Crates\n\n**Symptom**: Security vulnerabilities, incompatibilities\n\n```bash\n# Check last update\ncargo info <crate-name>\n\n# Check for alternatives\ncargo search <similar-crate>\n```\n\n### 3. Version Conflicts\n\n**Symptom**: Build failures, duplicate dependencies\n\n```bash\n# Diagnose conflicts\ncargo tree -d\n\n# Use same version across workspace\n[workspace.dependencies]\nserde = \"1\"\n```\n\n\n## Related Skills\n\n- **rust-async** - Async runtime patterns\n- **rust-web** - Web framework usage\n- **rust-error** - Error handling libraries\n- **rust-testing** - Testing libraries\n- **rust-performance** - Performance-critical crates\n\n\n## Localized Reference\n\n- **Chinese version**: [SKILL_ZH.md](./SKILL_ZH.md) - 完整中文版本，包含所有内容\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:42:26.052Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Systems Programming Agents requiring advanced Rust ecosystem integration and async runtime management.","zh":"适用于需要高级Rust生态系统集成和异步运行时管理的系统编程代理。","ja":"Rustエコシステムの高度な統合と非同期ランタイム管理を必要とするシステムプログラミングエージェントに適しています。","ko":"고급 Rust 생태계 통합 및 비동기 런타임 관리가 필요한 시스템 프로그래밍 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de programación de sistemas que requieren una integración avanzada del ecosistema Rust y una gestión de tiempo de ejecución asíncrona.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de programmation de systèmes nécessitant une intégration avancée de l''écosystème Rust et une gestion de runtime asynchrone.","de":"Ideal für Systemprogrammierungsagenten, die eine erweiterte Rust-Ökosystem-Integration und eine asynchrone Laufzeitverwaltung erfordern.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Programação de Sistemas que exigem integração avançada com o ecossistema Rust e gerenciamento de runtime assíncrono.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов системного программирования, требующих расширенной интеграции с экосистемой Rust и управления асинхронной средой выполнения.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء برمجة الأنظمة التي تتطلب تكاملاً متقدماً مع بيئة Rust وإدارة وقت التشغيل غير المتزامن."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage tokio, async-std, smol, and async-executors for building scalable and efficient async applications, utilizing features like unified interfaces and runtime portability, while managing dependencies through toml configurations.","zh":"赋予代理使用tokio、async-std、smol和async-executors构建可扩展和高效的异步应用的能力，利用统一接口和运行时可移植性等功能，同时通过toml配置管理依赖项。","ja":"tokio、async-std、smol、async-executorsを使用してスケーラブルで効率的な非同期アプリケーションを構築するエージェントの能力を提供し、統一されたインターフェイスやランタイムの移植性などの機能を利用しながら、toml構成を介して依存関係を管理します。","ko":"tokio, async-std, smol 및 async-executors를 사용하여 확장 가능하고 효율적인 비동기 애플리케이션을 구축할 수 있는 에이전트의 능력을 제공하며, 통일된 인터페이스 및 런타임 이식성과 같은 기능을 활용하여 toml 구성 통해 의존성을 관리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar tokio, async-std, smol y async-executors para construir aplicaciones asíncronas escalables y eficientes, utilizando características como interfaces unificadas y portabilidad de tiempo de ejecución, mientras se gestionan las dependencias a través de configuraciones toml.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''utiliser tokio, async-std, smol et async-executors pour construire des applications asynchrones évolutives et efficaces, en utilisant des fonctionnalités comme des interfaces unifiées et une portabilité du runtime, tout en gérant les dépendances via des configurations toml.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, tokio, async-std, smol und async-executors zu nutzen, um skalierbare und effiziente asynchrone Anwendungen zu erstellen, die Funktionen wie einheitliche Schnittstellen und Laufzeitportabilität verwenden, während Abhängigkeiten über toml-Konfigurationen verwaltet werden.","pt":"Permite que os agentes aproveitem tokio, async-std, smol e async-executors para criar aplicações assíncronas escaláveis e eficientes, utilizando recursos como interfaces unificadas e portabilidade de runtime, enquanto gerencia dependências através de configurações toml.","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать tokio, async-std, smol и async-executors для создания масштабируемых и эффективных асинхронных приложений, используя такие функции, как унифицированные интерфейсы и переносимость среды выполнения, при управлении зависимостями через конфигурации toml.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من الاستفادة من tokio و async-std و smol و async-executors لبناء تطبيقات غير متزامنة قابلة للتطوير وفعالة، باستخدام ميزات مثل الواجهات الموحدة وقابلية نقل وقت التشغيل، مع إدارة التبعيات من خلال تكوينات toml."},"useCases":{"en":["Designing modular skill orchestration for complex Rust projects","Optimizing async runtime performance using tokio and async-std","Building lightweight applications with smol and async-executors"],"zh":["为复杂的Rust项目设计模块化的技能编排","使用tokio和async-std优化异步运行时性能","使用smol和async-executors构建轻量级应用"],"ja":["複雑なRustプロジェクトのためのモジュラーシステムのスキルオーケストレーションの設計","tokioとasync-stdを使用した非同期ランタイムのパフォーマンス最適化","smolとasync-executorsを使用した軽量アプリケーションの構築"],"ko":["복잡한 Rust 프로젝트를 위한 모듈화된 스킬 오케스트레이션 설계","tokio 및 async-std를 사용한 비동기 런타임 성능 최적화","smol 및 async-executors를 사용한 경량 애플리케이션 구축"],"es":["Diseñar una orquestación de habilidades modulares para proyectos Rust complejos","Optimizar el rendimiento del tiempo de ejecución asíncrono utilizando tokio y async-std","Construir aplicaciones ligeras con smol y async-executors"],"fr":["Concevoir une orchestration de compétences modulaires pour des projets Rust complexes","Optimiser les performances du runtime asynchrone en utilisant tokio et async-std","Construire des applications légères avec smol et async-executors"],"de":["Entwerfen einer modularen Fähigkeitsorchesterierung für komplexe Rust-Projekte","Optimieren der asynchronen Laufzeitleistung mit tokio und async-std","Erstellen von leichten Anwendungen mit smol und async-executors"],"pt":["Projetar orquestração modular de habilidades para projetos complexos em Rust","Otimizar o desempenho do runtime assíncrono usando tokio e async-std","Construir aplicações leves com smol e async-executors"],"ru":["Проектирование модульной оркестровки навыков для сложных проектов на Rust","Оптимизация производительности асинхронной среды выполнения с использованием tokio и async-std","Создание легковесных приложений с помощью smol и async-executors"],"ar":["تصميم أوركسترا المهارات المعيارية لمشاريع Rust المعقدة","تحسين أداء وقت التشغيل غير المتزامن باستخدام tokio و async-std","بناء تطبيقات خفيفة الوزن باستخدام smol و async-executors"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rust programming knowledge","Limited to Rust ecosystem and async runtime management"],"zh":["需要Rust编程知识","仅限于Rust生态系统和异步运行时管理"],"ja":["Rustプログラミングの知識が必要","Rustエコシステムと非同期ランタイム管理に限定される"],"ko":["Rust 프로그래밍 지식이 필요","Rust 생태계 및 비동기 런타임 관리에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere conocimientos de programación Rust","Limitado al ecosistema Rust y la gestión de tiempo de ejecución asíncrona"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances en programmation Rust","Limité à l''écosystème Rust et à la gestion de runtime asynchrone"],"de":["Benötigt Rust-Programmierkenntnisse","Begrenzt auf das Rust-Ökosystem und die asynchrone Laufzeitverwaltung"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento de programação em Rust","Limitado ao ecossistema Rust e ao gerenciamento de runtime assíncrono"],"ru":["Требует знания программирования на Rust","Ограничено экосистемой Rust и управлением асинхронной средой выполнения"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة ببرمجة Rust","مقتصر على بيئة Rust وإدارة وقت التشغيل غير المتزامن"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
