tions structurées","Planification et mise en œuvre systématiques","Classification et étiquetage des spécifications","Budgets de jetons et artefacts auditable","Maximum de 3 clarifications en utilisant des heuristiques de supposition informée"],"de":["Umwandlung von Funktionsanforderungen in strukturierte Spezifikationen","Systematische Planung und Umsetzung","Klassifizierung und Kennzeichnung von Spezifikationen","Token-Budgets und überprüfbare Artefakte","Maximal 3 Klarstellungen unter Verwendung von heuristischen Vermutungsstrategien"],"pt":["Transformação de solicitações de recursos de linguagem natural em especificações estruturadas","Classificação sistemática e abordagem de clarificação mínima","Orquestração da fase de especificação com qualidade e orçamento de tokens","Produção de artefatos auditáveis e critérios de sucesso mensuráveis","Utilização de heurísticas de adivinhação informada para padrões técnicos","Integração com fluxos de trabalho downstream"],"ru":["Преобразование запросов функций естественного языка в структурированные спецификации","Систематическая классификация и минимальный подход к разъяснению","Оркестровка фазы спецификации с качеством и бюджетом токенов","Производство аудиторских артефактов и измеримых критериев успеха","Использование эвристических алгоритмов для технических шаблонов","Интеграция с рабочими процессами downstream"],"ar":["تحويل طلبات الميزات اللغة الطبيعية إلى مواصفات منظم","التصنيف النظامي ومنهجية التفسير الأقل","أوركسترا مرحلة التخصيص مع الجودة وميزانية الرموز","إنتاج مكونات قابلة للتدقيق ومعيار نجاح قابل للقياس","استخدام خوارزميات التخمين للمعايير الفنية","التكامل مع سير العمل المتدفق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development"],"ja":["Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development"],"ko":["Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development","Spec-Driven Development"],"es":["desarrollo de especificaciones","transformación de ideas de producto","planificación de productos","implementación de productos","especificaciones estructuradas","clasificación de especificaciones"],"fr":["développement de spécifications","transformation d''idées de produit","planification de produits","mise en œuvre de produits","spécifications structurées","classification de spécifications"],"de":["Spezifikationsentwicklung","Umwandlung von Produktideen","Produktplanung","Produktumsetzung","strukturierte Spezifikationen","Klassifizierung von Spezifikationen"],"pt":["desenvolvimento dirigido por especificações","transformação de solicitações de recursos","classificação sistemática","abordagem de clarificação mínima","orquestração da fase de especificação","qualidade e orçamento de tokens","artefatos auditáveis","critérios de sucesso mensuráveis","heurísticas de adivinhação informada"],"ru":["разработка на основе спецификаций","преобразование запросов функций","систематическая классификация","минимальный подход к разъяснению","оркестровка фазы спецификации","качество и бюджет токенов","аудиторские артефакты","измеримые критерии успеха","эвристические алгоритмы"],"ar":["التطوير الموجه بالمواصفات","تحويل طلبات الميزات","التصنيف النظامي","منهجية التفسير الأقل","أوركسترا مرحلة التخصيص","الجودة وميزانية الرموز","مكونات قابلة للتدقيق","معيار نجاح قابل للقياس","خوارزميات التخمين"]}},"owner":"marcusgoll","repo":"Spec-Flow","repoPath":"marcusgoll/Spec-Flow","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"specification-phase","description":"Provides standard operating procedures for the /specify phase including feature classification (HAS_UI, IS_IMPROVEMENT, HAS_METRICS, HAS_DEPLOYMENT_IMPACT), research depth determination, clarification strategy (max 3, informed guesses for defaults), and roadmap integration. Use when executing /specify command, classifying features, generating structured specs, or determining research depth for planning phase. (project)","bodyPreview":"<objective>\nTransform natural language feature requests into structured specifications that enable planning and implementation through systematic classification, informed guess strategy, and minimal clarification approach.\n\nThis skill orchestrates the /specify phase, producing spec.md with measurable success criteria, classification flags for downstream workflows, and maximum 3 clarifications using informed guess heuristics for technical defaults.\n\n**Core responsibilities**:\n\n- Parse and normali","body":"<objective>\nTransform natural language feature requests into structured specifications that enable planning and implementation through systematic classification, informed guess strategy, and minimal clarification approach.\n\nThis skill orchestrates the /specify phase, producing spec.md with measurable success criteria, classification flags for downstream workflows, and maximum 3 clarifications using informed guess heuristics for technical defaults.\n\n**Core responsibilities**:\n\n- Parse and normalize feature input to slug format (kebab-case, no filler words)\n- Check roadmap integration to reuse existing context\n- Load project documentation context (docs/project/) to prevent hallucination\n- Classify feature with 4 flags (HAS_UI, IS_IMPROVEMENT, HAS_METRICS, HAS_DEPLOYMENT_IMPACT)\n- Determine research depth based on complexity (FLAG_COUNT: 0→minimal, 1→standard, ≥2→full)\n- Apply informed guess strategy for non-critical technical decisions\n- Generate ≤3 clarifications (only scope/security critical)\n- Write measurable success criteria (quantifiable, user-facing)\n\nInputs: User''s feature description, existing roadmap entries, project docs (if exists), codebase context\nOutputs: specs/NNN-slug/spec.md, NOTES.md, state.yaml, updated roadmap (if FROM_ROADMAP=true)\nExpected duration: 10-15 minutes\n</objective>\n\n<quick_start>\nExecute /specify workflow in 9 steps:\n\n1. **Parse and normalize input** - Generate slug (remove filler words: \"add\", \"create\", \"we want to\"), assign feature number (NNN)\n2. **Check roadmap integration** - Search roadmap for slug match, reuse context if found (saves ~10 minutes)\n3. **Load project documentation** - Extract tech stack, API patterns, existing entities from docs/project/ (prevents hallucination)\n4. **Classify feature** - Set HAS_UI, IS_IMPROVEMENT, HAS_METRICS, HAS_DEPLOYMENT_IMPACT flags using decision tree\n5. **Determine research depth** - FLAG_COUNT → minimal (0), standard (1), full (≥2)\n6. **Apply informed guess strategy** - Use defaults for performance (<500ms), rate limits (100/min), auth (OAuth2), retention (90d logs)\n7. **Generate clarifications** - Max 3 critical clarifications (scope > security > UX > technical priority matrix)\n8. **Write success criteria** - Measurable, quantifiable, user-facing outcomes (not tech-specific)\n9. **Generate artifacts and commit** - Create spec.md, NOTES.md, state.yaml, update roadmap\n\nKey principle: Use informed guesses for non-critical decisions, document assumptions, limit clarifications to ≤3.\n</quick_start>\n\n<prerequisites>\n<environment_checks>\nBefore executing /specify phase:\n- [ ] Git working tree clean (no uncommitted changes)\n- [ ] Not on main branch (create feature branch: `feature/NNN-slug`)\n- [ ] Required templates exist in `.spec-flow/templates/`\n- [ ] If project docs exist, docs/project/ directory accessible\n</environment_checks>\n\n<knowledge_requirements>\nRequired understanding before execution:\n\n- **Classification decision tree**: UI keywords vs backend-only exclusions, improvement = baseline + target, metrics = user tracking, deployment = env vars/migrations/breaking changes\n- **Informed guess heuristics**: Performance (<500ms), retention (90d logs, 365d analytics), rate limits (100/min), auth (OAuth2), error handling (user-friendly + error ID)\n- **Clarification prioritization matrix**: Critical (scope, security, breaking changes) > High (UX) > Medium (performance SLA, tech stack) > Low (error messages, rate limits)\n- **Slug generation rules**: Remove filler words, lowercase kebab-case, 50 char limit, fuzzy match roadmap\n\nSee [reference.md](reference.md) for complete decision trees and heuristics.\n</knowledge_requirements>\n\n<warnings>\n- **Over-clarification**: >3 clarifications indicates missing informed guesses (check reference.md for defaults)\n- **Wrong classification**: Backend workers/APIs with HAS_UI=true wastes time generating UI artifacts\n- **Roadmap mismatch**: Filler words in slug prevent roadmap match (\"add-student-dashboard\" vs \"student-dashboard\")\n- **Vague success criteria**: \"Works correctly\", \"is fast\", \"looks good\" are not measurable - use quantifiable metrics\n</warnings>\n</prerequisites>\n\n<workflow>\n<step number=\"1\">\n**Parse and Normalize Input**\n\nExtract feature description and generate clean slug.\n\n**Slug Generation Rules**:\n\n```bash\n# Remove filler words and normalize\necho \"$ARGUMENTS\" |\n  sed ''s/\\bwe want to\\b//gi; s/\\bI want to\\b//gi'' |\n  sed ''s/\\badd\\b//gi; s/\\bcreate\\b//gi; s/\\bimplement\\b//gi'' |\n  sed ''s/\\bget our\\b//gi; s/\\bto a\\b//gi; s/\\bwith\\b//gi'' |\n  tr ''[:upper:]'' ''[:lower:]'' |\n  sed ''s/[^a-z0-9-]/-/g'' | sed ''s/--*/-/g'' | sed ''s/^-//;s/-$//'' |\n  cut -c1-50\n```\n\n**Example**:\n\n- Input: \"We want to add student progress dashboard\"\n- Slug: `student-progress-dashboard` ✅\n- Number: 042\n- Directory: `specs/042-student-progress-dashboard/`\n\n**Quality Check**: Slug is concise, descriptive, no filler words, matches roadmap format.\n\nSee [reference.md § Slug Generation Rules](reference.md#slug-generation-rules) for detailed normalization logic.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"2\">\n**Check Roadmap Integration**\n\nSearch roadmap for existing entry to reuse context.\n\n**Detection Logic**:\n\n```bash\nSLUG=\"student-progress-dashboard\"\nif grep -qi \"^### ${SLUG}\" .spec-flow/memory/roadmap.md; then\n  FROM_ROADMAP=true\n  # Extract requirements, area, role, impact/effort scores\n  # Move entry from \"Backlog\"/\"Next\" to \"In Progress\"\n  # Add branch and spec links\nfi\n```\n\n**Benefits**:\n\n- Saves ~10 minutes (requirements already documented)\n- Automatic status tracking (roadmap updates)\n- Context reuse (user already vetted scope)\n\n**Quality Check**: If roadmap match found, extracted requirements appear in spec.md.\n\nSee [reference.md § Roadmap Integration](reference.md#roadmap-integration) for fuzzy matching logic.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"3\">\n**Load Project Documentation Context**\n\nExtract architecture constraints from `docs/project/` to prevent hallucination.\n\n**Detection**:\n\n```bash\nif [ -d \"docs/project\" ]; then\n  HAS_PROJECT_DOCS=true\n  # Extract tech stack, API patterns, entities\nelse\n  echo \"ℹ️  No project documentation (run /init-project recommended)\"\n  HAS_PROJECT_DOCS=false\nfi\n```\n\n**Extraction**:\n\n```bash\n# Extract constraints from project docs\nFRONTEND=$(grep -A 1 \"| Frontend\" docs/project/tech-stack.md | tail -1)\nDATABASE=$(grep -A 1 \"| Database\" docs/project/tech-stack.md | tail -1)\nAPI_STYLE=$(grep -A 1 \"## API Style\" docs/project/api-strategy.md | tail -1)\nENTITIES=$(grep -oP ''[A-Z_]+(?= \\{)'' docs/project/data-architecture.md)\n```\n\n**Document in NOTES.md**:\n\n```markdown\n## Project Documentation Context\n\n**Tech Stack Constraints** (from tech-stack.md):\n\n- Frontend: Next.js 14\n- Database: PostgreSQL\n\n**Spec Requirements**:\n\n- ✅ MUST use documented tech stack\n- ✅ MUST follow API patterns from api-strategy.md\n- ✅ MUST check for duplicate entities before proposing new ones\n- ❌ MUST NOT hallucinate MongoDB if PostgreSQL is documented\n```\n\n**Quality Check**: NOTES.md includes project context section with constraints.\n\n**Skip if**: No docs/project/ directory exists (warn user but don''t block).\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"4\">\n**Classify Feature**\n\nSet classification flags using decision tree.\n\n**Classification Logic**:\n\n**HAS_UI** (user-facing screens/components):\n\n```\nUI keywords: screen, page, dashboard, form, modal, component, frontend, interface\n  → BUT NOT backend-only: API, endpoint, service, worker, cron, job, migration, health check\n  → HAS_UI = true\n\nExample: \"Add student dashboard\" → HAS_UI = true ✅\nExample: \"Add background worker\" → HAS_UI = false ✅ (backend-only)\n```\n\n**IS_IMPROVEMENT** (optimization with measurable baseline):\n\n```\nImprovement keywords: improve, optimize, enhance, speed up, reduce time\n  AND baseline: existing, current, slow, faster, better\n  → IS_IMPROVEMENT = true\n\nExample: \"Improve search performance from 3.2s to <500ms\" → IS_IMPROVEMENT = true ✅\nExample: \"Make search faster\" → IS_IMPROVEMENT = false ❌ (no baseline)\n```\n\n**HAS_METRICS** (user behavior tracking):\n\n```\nMetrics keywords: track user, measure user, engagement, retention, conversion, analytics, A/B test\n  → HAS_METRICS = true\n\nExample: \"Track dashboard engagement\" → HAS_METRICS = true ✅\n```\n\n**HAS_DEPLOYMENT_IMPACT** (env vars, migrations, breaking changes):\n\n```\nDeployment keywords: migration, schema change, env variable, breaking change, docker, platform change\n  → HAS_DEPLOYMENT_IMPACT = true\n\nExample: \"OAuth authentication (needs env vars)\" → HAS_DEPLOYMENT_IMPACT = true ✅\n```\n\n**Quality Check**: Classification matches feature intent. No UI artifacts for backend workers.\n\nSee [reference.md § Classification Decision Tree](reference.md#classification-decision-tree) for complete logic.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"5\">\n**Determine Research Depth**\n\nSelect research depth based on complexity (FLAG_COUNT).\n\n**Research Depth Guidelines**:\n\n| FLAG_COUNT | Depth    | Tools | Use Cases                                       |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| 0          | Minimal  | 1-2   | Simple backend endpoint, config change          |\n| 1          | Standard | 3-5   | Single-aspect feature (UI-only or backend-only) |\n| ≥2         | Full     | 5-8   | Complex multi-aspect feature                    |\n\n**Minimal Research** (FLAG_COUNT = 0):\n\n1. Constitution check (alignment with mission/values)\n2. Grep for similar patterns\n\n**Standard Research** (FLAG_COUNT = 1):\n1-2. Minimal research 3. UI inventory scan (if HAS_UI=true) 4. Performance budgets check 5. Similar spec search\n\n**Full Research** (FLAG_COUNT ≥ 2):\n1-5. Standard research 6. Design inspirations (if HAS_UI=true) 7. Web search for novel patterns 8. Integration points analysis\n\n**Quality Check**: Research depth matches complexity. Don''t over-research simple features.\n\nSee [reference.md § Research Depth Guidelines](reference.md#research-depth-guidelines) for tool selection logic.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"6\">\n**Apply Informed Guess Strategy**\n\nUse defaults for non-critical technical decisions.\n\n**Use Informed Guesses For** (do NOT clarify):\n\n- **Performance targets**: API <500ms (95th percentile), Frontend FCP <1.5s, TTI <3.0s\n- **Data retention**: User data indefinite (with deletion option), Logs 90 days, Analytics 365 days\n- **Error handling**: User-friendly messages + error ID (ERR-XXXX), logging to error-log.md\n- **Rate limiting**: 100 requests/minute per user, 1000/minute per IP\n- **Authentication**: OAuth2 for users, JWT for APIs, MFA optional (users), required (admins)\n- **Integration patterns**: RESTful API (unless GraphQL needed), JSON format, offset/limit pagination\n\n**Document Assumptions in spec.md**:\n\n```markdown\n## Performance Targets (Assumed)\n\n- API endpoints: <500ms (95th percentile)\n- Frontend FCP: <1.5s, TTI: <3.0s\n- Lighthouse: Performance ≥85, Accessibility ≥95\n\n_Assumption: Standard web application performance expectations applied._\n```\n\n**Do NOT Use Informed Guesses For**:\n\n- Scope-defining decisions (feature boundary, user roles)\n- Security/privacy critical choices (encryption, PII handling)\n- Breaking changes (API response format changes)\n- No reasonable default exists (business logic decisions)\n\n**Quality Check**: No clarifications for decisions with industry-standard defaults.\n\nSee [reference.md § Informed Guess Heuristics](reference.md#informed-guess-heuristics) for complete defaults catalog.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"7\">\n**Generate Clarifications (Max 3)**\n\nIdentify ambiguities that cannot be reasonably assumed.\n\n**Clarification Prioritization Matrix**:\n\n| Category         | Priority | Ask?             | Example                                                   |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Scope boundary   | Critical | ✅ Always        | \"Does this include admin features or only user features?\" |\n| Security/Privacy | Critical | ✅ Always        | \"Should PII be encrypted at rest?\"                        |\n| Breaking changes | Critical | ✅ Always        | \"Is it okay to change the API response format?\"           |\n| User experience  | High     | ✅ If ambiguous  | \"Should this be a modal or new page?\"                     |\n| Performance SLA  | Medium   | ❌ Use defaults  | \"What''s the target response time?\" → Assume <500ms        |\n| Technical stack  | Medium   | ❌ Defer to plan | \"Which database?\" → Planning-phase decision               |\n| Error messages   | Low      | ❌ Use standard  | \"What error message?\" → Standard pattern                  |\n| Rate limits      | Low      | ❌ Use defaults  | \"How many requests?\" → 100/min default                    |\n\n**Limit: Maximum 3 clarifications total**\n\n**Process**:\n\n1. Identify all ambiguities\n2. Rank by category priority\n3. Keep top 3 most critical\n4. Make informed guesses for remaining\n5. Document assumptions clearly\n\n**Good Clarifications**:\n\n```markdown\n[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: Should dashboard show all students or only assigned classes?]\n[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: Should parents have access to this dashboard?]\n```\n\n**Bad Clarifications** (have defaults):\n\n```markdown\n❌ [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: What''s the target response time?] → Use 500ms default\n❌ [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: Which database to use?] → Planning-phase decision\n❌ [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: What error message format?] → Use standard pattern\n```\n\n**Quality Check**: ≤3 clarifications total, all are scope/security/UX critical.\n\nSee [reference.md § Clarification Prioritization Matrix](reference.md#clarification-prioritization-matrix) for complete ranking system.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"8\">\n**Write Success Criteria**\n\nDefine measurable, quantifiable, user-facing outcomes.\n\n**Good Criteria Format**:\n\n```markdown\n## Success Criteria\n\n- User can complete registration in <3 minutes (measured via PostHog funnel)\n- API response time <500ms for 95th percentile (measured via Datadog APM)\n- Lighthouse accessibility score ≥95 (measured via CI Lighthouse check)\n- 95% of user searches return results in <1 second\n```\n\n**Criteria Requirements**:\n\n- **Measurable**: Can be validated objectively\n- **Quantifiable**: Has specific numeric target\n- **User-facing**: Focuses on outcomes, not implementation\n- **Measurement method**: Specifies how to validate (tool, metric)\n\n**Bad Criteria to Avoid**:\n\n```markdown\n❌ System works correctly (not measurable)\n❌ API is fast (not quantifiable)\n❌ UI looks good (subjective)\n❌ React components render efficiently (technology-specific, not outcome-focused)\n```\n\n**Quality Check**: Every criterion is measurable, quantifiable, and outcome-focused.\n</step>\n\n<step number=\"9\">\n**Generate Artifacts and Commit**\n\nCreate specification artifacts and commit to git.\n\n**Artifacts**:\n\n1. `specs/NNN-slug/spec.md` - Structured specification with classification flags, requirements, assumptions, clarifications (≤3), success criteria\n2. `specs/NNN-slug/NOTES.md` - Implementation decisions and project context\n3. `specs/NNN-slug/visuals/README.md` - Visual artifacts directory (if HAS_UI=true)\n4. `specs/NNN-slug/state.yaml` - Phase state tracking (currentPhase: specification, status: completed)\n5. Updated roadmap (if FROM_ROADMAP=true) - Move entry to \"In Progress\", add branch/spec links\n\n**Validation Checks**:\n\n- [ ] Requirements checklist complete (if exists)\n- [ ] Clarifications ≤3\n- [ ] Classification flags match feature description\n- [ ] Success criteria are measurable\n- [ ] Roadmap updated (if FROM_ROADMAP=true)\n\n**Commit Message**:\n\n```bash\ngit add specs/NNN-slug/\ngit commit -m \"feat: add spec for <feature-name>\n\nGenerated specification with classification:\n- HAS_UI: <true/false>\n- IS_IMPROVEMENT: <true/false>\n- HAS_METRICS: <true/false>\n- HAS_DEPLOYMENT_IMPACT: <true/false>\n\nClarifications: N\nResearch depth: <minimal/standard/full>\"\n```\n\n**Quality Check**: All artifacts created, spec committed, roadmap updated, state.yaml initialized.\n</step>\n</workflow>\n\n<validation>\n<phase_checklist>\n**Pre-phase checks**:\n- [ ] Git working tree clean\n- [ ] Not on main branch\n- [ ] Required templates exist\n\n**During phase**:\n\n- [ ] Slug normalized (no filler words, lowercase kebab-case)\n- [ ] Roadmap checked for existing entry\n- [ ] Project docs loaded (if exist)\n- [ ] Classification flags validated (no conflicting keywords)\n- [ ] Research depth appropriate for complexity (FLAG_COUNT-based)\n- [ ] Clarifications ≤3 (use informed guesses for rest)\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable and quantifiable\n- [ ] Assumptions documented clearly\n\n**Post-phase validation**:\n\n- [ ] spec.md committed with proper message\n- [ ] NOTES.md initialized\n- [ ] Roadmap updated (if FROM_ROADMAP=true)\n- [ ] visuals/ created (if HAS_UI=true)\n- [ ] state.yaml initialized\n      </phase_checklist>\n\n<quality_standards>\n**Specification quality targets**:\n\n- Clarifications: ≤3 per spec\n- Classification accuracy: ≥90%\n- Success criteria: 100% measurable\n- Time to spec: ≤15 minutes\n- Rework rate: <5%\n\n**What makes a good spec**:\n\n- Clear scope boundaries (what''s in, what''s out)\n- Measurable success criteria (with measurement methods)\n- Reasonable assumptions documented\n- Minimal clarifications (only critical scope/security)\n- Correct classification (matches feature intent)\n- Context reuse (from roadmap when available)\n\n**What makes a bad spec**:\n\n- > 5 clarifications (over-clarifying technical defaults)\n- Vague success criteria (\"works correctly\", \"is fast\")\n- Technology-specific criteria (couples to implementation)\n- Wrong classification (UI flag for backend-only)\n- Missing roadmap integration (duplicates planning work)\n  </quality_standards>\n  </validation>\n\n<anti_patterns>\n<pitfall name=\"over_clarification\">\n**Impact**: Delays planning phase, frustrates users\n\n**Scenario**:\n\n```\nSpec with 7 clarifications (limit: 3):\n- [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: What format? CSV or JSON?] → Use JSON default\n- [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: Rate limiting strategy?] → Use 100/min default\n- [NEEDS CLARIFICATION: Maximum file size?] → Use 50MB default\n```\n\n**Prevention**:\n\n- Use industry-standard defaults (see reference.md § Informed Guess Heuristics)\n- Only mark critical scope/security decisions as NEEDS CLARIFICATION\n- Document assumptions in spec.md \"Assumptions\" section\n- Prioritize by impact: scope > security > UX > technical\n\n**If encountered**: Reduce to 3 most critical, convert others to documented assumptions.\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"wrong_classification\">\n**Impact**: Creates unnecessary UI artifacts, wastes time\n\n**Scenario**:\n\n```\nFeature: \"Add background worker to process uploads\"\nClassified: HAS_UI=true (WRONG - no user-facing UI)\nResult: Generated screens.yaml for backend-only feature\n```\n\n**Root cause**: Keyword \"process\" triggered false positive without checking for backend-only keywords\n\n**Prevention**:\n\n1. Check for backend-only keywords: worker, cron, job, migration, health check, API, endpoint, service\n2. Require BOTH UI keyword AND absence of backend-only keywords\n3. Use classification decision tree (see reference.md § Classification Decision Tree)\n   </pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"roadmap_slug_mismatch\">\n**Impact**: Misses context reuse opportunity, duplicates planning work\n\n**Scenario**:\n\n```\nUser input: \"We want to add Student Progress Dashboard\"\nGenerated slug: \"add-student-progress-dashboard\" (BAD - includes \"add\")\nRoadmap entry: \"### student-progress-dashboard\" (slug without \"add\")\nResult: No match found, created fresh spec instead of reusing roadmap context\n```\n\n**Prevention**:\n\n1. Remove filler words during slug generation: \"add\", \"create\", \"we want to\"\n2. Normalize to lowercase kebab-case consistently\n3. Offer fuzzy matches if exact match not found\n   </pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"too_many_research_tools\">\n**Impact**: Wastes time, exceeds token budget\n\n**Scenario**:\n\n```bash\n# 15 research tools for simple backend endpoint (WRONG)\nGlob *.py, Glob *.ts, Glob *.tsx, Grep \"database\", Grep \"model\"...\n```\n\n**Prevention**:\n\n- Use research depth guidelines: FLAG_COUNT = 0 → 1-2 tools only\n- For simple features: Constitution check + pattern search is sufficient\n- Reserve full research (5-8 tools) for complex multi-aspect features\n\n**Correct approach**:\n\n```bash\n# 2 research tools for simple backend endpoint (CORRECT)\ngrep \"similar endpoint\" specs/*/spec.md\ngrep \"BaseModel\" api/app/models/*.py\n```\n\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"vague_success_criteria\">\n**Impact**: Cannot validate implementation, leads to scope creep\n\n**Bad examples**:\n\n```markdown\n❌ System works correctly (not measurable)\n❌ API is fast (not quantifiable)\n❌ UI looks good (subjective)\n```\n\n**Good examples**:\n\n```markdown\n✅ User can complete registration in <3 minutes (measured via PostHog funnel)\n✅ API response time <500ms for 95th percentile (measured via Datadog APM)\n✅ Lighthouse accessibility score ≥95 (measured via CI Lighthouse check)\n```\n\n**Prevention**: Every criterion must answer: \"How do we measure this objectively?\"\n</pitfall>\n\n<pitfall name=\"technology_specific_criteria\">\n**Impact**: Couples spec to implementation details, reduces flexibility\n\n**Bad examples**:\n\n```markdown\n❌ React components render efficiently\n❌ Redis cache hit rate >80%\n❌ PostgreSQL queries use proper indexes\n```\n\n**Good examples** (outcome-focused):\n\n```markdown\n✅ Page load time <1.5s (First Contentful Paint)\n✅ 95% of user searches return results in <1 second\n✅ Database queries complete in <100ms average\n```\n\n**Prevention**: Focus on user-facing outcomes, not implementation mechanisms.\n</pitfall>\n</anti_patterns>\n\n<best_practices>\n<informed_guess_strategy>\n**When to use**:\n\n- Non-critical technical decisions\n- Industry standards exist\n- Default won''t impact scope or security\n\n**When NOT to use**:\n\n- Scope-defining decisions\n- Security/privacy critical choices\n- No reasonable default exists\n\n**Approach**:\n\n1. Check if decision has reasonable default (see reference.md § Informed Guess Heuristics)\n2. Document assumption clearly in spec\n3. Note that user can override if needed\n\n**Example**:\n\n```markdown\n## Performance Targets (Assumed)\n\n- API response time: <500ms (95th percentile)\n- Frontend FCP: <1.5s\n- Database queries: <100ms\n\n**Assumptions**:\n\n- Standard web app performance expectations applied\n- If requirements differ, specify in \"Performance Requirements\" section\n```\n\n**Result**: Reduces clarifications from 5-7 to 0-2, saves ~10 minutes\n</informed_guess_strategy>\n\n<roadmap_integration>\n**When to use**:\n\n- Feature name matches roadmap entry\n- Roadmap uses consistent slug format\n\n**Approach**:\n\n1. Normalize user input to slug format\n2. Search roadmap for exact match\n3. If found: Extract requirements, area, role, impact/effort\n4. Move to \"In Progress\" section automatically\n5. Add branch and spec links\n\n**Result**: Saves ~10 minutes, requirements already vetted, automatic status tracking\n</roadmap_integration>\n\n<classification_decision_tree>\n**Best practice**: Follow decision tree systematically (see reference.md § Classification Decision Tree)\n\n**Process**:\n\n1. Check UI keywords → Set HAS_UI (but verify no backend-only exclusions)\n2. Check improvement keywords + baseline → Set IS_IMPROVEMENT\n3. Check metrics keywords → Set HAS_METRICS\n4. Check deployment keywords → Set HAS_DEPLOYMENT_IMPACT\n\n**Result**: 90%+ classification accuracy, correct artifacts generated\n</classification_decision_tree>\n</best_practices>\n\n<success_criteria>\nSpecification phase complete when:\n\n- [ ] All pre-phase checks passed\n- [ ] All 9 execution steps completed\n- [ ] All post-phase validations passed\n- [ ] Spec committed to git\n- [ ] state.yaml shows `currentPhase: specification` and `status: completed`\n\nReady to proceed when:\n\n- If clarifications >0 → Run `/clarify`\n- If clarifications = 0 → Run `/plan`\n  </success_criteria>\n\n<troubleshooting>\n**Issue**: Too many clarifications (>3)\n**Solution**: Review reference.md § Informed Guess Heuristics for defaults, convert non-critical questions to assumptions\n\n**Issue**: Classification seems wrong\n**Solution**: Re-check decision tree, verify no backend-only keywords for HAS_UI=true\n\n**Issue**: Roadmap entry exists but wasn''t matched\n**Solution**: Check slug normalization, offer fuzzy matches, update roadmap slug format\n\n**Issue**: Success criteria are vague\n**Solution**: Add quantifiable metrics and measurement methods, focus on user-facing outcomes\n\n**Issue**: Research depth excessive for simple feature\n**Solution**: Follow FLAG_COUNT guidelines (0→minimal, 1→standard, ≥2→full)\n\n**Issue**: Project context missing/incomplete\n**Solution**: Run /init-project to generate docs/project/, or manually create tech-stack.md and api-strategy.md\n</troubleshooting>\n\n<reference_guides>\nFor detailed documentation:\n\n**Classification & Defaults**: [reference.md](reference.md)\n\n- Classification decision tree (HAS_UI, IS_IMPROVEMENT, HAS_METRICS, HAS_DEPLOYMENT_IMPACT)\n- Informed guess heuristics (performance, retention, auth, rate limits)\n- Clarification prioritization matrix (scope > security > UX > technical)\n- Slug generation rules (normalization, filler word removal)\n\n**Real-World Examples**: [examples.md](examples.md)\n\n- Good specs (0-2 clarifications) vs bad specs (>5 clarifications)\n- Side-by-side comparisons with analysis\n- Progressive learning patterns (features 1-5, 6-15, 16+)\n- Classification accuracy examples\n\n**Execution Details**: reference.md § Research Depth Guidelines, Common Mistakes to Avoid\n\nNext phase after /specify:\n\n- If clarifications >0 → `/clarify` (reduces ambiguity via targeted questions)\n- If clarifications = 0 → `/plan` (generates design artifacts from spec)\n  </reference_guides>\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:44:16.401Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Development Agents requiring systematic classification and informed guess strategies for Spec-Driven Development.","zh":"适合需要系统化分类和明智猜测策略的开发代理，用于规格驱动开发。","ja":"開発エージェントが体系的な分類と情報に基づいた推測戦略を必要とするSpec-Driven Developmentに最適です。","ko":"시스템 분류 및 정보 기반 추측 전략이 필요한 개발 에이전트를 위한 규格 주도 개발에 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de desarrollo que requieren clasificación sistemática y estrategias de conjetura informada para el desarrollo impulsado por especificaciones.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de développement nécessitant une classification systématique et des stratégies de conjecture éclairée pour le développement piloté par spécifications.","de":"Ideal für Entwicklungssagenten, die eine systematische Klassifizierung und informierte Vermutungsstrategien für die spezifikationsgetriebene Entwicklung benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que requerem classificação sistemática e estratégias de palpites informados para Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Especificações.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, требующих систематической классификации и обоснованных стратегий угадывания для разработки, управляемой спецификациями.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات التطوير التي تتطلب تصنيفًا منهجيًا واستراتيجيات تخمين مطلع للتنمية القائمة على المواصفات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform natural language feature requests into structured specifications using repeatable Claude Code workflows, quality gates, and token budgets, while producing measurable success criteria and auditable artifacts in spec.md format.","zh":"赋予代理将自然语言功能请求转换为结构化规格的能力，使用可重复的Claude Code工作流、质量门和令牌预算，同时产生可衡量的成功标准和可审计的制品，格式为spec.md。","ja":"エージェントに、自然言語の機能要求を、繰り返し可能なClaude Codeワークフロー、品質ゲート、トークン予算を使用して構造化された仕様書に変換する能力を付与し、測定可能な成功基準と監査可能な成果物をspec.md形式で生成します。","ko":"에이전트가 자연어 기능 요청을 구조화된 사양으로 변환할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 반복 가능한 Claude Code 워크플로, 품질 게이트 및 토큰 예산을 사용하여 측정 가능한 성공 기준 및 감사 가능한 아티팩트를 spec.md 형식으로 생성합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformar solicitudes de características de lenguaje natural en especificaciones estructuradas utilizando flujos de trabajo de Claude Code repetibles, puertas de calidad y presupuestos de tokens, mientras produce criterios de éxito medibles y artefactos auditables en formato spec.md.","fr":"Permet aux agents de transformer les demandes de fonctionnalités de langage naturel en spécifications structurées en utilisant des flux de travail de Claude Code répétitifs, des portes de qualité et des budgets de jetons, tout en produisant des critères de réussite mesurables et des artefacts auditable au format spec.md.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, natürliche Sprachfunktionenanforderungen in strukturierte Spezifikationen umzuwandeln, indem sie wiederholbare Claude-Code-Workflows, Qualitätsprüfungen und Token-Budgets verwenden, während sie messbare Erfolgskriterien und überprüfbare Artefakte im spec.md-Format erzeugen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a transformar solicitações de recursos de linguagem natural em especificações estruturadas usando fluxos de trabalho de Claude Code repetíveis, portões de qualidade e orçamentos de tokens, produzindo critérios de sucesso mensuráveis e artefatos auditáveis no formato spec.md.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью преобразовывать запросы функций естественного языка в структурированные спецификации с использованием повторяющихся рабочих процессов Claude Code, контроля качества и токенов, при этом производя измеримые критерии успеха и аудиторские артефакты в формате spec.md.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من تحويل طلبات الميزات بلغة طبيعية إلى مواصفات منظمّة باستخدام سير عمل Claude Code القابلة للتكرار، وبوّابات الجودة وميزانيات الرموز، مع إنتاج معايير نجاح قابلة للقياس ووثائق قابلة للتدقيق بصيغة spec.md."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating the specification phase with minimal clarification approach","Generating spec.md files with classification flags for downstream workflows","Streamlining feature request processing using systematic classification and informed guess heuristics"],"zh":["使用最小阐明方法自动执行规格阶段","使用分类标志生成spec.md文件以供下游工作流使用","使用系统化分类和信息猜测启发式简化功能请求处理"],"ja":["最小の明確化アプローチを使用して仕様段階を自動化する","分類フラグを使用してspec.mdファイルを生成し、ダウンストリームのワークフローで使用する","体系的な分類と情報に基づいた推測ヒューリスティックを使用して機能要求の処理を合理化する"],"ko":["최소한의 명료화 접근 방식을 사용하여 사양 단계를 자동화하는 것","분류 플래그를 사용하여 spec.md 파일을 생성하여 다운스트림 워크플로에서 사용","시스템 분류 및 정보 기반 추측 유추를 사용하여 기능 요청 처리를 간소화하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar la fase de especificación con un enfoque de aclaración mínimo","Generar archivos spec.md con indicadores de clasificación para flujos de trabajo posteriores","Optimizar el procesamiento de solicitudes de características utilizando la clasificación sistemática y heurísticas de conjetura informada"],"fr":["Automatiser la phase de spécification avec une approche de clarification minimale","Générer des fichiers spec.md avec des indicateurs de classification pour les flux de travail ultérieurs","Optimiser le traitement des demandes de fonctionnalités en utilisant la classification systématique et les heuristiques de conjecture éclairée"],"de":["Automatisieren der Spezifikationsphase mit einem minimalen Klärungsansatz","Erzeugen von spec.md-Dateien mit Klassifizierungsflaggen für nachgelagerte Workflows","Optimieren der Verarbeitung von Funktionsanforderungen unter Verwendung systematischer Klassifizierung und heuristischer Vermutung"],"pt":["Automatizar a fase de especificação com abordagem de esclarecimento mínima","Gerar arquivos spec.md com flags de classificação para fluxos de trabalho downstream","Otimizar o processamento de solicitações de recursos usando classificação sistemática e heurísticas de palpites informados"],"ru":["Автоматизировать фазу спецификации с минимальным подходом к уточнению","Генерировать файлы spec.md с флагами классификации для потоков работы downstream","Оптимизировать обработку запросов функций, используя систематическую классификацию и эвристику обоснованного угадывания"],"ar":["أتمتة مرحلة المواصفات باستخدام نهج توضيح 최소","توليد ملفات spec.md ذات أعلام التصنيف لتدفقات العمل الهابطة","جعل معالجة طلبات الميزات أكثر كفاءة باستخدام التصنيف المنهجي والخوارزميات المتعلقة بالتخمين المطلع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Maximum 3 clarifications using informed guess heuristics","Requires Claude Code workflows and token budgets","Dependent on quality gates and auditable artifacts"],"zh":["最多3次阐明使用信息猜测启发式","需要Claude Code工作流和令牌预算","依赖于质量门和可审计的制品"],"ja":["情報に基づいた推測ヒューリスティックを使用して最大3回の明確化","Claude Codeワークフローとトークン予算が必要","品質ゲートと監査可能な成果物に依存"],"ko":["정보 기반 추측 유추를 사용하여 최대 3번의 명료화","클라우드 코드 워크플로 및 토큰 예산이 필요","품질 게이트 및 감사 가능한 아티팩트에 의존"],"es":["Máximo 3 aclaraciones utilizando heurísticas de conjetura informada","Requiere flujos de trabajo de Claude Code y presupuestos de tokens","Dependiente de las puertas de calidad y los artefactos auditables"],"fr":["Maximum 3 clarifications en utilisant des heuristiques de conjecture éclairée","Nécessite des flux de travail de Claude Code et des budgets de jetons","Dépendant des portes de qualité et des artefacts auditable"],"de":["Maximal 3 Klarstellungen unter Verwendung informierter Vermutungsheuristiken","Benötigt Claude-Code-Workflows und Token-Budgets","Abhängig von Qualitätsprüfungen und überprüfbaren Artefakten"],"pt":["Máximo 3 esclarecimentos usando heurísticas de palpites informados","Exige fluxos de trabalho de Claude Code e orçamentos de tokens","Dependente de portões de qualidade e artefatos auditáveis"],"ru":["Максимально 3 уточнения, используя эвристику обоснованного угадывания","Требует рабочих процессов Claude Code и токенов","Зависит от контроля качества и аудиторских артефактов"],"ar":["الحد الأقصى 3 توضيحات باستخدام خوارزميات التخمين المطلع","يتطلب سير عمل Claude Code وميزانيات الرموز","يعتمد على بوابات الجودة والوثائق القابلة للتدقيق"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('0boluan0/Notes_on_Economic_Statistics/obsidian-markdown', 'community', '0boluan0', 'Notes_on_Economic_Statistics', '0boluan0/Notes_on_Economic_Statistics', 'obsidian-markdown', 0, 0, 45, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z', '2026-02-18T08:44:26.804Z', NULL, '{"id":"0boluan0/Notes_on_Economic_Statistics/obsidian-markdown","name":"obsidian-markdown","description":{"zh":"Obsidian Markdown 技能允许开发者创建和编辑 Obsidian 风格 Markdown 文档，支持多种语法扩展。","ja":"Obsidian Markdown スキルは、開発者が Obsidian スタイルの Markdown ドキュメントを作成および編集できるようにします。","ko":"오비디언 마크다운 스킬을 통해 개발자는 오비디언 스타일 마크다운 문서를 생성하고 편집할 수 있습니다.","es":"Obsidian Markdown es un lenguaje de marcado que combina CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown y LaTeX para crear contenido enriquecido.","fr":"Obsidian Markdown est un langage de balisage qui combine CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown et LaTeX pour créer du contenu enrichi.","de":"Obsidian Markdown ist eine Auszeichnungssprache, die CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown und LaTeX kombiniert, um erweitertes Inhaltsmaterial zu erstellen.","pt":"A habilidade Obsidian Markdown permite criar e editar arquivos de marcação válidos, incluindo extensões de sintaxe específicas do Obsidian.","ru":"Возможность Obsidian Markdown позволяет создавать и редактировать валидные файлы разметки, включая расширения синтаксиса, специфичные для Obsidian.","ar":"الوظيفة Obsidian Markdown تمكن من إنشاء وتحرير ملفات الترميز الصالح، بما في ذلك امتدادات البناء الجملة الخاصة بأوبسيديان","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Obsidian Markdown 技能","ja":"Obsidian Markdown スキル","ko":"오비디언 마크다운 스킬","es":"Obsidian Markdown: Creación y Edición de Contenido","fr":"Obsidian Markdown : Création et Édition de Contenu","de":"Obsidian Markdown: Erstellung und Bearbeitung von Inhalten","pt":"Obsidian Markdown: Criar e Editar Arquivos","ru":"Obsidian Markdown: создание и редактирование файлов","ar":"أوبسيديان ماركداون: إنشاء وتحرير الملفات","en":"obsidian-markdown"},"description":{"zh":"Obsidian Markdown 技能允许开发者创建和编辑 Obsidian 风格 Markdown 文档，支持多种语法扩展。","ja":"Obsidian Markdown スキルは、開発者が Obsidian スタイルの Markdown ドキュメントを作成および編集できるようにします。","ko":"오비디언 마크다운 스킬을 통해 개발자는 오비디언 스타일 마크다운 문서를 생성하고 편집할 수 있습니다.","es":"Obsidian Markdown es un lenguaje de marcado que combina CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown y LaTeX para crear contenido enriquecido.","fr":"Obsidian Markdown est un langage de balisage qui combine CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown et LaTeX pour créer du contenu enrichi.","de":"Obsidian Markdown ist eine Auszeichnungssprache, die CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown und LaTeX kombiniert, um erweitertes Inhaltsmaterial zu erstellen.","pt":"A habilidade Obsidian Markdown permite criar e editar arquivos de marcação válidos, incluindo extensões de sintaxe específicas do Obsidian.","ru":"Возможность Obsidian Markdown позволяет создавать и редактировать валидные файлы разметки, включая расширения синтаксиса, специфичные для Obsidian.","ar":"الوظيفة Obsidian Markdown تمكن من إنشاء وتحرير ملفات الترميز الصالح، بما في ذلك امتدادات البناء الجملة الخاصة بأوبسيديان","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["支持 CommonMark 语法","支持 GitHub Flavored Markdown 语法","支持 LaTeX 数学公式","支持 Obsidian 特定语法扩展","创建和编辑 Obsidian 风格 Markdown 文档"],"ja":["CommonMark 構文をサポート","GitHub Flavored Markdown 構文をサポート","LaTeX 数学式をサポート","Obsidian 特有の構文拡張をサポート","Obsidian スタイルの Markdown ドキュメントを作成および編集"],"ko":["CommonMark 구문을 지원","GitHub Flavored Markdown 구문을 지원","LaTeX 수학식을 지원","오비디언 특정 구문 확장을 지원","오비디언 스타일 마크다운 문서를 생성하고 편집"],"es":["Compatibilidad con CommonMark","Soporte para GitHub Flavored Markdown","Integración de LaTeX para ecuaciones matemáticas","Enlaces wiki y llamadas","Incrustaciones de contenido"],"fr":["Compatibilité avec CommonMark","Prise en charge de GitHub Flavored Markdown","Intégration de LaTeX pour les équations mathématiques","Liens wiki et appels","Inclusions de contenu"],"de":["Kompatibilität mit CommonMark","Unterstützung für GitHub Flavored Markdown","Integration von LaTeX für mathematische Gleichungen","Wikilinks und Aufrufe","Inhalts-Einbettungen"],"pt":["Criação e edição de arquivos de marcação válidos","Suporte a extensões de sintaxe específicas do Obsidian","Inclusão de elementos de formatação básicos","Suporte a fórmulas matemáticas com LaTeX","Integração com links e embeds do Obsidian"],"ru":["Создание и редактирование валидных файлов разметки","Поддержка расширений синтаксиса, специфичных для Obsidian","Включение базовых элементов форматирования","Поддержка математических формул с помощью LaTeX","Интеграция с ссылками и embeds Obsidian"],"ar":["إنشاء وتحرير ملفات الترميز الصالح","دعم لامتدادات البناء الجملة الخاصة بأوبسيديان","تشمل عناصر التنسيق الأساسية","دعم الصيغ الرياضية مع LaTeX","التكامل مع الروابط والملحقات الخاصة بأوبسيديان"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Obsidian Markdown","CommonMark","GitHub Flavored Markdown","LaTeX","Obsidian 特定语法扩展","Markdown 编辑器"],"ja":["Obsidian Markdown","CommonMark","GitHub Flavored Markdown","LaTeX","Obsidian 特有の構文拡張","Markdown エディター"],"ko":["오비디언 마크다운","CommonMark","GitHub Flavored Markdown","LaTeX","오비디언 특정 구문 확장","마크다운 편집기"],"es":["Obsidian Markdown","lenguaje de marcado","CommonMark","GitHub Flavored Markdown","LaTeX","desarrollo de contenido"],"fr":["Obsidian Markdown","langage de balisage","CommonMark","GitHub Flavored Markdown","LaTeX","développement de contenu"],"de":["Obsidian Markdown","Auszeichnungssprache","CommonMark","GitHub Flavored Markdown","LaTeX","Inhaltsentwicklung"],"pt":["Obsidian Markdown","marcação de texto","sintaxe de marcação","extensões de sintaxe","LaTeX","formatação de texto","edição de arquivos"],"ru":["Obsidian Markdown","разметка текста","синтаксис разметки","расширения синтаксиса","LaTeX","форматирование текста","редактирование файлов"],"ar":["أوبسيديان ماركداون","ترميز النص","بناء الجملة","امتدادات البناء الجملة","LaTeX","تنسيق النص","تحرير الملفات"]}},"owner":"0boluan0","repo":"Notes_on_Economic_Statistics","repoPath":"0boluan0/Notes_on_Economic_Statistics","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"obsidian-markdown","description":"Create and edit Obsidian Flavored Markdown with wikilinks, embeds, callouts, properties, and other Obsidian-specific syntax. Use when working with .md files in Obsidian, or when the user mentions wikilinks, callouts, frontmatter, tags, embeds, or Obsidian notes.","bodyPreview":"# Obsidian Flavored Markdown Skill\n\nThis skill enables skills-compatible agents to create and edit valid Obsidian Flavored Markdown, including all Obsidian-specific syntax extensions.\n\n## Overview\n\nObsidian uses a combination of Markdown flavors:\n- [CommonMark](https://commonmark.org/)\n- [GitHub Flavored Markdown](https://github.github.com/gfm/)\n- [LaTeX](https://www.latex-project.org/) for math\n- Obsidian-specific extensions (wikilinks, callouts, embeds, etc.)\n\n## Basic Formatting\n\n### Paragrap","body":"# Obsidian Flavored Markdown Skill\n\nThis skill enables skills-compatible agents to create and edit valid Obsidian Flavored Markdown, including all Obsidian-specific syntax extensions.\n\n## Overview\n\nObsidian uses a combination of Markdown flavors:\n- [CommonMark](https://commonmark.org/)\n- [GitHub Flavored Markdown](https://github.github.com/gfm/)\n- [LaTeX](https://www.latex-project.org/) for math\n- Obsidian-specific extensions (wikilinks, callouts, embeds, etc.)\n\n## Basic Formatting\n\n### Paragraphs and Line Breaks\n\n```markdown\nThis is a paragraph.\n\nThis is another paragraph (blank line between creates separate paragraphs).\n\nFor a line break within a paragraph, add two spaces at the end  \nor use Shift+Enter.\n```\n\n### Headings\n\n```markdown\n# Heading 1\n## Heading 2\n### Heading 3\n#### Heading 4\n##### Heading 5\n###### Heading 6\n```\n\n### Text Formatting\n\n| Style | Syntax | Example | Output |\n|-------|--------|---------|--------|\n| Bold | `**text**` or `__text__` | `**Bold**` | **Bold** |\n| Italic | `*text*` or `_text_` | `*Italic*` | *Italic* |\n| Bold + Italic | `***text***` | `***Both***` | ***Both*** |\n| Strikethrough | `~~text~~` | `~~Striked~~` | ~~Striked~~ |\n| Highlight | `==text==` | `==Highlighted==` | ==Highlighted== |\n| Inline code | `` `code` `` | `` `code` `` | `code` |\n\n### Escaping Formatting\n\nUse backslash to escape special characters:\n```markdown\n\\*This won''t be italic\\*\n\\#This won''t be a heading\n1\\. This won''t be a list item\n```\n\nCommon characters to escape: `\\*`, `\\_`, `\\#`, `` \\` ``, `\\|`, `\\~`\n\n## Internal Links (Wikilinks)\n\n### Basic Links\n\n```markdown\n[[Note Name]]\n[[Note Name.md]]\n[[Note Name|Display Text]]\n```\n\n### Link to Headings\n\n```markdown\n[[Note Name#Heading]]\n[[Note Name#Heading|Custom Text]]\n[[#Heading in same note]]\n[[##Search all headings in vault]]\n```\n\n### Link to Blocks\n\n```markdown\n[[Note Name#^block-id]]\n[[Note Name#^block-id|Custom Text]]\n```\n\nDefine a block ID by adding `^block-id` at the end of a paragraph:\n```markdown\nThis is a paragraph that can be linked to. ^my-block-id\n```\n\nFor lists and quotes, add the block ID on a separate line:\n```markdown\n> This is a quote\n> With multiple lines\n\n^quote-id\n```\n\n### Search Links\n\n```markdown\n[[##heading]]     Search for headings containing \"heading\"\n[[^^block]]       Search for blocks containing \"block\"\n```\n\n## Markdown-Style Links\n\n```markdown\n[Display Text](Note%20Name.md)\n[Display Text](Note%20Name.md#Heading)\n[Display Text](https://example.com)\n[Note](obsidian://open?vault=VaultName&file=Note.md)\n```\n\nNote: Spaces must be URL-encoded as `%20` in Markdown links.\n\n## Embeds\n\n### Embed Notes\n\n```markdown\n![[Note Name]]\n![[Note Name#Heading]]\n![[Note Name#^block-id]]\n```\n\n### Embed Images\n\n```markdown\n![[image.png]]\n![[image.png|640x480]]    Width x Height\n![[image.png|300]]        Width only (maintains aspect ratio)\n```\n\n### External Images\n\n```markdown\n![Alt text](https://example.com/image.png)\n![Alt text|300](https://example.com/image.png)\n```\n\n### Embed Audio\n\n```markdown\n![[audio.mp3]]\n![[audio.ogg]]\n```\n\n### Embed PDF\n\n```markdown\n![[document.pdf]]\n![[document.pdf#page=3]]\n![[document.pdf#height=400]]\n```\n\n### Embed Lists\n\n```markdown\n![[Note#^list-id]]\n```\n\nWhere the list has been defined with a block ID:\n```markdown\n- Item 1\n- Item 2\n- Item 3\n\n^list-id\n```\n\n### Embed Search Results\n\n````markdown\n```query\ntag:#project status:done\n```\n````\n\n## Callouts\n\n### Basic Callout\n\n```markdown\n> [!note]\n> This is a note callout.\n\n> [!info] Custom Title\n> This callout has a custom title.\n\n> [!tip] Title Only\n```\n\n### Foldable Callouts\n\n```markdown\n> [!faq]- Collapsed by default\n> This content is hidden until expanded.\n\n> [!faq]+ Expanded by default\n> This content is visible but can be collapsed.\n```\n\n### Nested Callouts\n\n```markdown\n> [!question] Outer callout\n> > [!note] Inner callout\n> > Nested content\n```\n\n### Supported Callout Types\n\n| Type | Aliases | Description |\n|------|---------|-------------|\n| `note` | - | Blue, pencil icon |\n| `abstract` | `summary`, `tldr` | Teal, clipboard icon |\n| `info` | - | Blue, info icon |\n| `todo` | - | Blue, checkbox icon |\n| `tip` | `hint`, `important` | Cyan, flame icon |\n| `success` | `check`, `done` | Green, checkmark icon |\n| `question` | `help`, `faq` | Yellow, question mark |\n| `warning` | `caution`, `attention` | Orange, warning icon |\n| `failure` | `fail`, `missing` | Red, X icon |\n| `danger` | `error` | Red, zap icon |\n| `bug` | - | Red, bug icon |\n| `example` | - | Purple, list icon |\n| `quote` | `cite` | Gray, quote icon |\n\n### Custom Callouts (CSS)\n\n```css\n.callout[data-callout=\"custom-type\"] {\n  --callout-color: 255, 0, 0;\n  --callout-icon: lucide-alert-circle;\n}\n```\n\n## Lists\n\n### Unordered Lists\n\n```markdown\n- Item 1\n- Item 2\n  - Nested item\n  - Another nested\n- Item 3\n\n* Also works with asterisks\n+ Or plus signs\n```\n\n### Ordered Lists\n\n```markdown\n1. First item\n2. Second item\n   1. Nested numbered\n   2. Another nested\n3. Third item\n\n1) Alternative syntax\n2) With parentheses\n```\n\n### Task Lists\n\n```markdown\n- [ ] Incomplete task\n- [x] Completed task\n- [ ] Task with sub-tasks\n  - [ ] Subtask 1\n  - [x] Subtask 2\n```\n\n## Quotes\n\n```markdown\n> This is a blockquote.\n> It can span multiple lines.\n>\n> And include multiple paragraphs.\n>\n> > Nested quotes work too.\n```\n\n## Code\n\n### Inline Code\n\n```markdown\nUse `backticks` for inline code.\nUse double backticks for ``code with a ` backtick inside``.\n```\n\n### Code Blocks\n\n````markdown\n```\nPlain code block\n```\n\n```javascript\n// Syntax highlighted code block\nfunction hello() {\n  console.log(\"Hello, world!\");\n}\n```\n\n```python\n# Python example\ndef greet(name):\n    print(f\"Hello, {name}!\")\n```\n````\n\n### Nesting Code Blocks\n\nUse more backticks or tildes for the outer block:\n\n`````markdown\n````markdown\nHere''s how to create a code block:\n```js\nconsole.log(\"Hello\")\n```\n````\n`````\n\n## Tables\n\n```markdown\n| Header 1 | Header 2 | Header 3 |\n|----------|----------|----------|\n| Cell 1   | Cell 2   | Cell 3   |\n| Cell 4   | Cell 5   | Cell 6   |\n```\n\n### Alignment\n\n```markdown\n| Left     | Center   | Right    |\n|:---------|:--------:|---------:|\n| Left     | Center   | Right    |\n```\n\n### Using Pipes in Tables\n\nEscape pipes with backslash:\n```markdown\n| Column 1 | Column 2 |\n|----------|----------|\n| [[Link\\|Display]] | ![[Image\\|100]] |\n```\n\n## Math (LaTeX)\n\n### Inline Math\n\n```markdown\nThis is inline math: $e^{i\\pi} + 1 = 0$\n```\n\n### Block Math\n\n```markdown\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}\na & b \\\\\nc & d\n\\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc\n$$\n```\n\n### Common Math Syntax\n\n```markdown\n$x^2$              Superscript\n$x_i$              Subscript\n$\\frac{a}{b}$      Fraction\n$\\sqrt{x}$         Square root\n$\\sum_{i=1}^{n}$   Summation\n$\\int_a^b$         Integral\n$\\alpha, \\beta$    Greek letters\n```\n\n## Diagrams (Mermaid)\n\n````markdown\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[Start] --> B{Decision}\n    B -->|Yes| C[Do this]\n    B -->|No| D[Do that]\n    C --> E[End]\n    D --> E\n```\n````\n\n### Sequence Diagrams\n\n````markdown\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    Alice->>Bob: Hello Bob\n    Bob-->>Alice: Hi Alice\n```\n````\n\n### Linking in Diagrams\n\n````markdown\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[Biology]\n    B[Chemistry]\n    A --> B\n    class A,B internal-link;\n```\n````\n\n## Footnotes\n\n```markdown\nThis sentence has a footnote[^1].\n\n[^1]: This is the footnote content.\n\nYou can also use named footnotes[^note].\n\n[^note]: Named footnotes still appear as numbers.\n\nInline footnotes are also supported.^[This is an inline footnote.]\n```\n\n## Comments\n\n```markdown\nThis is visible %%but this is hidden%% text.\n\n%%\nThis entire block is hidden.\nIt won''t appear in reading view.\n%%\n```\n\n## Horizontal Rules\n\n```markdown\n---\n***\n___\n- - -\n* * *\n```\n\n## Properties (Frontmatter)\n\nProperties use YAML frontmatter at the start of a note:\n\n```yaml\n---\ntitle: My Note Title\ndate: 2024-01-15\ntags:\n  - project\n  - important\naliases:\n  - My Note\n  - Alternative Name\ncssclasses:\n  - custom-class\nstatus: in-progress\nrating: 4.5\ncompleted: false\ndue: 2024-02-01T14:30:00\n---\n```\n\n### Property Types\n\n| Type | Example |\n|------|---------|\n| Text | `title: My Title` |\n| Number | `rating: 4.5` |\n| Checkbox | `completed: true` |\n| Date | `date: 2024-01-15` |\n| Date & Time | `due: 2024-01-15T14:30:00` |\n| List | `tags: [one, two]` or YAML list |\n| Links | `related: \"[[Other Note]]\"` |\n\n### Default Properties\n\n- `tags` - Note tags\n- `aliases` - Alternative names for the note\n- `cssclasses` - CSS classes applied to the note\n\n## Tags\n\n```markdown\n#tag\n#nested/tag\n#tag-with-dashes\n#tag_with_underscores\n\nIn frontmatter:\n---\ntags:\n  - tag1\n  - nested/tag2\n---\n```\n\nTags can contain:\n- Letters (any language)\n- Numbers (not as first character)\n- Underscores `_`\n- Hyphens `-`\n- Forward slashes `/` (for nesting)\n\n## HTML Content\n\nObsidian supports HTML within Markdown:\n\n```markdown\n<div class=\"custom-container\">\n  <span style=\"color: red;\">Colored text</span>\n</div>\n\n<details>\n  <summary>Click to expand</summary>\n  Hidden content here.\n</details>\n\n<kbd>Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>C</kbd>\n```\n\n## Complete Example\n\n````markdown\n---\ntitle: Project Alpha\ndate: 2024-01-15\ntags:\n  - project\n  - active\nstatus: in-progress\npriority: high\n---\n\n# Project Alpha\n\n## Overview\n\nThis project aims to [[improve workflow]] using modern techniques.\n\n> [!important] Key Deadline\n> The first milestone is due on ==January 30th==.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [x] Initial planning\n- [x] Resource allocation\n- [ ] Development phase\n  - [ ] Backend implementation\n  - [ ] Frontend design\n- [ ] Testing\n- [ ] Deployment\n\n## Technical Notes\n\nThe main algorithm uses the formula $O(n \\log n)$ for sorting.\n\n```python\ndef process_data(items):\n    return sorted(items, key=lambda x: x.priority)\n```\n\n## Architecture\n\n```mermaid\ngraph LR\n    A[Input] --> B[Process]\n    B --> C[Output]\n    B --> D[Cache]\n```\n\n## Related Documents\n\n- ![[Meeting Notes 2024-01-10#Decisions]]\n- [[Budget Allocation|Budget]]\n- [[Team Members]]\n\n## References\n\nFor more details, see the official documentation[^1].\n\n[^1]: https://example.com/docs\n\n%%\nInternal notes:\n- Review with team on Friday\n- Consider alternative approaches\n%%\n````\n\n## References\n\n- [Basic formatting syntax](https://help.obsidian.md/syntax)\n- [Advanced formatting syntax](https://help.obsidian.md/advanced-syntax)\n- [Obsidian Flavored Markdown](https://help.obsidian.md/obsidian-flavored-markdown)\n- [Internal links](https://help.obsidian.md/links)\n- [Embed files](https://help.obsidian.md/embeds)\n- [Callouts](https://help.obsidian.md/callouts)\n- [Properties](https://help.obsidian.md/properties)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:44:26.804Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Knowledge Management Agents needing to create and edit Obsidian Flavored Markdown documents with advanced syntax extensions.","zh":"非常适合需要创建和编辑具有高级语法扩展的 Obsidian 风格 Markdown 文档的知识管理代理。","ja":"Obsidian フレーバーの Markdown ドキュメントを作成および編集するために、高度な構文拡張機能が必要なナレッジマネジメントエージェントに最適です。","ko":"고급 구문 확장 기능을 갖춘 Obsidian风格의 Markdown 문서를 만들고 편집하는 데 필요한 지식 관리 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de gestión de conocimiento que necesitan crear y editar documentos de Markdown con extensiones de sintaxis avanzadas de Obsidian.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de gestion des connaissances ayant besoin de créer et de modifier des documents Markdown avec des extensions de syntaxe avancées Obsidian.","de":"Perfekt für Wissensmanagement-Agenten, die Obsidian-Flavored-Markdown-Dokumente mit erweiterten Syntax-Erweiterungen erstellen und bearbeiten müssen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Conhecimento que precisam criar e editar documentos no formato Obsidian Flavored Markdown com extensões de sintaxe avançadas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов управления знаниями, которым необходимо создавать и редактировать документы в формате Obsidian Flavored Markdown с расширенными синтаксическими расширениями.","ar":"مثالي لعميل إدارة المعرفة الذي يحتاج إلى إنشاء وتحرير مستندات Obsidian Flavored Markdown ذات امتدادات بنية متقدمة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to generate and manipulate markdown files with Obsidian-specific features like wikilinks, callouts, and embeds, while supporting CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown, and LaTeX for math expressions.","zh":"赋予代理生成和操作带有 Obsidian 特定功能（如 wikilinks、callouts 和 embeds）的 markdown 文件的能力，同时支持 CommonMark、GitHub 风格的 Markdown 和 LaTeX 用于数学表达式。","ja":"エージェントに、ウィキリンク、コールアウト、埋め込みなどの Obsidian 固有機能を持つ Markdown ファイルを生成および操作する能力を付与し、CommonMark、GitHub フレーバーの Markdown、LaTeX を数学式に使用することもサポートします。","ko":"에이전트가 Obsidian 특정 기능(wikilinks, callouts, embeds 등)을 갖춘 markdown 파일을 생성하고 조작할 수 있는 능력을 부여하며, CommonMark, GitHub风格의 Markdown, LaTeX를 수식에 사용하는 것도 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a generar y manipular archivos de markdown con características específicas de Obsidian como wikienlaces, llamadas y elementos incrustados, al mismo tiempo que admite CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown y LaTeX para expresiones matemáticas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de générer et de manipuler des fichiers markdown avec des fonctionnalités spécifiques à Obsidian comme les wikiliens, les appels et les éléments intégrés, tout en prenant en charge CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown et LaTeX pour les expressions mathématiques.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Markdown-Dateien mit Obsidian-spezifischen Funktionen wie Wikilinks, Callouts und Embedded-Elementen zu generieren und zu manipulieren, während CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown und LaTeX für mathematische Ausdrücke unterstützt werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerar e manipular arquivos markdown com recursos específicos do Obsidian, como wikilinks, callouts e embeds, além de suportar CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown e LaTeX para expressões matemáticas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью генерировать и манипулировать файлами markdown с функциями, специфичными для Obsidian, такими как wikilinks, callouts и embeds, при этом поддерживая CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown и LaTeX для математических выражений.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل إمكانية إنشاء وتعديل ملفات markdown باستخدام ميزات محددة ل Obsidian مثل wikilinks و callouts و embeds، مع دعم CommonMark و GitHub Flavored Markdown و LaTeX للتعبيرات الرياضية."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating documentation with Obsidian Flavored Markdown","Automating note-taking with wikilinks and callouts","Creating knowledge graphs with embedded content"],"zh":["使用 Obsidian 风格的 Markdown 生成文档","使用 wikilinks 和 callouts 自动化笔记记录","使用嵌入内容创建知识图"],"ja":["Obsidian フレーバーの Markdown を使用してドキュメントを生成する","ウィキリンクとコールアウトを使用してノートの記録を自動化する","埋め込みコンテンツを使用してナレッジグラフを作成する"],"ko":["Obsidian风格의 Markdown를 사용하여 문서를 생성","wikilinks와 callouts를 사용하여 노트 기록을 자동화","埋め込み 콘텐츠를 사용하여 지식 그래프를 생성"],"es":["Generación de documentación con Markdown con sabor a Obsidian","Automatización de la toma de notas con wikienlaces y llamadas","Creación de gráficos de conocimiento con contenido incrustado"],"fr":["Génération de documentation avec Markdown à saveur Obsidian","Automatisation de la prise de notes avec des wikiliens et des appels","Création de graphiques de connaissances avec du contenu intégré"],"de":["Erstellung von Dokumentationen mit Obsidian-Flavored-Markdown","Automatisierung der Notizen mit Wikilinks und Callouts","Erstellung von Wissensgraphen mit eingebettetem Inhalt"],"pt":["Geração de documentação com Obsidian Flavored Markdown","Automatização da tomada de notas com wikilinks e callouts","Criação de grafos de conhecimento com conteúdo incorporado"],"ru":["Генерация документации в формате Obsidian Flavored Markdown","Автоматизация ведения заметок с помощью wikilinks и callouts","Создание графов знаний с встроенным контентом"],"ar":["إنشاء توثيق باستخدام Obsidian Flavored Markdown","أتمتة تسجيل الملاحظات باستخدام wikilinks و callouts","إنشاء رسوم بيانية للمعرفة مع محتوى مدمج"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Markdown syntax and Obsidian extensions","Limited to text-based content creation"],"zh":["需要了解 Markdown 语法和 Obsidian 扩展","仅限于基于文本的内容创建"],"ja":["Markdown 構文と Obsidian 拡張機能の理解が必要","テキストベースのコンテンツ作成のみに限定される"],"ko":["Markdown 구문과 Obsidian 확장 기능을 이해해야 함","텍스트 기반 콘텐츠 생성만으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la sintaxis de Markdown y las extensiones de Obsidian","Limitado a la creación de contenido basado en texto"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la syntaxe Markdown et des extensions Obsidian","Limité à la création de contenu basé sur du texte"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis der Markdown-Syntax und der Obsidian-Erweiterungen","Begrenzt auf die Erstellung von textbasiertem Inhalt"],"pt":["Exige compreensão da sintaxe Markdown e das extensões do Obsidian","Limitado à criação de conteúdo baseado em texto"],"ru":["Требует понимания синтаксиса Markdown и расширений Obsidian","Ограничен созданием текстового контента"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم بنية Markdown وامتدادات Obsidian","محدود بالمحتوى القائم على النص"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":45}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('mhbdev/git-pal/swr', 'community', 'mhbdev', 'git-pal', 'mhbdev/git-pal', 'swr', 0, 0, 55, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z', '2026-02-18T08:44:25.899Z', NULL, '{"id":"mhbdev/git-pal/swr","name":"swr","description":{"zh":"SWR是一种React Hooks库，用于优化数据获取和缓存。通过SWR，开发者可以轻松实现数据的缓存和重新验证","ja":"SWRは、データ取得とキャッシュの最適化を行うReact Hooksライブラリです。SWRを使用すると、開発者はデータのキャッシュと再検証を簡単に実装できます","ko":"SWR는 데이터 가져오기와 캐싱을 최적화하는 리액트 훅스 라이브러리입니다. SWR를 사용하면 개발자가 데이터의 캐싱과 재검증을 쉽게 구현할 수 있습니다","es":"SWR es una biblioteca de React Hooks para la fetching de datos que devuelve datos de la caché y luego envía la solicitud para obtener datos actualizados","fr":"SWR est une bibliothèque de React Hooks pour la récupération de données qui renvoie des données de la mémoire cache puis envoie la requête pour obtenir des données à jour","de":"SWR ist eine React-Hooks-Bibliothek für Datenabruf, die Daten aus dem Cache zurückgibt und dann die Anfrage sendet, um aktuelle Daten zu erhalten","pt":"A biblioteca SWR é uma ferramenta poderosa para buscar dados em aplicativos React, oferecendo caching e revalidação automática","ru":"Библиотека SWR является мощным инструментом для запроса данных в приложениях React, предлагающим автоматическое кэширование и ревалидацию","ar":"مكتبة SWR هي أداة قوية لاسترجاع البيانات في تطبيقات React، توفر التخزين المؤقت والتحديث التلقائي","en":"Your friendly neighborhood GitPal!"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"SWR最佳实践：优化React数据获取","ja":"SWRベストプラクティス：Reactのデータ取得を最適化","ko":"SWR 최적화 방법: 리액트 데이터 가져오기 최적화","es":"SWR: Mejores prácticas para desarrolladores","fr":"SWR : Meilleures pratiques pour les développeurs","de":"SWR: Best Practices für Entwickler","pt":"Melhores Práticas SWR para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Лучшие практики SWR для разработчиков","ar":"أفضل الممارسات لبرنامج SWR للمطورين","en":"swr"},"description":{"zh":"SWR是一种React Hooks库，用于优化数据获取和缓存。通过SWR，开发者可以轻松实现数据的缓存和重新验证","ja":"SWRは、データ取得とキャッシュの最適化を行うReact Hooksライブラリです。SWRを使用すると、開発者はデータのキャッシュと再検証を簡単に実装できます","ko":"SWR는 데이터 가져오기와 캐싱을 최적화하는 리액트 훅스 라이브러리입니다. SWR를 사용하면 개발자가 데이터의 캐싱과 재검증을 쉽게 구현할 수 있습니다","es":"SWR es una biblioteca de React Hooks para la fetching de datos que devuelve datos de la caché y luego envía la solicitud para obtener datos actualizados","fr":"SWR est une bibliothèque de React Hooks pour la récupération de données qui renvoie des données de la mémoire cache puis envoie la requête pour obtenir des d...","de":"SWR ist eine React-Hooks-Bibliothek für Datenabruf, die Daten aus dem Cache zurückgibt und dann die Anfrage sendet, um aktuelle Daten zu erhalten","pt":"A biblioteca SWR é uma ferramenta poderosa para buscar dados em aplicativos React, oferecendo caching e revalidação automática","ru":"Библиотека SWR является мощным инструментом для запроса данных в приложениях React, предлагающим автоматическое кэширование и ревалидацию","ar":"مكتبة SWR هي أداة قوية لاسترجاع البيانات في تطبيقات React، توفر التخزين المؤقت والتحديث التلقائي","en":"Your friendly neighborhood GitPal!"},"definition":{"en":"Your friendly neighborhood GitPal!"},"features":{"zh":["自动缓存和重新验证","最小化样板代码","实现适当的错误处理和加载状态","支持TypeScript和React开发"],"ja":["自動キャッシュと再検証","ボイラープレートコードの最小化","適切なエラーハンドリングとロード状態の実装","TypeScriptとReact開発のサポート"],"ko":["자동 캐싱 및 재검증","보일러เพล이트 코드 최소화","適切한 오류 처리 및 로딩 상태 구현","타입스크립트 및 리액트 개발 지원"],"es":["Uso de SWR para todas las operaciones de fetching de datos del lado del cliente","Caché automático y revalidación","Minimización del código boilerplate con el estado de gestión integrado de SWR","Implementación de manejo de errores y estados de carga adecuados","Integración con TypeScript y React"],"fr":["Utilisation de SWR pour toutes les opérations de récupération de données côté client","Mise en cache automatique et revalidation","Minimisation du code boilerplate avec la gestion d''état intégrée de SWR","Implémentation d''un traitement des erreurs et d''états de chargement appropriés","Intégration avec TypeScript et React"],"de":["Verwendung von SWR für alle Client-seitigen Datenabrufoperationen","Automatisches Caching und Revalidierung","Minimierung von Boilerplate-Code mit der integrierten Zustandsverwaltung von SWR","Implementierung einer geeigneten Fehlerbehandlung und Ladezustände","Integration mit TypeScript und React"],"pt":["Uso de caching automático","Revalidação de dados em tempo real","Gerenciamento de estado integrado","Tratamento de erros e estados de carregamento","Integração com React e TypeScript"],"ru":["Использование автоматического кэширования","Реалидация данных в режиме реального времени","Встроенное управление состоянием","Обработка ошибок и состояний загрузки","Интеграция с React и TypeScript"],"ar":["استخدام التخزين المؤقت التلقائي","التحقق من البيانات في الوقت الفعلي","إدارة الحالة المدمجة","معالجة الأخطاء و_states التحميل","التكامل مع React و TypeScript"]},"keywords":{"zh":["SWR","React Hooks","数据获取","缓存","重新验证","TypeScript","React开发"],"ja":["SWR","React Hooks","データ取得","キャッシュ","再検証","TypeScript","React開発"],"ko":["SWR","리액트 훅스","데이터 가져오기","캐싱","재검증","타입스크립트","리액트 개발"],"es":["SWR","React Hooks","fetching de datos","caché","revalidación","TypeScript","React","desarrollo web","mejores prácticas"],"fr":["SWR","React Hooks","récupération de données","cache","revalidation","TypeScript","React","développement web","meilleures pratiques"],"de":["SWR","React Hooks","Datenabruf","Cache","Revalidierung","TypeScript","React","Webentwicklung","Best Practices"],"pt":["SWR","React","TypeScript","caching","revalidação","gerenciamento de estado","tratamento de erros","desenvolvimento web"],"ru":["SWR","React","TypeScript","кэширование","реалидация","управление состоянием","обработка ошибок","веб-разработка"],"ar":["SWR","React","TypeScript","التخزين المؤقت","التحقق","إدارة الحالة","معالجة الأخطاء","تطوير الويب"]}},"owner":"mhbdev","repo":"git-pal","repoPath":"mhbdev/git-pal","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"swr","description":"Guidelines for using SWR (stale-while-revalidate) React Hooks for efficient data fetching, caching, and revalidation","bodyPreview":"# SWR Best Practices\n\nYou are an expert in SWR (stale-while-revalidate), TypeScript, and React development. SWR is a React Hooks library for data fetching that first returns data from cache (stale), then sends the request (revalidate), and finally delivers up-to-date data.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n- Use SWR for all client-side data fetching\n- Leverage automatic caching and revalidation\n- Minimize boilerplate with SWR''s built-in state management\n- Implement proper error handling and loading states\n-","body":"# SWR Best Practices\n\nYou are an expert in SWR (stale-while-revalidate), TypeScript, and React development. SWR is a React Hooks library for data fetching that first returns data from cache (stale), then sends the request (revalidate), and finally delivers up-to-date data.\n\n## Core Principles\n\n- Use SWR for all client-side data fetching\n- Leverage automatic caching and revalidation\n- Minimize boilerplate with SWR''s built-in state management\n- Implement proper error handling and loading states\n- Use TypeScript for full type safety\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Stale-While-Revalidate**: Returns cached data immediately, then revalidates in background\n- **Automatic Revalidation**: On mount, window focus, and network reconnection\n- **Request Deduplication**: Multiple components using same key share one request\n- **Built-in Caching**: Zero-configuration caching with smart invalidation\n- **Minimal API**: Simple hook-based interface\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\nsrc/\n  hooks/\n    swr/\n      useUser.ts\n      usePosts.ts\n      useProducts.ts\n  lib/\n    fetcher.ts           # Global fetcher configuration\n  providers/\n    SWRProvider.tsx      # SWR configuration provider\n  types/\n    api.ts               # API response types\n```\n\n## Setup and Configuration\n\n### Global Configuration\n\n```typescript\n// providers/SWRProvider.tsx\nimport { SWRConfig } from ''swr'';\n\nconst fetcher = async (url: string) => {\n  const res = await fetch(url);\n\n  if (!res.ok) {\n    const error = new Error(''An error occurred while fetching data.'');\n    throw error;\n  }\n\n  return res.json();\n};\n\nexport function SWRProvider({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {\n  return (\n    <SWRConfig\n      value={{\n        fetcher,\n        revalidateOnFocus: true,\n        revalidateOnReconnect: true,\n        shouldRetryOnError: true,\n        errorRetryCount: 3,\n        dedupingInterval: 2000,\n      }}\n    >\n      {children}\n    </SWRConfig>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Custom Fetcher\n\n```typescript\n// lib/fetcher.ts\nexport async function fetcher<T>(url: string): Promise<T> {\n  const response = await fetch(url, {\n    headers: {\n      ''Content-Type'': ''application/json'',\n    },\n  });\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);\n  }\n\n  return response.json();\n}\n\n// With authentication\nexport async function authFetcher<T>(url: string): Promise<T> {\n  const token = getAuthToken();\n\n  const response = await fetch(url, {\n    headers: {\n      ''Content-Type'': ''application/json'',\n      ''Authorization'': `Bearer ${token}`,\n    },\n  });\n\n  if (!response.ok) {\n    throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);\n  }\n\n  return response.json();\n}\n```\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n### useSWR Hook\n\nThe `useSWR` hook accepts three parameters:\n- **key**: A unique string identifier for the request (like a URL)\n- **fetcher**: An async function that fetches the data\n- **options**: Configuration options\n\n```typescript\nimport useSWR from ''swr'';\n\ninterface User {\n  id: string;\n  name: string;\n  email: string;\n}\n\nfunction useUser(userId: string) {\n  const { data, error, isLoading, isValidating, mutate } = useSWR<User>(\n    userId ? `/api/users/${userId}` : null,\n    fetcher\n  );\n\n  return {\n    user: data,\n    isLoading,\n    isError: !!error,\n    isValidating,\n    mutate,\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### Conditional Fetching\n\nPass `null` or a falsy value as key to conditionally skip fetching:\n\n```typescript\n// Only fetch when userId is available\nconst { data } = useSWR(userId ? `/api/users/${userId}` : null, fetcher);\n\n// Using a function for dynamic keys\nconst { data } = useSWR(() => `/api/users/${userId}`, fetcher);\n```\n\n## Revalidation Strategies\n\n### Automatic Revalidation\n\nSWR automatically revalidates data in three cases:\n1. Component is mounted (even with cached data)\n2. Window gains focus\n3. Browser regains network connection\n\n```typescript\n// Disable specific revalidation behaviors\nconst { data } = useSWR(''/api/data'', fetcher, {\n  revalidateOnFocus: false,\n  revalidateOnReconnect: false,\n  revalidateOnMount: true,\n});\n```\n\n### Manual Revalidation\n\n```typescript\nimport { useSWRConfig } from ''swr'';\n\nfunction UpdateButton() {\n  const { mutate } = useSWRConfig();\n\n  const handleUpdate = async () => {\n    // Revalidate specific key\n    await mutate(''/api/users'');\n\n    // Revalidate all keys matching a filter\n    await mutate(\n      (key) => typeof key === ''string'' && key.startsWith(''/api/users''),\n      undefined,\n      { revalidate: true }\n    );\n  };\n\n  return <button onClick={handleUpdate}>Refresh</button>;\n}\n```\n\n### Polling / Interval Refresh\n\n```typescript\n// Refresh every 3 seconds\nconst { data } = useSWR(''/api/realtime'', fetcher, {\n  refreshInterval: 3000,\n});\n\n// Conditional polling\nconst { data } = useSWR(''/api/realtime'', fetcher, {\n  refreshInterval: isVisible ? 1000 : 0,\n});\n```\n\n## Mutation Patterns\n\n### Optimistic Updates\n\n```typescript\nimport useSWR, { useSWRConfig } from ''swr'';\n\nfunction useUpdateUser() {\n  const { mutate } = useSWRConfig();\n\n  const updateUser = async (userId: string, newData: Partial<User>) => {\n    // Optimistic update\n    await mutate(\n      `/api/users/${userId}`,\n      async (currentData: User | undefined) => {\n        // Update API\n        const updated = await fetch(`/api/users/${userId}`, {\n          method: ''PATCH'',\n          body: JSON.stringify(newData),\n        }).then(r => r.json());\n\n        return updated;\n      },\n      {\n        optimisticData: (current) => ({ ...current, ...newData } as User),\n        rollbackOnError: true,\n        populateCache: true,\n        revalidate: false,\n      }\n    );\n  };\n\n  return { updateUser };\n}\n```\n\n### Bound Mutate\n\n```typescript\nfunction UserProfile({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\n  const { data: user, mutate } = useSWR(`/api/users/${userId}`, fetcher);\n\n  const handleUpdate = async (newName: string) => {\n    // Update local data immediately\n    mutate({ ...user, name: newName }, false);\n\n    // Send update to server\n    await updateUserName(userId, newName);\n\n    // Revalidate to ensure consistency\n    mutate();\n  };\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <p>{user?.name}</p>\n      <button onClick={() => handleUpdate(''New Name'')}>Update</button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Pagination\n\n### Basic Pagination\n\n```typescript\nfunction usePaginatedUsers(page: number) {\n  return useSWR(`/api/users?page=${page}`, fetcher, {\n    keepPreviousData: true,\n  });\n}\n```\n\n### Infinite Loading with useSWRInfinite\n\n```typescript\nimport useSWRInfinite from ''swr/infinite'';\n\nfunction useInfiniteUsers() {\n  const getKey = (pageIndex: number, previousPageData: User[] | null) => {\n    // Return null to stop fetching\n    if (previousPageData && previousPageData.length === 0) return null;\n\n    // Return key for next page\n    return `/api/users?page=${pageIndex + 1}`;\n  };\n\n  const { data, error, size, setSize, isValidating } = useSWRInfinite(\n    getKey,\n    fetcher\n  );\n\n  const users = data ? data.flat() : [];\n  const isLoadingMore = size > 0 && data && typeof data[size - 1] === ''undefined'';\n  const isEmpty = data?.[0]?.length === 0;\n  const isReachingEnd = isEmpty || (data && data[data.length - 1]?.length < 10);\n\n  return {\n    users,\n    isLoadingMore,\n    isReachingEnd,\n    loadMore: () => setSize(size + 1),\n  };\n}\n```\n\n### Cursor-Based Pagination\n\n```typescript\nimport useSWRInfinite from ''swr/infinite'';\n\nfunction useCursorPagination() {\n  const getKey = (pageIndex: number, previousPageData: any) => {\n    if (previousPageData && !previousPageData.nextCursor) return null;\n\n    if (pageIndex === 0) return ''/api/items'';\n\n    return `/api/items?cursor=${previousPageData.nextCursor}`;\n  };\n\n  return useSWRInfinite(getKey, fetcher);\n}\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\n### Component-Level Error Handling\n\n```typescript\nfunction UserProfile({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\n  const { data, error, isLoading } = useSWR(`/api/users/${userId}`, fetcher);\n\n  if (isLoading) return <Skeleton />;\n\n  if (error) {\n    return (\n      <ErrorMessage\n        message=\"Failed to load user profile\"\n        retry={() => mutate(`/api/users/${userId}`)}\n      />\n    );\n  }\n\n  return <ProfileCard user={data} />;\n}\n```\n\n### Global Error Handler\n\n```typescript\n<SWRConfig\n  value={{\n    onError: (error, key) => {\n      if (error.status !== 403 && error.status !== 404) {\n        // Send error to tracking service\n        reportError(error, key);\n      }\n    },\n  }}\n>\n  <App />\n</SWRConfig>\n```\n\n## Prefetching\n\n```typescript\nimport { preload } from ''swr'';\n\n// Prefetch data before component renders\nfunction prefetchUser(userId: string) {\n  preload(`/api/users/${userId}`, fetcher);\n}\n\n// Usage: Call on hover or route change\nfunction UserLink({ userId }: { userId: string }) {\n  return (\n    <Link\n      to={`/users/${userId}`}\n      onMouseEnter={() => prefetchUser(userId)}\n    >\n      View Profile\n    </Link>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Key Conventions\n\n1. Use SWR for client-side data fetching with minimal configuration\n2. Implement conditional rendering for loading states and error messages\n3. Validate data to ensure expected format and handle errors gracefully\n4. Use prefetching to improve performance before users request data\n5. Leverage automatic revalidation for real-time data freshness\n6. Use `useSWRInfinite` for paginated and infinite scroll patterns\n\n## Integration with Next.js\n\n```typescript\n// For server-side data, use getServerSideProps or getStaticProps\n// For client-side caching and revalidation, use SWR\n\n// pages/user/[id].tsx\nexport async function getStaticProps({ params }) {\n  const user = await fetchUser(params.id);\n  return { props: { fallback: { [`/api/users/${params.id}`]: user } } };\n}\n\nexport default function UserPage({ fallback }) {\n  return (\n    <SWRConfig value={{ fallback }}>\n      <UserProfile />\n    </SWRConfig>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n- Do not use `useEffect` for data fetching when SWR can handle it\n- Do not ignore error states - always provide user feedback\n- Do not forget to handle loading states appropriately\n- Do not use polling when WebSocket or SSE would be more efficient\n- Do not skip conditional fetching for dependent data\n- Do not ignore TypeScript types for fetched data\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:44:25.899Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Frontend Agents needing efficient client-side data fetching with React Hooks.","zh":"适合需要在客户端高效获取数据并使用React Hooks的前端代理。","ja":"フロントエンドエージェントがクライアントサイドで効率的にデータを取得するためにReact Hooksを必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"클라이언트 측에서 데이터를 효율적으로 가져오는 데 리액트 훅이 필요한 프론트엔드 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes Frontend que necesitan una recuperación de datos eficiente del lado del cliente con React Hooks.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents Frontend qui ont besoin d''une récupération de données efficace côté client avec React Hooks.","de":"Perfekt für Frontend-Agents, die eine effiziente Client-seitige Datenabfrage mit React Hooks benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Frontend que necessitam de busca de dados eficiente no lado do cliente com React Hooks.","ru":"Идеально для агентов Frontend, которым требуется эффективная выборка данных на стороне клиента с помощью React Hooks.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الأمامي الذين يحتاجون إلى استرجاع البيانات الفعالة على جانب العميل مع React Hooks."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage automatic caching and revalidation with SWR, minimizing boilerplate code and implementing proper error handling and loading states using TypeScript and React.","zh":"赋予代理使用SWR实现自动缓存和重新验证，最大限度地减少样板代码，并使用TypeScript和React实现适当的错误处理和加载状态。","ja":"エージェントがSWRを使用して自動キャッシュと再検証を利用できるようにし、ボイラープレートコードを最小限に抑え、TypeScriptとReactを使用して適切なエラー処理とロード状態を実装します。","ko":"에이전트가 SWR을 사용하여 자동 캐싱 및 재검증을 활용할 수 있도록 하여 불필요한 코드를 최소화하고, 타입스크립트 및 리액트를 사용하여 적절한 오류 처리 및 로딩 상태를 구현합니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes aprovechar la caché automática y la revalidación con SWR, minimizando el código de plantilla y implementando un manejo de errores y estados de carga adecuados con TypeScript y React.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exploiter la mise en cache automatique et la révalidation avec SWR, en minimisant le code de modèle et en mettant en œuvre une gestion des erreurs et des états de chargement appropriée avec TypeScript et React.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, automatisches Caching und Revalidierung mit SWR zu nutzen, Boilerplate-Code zu minimieren und ordnungsgemäßes Fehlerhandling und Ladezustände mit TypeScript und React umzusetzen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitar o cache automático e a revalidação com SWR, minimizando o código boilerplate e implementando o tratamento de erros e estados de carregamento adequados usando TypeScript e React.","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать автоматический кэш и ревалидацию с помощью SWR, минимизируя код boilerplate и реализуя правильную обработку ошибок и состояния загрузки с помощью TypeScript и React.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من الاستفادة من التخزين المؤقت التلقائي وإعادة التحقق مع SWR، وتقليل代码 boilerplate وتنفيذ معالجة الأخطاء وال стану التحميل الصحيحة باستخدام TypeScript و React."},"useCases":{"en":["Implementing stale-while-revalidate caching for faster data retrieval","Optimizing React applications with SWR''s built-in state management","Handling errors and loading states in client-side data fetching"],"zh":["实现stale-while-revalidate缓存以加快数据检索","使用SWR的内置状态管理优化React应用程序","处理客户端数据获取中的错误和加载状态"],"ja":["stale-while-revalidateキャッシュを実装してデータ取得を高速化する","SWRの組み込みステート管理を使用してReactアプリケーションを最適化する","クライアントサイドのデータ取得におけるエラーとロード状態を処理する"],"ko":["캐싱을 사용하여 데이터 검색을 더 빠르게 하는 stale-while-revalidate 구현","SWR의 기본 상태 관리를 사용하여 리액트 애플리케이션 최적화","클라이언트 측 데이터 가져오기에서 오류 및 로딩 상태 처리"],"es":["Implementar caché stale-while-revalidate para una recuperación de datos más rápida","Optimizar aplicaciones React con la administración de estado integrada de SWR","Manejar errores y estados de carga en la recuperación de datos del lado del cliente"],"fr":["Mettre en œuvre une mise en cache stale-while-revalidate pour une récupération de données plus rapide","Optimiser les applications React avec la gestion d''état intégrée de SWR","Gérer les erreurs et les états de chargement dans la récupération de données côté client"],"de":["Implementierung von stale-while-revalidate-Caching für schnellere Datenabruf","Optimierung von React-Anwendungen mit der integrierten Zustandsverwaltung von SWR","Handhabung von Fehlern und Ladezuständen bei der clientseitigen Datenabfrage"],"pt":["Implementação de cache stale-while-revalidate para recuperação de dados mais rápida","Otimização de aplicações React com gerenciamento de estado incorporado do SWR","Tratamento de erros e estados de carregamento na busca de dados no lado do cliente"],"ru":["Реализация кэширования stale-while-revalidate для более быстрого извлечения данных","Оптимизация приложений React с помощью встроенного управления состоянием SWR","Обработка