OpenSpec: دورة العمل الكاملة الأولى","en":"openspec-onboard"},"description":{"zh":"本教程指导用户完成首个OpenSpec工作流程周期，实践代码库中的每一步","ja":"OpenSpecのワークフローを実践しながら、各ステップを理解する","ko":"OpenSpec의 첫 번째 워크플로 사이클을 완료하고 코드베이스에서 실제 작업을 수행합니다","es":"OpenSpec es una herramienta para guiar a los usuarios a través de su primer ciclo de trabajo completo. Incluye la inicialización y configuración de OpenSpec.","fr":"OpenSpec est un outil pour guider les utilisateurs à travers leur premier cycle de travail complet. Il inclut l''initialisation et la configuration d''OpenSpec.","de":"OpenSpec ist ein Tool, um Benutzer durch ihren ersten kompletten Arbeitszyklus zu führen. Es umfasst die Initialisierung und Konfiguration von OpenSpec.","pt":"O OpenSpec é uma ferramenta para automatizar o fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento. Neste guia, você aprenderá a configurar e utilizar o OpenSpec com o Kirb...","ru":"OpenSpec — это инструмент для автоматизации рабочего процесса разработки. В этом руководстве вы узнаете, как настроить и использовать OpenSpec с Kirby Site S...","ar":"OpenSpec هو أداة لتسريع دورة العمل التطويرية. في هذا الدليل، ستتعلم كيفية تشغيل وتكوين OpenSpec باستخدام Kirby Site Starter.","en":"Michael van Laar’s Kirby Site Starter"},"definition":{"en":"Michael van Laar’s Kirby Site Starter"},"features":{"zh":["开源的代码管理工具","支持多语言","简单易用","高效的代码管理"],"ja":["オープンソースのコード管理ツール","複数言語対応","シンプルで使いやすい","効率的なコード管理"],"ko":["오픈소스의 코드 관리 도구","다중 언어 지원","간단하고 쉽게 사용","효율적인 코드 관리"],"es":["Guía de onboarding para desarrolladores","Inicialización y configuración de OpenSpec","Ciclo de trabajo completo con OpenSpec","Integración con proyectos de código abierto","Automatización de flujos de trabajo"],"fr":["Guide d''onboarding pour les développeurs","Initialisation et configuration d''OpenSpec","Cycle de travail complet avec OpenSpec","Intégration avec des projets open source","Automatisation de flux de travail"],"de":["Onboarding-Anleitung für Entwickler","Initialisierung und Konfiguration von OpenSpec","Kompletter Arbeitszyklus mit OpenSpec","Integration mit Open-Source-Projekten","Automatisierung von Arbeitsabläufen"],"pt":["Configuração inicial do OpenSpec","Ciclo de trabalho completo com o Kirby Site Starter","Explicação passo a passo do fluxo de trabalho","Verificação de inicialização do OpenSpec","Integração com o código da aplicação"],"ru":["Первоначальная настройка OpenSpec","Полный цикл работы с Kirby Site Starter","Пошаговое объяснение рабочего процесса","Проверка инициализации OpenSpec","Интеграция с кодом приложения"],"ar":["تكوين الأولي لبرنامج OpenSpec","دورة العمل الكاملة مع Kirby Site Starter","شرح خطوة بخطوة لدورة العمل","فحص تشغيل برنامج OpenSpec","التكامل مع كود التطبيق"]},"keywords":{"zh":["OpenSpec","代码管理","开源工具","开发者工具","代码库管理","工作流程"],"ja":["OpenSpec","コード管理","オープンソースツール","開発者ツール","コードライブラリ管理","ワークフロー"],"ko":["OpenSpec","코드 관리","오픈소스 도구","개발자 도구","코드 라이브러리 관리","워크플로우"],"es":["OpenSpec","onboarding","desarrollo de software","automatización de flujos de trabajo","código abierto","guía para desarrolladores"],"fr":["OpenSpec","onboarding","développement de logiciels","automatisation de flux de travail","code source ouvert","guide pour les développeurs"],"de":["OpenSpec","Onboarding","Softwareentwicklung","Automatisierung von Arbeitsabläufen","Open-Source-Code","Anleitung für Entwickler"],"pt":["OpenSpec","Kirby Site Starter","fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento","automação de fluxo de trabalho","desenvolvimento de software","ferramentas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["OpenSpec","Kirby Site Starter","рабочий процесс разработки","автоматизация рабочего процесса","разработка программного обеспечения","инструменты разработки"],"ar":["OpenSpec","Kirby Site Starter","دورة العمل التطويرية","تسريع دورة العمل","تطوير البرمجيات","أدوات التطوير"]}},"owner":"MichaelvanLaar","repo":"mvlkss","repoPath":"MichaelvanLaar/mvlkss","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"openspec-onboard","description":"Guided onboarding for OpenSpec - walk through a complete workflow cycle with narration and real codebase work.","version":"1.0","bodyPreview":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay","body":"Guide the user through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle. This is a teaching experience—you''ll do real work in their codebase while explaining each step.\n\n---\n\n## Preflight\n\nBefore starting, check if OpenSpec is initialized:\n\n```bash\nopenspec status --json 2>&1 || echo \"NOT_INITIALIZED\"\n```\n\n**If not initialized:**\n> OpenSpec isn''t set up in this project yet. Run `openspec init` first, then come back to `/opsx:onboard`.\n\nStop here if not initialized.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 1: Welcome\n\nDisplay:\n\n```\n## Welcome to OpenSpec!\n\nI''ll walk you through a complete change cycle—from idea to implementation—using a real task in your codebase. Along the way, you''ll learn the workflow by doing it.\n\n**What we''ll do:**\n1. Pick a small, real task in your codebase\n2. Explore the problem briefly\n3. Create a change (the container for our work)\n4. Build the artifacts: proposal → specs → design → tasks\n5. Implement the tasks\n6. Archive the completed change\n\n**Time:** ~15-20 minutes\n\nLet''s start by finding something to work on.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2: Task Selection\n\n### Codebase Analysis\n\nScan the codebase for small improvement opportunities. Look for:\n\n1. **TODO/FIXME comments** - Search for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX` in code files\n2. **Missing error handling** - `catch` blocks that swallow errors, risky operations without try-catch\n3. **Functions without tests** - Cross-reference `src/` with test directories\n4. **Type issues** - `any` types in TypeScript files (`: any`, `as any`)\n5. **Debug artifacts** - `console.log`, `console.debug`, `debugger` statements in non-debug code\n6. **Missing validation** - User input handlers without validation\n\nAlso check recent git activity:\n```bash\ngit log --oneline -10 2>/dev/null || echo \"No git history\"\n```\n\n### Present Suggestions\n\nFrom your analysis, present 3-4 specific suggestions:\n\n```\n## Task Suggestions\n\nBased on scanning your codebase, here are some good starter tasks:\n\n**1. [Most promising task]**\n   Location: `src/path/to/file.ts:42`\n   Scope: ~1-2 files, ~20-30 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**2. [Second task]**\n   Location: `src/another/file.ts`\n   Scope: ~1 file, ~15 lines\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**3. [Third task]**\n   Location: [location]\n   Scope: [estimate]\n   Why it''s good: [brief reason]\n\n**4. Something else?**\n   Tell me what you''d like to work on.\n\nWhich task interests you? (Pick a number or describe your own)\n```\n\n**If nothing found:** Fall back to asking what the user wants to build:\n> I didn''t find obvious quick wins in your codebase. What''s something small you''ve been meaning to add or fix?\n\n### Scope Guardrail\n\nIf the user picks or describes something too large (major feature, multi-day work):\n\n```\nThat''s a valuable task, but it''s probably larger than ideal for your first OpenSpec run-through.\n\nFor learning the workflow, smaller is better—it lets you see the full cycle without getting stuck in implementation details.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Slice it smaller** - What''s the smallest useful piece of [their task]? Maybe just [specific slice]?\n2. **Pick something else** - One of the other suggestions, or a different small task?\n3. **Do it anyway** - If you really want to tackle this, we can. Just know it''ll take longer.\n\nWhat would you prefer?\n```\n\nLet the user override if they insist—this is a soft guardrail.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 3: Explore Demo\n\nOnce a task is selected, briefly demonstrate explore mode:\n\n```\nBefore we create a change, let me quickly show you **explore mode**—it''s how you think through problems before committing to a direction.\n```\n\nSpend 1-2 minutes investigating the relevant code:\n- Read the file(s) involved\n- Draw a quick ASCII diagram if it helps\n- Note any considerations\n\n```\n## Quick Exploration\n\n[Your brief analysis—what you found, any considerations]\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│   [Optional: ASCII diagram if helpful]  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nExplore mode (`/opsx:explore`) is for this kind of thinking—investigating before implementing. You can use it anytime you need to think through a problem.\n\nNow let''s create a change to hold our work.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user acknowledgment before proceeding.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 4: Create the Change\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Creating a Change\n\nA \"change\" in OpenSpec is a container for all the thinking and planning around a piece of work. It lives in `openspec/changes/<name>/` and holds your artifacts—proposal, specs, design, tasks.\n\nLet me create one for our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the change with a derived kebab-case name:\n```bash\nopenspec new change \"<derived-name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nCreated: `openspec/changes/<name>/`\n\nThe folder structure:\n```\nopenspec/changes/<name>/\n├── proposal.md    ← Why we''re doing this (empty, we''ll fill it)\n├── design.md      ← How we''ll build it (empty)\n├── specs/         ← Detailed requirements (empty)\n└── tasks.md       ← Implementation checklist (empty)\n```\n\nNow let''s fill in the first artifact—the proposal.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 5: Proposal\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## The Proposal\n\nThe proposal captures **why** we''re making this change and **what** it involves at a high level. It''s the \"elevator pitch\" for the work.\n\nI''ll draft one based on our task.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft the proposal content (don''t save yet):\n\n```\nHere''s a draft proposal:\n\n---\n\n## Why\n\n[1-2 sentences explaining the problem/opportunity]\n\n## What Changes\n\n[Bullet points of what will be different]\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### New Capabilities\n- `<capability-name>`: [brief description]\n\n### Modified Capabilities\n<!-- If modifying existing behavior -->\n\n## Impact\n\n- `src/path/to/file.ts`: [what changes]\n- [other files if applicable]\n\n---\n\nDoes this capture the intent? I can adjust before we save it.\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user approval/feedback.\n\nAfter approval, save the proposal:\n```bash\nopenspec instructions proposal --change \"<name>\" --json\n```\nThen write the content to `openspec/changes/<name>/proposal.md`.\n\n```\nProposal saved. This is your \"why\" document—you can always come back and refine it as understanding evolves.\n\nNext up: specs.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 6: Specs\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Specs\n\nSpecs define **what** we''re building in precise, testable terms. They use a requirement/scenario format that makes expected behavior crystal clear.\n\nFor a small task like this, we might only need one spec file.\n```\n\n**DO:** Create the spec file:\n```bash\nmkdir -p openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability-name>\n```\n\nDraft the spec content:\n\n```\nHere''s the spec:\n\n---\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: <Name>\n\n<Description of what the system should do>\n\n#### Scenario: <Scenario name>\n\n- **WHEN** <trigger condition>\n- **THEN** <expected outcome>\n- **AND** <additional outcome if needed>\n\n---\n\nThis format—WHEN/THEN/AND—makes requirements testable. You can literally read them as test cases.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/specs/<capability>/spec.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 7: Design\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Design\n\nThe design captures **how** we''ll build it—technical decisions, tradeoffs, approach.\n\nFor small changes, this might be brief. That''s fine—not every change needs deep design discussion.\n```\n\n**DO:** Draft design.md:\n\n```\nHere''s the design:\n\n---\n\n## Context\n\n[Brief context about the current state]\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- [What we''re trying to achieve]\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- [What''s explicitly out of scope]\n\n## Decisions\n\n### Decision 1: [Key decision]\n\n[Explanation of approach and rationale]\n\n---\n\nFor a small task, this captures the key decisions without over-engineering.\n```\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/design.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 8: Tasks\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Tasks\n\nFinally, we break the work into implementation tasks—checkboxes that drive the apply phase.\n\nThese should be small, clear, and in logical order.\n```\n\n**DO:** Generate tasks based on specs and design:\n\n```\nHere are the implementation tasks:\n\n---\n\n## 1. [Category or file]\n\n- [ ] 1.1 [Specific task]\n- [ ] 1.2 [Specific task]\n\n## 2. Verify\n\n- [ ] 2.1 [Verification step]\n\n---\n\nEach checkbox becomes a unit of work in the apply phase. Ready to implement?\n```\n\n**PAUSE** - Wait for user to confirm they''re ready to implement.\n\nSave to `openspec/changes/<name>/tasks.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 9: Apply (Implementation)\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Implementation\n\nNow we implement each task, checking them off as we go. I''ll announce each one and occasionally note how the specs/design informed the approach.\n```\n\n**DO:** For each task:\n\n1. Announce: \"Working on task N: [description]\"\n2. Implement the change in the codebase\n3. Reference specs/design naturally: \"The spec says X, so I''m doing Y\"\n4. Mark complete in tasks.md: `- [ ]` → `- [x]`\n5. Brief status: \"✓ Task N complete\"\n\nKeep narration light—don''t over-explain every line of code.\n\nAfter all tasks:\n\n```\n## Implementation Complete\n\nAll tasks done:\n- [x] Task 1\n- [x] Task 2\n- [x] ...\n\nThe change is implemented! One more step—let''s archive it.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 10: Archive\n\n**EXPLAIN:**\n```\n## Archiving\n\nWhen a change is complete, we archive it. This moves it from `openspec/changes/` to `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`.\n\nArchived changes become your project''s decision history—you can always find them later to understand why something was built a certain way.\n```\n\n**DO:**\n```bash\nopenspec archive \"<name>\"\n```\n\n**SHOW:**\n```\nArchived to: `openspec/changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-<name>/`\n\nThe change is now part of your project''s history. The code is in your codebase, the decision record is preserved.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Phase 11: Recap & Next Steps\n\n```\n## Congratulations!\n\nYou just completed a full OpenSpec cycle:\n\n1. **Explore** - Thought through the problem\n2. **New** - Created a change container\n3. **Proposal** - Captured WHY\n4. **Specs** - Defined WHAT in detail\n5. **Design** - Decided HOW\n6. **Tasks** - Broke it into steps\n7. **Apply** - Implemented the work\n8. **Archive** - Preserved the record\n\nThis same rhythm works for any size change—a small fix or a major feature.\n\n---\n\n## Command Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems before/during work |\n| `/opsx:new` | Start a new change, step through artifacts |\n| `/opsx:ff` | Fast-forward: create all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue` | Continue working on an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply` | Implement tasks from a change |\n| `/opsx:verify` | Verify implementation matches artifacts |\n| `/opsx:archive` | Archive a completed change |\n\n---\n\n## What''s Next?\n\nTry `/opsx:new` or `/opsx:ff` on something you actually want to build. You''ve got the rhythm now!\n```\n\n---\n\n## Graceful Exit Handling\n\n### User wants to stop mid-way\n\nIf the user says they need to stop, want to pause, or seem disengaged:\n\n```\nNo problem! Your change is saved at `openspec/changes/<name>/`.\n\nTo pick up where we left off later:\n- `/opsx:continue <name>` - Resume artifact creation\n- `/opsx:apply <name>` - Jump to implementation (if tasks exist)\n\nThe work won''t be lost. Come back whenever you''re ready.\n```\n\nExit gracefully without pressure.\n\n### User just wants command reference\n\nIf the user says they just want to see the commands or skip the tutorial:\n\n```\n## OpenSpec Quick Reference\n\n| Command | What it does |\n|---------|--------------|\n| `/opsx:explore` | Think through problems (no code changes) |\n| `/opsx:new <name>` | Start a new change, step by step |\n| `/opsx:ff <name>` | Fast-forward: all artifacts at once |\n| `/opsx:continue <name>` | Continue an existing change |\n| `/opsx:apply <name>` | Implement tasks |\n| `/opsx:verify <name>` | Verify implementation |\n| `/opsx:archive <name>` | Archive when done |\n\nTry `/opsx:new` to start your first change, or `/opsx:ff` if you want to move fast.\n```\n\nExit gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## Guardrails\n\n- **Follow the EXPLAIN → DO → SHOW → PAUSE pattern** at key transitions (after explore, after proposal draft, after tasks, after archive)\n- **Keep narration light** during implementation—teach without lecturing\n- **Don''t skip phases** even if the change is small—the goal is teaching the workflow\n- **Pause for acknowledgment** at marked points, but don''t over-pause\n- **Handle exits gracefully**—never pressure the user to continue\n- **Use real codebase tasks**—don''t simulate or use fake examples\n- **Adjust scope gently**—guide toward smaller tasks but respect user choice\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:45:29.820Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Development Agents needing guided OpenSpec workflow integration.","zh":"非常适合需要指导的 OpenSpec 工作流集成的开发代理。","ja":"OpenSpec ワークフロー統合のガイドが必要な開発エージェントに最適です。","ko":"가이드가 필요한 OpenSpec 워크플로 통합을 필요로 하는 개발 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de desarrollo que necesitan integración de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec guiada.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de développement ayant besoin d''une intégration du flux de travail OpenSpec guidée.","de":"Perfekt für Entwicklungsmittel, die eine guidierte OpenSpec-Workflow-Integration benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Desenvolvimento que precisam de integração de fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec orientada.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки, которым требуется интеграция рабочего процесса OpenSpec с руководством.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التطوير الذين يحتاجون إلى دمج تدفق عمل OpenSpec الموجه."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to navigate the OpenSpec workflow cycle, utilizing `openspec init` and `openspec status` commands for seamless project setup and initialization, while explaining each step in a teaching experience.","zh":"赋予代理导航 OpenSpec 工作流周期的能力，利用 `openspec init` 和 `openspec status` 命令实现无缝的项目设置和初始化，同时以教学经验的形式解释每一步。","ja":"エージェントに OpenSpec ワークフローサイクルをナビゲートする能力を付与し、`openspec init` と `openspec status` コマンドを使用してプロジェクトの設定と初期化をシームレスに行い、同時に各ステップを教える体験を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클을 탐색할 수 있도록 해주고, `openspec init` 및 `openspec status` 명령을 사용하여 프로젝트 설정 및 초기화를无缝하게 수행하며, 각 단계를教学 경험의 형식으로 설명합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a navegar por el ciclo de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec, utilizando los comandos `openspec init` y `openspec status` para una configuración y inicialización de proyecto sin problemas, mientras explica cada paso en una experiencia de enseñanza.","fr":"Permet aux agents de naviguer dans le cycle de flux de travail OpenSpec, en utilisant les commandes `openspec init` et `openspec status` pour une configuration et une initialisation de projet sans problème, tout en expliquant chaque étape dans une expérience d''enseignement.","de":"Ermächtigt Mittel, den OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklus zu durchlaufen, indem die Befehle `openspec init` und `openspec status` für eine reibungslose Projektsetup und -initialisierung verwendet werden, während jeder Schritt in einer Lehrerfahrung erklärt wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a navegar pelo ciclo de trabalho OpenSpec, utilizando os comandos `openspec init` e `openspec status` para configuração e inicialização de projeto sem problemas, ao explicar cada etapa em uma experiência de ensino.","ru":"Позволяет агентам ориентироваться в цикле рабочего процесса OpenSpec, используя команды `openspec init` и `openspec status` для бесшовной настройки и инициализации проекта, объясняя каждую ступень в обучающем опыте.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على التنقل في دورة عمل OpenSpec، باستخدام أوامر `openspec init` و `openspec status` لإعداد مشروع متكامل وتشغيله، مع شرح كل خطوة في تجربة تعليمية."},"useCases":{"en":["Initializing OpenSpec in new projects","Guiding users through their first complete OpenSpec workflow cycle","Debugging OpenSpec initialization issues with `openspec status --json`"],"zh":["在新项目中初始化 OpenSpec","引导用户完成第一个完整的 OpenSpec 工作流周期","使用 `openspec status --json` 调试 OpenSpec 初始化问题"],"ja":["新しいプロジェクトで OpenSpec を初期化する","ユーザーを最初の完全な OpenSpec ワークフローサイクルに導く","`openspec status --json` を使用して OpenSpec 初期化の問題をデバッグする"],"ko":["새로운 프로젝트에서 OpenSpec 초기화","사용자를 처음으로 완전한 OpenSpec 워크플로 사이클로 안내","`openspec status --json` 사용하여 OpenSpec 초기화 문제 디버깅"],"es":["Inicialización de OpenSpec en nuevos proyectos","Guía a los usuarios a través de su primer ciclo de flujo de trabajo OpenSpec completo","Depuración de problemas de inicialización de OpenSpec con `openspec status --json`"],"fr":["Initialisation d''OpenSpec dans de nouveaux projets","Guide les utilisateurs à travers leur premier cycle de flux de travail OpenSpec complet","Débogage des problèmes d''initialisation d''OpenSpec avec `openspec status --json`"],"de":["Initialisierung von OpenSpec in neuen Projekten","Benutzer durch ihren ersten vollständigen OpenSpec-Workflow-Zyklus führen","Fehlerbehebung bei OpenSpec-Initialisierungsproblemen mit `openspec status --json`"],"pt":["Inicializando OpenSpec em novos projetos","Orientando os usuários por meio do seu primeiro ciclo de trabalho OpenSpec completo","Depurando problemas de inicialização OpenSpec com `openspec status --json`"],"ru":["Инициализация OpenSpec в новых проектах","Проведение пользователей через их первый полный цикл рабочего процесса OpenSpec","Отладка проблем инициализации OpenSpec с помощью `openspec status --json`"],"ar":["تشغيل OpenSpec في مشاريع جديدة","توجيه المستخدمين خلال دورة عمل OpenSpec الكاملة الأولى","تصحيح أخطاء بدء تشغيل OpenSpec باستخدام `openspec status --json`"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires OpenSpec installation","Project must be compatible with OpenSpec workflow"],"zh":["需要 OpenSpec 安装","项目必须与 OpenSpec 工作流兼容"],"ja":["OpenSpec のインストールが必要","プロジェクトは OpenSpec ワークフローと互換性がある必要がある"],"ko":["OpenSpec 설치가 필요","프로젝트는 OpenSpec 워크플로와 호환되어야 함"],"es":["Requiere instalación de OpenSpec","El proyecto debe ser compatible con el flujo de trabajo OpenSpec"],"fr":["Nécessite l''installation d''OpenSpec","Le projet doit être compatible avec le flux de travail OpenSpec"],"de":["Benötigt OpenSpec-Installation","Das Projekt muss mit dem OpenSpec-Workflow kompatibel sein"],"pt":["Requer instalação do OpenSpec","O projeto deve ser compatível com o fluxo de trabalho OpenSpec"],"ru":["Требуется установка OpenSpec","Проект должен быть совместим с рабочим процессом OpenSpec"],"ar":["يتطلب تثبيت OpenSpec","يجب أن يكون المشروع متوافقًا مع تدفق عمل OpenSpec"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('jandragsbaek/codex-template/create-pr', 'community', 'jandragsbaek', 'codex-template', 'jandragsbaek/codex-template', 'create-pr', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z', '2026-02-18T08:45:25.264Z', NULL, '{"id":"jandragsbaek/codex-template/create-pr","name":"create-pr","description":{"zh":"create-pr技能提供了快速、安全的分支设置和合并请求创建，简化开发流程","ja":"create-prスキルは、高速で安全なブランチ設定とプルリクエスト作成を提供し、開発プロセスを簡素化する","ko":"create-pr 스킬은 빠르고 안전한 분기 설정과 풀 요청 생성을 제공하며 개발 프로세스를 간소화한다","es":"El agente create-pr te permite configurar ramas y solicitar revisiones de forma rápida y segura.","fr":"L''agent create-pr vous permet de configurer des branches et de demander des révisions rapidement et en toute sécurité.","de":"Der Agent create-pr ermöglicht es Ihnen, Branches zu konfigurieren und Überprüfungen schnell und sicher anzufordern.","pt":"A ferramenta create-pr oferece uma configuração rápida e segura de branch, rebase e criação de PR com rótulos e descrição detalhada.","ru":"Инструмент create-pr обеспечивает быструю и безопасную настройку ветки, ребейз и создание PR с метками и подробным описанием.","ar":"أداة create-pr توفر إعداد سريع وآمن للفرع وإعادة الترتيب وإنشاء طلب سحب مع تسميات ووصف مفصل.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"创建PR技能：自动化分支设置和合并请求","ja":"PR作成スキル：自動化ブランチ設定とプルリクエスト","ko":"PR 생성 스킬: 자동화 분기 설정 및 풀 요청","es":"Crear PR: Configuración de ramas y solicitud de revisión","fr":"Créer PR: Configuration de branches et demande de révision","de":"Erstellen von PR: Branch-Konfiguration und Überprüfungsan...","pt":"Crie PR: Configuração Rápida e Segura de Branch","ru":"Создание PR: Быстрая и Безопасная Настройка Ветки","ar":"إنشاء طلب سحب: إعداد سريع وآمن للفرع","en":"create-pr"},"description":{"zh":"create-pr技能提供了快速、安全的分支设置和合并请求创建，简化开发流程","ja":"create-prスキルは、高速で安全なブランチ設定とプルリクエスト作成を提供し、開発プロセスを簡素化する","ko":"create-pr 스킬은 빠르고 안전한 분기 설정과 풀 요청 생성을 제공하며 개발 프로세스를 간소화한다","es":"El agente create-pr te permite configurar ramas y solicitar revisiones de forma rápida y segura.","fr":"L''agent create-pr vous permet de configurer des branches et de demander des révisions rapidement et en toute sécurité.","de":"Der Agent create-pr ermöglicht es Ihnen, Branches zu konfigurieren und Überprüfungen schnell und sicher anzufordern.","pt":"A ferramenta create-pr oferece uma configuração rápida e segura de branch, rebase e criação de PR com rótulos e descrição detalhada.","ru":"Инструмент create-pr обеспечивает быструю и безопасную настройку ветки, ребейз и создание PR с метками и подробным описанием.","ar":"أداة create-pr توفر إعداد سريع وآمن للفرع وإعادة الترتيب وإنشاء طلب سحب مع تسميات ووصف مفصل.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["自动分支设置","安全合并","PR创建","必需标签添加","开发流程简化"],"ja":["自動ブランチ設定","安全な合併","PR作成","必須ラベル追加","開発プロセスの簡素化"],"ko":["자동 분기 설정","안전한 병합","PR 생성","필수 레이블 추가","개발 프로세스 간소화"],"es":["Configuración rápida de ramas","Rebase en origin/main","Solicitud de revisiones con etiquetas requeridas","Descripción detallada de la solicitud de revisión","Verificación del estado del árbol de trabajo","Creación de una nueva rama desde origin/main"],"fr":["Configuration rapide de branches","Rebase sur origin/main","Demande de révision avec étiquettes requises","Description détaillée de la demande de révision","Vérification de l''état de l''arbre de travail","Création d''une nouvelle branche depuis origin/main"],"de":["Schnelle Branch-Konfiguration","Rebase auf origin/main","Anforderung von Überprüfungen mit erforderlichen Labels","Detaillierte Beschreibung der Überprüfungsanfrage","Überprüfung des Arbeitsbaumzustands","Erstellung einer neuen Branch aus origin/main"],"pt":["Configuração rápida de branch","Rebase seguro em origin/main","Criação de PR com rótulos e descrição detalhada","Verificação de árvore de trabalho suja","Criação de nova branch a partir de origin/main"],"ru":["Быстрая настройка ветки","Безопасный ребейз на origin/main","Создание PR с метками и подробным описанием","Проверка грязной рабочей директории","Создание новой ветки из origin/main"],"ar":["إعداد سريع للفرع","إعادة ترتيب آمن على origin/main","إنشاء طلب سحب مع تسميات ووصف مفصل","فحص شجرة العمل المتسخة","إنشاء فرع جديدة من origin/main"]},"keywords":{"zh":["create-pr","自动化分支设置","合并请求","开发效率","git","github"],"ja":["create-pr","自動ブランチ設定","プルリクエスト","開発効率","git","github"],"ko":["create-pr","자동 분기 설정","풀 요청","개발 효율성","git","github"],"es":["create-pr","configuración de ramas","solicitud de revisión","rebase","origin/main","etiquetas requeridas","descripción detallada","árbol de trabajo","nueva rama"],"fr":["create-pr","configuration de branches","demande de révision","rebase","origin/main","étiquettes requises","description détaillée","arbre de travail","nouvelle branche"],"de":["create-pr","Branch-Konfiguration","Überprüfungsanfrage","Rebase","origin/main","erforderliche Labels","detaillierte Beschreibung","Arbeitsbaumzustand","neue Branch"],"pt":["criar pr","configuração de branch","rebase","criação de pr","rótulos de pr","descrição de pr","git","github"],"ru":["создать pr","настройка ветки","ребейз","создание pr","метки pr","описание pr","git","github"],"ar":["إنشاء طلب سحب","إعداد الفرع","إعادة الترتيب","إنشاء طلب سحب","تسميات طلب السحب","وصف طلب السحب","git","github"]}},"owner":"jandragsbaek","repo":"codex-template","repoPath":"jandragsbaek/codex-template","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"create-pr","description":"Create a fresh feature branch from main, rebase on latest main, and open a GitHub PR with a solid summary/testing notes. Use when asked to “start a branch,” “rebase from main,” “open a PR,” or “get a PR going.”","bodyPreview":"# Create PR\n\n## Overview\n\nFast, safe branch setup + rebase on `origin/main`, then open a PR with required labels and a detailed description.\n\n## Workflow Decision Tree\n\n- Working tree dirty? Review `git status/diff` to confirm scope; ask before proceed if unrelated/unexpected.\n- User asked for new branch? Create from `origin/main`.\n- User asked for rebase? Rebase branch onto `origin/main`.\n- PR requested? Create via `gh pr create` and add required label.\n- Skill invoked: you have consent to swit","body":"# Create PR\n\n## Overview\n\nFast, safe branch setup + rebase on `origin/main`, then open a PR with required labels and a detailed description.\n\n## Workflow Decision Tree\n\n- Working tree dirty? Review `git status/diff` to confirm scope; ask before proceed if unrelated/unexpected.\n- User asked for new branch? Create from `origin/main`.\n- User asked for rebase? Rebase branch onto `origin/main`.\n- PR requested? Create via `gh pr create` and add required label.\n- Skill invoked: you have consent to switch branches and must generate a sensible branch name.\n- Check available skills; apply any that match the request.\n\n## Step 1: Preflight\n\n- `git status -sb`\n- `git --no-pager diff --color=never`\n- If dirty: check for unrelated/unexpected changes; ask before proceed.\n- Skill invocation grants branch switch consent.\n- Branch naming: infer from scope + change type. Format: `<type>/<topic>-<short-detail>`, lowercase, hyphens.\n  - Examples: `chore/skills-pr-flow`, `docs/skills-docs-first`, `fix/ci-loop-q-lty`.\n\n## Step 2: Sync main\n\n- `git fetch origin`\n- `git checkout main`\n- `git pull --ff-only`\n\n## Step 3: Create or update branch\n\nNew branch:\n- `git checkout -b <branch> origin/main`\n\nExisting branch:\n- `git checkout <branch>`\n- `git rebase origin/main`\n\n## Step 4: Commit (if changes)\n\nAlways ensure you are on the PR branch before committing.\n\nUse Conventional Commits:\n- `feat:` new behavior\n- `fix:` bug fix\n- `refactor:` refactor only\n- `chore:` tooling/docs/cleanup\n- Prefer `./scripts/committer` for commits.\n\nOne-line summary: imperative, concise. Body (if needed): why + risk/impact.\n\n## Step 5: Push + PR\n\n- `git push -u origin <branch>`\n- If skill invoked: you have permission to open the PR.\n- Read the changes (`git status/diff`, key files) to build a specific PR summary/changes/testing section.\n- Always provide a PR body using `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`.\n  - Prefer: `gh pr create --label <type> --title \"<title>\" --body-file <(printf \"...\")`\n  - If PR already exists or `--fill` is required: `gh pr edit <number> --body \"<body>\"`\n- Use `gh pr view/diff` to inspect the PR state/diff.\n - Consider optional version bump labels (`version:bump-minor|version:bump-major`) based on change impact.\n\nRequired labels:\n- `type/feature`\n- `type/fix`\n- `type/chore`\n- `type/skip-changelog`\n\n## Step 6: CI check\n\n- Loop: `gh run list` → `gh run view <id>` → fix → push → repeat until green (usually 60–90s).\n- If CI returns qlty feedback, address it, then re-run.\n- Run `bin/ci --no-signoff` before pushing; after push, run `bin/ci`.\n\n## PR Body Template (from `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`)\n\n```\n## Summary\n- ...\n\n## Label Checklist\n\n**Required** — pick exactly one `type/` label:\n- [ ] `type/feature` — new functionality\n- [ ] `type/fix` — bug fix or correction\n- [ ] `type/chore` — maintenance, refactor, deps\n- [ ] `type/skip-changelog` — docs/CI, no user impact\n\n**Optional** — version bump (default: patch):\n- [ ] `version:bump-minor` — new feature (1.0 → 1.1)\n- [ ] `version:bump-major` — breaking change (1.0 → 2.0)\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:45:25.264Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Git-based AI Agents needing streamlined pull request creation and branch management.","zh":"非常适合需要简化 Git 拉取请求创建和分支管理的基于 Git 的 AI 代理。","ja":"Git に基づく AI エージェントがストリームライン化されたプルリクエストの作成とブランチ管理を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"Git 기반 AI 에이전트가 간소화된 풀 요청 생성 및 브랜치 관리를 필요로 할 때 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA basados en Git que necesitan una creación de solicitudes de extracción y gestión de ramas optimizadas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''IA basés sur Git nécessitant une création de demande de tirage et une gestion de branche rationalisées.","de":"Perfekt für Git-basierte KI-Agents, die eine optimierte Erstellung von Pull-Requests und eine Verwaltung von Zweigen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA baseados em Git que precisam de criação de solicitações de pull e gerenciamento de branches otimizados.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ на основе Git, требующих оптимизированного создания запросов на включение и управления ветками.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوسائط الذكية القائمة على جيت التي تحتاج إلى إنشاء طلبات السحب وإدارة الفروع بسهولة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate branch setup, rebase onto origin/main, and create PRs with required labels via gh pr create, ensuring a fast and safe development workflow using Git protocols.","zh":"赋予代理自动设置分支、重新基准到 origin/main 并通过 gh pr create 创建带有必需标签的 PR 的能力，确保使用 Git 协议的快速安全开发工作流。","ja":"エージェントにブランチの自動設定、origin/main へのリベース、gh pr create を使用して必須のラベルを付けた PR の作成を行う能力を付与し、Git プロトコルを使用した迅速かつ安全な開発ワークフローを保証します。","ko":"에이전트가 자동으로 브랜치를 설정하고 origin/main으로 리베이스하고 gh pr create를 사용하여 필요한 레이블이 있는 PR을 생성하여 Git 프로토콜을 사용한 빠르고 안전한 개발 워크플로를 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar la configuración de la rama, rebase en origin/main y crear solicitudes de extracción con etiquetas requeridas a través de gh pr create, garantizando un flujo de desarrollo rápido y seguro utilizando protocolos de Git.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser la configuration de la branche, de rebase sur origin/main et de créer des demandes de tirage avec des étiquettes requises via gh pr create, garantissant un flux de développement rapide et sécurisé en utilisant les protocoles Git.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agents, die Einrichtung von Zweigen zu automatisieren, auf origin/main umzubasieren und Pull-Requests mit erforderlichen Labels über gh pr create zu erstellen, wodurch ein schneller und sicherer Entwicklungsworkflow mit Git-Protokollen gewährleistet wird.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar a configuração de branches, rebase para origin/main e criar PRs com rótulos necessários via gh pr create, garantindo um fluxo de trabalho de desenvolvimento rápido e seguro usando protocolos Git.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью автоматизировать настройку веток, ребейзить на origin/main и создавать запросы на включение с необходимыми метками через gh pr create, обеспечивая быстрый и безопасный процесс разработки с использованием протоколов Git.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من توفير إعداد الفروع، وإعادة التوجيه إلى origin/main، وإنشاء طلبات السحب مع التسميات المطلوبة عبر gh pr create، وضمان سير عمل سريع وأمن لتطوير البرمجيات باستخدام بروتوكولات جيت."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating branch creation from origin/main","Rebasing branches for up-to-date code","Generating pull requests with detailed descriptions and required labels"],"zh":["从 origin/main 自动创建分支","为最新代码重新基准分支","生成带有详细描述和必需标签的拉取请求"],"ja":["origin/main から自動的にブランチを作成する","最新のコードのためにブランチをリベースする","詳細な説明と必須のラベルを付けたプルリクエストを生成する"],"ko":["origin/main에서 자동으로 브랜치를 생성하는 것","최신 코드를 위해 브랜치를 리베이스하는 것","세부 설명 및 필요한 레이블이 있는 풀 요청을 생성하는 것"],"es":["Automatizar la creación de ramas desde origin/main","Rebasar ramas para obtener un código actualizado","Generar solicitudes de extracción con descripciones detalladas y etiquetas requeridas"],"fr":["Automatiser la création de branches à partir de origin/main","Réorganiser les branches pour obtenir un code à jour","Générer des demandes de tirage avec des descriptions détaillées et des étiquettes requises"],"de":["Automatisieren der Erstellung von Zweigen von origin/main","Zweige auf den neuesten Stand bringen","Erstellen von Pull-Requests mit detaillierten Beschreibungen und erforderlichen Labels"],"pt":["Automatizar a criação de branches a partir de origin/main","Rebase de branches para código atualizado","Gerar solicitações de pull com descrições detalhadas e rótulos necessários"],"ru":["Автоматизировать создание веток из origin/main","Ребейзить ветки для актуального кода","Генерировать запросы на включение с подробными описаниями и необходимыми метками"],"ar":["توفير إنشاء الفروع من origin/main","إعادة التوجيه للفروع للحصول على كود محدث","إنشاء طلبات السحب مع وصف مفصل والتسميات المطلوبة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Git repository access","Needs gh command-line tool installed","User consent required for branch and PR operations"],"zh":["需要 Git 仓库访问权限","需要安装 gh 命令行工具","需要用户同意进行分支和 PR 操作"],"ja":["Git リポジトリへのアクセスが必要","gh コマンドラインツールのインストールが必要","ブランチと PR 操作のためにユーザーの同意が必要"],"ko":["Git 저장소 액세스가 필요합니다.","gh 명령줄 도구가 설치되어야 합니다.","브랜치 및 PR 작업을 위해 사용자 동의가 필요합니다."],"es":["Requiere acceso al repositorio de Git","Necesita la herramienta de línea de comandos gh instalada","Se requiere el consentimiento del usuario para las operaciones de rama y PR"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au référentiel Git","Nécessite l''outil de ligne de commande gh installé","Le consentement de l''utilisateur est requis pour les opérations de branche et de PR"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf das Git-Repository","Benötigt das installierte gh-Kommandozeilen-Tool","Benutzereinwilligung erforderlich für Zweig- und PR-Vorgänge"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao repositório Git","Necessita da ferramenta de linha de comando gh instalada","Consentimento do usuário necessário para operações de branch e PR"],"ru":["Требует доступа к репозиторию Git","Требует установки командной строки gh","Требуется согласие пользователя для операций с ветками и запросами на включение"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى مستودع جيت","يحتاج إلى تثبيت أداة سطر الأوامر gh","يتطلب موافقة المستخدم على عمليات الفروع وطلبات السحب"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('HosungYou/Diverga/diverga-f1', 'community', 'HosungYou', 'Diverga', 'HosungYou/Diverga', 'diverga-f1', 0, 0, 65, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z', '2026-02-18T08:46:25.290Z', NULL, '{"id":"HosungYou/Diverga/diverga-f1","name":"diverga-f1","description":{"es":"Diverga F1 es un verificador de coherencia lógica que garantiza la consistencia en números, terminología y estadísticas en documentos de investigación.","fr":"Diverga F1 est un vérificateur de cohérence logique qui assure la cohérence dans les numéros, la terminologie et les statistiques dans les documents de recherche.","de":"Diverga F1 ist ein logischer Konsistenzprüfer, der die Konsistenz in Zahlen, Terminologie und Statistiken in Forschungsdokumenten gewährleistet.","pt":"O Diverga F1 é um verificador de consistência lógica que analisa a coerência em documentos de pesquisa, garantindo a precisão e a confiabilidade dos dados.","ru":"Diverga F1 — это проверка логической последовательности, которая анализирует согласованность в исследовательских документах, обеспечивая точность и надежность данных.","ar":"ديفرجا إف 1 هو فحص للاتساق اللوجي الذي يقوم بتحليل الاتساق في مستندات البحث، وضمان دقة وموثوقية البيانات.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"es":"Verificador de Coherencia Lógica Diverga F1","fr":"Vérificateur de Cohérence Logique Diverga F1","de":"Logische Konsistenzprüfer Diverga F1","pt":"Verificador de Consistência Lógica Diverga F1","ru":"Проверка логической последовательности Diverga F1","ar":"فحص الاتساق اللوجي لتقنيه ديفرجا إف 1","en":"diverga-f1"},"description":{"es":"Diverga F1 es un verificador de coherencia lógica que garantiza la consistencia en números, terminología y estadísticas en documentos de investigación.","fr":"Diverga F1 est un vérificateur de cohérence logique qui assure la cohérence dans les numéros, la terminologie et les statistiques dans les documents de reche...","de":"Diverga F1 ist ein logischer Konsistenzprüfer, der die Konsistenz in Zahlen, Terminologie und Statistiken in Forschungsdokumenten gewährleistet.","pt":"O Diverga F1 é um verificador de consistência lógica que analisa a coerência em documentos de pesquisa, garantindo a precisão e a confiabilidade dos dados.","ru":"Diverga F1 — это проверка логической последовательности, которая анализирует согласованность в исследовательских документах, обеспечивая точность и надежност...","ar":"ديفرجا إف 1 هو فحص للاتساق اللوجي الذي يقوم بتحليل الاتساق في مستندات البحث، وضمان دقة وموثوقية البيانات.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"es":["Verificación de coherencia lógica","Análisis de consistencia en números y estadísticas","Comprobación de terminología y referencias","Aplicación de la metodología VS para un análisis profundo","Compatibilidad con Codex CLI en modo degradado"],"fr":["Vérification de la cohérence logique","Analyse de la cohérence dans les numéros et les statistiques","Vérification de la terminologie et des références","Application de la méthodologie VS pour une analyse approfondie","Compatibilité avec Codex CLI en mode dégradé"],"de":["Überprüfung der logischen Konsistenz","Analyse der Konsistenz in Zahlen und Statistiken","Überprüfung der Terminologie und Referenzen","Anwendung der VS-Methode für eine tiefe Analyse","Kompatibilität mit Codex CLI im abgesunkenen Modus"],"pt":["Verificação de consistência lógica em documentos de pesquisa","Análise de coerência profunda com metodologia VS","Verificação de números, terminologia e referências","Relatórios estatísticos precisos","Execução em modo degradado do Codex CLI","Utiliza o modelo gpt-5.1-codex-mini"],"ru":["Проверка логической последовательности в исследовательских документах","Глубокий анализ согласованности с помощью методологии VS","Проверка чисел, терминологии и ссылок","Точные статистические отчеты","Выполнение в режиме снижения Codex CLI","Использует модель gpt-5.1-codex-mini"],"ar":["فحص الاتساق اللوجي في مستندات البحث","تحليل الاتساق العميق باستخدام منهجية VS","فحص الأرقام والمصطلحات والمراجع","تقارير إحصائية دقيقة","التشغيل في وضع التدهور من Codex CLI","استخدام نموذج gpt-5.1-codex-mini"]},"keywords":{"es":["verificador de coherencia lógica","coherencia en documentos de investigación","análisis de consistencia","terminología y referencias","metodología VS","Codex CLI"],"fr":["vérificateur de cohérence logique","cohérence dans les documents de recherche","analyse de la cohérence","terminologie et références","méthodologie VS","Codex CLI"],"de":["logischer Konsistenzprüfer","Konsistenz in Forschungsdokumenten","Konsistenzanalyse","Terminologie und Referenzen","VS-Methode","Codex CLI"],"pt":["verificação de consistência lógica","análise de coerência","documentos de pesquisa","metodologia VS","Codex CLI","gpt-5.1-codex-mini","desenvolvimento de software","tecnologia de pesquisa"],"ru":["проверка логической последовательности","анализ согласованности","исследовательские документы","методология VS","Codex CLI","gpt-5.1-codex-mini","разработка программного обеспечения","технология исследования"],"ar":["فحص الاتساق اللوجي","تحليل الاتساق","مستندات البحث","منهجية VS","Codex CLI","gpt-5.1-codex-mini","تطوير البرمجيات","تكنولوجيا البحث"]}},"owner":"HosungYou","repo":"Diverga","repoPath":"HosungYou/Diverga","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"diverga-f1","description":"|","version":"9.0.0","bodyPreview":"# F1-InternalConsistencyChecker\n\n**Agent ID**: F1\n**Category**: F - Quality & Validation\n**Model**: gpt-5.1-codex-mini\n\n## Overview\n\nVerifies logical consistency and coherence throughout research documents. Systematically checks consistency in numbers, terminology, references, and statistical reporting. Applies VS methodology (Light) for deep logical coherence analysis beyond superficial checklists.\n\n## Codex CLI Degraded Mode\nThis agent runs in Codex CLI''s single-model mode. Key differences fro","body":"# F1-InternalConsistencyChecker\n\n**Agent ID**: F1\n**Category**: F - Quality & Validation\n**Model**: gpt-5.1-codex-mini\n\n## Overview\n\nVerifies logical consistency and coherence throughout research documents. Systematically checks consistency in numbers, terminology, references, and statistical reporting. Applies VS methodology (Light) for deep logical coherence analysis beyond superficial checklists.\n\n## Codex CLI Degraded Mode\nThis agent runs in Codex CLI''s single-model mode. Key differences from Claude Code:\n- No parallel agent execution - tasks run sequentially\n- No MCP runtime checkpoints - uses text-based checkpoint protocol\n- No AskUserQuestion UI - uses text prompts for decisions\n\n## Checkpoint Protocol\nNo prerequisites required. No checkpoints during execution.\n\nWhen reaching a checkpoint:\n1. STOP and clearly mark: \"CHECKPOINT: {checkpoint_name}\"\n2. Present options with VS T-Scores where applicable\n3. Ask: \"Which direction would you like to proceed? (A/B/C)\"\n4. WAIT for user response before continuing\n5. Log decision: write_file(\".research/decision-log.yaml\") to record\n\n## Prerequisites\nNone required. This is a standalone quality check agent.\n\n## Core Capabilities\n\n### 1. Logic Flow Verification\n- RQ -> Hypothesis -> Method -> Results -> Conclusion connection\n- Cross-section consistency checks\n- Claims-to-evidence alignment\n\n### 2. Numerical Consistency\n- Number matching across tables/figures/text\n- Sum/percentage verification\n- Statistical recalculation checks\n\n### 3. Terminology Consistency\n- Same term for same concept verification\n- Abbreviation definition and usage tracking\n- Variable name consistency across sections\n\n### 4. Reference Accuracy\n- Citation-bibliography cross-matching\n- Table/figure number reference verification\n- Section/page reference accuracy\n\n### 5. Statistical Reporting\n- APA format compliance checking\n- Degrees of freedom, statistics, p-values verification\n- Effect size reporting completeness\n\n### VS Modal Awareness (Light)\n\n| Area | Modal Approach (T>0.8) | Deep Approach (T<0.5) |\n|------|------------------------|----------------------|\n| Numbers | \"Check table/text N match\" | Statistical recalculation verification |\n| Terminology | \"Check same term used\" | Conceptual consistency (definition vs. operationalization) |\n| Logic | \"Check section connections\" | Hypothesis-results-conclusion triangulation |\n| References | \"Match citation-bibliography\" | Citation context appropriateness review |\n\n## Output Format\n\nProduces an Internal Consistency Check Report with:\n- Logic flow verification matrix (RQ -> H -> Method -> Results)\n- Numerical consistency table with match status\n- Terminology consistency findings\n- Reference accuracy cross-check\n- Statistical reporting format compliance\n- Overall consistency score (/100) with priority revision list\n\n## Tool Mapping (Codex)\n| Claude Code | Codex CLI |\n|-------------|-----------|\n| Read | read_file |\n| Edit | apply_diff |\n| Write | write_file |\n| Grep | grep |\n| Bash | shell |\n| Task (subagent) | Read skill file, follow instructions |\n\n## Related Agents\n- **F2-ChecklistManager**: Guideline-based checking\n- **A3-DevilsAdvocate**: Identifying logical weaknesses\n- **G3-PeerReviewStrategist**: Reviewer response preparation\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:46:25.290Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Research Agents needing advanced logical consistency verification and validation in documents.","zh":"非常适合需要在文档中进行高级逻辑一致性验证和验证的研究代理。","ja":"研究エージェントが文書で高度な論理的一貫性の検証と検証を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"문서에서 고급 논리적 일관성을 검증하고 검사해야 하는 연구 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de investigación que necesitan una verificación y validación de coherencia lógica avanzada en documentos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de recherche nécessitant une vérification et une validation de cohérence logique avancée dans les documents.","de":"Perfekt für Forschungsagenten, die eine erweiterte logische Konsistenzprüfung und -validierung in Dokumenten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Pesquisa que necessitam de verificação e validação de consistência lógica avançada em documentos.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов-исследователей, которым необходима проверка и верификация продвинутой логической последовательности в документах.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء البحثيين الذين يحتاجون إلى التحقق والتحقق من الصحة للموثوقية المنطقية المتقدمة في المستندات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to systematically check consistency in numbers, terminology, references, and statistical reporting using the VS methodology for deep logical coherence analysis, applying gpt-5.1-codex-mini model capabilities.","zh":"赋予代理人使用VS方法论进行深入的逻辑一致性分析的能力，应用gpt-5.1-codex-mini模型能力，以系统地检查数字、术语、引用和统计报告的一致性。","ja":"VSメソドロジーを使用した深い論理的一貫性分析を適用するGPT-5.1-Codex-Miniモデル機能を使用して、数字、用語、参照、統計報告の一貫性を体系的にチェックするエージェントの能力を与えます。","ko":"VS 방법론을 사용하여 깊은 논리적 일관성 분석을 적용하는 GPT-5.1-Codex-Mini 모델 기능을 사용하여 숫자, 용어, 참조 및 통계 보고서의 일관성을 체계적으로 확인하는 에이전트의 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a verificar sistemáticamente la coherencia en números, terminología, referencias y reportes estadísticos utilizando la metodología VS para un análisis profundo de coherencia lógica, aplicando las capacidades del modelo gpt-5.1-codex-mini.","fr":"Permet aux agents de vérifier systématiquement la cohérence dans les chiffres, la terminologie, les références et les rapports statistiques en utilisant la méthodologie VS pour une analyse approfondie de la cohérence logique, en appliquant les capacités du modèle gpt-5.1-codex-mini.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Konsistenz in Zahlen, Terminologie, Referenzen und statistischer Berichterstattung systematisch zu überprüfen, indem die VS-Methode für eine tiefe logische Kohärenzanalyse verwendet wird, wobei die Fähigkeiten des gpt-5.1-codex-mini-Modells angewendet werden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a verificar sistematicamente a consistência em números, terminologia, referências e relatórios estatísticos usando a metodologia VS para análise profunda de coerência lógica, aplicando as capacidades do modelo gpt-5.1-codex-mini.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью систематически проверять последовательность в числах, терминологии, ссылках и статистических отчетах, используя методологию VS для глубокого анализа логической последовательности, применяя возможности модели gpt-5.1-codex-mini.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على التحقق المنهجي من الاتساق في الأرقام والمصطلحات والمراجع والتقرير الإحصائي باستخدام منهجية VS لتحليل الاتساق المنطقي العميق، bằng cách تطبيق إمكانيات نموذج gpt-5.1-codex-mini."},"useCases":{"en":["Verifying internal consistency in research papers","Validating statistical reporting accuracy","Checking terminology consistency across documents"],"zh":["验证研究论文中的内部一致性","验证统计报告的准确性","检查文档中的术语一致性"],"ja":["研究論文内の内部的一貫性を検証する","統計報告の精度を検証する","文書間の用語的一貫性をチェックする"],"ko":["연구 논문의 내부 일관성을 확인하는 것","통계 보고서의 정확성을 확인하는 것","문서 간의 용어 일관성을 확인하는 것"],"es":["Verificar la coherencia interna en artículos de investigación","Validar la precisión de los informes estadísticos","Comprobar la coherencia de la terminología en varios documentos"],"fr":["Vérifier la cohérence interne dans les articles de recherche","Valider la précision des rapports statistiques","Vérifier la cohérence de la terminologie dans plusieurs documents"],"de":["Überprüfung der internen Konsistenz in Forschungsartikeln","Validierung der Genauigkeit der statistischen Berichte","Überprüfung der Konsistenz der Terminologie in verschiedenen Dokumenten"],"pt":["Verificar a consistência interna em artigos de pesquisa","Verificar a precisão do relatório estatístico","Verificar a consistência da terminologia em todo o documento"],"ru":["Проверка внутренней последовательности в исследовательских статьях","Проверка точности статистического отчета","Проверка последовательности терминологии во всех документах"],"ar":["التحقق من الاتساق الداخلي في أوراق البحث","التحقق من دقة التقرير الإحصائي","التحقق من اتساق المصطلحات في جميع المستندات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Runs in Codex CLI''s single-model mode","Specifically designed for research documents"],"zh":["仅在Codex CLI的单模型模式下运行","专门为研究文档设计"],"ja":["Codex CLIのシングルモデルモードでのみ実行","研究文書専用に設計"],"ko":["Codex CLI의 단일 모델 모드에서만 실행","연구 문서 전용으로 설계됨"],"es":["Se ejecuta en el modo de un solo modelo de Codex CLI","Diseñado específicamente para documentos de investigación"],"fr":["Fonctionne en mode modèle unique de Codex CLI","Conçu spécifiquement pour les documents de recherche"],"de":["Funktioniert im Ein-Modus-Modus von Codex CLI","Speziell für Forschungsdokumente konzipiert"],"pt":["Executa no modo de modelo único do Codex CLI","Especificamente projetado para documentos de pesquisa"],"ru":["Выполняется в режиме одного модели в Codex CLI","Специально разработан для исследовательских документов"],"ar":["يعمل في وضع نموذج واحد في Codex CLI","تم تصميمه خصيصًا للوثائق البحثية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('cacr92/WeReply/api-design', 'community', 'cacr92', 'WeReply', 'cacr92/WeReply', 'api-design', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z', '2026-02-18T08:45:58.026Z', NULL, '{"id":"cacr92/WeReply/api-design","name":"api-design","description":{"zh":"本文介绍了 API 设计的最佳实践，包括关键规则、DTO 规范和标准响应","ja":"この記事では、API デザインのベストプラクティスについて説明します。重要なルール、DTO 規範、標準的なレスポンスなど","ko":"이 문서는 API 디자인의 가이드를 제공합니다. 핵심 규칙, DTO 규격, 표준 응답 등","es":"El diseño de API es fundamental para desarrolladores. Aprende a crear APIs escalables y eficientes con nuestras recomendaciones","fr":"La conception d''API est essentielle pour les développeurs. Découvrez comment créer des API évolutives et efficaces avec nos recommandations","de":"Das API-Design ist für Entwickler von entscheidender Bedeutung. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie skalierbare und effiziente APIs erstellen können, mit unseren Empfehlungen","pt":"O design de API é fundamental para a criação de interfaces de programação eficazes. Aprenda a projetar APIs com estruturas de resposta e validação de dados.","ru":"Проектирование API является фундаментальным для создания эффективных интерфейсов программирования. Узнайте, как проектировать API с структурами ответов и валидацией данных.","ar":"تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات هو أساسي لإنشاء واجهات برمجة فعالة. تعلم كيفية تصميم واجهات برمجة التطبيقات مع هياكل الاستجابة وتحقق البيانات.","en":"微信聊天自动回复助手"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"API 设计最佳实践","ja":"API デザインのベストプラクティス","ko":"API 디자인 가이드","es":"Diseño de API: Mejores prácticas para desarrolladores","fr":"Conception d''API: Meilleures pratiques pour les développeurs","de":"API-Design: Beste Praktiken für Entwickler","pt":"Desenvolvimento de API: Melhores Práticas de Design","ru":"Проектирование API: Лучшие Практики","ar":"تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات: أفضل الممارسات","en":"api-design"},"description":{"zh":"本文介绍了 API 设计的最佳实践，包括关键规则、DTO 规范和标准响应","ja":"この記事では、API デザインのベストプラクティスについて説明します。重要なルール、DTO 規範、標準的なレスポンスなど","ko":"이 문서는 API 디자인의 가이드를 제공합니다. 핵심 규칙, DTO 규격, 표준 응답 등","es":"El diseño de API es fundamental para desarrolladores. Aprende a crear APIs escalables y eficientes con nuestras recomendaciones","fr":"La conception d''API est essentielle pour les développeurs. Découvrez comment créer des API évolutives et efficaces avec nos recommandations","de":"Das API-Design ist für Entwickler von entscheidender Bedeutung. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie skalierbare und effiziente APIs erstellen können, mit unseren Empfehlungen","pt":"O design de API é fundamental para a criação de interfaces de programação eficazes. Aprenda a projetar APIs com estruturas de resposta e validação de dados.","ru":"Проектирование API является фундаментальным для создания эффективных интерфейсов программирования. Узнайте, как проектировать API с структурами ответов и вал...","ar":"تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات هو أساسي لإنشاء واجهات برمجة فعالة. تعلم كيفية تصميم واجهات برمجة التطبيقات مع هياكل الاستجابة وتحقق البيانات.","en":"微信聊天自动回复助手"},"definition":{"en":"微信聊天自动回复助手"},"features":{"zh":["统一命名和校验策略","DTO 规范和响应结构","标准响应和错误处理","使用 Serde 和 Specta::Type","命令边界的校验和业务层返回"],"ja":["統一命名と検証戦略","DTO 規範とレスポンス構造","標準的なレスポンスとエラーハンドリング","Serde と Specta::Type の使用","コマンド境界の検証とビジネス層の返却"],"ko":["통일 명명과 검증 전략","DTO 규격과 응답 구조","표준 응답과 오류 처리","Serde와 Specta::Type의 사용","명령 경계의 검증과 비즈니스 계층의 반환"],"es":["Diseño de API RESTful","Uso de DTO y respuestas estructuradas","Validación de datos en el límite de la API","Manejo de errores y excepciones","Uso de serialización y deserialización de datos"],"fr":["Conception d''API RESTful","Utilisation de DTO et de réponses structurées","Validation des données à la limite de l''API","Gestion des erreurs et des exceptions","Utilisation de la sérialisation et de la désérialisation de données"],"de":["Entwurf von RESTful-APIs","Verwendung von DTO und strukturierten Antworten","Validierung von Daten an der API-Grenze","Behandlung von Fehlern und Ausnahmen","Verwendung von Serialisierung und Deserialisierung von Daten"],"pt":["Estruturas de resposta unificadas","Validação de dados em tempo de execução","Uso de serde e specta::Type para DTO","Respostas personalizadas com ApiResponse","Documentação de API clara e concisa"],"ru":["Унифицированные структуры ответов","Валидация данных в runtime","Использование serde и specta::Type для DTO","Пользовательские ответы с ApiResponse","Ясная и краткая документация API"],"ar":["هياكل استجابة موحدة","تحقق البيانات في وقت التشغيل","استخدام serde و specta::Type ل DTO","استجابات مخصصة مع ApiResponse","توثيق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات واضح وموجز"]},"keywords":{"zh":["API 设计","DTO 规范","标准响应","错误处理","Serde","Specta::Type","命令边界","业务层返回"],"ja":["API デザイン","DTO 規範","標準的なレスポンス","エラーハンドリング","Serde","Specta::Type","コマンド境界","ビジネス層の返却"],"ko":["API 디자인","DTO 규격","표준 응답","오류 처리","Serde","Specta::Type","명령 경계","비즈니스 계층의 반환"],"es":["diseño de API","API RESTful","DTO","respuestas estructuradas","validación de datos","manejo de errores","serialización de datos","desarrollo de API"],"fr":["conception d''API","API RESTful","DTO","réponses structurées","validation des données","gestion des erreurs","sérialisation de données","développement d''API"],"de":["API-Design","RESTful-API","DTO","strukturierte Antworten","Validierung von Daten","Behandlung von Fehlern","Serialisierung von Daten","API-Entwicklung"],"pt":["design de api","desenvolvimento de api","estruturas de resposta","validação de dados","serde","specta::Type","ApiResponse","documentação de api"],"ru":["проектирование api","разработка api","структуры ответов","валидация данных","serde","specta::Type","ApiResponse","документация api"],"ar":["تصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","تطوير واجهة برمجة التطبيقات","هياكل الاستجابة","تحقق البيانات","serde","specta::Type","ApiResponse","توثيق واجهة برمجة التطبيقات"]}},"owner":"cacr92","repo":"WeReply","repoPath":"cacr92/WeReply","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"api-design","description":"当用户要求API/接口/DTO设计、请求响应结构、分页、命名规范或校验规则时使用。","bodyPreview":"# API Design Skill\n\n## 适用范围\n- 设计或调整 Tauri 命令接口\n- 设计 DTO/响应结构\n- 统一命名与校验策略\n\n## 关键规则（Critical Rules）\n- 外层响应统一 `ApiResponse<T>`\n- DTO 使用 `serde` + `specta::Type`，字段 camelCase 与前端一致\n- 校验在命令边界完成，业务层返回 `anyhow::Result` 并补充上下文\n- 错误信息面向用户，简洁明确\n\n## 标准响应\n```rust\n#[derive(serde::Serialize, specta::Type)]\n#[specta(inline)]\npub struct ApiResponse<T: specta::Type> {\n    pub success: bool,\n    pub data: Option<T>,\n    pub error: Option<String>,\n}\n```\n\n## DTO 规范（示例）\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Dese","body":"# API Design Skill\n\n## 适用范围\n- 设计或调整 Tauri 命令接口\n- 设计 DTO/响应结构\n- 统一命名与校验策略\n\n## 关键规则（Critical Rules）\n- 外层响应统一 `ApiResponse<T>`\n- DTO 使用 `serde` + `specta::Type`，字段 camelCase 与前端一致\n- 校验在命令边界完成，业务层返回 `anyhow::Result` 并补充上下文\n- 错误信息面向用户，简洁明确\n\n## 标准响应\n```rust\n#[derive(serde::Serialize, specta::Type)]\n#[specta(inline)]\npub struct ApiResponse<T: specta::Type> {\n    pub success: bool,\n    pub data: Option<T>,\n    pub error: Option<String>,\n}\n```\n\n## DTO 规范（示例）\n```rust\n#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, specta::Type)]\n#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\npub struct CreateFactoryDto {\n    pub factory_code: Code,\n    pub factory_name: Name,\n    pub description: Description,\n    pub address: Option<String>,\n    pub contact: Option<String>,\n    pub phone: Option<String>,\n    pub is_active: Boolean,\n}\n```\n\n## 命名与契约\n- 命令：动词 + 名词（`get`/`create`/`update`/`delete`）\n- DTO：`CreateXDto` / `UpdateXDto` / `XDto`\n- 前后端字段统一 camelCase，Rust 侧使用 `#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]`\n\n## 分页与列表\n- 优先复用现有类型：`crate::material::material_service::MaterialsPage` / `MaterialsPaginatedResult`\n- 返回列表时保持字段可直接渲染，避免二次拼装\n\n## 校验建议\n- 对 `String` 长度、`Option` 必填进行检查\n- SQLx 之前完成基本校验，避免 DB 错误直接暴露\n\n## 检查清单\n- [ ] 响应使用 `ApiResponse<T>`\n- [ ] DTO 实现 `specta::Type` 且字段 camelCase\n- [ ] 校验在命令边界完成\n- [ ] 命名与既有命令风格一致\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:45:58.026Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for API-centric Agents needing standardized API design and response handling using Rust, serde, and specta","zh":"非常适合需要标准化API设计和使用Rust、serde和specta进行响应处理的API中心代理","ja":"Rust、serde、spectaを使用した標準化されたAPI設計とレスポンスハンドリングが必要なAPI中心のエージェントに最適","ko":"Rust, serde, specta를 사용하여 표준화된 API 설계 및 응답 처리가 필요한 API 중심 에이전트에 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes centrados en API que necesitan un diseño de API estandarizado y un manejo de respuestas utilizando Rust, serde y specta","fr":"Parfait pour les agents centrés sur l''API nécessitant une conception d''API standardisée et un traitement de réponses utilisant Rust, serde et specta","de":"Perfekt für API-zentrierte Agenten, die ein standardisiertes API-Design und eine Response-Verarbeitung mit Rust, serde und specta benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes centrados em API que necessitam de design de API padronizado e tratamento de respostas usando Rust, serde e specta","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, ориентированных на API, которым необходим стандартизированный дизайн API и обработка ответов с использованием Rust, serde и specta","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء المركزين على واجهات برمجة التطبيقات التي تحتاج إلى تصميم واجهة برمجة تطبيقات معيارية ومعالجة استجابة باستخدام Rust و serde و specta"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design unified APIs with standardized response structures like ApiResponse<T>, utilizing serde for serialization and specta for type definitions, ensuring consistency in naming conventions and validation strategies","zh":"赋予代理设计统一的API，具有标准化的响应结构，如ApiResponse<T>，利用serde进行序列化和specta进行类型定义，确保命名约定和验证策略的一致性","ja":"エージェントが統一されたAPIを設計できるようにし、ApiResponse<T>などの標準化されたレスポンス構造を使用し、serdeを使用したシリアル化とspectaを使用した型定義を行い、命名規則とバリデーション戦略の一貫性を確保する","ko":"에이전트가 통일된 API를 설계할 수 있도록 하며, ApiResponse<T>와 같은 표준화된 응답 구조를 사용하고, serde를 사용한 시리얼라이제이션 및 specta를 사용한 타입 정의를 통해 명명 규칙 및 유효성 검사 전략의 일관성을 보장","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar APIs unificadas con estructuras de respuestas estandarizadas como ApiResponse<T>, utilizando serde para la serialización y specta para las definiciones de tipos, garantizando la consistencia en las convenciones de nomenclatura y las estrategias de validación","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir des API unifiées avec des structures de réponses standardisées comme ApiResponse<T>, en utilisant serde pour la sérialisation et specta pour les définitions de types, en garantissant la cohérence dans les conventions de nommage et les stratégies de validation","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, einheitliche APIs mit standardisierten Response-Strukturen wie ApiResponse<T> zu entwerfen, indem serde für die Serialisierung und specta für die Typdefinitionen verwendet werden, um die Konsistenz in den Namenskonventionen und Validierungsstrategien sicherzustellen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetar APIs unificadas com estruturas de respostas padronizadas como ApiResponse<T>, utilizando serde para serialização e specta para definições de tipo, garantindo consistência em convenções de nomenclatura e estratégias de validação","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать унифицированные API с стандартизированными структурами ответов, такими как ApiResponse<T>, используя serde для сериализации и specta для определений типов, обеспечивая согласованность в именах и стратегиях валидации","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تصميم واجهات برمجة تطبيقات موحدة مع هياكل استجابة معيارية مثل ApiResponse<T>، باستخدام serde للترميز و specta لتعريفات النوع، مما يضمن الاتساق في اتفاقيات التسمية و στρατηγίες التحقق"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing Tauri command interfaces","Creating DTOs with serde and specta","Implementing unified error handling and response structures"],"zh":["设计Tauri命令接口","使用serde和specta创建DTO","实现统一的错误处理和响应结构"],"ja":["Tauriコマンドインターフェイスの設計","serdeとspectaを使用したDTOの作成","統一されたエラーハンドリングとレスポンス構造の実装"],"ko":["Tauri 명령 인터페이스 설계","serde와 specta를 사용한 DTO 생성","統一된 오류 처리 및 응답 구조 구현"],"es":["Diseñar interfaces de comando Tauri","Crear DTO con serde y specta","Implementar un manejo de errores y estructuras de respuestas unificadas"],"fr":["Concevoir des interfaces de commande Tauri","Créer des DTO avec serde et specta","Mettre en œuvre un traitement d''erreurs et des structures de réponses unifiées"],"de":["Entwerfen von Tauri-Befehlschnittstellen","Erstellen von DTOs mit serde und specta","Implementieren eines einheitlichen Fehler- und Response-Handlings"],"pt":["Projeto de interfaces de comando Tauri","Criação de DTOs com serde e specta","Implementação de tratamento de erros unificado e estruturas de respostas"],"ru":["Проектирование интерфейсов команд Tauri","Создание DTO с помощью serde и specta","Реализация унифицированного обработки ошибок и структур ответов"],"ar":["تصميم واجهات أوامر Tauri","إنشاء DTOs باستخدام serde و specta","تنفيذ معالجة أخطاء موحدة وهياكل استجابة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Rust programming language","Dependent on serde and specta libraries","Specific to API design and may not be directly applicable to other areas of development"],"zh":["需要Rust编程语言","依赖于serde和specta库","仅特定于API设计，可能不直接适用于开发的其他领域"],"ja":["Rustプログラミング言語が必要","serdeとspectaライブラリに依存している","API設計に特化しており、開発の他の分野には直接適用できない可能性がある"],"ko":["Rust 프로그래밍 언어가 필요","serde와 specta 라이브러리에 의존","API 설계에 특화되어 있으며, 개발의 다른 분야에 직접적용할 수 없을 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere el lenguaje de programación Rust","Dependiente de las bibliotecas serde y specta","Específico para el diseño de API y puede que no sea directamente aplicable a otras áreas de desarrollo"],"fr":["Nécessite le langage de programmation Rust","Dépendant des bibliothèques serde et specta","Spécifique à la conception d''API et peut ne pas être directement applicable à d''autres domaines de développement"],"de":["Erfordert die Programmiersprache Rust","Abhängig von den Bibliotheken serde und specta","Spezifisch für die API-Entwicklung und kann möglicherweise nicht direkt auf andere Entwicklungsbereiche angewendet werden"],"pt":["Exige linguagem de programação Rust","Dependente das bibliotecas serde e specta","Específico para design de API e pode não ser diretamente aplicável a outras áreas de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Требует языка программирования Rust","Зависит от библиотек serde и specta","Относится к дизайну API и может не быть напрямую применим к другим областям разработки"],"ar":["يتطلب لغة برمجة Rust","يعتمد على مكتبات serde و specta","محدد لتصميم واجهة برمجة التطبيقات و قد لا يكون قابلا للتطبيق مباشرة على مجالات أخرى من التطوير"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Mrgig7/Multi-Agent-Enterprise-CRM/backend-go', 'community', 'Mrgig7', 'Multi-Agent-Enterprise-CRM', 'Mrgig7/Multi-Agent-Enterprise-CRM', 'backend-go', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z', '2026-02-18T08:45:35.787Z', NULL, '{"id":"Mrgig7/Multi-Agent-Enterprise-CRM/backend-go","name":"backend-go","description":{"zh":"Go后端开发技能，用于构建高性能、可扩展的CRM系统，具有事件驱动架构和人工智能治理","ja":"Goバックエンド開発スキルを使用して、高性能でスケーラブルなCRMシステムを構築し、イベントドリブンアーキテクチャと人工知能ガバナンスを実現","ko":"Go 백엔드 개발 스킬을 사용하여 고성능, 확장 가능한 CRM 시스템을 구축하고, 이벤트驱동 아키텍처와 인공지능 거버넌스를 구현","es":"El desarrollo de backend con Go implica el uso de contextos de propagación, piscinas de trabajadores y apagado elegante para crear aplicaciones escalables y seguras","fr":"Le développement backend avec Go implique l''utilisation de contextes de propagation, de piscines de travailleurs et d''arrêt élégant pour créer des applications évolutives et sécurisées","de":"Die Backend-Entwicklung mit Go beinhaltet die Verwendung von Kontextweitergabe, Arbeitspool und eleganter Herunterfahren, um skalierbare und sichere Anwendungen zu erstellen","pt":"O backend-go é uma habilidade que permite criar soluções de backend em Go, com recursos como context propagation e worker pools.","ru":"Бэкенд на Go - это навык, который позволяет создавать решения бэкенда на Go с функциями контекстной пропагации и пулами рабочих.","ar":"الخلفية Go هي مهارة تتيح إنشاء حلول خلفية باستخدام Go، مع ميزات مثل انتشار السياق وبرك العمال.","en":"🤖 AI-Native Enterprise CRM with autonomous agents for sales, support, and compliance. Built with LangGraph, Kafka, Next.js, and Ollama. Features event-driven architecture, multi-tenant security, and human-in-the-loop AI governance."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Go后端开发：高性能CRM解决方案","ja":"Goバックエンド開発：高性能CRMソリューション","ko":"Go 백엔드 개발: 고성능 CRM 솔루션","es":"Desarrollo de Backend con Go: Características y F