ng structured workflow planning and module sequencing.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化工作流规划和模块顺序的AI代理。","ja":"構造化されたワークフロー計画とモジュールシーケンシングが必要なAIエージェントに最適です。","ko":"구조화된 워크플ロー 계획 및 모듈 시퀀싱이 필요한 AI 에이전트에게 완벽합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que necesitan una planificación de flujo de trabajo estructurada y secuenciación de módulos.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA ayant besoin d''une planification de flux de travail structurée et d''une séquenciation de modules.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die eine strukturierte Workflow-Planung und Modul-Sequenzierung benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para agentes de IA que necessitam de planejamento de fluxo de trabalho estruturado e sequenciamento de módulos.","ru":"Идеально для ИИ-агентов, которым требуется структурированное планирование рабочего процесса и последовательное управление модулями.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي التي تحتاج إلى تخطيط تدفق عمل منظم وتسلسل وحدة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to identify module boundaries, provide low-risk step plans, and call out dependencies using workflow sequencing and dependency management protocols.","zh":"赋予代理识别模块边界、提供低风险步骤计划并使用工作流序列和依赖管理协议调用依赖项的能力。","ja":"エージェントにモジュールの境界を特定し、低リスクのステッププランを提供し、ワークフローシーケンシングと依存関係管理プロトコルを使用して依存関係を呼び出す機能を提供します。","ko":"에이전트가 모듈 경계를 식별하고 저위험 단계 계획을 제공하며 워크플ロー 시퀀싱 및 종속성 관리 프로토콜을 사용하여 종속성을 호출할 수 있는 능력을 부여합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a identificar límites de módulos, proporcionar planes de pasos de bajo riesgo y señalarizar dependencias utilizando protocolos de secuenciación y gestión de dependencias de flujo de trabajo.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''identifier les limites des modules, de fournir des plans d''étapes à faible risque et de signaler les dépendances en utilisant des protocoles de séquenciation et de gestion des dépendances de flux de travail.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, Modul-Grenzen zu identifizieren, Pläne mit niedrigem Risiko bereitzustellen und Abhängigkeiten mithilfe von Workflow-Sequenzierungs- und Abhängigkeitsmanagement-Protokollen aufzurufen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a identificar limites de módulos, fornecer planos de etapas de baixo risco e chamar dependências usando protocolos de sequenciamento de fluxo de trabalho e gerenciamento de dependências.","ru":"Позволяет агентам определять границы модулей, предоставлять планы шагов с низким риском и указывать зависимости с помощью протоколов последовательного управления рабочим процессом и управления зависимостями.","ar":"يتمكن الوكلاء من تحديد حدود الوحدات وتقديم خطط خطوات منخفضة المخاطر والاستدعاء التبعيات باستخدام بروتوكولات تسلسل تدفق العمل وإدارة التبعيات"},"useCases":{"en":["Modularizing complex AI workflows","Sequencing dependencies for low-risk plans","Identifying module boundaries for efficient workflow execution"],"zh":["复杂AI工作流的模块化","低风险计划的依赖关系序列化","高效工作流执行的模块边界识别"],"ja":["複雑なAIワークフローのモジュール化","低リスクプランの依存関係シーケンシング","効率的なワークフローの実行のモジュール境界の特定"],"ko":["복잡한 AI 워크플로의 모듈화","저위험 계획의 종속성 시퀀싱","효율적인 워크플로 실행의 모듈 경계 식별"],"es":["Modularizar flujos de trabajo de IA complejos","Secuenciar dependencias para planes de bajo riesgo","Identificar límites de módulos para una ejecución eficiente del flujo de trabajo"],"fr":["Modulariser des flux de travail d''IA complexes","Séquencer les dépendances pour des plans à faible risque","Identifier les limites des modules pour une exécution efficace du flux de travail"],"de":["Komplexe KI-Workflows modularisieren","Abhängigkeiten für Pläne mit geringem Risiko sequenzieren","Modul-Grenzen für eine effiziente Workflow-Ausführung identifizieren"],"pt":["Modularizar fluxos de trabalho de IA complexos","Sequenciar dependências para planos de baixo risco","Identificar limites de módulos para execução eficiente de fluxo de trabalho"],"ru":["Модульное упрощение сложных рабочих процессов ИИ","Последовательное определение зависимостей для планов с низким риском","Определение границ модулей для эффективного выполнения рабочего процесса"],"ar":["تجزئة تدفقات عمل ذكية معقدة","تسلسل التبعيات لخطط منخفضة المخاطر","تحديد حدود الوحدات للتشغيل الفعال لتدفق العمل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires clear workflow definition","Dependent on accurate dependency mapping"],"zh":["需要明确的工作流定义","依赖于准确的依赖映射"],"ja":["明確なワークフロー定義が必要","正確な依存関係マッピングに依存する"],"ko":["명확한 워크플ロー 정의가 필요","정확한 종속성 매핑에 의존"],"es":["Requiere una definición clara del flujo de trabajo","Dependiente de un mapeo de dependencias preciso"],"fr":["Nécessite une définition claire du flux de travail","Dépend d''une cartographie précise des dépendances"],"de":["Benötigt eine klare Workflow-Definition","Hängt von einer genauen Abhängigkeitszuordnung ab"],"pt":["Requer definição clara do fluxo de trabalho","Depende de mapeamento de dependências preciso"],"ru":["Требует четкого определения рабочего процесса","Зависит от точного картографирования зависимостей"],"ar":["يتطلب تعريفًا واضحًا لتدفق العمل","يعتمد على تعيين دقيق للتبعيات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":0}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('davidkelley/searchlite/index-lifecycle', 'community', 'davidkelley', 'searchlite', 'davidkelley/searchlite', 'index-lifecycle', 0, 0, 40, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z', '2026-02-18T08:47:32.321Z', NULL, '{"id":"davidkelley/searchlite/index-lifecycle","name":"index-lifecycle","description":{"zh":"Searchlite 是一个嵌入式搜索引擎，提供单一索引目录和清晰的 Rust API","ja":"Searchlite は埋め込み可能な検索エンジンで、シングルインデックスディレクトリとクリーンな Rust API を提供します","ko":"Searchlite는 내장 검색 엔진으로 단일 인덱스 디렉토리와 깨끗한 Rust API를 제공합니다","es":"Searchlite es un motor de búsqueda integrado que gestiona un índice en disco y ofrece una API de Rust, CLI y enlaces opcionales de C/WASM","fr":"Searchlite est un moteur de recherche intégré qui gère un index sur disque et propose une API Rust, CLI et des liens optionnels C/WASM","de":"Searchlite ist ein integrierter Suchmaschinen-Motor, der einen Index auf Disk verwaltet und eine Rust-API, CLI und optionale C/WASM-Verbindungen bietet","pt":"O Searchlite é uma engine de busca embutida que mantém um único índice em disco e oferece uma API limpa em Rust, CLI e ligações opcionais em C/WASM.","ru":"Searchlite — это встроенный поисковый движок, который поддерживает один дисковый индекс и предлагает чистый API на Rust, CLI и необязательные связи на C/WASM.","ar":"Searchlite هو محرك بحث مدمج يحتفظ بفهرس واحد على القرص ويوفر واجهة برمجة تطبيقات نظيفة في Rust وCLI ورابط اختياري في C/WASM.","en":"🔍 Searchlite is an embedded search engine that keeps a single on‑disk index and exposes a clean Rust API, CLI, and optional C/WASM bindings. It offers BM25 with phrase matching, filters/aggregations, stored fields, highlighting, and optional vectors/GPU stubs for fast, schema-driven full‑text se..."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"索引生命周期 - Searchlite 技术概述","ja":"インデックスライフサイクル - Searchlite 技術概要","ko":"인덱스 라이프사이클 - Searchlite 기술 개요","es":"Index Lifecycle: Optimiza tu búsqueda con Searchlite","fr":"Cycle de vie d''index : Optimisez votre recherche avec Sea...","de":"Index-Lebenszyklus: Optimieren Sie Ihre Suche mit Searchlite","pt":"Index Lifecycle: Otimizando Buscas com Searchlite","ru":"Index Lifecycle: Ускорение поиска с Searchlite","ar":"دورة حياة الفهرس: تحسين البحث مع Searchlite","en":"index-lifecycle"},"description":{"zh":"Searchlite 是一个嵌入式搜索引擎，提供单一索引目录和清晰的 Rust API","ja":"Searchlite は埋め込み可能な検索エンジンで、シングルインデックスディレクトリとクリーンな Rust API を提供します","ko":"Searchlite는 내장 검색 엔진으로 단일 인덱스 디렉토리와 깨끗한 Rust API를 제공합니다","es":"Searchlite es un motor de búsqueda integrado que gestiona un índice en disco y ofrece una API de Rust, CLI y enlaces opcionales de C/WASM","fr":"Searchlite est un moteur de recherche intégré qui gère un index sur disque et propose une API Rust, CLI et des liens optionnels C/WASM","de":"Searchlite ist ein integrierter Suchmaschinen-Motor, der einen Index auf Disk verwaltet und eine Rust-API, CLI und optionale C/WASM-Verbindungen bietet","pt":"O Searchlite é uma engine de busca embutida que mantém um único índice em disco e oferece uma API limpa em Rust, CLI e ligações opcionais em C/WASM.","ru":"Searchlite — это встроенный поисковый движок, который поддерживает один дисковый индекс и предлагает чистый API на Rust, CLI и необязательные связи на C/WASM.","ar":"Searchlite هو محرك بحث مدمج يحتفظ بفهرس واحد على القرص ويوفر واجهة برمجة تطبيقات نظيفة في Rust وCLI ورابط اختياري في C/WASM.","en":"🔍 Searchlite is an embedded search engine that keeps a single on‑disk index and exposes a clean Rust API, CLI, and optional C/WASM bindings. It offers BM25 ..."},"definition":{"en":"🔍 Searchlite is an embedded search engine that keeps a single on‑disk index and exposes a clean Rust API, CLI, and optional C/WASM bindings. It offers BM25 with phrase matching, filters/aggregations, stored fields, highlighting, and optional vectors/GPU stubs for fast, schema-driven full‑text search in a small footprint."},"features":{"zh":["单一索引目录","写入缓冲和 WAL 机制","提交和压缩","BM25 和短语匹配","过滤和聚合"],"ja":["シングルインデックスディレクトリ","書き込みバッファリングと WAL メカニズム","コミットと圧縮","BM25 とフレーズマッチング","フィルタリングと集約"],"ko":["단일 인덱스 디렉토리","쓰기 버퍼링 및 WAL 메커니즘","커밋 및 압축","BM25 및 구문 일치","필터링 및 집계"],"es":["BM25 con coincidencia de frases","Filtros y agregaciones","Campos almacenados","Resaltado de resultados","Vectores y aceleración por GPU"],"fr":["BM25 avec correspondance de phrases","Filtres et agrégations","Champs stockés","Mise en évidence des résultats","Vecteurs et accélération par GPU"],"de":["BM25 mit Phrasenübereinstimmung","Filter und Aggregationen","Gespeicherte Felder","Hervorhebung von Ergebnissen","Vektoren und GPU-Beschleunigung"],"pt":["BM25 com correspondência de frases","Filtros e agregações","Campos armazenados","Realce de resultados","Vetores e suporte a GPU"],"ru":["BM25 с фразовой соответствием","Фильтры и агрегации","Хранимые поля","Выделение результатов","Векторы и поддержка GPU"],"ar":["BM25 مع مطابقة الجمل","مرشحات وتجميعات","حقول مخزنة","تأكيد نتائج","متجهات ودعم GPU"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Searchlite","索引生命周期","嵌入式搜索引擎","Rust API","BM25","短语匹配","过滤","聚合"],"ja":["Searchlite","インデックスライフサイクル","埋め込み可能な検索エンジン","Rust API","BM25","フレーズマッチング","フィルタリング","集約"],"ko":["Searchlite","인덱스 라이프사이클","내장 검색 엔진","Rust API","BM25","구문 일치","필터링","집계"],"es":["index lifecycle","Searchlite","búsqueda integrada","BM25","coincidencia de frases","filtros y agregaciones","campos almacenados","resaltado de resultados"],"fr":["cycle de vie d''index","Searchlite","recherche intégrée","BM25","correspondance de phrases","filtres et agrégations","champs stockés","mise en évidence des résultats"],"de":["Index-Lebenszyklus","Searchlite","integrierte Suche","BM25","Phrasenübereinstimmung","Filter und Aggregationen","gespeicherte Felder","Hervorhebung von Ergebnissen"],"pt":["index lifecycle","searchlite","engine de busca embutida","rust","CLI","C/WASM","BM25","filtros","agregações"],"ru":["жизненный цикл индекса","searchlite","встроенный поисковый движок","rust","CLI","C/WASM","BM25","фильтры","агрегации"],"ar":["دورة حياة الفهرس","searchlite","محرك بحث مدمج","rust","CLI","C/WASM","BM25","مرشحات","تجميعات"]}},"owner":"davidkelley","repo":"searchlite","repoPath":"davidkelley/searchlite","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.470Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"index-lifecycle","description":"Understanding and modifying Searchlite’s storage/indexing pipeline (WAL → segment build → manifest/compaction) and storage backends; use when working on ingest, durability, fast fields, or segment layouts.","bodyPreview":"# Index Lifecycle Cheatsheet\n\n## The Searchlite mental model (one paragraph)\n\nSearchlite serves **one index directory** per instance (CLI path or HTTP `--index`). A **single writer** buffers operations, appends them to a WAL, and on `commit` writes a new immutable segment and atomically updates a manifest. Readers consult the manifest to know which segments exist; compaction merges segments and drops deleted/obsolete data.\n\n---\n\n## Glossary\n\n- **Schema**: declares fields, analyzers, what’s store","body":"# Index Lifecycle Cheatsheet\n\n## The Searchlite mental model (one paragraph)\n\nSearchlite serves **one index directory** per instance (CLI path or HTTP `--index`). A **single writer** buffers operations, appends them to a WAL, and on `commit` writes a new immutable segment and atomically updates a manifest. Readers consult the manifest to know which segments exist; compaction merges segments and drops deleted/obsolete data.\n\n---\n\n## Glossary\n\n- **Schema**: declares fields, analyzers, what’s stored vs fast vs indexed.\n- **WAL**: write-ahead log for durability of add/delete operations.\n- **Segment**: immutable set of postings/docstore/fast fields written on commit.\n- **Manifest**: authoritative list of segments that define the current index state.\n- **Refresh**: reload readers so they observe the latest manifest.\n- **Compaction**: rewrite live docs into fewer segments; cleans duplicates/old versions.\n\n---\n\n## Lifecycle steps (authoritative sequence)\n\n### 1) Init\n\n- Creates the index directory and writes schema/manifest state so it can accept docs.\n\n### 2) Ingest (add/update/delete)\n\n- Docs are upserted by primary key (`doc_id_field`, default `_id`)\n- Deletes are queued by id\n- Important: writes are buffered/queued; they are not visible to search yet\n\n### 3) Commit\n\nCommit is the “durable + visible” boundary:\n\n- writer flushes buffered ops\n- builds new segment files\n- persists them\n- atomically updates manifest\n\nDurability contract:\n\n- segment files/manifests are fsync’d on write\n- WAL truncation only happens after manifest is persisted/synced\n- manifest uses atomic rename + directory fsync\n\nCrash window (expected behavior):\n\n- if the process dies after manifest persisted but before WAL truncation, WAL replay re-applies the last batch\n- no data loss; compaction cleans extra generations\n\n### 4) Refresh (reader visibility)\n\n- With HTTP, visibility may require explicit `POST /refresh` unless configured with `--refresh-on-commit`.\n\n### 5) Search\n\nSearch uses:\n\n- BM25 scoring by default (with pruning modes)\n- phrase and fuzzy matching\n- filters on fast fields\n- aggregations on fast fields\n- optional highlights, collapse/inner_hits, suggest, rescore, profile/explain\n\nExecution modes (perf/correctness relevant):\n\n- `bm25` full evaluation\n- `wand` exact pruning (default)\n- `bmw` block-max WAND pruning (tunable block size)\n\n### 6) Maintain\n\n- Inspect: see manifest + segments\n- Stats: see doc/segment counts\n- Compact: merge segments and drop tombstoned/obsolete docs\n\n---\n\n## File layout expectations (conceptual)\n\nThe exact file names are an implementation detail, but the directory contains:\n\n- a manifest file (authoritative segment list)\n- a WAL file\n- per-segment files (postings/docstore/fast/meta/etc)\n- optional vector index structures when `vectors` is enabled\n\nWhen changing segment layout, preserve:\n\n- compatibility with existing indexes or provide a migration story\n- checksum/validation (if present)\n- atomicity during commit and cleanup after rollback/failed commit\n\n---\n\n## Schema invariants that drive the whole system\n\n- `doc_id_field` is required and is the key for upsert/delete semantics.\n- `stored: true` controls whether values can be returned/highlighted.\n- `fast: true` controls filters + aggregations performance/feasibility.\n- Nested fields flatten to dotted paths (e.g. `comment.author`) while preserving stored nested structure in responses.\n- Nested filters must be expressed with `Nested` blocks so clauses bind to the same object instance.\n\n---\n\n## Aggregations/filters coupling (easy to break)\n\n- `terms`, `significant_terms`, `rare_terms` require a fast keyword field.\n- numeric/date aggregations require fast numeric fields.\n- multi-valued fields contribute multiple values to metrics (doc_count remains per-doc).\n\nIf you modify fast-field encoding, bucket iteration, or numeric parsing:\n\n- add tests that validate aggs outputs (not just existence of buckets).\n\n---\n\n## Vector search (feature `vectors`)\n\nVector search is approximate ANN (HNSW):\n\n- dimension mismatches are rejected\n- cosine vectors are normalized automatically\n- tune recall/perf with `candidate_size` and `ef_search`\n- `vector_filter` can reduce candidate selection set\n\nIf you touch vector integration:\n\n- test both vector-only and hybrid search paths\n- confirm response includes `vector_score` when vector search runs\n\n---\n\n## “Where to make changes” guidance\n\n- Core indexing/query/durability lives in `searchlite-core`\n- CLI wiring + UX lives in `searchlite-cli`\n- HTTP server wiring + limits + endpoints live in `searchlite-http` (and/or the CLI `http` subcommand)\n- wasm storage backend + bindings live in `searchlite-wasm`\n- C ABI lives in `searchlite-ffi`\n\nKeep boundaries clean:\n\n- `searchlite-core` should remain the source of truth for correctness; CLI/HTTP adapt surfaces around it.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T08:47:32.321Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents requiring efficient full-text search capabilities with BM25 and phrase matching","zh":"适合需要高效全文搜索能力的AI代理，特别是BM25和短语匹配","ja":"全文検索機能のBM25およびフレーズマッチングを効率的に実行する必要があるAIエージェントに適しています","ko":"효율적인 全文 검색 기능과 BM25 및 구문 일치를 필요로 하는 AI 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA que requieren capacidades de búsqueda de texto completo eficientes con BM25 y coincidencia de frases","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA nécessitant des capacités de recherche de texte complet efficaces avec BM25 et correspondance de phrases","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents, die effiziente Volltextsuchefunktionen mit BM25 und Phrasenübereinstimmung benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA que exigem capacidades de pesquisa de texto completo eficientes com BM25 e combinação de frases","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, требующих эффективных возможностей полнотекстового поиска с BM25 и фразового поиска","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي الذي يتطلب إمكانيات بحث نص كامل فعالة مع BM25 و مطابقة العبارات"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to manage on-disk indexes with a clean Rust API, utilizing WAL for buffering operations and providing features like filters, aggregations, and highlighting, all while leveraging optional vectors and GPU stubs for accelerated performance","zh":"赋予代理使用干净的Rust API管理磁盘索引的能力，利用WAL缓冲操作，并提供诸如过滤器、聚合和突出显示等功能，同时利用可选的向量和GPU存根实现加速性能","ja":"クリーンなRust APIを使用してディスクインデックスを管理する能力をエージェントに与え、WALを使用してバッファリング操作を行い、フィルターや集計、ハイライトなどの機能を提供し、オプションのベクトルとGPUスタブを使用して加速パフォーマンスを実現する","ko":"클린한 러스트 API를 사용하여 디스크 인덱스를 관리하는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하며, WAL을 사용하여 버퍼링 연산을 수행하고, 필터 및 집계, 하이라이트 등의 기능을 제공하며, 선택적인 벡터 및 GPU 스텁을 사용하여 가속 성능을 구현합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a gestionar índices en disco con una API de Rust limpia, utilizando WAL para operaciones de buffering y proporcionando características como filtros, agregaciones y resaltado, todo mientras aprovecha vectores opcionales y stubs de GPU para un rendimiento acelerado","fr":"Permet aux agents de gérer des indexes sur disque avec une API Rust propre, en utilisant WAL pour les opérations de tampon et en fournissant des fonctionnalités comme des filtres, des agrégations et un éclairage, le tout en exploitant des vecteurs optionnels et des stubs GPU pour des performances accélérées","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, On-Disk-Indizes mit einer sauberen Rust-API zu verwalten, WAL für Pufferoperationen zu nutzen und Funktionen wie Filter, Aggregationen und Hervorhebung bereitzustellen, während optional Vektoren und GPU-Stubs für beschleunigte Leistung genutzt werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a gerenciar índices em disco com uma API Rust limpa, utilizando WAL para operações de buffer e fornecendo recursos como filtros, agregações e realce, tudo isso aproveitando vetores opcionais e stubs de GPU para desempenho acelerado","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью управлять индексами на диске с помощью чистого API Rust, используя WAL для операций буферизации и предоставляя функции, такие как фильтры, агрегации и выделение, все это при использовании необязательных векторов и стабов GPU для ускорения производительности","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من إدارة الفهارس على القرص باستخدام واجهة برمجة تطبيقات Rust نظيفة ، واستخدام WAL لعمليات التخزين المؤقت وتوفير الميزات مثل المرشحات والتجميعات والتأكيد ، كل ذلك مع استخدام متجهات اختيارية وخرافات GPU للحصول على أداء معزز"},"useCases":{"en":["Indexing large datasets for fast full-text search","Implementing filters and aggregations for refined search results","Utilizing BM25 with phrase matching for advanced search queries"],"zh":["为快速全文搜索而对大型数据集进行索引","为精细搜索结果实现过滤器和聚合","使用BM25和短语匹配进行高级搜索查询"],"ja":["高速全文検索のための大規模なデータセットのインデックス作成","精密な検索結果のためのフィルターや集計の実装","BM25およびフレーズマッチングを使用した高度な検索クエリー"],"ko":["빠른 全文 검색을 위한 대형 데이터셋 인덱싱","정교한 검색 결과를 위한 필터 및 집계 구현","고급 검색 쿼리를 위한 BM25 및 구문 일치 사용"],"es":["Indexación de grandes conjuntos de datos para búsqueda de texto completo rápida","Implementación de filtros y agregaciones para resultados de búsqueda refinados","Uso de BM25 con coincidencia de frases para consultas de búsqueda avanzadas"],"fr":["Indexation de grands ensembles de données pour une recherche de texte complet rapide","Mise en œuvre de filtres et d''agrégations pour des résultats de recherche affinés","Utilisation de BM25 avec correspondance de phrases pour des requêtes de recherche avancées"],"de":["Indizierung großer Datensätze für schnelle Volltextsuche","Implementierung von Filtern und Aggregationen für verfeinerte Suchergebnisse","Verwendung von BM25 mit Phrasenübereinstimmung für erweiterte Suchabfragen"],"pt":["Indexação de grandes conjuntos de dados para pesquisa de texto completo rápida","Implementação de filtros e agregações para resultados de pesquisa refinados","Utilização de BM25 com combinação de frases para consultas de pesquisa avançadas"],"ru":["Индексация больших наборов данных для быстрого полнотекстового поиска","Реализация фильтров и агрегаций для уточнения результатов поиска","Использование BM25 с фразовым поиском для продвинутых запросов поиска"],"ar":["فهرسة مجموعات بيانات كبيرة للبحث النصي الكامل السريع","تطبيق المرشحات والتجميعات للحصول على نتائج بحث دقيقة","استخدام BM25 مع مطابقة العبارات لاستعلامات البحث المتقدمة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires a single writer for index operations","Limited to a single on-disk index per instance"],"zh":["需要单个写入者进行索引操作","每个实例仅限单个磁盘索引"],"ja":["インデックス操作には単一のライターが必要","インスタンスごとにディスクインデックスは1つのみ"],"ko":["인덱스 연산을 위해 단일 작성자가 필요","인스턴스당 단일 디스크 인덱스만 제한"],"es":["Requiere un solo escritor para operaciones de índice","Limitado a un solo índice en disco por instancia"],"fr":["Nécessite un seul auteur pour les opérations d''index","Limité à un seul index sur disque par instance"],"de":["Benötigt einen einzelnen Schreiber für Indexoperationen","Begrenzt auf einen einzelnen On-Disk-Index pro Instanz"],"pt":["Exige um único escritor para operações de índice","Limitado a um único índice em disco por instância"],"ru":["Требует одного писателя для операций с индексом","Ограничен одним индексом на диск на экземпляр"],"ar":["يتطلب كاتب واحد لعمليات الفهرسة","محدود بفهرس واحد على القرص لكل مثيل"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":40}');
