texte de Modèle","Outils et options de configuration disponibles","Documentation automatique et mise à jour"],"de":["Programmatischer Zugriff auf die GitHub-API","Unterstützung für KI-Agents","Implementierung des Modell-Kontext-Protokolls","Verfügbare Tools und Konfigurationsoptionen","Automatische und aktuelle Dokumentation"],"pt":["Acesso programático à API do GitHub","Integração com agentes de IA","Ferramentas de configuração e personalização","Automatização de tarefas e fluxos de trabalho","Suporte a protocolo Model Context Protocol (MCP)"],"ru":["Программный доступ к API GitHub","Интеграция с агентами ИИ","Инструменты конфигурации и настройки","Автоматизация задач и рабочих процессов","Поддержка протокола Model Context Protocol (MCP)"],"ar":["الوصول البرمجي إلى واجهة برمجة تطبيقات GitHub","التكامل مع الوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات التكوين والتحكم","تأتمة المهام والعمليات","دعم بروتوكول.Model Context Protocol (MCP)"]},"keywords":{"zh":["GitHub MCP 服务器","Model Context Protocol","AI 代理","GitHub API","程序化访问","自动化生成"],"ja":["GitHub MCP サーバー","Model Context Protocol","AI エージェント","GitHub API","プログラムによるアクセス","自動生成"],"ko":["GitHub MCP 서버","Model Context Protocol","AI 에이전트","GitHub API","프로그래밍 방식 액세스","자동 생성"],"es":["servidor GitHub MCP","acceso a la API de GitHub","agentes de inteligencia artificial","Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo","desarrollo de software","integración de API"],"fr":["serveur GitHub MCP","accès à l''API GitHub","agents d''intelligence artificielle","Protocole de Contexte de Modèle","développement de logiciels","intégration d''API"],"de":["GitHub-MCP-Server","Zugriff auf die GitHub-API","KI-Agents","Modell-Kontext-Protokoll","Software-Entwicklung","API-Integration"],"pt":["GitHub MCP","servidor GitHub","acesso programático","API do GitHub","agentes de IA","integração","automatização","Model Context Protocol"],"ru":["GitHub MCP","сервер GitHub","программный доступ","API GitHub","агенты ИИ","интеграция","автоматизация","Model Context Protocol"],"ar":["GitHub MCP","خادم GitHub","الوصول البرمجي","واجهة برمجة تطبيقات GitHub","الوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي","التكامل","تأتمة","بروتوكول.Model Context Protocol"]}},"owner":"maxfraieho","repo":"garden-seedling","repoPath":"maxfraieho/garden-seedling","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.473Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"github-mcp-server","description":"GitHub MCP Server Documentation","bodyPreview":"# GitHub MCP Server Documentation\n\nThis file contains comprehensive documentation about the GitHub MCP (Model Context Protocol) server, including available tools and configuration options.\n\n**Note**: This file is automatically generated and updated by the `github-mcp-tools-report.md` workflow. Manual edits may be overwritten.\n\n**Last Updated**: [To be filled by workflow]\n\n## Overview\n\nThe GitHub MCP server provides AI agents with programmatic access to GitHub''s API through the Model Context Prot","body":"# GitHub MCP Server Documentation\n\nThis file contains comprehensive documentation about the GitHub MCP (Model Context Protocol) server, including available tools and configuration options.\n\n**Note**: This file is automatically generated and updated by the `github-mcp-tools-report.md` workflow. Manual edits may be overwritten.\n\n**Last Updated**: [To be filled by workflow]\n\n## Overview\n\nThe GitHub MCP server provides AI agents with programmatic access to GitHub''s API through the Model Context Protocol. It supports two modes of operation:\n\n### Local Mode (Docker-based)\n- Runs as a Docker container on the GitHub Actions runner\n- Uses `GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN` environment variable for authentication\n- Configurable toolsets via `GITHUB_TOOLSETS` environment variable\n- Supports read-only mode via `GITHUB_READ_ONLY` environment variable\n\n### Remote Mode (Hosted)\n- Connects to hosted GitHub MCP server at `https://api.githubcopilot.com/mcp/`\n- Uses Bearer token authentication in HTTP headers\n- Supports read-only mode via `X-MCP-Readonly` header\n- No Docker container required\n\n## Configuration\n\n### Basic Configuration\n\n**Local Mode (Docker)**:\n```yaml\ntools:\n  github:\n    mode: \"local\"\n    toolsets: [default]  # or [repos, issues, pull_requests]\n```\n\n**Remote Mode (Hosted)**:\n```yaml\ntools:\n  github:\n    mode: \"remote\"\n    toolsets: [default]  # or [repos, issues, pull_requests]\n```\n\n### Read-Only Mode\n\nTo restrict the GitHub MCP server to read-only operations:\n\n```yaml\ntools:\n  github:\n    mode: \"remote\"\n    read-only: true\n    toolsets: [repos, issues]\n```\n\n### Custom Authentication\n\nUse a custom GitHub token instead of the default:\n\n```yaml\ntools:\n  github:\n    mode: \"remote\"\n    github-token: \"${{ secrets.CUSTOM_GITHUB_PAT }}\"\n    toolsets: [repos, issues]\n```\n\n## Available Toolsets\n\nThe GitHub MCP server organizes tools into logical toolsets. You can enable specific toolsets, use `[default]` for the recommended defaults, or use `[all]` to enable everything.\n\n:::note[Why Use Toolsets?]\nThe `allowed:` pattern for listing individual GitHub tools is **not recommended for new workflows**. Individual tool names may change between GitHub MCP server versions, but toolsets provide a stable API. Always use `toolsets:` instead. See [Migration from Allowed to Toolsets](#migration-from-allowed-to-toolsets) for guidance on updating existing workflows.\n:::\n\n:::tip[Best Practice]\n**Always use `toolsets:` for GitHub tools.** Toolsets provide:\n- **Stability**: Tool names may change between MCP server versions, but toolsets remain stable\n- **Better organization**: Clear groupings of related functionality\n- **Complete functionality**: Get all related tools automatically\n- **Reduced verbosity**: Cleaner configuration\n- **Future-proof**: New tools are automatically included as they''re added\n:::\n\n### Recommended Default Toolsets\n\nThe following toolsets are enabled by default when `toolsets:` is not specified:\n- `context` - User and environment context (strongly recommended)\n- `repos` - Repository management\n- `issues` - Issue management  \n- `pull_requests` - Pull request operations\n\n**Note**: The `users` toolset is not included by default and must be explicitly specified if needed.\n\n### All Available Toolsets\n\n| Toolset | Description | Common Tools |\n|---------|-------------|--------------|\n| `context` | User and environment context | `get_teams`, `get_team_members` |\n| `repos` | Repository management | `get_repository`, `get_file_contents`, `search_code`, `list_commits` |\n| `issues` | Issue management | `issue_read`, `list_issues`, `create_issue`, `search_issues` |\n| `pull_requests` | Pull request operations | `pull_request_read`, `list_pull_requests`, `create_pull_request` |\n| `actions` | GitHub Actions/CI/CD | `list_workflows`, `list_workflow_runs`, `download_workflow_run_artifact` |\n| `code_security` | Code scanning and security | `list_code_scanning_alerts`, `get_code_scanning_alert` |\n| `dependabot` | Dependency management | Dependabot alerts and updates |\n| `discussions` | GitHub Discussions | `list_discussions`, `create_discussion` |\n| `experiments` | Experimental features | Unstable/preview APIs |\n| `gists` | Gist operations | `create_gist`, `list_gists` |\n| `labels` | Label management | `get_label`, `list_labels`, `create_label` |\n| `notifications` | Notifications | `list_notifications`, `mark_notifications_read` |\n| `orgs` | Organization management | `get_organization`, `list_organizations` |\n| `projects` | GitHub Projects | Project board operations |\n| `secret_protection` | Secret scanning | Secret detection and management |\n| `security_advisories` | Security advisories | Advisory creation and management |\n| `stargazers` | Repository stars | Star-related operations |\n| `users` | User profiles | `get_me`, `get_user`, `list_users` |\n| `search` | Advanced search | Search across repos, code, users |\n\n## Available Tools by Toolset\n\nThis section maps individual tools to their respective toolsets to help with migration from `allowed:` to `toolsets:`.\n\n### Context Toolset\n- `get_teams` - List teams the user belongs to\n- `get_team_members` - List members of a specific team\n\n### Repos Toolset\n- `get_repository` - Get repository information\n- `get_file_contents` - Read file contents from repository\n- `search_code` - Search code across repositories\n- `list_commits` - List commits in a repository\n- `get_commit` - Get details of a specific commit\n- `get_latest_release` - Get the latest release\n- `list_releases` - List all releases\n\n### Issues Toolset\n- `issue_read` - Read issue details\n- `list_issues` - List issues in a repository\n- `create_issue` - Create a new issue\n- `update_issue` - Update an existing issue\n- `search_issues` - Search issues across repositories\n- `add_reaction` - Add reaction to an issue or comment\n- `create_issue_comment` - Add a comment to an issue\n\n### Pull Requests Toolset\n- `pull_request_read` - Read pull request details\n- `list_pull_requests` - List pull requests in a repository\n- `get_pull_request` - Get details of a specific pull request\n- `create_pull_request` - Create a new pull request\n- `search_pull_requests` - Search pull requests across repositories\n\n### Actions Toolset\n- `list_workflows` - List GitHub Actions workflows\n- `list_workflow_runs` - List workflow runs\n- `get_workflow_run` - Get details of a specific workflow run\n- `download_workflow_run_artifact` - Download workflow artifacts\n\n### Code Security Toolset\n- `list_code_scanning_alerts` - List code scanning alerts\n- `get_code_scanning_alert` - Get details of a specific alert\n- `create_code_scanning_alert` - Create a code scanning alert\n\n### Discussions Toolset\n- `list_discussions` - List discussions in a repository\n- `create_discussion` - Create a new discussion\n\n### Labels Toolset\n- `get_label` - Get label details\n- `list_labels` - List labels in a repository\n- `create_label` - Create a new label\n\n### Users Toolset\n- `get_me` - Get current authenticated user information\n- `get_user` - Get user profile information\n- `list_users` - List users\n\n### Notifications Toolset\n- `list_notifications` - List user notifications\n- `mark_notifications_read` - Mark notifications as read\n\n### Organizations Toolset\n- `get_organization` - Get organization details\n- `list_organizations` - List organizations\n\n### Gists Toolset\n- `create_gist` - Create a new gist\n- `list_gists` - List user''s gists\n\n## Authentication Details\n\n### Remote Mode Authentication\n\nThe remote mode uses Bearer token authentication:\n\n**Headers**:\n- `Authorization: Bearer <token>` - Required for authentication\n- `X-MCP-Readonly: true` - Optional, enables read-only mode\n\n**Token Source**:\n- Default: `${{ secrets.GH_AW_GITHUB_TOKEN }}` or `${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}`\n- Custom: Configure via `github-token` field\n\n### Local Mode Authentication\n\nThe local mode uses environment variables:\n\n**Environment Variables**:\n- `GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN` - Required for authentication\n- `GITHUB_READ_ONLY=1` - Optional, enables read-only mode\n- `GITHUB_TOOLSETS=<comma-separated-list>` - Optional, specifies enabled toolsets\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Toolset Selection\n\n1. **Start with defaults**: For most workflows, the recommended default toolsets provide sufficient functionality\n2. **Enable specific toolsets**: Only enable additional toolsets when you need their specific functionality\n3. **Security consideration**: Be mindful of write operations - consider using read-only mode when possible\n4. **Performance**: Using fewer toolsets reduces initialization time and memory usage\n\n### Token Permissions\n\nEnsure your GitHub token has appropriate permissions for the toolsets you''re enabling:\n\n- `repos` toolsets: Requires repository read/write permissions\n- `issues` toolsets: Requires issues read/write permissions\n- `pull_requests` toolsets: Requires pull requests read/write permissions\n- `actions` toolsets: Requires actions read/write permissions\n- `discussions` toolsets: Requires discussions read/write permissions\n\n### Remote vs Local Mode\n\n**Use Remote Mode when**:\n- You want faster initialization (no Docker container to start)\n- You''re running in a GitHub Actions environment with internet access\n- You want to use the latest version without specifying Docker image tags\n\n**Use Local Mode when**:\n- You need a specific version of the MCP server\n- You want to use custom arguments\n- You''re running in an environment without internet access\n- You want to test with a local build of the MCP server\n\n## Migration from Allowed to Toolsets\n\nIf you have existing workflows using the `allowed:` pattern, we recommend migrating to `toolsets:` for better maintainability and stability. Individual tool names may change between MCP server versions, but toolsets provide a stable API that won''t break your workflows.\n\n### Migration Examples\n\n**Using `allowed:` (not recommended):**\n```yaml\ntools:\n  github:\n    allowed:\n      - get_repository\n      - get_file_contents\n      - list_commits\n      - list_issues\n      - create_issue\n      - update_issue\n```\n\n**Using `toolsets:` (recommended):**\n```yaml\ntools:\n  github:\n    toolsets: [repos, issues]\n```\n\n### Tool-to-Toolset Mapping\n\nUse this table to identify which toolset contains the tools you need:\n\n| `allowed:` Tools | Migrate to `toolsets:` |\n|------------------|------------------------|\n| `get_me` | `users` |\n| `get_teams`, `get_team_members` | `context` |\n| `get_repository`, `get_file_contents`, `search_code`, `list_commits` | `repos` |\n| `issue_read`, `list_issues`, `create_issue`, `update_issue`, `search_issues` | `issues` |\n| `pull_request_read`, `list_pull_requests`, `create_pull_request` | `pull_requests` |\n| `list_workflows`, `list_workflow_runs`, `get_workflow_run` | `actions` |\n| `list_code_scanning_alerts`, `get_code_scanning_alert` | `code_security` |\n| `list_discussions`, `create_discussion` | `discussions` |\n| `get_label`, `list_labels`, `create_label` | `labels` |\n| `get_user`, `list_users` | `users` |\n| Mixed repos/issues/PRs tools | `[default]` |\n| All tools | `[all]` |\n\n### Quick Migration Steps\n\n1. **Identify tools in use**: Review your current `allowed:` list\n2. **Map to toolsets**: Use the table above to find corresponding toolsets\n3. **Replace configuration**: Change `allowed:` to `toolsets:`\n4. **Test**: Run `gh aw mcp inspect <workflow>` to verify tools are available\n5. **Compile**: Run `gh aw compile` to update the lock file\n\n## Using Allowed Pattern with Custom MCP Servers\n\n:::note[When to Use Allowed]\nThe `allowed:` pattern is appropriate for:\n- Custom MCP servers (non-GitHub)\n- Gradual migration of existing workflows\n- Fine-grained restriction of specific tools within a toolset\n\nFor GitHub tools, always use `toolsets:` instead of `allowed:`.\n:::\n\nThe `allowed:` field can still be used to restrict tools for custom MCP servers:\n\n```yaml\nmcp-servers:\n  notion:\n    container: \"mcp/notion\"\n    allowed: [\"search_pages\", \"get_page\"]  # Fine for custom MCP servers\n```\n\nFor GitHub tools, `allowed:` can be combined with `toolsets:` to further restrict access, but this pattern is not recommended for new workflows.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Issues\n\n**Issue**: Tool not found or not available\n- **Solution**: Check if you''re using `allowed:` to restrict tools. Consider using `toolsets:` instead to get all related tools.\n- **Verify**: Run `gh aw mcp inspect <workflow-name>` to see which tools are actually available.\n\n**Issue**: Missing functionality after specifying toolset\n- **Cause**: Using a too-narrow toolset that doesn''t include all needed tools\n- **Solution**: Either add additional toolsets (e.g., `toolsets: [default, actions]`) or use `[all]` for full access\n\n**Issue**: Workflow using `allowed:` list is verbose and hard to maintain\n- **Solution**: Migrate to `toolsets:` configuration using the migration guide above\n\n### Best Practices for Debugging\n\n1. **Start with `[default]` toolset**: Most workflows work well with default toolsets\n2. **Add specific toolsets as needed**: Incrementally add toolsets like `actions`, `discussions`, etc.\n3. **Use `gh aw mcp inspect`**: Verify which tools are actually available\n4. **Check tool-to-toolset mapping**: Reference the tables above to find the right toolset\n\n## References\n\n- [GitHub MCP Server Repository](https://github.com/github/github-mcp-server)\n- [Model Context Protocol Specification](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/)\n- [GitHub Actions Documentation](https://docs.github.com/actions)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:01:47.315Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Cursor, Windsurf, and Claude Code needing programmatic access to GitHub''s API through the Model Context Protocol","zh":"适用于像 Cursor、Windsurf 和 Claude Code 这样的 AI Agent，需要通过模型上下文协议以编程方式访问 GitHub 的 API","ja":"Cursor、Windsurf、Claude Code などの AI エージェントに適しており、モデルコンテキストプロトコルを介して GitHub の API にプログラム的にアクセスする必要がある","ko":"Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code와 같은 AI 에이전트에게 적합하며, 모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜을 통해 GitHub의 API에 프로그래밍 방식으로 액세스할 수 있는 기능을 제공한다","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf y Claude Code que necesitan acceso programático a la API de GitHub a través del Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo","fr":"Idéal pour les agents IA comme Cursor, Windsurf et Claude Code nécessitant un accès programmatique à l''API GitHub via le Protocole de Contexte de Modèle","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Cursor, Windsurf und Claude Code, die programmatischen Zugriff auf die GitHub-API über das Modellkontextprotokoll benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Cursor, Windsurf e Claude Code que necessitam de acesso programático à API do GitHub por meio do Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, таких как Cursor, Windsurf и Claude Code, требующих программного доступа к API GitHub через Протокол контекста модели","ar":"مثالي لعميل الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Cursor و Windsurf و Claude Code الذين يحتاجون إلى الوصول البرمجي إلى واجهة برمجة التطبيقات GitHub من خلال بروتوكول سياق النموذج"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to leverage the GitHub MCP server for automated interactions with GitHub''s API, utilizing the Model Context Protocol for seamless integration, and enables access to comprehensive documentation and configuration options, all while ensuring compatibility with various AI agent ecosystems","zh":"赋予代理通过模型上下文协议无缝集成的方式访问 GitHub MCP 服务器，以进行 GitHub API 的自动化交互，并提供全面文档和配置选项，同时确保与各种 AI 代理生态系统的兼容性","ja":"エージェントがモデルコンテキストプロトコルを介して GitHub MCP サーバーにアクセスし、GitHub API との自動化されたやり取りを実行できるようにし、シームレスな統合を実現し、包括的なドキュメントと構成オプションにアクセスできるようにし、同時にさまざまな AI エージェントのエコシステムとの互換性を確保する","ko":"에이전트가 모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜을 통해 GitHub MCP 서버에 액세스하여 GitHub API와의 자동화된 상호 작용을 수행할 수 있도록 하며, 무제한 통합을 제공하고, 포괄적인 문서 및 구성 옵션에 액세스할 수 있도록 하며,同時에 다양한 AI 에이전트 에코시스템과 호환성을 보장한다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aprovechar el servidor GitHub MCP para interacciones automatizadas con la API de GitHub, utilizando el Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo para una integración sin problemas, y permite el acceso a documentación completa y opciones de configuración, todo mientras garantiza la compatibilidad con varios ecosistemas de agentes de IA","fr":"Permet aux agents d''utiliser le serveur GitHub MCP pour des interactions automatisées avec l''API GitHub, en utilisant le Protocole de Contexte de Modèle pour une intégration transparente, et permet l''accès à une documentation complète et des options de configuration, tout en garantissant la compatibilité avec divers écosystèmes d''agents IA","de":"Ermöglicht es Agents, den GitHub-MCP-Server für automatisierte Interaktionen mit der GitHub-API zu nutzen, indem das Modellkontextprotokoll für eine nahtlose Integration verwendet wird, und ermöglicht den Zugriff auf umfassende Dokumentation und Konfigurationsoptionen, während die Kompatibilität mit verschiedenen KI-Agent-Ökosystemen gewährleistet wird","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aproveitarem o servidor GitHub MCP para interações automatizadas com a API do GitHub, utilizando o Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo para integração sem problemas, e permite o acesso a documentação abrangente e opções de configuração, garantindo compatibilidade com vários ecossistemas de agentes de IA","ru":"Позволяет агентам использовать сервер GitHub MCP для автоматизированных взаимодействий с API GitHub, используя Протокол контекста модели для бесшовной интеграции, и обеспечивает доступ к всесторонней документации и опциям конфигурации, сохраняя при этом совместимость с различными экосистемами агентов ИИ","ar":"تمكن الوكلاء من استخدام خادم GitHub MCP للتفاعلات الآلية مع واجهة برمجة التطبيقات GitHub، باستخدام بروتوكول سياق النموذج للتكامل السلس، ويسمح بالوصول إلى المستندات الشاملة وخيارات التكوين، مع الحفاظ على التوافق مع بيئات عميل الذكاء الاصطناعي المختلفة"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating GitHub repository management","Generating Model Context Protocol requests","Debugging API interactions through the GitHub MCP server"],"zh":["自动化 GitHub 仓库管理","生成模型上下文协议请求","通过 GitHub MCP 服务器调试 API 交互"],"ja":["GitHub リポジトリの管理を自動化する","モデルコンテキストプロトコルリクエストを生成する","GitHub MCP サーバーを介して API のやり取りをデバッグする"],"ko":["GitHub 리포지토리 관리 자동화","모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜 요청 생성","GitHub MCP 서버를 통해 API 상호 작용 디버깅"],"es":["Automatizar la administración de repositorios de GitHub","Generar solicitudes del Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo","Depurar interacciones de API a través del servidor GitHub MCP"],"fr":["Automatiser la gestion des référentiels GitHub","Générer des requêtes du Protocole de Contexte de Modèle","Déboguer les interactions API via le serveur GitHub MCP"],"de":["Automatisierung der Verwaltung von GitHub-Repositorys","Erzeugen von Anfragen des Modellkontextprotokolls","Fehlerbehebung von API-Interaktionen über den GitHub-MCP-Server"],"pt":["Automatizar a gestão de repositórios GitHub","Gerar solicitações do Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo","Depurar interações de API por meio do servidor GitHub MCP"],"ru":["Автоматизировать управление репозиториями GitHub","Генерировать запросы Протокола контекста модели","Отладить взаимодействия API через сервер GitHub MCP"],"ar":["تحسين إدارة مستودعات GitHub","توليد طلبات بروتوكول سياق النموذج","تصحيح أخطاء التفاعلات البرمجية من خلال خادم GitHub MCP"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to GitHub''s API","Limited to Model Context Protocol compatibility","Automatically generated documentation may overwrite manual edits"],"zh":["需要访问 GitHub 的 API","仅限模型上下文协议兼容性","自动生成的文档可能会覆盖手动编辑"],"ja":["GitHub の API にアクセスする必要がある","モデルコンテキストプロトコルとの互換性のみ","自動生成されたドキュメントは手動で編集した内容を上書きする可能性がある"],"ko":["GitHub의 API에 액세스해야 함","모델 컨텍스트 프로토콜 호환성만 해당","자동 생성된 문서는 수동 편집을 덮어쓸 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere acceso a la API de GitHub","Limitado a la compatibilidad con el Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo","La documentación generada automáticamente puede sobreescribir ediciones manuales"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à l''API GitHub","Limité à la compatibilité avec le Protocole de Contexte de Modèle","La documentation générée automatiquement peut écraser les éditions manuelles"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf die GitHub-API","Begrenzt auf die Kompatibilität mit dem Modellkontextprotokoll","Automatisch generierte Dokumentation kann manuelle Bearbeitungen überschreiben"],"pt":["Exige acesso à API do GitHub","Limitado à compatibilidade com o Protocolo de Contexto de Modelo","Documentação gerada automaticamente pode substituir edições manuais"],"ru":["Требует доступа к API GitHub","Ограничен совместимостью с Протоколом контекста модели","Автоматически сгенерированная документация может перезаписать ручные правки"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى واجهة برمجة التطبيقات GitHub","محدود بالتوافق مع بروتوكول سياق النموذج","يمكن للمستندات المولدة تلقائيًا كتابة التعديلات اليدوية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
