egue en Azure con patrones de diseño y mejores prácticas para servicios en la nube","fr":"Déploiement sur Azure avec des modèles de conception et des meilleures pratiques pour les services cloud","de":"Azure-Bereitstellung mit Entwurfsmustern und Best Practices für Cloud-Dienste","pt":"Implantação no Azure é um conjunto de habilidades para projetar e implementar arquiteturas de nuvem seguras e otimizadas. Aprenda a selecionar serviços de co...","ru":"Развертывание на Azure - это набор навыков для проектирования и внедрения безопасных и оптимизированных облачных архитектур. Узнайте, как выбрать подходящие ...","ar":"تثبيت على Azure هو مجموعة من المهارات لتصميم وتنفيذ البنية التحتية السحابية الآمنة والمثلى. تعلم كيفية اختيار خدمات الحوسبة والتخزين المناسبة.","en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"definition":{"en":"The most comprehensive Claude Code skills registry | Web Search: https://skills-registry-web.vercel.app"},"features":{"zh":["Azure","Azure","Azure","Azure OpenAI","Azure"],"ja":["Azure","Azure","Azure","Azure OpenAI","Azure"],"ko":["Azure ","Azure ","Azure ","Azure OpenAI","Azure "],"es":["Diseño de arquitecturas en la nube de Azure","Selección de servicios de computación en la nube","Implementación de soluciones de almacenamiento en la nube","Integración de Azure OpenAI o Cognitive Services","Implementación de patrones de mensajería"],"fr":["Conception d''architectures cloud Azure","Sélection de services de calcul en cloud","Mise en œuvre de solutions de stockage en cloud","Intégration d''Azure OpenAI ou Cognitive Services","Mise en œuvre de modèles de messagerie"],"de":["Entwurf von Azure-Cloud-Architekturen","Auswahl von Cloud-Computing-Diensten","Implementierung von Cloud-Speicherlösungen","Integration von Azure OpenAI oder Cognitive Services","Implementierung von Messaging-Mustern"],"pt":["Projetar arquiteturas de nuvem seguras e otimizadas","Selecionar serviços de computação adequados (Container Apps, AKS, Functions, App Service)","Arquitetar soluções de armazenamento (Blob Storage, Files, Cosmos DB)","Integrar Azure OpenAI ou Cognitive Services","Implementar padrões de mensagens"],"ru":["Проектировать безопасные и оптимизированные облачные архитектуры","Выбирать подходящие вычислительные услуги (Container Apps, AKS, Functions, App Service)","Проектировать хранилищные решения (Blob Storage, Files, Cosmos DB)","Интегрировать Azure OpenAI или Cognitive Services","Внедрять шаблоны обмена сообщениями"],"ar":["تصميم بنية تحتية سحابية آمنة ومثلى","اختيار خدمات حوسبة مناسبة (Container Apps, AKS, Functions, App Service)","تصميم حلول تخزين (Blob Storage, Files, Cosmos DB)","دمج Azure OpenAI أو Cognitive Services","تنفيذ أنماط الرسائل"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Azure","Azure","Azure","Azure OpenAI","Azure","Azure"],"ja":["Azure","Azure","Azure","Azure OpenAI","Azure","Azure"],"ko":["Azure ","Azure ","Azure ","Azure OpenAI","Azure ","Azure "],"es":["despliegue en azure","patrones de diseño en la nube","mejores prácticas de azure","servicios de computación en la nube","soluciones de almacenamiento en la nube","azure openai","cognitive services"],"fr":["déploiement sur azure","modèles de conception en cloud","meilleures pratiques azure","services de calcul en cloud","solutions de stockage en cloud","azure openai","cognitive services"],"de":["azure-bereitstellung","entwurfsmuster für die cloud","azure-best-practices","cloud-computing-dienste","cloud-speicherlösungen","azure openai","cognitive services"],"pt":["implantação no azure","desenvolvimento de nuvem","arquitetura de nuvem","segurança de nuvem","otimização de custos","serviços de computação","armazenamento de nuvem","azure openai","cognitive services"],"ru":["развертывание на azure","облачное разработка","облачная архитектура","облачная безопасность","оптимизация затрат","вычислительные услуги","облачное хранилище","azure openai","cognitive services"],"ar":["تثبيت على azure","تطوير سحابي","بنية تحتية سحابية","أمان سحابي","تحسين التكاليف","خدمات حوسبة","تخزين سحابي","azure openai","cognitive services"]}},"owner":"majiayu000","repo":"claude-skill-registry","repoPath":"majiayu000/claude-skill-registry","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.473Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"deploying-on-azure","description":"Design and implement Azure cloud architectures using best practices for compute, storage, databases, AI services, networking, and governance. Use when building applications on Microsoft Azure or migrating workloads to Azure cloud platform.","bodyPreview":"# Azure Patterns\n\nDesign and implement Azure cloud architectures following Microsoft''s Well-Architected Framework and best practices for service selection, cost optimization, and security.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Designing new applications for Azure cloud\n- Selecting Azure compute services (Container Apps, AKS, Functions, App Service)\n- Architecting storage solutions (Blob Storage, Files, Cosmos DB)\n- Integrating Azure OpenAI or Cognitive Services\n- Implementing messaging pattern","body":"# Azure Patterns\n\nDesign and implement Azure cloud architectures following Microsoft''s Well-Architected Framework and best practices for service selection, cost optimization, and security.\n\n## When to Use\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Designing new applications for Azure cloud\n- Selecting Azure compute services (Container Apps, AKS, Functions, App Service)\n- Architecting storage solutions (Blob Storage, Files, Cosmos DB)\n- Integrating Azure OpenAI or Cognitive Services\n- Implementing messaging patterns (Service Bus, Event Grid, Event Hubs)\n- Designing secure networks with Private Endpoints\n- Applying Azure governance and compliance policies\n- Optimizing Azure costs and performance\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### Service Selection Philosophy\n\nAzure offers 200+ services. Choose based on:\n1. **Managed vs. IaaS** - Prefer fully managed services (lower operational burden)\n2. **Cost Model** - Consumption vs. dedicated capacity\n3. **Integration Requirements** - Microsoft 365, Active Directory, hybrid cloud\n4. **Control vs. Simplicity** - More control = more operational overhead\n\n### Azure Well-Architected Framework (Five Pillars)\n\n| Pillar | Focus | Key Practices |\n|--------|-------|---------------|\n| **Cost Optimization** | Maximize value within budget | Reserved Instances, auto-scaling, lifecycle management |\n| **Operational Excellence** | Run reliable systems | Azure Policy, automation, monitoring |\n| **Performance Efficiency** | Scale to meet demand | Autoscaling, caching, CDN |\n| **Reliability** | Recover from failures | Availability Zones, multi-region, backup |\n| **Security** | Protect data and assets | Managed Identity, Private Endpoints, Key Vault |\n\nReference `references/well-architected.md` for detailed pillar implementation patterns.\n\n## Compute Service Selection\n\n### Decision Framework\n\n```\nContainer-based workload?\n  YES → Need Kubernetes control plane?\n          YES → Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS)\n          NO → Azure Container Apps (recommended)\n  NO → Event-driven function?\n         YES → Azure Functions\n         NO → Web application?\n                YES → Azure App Service\n                NO → Legacy/specialized → Virtual Machines\n```\n\n### Service Comparison\n\n| Service | Best For | Pricing Model | Operational Overhead |\n|---------|----------|---------------|---------------------|\n| **Container Apps** | Microservices, APIs, background jobs | Consumption or dedicated | Low |\n| **AKS** | Complex K8s workloads, service mesh | Node-based | High |\n| **Functions** | Event-driven, short tasks (<10 min) | Consumption or premium | Low |\n| **App Service** | Web apps, simple APIs | Dedicated plans | Low |\n| **Virtual Machines** | Legacy apps, specialized software | VM-based | High |\n\n**Recommendation:** Start with Azure Container Apps for 80% of containerized workloads (simpler and cheaper than AKS).\n\nReference `references/compute-services.md` for detailed comparison with Bicep and Terraform examples.\n\n## Storage Architecture\n\n### Blob Storage Tier Selection\n\n| Tier | Access Pattern | Cost/GB/Month | Minimum Storage Duration |\n|------|---------------|---------------|--------------------------|\n| **Hot** | Daily access | $0.018 | None |\n| **Cool** | <1/month access | $0.010 | 30 days |\n| **Cold** | <90 days access | $0.0045 | 90 days |\n| **Archive** | Rare access | $0.00099 | 180 days |\n\n**Pattern:** Use lifecycle management policies to automatically move data to lower-cost tiers.\n\n### Storage Service Decision\n\n```\nFile system interface required?\n  YES → Protocol?\n          SMB → Azure Files (or NetApp Files for high performance)\n          NFS → Azure Files (NFS 4.1)\n  NO → Object storage → Blob Storage\n       Block storage → Managed Disks (Standard/Premium SSD/Ultra)\n       Analytics → Data Lake Storage Gen2\n```\n\nReference `references/storage-patterns.md` for lifecycle policies, redundancy options, and performance tuning.\n\n## Database Service Selection\n\n### Decision Framework\n\n```\nRelational data?\n  YES → SQL Server compatible?\n          YES → Need VM-level access?\n                  YES → SQL Managed Instance\n                  NO → Azure SQL Database\n          NO → Open source?\n                 PostgreSQL → PostgreSQL Flexible Server\n                 MySQL → MySQL Flexible Server\n  NO → Data model?\n         Document/JSON → Cosmos DB (NoSQL API)\n         Graph → Cosmos DB (Gremlin API)\n         Wide-column → Cosmos DB (Cassandra API)\n         Key-value cache → Azure Cache for Redis\n         Time-series → Azure Data Explorer\n```\n\n### Cosmos DB Consistency Levels\n\n| Level | Use Case | Latency | Throughput |\n|-------|----------|---------|------------|\n| **Strong** | Financial transactions, inventory | Highest | Lowest |\n| **Bounded Staleness** | Real-time leaderboards with acceptable lag | High | Low |\n| **Session** | Shopping carts, user sessions (default) | Medium | Medium |\n| **Consistent Prefix** | Social feeds, IoT telemetry | Low | High |\n| **Eventual** | Analytics, ML training data | Lowest | Highest |\n\nReference `references/database-selection.md` for capacity planning, indexing strategies, and migration patterns.\n\n## AI and Machine Learning Integration\n\n### Azure OpenAI Service\n\n**Use Cases:**\n- Chatbots and conversational AI (GPT-4)\n- Content generation and summarization\n- Semantic search with embeddings (RAG pattern)\n- Code generation and completion\n- Function calling for structured outputs\n\n**Key Advantages:**\n- Enterprise data privacy (no model training on customer data)\n- Regional deployment for data residency\n- Microsoft enterprise SLAs\n- Built-in content filtering\n\n**Integration Pattern:**\n```python\nfrom openai import AzureOpenAI\nfrom azure.identity import DefaultAzureCredential\n\ncredential = DefaultAzureCredential()\nclient = AzureOpenAI(\n    azure_endpoint=\"https://myopenai.openai.azure.com\",\n    azure_ad_token_provider=token_provider,\n    api_version=\"2024-02-15-preview\"\n)\n\nresponse = client.chat.completions.create(\n    model=\"gpt-4-turbo\",\n    messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello!\"}]\n)\n```\n\n### Other AI Services\n\n| Service | Purpose | Common Use Cases |\n|---------|---------|------------------|\n| **Cognitive Services** | Pre-built AI models | Vision, Speech, Language, Decision |\n| **Azure Machine Learning** | Custom model training | MLOps, model deployment, feature engineering |\n| **Azure AI Search** | Semantic search engine | RAG patterns, document search |\n\nReference `references/ai-integration.md` for RAG architecture, function calling, and fine-tuning patterns.\n\n## Messaging and Integration\n\n### Service Selection Matrix\n\n| Service | Pattern | Message Size | Ordering | Transactions | Best For |\n|---------|---------|--------------|----------|--------------|----------|\n| **Service Bus** | Queue/Topic | 256 KB - 100 MB | Yes (sessions) | Yes | Enterprise messaging |\n| **Event Grid** | Pub/Sub | 1 MB | No | No | Event-driven architectures |\n| **Event Hubs** | Streaming | 1 MB | Yes (partitions) | No | Big data ingestion, telemetry |\n| **Storage Queues** | Simple queue | 64 KB | No | No | Async work, <500k msgs/sec |\n\n**When to Use What:**\n- **Service Bus:** Reliable messaging with transactions (e.g., order processing)\n- **Event Grid:** React to Azure resource events (e.g., blob created, VM stopped)\n- **Event Hubs:** High-throughput streaming (e.g., IoT telemetry, application logs)\n\nReference `references/messaging-patterns.md` for implementation examples, retry policies, and dead-letter handling.\n\n## Networking Architecture\n\n### Private Endpoints vs. Service Endpoints\n\n| Aspect | Private Endpoint | Service Endpoint |\n|--------|------------------|------------------|\n| **Security Model** | Private IP in VNet | Optimized route to public endpoint |\n| **Data Exfiltration Protection** | Yes (network-isolated) | Limited (service firewall only) |\n| **Cost** | ~$7.30/month per endpoint | Free |\n| **Recommendation** | Production workloads | Dev/test environments |\n\n**Best Practice:** Use Private Endpoints for all PaaS services in production (treat public endpoints as anti-pattern).\n\n### Hub-and-Spoke Topology\n\n**Components:**\n- **Hub VNet:** Shared services (Azure Firewall, VPN Gateway, Private Endpoints)\n- **Spoke VNets:** Application workloads (isolated per environment or team)\n- **VNet Peering:** Low-latency connectivity between hub and spokes\n\n**Benefits:**\n- Centralized security (firewall, DNS)\n- Cost optimization (shared egress)\n- Simplified governance\n\nReference `references/networking-architecture.md` for hub-spoke Bicep templates, NSG patterns, and DNS configuration.\n\n## Identity and Access Management\n\n### Managed Identity Pattern\n\n**Always use Managed Identity instead of:**\n- Connection strings in code\n- Storage account keys\n- Service principal credentials\n- API keys\n\n**System-Assigned vs. User-Assigned:**\n\n| Type | Lifecycle | Use Case |\n|------|-----------|----------|\n| **System-Assigned** | Tied to resource | Single resource needs access |\n| **User-Assigned** | Independent | Multiple resources share identity |\n\n**Example Flow:**\n1. Enable Managed Identity on Container App\n2. Grant identity access to Key Vault (RBAC or Access Policy)\n3. Application authenticates automatically (no credentials)\n\n```python\nfrom azure.identity import DefaultAzureCredential\n\n# Works automatically with Managed Identity\ncredential = DefaultAzureCredential()\nkeyvault_client = SecretClient(vault_url=\"...\", credential=credential)\n```\n\n### Azure RBAC Best Practices\n\n- Use built-in roles when possible (Owner, Contributor, Reader)\n- Apply least privilege principle\n- Assign roles at resource group level (not subscription)\n- Use Azure AD groups for user management\n- Audit role assignments regularly\n\nReference `references/identity-access.md` for Entra ID integration, Conditional Access policies, and B2C patterns.\n\n## Governance and Compliance\n\n### Azure Policy for Guardrails\n\n**Common Policy Patterns:**\n- Require tags on all resources (Environment, Owner, CostCenter)\n- Restrict allowed Azure regions\n- Enforce TLS 1.2 minimum\n- Require Private Endpoints for storage accounts\n- Deny public IP addresses on VMs\n\n**Policy Effects:**\n- **Deny:** Block non-compliant resource creation\n- **Audit:** Log non-compliance but allow creation\n- **DeployIfNotExists:** Auto-remediate missing configurations\n- **Modify:** Change resource properties during deployment\n\n### Cost Management\n\n**Optimization Strategies:**\n\n| Pattern | Savings | Use Case |\n|---------|---------|----------|\n| **Reserved Instances (1-year)** | 40-50% | Steady-state workloads (databases, VMs) |\n| **Reserved Instances (3-year)** | 60-70% | Long-term commitments |\n| **Spot VMs** | Up to 90% | Fault-tolerant batch processing |\n| **Auto-shutdown** | Variable | Dev/test resources (off-hours) |\n| **Storage lifecycle policies** | 50-90% | Move to Cool/Archive tiers |\n\n**Monitoring:**\n- Set budgets and alerts in Azure Cost Management\n- Review Azure Advisor cost recommendations weekly\n- Tag resources for cost allocation\n- Use FinOps Toolkit for Power BI dashboards\n\nReference `references/governance-compliance.md` for Azure Landing Zones, Policy definitions, and Blueprints.\n\n## Infrastructure as Code\n\n### Tool Selection\n\n| Tool | Best For | Azure Integration | Multi-Cloud |\n|------|----------|-------------------|-------------|\n| **Bicep** | Azure-native projects | Excellent (official) | No |\n| **Terraform** | Multi-cloud environments | Good (azurerm provider) | Yes |\n| **Pulumi** | Developer-first approach | Good (native SDK) | Yes |\n| **Azure CLI** | Scripts and automation | Excellent | No |\n\n**Recommendation:**\n- Use **Bicep** for Azure-only infrastructure (best Azure integration, native type safety)\n- Use **Terraform** for multi-cloud or existing Terraform shops\n- Use **Azure CLI** for quick scripts and CI/CD automation\n\n### Bicep Best Practices\n\n- Use parameter files for environment-specific values\n- Leverage Azure Verified Modules (AVM) for tested patterns\n- Organize by resource lifecycle (networking, data, compute)\n- Use symbolic names (not string interpolation)\n- Enable linting and validation in CI/CD\n\nReference Bicep and Terraform examples in `examples/bicep/` and `examples/terraform/` directories.\n\n## Security Best Practices\n\n### Essential Security Controls\n\n| Control | Implementation | Priority |\n|---------|---------------|----------|\n| **Managed Identity** | Enable on all compute resources | Critical |\n| **Private Endpoints** | All PaaS services in production | Critical |\n| **Key Vault** | Store secrets, keys, certificates | Critical |\n| **Network Segmentation** | NSGs, application security groups | High |\n| **Microsoft Defender** | Enable for all resource types | High |\n| **Azure Policy** | Preventive controls | High |\n| **Just-In-Time Access** | VMs and privileged access | Medium |\n\n### Defense-in-Depth Layers\n\n1. **Network:** Private Endpoints, NSGs, Azure Firewall\n2. **Identity:** Entra ID, Managed Identity, Conditional Access\n3. **Application:** Web Application Firewall, API Management\n4. **Data:** Encryption at rest, encryption in transit (TLS 1.2+)\n5. **Monitoring:** Microsoft Defender, Azure Monitor, Sentinel\n\nReference `references/security-architecture.md` (see also `security-hardening` and `auth-security` skills).\n\n## Cost Estimation\n\n### Pricing Considerations\n\n**Compute:**\n- Container Apps: ~$60/month (1 vCPU, 2GB RAM, 24/7)\n- AKS: ~$400/month (3-node D4s_v5 cluster)\n- App Service P1v3: ~$145/month (2 vCPU, 8GB RAM)\n- Functions Consumption: ~$0.20 per 1M executions\n\n**Storage:**\n- Blob Hot: $0.018/GB/month\n- Blob Cool: $0.010/GB/month\n- Blob Archive: $0.00099/GB/month\n- Managed Disks Premium SSD: $0.15/GB/month\n\n**Database:**\n- Azure SQL Database (2 vCores): ~$280/month\n- Cosmos DB Serverless: Pay per RU consumed\n- PostgreSQL Flexible (2 vCores): ~$125/month\n\n**Use Azure Pricing Calculator:** https://azure.microsoft.com/pricing/calculator/\n\n## Quick Reference Tables\n\n### Compute Service Decision Matrix\n\n| If You Need... | Choose |\n|----------------|--------|\n| Kubernetes features (CRDs, operators) | Azure Kubernetes Service |\n| Microservices without K8s complexity | Azure Container Apps |\n| Event-driven functions (<10 min) | Azure Functions |\n| Traditional web app (Node, .NET, Python) | Azure App Service |\n| Batch processing, HPC | Azure Batch or VM Scale Sets |\n| Legacy application migration | Virtual Machines |\n\n### Storage Service Decision Matrix\n\n| If You Need... | Choose |\n|----------------|--------|\n| SMB file shares | Azure Files |\n| NFS file shares | Azure Files (NFS 4.1) |\n| Object storage (images, backups) | Blob Storage |\n| High-performance file storage | Azure NetApp Files |\n| Block storage for VMs | Managed Disks |\n| Big data analytics | Data Lake Storage Gen2 |\n\n### Database Service Decision Matrix\n\n| If You Need... | Choose |\n|----------------|--------|\n| SQL Server features (T-SQL, SQL Agent) | Azure SQL Database or Managed Instance |\n| PostgreSQL | PostgreSQL Flexible Server |\n| MySQL | MySQL Flexible Server |\n| Global distribution, multi-model | Cosmos DB |\n| In-memory cache | Azure Cache for Redis |\n| Graph database | Cosmos DB (Gremlin API) |\n| Time-series data | Azure Data Explorer |\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n- **infrastructure-as-code:** Implement Azure patterns using Bicep or Terraform\n- **kubernetes-operations:** AKS-specific configuration and operations\n- **deploying-applications:** Container Apps and App Service deployment\n- **building-ci-pipelines:** Azure DevOps and GitHub Actions integration\n- **auth-security:** Entra ID authentication and authorization patterns\n- **observability:** Azure Monitor and Application Insights\n- **ai-chat:** Azure OpenAI Service for chat applications\n- **databases-nosql:** Cosmos DB implementation details\n- **secret-management:** Azure Key Vault integration patterns\n\n## Reference Documentation\n\nFor detailed implementation guidance, see:\n\n- **`references/compute-services.md`** - Container Apps, AKS, Functions, App Service with Bicep/Terraform\n- **`references/storage-patterns.md`** - Blob Storage, Files, Disks, lifecycle management\n- **`references/database-selection.md`** - SQL Database, Cosmos DB, PostgreSQL patterns\n- **`references/ai-integration.md`** - Azure OpenAI, RAG architecture, function calling\n- **`references/messaging-patterns.md`** - Service Bus, Event Grid, Event Hubs examples\n- **`references/networking-architecture.md`** - Hub-spoke, Private Endpoints, DNS configuration\n- **`references/identity-access.md`** - Entra ID, Managed Identity, RBAC\n- **`references/governance-compliance.md`** - Azure Policy, Landing Zones, cost optimization\n- **`references/well-architected.md`** - Five pillars implementation guide\n\n## Code Examples\n\nWorking examples available in:\n\n- **`examples/bicep/`** - Infrastructure templates (Container Apps, AKS, networking, databases)\n- **`examples/terraform/`** - Multi-cloud IaC examples\n- **`examples/sdk/python/`** - Python SDK integration (OpenAI, Managed Identity, messaging)\n- **`examples/sdk/typescript/`** - TypeScript SDK examples\n\n## Additional Resources\n\n- Azure Architecture Center: https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/architecture/\n- Azure Well-Architected Framework: https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/well-architected/\n- Azure Verified Modules: https://aka.ms/avm\n- Azure Charts (Service Comparison): https://azurecharts.com/\n- Azure Updates: https://azure.microsoft.com/updates/\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:02:56.693Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloud Agents requiring expertise in Azure cloud architecture design and deployment following Microsoft''s Well-Architected Framework","zh":"适合需要在 Azure 云架构设计和部署方面具有专业知识的云代理，特别是遵循 Microsoft 的良好架构框架","ja":"Azure クラウドアーキテクチャの設計および展開に特化したクラウドエージェントに適しています。マイクロソフトの Well-Architected フレームワークに従った設計および展開が必要です","ko":"Azure 클라우드 아키텍처 설계 및 배포에 전문 지식이 필요한 클라우드 에이전트에게 적합합니다. Microsoft의 Well-Architected Framework를 따르는 아키텍처 설계 및 배포를 따르는 것이 이상적입니다","es":"Ideal para Agentes de la Nube que requieren experiencia en diseño y implementación de arquitectura de nube de Azure siguiendo el Marco de Arquitectura Bien Diseñada de Microsoft","fr":"Idéal pour les agents cloud nécessitant une expertise en conception et déploiement d''architecture cloud Azure suivant le Cadre d''architecture bien conçu de Microsoft","de":"Ideal für Cloud-Agents, die Expertenwissen in der Gestaltung und Bereitstellung von Azure-Cloud-Architektur nach dem Microsoft-Well-Architected-Framework benötigen","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Nuvem que requerem especialização em design e implantação de arquitetura de nuvem Azure, seguindo o Framework de Arquitetura Bem-Projetada da Microsoft","ru":"Идеально для облачных агентов, требующих экспертизы в области проектирования и развертывания облачной архитектуры Azure, следующей за_frameworkом хорошо спроектированной архитектуры Microsoft","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء السحابيين الذين يتطلبون الخبرة في تصميم وبناء بنية سحابية من Azure، متبعين لإطار عمل Microsoft المعماري الجيد"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design and implement scalable Azure cloud architectures, leveraging best practices for service selection, cost optimization, and security, including integration with Azure OpenAI, Cognitive Services, and messaging patterns using Azure compute services like Container Apps, AKS, Functions, and App Service","zh":"赋予代理设计和实现可扩展的 Azure 云架构的能力，利用服务选择、成本优化和安全的最佳实践，包括与 Azure OpenAI、认知服务以及使用 Azure 计算服务（如容器应用、AKS、函数和应用服务）进行的消息模式集成","ja":"エージェントがスケーラブルな Azure クラウドアーキテクチャを設計および実装できるようにし、サービス選択、コスト最適化、セキュリティのベストプラクティスを活用し、Azure OpenAI、認知サービス、および Azure コンピューティング サービス（コンテナー アプリ、AKS、関数、アプリ サービスなど）を使用したメッセージ パターンの統合を含む","ko":"에이전트가 확장 가능한 Azure 클라우드 아키텍처를 설계하고 구현할 수 있도록 해주며, 서비스 선택, 비용 최적화 및 보안을 위한 최선의 관행을 활용하며, Azure OpenAI, 인지 서비스 및 Azure 컴퓨팅 서비스(컨테이너 앱, AKS, 함수, 앱 서비스 등)를 사용한 메시지 패턴 통합을 포함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a diseñar e implementar arquitecturas de nube de Azure escalables, aprovechando las mejores prácticas para la selección de servicios, la optimización de costos y la seguridad, incluyendo la integración con Azure OpenAI, Cognitive Services y patrones de mensajería utilizando servicios de cálculo de Azure como Container Apps, AKS, Functions y App Service","fr":"Permet aux agents de concevoir et de mettre en œuvre des architectures cloud Azure évolutives, en exploitant les meilleures pratiques pour la sélection de services, l''optimisation des coûts et la sécurité, y compris l''intégration avec Azure OpenAI, Cognitive Services et des modèles de messagerie utilisant des services de calcul Azure tels que Container Apps, AKS, Functions et App Service","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, skalierbare Azure-Cloud-Architekturen zu entwerfen und zu implementieren, indem sie bewährte Verfahren für die Dienstauswahl, die Kostenerfassung und die Sicherheit nutzen, einschließlich der Integration mit Azure OpenAI, Cognitive Services und Messaging-Mustern unter Verwendung von Azure-Computing-Diensten wie Container-Apps, AKS, Functions und App Service","pt":"Habilita os agentes a projetarem e implementarem arquiteturas de nuvem Azure escaláveis, aproveitando as melhores práticas para seleção de serviços, otimização de custos e segurança, incluindo integração com Azure OpenAI, Serviços Cognitivos e padrões de mensagens usando serviços de computação Azure, como Container Apps, AKS, Functions e App Service","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проектировать и реализовывать масштабируемые облачные архитектуры Azure, используя лучшие практики для выбора сервисов, оптимизации затрат и безопасности, включая интеграцию с Azure OpenAI, Когнитивными сервисами и шаблонами обмена сообщениями с помощью сервисов вычислений Azure, таких как Container Apps, AKS, Functions и App Service","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تصميم وتنفيذ هندسة سحابية قابلة للتوسيع من Azure، مستفيدة من أفضل الممارسات لاختيار الخدمات وتحسين التكاليف والأمان، بما في ذلك التكامل مع Azure OpenAI وخدمات الإدراك والأنماط المراسلة باستخدام خدمات الحوسبة من Azure، مثل تطبيقات الحاويات و AKS ووظائف وخدمة التطبيق"},"useCases":{"en":["Architecting secure and cost-optimized storage solutions using Blob Storage, Files, and Cosmos DB","Integrating Azure OpenAI for advanced AI capabilities within cloud applications","Implementing messaging patterns for efficient communication between Azure services"],"zh":["使用 Blob 存储、文件和 Cosmos DB 架构安全且成本优化的存储解决方案","将 Azure OpenAI 集成到云应用程序中以实现高级 AI 能力","实现消息模式以实现 Azure 服务之间的高效通信"],"ja":["Blob ストレージ、ファイル、Cosmos DB を使用してセキュリティとコスト最適化されたストレージ ソリューションを設計する","Azure OpenAI をクラウド アプリケーションに統合して高度な AI 機能を実現する","Azure サービス間の効率的な通信を実現するメッセージ パターンを実装する"],"ko":["Blob 스토리지, 파일, Cosmos DB를 사용하여 보안 및 비용 최적화된 스토리지 솔루션을 아키텍처","Azure OpenAI를 클라우드 애플리케이션에 통합하여 고급 AI 기능을 구현","Azure 서비스 간의 효율적인 통신을 위한 메시지 패턴을 구현"],"es":["Diseñar soluciones de almacenamiento seguras y optimizadas de costos utilizando Blob Storage, Files y Cosmos DB","Integrar Azure OpenAI para capacidades de inteligencia artificial avanzadas dentro de aplicaciones en la nube","Implementar patrones de mensajería para una comunicación eficiente entre los servicios de Azure"],"fr":["Concevoir des solutions de stockage sécurisées et optimisées en termes de coûts en utilisant le stockage d''objets Blob, Files et Cosmos DB","Intégrer Azure OpenAI pour des capacités d''intelligence artificielle avancées au sein d''applications cloud","Mettre en œuvre des modèles de messagerie pour une communication efficace entre les services Azure"],"de":["Entwerfen von sicheren und kostengünstigen Speicherlösungen unter Verwendung von Blob Storage, Dateien und Cosmos DB","Integration von Azure OpenAI für erweiterte KI-Funktionen innerhalb von Cloud-Anwendungen","Implementierung von Messaging-Mustern für eine effiziente Kommunikation zwischen Azure-Diensten"],"pt":["Arquitetar soluções de armazenamento seguras e otimizadas de custos, utilizando Blob Storage, Arquivos e Cosmos DB","Integrar Azure OpenAI para capacidades avançadas de IA dentro de aplicações em nuvem","Implementar padrões de mensagens para comunicação eficiente entre serviços Azure"],"ru":["Проектировать безопасные и оптимизированные по затратам решения для хранения данных, используя Blob Storage, Файлы и Cosmos DB","Интегрировать Azure OpenAI для расширенных возможностей ИИ внутри облачных приложений","Реализовывать шаблоны обмена сообщениями для эффективного взаимодействия между сервисами Azure"],"ar":["تصميم حلول تخزين آمنة ومحسنة التكلفة، باستخدام تخزين Blob وملفات وقاعدة بيانات Cosmos","دمج Azure OpenAI للقدرات المتقدمة من ذكاء الاصطناعي داخل التطبيقات السحابية","تنفيذ أنماط مراسلة لتواصل فعال بين خدمات Azure"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Microsoft Azure subscription","Knowledge of Microsoft''s Well-Architected Framework is necessary","Familiarity with Azure services such as Container Apps, AKS, Functions, and App Service is recommended"],"zh":["需要 Microsoft Azure 订阅","需要了解 Microsoft 的 Well-Architected Framework","建议熟悉 Azure 服务，例如容器应用、AKS、函数和应用服务"],"ja":["Microsoft Azure サブスクリプションが必要","Microsoft の Well-Architected フレームワークの知識が必要","コンテナー アプリ、AKS、関数、アプリ サービスなどの Azure サービスの知識が推奨される"],"ko":["Microsoft Azure 구독이 필요","Microsoft의 Well-Architected Framework에 대한 지식이 필요","컨테이너 앱, AKS, 함수, 앱 서비스 등과 같은 Azure 서비스에 대한 지식이 권장됨"],"es":["Requiere una suscripción a Microsoft Azure","El conocimiento del Marco de Arquitectura Bien Diseñada de Microsoft es necesario","Se recomienda familiaridad con los servicios de Azure como Container Apps, AKS, Functions y App Service"],"fr":["Nécessite un abonnement Microsoft Azure","La connaissance du Cadre d''architecture bien conçu de Microsoft est nécessaire","Il est recommandé d''avoir une connaissance des services Azure tels que Container Apps, AKS, Functions et App Service"],"de":["Benötigt ein Abonnement für Microsoft Azure","Kenntnisse des Microsoft-Well-Architected-Frameworks sind erforderlich","Vertrautheit mit Azure-Diensten wie Container-Apps, AKS, Functions und App Service wird empfohlen"],"pt":["Exige assinatura do Microsoft Azure","Conhecimento do Framework de Arquitetura Bem-Projetada da Microsoft é necessário","Familiaridade com serviços Azure, como Container Apps, AKS, Functions e App Service, é recomendada"],"ru":["Требует подписки на Microsoft Azure","Знание фреймворка хорошо спроектированной архитектуры Microsoft является необходимым","Знакомство с сервисами Azure, такими как Container Apps, AKS, Functions и App Service, рекомендуется"],"ar":["يتطلب اشتراكًا في Microsoft Azure","معرفة إطار عمل Microsoft المعماري الجيد ضرورية","الاطلاع على خدمات Azure، مثل تطبيقات الحاويات و AKS ووظائف وخدمة التطبيق، يوصى به"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
