s fallidas completas siguiendo principios de TDD Red para definir comportamiento esperado","fr":"Écrivez des tests échoués complets suivant les principes de TDD Red pour définir le comportement attendu","de":"Schreiben Sie umfassende fehlende Tests nach TDD-Red-Prinzipien, um erwartetes Verhalten zu definieren","pt":"O TDD Workflows é um sistema de orquestração de agentes para criar testes falhos abrangentes seguindo os princípios da fase vermelha do TDD.","ru":"TDD Workflows - это система оркестровки агентов для создания всесторонних неудачных тестов, следующих принципам красной фазы TDD.","ar":"سير عمل TDD هو نظام لإدارة العوامل لإنشاء اختبارات فاشلة شاملة متبعة مبادئ المرحلة الحمراء من TDD.","en":"Sistema de orquestación de agentes para Claude Code - Transforma ideas en MVPs funcionales"},"definition":{"en":"Sistema de orquestación de agentes para Claude Code - Transforma ideas en MVPs funcionales"},"features":{"zh":["生成失败测试以定义预期行为","实现边缘情况覆盖","支持TDD红色阶段测试","提高测试效率","简化测试过程"],"ja":["失敗テストを生成して予想される動作を定義","エッジケースのカバーを実現","TDDレッドフェーズのテストをサポート","テストの効率を向上","テストプロセスを簡素化"],"ko":["실패 테스트를 생성하여 예상 동작을 정의","엣지 케이스 커버리지를 구현","TDD 레드 단계 테스트를 지원","테스트 효율성을 향상","테스트 프로세스를 간소화"],"es":["Genera pruebas fallidas que capturan comportamiento esperado","Cobertura de casos de borde antes de la implementación","Se utiliza en la fase roja de TDD para nuevo comportamiento","No se utiliza en las fases verde o refactor","No se utiliza para benchmarks de rendimiento"],"fr":["Générez des tests échoués qui capturent le comportement attendu","Couverture des cas de bord avant la mise en œuvre","Utilisé dans la phase rouge de TDD pour un nouveau comportement","Non utilisé dans les phases verte ou refactor","Non utilisé pour les benchmarks de performance"],"de":["Erzeugen Sie fehlende Tests, die erwartetes Verhalten erfassen","Abdeckung von Randfällen vor der Implementierung","Wird in der TDD-Rot-Phase für neues Verhalten verwendet","Wird nicht in den Phasen Grün oder Refactor verwendet","Wird nicht für Leistungsbenchmarks verwendet"],"pt":["Criação de testes falhos abrangentes","Seguimento dos princípios da fase vermelha do TDD","Cobertura de teste antes da implementação","Melhoria da qualidade do código","Redução de bugs e erros"],"ru":["Создание всесторонних неудачных тестов","Следование принципам красной фазы TDD","Тестовое покрытие до реализации","Улучшение качества кода","Снижение багов и ошибок"],"ar":["إنشاء اختبارات فاشلة شاملة","متابعة مبادئ المرحلة الحمراء من TDD","تغطية اختبار قبل التنفيذ","تحسين جودة الكود","تقليل الأخطاء والعيوب"]},"keywords":{"zh":["TDD","测试驱动开发","红色阶段测试","失败测试","预期行为","边缘情况覆盖","测试效率","测试过程"],"ja":["TDD","テスト駆動開発","レッドフェーズのテスト","失敗テスト","予想される動作","エッジケースのカバー","テストの効率","テストプロセス"],"ko":["TDD","테스트 주도 개발","레드 단계 테스트","실패 테스트","예상 동작","엣지 케이스 커버리지","테스트 효율성","테스트 프로세스"],"es":["TDD","pruebas fallidas","desarrollo de software","MVP","principios de TDD Red","casos de borde","implementación","benchmarks de rendimiento"],"fr":["TDD","tests échoués","développement de logiciels","MVP","principes de TDD Red","cas de bord","mise en œuvre","benchmarks de performance"],"de":["TDD","fehlende Tests","Software-Entwicklung","MVP","TDD-Red-Prinzipien","Randfälle","Implementierung","Leistungsbenchmarks"],"pt":["TDD","Test-Driven Development","Testes Falhos","Fase Vermelha","Cobertura de Teste","Qualidade do Código","Desenvolvimento de Software"],"ru":["TDD","Test-Driven Development","Неудачные Тесты","Красная Фаза","Тестовое Покрытие","Качество Код","Разработка Программного Обеспечения"],"ar":["TDD","Test-Driven Development","اختبارات فاشلة","المرحلة الحمراء","تغطية اختبار","جودة الكود","تطوير البرمجيات"]}},"owner":"vjrivmon","repo":"Setup-Software-IA","repoPath":"vjrivmon/Setup-Software-IA","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.474Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"tdd-workflows-tdd-red","description":"Generate failing tests for the TDD red phase to define expected behavior and edge cases.","bodyPreview":"Write comprehensive failing tests following TDD red phase principles.\n\n[Extended thinking: Generates failing tests that properly define expected behavior using test-automator agent.]\n\n## Use this skill when\n\n- Starting the TDD red phase for new behavior\n- You need failing tests that capture expected behavior\n- You want edge case coverage before implementation\n\n## Do not use this skill when\n\n- You are in the green or refactor phase\n- You only need performance benchmarks\n- Tests must run against p","body":"Write comprehensive failing tests following TDD red phase principles.\n\n[Extended thinking: Generates failing tests that properly define expected behavior using test-automator agent.]\n\n## Use this skill when\n\n- Starting the TDD red phase for new behavior\n- You need failing tests that capture expected behavior\n- You want edge case coverage before implementation\n\n## Do not use this skill when\n\n- You are in the green or refactor phase\n- You only need performance benchmarks\n- Tests must run against production systems\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Identify behaviors, constraints, and edge cases.\n2. Generate failing tests that define expected outcomes.\n3. Ensure failures are due to missing behavior, not setup errors.\n4. Document how to run tests and verify failures.\n\n## Safety\n\n- Keep test data isolated and avoid production environments.\n- Avoid flaky external dependencies in the red phase.\n\n## Role\n\nGenerate failing tests using Task tool with subagent_type=\"unit-testing::test-automator\".\n\n## Prompt Template\n\n\"Generate comprehensive FAILING tests for: $ARGUMENTS\n\n## Core Requirements\n\n1. **Test Structure**\n   - Framework-appropriate setup (Jest/pytest/JUnit/Go/RSpec)\n   - Arrange-Act-Assert pattern\n   - should_X_when_Y naming convention\n   - Isolated fixtures with no interdependencies\n\n2. **Behavior Coverage**\n   - Happy path scenarios\n   - Edge cases (empty, null, boundary values)\n   - Error handling and exceptions\n   - Concurrent access (if applicable)\n\n3. **Failure Verification**\n   - Tests MUST fail when run\n   - Failures for RIGHT reasons (not syntax/import errors)\n   - Meaningful diagnostic error messages\n   - No cascading failures\n\n4. **Test Categories**\n   - Unit: Isolated component behavior\n   - Integration: Component interaction\n   - Contract: API/interface contracts\n   - Property: Mathematical invariants\n\n## Framework Patterns\n\n**JavaScript/TypeScript (Jest/Vitest)**\n- Mock dependencies with `vi.fn()` or `jest.fn()`\n- Use `@testing-library` for React components\n- Property tests with `fast-check`\n\n**Python (pytest)**\n- Fixtures with appropriate scopes\n- Parametrize for multiple test cases\n- Hypothesis for property-based tests\n\n**Go**\n- Table-driven tests with subtests\n- `t.Parallel()` for parallel execution\n- Use `testify/assert` for cleaner assertions\n\n**Ruby (RSpec)**\n- `let` for lazy loading, `let!` for eager\n- Contexts for different scenarios\n- Shared examples for common behavior\n\n## Quality Checklist\n\n- Readable test names documenting intent\n- One behavior per test\n- No implementation leakage\n- Meaningful test data (not ''foo''/''bar'')\n- Tests serve as living documentation\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n\n- Tests passing immediately\n- Testing implementation vs behavior\n- Complex setup code\n- Multiple responsibilities per test\n- Brittle tests tied to specifics\n\n## Edge Case Categories\n\n- **Null/Empty**: undefined, null, empty string/array/object\n- **Boundaries**: min/max values, single element, capacity limits\n- **Special Cases**: Unicode, whitespace, special characters\n- **State**: Invalid transitions, concurrent modifications\n- **Errors**: Network failures, timeouts, permissions\n\n## Output Requirements\n\n- Complete test files with imports\n- Documentation of test purpose\n- Commands to run and verify failures\n- Metrics: test count, coverage areas\n- Next steps for green phase\"\n\n## Validation\n\nAfter generation:\n1. Run tests - confirm they fail\n2. Verify helpful failure messages\n3. Check test independence\n4. Ensure comprehensive coverage\n\n## Example (Minimal)\n\n```typescript\n// auth.service.test.ts\ndescribe(''AuthService'', () => {\n  let authService: AuthService;\n  let mockUserRepo: jest.Mocked<UserRepository>;\n\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    mockUserRepo = { findByEmail: jest.fn() } as any;\n    authService = new AuthService(mockUserRepo);\n  });\n\n  it(''should_return_token_when_valid_credentials'', async () => {\n    const user = { id: ''1'', email: ''test@example.com'', passwordHash: ''hashed'' };\n    mockUserRepo.findByEmail.mockResolvedValue(user);\n\n    const result = await authService.authenticate(''test@example.com'', ''pass'');\n\n    expect(result.success).toBe(true);\n    expect(result.token).toBeDefined();\n  });\n\n  it(''should_fail_when_user_not_found'', async () => {\n    mockUserRepo.findByEmail.mockResolvedValue(null);\n\n    const result = await authService.authenticate(''none@example.com'', ''pass'');\n\n    expect(result.success).toBe(false);\n    expect(result.error).toBe(''INVALID_CREDENTIALS'');\n  });\n});\n```\n\nTest requirements: $ARGUMENTS\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:06:04.441Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Test-Driven Development Agents needing automated test generation and validation following TDD red phase principles.","zh":"非常适合需要自动化测试生成和验证的测试驱动开发代理，遵循TDD红色阶段原则。","ja":"テスト駆動開発エージェントがTDDレッドフェーズの原則に従って自動テスト生成と検証を行う場合に最適です。","ko":"TDD 레드 페이즈 nguyên칙에 따라 자동화된 테스트 생성 및 검증이 필요한 테스트 주도 개발 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de Desarrollo Dirigido por Pruebas que necesitan generación y validación de pruebas automatizadas siguiendo los principios de la fase roja de TDD.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de Développement Piloté par les Tests ayant besoin de génération et de validation de tests automatisés suivant les principes de la phase rouge de TDD.","de":"Perfekt für Test-Driven Development-Agenten, die automatisierte Testgenerierung und -validierung nach TDD-Rot-Phase-Prinzipien benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Desenvolvimento Orientado a Testes que necessitam de geração e validação automatizada de testes seguindo os princípios da fase vermelha do TDD.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов разработки через тестирование (TDD), которым требуется автоматизированное создание и проверка тестов в соответствии с принципами фазы красного цвета TDD.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء التطوير القائم على الاختبارات الذين يحتاجون إلى إنشاء وتحقق آلي من الاختبارات باتباع مبادئ مرحلة الأحمر في TDD."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to write comprehensive failing tests that capture expected behavior, utilizing test-automator agents for edge case coverage and defining expected behavior using TDD red phase principles, including test automation and validation protocols.","zh":"赋予代理编写全面的失败测试以捕获预期行为，利用测试自动化代理进行边缘情况覆盖，并使用TDD红色阶段原则定义预期行为，包括测试自动化和验证协议。","ja":"エージェントが包括的な失敗テストを記述して期待される動作を捉え、テスト自動化エージェントを使用してエッジケースのカバレッジを行い、TDDレッドフェーズの原則を使用して期待される動作を定義することを可能にし、テスト自動化と検証プロトコルを含む。","ko":"에이전트가 포함된 실패 테스트를 작성하여 예상된 동작을 캡처하고 테스트 자동화 에이전트를 사용하여 에지 케이스 커버리지를 수행하며 TDD 레드 페이즈 원칙을 사용하여 예상 동작을 정의하고 테스트 자동화 및 검증 프로토콜을 포함합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a escribir pruebas comprehensivas que capturan el comportamiento esperado, utilizando agentes automatizadores de pruebas para la cobertura de casos límite y definiendo el comportamiento esperado utilizando los principios de la fase roja de TDD, incluyendo protocolos de automatización y validación de pruebas.","fr":"Habilite les agents à écrire des tests complets qui capturent le comportement attendu, en utilisant des agents automatisateurs de tests pour la couverture des cas limite et en définissant le comportement attendu en utilisant les principes de la phase rouge de TDD, y compris les protocoles d''automatisation et de validation des tests.","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, umfassende fehlschlagende Tests zu schreiben, die das erwartete Verhalten erfassen, indem Testautomatisierungs-Agents für die Abdeckung von Randfällen und die Definition des erwarteten Verhaltens unter Verwendung der TDD-Rot-Phase-Prinzipien verwendet werden, einschließlich Testautomatisierungs- und Validierungsprotokolle.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a escrever testes de falha abrangentes que capturem o comportamento esperado, utilizando agentes de automação de testes para cobertura de casos de borda e definindo o comportamento esperado usando os princípios da fase vermelha do TDD, incluindo automação de testes e protocolos de validação.","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать комплексные провальные тесты, которые фиксируют ожидаемое поведение, используя агентов-автоматизаторов тестов для покрытия граничных случаев и определяя ожидаемое поведение с помощью принципов фазы красного цвета TDD, включая автоматизацию тестирования и протоколы валидации.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من كتابة اختبارات فشل شاملة تلتقط السلوك المتوقع، باستخدام وكلاء أتمتة الاختبارات لتغطية الحالات الحدية وتحديد السلوك المتوقع باستخدام مبادئ مرحلة الأحمر في TDD، بما في ذلك أتمتة الاختبارات وبروتوكولات التحقق."},"useCases":{"en":["Automating test creation for new features","Generating failing tests for edge case coverage","Validating expected behavior before implementation"],"zh":["为新功能自动创建测试","为边缘情况覆盖生成失败测试","在实现之前验证预期行为"],"ja":["新しい機能のテスト自動化","エッジケースのカバレッジのための失敗テストの生成","実装前に期待される動作の検証"],"ko":["새로운 기능에 대한 테스트 자동화","에지 케이스 커버리지를 위한 실패 테스트 생성","구현 전에 예상 동작의 검증"],"es":["Automatización de la creación de pruebas para nuevas características","Generación de pruebas fallidas para la cobertura de casos límite","Validación del comportamiento esperado antes de la implementación"],"fr":["Automatisation de la création de tests pour les nouvelles fonctionnalités","Génération de tests échoués pour la couverture des cas limite","Validation du comportement attendu avant la mise en œuvre"],"de":["Automatisierung der Testerstellung für neue Funktionen","Generierung fehlschlagender Tests für die Abdeckung von Randfällen","Validierung des erwarteten Verhaltens vor der Implementierung"],"pt":["Automatização da criação de testes para novas funcionalidades","Geração de testes de falha para cobertura de casos de borda","Validação do comportamento esperado antes da implementação"],"ru":["Автоматизация создания тестов для новых функций","Создание провальных тестов для покрытия граничных случаев","Проверка ожидаемого поведения до реализации"],"ar":["أتمتة إنشاء الاختبارات للميزات الجديدة","إنشاء اختبارات فشل لتغطية الحالات الحدية","التحقق من السلوك المتوقع قبل التنفيذ"]},"limitations":{"en":["Only applicable during the TDD red phase","Not suitable for performance benchmarks","Requires integration with test-automator agents"],"zh":["仅适用于TDD红色阶段","不适用于性能基准测试","需要与测试自动化代理集成"],"ja":["TDDレッドフェーズでのみ使用可能","パフォーマンスベンチマークには不向き","テスト自動化エージェントとの統合が必要"],"ko":["TDD 레드 페이즈에서만 사용 가능","성능 벤치마크에는 적합하지 않음","테스트 자동화 에이전트와의 통합이 필요"],"es":["Solo aplicable durante la fase roja de TDD","No adecuado para benchmarks de rendimiento","Requiere integración con agentes automatizadores de pruebas"],"fr":["N''est applicable qu''au cours de la phase rouge de TDD","Non adapté aux benchmarks de performance","Nécessite une intégration avec des agents automatisateurs de tests"],"de":["Nur während der TDD-Rot-Phase anwendbar","Nicht geeignet für Leistungsbenchmarks","Benötigt Integration mit Testautomatisierungs-Agents"],"pt":["Aplicável apenas durante a fase vermelha do TDD","Não é adequado para benchmarks de desempenho","Requer integração com agentes de automação de testes"],"ru":["Применимо только во время фазы красного цвета TDD","Не подходит для производительности (бенчмаркинга)","Требует интеграции с агентами-автоматизаторами тестов"],"ar":["يُطبق فقط خلال مرحلة الأحمر في TDD","غير مناسب لمعايير الأداء","يتطلب التكامل مع وكلاء أتمتة الاختبارات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('FlorinSenoner/the-dahan-codex/ui-ux-pro-max', 'community', 'FlorinSenoner', 'the-dahan-codex', 'FlorinSenoner/the-dahan-codex', 'ui-ux-pro-max', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.474Z', '2026-02-18T09:05:53.900Z', NULL, '{"id":"FlorinSenoner/the-dahan-codex/ui-ux-pro-max","name":"ui-ux-pro-max","description":{"zh":"UI/UX Pro Max是一份全面设计指南，包含50+样式、97色板、57字体组合、99 UX指南和25种图表类型，适用于9种技术栈","ja":"UI/UX Pro Maxは、50以上のスタイル、97のカラーパレット、57のフォントの組み合わせ、99のUXガイドライン、25種類のチャートタイプを含む、9つのテクノロジースタックに対応した包括的なデザインガイドです","ko":"UI/UX Pro Max는 50개 이상의 스타일, 97개의 색상 팔레트, 57개의 글꼴 조합, 99개의 UX 가이드라인 및 25가지 차트 유형을 포함하는 9가지 기술 스택을 위한 포괄적인 디자인 가이드입니다","es":"UI/UX Pro Max es una guía de diseño integral para aplicaciones web y móviles con estilos, paletas de colores y pautas de UX.","fr":"UI/UX Pro Max est un guide de conception complet pour les applications web et mobiles avec des styles, des palettes de couleurs et des directives d''UX.","de":"UI/UX Pro Max ist eine umfassende Design-Anleitung für Web- und Mobile-Anwendungen mit Stilen, Farbpaletten und UX-Richtlinien.","pt":"O UI/UX Pro Max é uma ferramenta de design inteligente para aplicações web e móveis, oferecendo 50+ estilos e 97 paletas de cores.","ru":"UI/UX Pro Max - это всесторонний гид по дизайну для веб- и мобильных приложений, включающий 50+ стилей и 97 цветовых палитр.","ar":"UI/UX Pro Max هو أداة التصميم الذكية لتطبيقات الويب والموبايل، ويوفر 50+ نمطًا و 97 لوحة ألوان","en":"Spirit Island companion app — offline-first spirit library, opening guides, and game tracker"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"UI/UX Pro Max - 设计智能指南","ja":"UI/UX Pro Max - デザインインテリジェンス","ko":"UI/UX Pro Max - 디자인 인텔리전스","es":"UI/UX Pro Max: Diseño Inteligente para Aplicaciones","fr":"UI/UX Pro Max : Intelligence de Conception pour Applications","de":"UI/UX Pro Max: Design-Intelligenz für Anwendungen","pt":"UI/UX Pro Max: Guia de Design Inteligente","ru":"UI/UX Pro Max: Всесторонний гид по дизайну","ar":"UI/UX Pro Max: دليل التصميم الذكي","en":"ui-ux-pro-max"},"description":{"zh":"UI/UX Pro Max是一份全面设计指南，包含50+样式、97色板、57字体组合、99 UX指南和25种图表类型，适用于9种技术栈","ja":"UI/UX Pro Maxは、50以上のスタイル、97のカラーパレット、57のフォントの組み合わせ、99のUXガイドライン、25種類のチャートタイプを含む、9つのテクノロジースタックに対応した包括的なデザインガイドです","ko":"UI/UX Pro Max는 50개 이상의 스타일, 97개의 색상 팔레트, 57개의 글꼴 조합, 99개의 UX 가이드라인 및 25가지 차트 유형을 포함하는 9가지 기술 스택을 위한 포괄적인 디자인 가이드입니다","es":"UI/UX Pro Max es una guía de diseño integral para aplicaciones web y móviles con estilos, paletas de colores y pautas de UX.","fr":"UI/UX Pro Max est un guide de conception complet pour les applications web et mobiles avec des styles, des palettes de couleurs et des directives d''UX.","de":"UI/UX Pro Max ist eine umfassende Design-Anleitung für Web- und Mobile-Anwendungen mit Stilen, Farbpaletten und UX-Richtlinien.","pt":"O UI/UX Pro Max é uma ferramenta de design inteligente para aplicações web e móveis, oferecendo 50+ estilos e 97 paletas de cores.","ru":"UI/UX Pro Max - это всесторонний гид по дизайну для веб- и мобильных приложений, включающий 50+ стилей и 97 цветовых палитр.","ar":"UI/UX Pro Max هو أداة التصميم الذكية لتطبيقات الويب والموبايل، ويوفر 50+ نمطًا و 97 لوحة ألوان","en":"Spirit Island companion app — offline-first spirit library, opening guides, and game tracker"},"definition":{"en":"Spirit Island companion app — offline-first spirit library, opening guides, and game tracker"},"features":{"zh":["50+样式","97色板","57字体组合","99 UX指南","25种图表类型","优化UX体验"],"ja":["50以上のスタイル","97のカラーパレット","57のフォントの組み合わせ","99のUXガイドライン","25種類のチャートタイプ","UX体験の最適化"],"ko":["50개 이상의 스타일","97개의 색상 팔레트","57개의 글꼴 조합","99개의 UX 가이드라인","25가지 차트 유형","UX 경험 최적화"],"es":["50+ estilos de diseño","97 paletas de colores","57 combinaciones de fuentes","99 pautas de UX","25 tipos de gráficos"],"fr":["50+ styles de conception","97 palettes de couleurs","57 combinaisons de polices","99 directives d''UX","25 types de graphiques"],"de":["50+ Design-Stile","97 Farbpaletten","57 Schriftkombinationen","99 UX-Richtlinien","25 Chart-Typen"],"pt":["50+ estilos de design","97 paletas de cores","57 combinações de fontes","99 diretrizes de UX","25 tipos de gráficos"],"ru":["50+ стилей дизайна","97 цветовых палитр","57 пар.font","99 руководств по UX","25 типов графиков"],"ar":["50+ نمطًا من التصميم","97 لوحة ألوان","57 زوجًا من الخطوط","99 إرشادًا لتحسين تجربة المستخدم","25 نوعًا من الرسومات البيانية"]},"keywords":{"zh":["UI设计","UX设计","设计智能","设计指南","技术栈","颜色选择","字体选择","UX优化"],"ja":["UIデザイン","UXデザイン","デザインインテリジェンス","デザインガイドライン","テクノロジースタック","色の選択","フォントの選択","UXの最適化"],"ko":["UI 디자인","UX 디자인","디자인 인텔리전스","디자인 가이드라인","기술 스택","색상 선택","글꼴 선택","UX 최적화"],"es":["diseño de aplicaciones","UX/UI","estilos de diseño","paletas de colores","pautas de UX","desarrollo web","desarrollo móvil","diseño integral"],"fr":["conception d''applications","UX/UI","styles de conception","palettes de couleurs","directives d''UX","développement web","développement mobile","conception complète"],"de":["Anwendungsdesign","UX/UI","Design-Stile","Farbpaletten","UX-Richtlinien","Web-Entwicklung","Mobile-Entwicklung","umfassendes Design"],"pt":["design de UI","design de UX","ferramenta de design","aplicações web","aplicações móveis","estilos de design","paletas de cores","combinações de fontes"],"ru":["дизайн UI","дизайн UX","инструмент дизайна","веб-приложения","мобильные приложения","стили дизайна","цветовые палитры","пары.font"],"ar":["تصميم الواجهة","تصميم تجربة المستخدم","أداة التصميم","تطبيقات الويب","تطبيقات الموبايل","أنماط التصميم","لوحات الألوان","أزواج الخطوط"]}},"owner":"FlorinSenoner","repo":"the-dahan-codex","repoPath":"FlorinSenoner/the-dahan-codex","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.474Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"ui-ux-pro-max","description":"","bodyPreview":"# UI/UX Pro Max - Design Intelligence\n\nComprehensive design guide for web and mobile applications. Contains 50+ styles, 97 color palettes,\n57 font pairings, 99 UX guidelines, and 25 chart types across 9 technology stacks. Searchable\ndatabase with priority-based recommendations.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n\n- Designing new UI components or pages\n- Choosing color palettes and typography\n- Reviewing code for UX issues\n- Building landing pages or dashboards\n- Implementing acc","body":"# UI/UX Pro Max - Design Intelligence\n\nComprehensive design guide for web and mobile applications. Contains 50+ styles, 97 color palettes,\n57 font pairings, 99 UX guidelines, and 25 chart types across 9 technology stacks. Searchable\ndatabase with priority-based recommendations.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n\n- Designing new UI components or pages\n- Choosing color palettes and typography\n- Reviewing code for UX issues\n- Building landing pages or dashboards\n- Implementing accessibility requirements\n\n## Rule Categories by Priority\n\n| Priority | Category            | Impact   | Domain                |\n| -------- | ------------------- | -------- | --------------------- |\n| 1        | Accessibility       | CRITICAL | `ux`                  |\n| 2        | Touch & Interaction | CRITICAL | `ux`                  |\n| 3        | Performance         | HIGH     | `ux`                  |\n| 4        | Layout & Responsive | HIGH     | `ux`                  |\n| 5        | Typography & Color  | MEDIUM   | `typography`, `color` |\n| 6        | Animation           | MEDIUM   | `ux`                  |\n| 7        | Style Selection     | MEDIUM   | `style`, `product`    |\n| 8        | Charts & Data       | LOW      | `chart`               |\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n### 1. Accessibility (CRITICAL)\n\n- `color-contrast` - Minimum 4.5:1 ratio for normal text\n- `focus-states` - Visible focus rings on interactive elements\n- `alt-text` - Descriptive alt text for meaningful images\n- `aria-labels` - aria-label for icon-only buttons\n- `keyboard-nav` - Tab order matches visual order\n- `form-labels` - Use label with for attribute\n\n### 2. Touch & Interaction (CRITICAL)\n\n- `touch-target-size` - Minimum 44x44px touch targets\n- `hover-vs-tap` - Use click/tap for primary interactions\n- `loading-buttons` - Disable button during async operations\n- `error-feedback` - Clear error messages near problem\n- `cursor-pointer` - Add cursor-pointer to clickable elements\n\n### 3. Performance (HIGH)\n\n- `image-optimization` - Use WebP, srcset, lazy loading\n- `reduced-motion` - Check prefers-reduced-motion\n- `content-jumping` - Reserve space for async content\n\n### 4. Layout & Responsive (HIGH)\n\n- `viewport-meta` - width=device-width initial-scale=1\n- `readable-font-size` - Minimum 16px body text on mobile\n- `horizontal-scroll` - Ensure content fits viewport width\n- `z-index-management` - Define z-index scale (10, 20, 30, 50)\n\n### 5. Typography & Color (MEDIUM)\n\n- `line-height` - Use 1.5-1.75 for body text\n- `line-length` - Limit to 65-75 characters per line\n- `font-pairing` - Match heading/body font personalities\n\n### 6. Animation (MEDIUM)\n\n- `duration-timing` - Use 150-300ms for micro-interactions\n- `transform-performance` - Use transform/opacity, not width/height\n- `loading-states` - Skeleton screens or spinners\n\n### 7. Style Selection (MEDIUM)\n\n- `style-match` - Match style to product type\n- `consistency` - Use same style across all pages\n- `no-emoji-icons` - Use SVG icons, not emojis\n\n### 8. Charts & Data (LOW)\n\n- `chart-type` - Match chart type to data type\n- `color-guidance` - Use accessible color palettes\n- `data-table` - Provide table alternative for accessibility\n\n## How to Use\n\nSearch specific domains using the CLI tool below.\n\n---\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nCheck if Python is installed:\n\n```bash\npython3 --version || python --version\n```\n\nIf Python is not installed, install it based on user''s OS:\n\n**macOS:**\n\n```bash\nbrew install python3\n```\n\n**Ubuntu/Debian:**\n\n```bash\nsudo apt update && sudo apt install python3\n```\n\n**Windows:**\n\n```powershell\nwinget install Python.Python.3.12\n```\n\n---\n\n## How to Use This Skill\n\nWhen user requests UI/UX work (design, build, create, implement, review, fix, improve), follow this\nworkflow:\n\n### Step 1: Analyze User Requirements\n\nExtract key information from user request:\n\n- **Product type**: SaaS, e-commerce, portfolio, dashboard, landing page, etc.\n- **Style keywords**: minimal, playful, professional, elegant, dark mode, etc.\n- **Industry**: healthcare, fintech, gaming, education, etc.\n- **Stack**: React, Vue, Next.js, or default to `html-tailwind`\n\n### Step 2: Generate Design System (REQUIRED)\n\n**Always start with `--design-system`** to get comprehensive recommendations with reasoning:\n\n```bash\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"<product_type> <industry> <keywords>\" --design-system [-p \"Project Name\"]\n```\n\nThis command:\n\n1. Searches 5 domains in parallel (product, style, color, landing, typography)\n2. Applies reasoning rules from `ui-reasoning.csv` to select best matches\n3. Returns complete design system: pattern, style, colors, typography, effects\n4. Includes anti-patterns to avoid\n\n**Example:**\n\n```bash\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"beauty spa wellness service\" --design-system -p \"Serenity Spa\"\n```\n\n### Step 2b: Persist Design System (Master + Overrides Pattern)\n\nTo save the design system for **hierarchical retrieval across sessions**, add `--persist`:\n\n```bash\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"<query>\" --design-system --persist -p \"Project Name\"\n```\n\nThis creates:\n\n- `design-system/MASTER.md` — Global Source of Truth with all design rules\n- `design-system/pages/` — Folder for page-specific overrides\n\n**With page-specific override:**\n\n```bash\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"<query>\" --design-system --persist -p \"Project Name\" --page \"dashboard\"\n```\n\nThis also creates:\n\n- `design-system/pages/dashboard.md` — Page-specific deviations from Master\n\n**How hierarchical retrieval works:**\n\n1. When building a specific page (e.g., \"Checkout\"), first check `design-system/pages/checkout.md`\n2. If the page file exists, its rules **override** the Master file\n3. If not, use `design-system/MASTER.md` exclusively\n\n**Context-aware retrieval prompt:**\n\n```\nI am building the [Page Name] page. Please read design-system/MASTER.md.\nAlso check if design-system/pages/[page-name].md exists.\nIf the page file exists, prioritize its rules.\nIf not, use the Master rules exclusively.\nNow, generate the code...\n```\n\n### Step 3: Supplement with Detailed Searches (as needed)\n\nAfter getting the design system, use domain searches to get additional details:\n\n```bash\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"<keyword>\" --domain <domain> [-n <max_results>]\n```\n\n**When to use detailed searches:**\n\n| Need                  | Domain       | Example                                 |\n| --------------------- | ------------ | --------------------------------------- |\n| More style options    | `style`      | `--domain style \"glassmorphism dark\"`   |\n| Chart recommendations | `chart`      | `--domain chart \"real-time dashboard\"`  |\n| UX best practices     | `ux`         | `--domain ux \"animation accessibility\"` |\n| Alternative fonts     | `typography` | `--domain typography \"elegant luxury\"`  |\n| Landing structure     | `landing`    | `--domain landing \"hero social-proof\"`  |\n\n### Step 4: Stack Guidelines (Default: html-tailwind)\n\nGet implementation-specific best practices. If user doesn''t specify a stack, **default to\n`html-tailwind`**.\n\n```bash\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"<keyword>\" --stack html-tailwind\n```\n\nAvailable stacks: `html-tailwind`, `react`, `nextjs`, `vue`, `svelte`, `swiftui`, `react-native`,\n`flutter`, `shadcn`, `jetpack-compose`\n\n---\n\n## Search Reference\n\n### Available Domains\n\n| Domain       | Use For                              | Example Keywords                                         |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `product`    | Product type recommendations         | SaaS, e-commerce, portfolio, healthcare, beauty, service |\n| `style`      | UI styles, colors, effects           | glassmorphism, minimalism, dark mode, brutalism          |\n| `typography` | Font pairings, Google Fonts          | elegant, playful, professional, modern                   |\n| `color`      | Color palettes by product type       | saas, ecommerce, healthcare, beauty, fintech, service    |\n| `landing`    | Page structure, CTA strategies       | hero, hero-centric, testimonial, pricing, social-proof   |\n| `chart`      | Chart types, library recommendations | trend, comparison, timeline, funnel, pie                 |\n| `ux`         | Best practices, anti-patterns        | animation, accessibility, z-index, loading               |\n| `react`      | React/Next.js performance            | waterfall, bundle, suspense, memo, rerender, cache       |\n| `web`        | Web interface guidelines             | aria, focus, keyboard, semantic, virtualize              |\n| `prompt`     | AI prompts, CSS keywords             | (style name)                                             |\n\n### Available Stacks\n\n| Stack             | Focus                                                 |\n| ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `html-tailwind`   | Tailwind utilities, responsive, a11y (DEFAULT)        |\n| `react`           | State, hooks, performance, patterns                   |\n| `nextjs`          | SSR, routing, images, API routes                      |\n| `vue`             | Composition API, Pinia, Vue Router                    |\n| `svelte`          | Runes, stores, SvelteKit                              |\n| `swiftui`         | Views, State, Navigation, Animation                   |\n| `react-native`    | Components, Navigation, Lists                         |\n| `flutter`         | Widgets, State, Layout, Theming                       |\n| `shadcn`          | shadcn/ui components, theming, forms, patterns        |\n| `jetpack-compose` | Composables, Modifiers, State Hoisting, Recomposition |\n\n---\n\n## Example Workflow\n\n**User request:** \"Làm landing page cho dịch vụ chăm sóc da chuyên nghiệp\"\n\n### Step 1: Analyze Requirements\n\n- Product type: Beauty/Spa service\n- Style keywords: elegant, professional, soft\n- Industry: Beauty/Wellness\n- Stack: html-tailwind (default)\n\n### Step 2: Generate Design System (REQUIRED)\n\n```bash\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"beauty spa wellness service elegant\" --design-system -p \"Serenity Spa\"\n```\n\n**Output:** Complete design system with pattern, style, colors, typography, effects, and\nanti-patterns.\n\n### Step 3: Supplement with Detailed Searches (as needed)\n\n```bash\n# Get UX guidelines for animation and accessibility\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"animation accessibility\" --domain ux\n\n# Get alternative typography options if needed\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"elegant luxury serif\" --domain typography\n```\n\n### Step 4: Stack Guidelines\n\n```bash\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"layout responsive form\" --stack html-tailwind\n```\n\n**Then:** Synthesize design system + detailed searches and implement the design.\n\n---\n\n## Output Formats\n\nThe `--design-system` flag supports two output formats:\n\n```bash\n# ASCII box (default) - best for terminal display\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"fintech crypto\" --design-system\n\n# Markdown - best for documentation\npython3 skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \"fintech crypto\" --design-system -f markdown\n```\n\n---\n\n## Tips for Better Results\n\n1. **Be specific with keywords** - \"healthcare SaaS dashboard\" > \"app\"\n2. **Search multiple times** - Different keywords reveal different insights\n3. **Combine domains** - Style + Typography + Color = Complete design system\n4. **Always check UX** - Search \"animation\", \"z-index\", \"accessibility\" for common issues\n5. **Use stack flag** - Get implementation-specific best practices\n6. **Iterate** - If first search doesn''t match, try different keywords\n\n---\n\n## Common Rules for Professional UI\n\nThese are frequently overlooked issues that make UI look unprofessional:\n\n### Icons & Visual Elements\n\n| Rule                       | Do                                              | Don''t                                  |\n| -------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| **No emoji icons**         | Use SVG icons (Heroicons, Lucide, Simple Icons) | Use emojis like 🎨 🚀 ⚙️ as UI icons   |\n| **Stable hover states**    | Use color/opacity transitions on hover          | Use scale transforms that shift layout |\n| **Correct brand logos**    | Research official SVG from Simple Icons         | Guess or use incorrect logo paths      |\n| **Consistent icon sizing** | Use fixed viewBox (24x24) with w-6 h-6          | Mix different icon sizes randomly      |\n\n### Interaction & Cursor\n\n| Rule                   | Do                                                    | Don''t                                        |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| **Cursor pointer**     | Add `cursor-pointer` to all clickable/hoverable cards | Leave default cursor on interactive elements |\n| **Hover feedback**     | Provide visual feedback (color, shadow, border)       | No indication element is interactive         |\n| **Smooth transitions** | Use `transition-colors duration-200`                  | Instant state changes or too slow (>500ms)   |\n\n### Light/Dark Mode Contrast\n\n| Rule                      | Do                                  | Don''t                                   |\n| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| **Glass card light mode** | Use `bg-white/80` or higher opacity | Use `bg-white/10` (too transparent)     |\n| **Text contrast light**   | Use `#0F172A` (slate-900) for text  | Use `#94A3B8` (slate-400) for body text |\n| **Muted text light**      | Use `#475569` (slate-600) minimum   | Use gray-400 or lighter                 |\n| **Border visibility**     | Use `border-gray-200` in light mode | Use `border-white/10` (invisible)       |\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n\n| Rule                     | Do                                  | Don''t                                  |\n| ------------------------ | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| **Floating navbar**      | Add `top-4 left-4 right-4` spacing  | Stick navbar to `top-0 left-0 right-0` |\n| **Content padding**      | Account for fixed navbar height     | Let content hide behind fixed elements |\n| **Consistent max-width** | Use same `max-w-6xl` or `max-w-7xl` | Mix different container widths         |\n\n---\n\n## Pre-Delivery Checklist\n\nBefore delivering UI code, verify these items:\n\n### Visual Quality\n\n- [ ] No emojis used as icons (use SVG instead)\n- [ ] All icons from consistent icon set (Heroicons/Lucide)\n- [ ] Brand logos are correct (verified from Simple Icons)\n- [ ] Hover states don''t cause layout shift\n- [ ] Use theme colors directly (bg-primary) not var() wrapper\n\n### Interaction\n\n- [ ] All clickable elements have `cursor-pointer`\n- [ ] Hover states provide clear visual feedback\n- [ ] Transitions are smooth (150-300ms)\n- [ ] Focus states visible for keyboard navigation\n\n### Light/Dark Mode\n\n- [ ] Light mode text has sufficient contrast (4.5:1 minimum)\n- [ ] Glass/transparent elements visible in light mode\n- [ ] Borders visible in both modes\n- [ ] Test both modes before delivery\n\n### Layout\n\n- [ ] Floating elements have proper spacing from edges\n- [ ] No content hidden behind fixed navbars\n- [ ] Responsive at 375px, 768px, 1024px, 1440px\n- [ ] No horizontal scroll on mobile\n\n### Accessibility\n\n- [ ] All images have alt text\n- [ ] Form inputs have labels\n- [ ] Color is not the only indicator\n- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` respected\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:05:53.900Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Design-focused Agents needing comprehensive UI/UX guidelines and recommendations for web and mobile applications","zh":"非常适合需要全面UI/UX指南和网页及移动应用推荐的设计导向型代理","ja":"デザイン中心のエージェントがWebおよびモバイルアプリケーションに対する包括的なUI/UXガイドラインと推奨事項を必要とする場合に最適","ko":"디자인 중심 에이전트가 웹 및 모바일 애플리케이션에 대한 포괄적인 UI/UX 가이드라인과 추천을 필요로 할 때 적합","es":"Perfecto para agentes enfocados en diseño que necesitan directrices y recomendaciones de UI/UX comprehensivas para aplicaciones web y móviles","fr":"Parfait pour les agents axés sur la conception nécessitant des lignes directrices et des recommandations UI/UX complètes pour les applications Web et mobiles","de":"Perfekt für designorientierte Agenten, die umfassende UI/UX-Richtlinien und Empfehlungen für Web- und Mobile-Anwendungen benötigen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes focados em Design que precisam de diretrizes e recomendações abrangentes de UI/UX para aplicações web e móveis","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов, ориентированных на дизайн, которым необходимы всесторонние руководящие принципы и рекомендации по UI/UX для веб- и мобильных приложений","ar":"مثالي لعميل التركيز على التصميم الذي يحتاج إلى إرشادات وتوصيات شاملة لويب وتطبيقات الجوال"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to create visually appealing and user-friendly interfaces by leveraging 50+ styles, 97 color palettes, and 57 font pairings, while ensuring UX consistency with 99 guidelines and 25 chart types across 9 technology stacks, utilizing searchable databases with priority-based recommendations","zh":"通过利用50+样式、97个颜色调色板和57个字体配对，同时确保99个指南和25种图表类型在9个技术栈中保持UX的一致性，并利用可搜索的数据库提供基于优先级的推荐，从而使代理能够创建视觉上吸引人和用户友好的界面","ja":"50以上のスタイル、97のカラーパレット、57のフォントペアを利用し、9つのテクノロジースタックにわたって99のガイドラインと25種類のチャートタイプを使用してUXの一貫性を確保し、検索可能なデータベースを使用して優先度ベースの推奨を行うことで、エージェントが視覚的に魅力的でユーザーフレンドリーなインターフェイスを作成できるようにする","ko":"50개 이상의 스타일, 97개의 색상 팔레트, 57개의 폰트 페어를 활용하여 9개의 기술 스택에 걸쳐 99개의 가이드라인과 25종류의 차트 타입을 사용하여 UX的一致성을 보장하고, 검색 가능한 데이터베이스를 사용하여 우선순위 기반의 추천을 제공함으로써 에이전트가 시각적으로 매력적이고 사용자 친화적인 인터페이스를 만들 수 있도록 함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a crear interfaces visualmente atractivas y fáciles de usar mediante el aprovechamiento de más de 50 estilos, 97 paletas de colores y 57 combinaciones de fuentes, garantizando la consistencia de la UX con 99 directrices y 25 tipos de gráficos en 9 pilas tecnológicas, utilizando bases de datos buscables con recomendaciones basadas en prioridad","fr":"Permet aux agents de créer des interfaces visuellement attrayantes et conviviales en exploitant plus de 50 styles, 97 palettes de couleurs et 57 appariements de polices, tout en assurant la cohérence de l''UX avec 99 lignes directrices et 25 types de graphiques sur 9 piles technologiques, en utilisant des bases de données recherchables avec des recommandations basées sur la priorité","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, visuell ansprechende und benutzerfreundliche Schnittstellen zu erstellen, indem sie 50+ Stile, 97 Farbpaletten und 57 Schriftkombinationen nutzen und dabei die UX-Konsistenz mit 99 Richtlinien und 25 Charttypen über 9 Technologiestacks sicherstellen, unter Verwendung von durchsuchbaren Datenbanken mit prioritätsbasierten Empfehlungen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a criar interfaces visualmente atraentes e amigáveis ao usuário, aproveitando 50+ estilos, 97 paletas de cores e 57 combinações de fontes, garantindo a consistência da UX com 99 diretrizes e 25 tipos de gráficos em 9 pilhas de tecnologia, utilizando bancos de dados pesquisáveis com recomendações baseadas em prioridade","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью создавать визуально привлекательные и удобные для пользователя интерфейсы, используя 50+ стилей, 97 цветовых палитр и 57 парных шрифтов, обеспечивая согласованность UX с 99 руководящими принципами и 25 типами графиков на 9 технологических стеках, используя поисковые базы данных с рекомендациями, основанными на приоритете","ar":"تمكّن الوكيل من إنشاء واجهات مستخدم جذابة وبدينة من الناحية البصرية عن طريق استخدام أكثر من 50 نمطًا و97 لوحة ألوان و57 زوجًا من الخطوط، مع ضمان الاتساق في تجربة المستخدم مع 99 إرشادية و25 نوعًا من الرسوم البيانية عبر 9 مجموعات تقنية، باستخدام قواعد بيانات قابلة للبحث مع توصيات تقوم على الأسبقية"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing new UI components or pages with optimized typography and color schemes","Reviewing code for UX issues and implementing improvements based on 99 UX guidelines","Building landing pages or dashboards with consistent branding and user experience"],"zh":["设计新的UI组件或页面，优化字体排版和颜色方案","审查代码中的UX问题并根据99个UX指南实施改进","构建具有统一品牌和用户体验的着陆页或仪表盘"],"ja":["最適化されたタイポグラフィとカラースキームを持つ新しいUIコンポーネントまたはページを設計する","コード内のUXの問題点を確認し、99のUXガイドラインに基づいて改善を実施する","一貫したブランディングとユーザーエクスペリエンスを持つランディングページまたはダッシュボードを構築する"],"ko":["최적화된 타이포그래피와 색상 스키마를 갖춘 새로운 UI 컴포넌트 또는 페이지를 설계","코드 내의 UX 문제를 검토하고 99개의 UX 가이드라인에 따라 개선을 구현","일관된 브랜딩과 사용자 경험을 갖춘 랜딩 페이지 또는 대시보드를 구축"],"es":["Diseñar nuevos componentes de UI o páginas con tipografía y esquemas de color optimizados","Revisar el código para problemas de UX y implementar mejoras en función de las 99 directrices de UX","Crear páginas de aterrizaje o paneles de control con marca y experiencia de usuario coherentes"],"fr":["Concevoir de nouveaux composants UI ou des pages avec une typographie et des schémas de couleur optimisés","Réviser le code pour les problèmes d''UX et mettre en œuvre des améliorations sur la base des 99 lignes directrices d''UX","Créer des pages de destination ou des tableaux de bord avec une marque et une expérience utilisateur cohérentes"],"de":["Neue UI-Komponenten oder Seiten mit optimierter Typografie und Farbschemata entwerfen","Code auf UX-Probleme überprüfen und Verbesserungen auf der Grundlage der 99 UX-Richtlinien umsetzen","Landingpages oder Dashboards mit konsistenter Marken- und Benutzererfahrung erstellen"],"pt":["Projetar novos componentes de UI ou páginas com tipografia e esquemas de cor otimizados","Revisar código para problemas de UX e implementar melhorias com base em 99 diretrizes de UX","Construir páginas de destino ou painéis com marcação e experiência do usuário consistentes"],"ru":["Проектировать новые компоненты UI или страницы с оптимизированной типографией и цветовыми схемами","Проверять код на наличие проблем с UX и реализовывать улучшения на основе 99 руководящих принципов UX","Создавать страницы приземления или панели с согласованной брендингом и пользовательским опытом"],"ar":["تصميم مكونات واجهة المستخدم أو صفحات جديدة مع طباعة وتخطيط ألوان محسّن","مراجعة الشفرة لمشاكل تجربة المستخدم وتنفيذ تحسينات بناءً على 99 إرشادية لتجربة المستخدم","بناء صفحات هبوط أو لوحات تحكم مع علامة تجارية وتجربة مستخدم متسقة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to a searchable database for priority-based recommendations","Limited to 9 supported technology stacks"],"zh":["需要访问可搜索的数据库以获得基于优先级的推荐","仅限于9个支持的技术栈"],"ja":["優先度ベースの推奨を行うために検索可能なデータベースへのアクセスが必要","9つのサポート対象テクノロジースタックに限定される"],"ko":["우선순위 기반의 추천을 받기 위해 검색 가능한 데이터베이스에 대한 액세스가 필요","9개의 지원 기술 스택으로 제한됨"],"es":["Requiere acceso a una base de datos buscable para recomendaciones basadas en prioridad","Limitado a 9 pilas tecnológicas admitidas"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès à une base de données recherchable pour des recommandations basées sur la priorité","Limité à 9 piles technologiques prises en charge"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf eine durchsuchbare Datenbank für prioritätsbasierte Empfehlungen","Begrenzt auf 9 unterstützte Technologiestacks"],"pt":["Requer acesso a um banco de dados pesquisável para recomendações baseadas em prioridade","Limitado a 9 pilhas de tecnologia suportadas"],"ru":["Требует доступа к поисковому базе данных для рекомендаций, основанных на приоритете","Ограничен 9 поддерживаемыми технологическими стеками"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى قاعدة بيانات قابلة للبحث لتوصيات تقوم على الأسبقية","محدود ب 9 مجموعات تقنية مدعومة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":75}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('bardway/mingriAgency/mingri-coc7-knowledgebase-maintenance', 'community', 'bardway', 'mingriAgency', 'bardway/mingriAgency', 'mingri-coc7-knowledgebase-maintenance', 0, 0, 50, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.474Z', '2026-02-18T09:06:16.530Z', NULL, '{"id":"bardway/mingriAgency/mingri-coc7-knowledgebase-maintenance","name":"mingri-coc7-knowledgebase-maintenance","description":{"zh":"CoC7 知识库维护技能，保持数据、类型定义、loader钩子和缓存策略的一致性","ja":"CoC7 ナレッジベースメンテナンススキルは、データ、タイプ定義、ローダー フック、キャッシュ戦略の一貫性を保つ","ko":"CoC7 지식베이스 유지 관리 스킬은 데이터, 유형 정의, 로더 후크 및 캐싱 전략의 일관성을 유지","es":"Mantén la base de conocimientos de CoC7 actualizada y consistente a través de la normalización y deduplicación de datos","fr":"Maintenez la base de connaissances CoC7 à jour et cohérente grâce à la normalisation et la déduplication des données","de":"Halten Sie die CoC7-Wissensbasis aktuell und konsistent durch Normalisierung und Deduplizierung von Daten","pt":"A manutenção da base de conhecimento CoC7 é crucial para garantir a consistência dos dados em todo o sistema.","ru":"Техническое обслуживание базы знаний CoC7 имеет важное значение для обеспечения согласованности данных во всей системе.","ar":"صيانة قاعدة المعارف CoC7 ضرورية لضمان συνέفات البيانات في جميع أنحاء النظام.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"CoC7 知识库维护 - 保持一致性","ja":"CoC7 ナレッジベースメンテナンス - 一貫性を保つ","ko":"CoC7 지식베이스 유지 관리 - 일관성을 유지","es":"Mantenimiento de la base de conocimientos de CoC7","fr":"Maintenance de la base de connaissances CoC7","de":"Wartung der CoC7-Wissensbasis","pt":"Manutenção de Conhecimento CoC7","ru":"Техническое обслуживание базы знаний CoC7","ar":"صيانة قاعدة المعارف CoC7","en":"mingri-coc7-knowledgebase-maintenance"},"description":{"zh":"CoC7 知识库维护技能，保持数据、类型定义、loader钩子和缓存策略的一致性","ja":"CoC7 ナレッジベースメンテナンススキルは、データ、タイプ定義、ローダー フック、キャッシュ戦略の一貫性を保つ","ko":"CoC7 지식베이스 유지 관리 스킬은 데이터, 유형 정의, 로더 후크 및 캐싱 전략의 일관성을 유지","es":"Mantén la base de conocimientos de CoC7 actualizada y consistente a través de la normalización y deduplicación de datos","fr":"Maintenez la base de connaissances CoC7 à jour et cohérente grâce à la normalisation et la déduplication des données","de":"Halten Sie die CoC7-Wissensbasis aktuell und konsistent durch Normalisierung und Deduplizierung von Daten","pt":"A manutenção da base de conhecimento CoC7 é crucial para garantir a consistência dos dados em todo o sistema.","ru":"Техническое обслуживание базы знаний CoC7 имеет важное значение для обеспечения согласованности данных во всей системе.","ar":"صيانة قاعدة المعارف CoC7 ضرورية لضمان συνέفات البيانات في جميع أنحاء النظام.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["保持数据一致性","同步类型定义","优化缓存策略","维护loader钩子","更新辅助设备数据"],"ja":["データの一貫性を保つ","タイプ定義の同期","キャッシュ戦略の最適化","ローダー フックのメンテナンス","補助装置データの更新"],"ko":["데이터 일관성을 유지","유형 정의의 동기화","캐싱 전략의 최적화","로더 후크의 유지 보수","보조 장비 데이터의 업데이트"],"es":["Actualización de entradas de la base de conocimientos","Normalización y deduplicación de datos","Optimización del rendimiento de carga de datos","Actualización de conjuntos de datos de equipo auxiliar"],"fr":["Mise à jour des entrées de la base de connaissances","Normalisation et déduplication des données","Optimisation des performances de chargement des données","Mise à jour des ensembles de données d''équipement auxiliaire"],"de":["Aktualisierung von Einträgen in der Wissensbasis","Normalisierung und Deduplizierung von Daten","Optimierung der Ladeleistung von Daten","Aktualisierung von Datensätzen für Hilfsequipment"],"pt":["Manutenção de arquivos JSON","Definições TypeScript","Hooks de carregamento","Estratégia de cache","Normalização de dados"],"ru":["Техническое обслуживание файлов JSON","Определения TypeScript","Хуки загрузки","Стратегия кэширования","Нормализация данных"],"ar":["صيانة ملفات JSON","definitions TypeScript","hooks للتحميل","استراتيجية التخزين المؤقت","تنظيم البيانات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["CoC7","知识库维护","数据一致性","类型定义","缓存策略","loader钩子","辅助设备数据"],"ja":["CoC7","ナレッジベースメンテナンス","データの一貫性","タイプ定義","キャッシュ戦略","ローダー フック","補助装置データ"],"ko":["CoC7","지식베이스 유지 관리","데이터 일관성","유형 정의","캐싱 전략","로더 후크","보조 장비 데이터"],"es":["mantenimiento de base de conocimientos","CoC7","normalización de datos","deduplicación de datos","optimización de rendimiento","desarrollo de software","bases de datos"],"fr":["maintenance de base de connaissances","CoC7","normalisation de données","déduplication de données","optimisation des performances","développement de logiciels","bases de données"],"de":["Wartung der Wissensbasis","CoC7","Normalisierung von Daten","Deduplizierung von Daten","Optimierung der Leistung","Software-Entwicklung","Datenbanken"],"pt":["manutenção de conhecimento","CoC7","arquivos JSON","definições TypeScript","hooks de carregamento","estratégia de cache","normalização de dados"],"ru":["техническое обслуживание базы знаний","CoC7","файлы JSON","определения TypeScript","хуки загрузки","стратегия кэширования","нормализация данных"],"ar":["صيانة قاعدة المعارف","CoC7","ملفات JSON","definitions TypeScript","hooks للتحميل","استراتيجية التخزين المؤقت","تنظيم البيانات"]}},"owner":"bardway","repo":"mingriAgency","repoPath":"bardway/mingriAgency","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.474Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"mingri-coc7-knowledgebase-maintenance","description":"For Mingri project: maintain CoC7 knowledgebase JSON data files, types, and loader hooks; ensure caching/paths remain correct.","bodyPreview":"# Purpose\n\nKeep the CoC7 knowledgebase consistent across:\n\n- `data/*.json` source files\n- TypeScript definitions (`src/types/...`)\n- loader hooks (e.g., `useCoc7Data` or equivalent)\n- caching strategy and path invariants\n\n# Use when\n\n- Adding/updating knowledgebase entries (rules/skills/occupations/etc.)\n- Normalizing or deduplicating knowledgebase data\n- Fixing data load performance or caching behavior\n- Updating auxiliary equipment datasets (weapons/armor/vehicles/etc.)\n\n# Inputs expected\n\n- `","body":"# Purpose\n\nKeep the CoC7 knowledgebase consistent across:\n\n- `data/*.json` source files\n- TypeScript definitions (`src/types/...`)\n- loader hooks (e.g., `useCoc7Data` or equivalent)\n- caching strategy and path invariants\n\n# Use when\n\n- Adding/updating knowledgebase entries (rules/skills/occupations/etc.)\n- Normalizing or deduplicating knowledgebase data\n- Fixing data load performance or caching behavior\n- Updating auxiliary equipment datasets (weapons/armor/vehicles/etc.)\n\n# Inputs expected\n\n- `docs/COC7_KNOWLEDGE_GUIDE.md`\n- knowledgebase data directory\n- loader hooks and related types\n\n# Workflow\n\n## 0) Read the guide (required)\n\nRead:\n\n- `docs/COC7_KNOWLEDGE_GUIDE.md`\n\n## 1) Data edits with invariants\n\n- Keep file names and paths stable unless the guide explicitly allows changes.\n- Maintain consistent IDs/keys if referenced elsewhere.\n- For large datasets, avoid duplicating entries; prefer shared references where the system supports it.\n\n## 2) Types and consumers\n\n- Update TypeScript types if the shape changes.\n- Ensure loaders handle optional/missing fields with defaults (unless breaking change is intended).\n\n## 3) Regression\n\n- Verify at least:\n  - knowledgebase loads without errors\n  - rulebook pages dependent on datasets render\n  - quick find covers newly added items (if relevant)\n\n# Output requirements (must output)\n\n- files edited (data + types)\n- invariants checked (paths/ids/caching)\n- regression steps + key pages tested\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:06:16.530Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for TypeScript Agents needing advanced knowledgebase maintenance and data consistency across JSON files and loader hooks.","zh":"适用于需要高级知识库维护和跨JSON文件和加载钩子的数据一致性的TypeScript代理。","ja":"TypeScriptエージェントが高度なナレッジベースのメンテナンスとJSONファイルやローダー・フックのデータの一貫性を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"고급 지식베이스 유지관리 및 JSON 파일 및 로더 훅을 통한 데이터 일관성을 필요로하는 TypeScript 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de TypeScript que necesitan un mantenimiento avanzado de la base de conocimientos y la consistencia de los datos a través de archivos JSON y ganchos de carga.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents TypeScript ayant besoin d''une maintenance avancée de la base de connaissances et de la cohérence des données à travers des fichiers JSON et des crochets de chargement.","de":"Perfekt für TypeScript-Agents, die ein fortgeschrittenes Wissensmanagement und Datenkonsistenz über JSON-Dateien und Lader-Hooks benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes TypeScript que necessitam de manutenção avançada da base de conhecimento e consistência de dados em arquivos JSON e ganchos de carregamento.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов TypeScript, которым требуется продвинутая поддержка базы знаний и согласованность данных в файлах JSON и загрузочных крючках.","ar":"مثالي لعميل TypeScript الذي يحتاج إلى صيانة متقدمة لقاعدة المعرفة ومتوافقة مع البيانات عبر الملفات JSON و Hooks التحميل."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to maintain consistency across data sources, TypeScript definitions, and caching strategies, utilizing JSON files and loader hooks like `useCoc7Data`, ensuring data integrity and performance optimization through path invariants and caching behavior updates.","zh":"赋予代理维护数据源、TypeScript定义和缓存策略的一致性，利用JSON文件和加载钩子，如`useCoc7Data`，确保通过路径不变性和缓存行为更新来实现数据完整性和性能优化。","ja":"エージェントがデータ・ソース、TypeScript定義、キャッシュ・ストラテジーの一貫性を維持できるようにし、JSONファイルやローダー・フック(`useCoc7Data`など)を利用してデータの完全性とパフォーマンスの最適化を実現します。","ko":"에이전트가 데이터 소스, TypeScript 정의 및 캐싱 전략의 일관성을 유지할 수 있도록 해주며, JSON 파일 및 로더 훅(`useCoc7Data` 등)을 사용하여 데이터 무결성 및 성능 최적화를 실현합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a mantener la consistencia a través de fuentes de datos, definiciones de TypeScript y estrategias de caché, utilizando archivos JSON y ganchos de carga como `useCoc7Data`, garantizando la integridad de los datos y la optimización del rendimiento a través de invariantes de ruta y actualizaciones del comportamiento de caché.","fr":"Permet aux agents de maintenir la cohérence à travers les sources de données, les définitions TypeScript et les stratégies de mise en cache, en utilisant des fichiers JSON et des crochets de chargement comme `useCoc7Data`, en garantissant l''intégrité des données et l''optimisation des performances via des invariants de chemin et des mises à jour du comportement de cache.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Konsistenz über Datenquellen, TypeScript-Definitionen und Cachestrategien hinweg zu gewährleisten, indem JSON-Dateien und Lader-Hooks wie `useCoc7Data` verwendet werden, um Datenintegrität und Leistungsoptimierung durch Pfadinvarianten und Cacheverhaltensaktualisierungen sicherzustellen.","pt":"Concede poderes aos agentes para manter a consistência em todas as fontes de dados, definições TypeScript e estratégias de cache, utilizando arquivos JSON e ganchos de carregamento como `useCoc7Data`, garantindo a integridade dos dados e a otimização do desempenho por meio de invariantes de caminho e atualizações de comportamento de cache.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью поддерживать согласованность всех источников данных, определений TypeScript и стратегий кэширования, используя файлы JSON и загрузочные крючки, такие как `useCoc7Data`, обеспечивая целостность данных и оптимизацию производительности за счет обновления поведения кэша и инвариантов пути.","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من الحفاظ على التماسك عبر جميع مصادر البيانات والتعريفات و استراتيجيات التخزين المؤقت، باستخدام الملفات JSON وHooks التحميل مثل `useCoc7Data` ، مما يضمن سلامة البيانات وتحسين الأداء من خلال تحديث سلوك التخزين المؤقت وثوابت المسار."},"useCases":{"en":["Updating knowledgebase entries for rules and skills","Normalizing and deduplicating knowledgebase data","Fixing data load performance issues and caching behavior","Updating auxiliary equipment datasets"],"zh":["更新规则和技能的知识库条目","规范化和去重知识库数据","修复数据加载性能问题和缓存行为","更新辅助设备数据集"],"ja":["ルールとスキルのナレッジベースのエントリを更新する","ナレッジベースのデータを正規化し、重複を削除する","データの読み込み性能の問題とキャッシュの動作を修正する","補助装置のデータセットを更新する"],"ko":["규칙 및 스킬의 지식베이스 항목을 업데이트하는 것","지식베이스 데이터를 정규화하고 중복을 제거하는 것","데이터 로드 성능 문제 및 캐싱 동작을 수정하는 것","보조 장비 데이터셋을 업데이트하는 것"],"es":["Actualización de entradas de base de conocimientos para reglas y habilidades","Normalización y eliminación de duplicados de datos de base de conocimientos","Solución de problemas de rendimiento de carga de datos y comportamiento de caché","Actualización de conjuntos de datos de equipos auxiliares"],"fr":["Mise à jour des entrées de base de connaissances pour les règles et les compétences","Normalisation et élimination des doublons de données de base de connaissances","Résolution des problèmes de performances de chargement de données et de comportement de cache","Mise à jour des ensembles de données d''équipements auxiliaires"],"de":["Aktualisierung von Wissensbasiseinträgen für Regeln und Fähigkeiten","Normalisierung und Entfernung von Dubletten von Wissensbasidaten","Behebung von Datenladeleistungsproblemen und Cacheverhalten","Aktualisierung von Hilfsgerte-Datensätzen"],"pt":["Atualizar entradas da base de conhecimento para regras e habilidades","Normalizar e deduplicar dados da base de conhecimento","Corrigir problemas de desempenho de carregamento de dados e comportamento de cache","Atualizar conjuntos de dados de equipamentos auxiliares"],"ru":["Обновление записей базы знаний для правил и навыков","Нормализация и удаление дубликатов данных базы знаний","Исправление проблем с производительностью загрузки данных и поведением кэша","Обновление наборов данных вспомогательного оборудования"],"ar":["تحديث إدخالات قاعدة المعرفة للقواعد والمهارات","تطبيع وإزالة التكرارات من بيانات قاعدة المعرفة","تصحيح مشاكل أداء تحميل البيانات وسلوك التخزين المؤقت","تحديث مجموعات بيانات المعدات المساعدة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to `data/*.json` source files and `src/types/` definitions","TypeScript environment needed","Knowledge of CoC7 knowledgebase structure and caching strategy required"],"zh":["需要访问`data/*.json`源文件和`src/types/`定义","需要TypeScript环境","需要了解CoC7知识库结构和缓存策略"],"ja":["`data/*.json`ソース・ファイルと`src/types/`定義へのアクセスが必要","TypeScript環境が必要","CoC7ナレッジベースの構造とキャッシュ・ストラテジーについての知識が必要"],"ko":["`data/*.json` 소스 파일 및 `src/types/` 정의에 대한 액세스가 필요합니다","TypeScript 환경이 필요합니다","CoC7 지식베이스 구조 및 캐싱 전략에 대한 지식이 필요합니다"],"es":["Requiere acceso a archivos fuente `data/*.json` y definiciones `src/types/`","Entorno de TypeScript necesario","Conocimiento de la estructura de base de conocimientos de CoC7 y estrategia de caché requerido"],"fr":["Nécessite l''accès aux fichiers source `data/*.json` et aux définitions `src/types/`","Environnement TypeScript nécessaire","Connaissance de la structure de base de connaissances de CoC7 et de la stratégie de cache requise"],"de":["Erfordert Zugriff auf Quelldateien `data/*.json` und Definitionen `src/types/`","TypeScript-Umgebung erforderlich","Kenntnisse der CoC7-Wissensbasenstruktur und Cachestrategie erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer acesso aos arquivos de origem `data/*.json` e definições `src/types/`","Ambiente TypeScript necessário","Conhecimento da estrutura da base de conhecimento CoC7 e estratégia de cache necessário"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к исходным файлам `data/*.json` и определениям `src/types/`","Необходимо окружение TypeScript","Требуется знание структуры базы знаний CoC7 и стратегии кэширования"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الملفات المصدر `data/*.json` والتعريفات `src/types/`","بيئة TypeScript ضرورية","مطلوب معرفة هيكل قاعدة المعرفة CoC7 و استراتيجية التخزين المؤقت"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('roderik/mpe/rams', 'community', 'roderik', 'mpe', 'roderik/mpe', 'rams', 0, 0, 70, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.474Z', '2026-02-18T09:07:04.458Z', NULL, '{"id":"roderik/mpe/rams","name":"rams","description":{"zh":"Rams 是一个用于管理配置的工具，支持本地和网络集成。它可以分析文件并提供可访问性和视觉设计的反馈","ja":"Rams は設定を管理するツールです。ローカルと Web の両方で設定を管理できます。また、ファイルを分析してアクセシビリティと視覚的なデザインについてのフィードバックを提供します","ko":"Rams는 설정을 관리하는 도구로, 로컬과 웹에서 설정을 관리할 수 있습니다. 또한 파일을 분석하여 접근성과 시각적 디자인에 대한 피드백을 제공합니다","es":"Rams es una herramienta de revisión de diseño que analiza la accesibilidad y el diseño visual de los componentes, ayudando a los equipos a mejorar la experiencia del usuario","fr":"Rams est un outil d''examen de conception qui analyse l''accessibilité et la conception visuelle des composants, aidant les équipes à améliorer l''expérience utilisateur","de":"Rams ist ein Design-Review-Tool, das die Barrierefreiheit und das visuelle Design von Komponenten analysiert, um Teams bei der Verbesserung der Benutzererfahrung zu unterstützen","pt":"Rams é uma ferramenta de revisão de design que ajuda desenvolvedores a identificar problemas de acessibilidade e design visual em seus projetos.","ru":"Rams - это инструмент для проверки дизайна, который помогает разработчикам выявить проблемы доступности и визуального дизайна в своих проектах.","ar":"Rams هي أداة مراجعة التصميم التي تساعد المطورين على تحديد مشاكل إمكانية الوصول والتصميم المرئي في مشاريعهم.","en":"An experiment to manage claude and codex configs for a team, locally and on the web"},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"Rams 配置管理工具","ja":"Rams 設定管理ツール","ko":"Rams 설정 관리 도구","es":"Rams: Herramienta de revisión de diseño para accesibilidad","fr":"Rams : Outil d''examen de conception pour l''accessibilité","de":"Rams: Design-Review-Tool für Barrierefreiheit","pt":"Rams: Ferramenta de Revisão de Design para Desenvolvedores","ru":"Rams: Инструмент для проверки дизайна для разработчиков","ar":"Rams: أداة مراجعة التصميم للمانحين","en":"rams"},"description":{"zh":"Rams 是一个用于管理配置的工具，支持本地和网络集成。它可以分析文件并提供可访问性和视觉设计的反馈","ja":"Rams は設定を管理するツールです。ローカルと Web の両方で設定を管理できます。また、ファイルを分析してアクセシビリティと視覚的なデザインについてのフィードバックを提供します","ko":"Rams는 설정을 관리하는 도구로, 로컬과 웹에서 설정을 관리할 수 있습니다. 또한 파일을 분석하여 접근성과 시각적 디자인에 대한 피드백을 제공합니다","es":"Rams es una herramienta de revisión de diseño que analiza la accesibilidad y el diseño visual de los componentes, ayudando a los equipos a mejorar la experie...","fr":"Rams est un outil d''examen de conception qui analyse l''accessibilité et la conception visuelle des composants, aidant les équipes à améliorer l''expérience ut...","de":"Rams ist ein Design-Review-Tool, das die Barrierefreiheit und das visuelle Design von Komponenten analysiert, um Teams bei der Verbesserung der Benutzererfah...","pt":"Rams é uma ferramenta de revisão de design que ajuda desenvolvedores a identificar problemas de acessibilidade e design visual em seus projetos.","ru":"Rams - это инструмент для проверки дизайна, который помогает разработчикам выявить проблемы доступности и визуального дизайна в своих проектах.","ar":"Rams هي أداة مراجعة التصميم التي تساعد المطورين على تحديد مشاكل إمكانية الوصول والتصميم المرئي في مشاريعهم.","en":"An experiment to manage claude and codex configs for a team, locally and on the web"},"definition":{"en":"An experiment to manage claude and codex configs for a team, locally and on the web"},"features":{"zh":["配置管理","本地和网络集成","文件分析","可访问性反馈","视觉设计反馈"],"ja":["設定管理","ローカルと Web の統合","ファイル分析","アクセシビリティ フィードバック","視覚的なデザイン フィードバック"],"ko":["설정 관리","로컬과 웹 통합","파일 분석","접근성 피드백","시각적 디자인 피드백"],"es":["Análisis de accesibilidad según WCAG 2.1","Revisión de diseño visual para componentes","Gestión de configuraciones de Claude y Codex","Análisis de imágenes sin texto alternativo","Detección de problemas de diseño y accesibilidad"],"fr":["Analyse d''accessibilité selon WCAG 2.1","Examen de conception visuelle pour les composants","Gestion des configurations de Claude et Codex","Analyse d''images sans texte alternatif","Détection de problèmes de conception et d''accessibilité"],"de":["Barrierefreiheitsanalyse nach WCAG 2.1","Überprüfung des visuellen Designs für Komponenten","Verwaltung von Claude- und Codex-Konfigurationen","Analyse von Bildern ohne Alternativtext","Erkennung von Design- und Barrierefreiheitsproblemen"],"pt":["Análise de acessibilidade","Revisão de design visual","Verificação de conformidade com as diretrizes WCAG 2.1","Suporte a projetos locais e na web","Interface de usuário intuitiva"],"ru":["Анализ доступности","Проверка визуального дизайна","Проверка соответствия руководящим принципам WCAG 2.1","Поддержка локальных и веб-проектов","Интуитивный интерфейс пользователя"],"ar":["تحليل إمكانية الوصول","مراجعة التصميم المرئي","فحص مطابقة إرشادات WCAG 2.1","دعم المشاريع المحلية وعلى الويب","واجهة مستخدم直观"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Rams","配置管理","Claude","Codex","本地集成","网络集成","文件分析","可访问性"],"ja":["Rams","設定管理","Claude","Codex","ローカル統合","Web 統合","ファイル分析","アクセシビリティ"],"ko":["Rams","설정 관리","Claude","Codex","로컬 통합","웹 통합","파일 분석","접근성"],"es":["accesibilidad web","diseño visual","WCAG 2.1","herramientas de desarrollo","componentes web"," Claude","Codex"],"fr":["accessibilité web","conception visuelle","WCAG 2.1","outils de développement","composants web","Claude","Codex"],"de":["Barrierefreiheit im Web","visuelles Design","WCAG 2.1","Entwicklungstools","Webkomponenten","Claude","Codex"],"pt":["revisão de design","acessibilidade","WCAG 2.1","desenvolvimento web","ferramentas de design","desenvolvedores","projetos locais","projetos na web"],"ru":["проверка дизайна","доступность","WCAG 2.1","веб-разработка","инструменты дизайна","разработчики","локальные проекты","веб-проекты"],"ar":["مراجعة التصميم","إمكانية الوصول","WCAG 2.1","تطوير الويب","أدوات التصميم","المطورين","المشاريع المحلية","المشاريع على الويب"]}},"owner":"roderik","repo":"mpe","repoPath":"roderik/mpe","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.474Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"rams","description":"Run accessibility and visual design review on components. Use when reviewing UI code for WCAG compliance and design issues.","bodyPreview":"# Rams Design Review\n\nYou are Rams, an expert design engineer reviewing code for accessibility and visual design issues.\n\n## Mode\n\nIf `$ARGUMENTS` is provided, analyze that specific file.\nIf `$ARGUMENTS` is empty, ask the user which file(s) to review, or offer to scan the project for component files.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Accessibility Review (WCAG 2.1)\n\n### Critical (Must Fix)\n\n| Check | WCAG | What to look for |\n|-------|------|------------------|\n| Images without alt | 1.1.1 | `<img>` without `alt` att","body":"# Rams Design Review\n\nYou are Rams, an expert design engineer reviewing code for accessibility and visual design issues.\n\n## Mode\n\nIf `$ARGUMENTS` is provided, analyze that specific file.\nIf `$ARGUMENTS` is empty, ask the user which file(s) to review, or offer to scan the project for component files.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Accessibility Review (WCAG 2.1)\n\n### Critical (Must Fix)\n\n| Check | WCAG | What to look for |\n|-------|------|------------------|\n| Images without alt | 1.1.1 | `<img>` without `alt` attribute |\n| Icon-only buttons | 4.1.2 | `<button>` with only SVG/icon, no `aria-label` |\n| Form inputs without labels | 1.3.1 | `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>` without associated `<label>` or `aria-label` |\n| Non-semantic click handlers | 2.1.1 | `<div onClick>` or `<span onClick>` without `role`, `tabIndex`, `onKeyDown` |\n| Missing link destination | 2.1.1 | `<a>` without `href` using only `onClick` |\n\n### Serious (Should Fix)\n\n| Check | WCAG | What to look for |\n|-------|------|------------------|\n| Focus outline removed | 2.4.7 | `outline-none` or `outline: none` without visible focus replacement |\n| Missing keyboard handlers | 2.1.1 | Interactive elements with `onClick` but no `onKeyDown`/`onKeyUp` |\n| Color-only information | 1.4.1 | Status/error indicated only by color (no icon/text) |\n| Touch target too small | 2.5.5 | Clickable elements smaller than 44x44px |\n\n### Moderate (Consider Fixing)\n\n| Check | WCAG | What to look for |\n|-------|------|------------------|\n| Heading hierarchy | 1.3.1 | Skipped heading levels (h1 → h3) |\n| Positive tabIndex | 2.4.3 | `tabIndex` > 0 (disrupts natural tab order) |\n| Role without required attributes | 4.1.2 | `role=\"button\"` without `tabIndex=\"0\"` |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Visual Design Review\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- Inconsistent spacing values\n- Overflow issues, alignment problems\n- Z-index conflicts\n\n### Typography\n- Mixed font families, weights, or sizes\n- Line height issues\n- Missing font fallbacks\n\n### Color & Contrast\n- Contrast ratio below 4.5:1\n- Missing hover/focus states\n- Dark mode inconsistencies\n\n### Components\n- Missing button states (disabled, loading, hover, active, focus)\n- Missing form field states (error, success, disabled)\n- Inconsistent borders, shadows, or icon sizing\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\n```\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════\nRAMS DESIGN REVIEW: [filename]\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nCRITICAL (X issues)\n───────────────────\n[A11Y] Line 24: Button missing accessible name\n  <button><CloseIcon /></button>\n  Fix: Add aria-label=\"Close\"\n  WCAG: 4.1.2\n\nSERIOUS (X issues)\n──────────────────\n...\n\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════\nSUMMARY: X critical, X serious, X moderate\nScore: XX/100\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════\n```\n\n---\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Read the file(s) first before making assessments\n2. Be specific with line numbers and code snippets\n3. Provide fixes, not just problems\n4. Prioritize critical accessibility issues first\n\nIf asked, offer to fix the issues directly.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:07:04.458Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Review Agents needing advanced accessibility and visual design analysis capabilities, particularly with WCAG 2.1 compliance.","zh":"非常适合需要高级可访问性和视觉设计分析功能的代码审查代理，特别是WCAG 2.1合规性。","ja":"コードレビューエージェントが高度なアクセシビリティと視覚デザイン分析機能を必要とする場合、特にWCAG 2.1のコンプライアンスに適しています。","ko":"고급 접근성 및 시각적 디자인 분석 기능이 필요한 코드 리뷰 에이전트에 적합합니다. 특히 WCAG 2.1 규정 준수에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de revisión de código que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de accesibilidad y análisis de diseño visual, particularmente con la conformidad con WCAG 2.1.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de révision de code ayant besoin de capacités avancées d''accessibilité et d''analyse de conception visuelle, en particulier avec la conformité WCAG 2.1.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Review-Agenten, die erweiterte Barrierefreiheits- und visuelle Gestaltungsanalysefunktionen benötigen, insbesondere für die Konformität mit WCAG 2.1.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Revisão de Código que precisam de acessibilidade avançada e capacidades de análise de design visual, particularmente com conformidade com a WCAG 2.1.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов проверки кода, которым необходимы продвинутые возможности доступности и анализа визуального дизайна, особенно в отношении соблюдения требований WCAG 2.1.","ar":"مثالي لعمليات مراجعة الشفرة التي تحتاج إلى إمكانات إمكانية الوصول والتصميم المرئي المتقدمة، ولا سيما المتعلقة بالامتثال لمرجع WCAG 2.1."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to analyze code for accessibility issues, such as images without alt tags, and review visual design elements, utilizing configurations for Claude and Codex, and supporting both local and web-based project scanning, including component files.","zh":"赋予代理分析代码中的可访问性问题的能力，例如没有alt标签的图像，并审查视觉设计元素，利用Claude和Codex的配置，并支持本地和基于Web的项目扫描，包括组件文件。","ja":"エージェントがコードをアクセシビリティの問題、たとえばaltタグのない画像を分析する機能を与え、視覚デザインの要素をレビューし、ClaudeとCodexの構成を利用し、ローカルとWebベースのプロジェクトのスキャンをサポートし、コンポーネントファイルを含む。","ko":"에이전트가 코드를 분석하여 접근성 문제를 발견하는 능력을 부여합니다. 예를 들어 alt 태그가 없는 이미지와 같은 문제를 발견하고 시각적 디자인 요소를 검토하며 Claude와 Codex의 구성을 사용하여 로컬 및 웹 기반 프로젝트를 스캔하고 컴포�트 파일을 포함하여 지원합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a analizar el código en busca de problemas de accesibilidad, como imágenes sin etiquetas alternativas, y a revisar elementos de diseño visual, utilizando configuraciones para Claude y Codex, y admitiendo tanto la exploración de proyectos locales como basados en web, incluidos archivos de componentes.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''analyser le code pour les problèmes d''accessibilité, tels que les images sans balises alt, et de réviser les éléments de conception visuelle, en utilisant des configurations pour Claude et Codex, et en prenant en charge à la fois l''analyse de projets locaux et basés sur le web, y compris les fichiers de composants.","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Code auf Barrierefreiheitsprobleme zu analysieren, wie Bilder ohne Alternativtext, und visuelle Gestaltungselemente zu überprüfen, indem Konfigurationen für Claude und Codex verwendet werden, und sowohl lokale als auch webbasierte Projektscans, einschließlich Komponentendateien, unterstützt.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a analisar o código em busca de problemas de acessibilidade, como imagens sem tags de alternativa, e revisar elementos de design visual, utilizando configurações para Claude e Codex, e suportando a varredura de projetos locais e baseados na web, incluindo arquivos de componentes.","ru":"Предоставляет агентам возможность анализировать код на наличие проблем с доступностью, таких как изображения без тегов альтернативного текста, и проверять элементы визуального дизайна, используя конфигурации для Claude и Codex, и поддерживая сканирование как локальных, так и веб-проектов, включая файлы компонентов.","ar":"تمكين العوامل من تحليل الشفرة لتحديد مشاكل إمكانية الوصول، مثل الصور بدون علامات بديلة، ومراجعة عناصر التصميم المرئي، باستخدام التكوينات الخاصة بـ Claude و Codex، ودعم فحص المشاريع المحلية والقائمة على الويب، بما في ذلك ملفات المكونات."},"useCases":{"en":["Analyzing specific files for accessibility issues","Scanning entire projects for component files to review","Reviewing code for visual design inconsistencies"],"zh":["分析特定文件的可访问性问题","扫描整个项目以查看组件文件","审查代码的视觉设计不一致性"],"ja":["特定のファイルのアクセシビリティの問題を分析する","コンポーネントファイルをレビューするために全プロジェクトをスキャンする","コードの視覚デザインの不一致性をレビューする"],"ko":["특정 파일의 접근성 문제를 분석한다","컴포넌트 파일을 검토하기 위해 전체 프로젝트를 스캔한다","코드의 시각적 디자인 불일치성을 검토한다"],"es":["Analizar archivos específicos en busca de problemas de accesibilidad","Escaneo de proyectos completos para archivos de componentes para revisión","Revisar el código en busca de inconsistencias de diseño visual"],"fr":["Analyser des fichiers spécifiques pour les problèmes d''accessibilité","Analyse de projets complets pour les fichiers de composants à réviser","Réviser le code pour les incohérences de conception visuelle"],"de":["Spezifische Dateien auf Barrierefreiheitsprobleme analysieren","Komplette Projekte auf Komponentendateien zum Überprüfen scannen","Code auf visuelle Gestaltungsinkonsistenzen überprüfen"],"pt":["Analisar arquivos específicos em busca de problemas de acessibilidade","Digitalizar projetos inteiros para arquivos de componentes para revisão","Revisar o código em busca de inconsistências no design visual"],"ru":["Анализировать конкретные файлы на наличие проблем с доступностью","Сканировать все проекты для файлов компонентов для проверки","Проверять код на наличие несоответствий в визуальном дизайне"],"ar":["تحليل ملفات محددة لتحديد مشاكل إمكانية الوصول","فحص مشاريع كاملة لملفات المكونات لمراجعتها","مراجعة الشفرة لتحديد التباين في التصميم المرئي"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires $ARGUMENTS to be provided for specific file analysis","Limited to reviewing files and projects for accessibility and visual design issues"],"zh":["需要提供$ARGUMENTS以进行特定文件分析","仅限于审查文件和项目的可访问性和视觉设计问题"],"ja":["特定ファイルの分析には$ARGUMENTSを提供する必要がある","アクセシビリティと視覚デザインの問題をレビューするファイルとプロジェクトに限定"],"ko":["특정 파일 분석을 위해 $ARGUMENTS를 제공해야 함","파일과 프로젝트의 접근성 및 시각적 디자인 문제만을 검토하는 것에 제한"],"es":["Requiere que se proporcionen $ARGUMENTOS para el análisis de archivos específicos","Limitado a la revisión de archivos y proyectos para problemas de accesibilidad y diseño visual"],"fr":["Nécessite que des $ARGUMENTOS soient fournis pour l''analyse de fichiers spécifiques","Limité à la révision de fichiers et de projets pour les problèmes d''accessibilité et de conception visuelle"],"de":["Benötigt, dass $ARGUMENTS für die Analyse spezifischer Dateien bereitgestellt werden","Begrenzt auf die Überprüfung von Dateien und Projekten auf Barrierefreiheits- und visuelle Gestaltungsprobleme"],"pt":["Exige que os $ARGUMENTOS sejam fornecidos para análise de arquivos específicos","Limitado à revisão de arquivos e projetos para problemas de acessibilidade e design visual"],"ru":["Требует предоставления $ARGUMENTS для анализа конкретных файлов","Ограничен проверкой файлов и проектов на проблемы доступности и визуального дизайна"],"ar":["يتطلب تقديم $ARGUMENTOS لتحليل الملفات المحددة","محدود بفحص الملفات والمشاريع لمشاكل إمكانية الوصول والتصميم المرئي"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":70}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('smart-village-solutions/sva-studio/changelog-automation', 'community', 'smart-village-solutions', 'sva-studio', 'smart-village-solutions/sva-studio', 'changelog-automation', 0, 0, 80, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.474Z', '2026-02-18T09:07:16.550Z', NULL, '{"id":"smart-village-solutions/sva-studio/changelog-automation","name":"changelog-automation","description":{"zh":"自动变更日志是指使用行业标准自动化变更日志生成、发布说明和版本管理的技术","ja":"自動変更ログとは、業界標準に基づく自動変更ログ生成、リリースノート、バージョン管理の技術です","ko":"자동 변경 로그는 업계 표준을 기반으로 자동 변경 로그 생성, 릴리스 노트, 버전 관리 기술입니다","en":"Das SVA Studio soll als Headless- und API-first-System sowohl die Smart Village App versorgen als auch als Stadt-CMS bzw. Content-Hub für externe Kanäle dienen (Websites, Stelen, Fachsoftware)."},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"自动变更日志","ja":"自動変更ログ","ko":"자동 변경 로그","en":"changelog-automation"},"description":{"zh":"自动变更日志是指使用行业标准自动化变更日志生成、发布说明和版本管理的技术","ja":"自動変更ログとは、業界標準に基づく自動変更ログ生成、リリースノート、バージョン管理の技術です","ko":"자동 변경 로그는 업계 표준을 기반으로 자동 변경 로그 생성, 릴리스 노트, 버전 관리 기술입니다","en":"Das SVA Studio soll als Headless- und API-first-System sowohl die Smart Village App versorgen als auch als Stadt-CMS bzw. Content-Hub für externe Kanäle dien..."},"definition":{"en":"Das SVA Studio soll als Headless- und API-first-System sowohl die Smart Village App versorgen als auch als Stadt-CMS bzw. Content-Hub für externe Kanäle dienen (Websites, Stelen, Fachsoftware)."},"features":{"zh":["自动变更日志生成","Conventional Commits 实现","发布说明工作流","提交消息格式标准化","GitHub/GitLab 发布说明生成","语义版本管理"],"ja":["自動変更ログ生成","Conventional Commits の実装","リリースノートワークフロー","コミットメッセージ形式の標準化","GitHub/GitLab リリースノート生成","セマンティックバージョニング"],"ko":["자동 변경 로그 생성","Conventional Commits 구현","릴리스 노트 워크플로","提交 메시지 형식 표준화","GitHub/GitLab 릴리스 노트 생성","의미 버전 관리"]},"keywords":{"zh":["自动变更日志","变更日志生成","发布说明","版本管理","Conventional Commits","语义版本","自动化","行业标准"],"ja":["自動変更ログ","変更ログ生成","リリースノート","バージョン管理","Conventional Commits","セマンティックバージョニング","自動化","業界標準"],"ko":["자동 변경 로그","변경 로그 생성","릴리스 노트","버전 관리","Conventional Commits","의미 버전","자동화","업계 표준"]}},"owner":"smart-village-solutions","repo":"sva-studio","repoPath":"smart-village-solutions/sva-studio","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.474Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"changelog-automation","description":"Automate changelog generation from commits, PRs, and releases following Keep a Changelog format. Use when setting up release workflows, generating release notes, or standardizing commit conventions.","bodyPreview":"# Changelog Automation\n\nPatterns and tools for automating changelog generation, release notes, and version management following industry standards.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up automated changelog generation\n- Implementing Conventional Commits\n- Creating release note workflows\n- Standardizing commit message formats\n- Generating GitHub/GitLab release notes\n- Managing semantic versioning\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Keep a Changelog Format\n\n```markdown\n# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to","body":"# Changelog Automation\n\nPatterns and tools for automating changelog generation, release notes, and version management following industry standards.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up automated changelog generation\n- Implementing Conventional Commits\n- Creating release note workflows\n- Standardizing commit message formats\n- Generating GitHub/GitLab release notes\n- Managing semantic versioning\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n### 1. Keep a Changelog Format\n\n```markdown\n# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n\nThe format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),\nand this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).\n\n## [Unreleased]\n\n### Added\n\n- New feature X\n\n## [1.2.0] - 2024-01-15\n\n### Added\n\n- User profile avatars\n- Dark mode support\n\n### Changed\n\n- Improved loading performance by 40%\n\n### Deprecated\n\n- Old authentication API (use v2)\n\n### Removed\n\n- Legacy payment gateway\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Login timeout issue (#123)\n\n### Security\n\n- Updated dependencies for CVE-2024-1234\n\n[Unreleased]: https://github.com/user/repo/compare/v1.2.0...HEAD\n[1.2.0]: https://github.com/user/repo/compare/v1.1.0...v1.2.0\n```\n\n### 2. Conventional Commits\n\n```\n<type>[optional scope]: <description>\n\n[optional body]\n\n[optional footer(s)]\n```\n\n| Type       | Description      | Changelog Section  |\n| ---------- | ---------------- | ------------------ |\n| `feat`     | New feature      | Added              |\n| `fix`      | Bug fix          | Fixed              |\n| `docs`     | Documentation    | (usually excluded) |\n| `style`    | Formatting       | (usually excluded) |\n| `refactor` | Code restructure | Changed            |\n| `perf`     | Performance      | Changed            |\n| `test`     | Tests            | (usually excluded) |\n| `chore`    | Maintenance      | (usually excluded) |\n| `ci`       | CI changes       | (usually excluded) |\n| `build`    | Build system     | (usually excluded) |\n| `revert`   | Revert commit    | Removed            |\n\n### 3. Semantic Versioning\n\n```\nMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH\n\nMAJOR: Breaking changes (feat! or BREAKING CHANGE)\nMINOR: New features (feat)\nPATCH: Bug fixes (fix)\n```\n\n## Implementation\n\n### Method 1: Conventional Changelog (Node.js)\n\n```bash\n# Install tools\nnpm install -D @commitlint/cli @commitlint/config-conventional\nnpm install -D husky\nnpm install -D standard-version\n# or\nnpm install -D semantic-release\n\n# Setup commitlint\ncat > commitlint.config.js << ''EOF''\nmodule.exports = {\n  extends: [''@commitlint/config-conventional''],\n  rules: {\n    ''type-enum'': [\n      2,\n      ''always'',\n      [\n        ''feat'',\n        ''fix'',\n        ''docs'',\n        ''style'',\n        ''refactor'',\n        ''perf'',\n        ''test'',\n        ''chore'',\n        ''ci'',\n        ''build'',\n        ''revert'',\n      ],\n    ],\n    ''subject-case'': [2, ''never'', [''start-case'', ''pascal-case'', ''upper-case'']],\n    ''subject-max-length'': [2, ''always'', 72],\n  },\n};\nEOF\n\n# Setup husky\nnpx husky init\necho \"npx --no -- commitlint --edit \\$1\" > .husky/commit-msg\n```\n\n### Method 2: standard-version Configuration\n\n```javascript\n// .versionrc.js\nmodule.exports = {\n  types: [\n    { type: \"feat\", section: \"Features\" },\n    { type: \"fix\", section: \"Bug Fixes\" },\n    { type: \"perf\", section: \"Performance Improvements\" },\n    { type: \"revert\", section: \"Reverts\" },\n    { type: \"docs\", section: \"Documentation\", hidden: true },\n    { type: \"style\", section: \"Styles\", hidden: true },\n    { type: \"chore\", section: \"Miscellaneous\", hidden: true },\n    { type: \"refactor\", section: \"Code Refactoring\", hidden: true },\n    { type: \"test\", section: \"Tests\", hidden: true },\n    { type: \"build\", section: \"Build System\", hidden: true },\n    { type: \"ci\", section: \"CI/CD\", hidden: true },\n  ],\n  commitUrlFormat: \"{{host}}/{{owner}}/{{repository}}/commit/{{hash}}\",\n  compareUrlFormat:\n    \"{{host}}/{{owner}}/{{repository}}/compare/{{previousTag}}...{{currentTag}}\",\n  issueUrlFormat: \"{{host}}/{{owner}}/{{repository}}/issues/{{id}}\",\n  userUrlFormat: \"{{host}}/{{user}}\",\n  releaseCommitMessageFormat: \"chore(release): {{currentTag}}\",\n  scripts: {\n    prebump: ''echo \"Running prebump\"'',\n    postbump: ''echo \"Running postbump\"'',\n    prechangelog: ''echo \"Running prechangelog\"'',\n    postchangelog: ''echo \"Running postchangelog\"'',\n  },\n};\n```\n\n```json\n// package.json scripts\n{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"release\": \"standard-version\",\n    \"release:minor\": \"standard-version --release-as minor\",\n    \"release:major\": \"standard-version --release-as major\",\n    \"release:patch\": \"standard-version --release-as patch\",\n    \"release:dry\": \"standard-version --dry-run\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Method 3: semantic-release (Full Automation)\n\n```javascript\n// release.config.js\nmodule.exports = {\n  branches: [\n    \"main\",\n    { name: \"beta\", prerelease: true },\n    { name: \"alpha\", prerelease: true },\n  ],\n  plugins: [\n    \"@semantic-release/commit-analyzer\",\n    \"@semantic-release/release-notes-generator\",\n    [\n      \"@semantic-release/changelog\",\n      {\n        changelogFile: \"CHANGELOG.md\",\n      },\n    ],\n    [\n      \"@semantic-release/npm\",\n      {\n        npmPublish: true,\n      },\n    ],\n    [\n      \"@semantic-release/github\",\n      {\n        assets: [\"dist/**/*.js\", \"dist/**/*.css\"],\n      },\n    ],\n    [\n      \"@semantic-release/git\",\n      {\n        assets: [\"CHANGELOG.md\", \"package.json\"],\n        message:\n          \"chore(release): ${nextRelease.version} [skip ci]\\n\\n${nextRelease.notes}\",\n      },\n    ],\n  ],\n};\n```\n\n### Method 4: GitHub Actions Workflow\n\n```yaml\n# .github/workflows/release.yml\nname: Release\n\non:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      release_type:\n        description: \"Release type\"\n        required: true\n        default: \"patch\"\n        type: choice\n        options:\n          - patch\n          - minor\n          - major\n\npermissions:\n  contents: write\n  pull-requests: write\n\njobs:\n  release:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n          token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: \"20\"\n          cache: \"npm\"\n\n      - run: npm ci\n\n      - name: Configure Git\n        run: |\n          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n          git config user.email \"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n\n      - name: Run semantic-release\n        env:\n          GITHUB_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          NPM_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NPM_TOKEN }}\n        run: npx semantic-release\n\n  # Alternative: manual release with standard-version\n  manual-release:\n    if: github.event_name == ''workflow_dispatch''\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          fetch-depth: 0\n\n      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4\n        with:\n          node-version: \"20\"\n\n      - run: npm ci\n\n      - name: Configure Git\n        run: |\n          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n          git config user.email \"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n\n      - name: Bump version and generate changelog\n        run: npx standard-version --release-as ${{ inputs.release_type }}\n\n      - name: Push changes\n        run: git push --follow-tags origin main\n\n      - name: Create GitHub Release\n        uses: softprops/action-gh-release@v1\n        with:\n          tag_name: ${{ steps.version.outputs.tag }}\n          body_path: RELEASE_NOTES.md\n          generate_release_notes: true\n```\n\n### Method 5: git-cliff (Rust-based, Fast)\n\n```toml\n# cliff.toml\n[changelog]\nheader = \"\"\"\n# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n\n\"\"\"\nbody = \"\"\"\n{% if version %}\\\n    ## [{{ version | trim_start_matches(pat=\"v\") }}] - {{ timestamp | date(format=\"%Y-%m-%d\") }}\n{% else %}\\\n    ## [Unreleased]\n{% endif %}\\\n{% for group, commits in commits | group_by(attribute=\"group\") %}\n    ### {{ group | upper_first }}\n    {% for commit in commits %}\n        - {% if commit.scope %}**{{ commit.scope }}:** {% endif %}\\\n            {{ commit.message | upper_first }}\\\n            {% if commit.github.pr_number %} ([#{{ commit.github.pr_number }}](https://github.com/owner/repo/pull/{{ commit.github.pr_number }})){% endif %}\\\n    {% endfor %}\n{% endfor %}\n\"\"\"\nfooter = \"\"\"\n{% for release in releases -%}\n    {% if release.version -%}\n        {% if release.previous.version -%}\n            [{{ release.version | trim_start_matches(pat=\"v\") }}]: \\\n                https://github.com/owner/repo/compare/{{ release.previous.version }}...{{ release.version }}\n        {% endif -%}\n    {% else -%}\n        [unreleased]: https://github.com/owner/repo/compare/{{ release.previous.version }}...HEAD\n    {% endif -%}\n{% endfor %}\n\"\"\"\ntrim = true\n\n[git]\nconventional_commits = true\nfilter_unconventional = true\nsplit_commits = false\ncommit_parsers = [\n    { message = \"^feat\", group = \"Features\" },\n    { message = \"^fix\", group = \"Bug Fixes\" },\n    { message = \"^doc\", group = \"Documentation\" },\n    { message = \"^perf\", group = \"Performance\" },\n    { message = \"^refactor\", group = \"Refactoring\" },\n    { message = \"^style\", group = \"Styling\" },\n    { message = \"^test\", group = \"Testing\" },\n    { message = \"^chore\\\\(release\\\\)\", skip = true },\n    { message = \"^chore\", group = \"Miscellaneous\" },\n]\nfilter_commits = false\ntag_pattern = \"v[0-9]*\"\nskip_tags = \"\"\nignore_tags = \"\"\ntopo_order = false\nsort_commits = \"oldest\"\n\n[github]\nowner = \"owner\"\nrepo = \"repo\"\n```\n\n```bash\n# Generate changelog\ngit cliff -o CHANGELOG.md\n\n# Generate for specific range\ngit cliff v1.0.0..v2.0.0 -o RELEASE_NOTES.md\n\n# Preview without writing\ngit cliff --unreleased --dry-run\n```\n\n### Method 6: Python (commitizen)\n\n```toml\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.commitizen]\nname = \"cz_conventional_commits\"\nversion = \"1.0.0\"\nversion_files = [\n    \"pyproject.toml:version\",\n    \"src/__init__.py:__version__\",\n]\ntag_format = \"v$version\"\nupdate_changelog_on_bump = true\nchangelog_incremental = true\nchangelog_start_rev = \"v0.1.0\"\n\n[tool.commitizen.customize]\nmessage_template = \"{{change_type}}{% if scope %}({{scope}}){% endif %}: {{message}}\"\nschema = \"<type>(<scope>): <subject>\"\nschema_pattern = \"^(feat|fix|docs|style|refactor|perf|test|chore)(\\\\(\\\\w+\\\\))?:\\\\s.*\"\nbump_pattern = \"^(feat|fix|perf|refactor)\"\nbump_map = {\"feat\" = \"MINOR\", \"fix\" = \"PATCH\", \"perf\" = \"PATCH\", \"refactor\" = \"PATCH\"}\n```\n\n```bash\n# Install\npip install commitizen\n\n# Create commit interactively\ncz commit\n\n# Bump version and update changelog\ncz bump --changelog\n\n# Check commits\ncz check --rev-range HEAD~5..HEAD\n```\n\n## Release Notes Templates\n\n### GitHub Release Template\n\n```markdown\n## What''s Changed\n\n### 🚀 Features\n\n{{ range .Features }}\n\n- {{ .Title }} by @{{ .Author }} in #{{ .PR }}\n  {{ end }}\n\n### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n\n{{ range .Fixes }}\n\n- {{ .Title }} by @{{ .Author }} in #{{ .PR }}\n  {{ end }}\n\n### 📚 Documentation\n\n{{ range .Docs }}\n\n- {{ .Title }} by @{{ .Author }} in #{{ .PR }}\n  {{ end }}\n\n### 🔧 Maintenance\n\n{{ range .Chores }}\n\n- {{ .Title }} by @{{ .Author }} in #{{ .PR }}\n  {{ end }}\n\n## New Contributors\n\n{{ range .NewContributors }}\n\n- @{{ .Username }} made their first contribution in #{{ .PR }}\n  {{ end }}\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/owner/repo/compare/v{{ .Previous }}...v{{ .Current }}\n```\n\n### Internal Release Notes\n\n```markdown\n# Release v2.1.0 - January 15, 2024\n\n## Summary\n\nThis release introduces dark mode support and improves checkout performance\nby 40%. It also includes important security updates.\n\n## Highlights\n\n### 🌙 Dark Mode\n\nUsers can now switch to dark mode from settings. The preference is\nautomatically saved and synced across devices.\n\n### ⚡ Performance\n\n- Checkout flow is 40% faster\n- Reduced bundle size by 15%\n\n## Breaking Changes\n\nNone in this release.\n\n## Upgrade Guide\n\nNo special steps required. Standard deployment process applies.\n\n## Known Issues\n\n- Dark mode may flicker on initial load (fix scheduled for v2.1.1)\n\n## Dependencies Updated\n\n| Package | From    | To      | Reason                   |\n| ------- | ------- | ------- | ------------------------ |\n| react   | 18.2.0  | 18.3.0  | Performance improvements |\n| lodash  | 4.17.20 | 4.17.21 | Security patch           |\n```\n\n## Commit Message Examples\n\n```bash\n# Feature with scope\nfeat(auth): add OAuth2 support for Google login\n\n# Bug fix with issue reference\nfix(checkout): resolve race condition in payment processing\n\nCloses #123\n\n# Breaking change\nfeat(api)!: change user endpoint response format\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: The user endpoint now returns `userId` instead of `id`.\nMigration guide: Update all API consumers to use the new field name.\n\n# Multiple paragraphs\nfix(database): handle connection timeouts gracefully\n\nPreviously, connection timeouts would cause the entire request to fail\nwithout retry. This change implements exponential backoff with up to\n3 retries before failing.\n\nThe timeout threshold has been increased from 5s to 10s based on p99\nlatency analysis.\n\nFixes #456\nReviewed-by: @alice\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n### Do''s\n\n- **Follow Conventional Commits** - Enables automation\n- **Write clear messages** - Future you will thank you\n- **Reference issues** - Link commits to tickets\n- **Use scopes consistently** - Define team conventions\n- **Automate releases** - Reduce manual errors\n\n### Don''ts\n\n- **Don''t mix changes** - One logical change per commit\n- **Don''t skip validation** - Use commitlint\n- **Don''t manual edit** - Generated changelogs only\n- **Don''t forget breaking changes** - Mark with `!` or footer\n- **Don''t ignore CI** - Validate commits in pipeline\n\n## Resources\n\n- [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/)\n- [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)\n- [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/)\n- [semantic-release](https://semantic-release.gitbook.io/)\n- [git-cliff](https://git-cliff.org/)\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:07:16.550Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for DevOps Agents requiring streamlined changelog management and automation","zh":"适用于需要简化变更日志管理和自动化的DevOps代理","ja":"DevOpsエージェントが変更ログの管理と自動化を効率化するために最適","ko":"변경 기록 관리 및 자동화를 간소화해야 하는 DevOps 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de DevOps que requieren una gestión de registro de cambios simplificada y automatización","fr":"Idéal pour les agents DevOps nécessitant une gestion de journal des modifications simplifiée et une automatisation","de":"Ideal für DevOps-Agents, die eine vereinfachte Änderungsprotokollverwaltung und Automatisierung erfordern","pt":"Ideal para agentes DevOps que exigem gestão de changelog simplificada e automação","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов DevOps, требующих упрощенного управления журналом изменений и автоматизации","ar":"مثالي لعميل DevOps الذي يتطلب إدارة سجل التغييرات المبسطة والتحكم الآلي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to automate changelog generation, implement Conventional Commits, and manage semantic versioning using industry-standard tools and formats, including GitHub/GitLab release notes and standardized commit message formats","zh":"赋予代理自动化生成变更日志、实施标准提交、使用标准化工具和格式管理语义版本，包括GitHub/GitLab发布说明和标准化的提交消息格式","ja":"エージェントに変更ログの自動生成、Conventional Commitsの実装、業界標準のツールと形式を使用したセマンティックバージョニングの管理を可能にし、GitHub/GitLabのリリースノートや標準化されたコミットメッセージ形式を含む","ko":"에이전트가 변경 기록 자동 생성, 표준 커밋을 구현하고, 업계 표준 도구 및 형식을 사용하여 의미 버전 관리를 수행할 수 있도록 하며, GitHub/GitLab 发布说明 및 표준화된 커밋 메시지 형식을 포함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a automatizar la generación de registros de cambios, implementar Commits Convencionales y gestionar la versión semántica utilizando herramientas y formatos estándar de la industria, incluyendo notas de lanzamiento de GitHub/GitLab y formatos de mensajes de confirmación estandarizados","fr":"Permet aux agents d''automatiser la génération du journal des modifications, de mettre en œuvre des Commits Conventionnels et de gérer la version sémantique en utilisant des outils et des formats standard de l''industrie, notamment les notes de version de GitHub/GitLab et les formats de messages de validation standardisés","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, die Generierung von Änderungsprotokollen zu automatisieren, Conventional Commits zu implementieren und semantische Versionierung mit Hilfe von branchenüblichen Tools und Formaten zu verwalten, einschließlich GitHub/GitLab-Veröffentlichungshinweisen und standardisierten Überprüfungsnachrichtenformaten","pt":"Habilita os agentes a automatizar a geração de changelog, implementar Commits Convencionais e gerenciar a numeração de versão semântica usando ferramentas e formatos padrão da indústria, incluindo notas de lançamento do GitHub/GitLab e formatos de mensagem de commit padronizados","ru":"Позволяет агентам автоматизировать генерацию журнала изменений, реализовывать Конвенциональные Коммиты и управлять семантическим управлением версиями с помощью отраслевых стандартов инструментов и форматов, включая заметки о выпуске GitHub/GitLab и стандартизированные форматы сообщений о коммитах","ar":"تمكين العميل من توفير تلقائي لإنشاء سجل التغييرات، وتنفيذ التزامات التغييرات التقليدية، وإدارة إصدارات الإصدارات المسمى باستخدام أدوات وتنسيقات الصناعة، بما في ذلك ملاحظات الإصدار من GitHub/GitLab وتنسيقات رسائل الالتزام المعيارية"},"useCases":{"en":["Automating changelog generation for version releases","Implementing Conventional Commits for consistent version control","Generating GitHub/GitLab release notes for transparent project updates"],"zh":["为版本发布自动化生成变更日志","为一致的版本控制实施标准提交","为透明的项目更新生成GitHub/GitLab发布说明"],"ja":["バージョンリリースの変更ログを自動生成する","一貫性のあるバージョン管理のためにConventional Commitsを実装する","透明なプロジェクト更新のためにGitHub/GitLabのリリースノートを生成する"],"ko":["버전 릴리즈를 위한 변경 기록 자동 생성","일관된 버전 관리를 위한 표준 커밋 구현","투명한 프로젝트 업데이트 위한 GitHub/GitLab 릴리즈 노트 생성"],"es":["Automatizar la generación de registros de cambios para lanzamientos de versiones","Implementar Commits Convencionales para un control de versiones coherente","Generar notas de lanzamiento de GitHub/GitLab para actualizaciones de proyectos transparentes"],"fr":["Automatiser la génération du journal des modifications pour les versions de publication","Mettre en œuvre des Commits Conventionnels pour un contrôle de version cohérent","Générer des notes de version de GitHub/GitLab pour des mises à jour de projet transparentes"],"de":["Automatisieren der Generierung von Änderungsprotokollen für Version-Veröffentlichungen","Implementieren von Conventional Commits für konsistentes Versionskontrollmanagement","Generieren von GitHub/GitLab-Veröffentlichungshinweisen für transparente Projektaktualisierungen"],"pt":["Automatizar a geração de changelog para lançamentos de versão","Implementar Commits Convencionais para controle de versão consistente","Gerar notas de lançamento do GitHub/GitLab para atualizações de projeto transparentes"],"ru":["Автоматизировать генерацию журнала изменений для выпусков версий","Реализовывать Конвенциональные Коммиты для последовательного контроля версий","Генерировать заметки о выпуске GitHub/GitLab для прозрачных обновлений проекта"],"ar":["توفير تلقائي لإنشاء سجل التغييرات للإصدارات","تنفيذ التزامات التغييرات التقليدية للسيطرة على الإصدارات المتماسكة","توليد ملاحظات الإصدار من GitHub/GitLab للتحديثات الشفافة للمشروع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires integration with version control systems like GitHub or GitLab","Dependent on consistent commit message formatting","Limited to semantic versioning management"],"zh":["需要与GitHub或GitLab等版本控制系统集成","依赖于一致的提交消息格式","仅限语义版本管理"],"ja":["GitHubやGitLabなどのバージョン管理システムとの統合が必要","一貫性のあるコミットメッセージ形式に依存する","セマンティックバージョニングの管理のみ"],"ko":["GitHub 또는 GitLab와 같은 버전 관리 시스템과 통합 필요","일관된 커밋 메시지 형식에 의존","의미 버전 관리에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere integración con sistemas de control de versiones como GitHub o GitLab","Dependiente de la formatización coherente de mensajes de confirmación","Limitado a la gestión de versión semántica"],"fr":["Nécessite une intégration avec des systèmes de contrôle de version tels que GitHub ou GitLab","Dépend de la mise en forme cohérente des messages de validation","Limité à la gestion de la version sémantique"],"de":["Erfordert Integration mit Versionskontrollsystemen wie GitHub oder GitLab","Abhängig von konsistenter Formatierung von Überprüfungsnachrichten","Begrenzt auf die Verwaltung von semantischer Versionierung"],"pt":["Exige integração com sistemas de controle de versão como GitHub ou GitLab","Dependente de formatação de mensagens de commit consistente","Limitado à gestão de numeração de versão semântica"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с системами контроля версий, такими как GitHub или GitLab","Зависит от последовательного форматирования сообщений о коммитах","Ограничен управлением семантическим управлением версиями"],"ar":["يتطلب تكاملًا مع أنظمة التحكم في الإصدار مثل GitHub أو GitLab","يعتمد على تنسيق رسائل الالتزام الثابت","محدود لإدارة الإصدارات المسمى"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
