tidades y objetos de valor en Rust","fr":"La modélisation de domaine est essentielle pour développer des logiciels robustes. Apprenez à identifier les entités et les objets de valeur en Rust","de":"Die Domain-Modellierung ist entscheidend für die Entwicklung robuster Software. Lernen Sie, Entitäten und Wertobjekte in Rust zu identifizieren","pt":"Entenda como modelar conceitos de domínio em Rust, incluindo entidades e objetos de valor","ru":"Поймите, как моделировать доменные концепции в Rust, включая сущности и объекты значения","ar":"افهم كيف نمذجة مفاهيم النطاق في روست، بما في ذلك الكيانات والأشياء القيمة","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["实体和值对象的区别","不变量的定义","聚合边界的确定","Rust语言中的实现","所有权和唯一标识"],"ja":["エンティティと値オブジェクトの違い","不変量の定義","集約境界の決定","Rust言語における実装","所有権と一意の識別子"],"ko":["엔티티와 값 객체의 차이","불변량의 정의","집계 경계의 결정","Rust 언어中的 구현","소유권과 고유 식별자"],"es":["Identificación de entidades y objetos de valor","Definición de invariantes y límites de agregados","Aplicación de patrones de Rust para modelado de dominio","Comprensión de la propiedad y la identidad única en Rust","Diseño de modelos de dominio escalables y mantenibles"],"fr":["Identification d''entités et d''objets de valeur","Définition d''invariants et de limites d''agrégats","Application de modèles Rust pour la modélisation de domaine","Compréhension de la propriété et de l''identité unique en Rust","Conception de modèles de domaine évolutifs et maintenables"],"de":["Identifizierung von Entitäten und Wertobjekten","Definition von Invarianten und Aggregatgrenzen","Anwendung von Rust-Mustern für die Domain-Modellierung","Verständnis von Eigentum und eindeutiger Identität in Rust","Entwurf von skalierbaren und wartbaren Domain-Modellen"],"pt":["Entidades e objetos de valor","Limites de agregação","Invariantes de domínio","Padrões de design em Rust","Propriedade e identidade única"],"ru":["Сущности и объекты значения","Границы агрегации","Доменные инварианты","Паттерны проектирования в Rust","Владение и уникальная идентичность"],"ar":["الكيانات والأشياء القيمة","حدود التجميع","ثوابت النطاق","أنماط التصميم في روست","الملكية والهوية الفريدة"]},"keywords":{"zh":["领域建模","m09-domain","实体","值对象","不变量","聚合边界","Rust语言","所有权","唯一标识"],"ja":["ドメインモデリング","m09-domain","エンティティ","値オブジェクト","不変量","集約境界","Rust言語","所有権","一意の識別子"],"ko":["도메인 모델링","m09-domain","엔티티","값 객체","불변량","집계 경계","Rust 언어","소유권","고유 식별자"],"es":["modelado de dominio","Rust","entidades","objetos de valor","invariantes","límites de agregados","patrones de Rust","propiedad","identidad única"],"fr":["modélisation de domaine","Rust","entités","objets de valeur","invariants","limites d''agrégats","modèles Rust","propriété","identité unique"],"de":["Domain-Modellierung","Rust","Entitäten","Wertobjekte","Invarianten","Aggregatgrenzen","Rust-Muster","Eigentum","eindeutige Identität"],"pt":["modelagem de domínio","Rust","entidades","objetos de valor","padrões de design","desenvolvimento de software","conceitos de negócios","domínio de negócios"],"ru":["доменное моделирование","Rust","сущности","объекты значения","паттерны проектирования","разработка программного обеспечения","деловые концепции","деловой домен"],"ar":["نمذجة النطاق","روست","الكيانات","الأشياء القيمة","أنماط التصميم","تطوير البرمجيات","مفاهيم الأعمال","نطاق الأعمال"]}},"owner":"yumazak","repo":"kodo","repoPath":"yumazak/kodo","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.474Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"m09-domain","description":"CRITICAL: Use for domain modeling. Triggers: domain model, DDD, domain-driven design, entity, value object, aggregate, repository pattern, business rules, validation, invariant, 领域模型, 领域驱动设计, 业务规则","bodyPreview":"# Domain Modeling\n\n> **Layer 2: Design Choices**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**What is this concept''s role in the domain?**\n\nBefore modeling in code, understand:\n- Is it an Entity (identity matters) or Value Object (interchangeable)?\n- What invariants must be maintained?\n- Where are the aggregate boundaries?\n\n---\n\n## Domain Concept → Rust Pattern\n\n| Domain Concept | Rust Pattern | Ownership Implication |\n|----------------|--------------|----------------------|\n| Entity | struct + Id | Owned, unique ident","body":"# Domain Modeling\n\n> **Layer 2: Design Choices**\n\n## Core Question\n\n**What is this concept''s role in the domain?**\n\nBefore modeling in code, understand:\n- Is it an Entity (identity matters) or Value Object (interchangeable)?\n- What invariants must be maintained?\n- Where are the aggregate boundaries?\n\n---\n\n## Domain Concept → Rust Pattern\n\n| Domain Concept | Rust Pattern | Ownership Implication |\n|----------------|--------------|----------------------|\n| Entity | struct + Id | Owned, unique identity |\n| Value Object | struct + Clone/Copy | Shareable, immutable |\n| Aggregate Root | struct owns children | Clear ownership tree |\n| Repository | trait | Abstracts persistence |\n| Domain Event | enum | Captures state changes |\n| Service | impl block / free fn | Stateless operations |\n\n---\n\n## Thinking Prompt\n\nBefore creating a domain type:\n\n1. **What''s the concept''s identity?**\n   - Needs unique identity → Entity (Id field)\n   - Interchangeable by value → Value Object (Clone/Copy)\n\n2. **What invariants must hold?**\n   - Always valid → private fields + validated constructor\n   - Transition rules → type state pattern\n\n3. **Who owns this data?**\n   - Single owner (parent) → owned field\n   - Shared reference → Arc/Rc\n   - Weak reference → Weak\n\n---\n\n## Trace Up ↑\n\nTo domain constraints (Layer 3):\n\n```\n\"How should I model a Transaction?\"\n    ↑ Ask: What domain rules govern transactions?\n    ↑ Check: domain-fintech (audit, precision requirements)\n    ↑ Check: Business stakeholders (what invariants?)\n```\n\n| Design Question | Trace To | Ask |\n|-----------------|----------|-----|\n| Entity vs Value Object | domain-* | What makes two instances \"the same\"? |\n| Aggregate boundaries | domain-* | What must be consistent together? |\n| Validation rules | domain-* | What business rules apply? |\n\n---\n\n## Trace Down ↓\n\nTo implementation (Layer 1):\n\n```\n\"Model as Entity\"\n    ↓ m01-ownership: Owned, unique\n    ↓ m05-type-driven: Newtype for Id\n\n\"Model as Value Object\"\n    ↓ m01-ownership: Clone/Copy OK\n    ↓ m05-type-driven: Validate at construction\n\n\"Model as Aggregate\"\n    ↓ m01-ownership: Parent owns children\n    ↓ m02-resource: Consider Rc for shared within aggregate\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Reference\n\n| DDD Concept | Rust Pattern | Example |\n|-------------|--------------|---------|\n| Value Object | Newtype | `struct Email(String);` |\n| Entity | Struct + ID | `struct User { id: UserId, ... }` |\n| Aggregate | Module boundary | `mod order { ... }` |\n| Repository | Trait | `trait UserRepo { fn find(...) }` |\n| Domain Event | Enum | `enum OrderEvent { Created, ... }` |\n\n## Pattern Templates\n\n### Value Object\n\n```rust\nstruct Email(String);\n\nimpl Email {\n    pub fn new(s: &str) -> Result<Self, ValidationError> {\n        validate_email(s)?;\n        Ok(Self(s.to_string()))\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Entity\n\n```rust\nstruct UserId(Uuid);\n\nstruct User {\n    id: UserId,\n    email: Email,\n    // ... other fields\n}\n\nimpl PartialEq for User {\n    fn eq(&self, other: &Self) -> bool {\n        self.id == other.id  // Identity equality\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Aggregate\n\n```rust\nmod order {\n    pub struct Order {\n        id: OrderId,\n        items: Vec<OrderItem>,  // Owned children\n        // ...\n    }\n\n    impl Order {\n        pub fn add_item(&mut self, item: OrderItem) {\n            // Enforce aggregate invariants\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n| Mistake | Why Wrong | Better |\n|---------|-----------|--------|\n| Primitive obsession | No type safety | Newtype wrappers |\n| Public fields with invariants | Invariants violated | Private + accessor |\n| Leaked aggregate internals | Broken encapsulation | Methods on root |\n| String for semantic types | No validation | Validated newtype |\n\n---\n\n## Related Skills\n\n| When | See |\n|------|-----|\n| Type-driven implementation | m05-type-driven |\n| Ownership for aggregates | m01-ownership |\n| Domain error handling | m13-domain-error |\n| Specific domain rules | domain-* |\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:09:21.415Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Generation Agents needing advanced domain modeling capabilities with Rust.","zh":"非常适合需要使用Rust进行高级领域建模能力的代码生成代理。","ja":"Rustを使用した高度なドメインモデリング機能を必要とするコード生成エージェントに最適です。","ko":"Rust를 사용한 고급 도메인 모델링 기능이 필요한 코드 생성 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfect for Code Generation Agents needing advanced domain modeling capabilities with Rust.","fr":"Perfect for Code Generation Agents needing advanced domain modeling capabilities with Rust.","de":"Perfect for Code Generation Agents needing advanced domain modeling capabilities with Rust.","pt":"Perfect for Code Generation Agents needing advanced domain modeling capabilities with Rust.","ru":"Perfect for Code Generation Agents needing advanced domain modeling capabilities with Rust.","ar":"Perfect for Code Generation Agents needing advanced domain modeling capabilities with Rust."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to design robust domain models by identifying entities and value objects, maintaining invariants, and defining aggregate boundaries using Rust patterns, specifically leveraging struct and Id for unique identification and ownership implications.","zh":"使代理能够通过识别实体和值对象、维护不变量以及使用Rust模式定义聚合边界来设计强大的领域模型，特别是利用结构体和Id进行唯一标识和所有权含义。","ja":"エージェントが、エンティティと値オブジェクトを識別し、不変性を維持し、Rustのパターンを使用して集約境界を定義することで、堅牢なドメインモデルを設計できるようにします。特に、構造体とIdを使用した一意の識別と所有権の含意を活用します。","ko":"에이전트가 엔티티와 값 객체를 식별하고, 불변성을 유지하며, 러스트 패턴을 사용하여 집계 경계를 정의하여 강력한 도메인 모델을 설계할 수 있도록 합니다. 특히 구조체와 Id를 사용한 고유 식별과 소유권 함의를 활용합니다.","es":"Empowers agents to design robust domain models by identifying entities and value objects, maintaining invariants, and defining aggregate boundaries using Rust patterns, specifically leveraging struct and Id for unique identification and ownership implications.","fr":"Empowers agents to design robust domain models by identifying entities and value objects, maintaining invariants, and defining aggregate boundaries using Rust patterns, specifically leveraging struct and Id for unique identification and ownership implications.","de":"Empowers agents to design robust domain models by identifying entities and value objects, maintaining invariants, and defining aggregate boundaries using Rust patterns, specifically leveraging struct and Id for unique identification and ownership implications.","pt":"Empowers agents to design robust domain models by identifying entities and value objects, maintaining invariants, and defining aggregate boundaries using Rust patterns, specifically leveraging struct and Id for unique identification and ownership implications.","ru":"Empowers agents to design robust domain models by identifying entities and value objects, maintaining invariants, and defining aggregate boundaries using Rust patterns, specifically leveraging struct and Id for unique identification and ownership implications.","ar":"Empowers agents to design robust domain models by identifying entities and value objects, maintaining invariants, and defining aggregate boundaries using Rust patterns, specifically leveraging struct and Id for unique identification and ownership implications."},"useCases":{"en":["Modeling complex business domains with entity and value object distinctions","Defining aggregate boundaries for data consistency and integrity","Applying Rust patterns to ensure ownership and identification of domain concepts"],"zh":["使用实体和值对象区别对复杂业务领域进行建模","为数据一致性和完整性定义聚合边界","应用Rust模式以确保对领域概念的所有权和标识"],"ja":["エンティティと値オブジェクトの区別を使用した複雑なビジネスドメインのモデリング","データの一貫性と完全性のために集約境界を定義する","Rustのパターンを使用してドメイン概念の所有権と識別を確保する"],"ko":["엔티티와 값 객체의 차이를 사용하여 복잡한 비즈니스 도메인을 모델링하는 것","데이터 일관성과 무결성을 위해 