に使用され、動的決定と非決定性を考慮する","ko":"평가 스킬은 에이전트 시스템의 평가 프레임워크를 구축하는 데 사용되며 동적 결정과 비결정성을 고려합니다","es":"La evaluación de sistemas de agentes requiere enfoques diferentes a los de software tradicional. Los agentes toman decisiones dinámicas y no determinísticas.","fr":"L''évaluation des systèmes d''agents nécessite des approches différentes de celles du logiciel traditionnel. Les agents prennent des décisions dynamiques et no...","de":"Die Bewertung von Agentsystemen erfordert unterschiedliche Ansätze als traditionelle Software. Agenten treffen dynamische und nicht deterministische Entschei...","pt":"A avaliação de sistemas de agentes requer abordagens diferentes das tradicionais. Os agentes tomam decisões dinâmicas e não determinísticas.","ru":"Оценка систем агентов требует иного подхода, чем традиционный. Агенты принимают динамические и неопределенные решения.","ar":"تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء يتطلب نهجًا مختلفًا عن التقاليد. الوكلاء يتخذون قرارات ديناميكية وغير محددة.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["构建评估框架","考虑动态决策","处理非确定性","评估方法","代理系统"],"ja":["評価フレームワークの構築","動的決定の考慮","非決定性の処理","評価方法","エージェントシステム"],"ko":["평가 프레임워크 구축","동적 결정 고려","비결정성 처리","평가 방법","에이전트 시스템"],"es":["Construcción de marcos de evaluación","Toma de decisiones dinámicas","No determinismo entre ejecuciones","Falta de respuestas correctas únicas","Enfoques de evaluación personalizados"],"fr":["Construction de cadres d''évaluation","Prise de décision dynamique","Non-déterminisme entre exécutions","Manque de réponses correctes uniques","Approches d''évaluation personnalisées"],"de":["Erstellung von Bewertungsrahmen","Dynamische Entscheidungsfindung","Nicht-Determinismus zwischen Ausführungen","Fehlen von eindeutigen korrekten Antworten","Individuelle Bewertungsansätze"],"pt":["Frameworks de avaliação personalizados","Análise de decisões dinâmicas","Avaliação de desempenho de agentes","Abordagens não determinísticas","Integração com sistemas de agentes"],"ru":["Пользовательские фреймворки оценки","Анализ динамических решений","Оценка производительности агентов","Неопределенные подходы","Интеграция с системами агентов"],"ar":["إطارات تقييم مخصصة","تحليل القرارات الديناميكية","تقييم أداء الوكلاء","نهج غير محددة","التكامل مع أنظمة الوكلاء"]},"keywords":{"zh":["评估技能","代理系统","评估框架","动态决策","非确定性","评估方法"],"ja":["評価スキル","エージェントシステム","評価フレームワーク","動的決定","非決定性","評価方法"],"ko":["평가 스킬","에이전트 시스템","평가 프레임워크","동적 결정","비결정성","평가 방법"],"es":["evaluación de sistemas de agentes","agentes inteligentes","toma de decisiones dinámicas","no determinismo","evaluación de software","desarrollo de agentes"],"fr":["évaluation de systèmes d''agents","agents intelligents","prise de décision dynamique","non-déterminisme","évaluation de logiciel","développement d''agents"],"de":["Bewertung von Agentsystemen","intelligente Agenten","dynamische Entscheidungsfindung","Nicht-Determinismus","Software-Bewertung","Agenten-Entwicklung"],"pt":["avaliação de sistemas de agentes","frameworks de avaliação","agentes autônomos","desempenho de agentes","análise de decisões","sistemas de agentes"],"ru":["оценка систем агентов","фреймворки оценки","автономные агенты","производительность агентов","анализ решений","системы агентов"],"ar":["تقييم أنظمة الوكلاء","إطارات تقييم","وكلاء أوتوماتيكية","أداء الوكلاء","تحليل القرارات","أنظمة الوكلاء"]}},"owner":"andre-sugai","repo":"cine-explorer-mvp-block","repoPath":"andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.475Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"evaluation","description":"Build evaluation frameworks for agent systems","bodyPreview":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while prov","body":"## When to Use This Skill\n\nBuild evaluation frameworks for agent systems\n\nUse this skill when working with build evaluation frameworks for agent systems.\n# Evaluation Methods for Agent Systems\n\nEvaluation of agent systems requires different approaches than traditional software or even standard language model applications. Agents make dynamic decisions, are non-deterministic between runs, and often lack single correct answers. Effective evaluation must account for these characteristics while providing actionable feedback. A robust evaluation framework enables continuous improvement, catches regressions, and validates that context engineering choices achieve intended effects.\n\n## When to Activate\n\nActivate this skill when:\n- Testing agent performance systematically\n- Validating context engineering choices\n- Measuring improvements over time\n- Catching regressions before deployment\n- Building quality gates for agent pipelines\n- Comparing different agent configurations\n- Evaluating production systems continuously\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nAgent evaluation requires outcome-focused approaches that account for non-determinism and multiple valid paths. Multi-dimensional rubrics capture various quality aspects: factual accuracy, completeness, citation accuracy, source quality, and tool efficiency. LLM-as-judge provides scalable evaluation while human evaluation catches edge cases.\n\nThe key insight is that agents may find alternative paths to goals—the evaluation should judge whether they achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Performance Drivers: The 95% Finding**\nResearch on the BrowseComp evaluation (which tests browsing agents'' ability to locate hard-to-find information) found that three factors explain 95% of performance variance:\n\n| Factor | Variance Explained | Implication |\n|--------|-------------------|-------------|\n| Token usage | 80% | More tokens = better performance |\n| Number of tool calls | ~10% | More exploration helps |\n| Model choice | ~5% | Better models multiply efficiency |\n\nThis finding has significant implications for evaluation design:\n- **Token budgets matter**: Evaluate agents with realistic token budgets, not unlimited resources\n- **Model upgrades beat token increases**: Upgrading to Claude Sonnet 4.5 or GPT-5.2 provides larger gains than doubling token budgets on previous versions\n- **Multi-agent validation**: The finding validates architectures that distribute work across agents with separate context windows\n\n## Detailed Topics\n\n### Evaluation Challenges\n\n**Non-Determinism and Multiple Valid Paths**\nAgents may take completely different valid paths to reach goals. One agent might search three sources while another searches ten. They might use different tools to find the same answer. Traditional evaluations that check for specific steps fail in this context.\n\nThe solution is outcome-focused evaluation that judges whether agents achieve right outcomes while following reasonable processes.\n\n**Context-Dependent Failures**\nAgent failures often depend on context in subtle ways. An agent might succeed on simple queries but fail on complex ones. It might work well with one tool set but fail with another. Failures may emerge only after extended interaction when context accumulates.\n\nEvaluation must cover a range of complexity levels and test extended interactions, not just isolated queries.\n\n**Composite Quality Dimensions**\nAgent quality is not a single dimension. It includes factual accuracy, completeness, coherence, tool efficiency, and process quality. An agent might score high on accuracy but low in efficiency, or vice versa.\n\nEvaluation rubrics must capture multiple dimensions with appropriate weighting for the use case.\n\n### Evaluation Rubric Design\n\n**Multi-Dimensional Rubric**\nEffective rubrics cover key dimensions with descriptive levels:\n\nFactual accuracy: Claims match ground truth (excellent to failed)\n\nCompleteness: Output covers requested aspects (excellent to failed)\n\nCitation accuracy: Citations match claimed sources (excellent to failed)\n\nSource quality: Uses appropriate primary sources (excellent to failed)\n\nTool efficiency: Uses right tools reasonable number of times (excellent to failed)\n\n**Rubric Scoring**\nConvert dimension assessments to numeric scores (0.0 to 1.0) with appropriate weighting. Calculate weighted overall scores. Determine passing threshold based on use case requirements.\n\n### Evaluation Methodologies\n\n**LLM-as-Judge**\nLLM-based evaluation scales to large test sets and provides consistent judgments. The key is designing effective evaluation prompts that capture the dimensions of interest.\n\nProvide clear task description, agent output, ground truth (if available), evaluation scale with level descriptions, and request structured judgment.\n\n**Human Evaluation**\nHuman evaluation catches what automation misses. Humans notice hallucinated answers on unusual queries, system failures, and subtle biases that automated evaluation misses.\n\nEffective human evaluation covers edge cases, samples systematically, tracks patterns, and provides contextual understanding.\n\n**End-State Evaluation**\nFor agents that mutate persistent state, end-state evaluation focuses on whether the final state matches expectations rather than how the agent got there.\n\n### Test Set Design\n\n**Sample Selection**\nStart with small samples during development. Early in agent development, changes have dramatic impacts because there is abundant low-hanging fruit. Small test sets reveal large effects.\n\nSample from real usage patterns. Add known edge cases. Ensure coverage across complexity levels.\n\n**Complexity Stratification**\nTest sets should span complexity levels: simple (single tool call), medium (multiple tool calls), complex (many tool calls, significant ambiguity), and very complex (extended interaction, deep reasoning).\n\n### Context Engineering Evaluation\n\n**Testing Context Strategies**\nContext engineering choices should be validated through systematic evaluation. Run agents with different context strategies on the same test set. Compare quality scores, token usage, and efficiency metrics.\n\n**Degradation Testing**\nTest how context degradation affects performance by running agents at different context sizes. Identify performance cliffs where context becomes problematic. Establish safe operating limits.\n\n### Continuous Evaluation\n\n**Evaluation Pipeline**\nBuild evaluation pipelines that run automatically on agent changes. Track results over time. Compare versions to identify improvements or regressions.\n\n**Monitoring Production**\nTrack evaluation metrics in production by sampling interactions and evaluating randomly. Set alerts for quality drops. Maintain dashboards for trend analysis.\n\n## Practical Guidance\n\n### Building Evaluation Frameworks\n\n1. Define quality dimensions relevant to your use case\n2. Create rubrics with clear, actionable level descriptions\n3. Build test sets from real usage patterns and edge cases\n4. Implement automated evaluation pipelines\n5. Establish baseline metrics before making changes\n6. Run evaluations on all significant changes\n7. Track metrics over time for trend analysis\n8. Supplement automated evaluation with human review\n\n### Avoiding Evaluation Pitfalls\n\nOverfitting to specific paths: Evaluate outcomes, not specific steps.\nIgnoring edge cases: Include diverse test scenarios.\nSingle-metric obsession: Use multi-dimensional rubrics.\nNeglecting context effects: Test with realistic context sizes.\nSkipping human evaluation: Automated evaluation misses subtle issues.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Example 1: Simple Evaluation**\n```python\ndef evaluate_agent_response(response, expected):\n    rubric = load_rubric()\n    scores = {}\n    for dimension, config in rubric.items():\n        scores[dimension] = assess_dimension(response, expected, dimension)\n    overall = weighted_average(scores, config[\"weights\"])\n    return {\"passed\": overall >= 0.7, \"scores\": scores}\n```\n\n**Example 2: Test Set Structure**\n\nTest sets should span multiple complexity levels to ensure comprehensive evaluation:\n\n```python\ntest_set = [\n    {\n        \"name\": \"simple_lookup\",\n        \"input\": \"What is the capital of France?\",\n        \"expected\": {\"type\": \"fact\", \"answer\": \"Paris\"},\n        \"complexity\": \"simple\",\n        \"description\": \"Single tool call, factual lookup\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"medium_query\",\n        \"input\": \"Compare the revenue of Apple and Microsoft last quarter\",\n        \"complexity\": \"medium\",\n        \"description\": \"Multiple tool calls, comparison logic\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"multi_step_reasoning\",\n        \"input\": \"Analyze sales data from Q1-Q4 and create a summary report with trends\",\n        \"complexity\": \"complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Many tool calls, aggregation, analysis\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"name\": \"research_synthesis\",\n        \"input\": \"Research emerging AI technologies, evaluate their potential impact, and recommend adoption strategy\",\n        \"complexity\": \"very_complex\",\n        \"description\": \"Extended interaction, deep reasoning, synthesis\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\n## Guidelines\n\n1. Use multi-dimensional rubrics, not single metrics\n2. Evaluate outcomes, not specific execution paths\n3. Cover complexity levels from simple to complex\n4. Test with realistic context sizes and histories\n5. Run evaluations continuously, not just before release\n6. Supplement LLM evaluation with human review\n7. Track metrics over time for trend detection\n8. Set clear pass/fail thresholds based on use case\n\n## Integration\n\nThis skill connects to all other skills as a cross-cutting concern:\n\n- context-fundamentals - Evaluating context usage\n- context-degradation - Detecting degradation\n- context-optimization - Measuring optimization effectiveness\n- multi-agent-patterns - Evaluating coordination\n- tool-design - Evaluating tool effectiveness\n- memory-systems - Evaluating memory quality\n\n## References\n\nInternal reference:\n- [Metrics Reference](./references/metrics.md) - Detailed evaluation metrics and implementation\n\n## References\n\nInternal skills:\n- All other skills connect to evaluation for quality measurement\n\nExternal resources:\n- LLM evaluation benchmarks\n- Agent evaluation research papers\n- Production monitoring practices\n\n---\n\n## Skill Metadata\n\n**Created**: 2025-12-20\n**Last Updated**: 2025-12-20\n**Author**: Agent Skills for Context Engineering Contributors\n**Version**: 1.0.0\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:11:53.964Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Advanced AI Agents requiring dynamic evaluation frameworks for agent systems","zh":"适合需要动态评估框架的高级AI代理","ja":"高度なAIエージェントが動的評価フレームワークを必要とする場合に最適","ko":"동적 평가 프레임워크가 필요한 고급 AI 에이전트에 적합","es":"Ideal para agentes de inteligencia artificial avanzados que requieren marcos de evaluación dinámicos para sistemas de agentes","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''intelligence artificielle avancés nécessitant des cadres d''évaluation dynamiques pour les systèmes d''agents","de":"Ideal für fortgeschrittene KI-Agents, die dynamische Bewertungsframeworks für Agentsysteme erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA Avançados que requerem estruturas de avaliação dinâmicas para sistemas de agentes","ru":"Идеально для продвинутых агентов ИИ, требующих динамических рамок оценки для систем агентов","ar":"مثالي لعمليات الوكيل الذكي المتقدم التي تتطلب إطار تقييم ديناميكي لأنظمة الوكيل"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to build and utilize evaluation frameworks that account for dynamic decision-making and non-deterministic outcomes, leveraging approaches tailored for agent systems and their unique characteristics, including handling of dynamic decisions and non-deterministic runs","zh":"赋予代理构建和利用评估框架的能力，以适应动态决策和非确定性结果，利用针对代理系统及其独特特征的方法，包括处理动态决策和非确定性运行","ja":"エージェントは動的意思決定と非決定性結果を考慮した評価フレームワークを構築して利用できるようにし、エージェントシステムとその独自の特性に合わせたアプローチを利用し、動的意思決定と非決定性実行の処理を含む","ko":"에이전트가 동적 결정과 비결정적 결과를 고려한 평가 프레임워크를 구축하고 활용할 수 있도록 하여, 에이전트 시스템과 그 고유한 특성을 위한 접근 방식을 활용하고, 동적 결정 및 비결정적 실행 처리를 포함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a construir y utilizar marcos de evaluación que tengan en cuenta la toma de decisiones dinámicas y los resultados no deterministas, aprovechando enfoques adaptados a los sistemas de agentes y sus características únicas, incluyendo el manejo de decisiones dinámicas y ejecuciones no deterministas","fr":"Permet aux agents de construire et d''utiliser des cadres d''évaluation qui prennent en compte la prise de décision dynamique et les résultats non déterministes, en exploitant des approches adaptées aux systèmes d''agents et à leurs caractéristiques uniques, notamment la gestion des décisions dynamiques et des exécutions non déterministes","de":"Ermächtigt Agents, Bewertungsframeworks zu erstellen und zu nutzen, die dynamische Entscheidungsfindung und nicht-deterministische Ergebnisse berücksichtigen, indem sie Ansätze nutzen, die auf Agentsysteme und ihre einzigartigen Eigenschaften zugeschnitten sind, einschließlich der Behandlung dynamischer Entscheidungen und nicht-deterministischer Ausführungen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a construir e utilizar estruturas de avaliação que consideram a tomada de decisões dinâmicas e resultados não determinísticos, utilizando abordagens personalizadas para sistemas de agentes e suas características únicas, incluindo o tratamento de decisões dinâmicas e execuções não determinísticas","ru":"Позволяет агентам создавать и использовать рамки оценки, которые учитывают динамическое принятие решений и неопределенные результаты, используя подходы, адаптированные для систем агентов и их уникальных характеристик, включая обработку динамических решений и неопределенных запусков","ar":"تمكين الوكيل من بناء واستخدام أطر التقييم التي تأخذ في الاعتبار اتخاذ القرارات الديناميكي والنتائج غير المحددة، باستخدام نهج مخصصة لأنظمة الوكيل وسماتها الفريدة، بما في ذلك التعامل مع القرارات الديناميكي والتشغيل غير المحدد"},"useCases":{"en":["Building evaluation frameworks for agent systems","Assessing dynamic decision-making in agent systems","Comparing non-deterministic outcomes across different agent runs"],"zh":["为代理系统构建评估框架","评估代理系统中的动态决策","比较不同代理运行中的非确定性结果"],"ja":["エージェントシステムの評価フレームワークを構築する","エージェントシステム内の動的意思決定を評価する","異なるエージェント実行間の非決定性結果を比較する"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템을 위한 평가 프레임워크 구축","에이전트 시스템 내의 동적 결정 평가","다른 에이전트 실행 간의 비결정적 결과 비교"],"es":["Construir marcos de evaluación para sistemas de agentes","Evaluar la toma de decisiones dinámicas en sistemas de agentes","Comparar resultados no deterministas en diferentes ejecuciones de agentes"],"fr":["Construire des cadres d''évaluation pour les systèmes d''agents","Évaluer la prise de décision dynamique dans les systèmes d''agents","Comparer les résultats non déterministes entre différentes exécutions d''agents"],"de":["Bewertungsframeworks für Agentsysteme erstellen","Dynamische Entscheidungsfindung in Agentsystemen bewerten","Nicht-deterministische Ergebnisse über verschiedene Agentenausführungen vergleichen"],"pt":["Construção de estruturas de avaliação para sistemas de agentes","Avaliação da tomada de decisões dinâmicas em sistemas de agentes","Comparação de resultados não determinísticos em diferentes execuções de agentes"],"ru":["Создание рамок оценки для систем агентов","Оценка динамического принятия решений в системах агентов","Сравнение неопределенных результатов в разных запусках агентов"],"ar":["بناء إطارات التقييم لأنظمة الوكيل","تقييم اتخاذ القرارات الديناميكي في أنظمة الوكيل","مقارنة النتائج غير المحددة عبر تشغيلات مختلفة للوكيل"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of agent system dynamics","May need adaptation for specific agent system architectures"],"zh":["需要了解代理系统动态","可能需要适应特定的代理系统架构"],"ja":["エージェントシステムのダイナミクスを理解する必要がある","特定のエージェントシステムアーキテクチャに適応する必要があるかもしれない"],"ko":["에이전트 시스템 동적을 이해해야 함","특정 에이전트 시스템 아키텍처에 적응해야 할 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la dinámica del sistema de agentes","Puede necesitar adaptación para arquitecturas de sistemas de agentes específicas"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de la dynamique du système d''agents","Peut nécessiter une adaptation pour les architectures de systèmes d''agents spécifiques"],"de":["Benötigt Verständnis der Dynamik des Agentsystems","Kann eine Anpassung für bestimmte Agentsystemarchitekturen erfordern"],"pt":["Requer entendimento da dinâmica do sistema de agentes","Pode precisar de adaptação para arquiteturas de sistemas de agentes específicas"],"ru":["Требует понимания динамики системы агентов","Может потребовать адаптации для конкретных архитектур систем агентов"],"ar":["يتطلب فهم ديناميات نظام الوكيل","يمكن أن يحتاج إلى التكيف مع هياكل أنظمة الوكيل المحددة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
