},"description":{"zh":"技能创作者提供创建有效技能的指南，帮助开发者开发出能够扩展 Claude 能力的模块化技能","ja":"スキルクリエーターは、効果的なスキルを作成するためのガイドを提供し、開発者が Claude の能力を拡張するモジュール化スキルを開発できるようにします","ko":"스킬 생성기는 효과적인 스킬을 생성하기 위한 가이드를 제공하여 개발자가 Claude의 능력을 확장하는 모듈화된 스킬을 개발할 수 있도록 합니다","es":"Skill Creator es una herramienta para desarrolladores que proporciona orientación para crear habilidades efectivas y extender las capacidades de Claude","fr":"Skill Creator est un outil pour développeurs qui fournit des conseils pour créer des compétences efficaces et étendre les capacités de Claude","de":"Skill Creator ist ein Tool für Entwickler, das Anleitung zur Erstellung effektiver Fähigkeiten und zur Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude bietet","pt":"O Skill Creator fornece orientação para a criação de habilidades eficazes, permitindo que os desenvolvedores estendam as capacidades do Claude.","ru":"Создатель Навыков предоставляет руководство по созданию эффективных навыков, позволяя разработчикам расширить возможности Claude.","ar":"مُصمم المهارات يقدم إرشادات لإنشاء مهارات فعالة، مما يسمح للمطورين بتوسيع قدرات كلود.","en":"Light Keepers 災防平台 - Taiwan Xiwang Lighthouse Association"},"definition":{"en":"Light Keepers 災防平台 - Taiwan Xiwang Lighthouse Association"},"features":{"zh":["模块化技能","扩展 Claude 能力","提供专用工作流程","支持多种任务","开发者友好界面","高可定制性"],"ja":["モジュール化スキル","Claude の能力を拡張","専用のワークフローを提供","多種多様なタスクをサポート","開発者向けのインターフェース","高可定制性"],"ko":["모듈화된 스킬","Claude의 능력을 확장","전용 워크플로우 제공","다양한 작업 지원","개발자 친화적 인터페이스","고도화된 사용자 정의"],"es":["Creación de habilidades personalizadas","Flujos de trabajo especializados","Conocimientos y herramientas específicos","Extensión de las capacidades de Claude","Guía para desarrolladores"],"fr":["Création de compétences personnalisées","Flux de travail spécialisés","Connaissances et outils spécifiques","Étendre les capacités de Claude","Guide pour développeurs"],"de":["Erstellung benutzerdefinierter Fähigkeiten","Spezialisierte Workflows","Spezifische Kenntnisse und Tools","Erweiterung der Fähigkeiten von Claude","Anleitung für Entwickler"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades personalizadas","Extensão das capacidades do Claude","Conhecimento especializado","Fluxos de trabalho personalizados","Modularidade e flexibilidade","Integração com a plataforma do Claude"],"ru":["Создание настраиваемых навыков","Расширение возможностей Claude","Специализированные знания","Настраиваемые рабочие процессы","Модульность и гибкость","Интеграция с платформой Claude"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات مخصصة","توسيع قدرات كلود","معرفة متخصصة","تدفقات عمل مخصصة","الوحدة والمرنة","التكامل مع منصة كلود"]},"keywords":{"zh":["技能创作者","模块化技能","Claude 能力扩展","开发者工具","人工智能","自然语言处理","技能开发","AI 开发"],"ja":["スキルクリエーター","モジュール化スキル","Claude の能力拡張","開発者ツール","人工知能","自然言語処理","スキル開発","AI 開発"],"ko":["스킬 생성기","모듈화된 스킬","Claude의 능력 확장","개발자 도구","인공 지능","자연 언어 처리","스킬 개발","AI 개발"],"es":["desarrollo de habilidades","creador de habilidades","Claude","desarrollo de software","inteligencia artificial"," Machine Learning","desarrollo de competencias","tecnologías emergentes"],"fr":["développement de compétences","créateur de compétences","Claude","développement de logiciels","intelligence artificielle","Machine Learning","développement de compétences","technologies émergentes"],"de":["Fähigkeitsentwicklung","Fähigkeitscreator","Claude","Softwareentwicklung","künstliche Intelligenz","Machine Learning","Fähigkeitsentwicklung","aufkommende Technologien"],"pt":["criador de habilidades","desenvolvimento de habilidades","extensão de capacidades","conhecimento especializado","fluxos de trabalho personalizados","modularidade","flexibilidade","integração com plataforma","desenvolvedores de habilidades"],"ru":["создатель навыков","разработка навыков","расширение возможностей","специализированные знания","настраиваемые рабочие процессы","модульность","гибкость","интеграция с платформой","разработчики навыков"],"ar":["مُصمم المهارات","تطوير المهارات","توسيع القدرات","معرفة متخصصة","تدفقات عمل مخصصة","الوحدة","المرنة","التكامل مع المنصة","مطورو المهارات"]}},"owner":"xiangteng007","repo":"light-keepers","repoPath":"xiangteng007/light-keepers","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.475Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"skill-creator","description":"Guide for creating effective skills. This skill should be used when users want to create a new skill (or update an existing skill) that extends Claudes capabilities with specialized knowledge, workflows, or tool integrations.","bodyPreview":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi","body":"# Skill Creator\n\nThis skill provides guidance for creating effective skills.\n\n## About Skills\n\nSkills are modular, self-contained packages that extend Claude''s capabilities by providing\nspecialized knowledge, workflows, and tools. Think of them as \"onboarding guides\" for specific\ndomains or tasks—they transform Claude from a general-purpose agent into a specialized agent\nequipped with procedural knowledge that no model can fully possess.\n\n### What Skills Provide\n\n1. Specialized workflows - Multi-step procedures for specific domains\n2. Tool integrations - Instructions for working with specific file formats or APIs\n3. Domain expertise - Company-specific knowledge, schemas, business logic\n4. Bundled resources - Scripts, references, and assets for complex and repetitive tasks\n\n### Anatomy of a Skill\n\nEvery skill consists of a required SKILL.md file and optional bundled resources:\n\n```\nskill-name/\n├── SKILL.md (required)\n│   ├── YAML frontmatter metadata (required)\n│   │   ├── name: (required)\n│   │   └── description: (required)\n│   └── Markdown instructions (required)\n└── Bundled Resources (optional)\n    ├── scripts/          - Executable code (Python/Bash/etc.)\n    ├── references/       - Documentation intended to be loaded into context as needed\n    └── assets/           - Files used in output (templates, icons, fonts, etc.)\n```\n\n#### SKILL.md (required)\n\n**Metadata Quality:** The `name` and `description` in YAML frontmatter determine when Claude will use the skill. Be specific about what the skill does and when to use it. Use the third-person (e.g. \"This skill should be used when...\" instead of \"Use this skill when...\").\n\n#### Bundled Resources (optional)\n\n##### Scripts (`scripts/`)\n\nExecutable code (Python/Bash/etc.) for tasks that require deterministic reliability or are repeatedly rewritten.\n\n- **When to include**: When the same code is being rewritten repeatedly or deterministic reliability is needed\n- **Example**: `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` for PDF rotation tasks\n- **Benefits**: Token efficient, deterministic, may be executed without loading into context\n- **Note**: Scripts may still need to be read by Claude for patching or environment-specific adjustments\n\n##### References (`references/`)\n\nDocumentation and reference material intended to be loaded as needed into context to inform Claude''s process and thinking.\n\n- **When to include**: For documentation that Claude should reference while working\n- **Examples**: `references/finance.md` for financial schemas, `references/mnda.md` for company NDA template, `references/policies.md` for company policies, `references/api_docs.md` for API specifications\n- **Use cases**: Database schemas, API documentation, domain knowledge, company policies, detailed workflow guides\n- **Benefits**: Keeps SKILL.md lean, loaded only when Claude determines it''s needed\n- **Best practice**: If files are large (>10k words), include grep search patterns in SKILL.md\n- **Avoid duplication**: Information should live in either SKILL.md or references files, not both. Prefer references files for detailed information unless it''s truly core to the skill—this keeps SKILL.md lean while making information discoverable without hogging the context window. Keep only essential procedural instructions and workflow guidance in SKILL.md; move detailed reference material, schemas, and examples to references files.\n\n##### Assets (`assets/`)\n\nFiles not intended to be loaded into context, but rather used within the output Claude produces.\n\n- **When to include**: When the skill needs files that will be used in the final output\n- **Examples**: `assets/logo.png` for brand assets, `assets/slides.pptx` for PowerPoint templates, `assets/frontend-template/` for HTML/React boilerplate, `assets/font.ttf` for typography\n- **Use cases**: Templates, images, icons, boilerplate code, fonts, sample documents that get copied or modified\n- **Benefits**: Separates output resources from documentation, enables Claude to use files without loading them into context\n\n### Progressive Disclosure Design Principle\n\nSkills use a three-level loading system to manage context efficiently:\n\n1. **Metadata (name + description)** - Always in context (~100 words)\n2. **SKILL.md body** - When skill triggers (<5k words)\n3. **Bundled resources** - As needed by Claude (Unlimited*)\n\n*Unlimited because scripts can be executed without reading into context window.\n\n## Skill Creation Process\n\nTo create a skill, follow the \"Skill Creation Process\" in order, skipping steps only if there is a clear reason why they are not applicable.\n\n### Step 1: Understanding the Skill with Concrete Examples\n\nSkip this step only when the skill''s usage patterns are already clearly understood. It remains valuable even when working with an existing skill.\n\nTo create an effective skill, clearly understand concrete examples of how the skill will be used. This understanding can come from either direct user examples or generated examples that are validated with user feedback.\n\nFor example, when building an image-editor skill, relevant questions include:\n\n- \"What functionality should the image-editor skill support? Editing, rotating, anything else?\"\n- \"Can you give some examples of how this skill would be used?\"\n- \"I can imagine users asking for things like ''Remove the red-eye from this image'' or ''Rotate this image''. Are there other ways you imagine this skill being used?\"\n- \"What would a user say that should trigger this skill?\"\n\nTo avoid overwhelming users, avoid asking too many questions in a single message. Start with the most important questions and follow up as needed for better effectiveness.\n\nConclude this step when there is a clear sense of the functionality the skill should support.\n\n### Step 2: Planning the Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo turn concrete examples into an effective skill, analyze each example by:\n\n1. Considering how to execute on the example from scratch\n2. Identifying what scripts, references, and assets would be helpful when executing these workflows repeatedly\n\nExample: When building a `pdf-editor` skill to handle queries like \"Help me rotate this PDF,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Rotating a PDF requires re-writing the same code each time\n2. A `scripts/rotate_pdf.py` script would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When designing a `frontend-webapp-builder` skill for queries like \"Build me a todo app\" or \"Build me a dashboard to track my steps,\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Writing a frontend webapp requires the same boilerplate HTML/React each time\n2. An `assets/hello-world/` template containing the boilerplate HTML/React project files would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nExample: When building a `big-query` skill to handle queries like \"How many users have logged in today?\" the analysis shows:\n\n1. Querying BigQuery requires re-discovering the table schemas and relationships each time\n2. A `references/schema.md` file documenting the table schemas would be helpful to store in the skill\n\nTo establish the skill''s contents, analyze each concrete example to create a list of the reusable resources to include: scripts, references, and assets.\n\n### Step 3: Initializing the Skill\n\nAt this point, it is time to actually create the skill.\n\nSkip this step only if the skill being developed already exists, and iteration or packaging is needed. In this case, continue to the next step.\n\nWhen creating a new skill from scratch, always run the `init_skill.py` script. The script conveniently generates a new template skill directory that automatically includes everything a skill requires, making the skill creation process much more efficient and reliable.\n\nUsage:\n\n```bash\nscripts/init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <output-directory>\n```\n\nThe script:\n\n- Creates the skill directory at the specified path\n- Generates a SKILL.md template with proper frontmatter and TODO placeholders\n- Creates example resource directories: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/`\n- Adds example files in each directory that can be customized or deleted\n\nAfter initialization, customize or remove the generated SKILL.md and example files as needed.\n\n### Step 4: Edit the Skill\n\nWhen editing the (newly-generated or existing) skill, remember that the skill is being created for another instance of Claude to use. Focus on including information that would be beneficial and non-obvious to Claude. Consider what procedural knowledge, domain-specific details, or reusable assets would help another Claude instance execute these tasks more effectively.\n\n#### Start with Reusable Skill Contents\n\nTo begin implementation, start with the reusable resources identified above: `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` files. Note that this step may require user input. For example, when implementing a `brand-guidelines` skill, the user may need to provide brand assets or templates to store in `assets/`, or documentation to store in `references/`.\n\nAlso, delete any example files and directories not needed for the skill. The initialization script creates example files in `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` to demonstrate structure, but most skills won''t need all of them.\n\n#### Update SKILL.md\n\n**Writing Style:** Write the entire skill using **imperative/infinitive form** (verb-first instructions), not second person. Use objective, instructional language (e.g., \"To accomplish X, do Y\" rather than \"You should do X\" or \"If you need to do X\"). This maintains consistency and clarity for AI consumption.\n\nTo complete SKILL.md, answer the following questions:\n\n1. What is the purpose of the skill, in a few sentences?\n2. When should the skill be used?\n3. In practice, how should Claude use the skill? All reusable skill contents developed above should be referenced so that Claude knows how to use them.\n\n### Step 5: Packaging a Skill\n\nOnce the skill is ready, it should be packaged into a distributable zip file that gets shared with the user. The packaging process automatically validates the skill first to ensure it meets all requirements:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder>\n```\n\nOptional output directory specification:\n\n```bash\nscripts/package_skill.py <path/to/skill-folder> ./dist\n```\n\nThe packaging script will:\n\n1. **Validate** the skill automatically, checking:\n   - YAML frontmatter format and required fields\n   - Skill naming conventions and directory structure\n   - Description completeness and quality\n   - File organization and resource references\n\n2. **Package** the skill if validation passes, creating a zip file named after the skill (e.g., `my-skill.zip`) that includes all files and maintains the proper directory structure for distribution.\n\nIf validation fails, the script will report the errors and exit without creating a package. Fix any validation errors and run the packaging command again.\n\n### Step 6: Iterate\n\nAfter testing the skill, users may request improvements. Often this happens right after using the skill, with fresh context of how the skill performed.\n\n**Iteration workflow:**\n\n1. Use the skill on real tasks\n2. Notice struggles or inefficiencies\n3. Identify how SKILL.md or bundled resources should be updated\n4. Implement changes and test again\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:12:29.126Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for AI Agents like Claude needing specialized knowledge and workflows for domain-specific tasks.","zh":"适合像 Claude 这样的 AI Agent，它需要专门的知识和工作流程来执行特定领域的任务。","ja":"Claude のような AI エージェントが、ドメイン固有のタスクに特化した知識とワークフローを必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"클라우드와 같은 AI 에이전트가 특정 도메인 작업을 위한 전문 지식과 워크플로우를 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA como Claude que necesitan conocimientos y flujos de trabajo especializados para tareas específicas de dominio.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA comme Claude ayant besoin de connaissances et de flux de travail spécialisés pour des tâches spécifiques à un domaine.","de":"Perfekt für KI-Agents wie Claude, die spezialisierte Kenntnisse und Arbeitsabläufe für domänenspezifische Aufgaben benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como o Claude que necessitam de conhecimento especializado e fluxos de trabalho para tarefas específicas de domínio.","ru":"Идеально подходит для ИИ-агентов, таких как Claude, которым требуется специализированные знания и рабочие процессы для задач в конкретных предметных областях.","ar":"مثالي لوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude الذين يحتاجون إلى معرفة متخصصة وسير عمل لمهام محددة في المجال."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to transform into specialized entities equipped with procedural knowledge, providing modular and self-contained packages that extend capabilities through specialized workflows and tools, leveraging multi-step processes.","zh":"赋予代理转化为具有过程知识的专门实体的能力，提供模块化和自包含的软件包，以扩展能力，通过专门的工作流程和工具，利用多步骤过程。","ja":"エージェントを手順知識を備えた専門エンティティに変換する力を与え、機能を拡張するためのモジュール化および自己完結型のパッケージを提供し、専門のワークフローおよびツールを利用して、マルチステッププロセスを活用します。","ko":"에이전트가 절차 지식을 갖춘 전문 엔티티로 변신할 수 있는力を 부여하여, 능력을 확장하고, 전문 워크플로우와 도구를 활용하여, 다단계 프로세스를 활용하는 모듈화 및 자체 포함 패키지를 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a transformarse en entidades especializadas equipadas con conocimiento procedimental, proporcionando paquetes modulares y autocontenidos que amplían las capacidades a través de flujos de trabajo y herramientas especializados, aprovechando procesos multi-paso.","fr":"Permet aux agents de se transformer en entités spécialisées équipées de connaissances procédurales, fournissant des packages modulaires et auto-contenus qui étendent les capacités à travers des flux de travail et des outils spécialisés, en exploitant des processus multi-étapes.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, sich in spezialisierte Einheiten mit prozeduralem Wissen zu verwandeln, indem modulare und selbstenthaltene Pakete bereitgestellt werden, die die Fähigkeiten durch spezialisierte Arbeitsabläufe und Tools erweitern, indem multi-schrittige Prozesse genutzt werden.","pt":"Capacita os agentes a se transformarem em entidades especializadas equipadas com conhecimento processual, fornecendo pacotes modulares e autônomos que estendem as capacidades por meio de fluxos de trabalho e ferramentas especializadas, aproveitando processos de várias etapas.","ru":"Позволяет агентам превращаться в специализированные сущности, оснащенные процедурными знаниями, предоставляя модульные и самодостаточные пакеты, которые расширяют возможности за счет специализированных рабочих процессов и инструментов, используя многоэтапные процессы.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من التحول إلى كيانات متخصصة مجهزة بمعرفة إجرائية، وتوفر حزمًا معيارية مستقلة قائمة بذاتها تعزز القدرات من خلال سير العمل والأدوات المتخصصة، مستفيدة من العمليات متعددة الخطوات."},"useCases":{"en":["Creating modular skills for specific domains","Developing onboarding guides for tasks","Extending agent capabilities with procedural knowledge"],"zh":["为特定领域创建模块化技能","为任务开发入门指南","使用过程知识扩展代理能力"],"ja":["特定ドメインのモジュール化スキルを作成する","タスクのためのオンボーディングガイドを開発する","手順知識を使用してエージェントの機能を拡張する"],"ko":["특정 도메인에 대한 모듈화된 스킬을 생성하는 것","작업을 위한 온보딩 가이드 개발","절차 지식을 사용하여 에이전트 능력 확장"],"es":["Crear habilidades modulares para dominios específicos","Desarrollar guías de incorporación para tareas","Ampliar las capacidades de los agentes con conocimiento procedimental"],"fr":["Créer des compétences modulaires pour des domaines spécifiques","Développer des guides d''intégration pour les tâches","Étendre les capacités des agents avec des connaissances procédurales"],"de":["Erstellen von modularen Fähigkeiten für spezifische Domänen","Entwickeln von Einweisungshandbüchern für Aufgaben","Erweitern der Agentenfähigkeiten mit prozeduralem Wissen"],"pt":["Criação de habilidades modulares para domínios específicos","Desenvolvimento de guias de integração para tarefas","Extensão das capacidades do agente com conhecimento processual"],"ru":["Создание модульных навыков для конкретных предметных областей","Разработка руководств по вводу в эксплуатацию для задач","Расширение возможностей агента с помощью процедурных знаний"],"ar":["إنشاء مهارات معيارية لمجالات محددة","تطوير أدلات إدماج للمهام","توسيع قدرات الوكيل بالمعرفة الإجرائية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires understanding of Claude''s architecture and skill development framework"],"zh":["需要了解 Claude 的架构和技能开发框架"],"ja":["Claude のアーキテクチャとスキル開発フレームワークの理解が必要"],"ko":["클라우드의 아키텍처와 스킬 개발 프레임워크에 대한 이해가 필요"],"es":["Requiere comprensión de la arquitectura de Claude y del marco de desarrollo de habilidades"],"fr":["Nécessite une compréhension de l''architecture de Claude et du cadre de développement de compétences"],"de":["Erfordert das Verständnis der Architektur von Claude und des Skill-Entwicklungs-Frameworks"],"pt":["Requer compreensão da arquitetura do Claude e da estrutura de desenvolvimento de habilidades"],"ru":["Требует понимания архитектуры Claude и framework разработки навыков"],"ar":["يتطلب فهمًا لهندسة Claude وإطار عمل تطوير المهارات"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
