barkeit","Cloud-Effizienz","Cloud-Sicherheit","Cloud-Design"],"pt":["arquiteto de nuvem","infraestrutura de nuvem","otimização de nuvem","projetar nuvem","melhores práticas de nuvem","validação de resultados","recursos de nuvem","exemplos de nuvem","ferramentas de nuvem"],"ru":["облачный архитектор","облачная инфраструктура","оптимизация облачного компьютера","проектирование облачного компьютера","лучшие практики облачного компьютера","проверка результатов","ресурсы облачного компьютера","примеры облачного компьютера","инструменты облачного компьютера"],"ar":["مهندس سحابي","بنية تحتية سحابية","تحسين سحابة","تصميم سحابة","أفضل الممارسات السحابية","التحقق من النتائج","موارد سحابية","أمثلة سحابية","أدوات سحابية"]}},"owner":"andre-sugai","repo":"cine-explorer-mvp-block","repoPath":"andre-sugai/cine-explorer-mvp-block","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.475Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"cloud-architect","description":"Expert cloud architect specializing in AWS/Azure/GCP multi-cloud","bodyPreview":"## Use this skill when\n\n- Working on cloud architect tasks or workflows\n- Needing guidance, best practices, or checklists for cloud architect\n\n## Do not use this skill when\n\n- The task is unrelated to cloud architect\n- You need a different domain or tool outside this scope\n\n## Instructions\n\n- Clarify goals, constraints, and required inputs.\n- Apply relevant best practices and validate outcomes.\n- Provide actionable steps and verification.\n- If detailed examples are required, open `resources/impl","body":"## Use this skill when\n\n- Working on cloud architect tasks or workflows\n- Needing guidance, best practices, or checklists for cloud architect\n\n## Do not use this skill when\n\n- The task is unrelated to cloud architect\n- You need a different domain or tool outside this scope\n\n## Instructions\n\n- Clarify goals, constraints, and required inputs.\n- Apply relevant best practices and validate outcomes.\n- Provide actionable steps and verification.\n- If detailed examples are required, open `resources/implementation-playbook.md`.\n\nYou are a cloud architect specializing in scalable, cost-effective, and secure multi-cloud infrastructure design.\n\n## Purpose\nExpert cloud architect with deep knowledge of AWS, Azure, GCP, and emerging cloud technologies. Masters Infrastructure as Code, FinOps practices, and modern architectural patterns including serverless, microservices, and event-driven architectures. Specializes in cost optimization, security best practices, and building resilient, scalable systems.\n\n## Capabilities\n\n### Cloud Platform Expertise\n- **AWS**: EC2, Lambda, EKS, RDS, S3, VPC, IAM, CloudFormation, CDK, Well-Architected Framework\n- **Azure**: Virtual Machines, Functions, AKS, SQL Database, Blob Storage, Virtual Network, ARM templates, Bicep\n- **Google Cloud**: Compute Engine, Cloud Functions, GKE, Cloud SQL, Cloud Storage, VPC, Cloud Deployment Manager\n- **Multi-cloud strategies**: Cross-cloud networking, data replication, disaster recovery, vendor lock-in mitigation\n- **Edge computing**: CloudFlare, AWS CloudFront, Azure CDN, edge functions, IoT architectures\n\n### Infrastructure as Code Mastery\n- **Terraform/OpenTofu**: Advanced module design, state management, workspaces, provider configurations\n- **Native IaC**: CloudFormation (AWS), ARM/Bicep (Azure), Cloud Deployment Manager (GCP)\n- **Modern IaC**: AWS CDK, Azure CDK, Pulumi with TypeScript/Python/Go\n- **GitOps**: Infrastructure automation with ArgoCD, Flux, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI/CD\n- **Policy as Code**: Open Policy Agent (OPA), AWS Config, Azure Policy, GCP Organization Policy\n\n### Cost Optimization & FinOps\n- **Cost monitoring**: CloudWatch, Azure Cost Management, GCP Cost Management, third-party tools (CloudHealth, Cloudability)\n- **Resource optimization**: Right-sizing recommendations, reserved instances, spot instances, committed use discounts\n- **Cost allocation**: Tagging strategies, chargeback models, showback reporting\n- **FinOps practices**: Cost anomaly detection, budget alerts, optimization automation\n- **Multi-cloud cost analysis**: Cross-provider cost comparison, TCO modeling\n\n### Architecture Patterns\n- **Microservices**: Service mesh (Istio, Linkerd), API gateways, service discovery\n- **Serverless**: Function composition, event-driven architectures, cold start optimization\n- **Event-driven**: Message queues, event streaming (Kafka, Kinesis, Event Hubs), CQRS/Event Sourcing\n- **Data architectures**: Data lakes, data warehouses, ETL/ELT pipelines, real-time analytics\n- **AI/ML platforms**: Model serving, MLOps, data pipelines, GPU optimization\n\n### Security & Compliance\n- **Zero-trust architecture**: Identity-based access, network segmentation, encryption everywhere\n- **IAM best practices**: Role-based access, service accounts, cross-account access patterns\n- **Compliance frameworks**: SOC2, HIPAA, PCI-DSS, GDPR, FedRAMP compliance architectures\n- **Security automation**: SAST/DAST integration, infrastructure security scanning\n- **Secrets management**: HashiCorp Vault, cloud-native secret stores, rotation strategies\n\n### Scalability & Performance\n- **Auto-scaling**: Horizontal/vertical scaling, predictive scaling, custom metrics\n- **Load balancing**: Application load balancers, network load balancers, global load balancing\n- **Caching strategies**: CDN, Redis, Memcached, application-level caching\n- **Database scaling**: Read replicas, sharding, connection pooling, database migration\n- **Performance monitoring**: APM tools, synthetic monitoring, real user monitoring\n\n### Disaster Recovery & Business Continuity\n- **Multi-region strategies**: Active-active, active-passive, cross-region replication\n- **Backup strategies**: Point-in-time recovery, cross-region backups, backup automation\n- **RPO/RTO planning**: Recovery time objectives, recovery point objectives, DR testing\n- **Chaos engineering**: Fault injection, resilience testing, failure scenario planning\n\n### Modern DevOps Integration\n- **CI/CD pipelines**: GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, Azure DevOps, AWS CodePipeline\n- **Container orchestration**: EKS, AKS, GKE, self-managed Kubernetes\n- **Observability**: Prometheus, Grafana, DataDog, New Relic, OpenTelemetry\n- **Infrastructure testing**: Terratest, InSpec, Checkov, Terrascan\n\n### Emerging Technologies\n- **Cloud-native technologies**: CNCF landscape, service mesh, Kubernetes operators\n- **Edge computing**: Edge functions, IoT gateways, 5G integration\n- **Quantum computing**: Cloud quantum services, hybrid quantum-classical architectures\n- **Sustainability**: Carbon footprint optimization, green cloud practices\n\n## Behavioral Traits\n- Emphasizes cost-conscious design without sacrificing performance or security\n- Advocates for automation and Infrastructure as Code for all infrastructure changes\n- Designs for failure with multi-AZ/region resilience and graceful degradation\n- Implements security by default with least privilege access and defense in depth\n- Prioritizes observability and monitoring for proactive issue detection\n- Considers vendor lock-in implications and designs for portability when beneficial\n- Stays current with cloud provider updates and emerging architectural patterns\n- Values simplicity and maintainability over complexity\n\n## Knowledge Base\n- AWS, Azure, GCP service catalogs and pricing models\n- Cloud provider security best practices and compliance standards\n- Infrastructure as Code tools and best practices\n- FinOps methodologies and cost optimization strategies\n- Modern architectural patterns and design principles\n- DevOps and CI/CD best practices\n- Observability and monitoring strategies\n- Disaster recovery and business continuity planning\n\n## Response Approach\n1. **Analyze requirements** for scalability, cost, security, and compliance needs\n2. **Recommend appropriate cloud services** based on workload characteristics\n3. **Design resilient architectures** with proper failure handling and recovery\n4. **Provide Infrastructure as Code** implementations with best practices\n5. **Include cost estimates** with optimization recommendations\n6. **Consider security implications** and implement appropriate controls\n7. **Plan for monitoring and observability** from day one\n8. **Document architectural decisions** with trade-offs and alternatives\n\n## Example Interactions\n- \"Design a multi-region, auto-scaling web application architecture on AWS with estimated monthly costs\"\n- \"Create a hybrid cloud strategy connecting on-premises data center with Azure\"\n- \"Optimize our GCP infrastructure costs while maintaining performance and availability\"\n- \"Design a serverless event-driven architecture for real-time data processing\"\n- \"Plan a migration from monolithic application to microservices on Kubernetes\"\n- \"Implement a disaster recovery solution with 4-hour RTO across multiple cloud providers\"\n- \"Design a compliant architecture for healthcare data processing meeting HIPAA requirements\"\n- \"Create a FinOps strategy with automated cost optimization and chargeback reporting\"\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:12:46.156Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Cloud Agents requiring expertise in designing scalable and secure cloud architectures","zh":"适用于需要在设计可扩展和安全的云架构方面具有专业知识的云代理","ja":"スケーラブルでセキュアなクラウドアーキテクチャを設計するための専門知識を必要とするクラウドエージェントに適しています","ko":"확장 가능하고 보안이 강화된 클라우드 아키텍처를 설계하는 전문 지식이 필요한 클라우드 에이전트에 적합합니다","es":"Ideal para agentes en la nube que requieren experiencia en el diseño de arquitecturas de nube escalables y seguras","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Cloud nécessitant une expertise dans la conception d''architectures Cloud évolutives et sécurisées","de":"Ideal für Cloud-Agents, die Expertenwissen im Entwurf von skalierbaren und sicheren Cloud-Architekturen erfordern","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Nuvem que requerem especialização em projetar arquiteturas de nuvem escaláveis e seguras","ru":"Идеально для Облачных Агентов, требующих опыта в проектировании масштабируемых и безопасных облачных архитектур","ar":"مثالي لعميل السحابة الذي يتطلب خبرة في تصميم بنية سحابية قابلة للتطوير وأمنة"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to apply best practices for cloud architect tasks, providing guidance on workflows, checklists, and validation of outcomes using relevant cloud protocols and tools","zh":"使代理能够应用云架构任务的最佳实践，提供有关工作流、检查清单和使用相关云协议和工具验证结果的指导","ja":"エージェントがクラウドアーキテクチャタスクのベストプラクティスを適用できるようにし、ワークフロー、チェックリスト、関連するクラウドプロトコルとツールを使用した結果の検証に関するガイダンスを提供する","ko":"에이전트가 클라우드 아키텍처 작업의 모범 사례를 적용할 수 있도록 하며, 워크플로우, 체크 리스트 및 관련 클라우드 프로토콜 및 도구를 사용한 결과 확인에 대한 지침을 제공합니다","es":"Habilita a los agentes a aplicar las mejores prácticas para tareas de arquitecto de nube, proporcionando orientación sobre flujos de trabajo, listas de verificación y validación de resultados utilizando protocolos y herramientas de nube relevantes","fr":"Permet aux agents d''appliquer les meilleures pratiques pour les tâches d''architecte Cloud, fournissant des conseils sur les flux de travail, les listes de vérification et la validation des résultats en utilisant des protocoles et des outils Cloud pertinents","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, bewährte Verfahren für Cloud-Architektaufgaben anzuwenden, indem sie Anleitungen zu Workflows, Prüflisten und Überprüfung der Ergebnisse unter Verwendung relevanter Cloud-Protokolle und -Tools bereitstellen","pt":"Habilita os agentes a aplicar as melhores práticas para tarefas de arquiteto de nuvem, fornecendo orientação sobre fluxos de trabalho, listas de verificação e validação de resultados usando protocolos e ferramentas de nuvem relevantes","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью применять лучшие практики для задач облачного архитектора, предоставляя рекомендации по рабочим процессам, контрольным спискам и проверке результатов с использованием соответствующих облачных протоколов и инструментов","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من تطبيق أفضل الممارسات للمهام المعمارية السحابية، وتقديم إرشادات حول سير العمل وقوائم التحقق والتحقق من النتائج باستخدام بروتوكولات وأدوات السحابة ذات الصلة"},"useCases":{"en":["Designing hybrid cloud infrastructures","Optimizing cloud resource allocation","Validating cloud security configurations"],"zh":["设计混合云基础设施","优化云资源分配","验证云安全配置"],"ja":["ハイブリッドクラウドインフラストラクチャの設計","クラウドリソースの割り当ての最適化","クラウドセキュリティ設定の検証"],"ko":["하이브리드 클라우드 인프라 설계","클라우드 리소스 할당 최적화","클라우드 보안 구성 확인"],"es":["Diseñar infraestructuras de nube híbridas","Optimizar la asignación de recursos de nube","Validar configuraciones de seguridad de nube"],"fr":["Concevoir des infrastructures Cloud hybrides","Optimiser l''allocation des ressources Cloud","Valider les configurations de sécurité Cloud"],"de":["Entwurf von Hybrid-Cloud-Infrastrukturen","Optimierung der Cloud-Ressourcenzuweisung","Validierung von Cloud-Sicherheitskonfigurationen"],"pt":["Projeto de infraestruturas de nuvem híbrida","Otimização da alocação de recursos de nuvem","Validação de configurações de segurança de nuvem"],"ru":["Проектирование гибридной облачной инфраструктуры","Оптимизация распределения облачных ресурсов","Проверка конфигураций облачной безопасности"],"ar":["تصميم بنية سحابية هجينة","تحسين تخصيص موارد السحابة","تحقق من تفاصيل أمان السحابة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires cloud-specific knowledge","Limited to cloud architect tasks and workflows"],"zh":["需要云特定知识","仅限于云架构任务和工作流"],"ja":["クラウド特有の知識が必要","クラウドアーキテクチャタスクとワークフローのみに限定される"],"ko":["클라우드 특정 지식이 필요","클라우드 아키텍처 작업 및 워크플로에만 제한"],"es":["Requiere conocimientos específicos de nube","Limitado a tareas y flujos de trabajo de arquitecto de nube"],"fr":["Nécessite des connaissances spécifiques au Cloud","Limité aux tâches et flux de travail d''architecte Cloud"],"de":["Erfordert cloud-spezifisches Wissen","Begrenzt auf Cloud-Architektaufgaben und Workflows"],"pt":["Requer conhecimento específico de nuvem","Limitado a tarefas e fluxos de trabalho de arquiteto de nuvem"],"ru":["Требует специальных знаний об облаке","Ограничен задачами и рабочими процессами облачного архитектора"],"ar":["يتطلب معرفة سحابية محددة","محدود بمهام وعمليات معمارية السحابة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":55}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('Dknight203/AesopIDE/context-driven-development', 'community', 'Dknight203', 'AesopIDE', 'Dknight203/AesopIDE', 'context-driven-development', 0, 0, 75, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.475Z', '2026-02-18T09:12:43.052Z', NULL, '{"id":"Dknight203/AesopIDE/context-driven-development","name":"context-driven-development","description":{"zh":"上下文驱动开发是指在代码旁边管理上下文以实现一致的 AI 交互和团队对齐","ja":"コンテキスト駆動開発は、コードとともにコンテキストを管理して一貫性のある AI インタラクションとチームの整列を実現すること","ko":"컨텍스트 주도 개발은 코드와 함께 컨텍스트를 관리하여 일관된 AI 상호 작용 및 팀 정렬을 실현","es":"Guía para implementar y mantener el contexto como un artefacto gestionado junto con el código, permitiendo interacciones de IA coherentes y alineación del equipo a través de la documentación de proyectos estructurada","fr":"Guide pour mettre en œuvre et maintenir le contexte comme un artefact géré aux côtés du code, permettant des interactions IA cohérentes et une alignment de l''équipe via la documentation de projet structurée","de":"Anleitung zur Implementierung und Wartung des Kontexts als verwaltetes Artefakt neben dem Code, ermöglicht konsistente IA-Interaktionen und Teamausrichtung durch strukturierte Projektunterlagen","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por contexto é uma abordagem que permite a gestão do contexto como um artefato gerenciado ao lado do código, possibilitando interações de IA consistentes e alinhamento da equipe","ru":"Разработка, управляемая контекстом, - это подход, который позволяет управлять контекстом как управляемым артефактом наряду с кодом, обеспечивая последовательные взаимодействия ИИ и выравнивание команды","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالسياق هو نهج يسمح بإدارة السياق كartifact可 إدارة إلى جانب الكود، مما يتيح تفاعلات الذكاء الاصطناعي المتسقة وتنسيق الفريق","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"上下文驱动开发：AesopIDE 与 Antigravity 界面","ja":"コンテキスト駆動開発：AesopIDE と Antigravity インターフェイス","ko":"컨텍스트 주도 개발: AesopIDE 및 Antigravity 인터페이스","es":"Desarrollo Dirigido por Contexto: Guía para Devs","fr":"Développement Dirigé par le Contexte: Guide pour les Devs","de":"Kontextgetriebene Entwicklung: Anleitung für Entwickler","pt":"Desenvolvimento Dirigido por Contexto","ru":"Разработка, управляемая контекстом","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالسياق","en":"context-driven-development"},"description":{"zh":"上下文驱动开发是指在代码旁边管理上下文以实现一致的 AI 交互和团队对齐","ja":"コンテキスト駆動開発は、コードとともにコンテキストを管理して一貫性のある AI インタラクションとチームの整列を実現すること","ko":"컨텍스트 주도 개발은 코드와 함께 컨텍스트를 관리하여 일관된 AI 상호 작용 및 팀 정렬을 실현","es":"Guía para implementar y mantener el contexto como un artefacto gestionado junto con el código, permitiendo interacciones de IA coherentes y alineación del eq...","fr":"Guide pour mettre en œuvre et maintenir le contexte comme un artefact géré aux côtés du code, permettant des interactions IA cohérentes et une alignment de l...","de":"Anleitung zur Implementierung und Wartung des Kontexts als verwaltetes Artefakt neben dem Code, ermöglicht konsistente IA-Interaktionen und Teamausrichtung d...","pt":"O desenvolvimento dirigido por contexto é uma abordagem que permite a gestão do contexto como um artefato gerenciado ao lado do código, possibilitando intera...","ru":"Разработка, управляемая контекстом, - это подход, который позволяет управлять контекстом как управляемым артефактом наряду с кодом, обеспечивая последователь...","ar":"التطوير الموجه بالسياق هو نهج يسمح بإدارة السياق كartifact可 إدارة إلى جانب الكود، مما يتيح تفاعلات الذكاء الاصطناعي المتسقة وتنسيق الفريق","en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"definition":{"en":"AesopIDE with Antigravity-inspired UI\""},"features":{"zh":["实现一致的 AI 交互","团队对齐和协作","结构化项目文档","Conductor 项目设置","上下文更新和维护"],"ja":["一貫性のある AI インタラクションを実現","チームの整列とコラボレーション","構造化プロジェクト文書","Conductor プロジェクトの設定","コンテキストの更新と維持"],"ko":["일관된 AI 상호 작용을 실현","팀 정렬 및 협업","구조화된 프로젝트 문서","Conductor 프로젝트 설정","컨텍스트 업데이트 및 유지"],"es":["Implementación de contexto como artefacto gestionado","Interacciones de IA coherentes","Alineación del equipo a través de documentación estructurada","Mantenimiento de la consistencia en las sesiones de desarrollo asistidas por IA","Integración con Conductor"],"fr":["Mise en œuvre du contexte comme artefact géré","Interactions IA cohérentes","Alignement de l''équipe via la documentation structurée","Maintenance de la cohérence dans les sessions de développement assistées par IA","Intégration avec Conductor"],"de":["Implementierung des Kontexts als verwaltetes Artefakt","Konsistente IA-Interaktionen","Teamausrichtung durch strukturierte Projektunterlagen","Wartung der Konsistenz in den von IA unterstützten Entwicklungsessions","Integration mit Conductor"],"pt":["Gestão de contexto como artefato gerenciado","Interações de IA consistentes","Alinhamento da equipe através de documentação estruturada","Integração com Conductor","Suporte à configuração de novos projetos","Manutenção da consistência em sessões de desenvolvimento assistidas por IA"],"ru":["Управление контекстом как управляемым артефактом","Последовательные взаимодействия ИИ","Выравнивание команды через структурированную документацию","Интеграция с Conductor","Поддержка настройки новых проектов","Поддержание согласованности в сессиях разработки, ассистируемых ИИ"],"ar":["إدارة السياق كartifact可 إدارة","تفاعلات الذكاء الاصطناعي المتسقة","تنسيق الفريق من خلال توثيق منظم","التكامل مع Conductor","دعم إعداد مشاريع جديدة","صيانة الاتساق في جلسات التطوير المساعدة بالذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["上下文驱动开发","AesopIDE","Antigravity 界面","AI 交互","团队对齐","结构化项目文档","Conductor 项目"],"ja":["コンテキスト駆動開発","AesopIDE","Antigravity インターフェイス","AI インタラクション","チームの整列","構造化プロジェクト文書","Conductor プロジェクト"],"ko":["컨텍스트 주도 개발","AesopIDE","Antigravity 인터페이스","AI 상호 작용","팀 정렬","구조화된 프로젝트 문서","Conductor 프로젝트"],"es":["desarrollo dirigido por contexto","conductor","interacciones de ia","documentación de proyectos","desarrollo de software","integración de ia","gestión de contexto","coherencia en la ia"],"fr":["développement dirigé par le contexte","conductor","interactions ia","documentation de projet","développement de logiciel","intégration de ia","gestion de contexte","cohérence dans la ia"],"de":["kontextgetriebene entwicklung","conductor","ia-interaktionen","projektunterlagen","softwareentwicklung","ia-integration","kontextverwaltung","konsistenz in der ia"],"pt":["desenvolvimento dirigido por contexto","contexto como artefato","interações de IA","alinhamento da equipe","Conductor","desenvolvimento de software","gestão de contexto","documentação estruturada"],"ru":["разработка, управляемая контекстом","контекст как артефакт","взаимодействия ИИ","выравнивание команды","Conductor","разработка программного обеспечения","управление контекстом","структурированная документация"],"ar":["التطوير الموجه بالسياق","السياق كartifact","تفاعلات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تنسيق الفريق","Conductor","تطوير البرمجيات","إدارة السياق","توثيق منظم"]}},"owner":"Dknight203","repo":"AesopIDE","repoPath":"Dknight203/AesopIDE","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.475Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"context-driven-development","description":"Use this skill when working with Conductors context-driven development methodology, managing project context artifacts, or understanding the relationship between product.md, tech-stack.md, and workflow.md files.","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Context-Driven Development\n\nGuide for implementing and maintaining context as a managed artifact alongside code, enabling consistent AI interactions and team alignment through structured project documentation.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up new projects with Conductor\n- Understanding the relationship between context artifacts\n- Maintaining consistency across AI-assisted development sessions\n- Onboarding team members to an existing Conductor project\n- Deciding when to update context d","body":"# Context-Driven Development\n\nGuide for implementing and maintaining context as a managed artifact alongside code, enabling consistent AI interactions and team alignment through structured project documentation.\n\n## When to Use This Skill\n\n- Setting up new projects with Conductor\n- Understanding the relationship between context artifacts\n- Maintaining consistency across AI-assisted development sessions\n- Onboarding team members to an existing Conductor project\n- Deciding when to update context documents\n- Managing greenfield vs brownfield project contexts\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nContext-Driven Development treats project context as a first-class artifact managed alongside code. Instead of relying on ad-hoc prompts or scattered documentation, establish a persistent, structured foundation that informs all AI interactions.\n\nKey principles:\n\n1. **Context precedes code**: Define what you''re building and how before implementation\n2. **Living documentation**: Context artifacts evolve with the project\n3. **Single source of truth**: One canonical location for each type of information\n4. **AI alignment**: Consistent context produces consistent AI behavior\n\n## The Workflow\n\nFollow the **Context → Spec & Plan → Implement** workflow:\n\n1. **Context Phase**: Establish or verify project context artifacts exist and are current\n2. **Specification Phase**: Define requirements and acceptance criteria for work units\n3. **Planning Phase**: Break specifications into phased, actionable tasks\n4. **Implementation Phase**: Execute tasks following established workflow patterns\n\n## Artifact Relationships\n\n### product.md - Defines WHAT and WHY\n\nPurpose: Captures product vision, goals, target users, and business context.\n\nContents:\n\n- Product name and one-line description\n- Problem statement and solution approach\n- Target user personas\n- Core features and capabilities\n- Success metrics and KPIs\n- Product roadmap (high-level)\n\nUpdate when:\n\n- Product vision or goals change\n- New major features are planned\n- Target audience shifts\n- Business priorities evolve\n\n### product-guidelines.md - Defines HOW to Communicate\n\nPurpose: Establishes brand voice, messaging standards, and communication patterns.\n\nContents:\n\n- Brand voice and tone guidelines\n- Terminology and glossary\n- Error message conventions\n- User-facing copy standards\n- Documentation style\n\nUpdate when:\n\n- Brand guidelines change\n- New terminology is introduced\n- Communication patterns need refinement\n\n### tech-stack.md - Defines WITH WHAT\n\nPurpose: Documents technology choices, dependencies, and architectural decisions.\n\nContents:\n\n- Primary languages and frameworks\n- Key dependencies with versions\n- Infrastructure and deployment targets\n- Development tools and environment\n- Testing frameworks\n- Code quality tools\n\nUpdate when:\n\n- Adding new dependencies\n- Upgrading major versions\n- Changing infrastructure\n- Adopting new tools or patterns\n\n### workflow.md - Defines HOW to Work\n\nPurpose: Establishes development practices, quality gates, and team workflows.\n\nContents:\n\n- Development methodology (TDD, etc.)\n- Git workflow and commit conventions\n- Code review requirements\n- Testing requirements and coverage targets\n- Quality assurance gates\n- Deployment procedures\n\nUpdate when:\n\n- Team practices evolve\n- Quality standards change\n- New workflow patterns are adopted\n\n### tracks.md - Tracks WHAT''S HAPPENING\n\nPurpose: Registry of all work units with status and metadata.\n\nContents:\n\n- Active tracks with current status\n- Completed tracks with completion dates\n- Track metadata (type, priority, assignee)\n- Links to individual track directories\n\nUpdate when:\n\n- New tracks are created\n- Track status changes\n- Tracks are completed or archived\n\n## Context Maintenance Principles\n\n### Keep Artifacts Synchronized\n\nEnsure changes in one artifact reflect in related documents:\n\n- New feature in product.md → Update tech-stack.md if new dependencies needed\n- Completed track → Update product.md to reflect new capabilities\n- Workflow change → Update all affected track plans\n\n### Update tech-stack.md When Adding Dependencies\n\nBefore adding any new dependency:\n\n1. Check if existing dependencies solve the need\n2. Document the rationale for new dependencies\n3. Add version constraints\n4. Note any configuration requirements\n\n### Update product.md When Features Complete\n\nAfter completing a feature track:\n\n1. Move feature from \"planned\" to \"implemented\" in product.md\n2. Update any affected success metrics\n3. Document any scope changes from original plan\n\n### Verify Context Before Implementation\n\nBefore starting any track:\n\n1. Read all context artifacts\n2. Flag any outdated information\n3. Propose updates before proceeding\n4. Confirm context accuracy with stakeholders\n\n## Greenfield vs Brownfield Handling\n\n### Greenfield Projects (New)\n\nFor new projects:\n\n1. Run `/conductor:setup` to create all artifacts interactively\n2. Answer questions about product vision, tech preferences, and workflow\n3. Generate initial style guides for chosen languages\n4. Create empty tracks registry\n\nCharacteristics:\n\n- Full control over context structure\n- Define standards before code exists\n- Establish patterns early\n\n### Brownfield Projects (Existing)\n\nFor existing codebases:\n\n1. Run `/conductor:setup` with existing codebase detection\n2. System analyzes existing code, configs, and documentation\n3. Pre-populate artifacts based on discovered patterns\n4. Review and refine generated context\n\nCharacteristics:\n\n- Extract implicit context from existing code\n- Reconcile existing patterns with desired patterns\n- Document technical debt and modernization plans\n- Preserve working patterns while establishing standards\n\n## Benefits\n\n### Team Alignment\n\n- New team members onboard faster with explicit context\n- Consistent terminology and conventions across the team\n- Shared understanding of product goals and technical decisions\n\n### AI Consistency\n\n- AI assistants produce aligned outputs across sessions\n- Reduced need to re-explain context in each interaction\n- Predictable behavior based on documented standards\n\n### Institutional Memory\n\n- Decisions and rationale are preserved\n- Context survives team changes\n- Historical context informs future decisions\n\n### Quality Assurance\n\n- Standards are explicit and verifiable\n- Deviations from context are detectable\n- Quality gates are documented and enforceable\n\n## Directory Structure\n\n```\nconductor/\n├── index.md              # Navigation hub linking all artifacts\n├── product.md            # Product vision and goals\n├── product-guidelines.md # Communication standards\n├── tech-stack.md         # Technology preferences\n├── workflow.md           # Development practices\n├── tracks.md             # Work unit registry\n├── setup_state.json      # Resumable setup state\n├── code_styleguides/     # Language-specific conventions\n│   ├── python.md\n│   ├── typescript.md\n│   └── ...\n└── tracks/\n    └── <track-id>/\n        ├── spec.md\n        ├── plan.md\n        ├── metadata.json\n        └── index.md\n```\n\n## Context Lifecycle\n\n1. **Creation**: Initial setup via `/conductor:setup`\n2. **Validation**: Verify before each track\n3. **Evolution**: Update as project grows\n4. **Synchronization**: Keep artifacts aligned\n5. **Archival**: Document historical decisions\n\n## Context Validation Checklist\n\nBefore starting implementation on any track, validate context:\n\n### Product Context\n\n- [ ] product.md reflects current product vision\n- [ ] Target users are accurately described\n- [ ] Feature list is up to date\n- [ ] Success metrics are defined\n\n### Technical Context\n\n- [ ] tech-stack.md lists all current dependencies\n- [ ] Version numbers are accurate\n- [ ] Infrastructure targets are correct\n- [ ] Development tools are documented\n\n### Workflow Context\n\n- [ ] workflow.md describes current practices\n- [ ] Quality gates are defined\n- [ ] Coverage targets are specified\n- [ ] Commit conventions are documented\n\n### Track Context\n\n- [ ] tracks.md shows all active work\n- [ ] No stale or abandoned tracks\n- [ ] Dependencies between tracks are noted\n\n## Common Anti-Patterns\n\nAvoid these context management mistakes:\n\n### Stale Context\n\nProblem: Context documents become outdated and misleading.\nSolution: Update context as part of each track''s completion process.\n\n### Context Sprawl\n\nProblem: Information scattered across multiple locations.\nSolution: Use the defined artifact structure; resist creating new document types.\n\n### Implicit Context\n\nProblem: Relying on knowledge not captured in artifacts.\nSolution: If you reference something repeatedly, add it to the appropriate artifact.\n\n### Context Hoarding\n\nProblem: One person maintains context without team input.\nSolution: Review context artifacts in pull requests; make updates collaborative.\n\n### Over-Specification\n\nProblem: Context becomes so detailed it''s impossible to maintain.\nSolution: Keep artifacts focused on decisions that affect AI behavior and team alignment.\n\n## Integration with Development Tools\n\n### IDE Integration\n\nConfigure your IDE to display context files prominently:\n\n- Pin conductor/product.md for quick reference\n- Add tech-stack.md to project notes\n- Create snippets for common patterns from style guides\n\n### Git Hooks\n\nConsider pre-commit hooks that:\n\n- Warn when dependencies change without tech-stack.md update\n- Remind to update product.md when feature branches merge\n- Validate context artifact syntax\n\n### CI/CD Integration\n\nInclude context validation in pipelines:\n\n- Check tech-stack.md matches actual dependencies\n- Verify links in context documents resolve\n- Ensure tracks.md status matches git branch state\n\n## Session Continuity\n\nConductor supports multi-session development through context persistence:\n\n### Starting a New Session\n\n1. Read index.md to orient yourself\n2. Check tracks.md for active work\n3. Review relevant track''s plan.md for current task\n4. Verify context artifacts are current\n\n### Ending a Session\n\n1. Update plan.md with current progress\n2. Note any blockers or decisions made\n3. Commit in-progress work with clear status\n4. Update tracks.md if status changed\n\n### Handling Interruptions\n\nIf interrupted mid-task:\n\n1. Mark task as `[~]` with note about stopping point\n2. Commit work-in-progress to feature branch\n3. Document any uncommitted decisions in plan.md\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Read context first**: Always read relevant artifacts before starting work\n2. **Small updates**: Make incremental context changes, not massive rewrites\n3. **Link decisions**: Reference context when making implementation choices\n4. **Version context**: Commit context changes alongside code changes\n5. **Review context**: Include context artifact reviews in code reviews\n6. **Validate regularly**: Run context validation checklist before major work\n7. **Communicate changes**: Notify team when context artifacts change significantly\n8. **Preserve history**: Use git to track context evolution over time\n9. **Question staleness**: If context feels wrong, investigate and update\n10. **Keep it actionable**: Every context item should inform a decision or behavior\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:12:43.052Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Conductor-enabled AI Agents requiring structured project documentation and context management alongside code.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化项目文档和上下文管理的 Conductor 启用的 AI Agents。","ja":"Conductor 有効化された AI エージェントが構造化されたプロジェクトの文書化とコンテキスト管理を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"Conductor가 활성화된 AI 에이전트가 구조화된 프로젝트 문서화와 컨텍스트 관리를 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de IA habilitados para Conductor que requieren documentación de proyecto estructurada y gestión de contexto junto con el código.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents IA compatibles Conductor nécessitant une documentation de projet structurée et une gestion de contexte aux côtés du code.","de":"Perfekt für Conductor-aktivierte KI-Agents, die eine strukturierte Projektdokumentation und Kontextverwaltung neben dem Code benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de IA habilitados para Conductor que exigem documentação de projeto estruturada e gerenciamento de contexto ao lado do código.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов ИИ, поддерживающих Conductor, требующих структурированной документации проекта и управления контекстом наряду с кодом.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكية المدعومة من Conductor التي تتطلب توثيق مشروع منظمًا وإدارة السياق جنبًا إلى جنب مع الشفرة."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to maintain consistency across AI-assisted development sessions through managed context artifacts, enabling seamless team alignment and efficient onboarding processes using Conductor, while ensuring consistent AI interactions.","zh":"通过管理的上下文工件，实现 AI 辅助开发会话的一致性，促进团队无缝对齐和高效的入职流程，同时确保一致的 AI 交互。","ja":"管理されたコンテキスト・アーティファクトを使用して、AI アシスト開発セッションの一貫性を維持し、チームの無駄な作業を排除し、効率的なオンボーディングプロセスを可能にし、同時に一貫した AI インタラクションを保証します。","ko":"관리되는 컨텍스트 아티팩트를 통해 AI 지원 개발 세션의 일관성을 유지하고, 팀의 무결성을 보장하며, 효율적인 온보딩 프로세스를 가능하게 하며,同時에 일관된 AI 상호작용을 보장합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a mantener la consistencia en las sesiones de desarrollo asistidas por IA a través de artefactos de contexto administrados, lo que permite una alineación en equipo sin problemas y procesos de incorporación eficientes que utilizan Conductor, al mismo tiempo que garantiza interacciones de IA coherentes.","fr":"Permet aux agents de maintenir la cohérence à travers les sessions de développement assistées par IA grâce à des artefacts de contexte gérés, permettant une alignement d''équipe sans heurts et des processus d''intégration efficaces utilisant Conductor, tout en garantissant des interactions d''IA cohérentes.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agents, Konsistenz über KI-unterstützte Entwicklungssitzungen hinweg durch verwaltete Kontextartefakte aufrechtzuerhalten, wodurch eine nahtlose Teamausrichtung und effiziente Onboarding-Prozesse mit Conductor ermöglicht werden, während gleichzeitig konsistente KI-Interaktionen sichergestellt sind.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a manter a consistência em sessões de desenvolvimento assistidas por IA por meio de artefatos de contexto gerenciados, permitindo uma alinhamento de equipe sem interrupções e processos de integração eficientes usando o Conductor, garantindo interações de IA consistentes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью поддерживать согласованность на протяжении сессий разработки с помощью ИИ посредством управляемых артефактов контекста, обеспечивая бесперебойную согласованность команд и эффективные процессы интеграции с использованием Conductor, гарантируя последовательные взаимодействия ИИ.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من الحفاظ على التماسك عبر جلسات التطوير المدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي من خلال إدارة مكونات السياق، وتمكين انسجام الفريق بدون انقطاع وعمليات توجيه فعالة باستخدام Conductor، مع ضمان تفاعلات الذكاء الاصطناعي المتسقة."},"useCases":{"en":["Setting up new projects with structured context documentation","Maintaining consistency across AI-assisted development sessions","Onboarding team members to existing Conductor projects with clear context","Updating context artifacts to reflect project changes"],"zh":["设置具有结构化上下文文档的新项目","在 AI 辅助开发会话中保持一致性","将团队成员入职到现有的 Conductor 项目中，具有清晰的上下文","更新上下文工件以反映项目更改"],"ja":["構造化されたコンテキスト文書を持つ新しいプロジェクトを設定する","AI アシスト開発セッションの一貫性を維持する","チームメンバーを既存の Conductor プロジェクトにオンボーディングする、明確なコンテキストを伴う","コンテキスト・アーティファクトを更新してプロジェクトの変更を反映する"],"ko":["구조화된 컨텍스트 문서를 갖는 새로운 프로젝트 설정","AI 지원 개발 세션에서 일관성을 유지","팀 구성원을 기존의 Conductor 프로젝트에 온보딩하여, 명확한 컨텍스트를 제공","컨텍스트 아티팩트를 업데이트하여 프로젝트 변경을 반영"],"es":["Configuración de nuevos proyectos con documentación de contexto estructurada","Mantenimiento de la consistencia en las sesiones de desarrollo asistidas por IA","Incorporación de miembros del equipo a proyectos de Conductor existentes con contexto claro","Actualización de artefactos de contexto para reflejar los cambios del proyecto"],"fr":["Configuration de nouveaux projets avec une documentation de contexte structurée","Maintenance de la cohérence à travers les sessions de développement assistées par IA","Intégration des membres de l''équipe aux projets Conductor existants avec un contexte clair","Mise à jour des artefacts de contexte pour refléter les modifications du projet"],"de":["Einrichtung neuer Projekte mit strukturierter Kontextdokumentation","Aufrechterhaltung der Konsistenz über KI-unterstützte Entwicklungssitzungen hinweg","Onboarding von Teammitgliedern in bestehende Conductor-Projekte mit klarem Kontext","Aktualisierung von Kontextartefakten, um Änderungen des Projekts widerzuspiegeln"],"pt":["Configurar novos projetos com documentação de contexto estruturada","Manter a consistência em sessões de desenvolvimento assistidas por IA","Integrar membros da equipe a projetos existentes do Conductor com contexto claro","Atualizar artefatos de contexto para refletir alterações de projeto"],"ru":["Настройка новых проектов со структурированной документацией контекста","Поддержание согласованности на протяжении сессий разработки с помощью ИИ","Интеграция членов команды в существующие проекты Conductor с четким контекстом","Обновление артефактов контекста для отражения изменений проекта"],"ar":["تكوين مشاريع جديدة مع توثيق سياق منظم","الحفاظ على التماسك عبر جلسات التطوير المدعومة بالذكاء الاصطناعي","توجيه أعضاء الفريق إلى مشاريع Conductor الحالية مع سياق واضح","تحديث مكونات السياق لتعكس التغييرات في المشروع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Conductor setup","Limited to projects with managed context artifacts","Dependent on team adherence to context-driven development practices"],"zh":["需要 Conductor 设置","仅限于具有管理的上下文工件的项目","依赖于团队遵循上下文驱动的开发实践"],"ja":["Conductor の設定が必要","管理されたコンテキスト・アーティファクトを持つプロジェクトに限定される","コンテキスト駆動の開発実践に従うチームに依存する"],"ko":["Conductor 설정이 필요","관리되는 컨텍스트 아티팩트를 갖