y/cb-reborn","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.475Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"frontend-to-backend-requirements","description":"Document frontend data needs for backend developers. Use when frontend needs to communicate API requirements to backend, or user says backend requirements, what data do I need, API requirements, or is describing data needs for a UI.","bodyPreview":"# Backend Requirements Mode\n\nYou are a frontend developer documenting what data you need from backend. You describe the **what**, not the **how**. Backend owns implementation details.\n\n> **No Chat Output**: ALL responses go to `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`\n> **No Implementation Details**: Don''t specify endpoints, field names, or API structure—that''s backend''s call.\n\n---\n\n## The Point\n\nThis mode is for frontend devs to communicate data needs:\n- What data do I need to re","body":"# Backend Requirements Mode\n\nYou are a frontend developer documenting what data you need from backend. You describe the **what**, not the **how**. Backend owns implementation details.\n\n> **No Chat Output**: ALL responses go to `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`\n> **No Implementation Details**: Don''t specify endpoints, field names, or API structure—that''s backend''s call.\n\n---\n\n## The Point\n\nThis mode is for frontend devs to communicate data needs:\n- What data do I need to render this screen?\n- What actions should the user be able to perform?\n- What business rules affect the UI?\n- What states and errors should I handle?\n\n**You''re requesting, not demanding.** Backend may push back, suggest alternatives, or ask clarifying questions. That''s healthy collaboration.\n\n---\n\n## What You Own vs. What Backend Owns\n\n| Frontend Owns | Backend Owns |\n|---------------|--------------|\n| What data is needed | How data is structured |\n| What actions exist | Endpoint design |\n| UI states to handle | Field names, types |\n| User-facing validation | API conventions |\n| Display requirements | Performance/caching |\n\n---\n\n## Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Describe the Feature\n\nBefore listing requirements:\n\n1. **What is this?** — Screen, flow, component\n2. **Who uses it?** — User type, permissions\n3. **What''s the goal?** — What does success look like?\n\n### Step 2: List Data Needs\n\nFor each screen/component, describe:\n\n**Data I need to display:**\n- What information appears on screen?\n- What''s the relationship between pieces?\n- What determines visibility/state?\n\n**Actions user can perform:**\n- What can the user do?\n- What''s the expected outcome?\n- What feedback should they see?\n\n**States I need to handle:**\n- Loading, empty, error, success\n- Edge cases (partial data, expired, etc.)\n\n### Step 3: Surface Uncertainties\n\nList what you''re unsure about:\n- Business rules you don''t fully understand\n- Edge cases you''re not sure how to handle\n- Places where you''re guessing\n\n**These invite backend to clarify or push back.**\n\n### Step 4: Leave Room for Discussion\n\nEnd with open questions:\n- \"Would it make sense to...?\"\n- \"Should I expect...?\"\n- \"Is there a simpler way to...?\"\n\n---\n\n## Output Format\n\nCreate `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Backend Requirements: <Feature Name>\n\n## Context\n[What we''re building, who it''s for, what problem it solves]\n\n## Screens/Components\n\n### <Screen/Component Name>\n**Purpose**: What this screen does\n\n**Data I need to display**:\n- [Description of data piece, not field name]\n- [Another piece]\n- [Relationships between pieces]\n\n**Actions**:\n- [Action description] → [Expected outcome]\n- [Another action] → [Expected outcome]\n\n**States to handle**:\n- **Empty**: [When/why this happens]\n- **Loading**: [What''s being fetched]\n- **Error**: [What can go wrong, what user sees]\n- **Special**: [Any edge cases]\n\n**Business rules affecting UI**:\n- [Rule that changes what''s visible/enabled]\n- [Permissions that affect actions]\n\n### <Next Screen/Component>\n...\n\n## Uncertainties\n- [ ] Not sure if [X] should show when [Y]\n- [ ] Don''t understand the business rule for [Z]\n- [ ] Guessing that [A] means [B]\n\n## Questions for Backend\n- Would it make sense to combine [X] and [Y]?\n- Should I expect [Z] to always be present?\n- Is there existing data I can reuse for [W]?\n\n## Discussion Log\n[Backend responses, decisions made, changes to requirements]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Good vs. Bad Requests\n\n### Bad (Dictating Implementation)\n> \"I need a GET /api/contracts endpoint that returns an array with fields: id, title, status, created_at\"\n\n### Good (Describing Needs)\n> \"I need to show a list of contracts. Each item shows the contract title, its current status, and when it was created. User should be able to filter by status.\"\n\n### Bad (Assuming Structure)\n> \"The provider object should be nested inside the contract response\"\n\n### Good (Describing Relationship)\n> \"For each contract, I need to show who the provider is (their name and maybe logo)\"\n\n### Bad (No Context)\n> \"I need contract data\"\n\n### Good (With Context)\n> \"On the dashboard, there''s a ''Recent Contracts'' widget showing the 5 most recent contracts. User clicks one to go to detail page.\"\n\n---\n\n## Encouraging Pushback\n\nInclude these prompts in your requirements:\n\n- \"Let me know if this doesn''t make sense for how the data is structured\"\n- \"Open to suggestions on a better approach\"\n- \"Not sure if this is the right way to think about it\"\n- \"Push back if this complicates things unnecessarily\"\n\n**Good collaboration = frontend describes the problem, backend proposes the solution.**\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\n- **NO IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS**—don''t specify endpoints, methods, field names\n- **DESCRIBE, DON''T PRESCRIBE**—say what you need, not how to provide it\n- **INCLUDE CONTEXT**—why you need it helps backend make better choices\n- **SURFACE UNKNOWNS**—don''t hide confusion, invite clarification\n- **INVITE PUSHBACK**—explicitly ask for backend''s input\n- **UPDATE THE DOC**—add backend responses to Discussion Log\n- **STAY HUMBLE**—you''re asking, not demanding\n\n---\n\n## After Backend Responds\n\nUpdate the requirements doc:\n1. Add responses to Discussion Log\n2. Adjust requirements based on feedback\n3. Mark resolved uncertainties\n4. Note any decisions made\n\nThe doc becomes the source of truth for what was agreed.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:13:41.583Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Full Stack Agents needing to streamline frontend-to-backend communication and documentation","zh":"适合需要简化前端到后端通信和文档的全栈代理","ja":"フルスタックエージェントがフロントエンドからバックエンドへのコミュニケーションとドキュメントを簡素化する必要がある場合に最適","ko":"전체 스택 에이전트가 프론트 엔드에서 백 엔드까지의 통신과 문서를 간소화해야 하는 경우에 적합","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Full Stack que necesitan optimizar la comunicación y documentación de frontend a backend","fr":"Idéal pour les agents Full Stack ayant besoin de rationaliser la communication et la documentation de frontend à backend","de":"Perfekt für Full-Stack-Agents, die die Kommunikation und Dokumentation von Frontend zu Backend optimieren müssen","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes Full Stack que precisam otimizar a comunicação e a documentação do frontend para o backend","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов Full Stack, которым необходимо оптимизировать связь между frontend и backend и документацию","ar":"مثالي لعميل البرمجيات الكاملة الذين يحتاجون إلى简يم التواصل والتوثيق من الجانب الأمامي إلى الجانب الخلفي"},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to effectively document data needs using Markdown files, specifically generating backend requirements in `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md` format, while avoiding implementation details like endpoint specifications and API structures","zh":"赋予代理有效记录数据需求的能力，使用Markdown文件，特别是在`.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`格式中生成后端需求，同时避免实现细节，如端点规范和API结构","ja":"エージェントにデータ要件を効果的に文書化する能力を付与し、Markdownファイルを使用し、特に`.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`形式でバックエンド要件を生成し、エンドポイントの仕様やAPI構造などの実装の詳細を避ける","ko":"에이전트에게 데이터 요구 사항을 효과적으로 문서화하는 능력을 부여하고, Markdown 파일을 사용하고, 특히 `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md` 형식으로 백엔드 요구 사항을 생성하며, 엔드ポイント 사양 또는 API 구조와 같은 구현 세부 정보를 피함","es":"Habilita a los agentes a documentar eficazmente las necesidades de datos utilizando archivos Markdown, generando específicamente requisitos de backend en formato `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`, mientras evita detalles de implementación como especificaciones de puntos de conexión y estructuras de API","fr":"Permet aux agents de documenter efficacement les besoins de données en utilisant des fichiers Markdown, en générant spécifiquement des exigences de backend au format `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`, tout en évitant les détails d''implémentation tels que les spécifications de points de terminaison et les structures d''API","de":"Ermöglicht es Agenten, Datenanforderungen effektiv mithilfe von Markdown-Dateien zu dokumentieren, insbesondere die Generierung von Backend-Anforderungen im Format `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`, während Implementierungsdetails wie Endpunktspezifikationen und API-Strukturen vermieden werden","pt":"Habilita os agentes a documentar efetivamente as necessidades de dados usando arquivos Markdown, gerando especificações de requisitos de backend no formato `.claude/docs/ai/<nome-da-funcionalidade>/requisitos-de-backend.md`, sem incluir detalhes de implementação como especificações de endpoint e estruturas de API","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью эффективно документировать потребности в данных с помощью файлов Markdown, генерируя требования к бэкенду в формате `.claude/docs/ai/<имя-функции>/требования-бэкенда.md`, при этом избегая деталей реализации, таких как спецификации конечных точек и структуры API","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على توثيق احتياجات البيانات بشكل فعال باستخدام ملفات Markdown، وتنظيف متطلبات الخلفية في تنسيق `.claude/docs/ai/<اسم-الميزة>/متطلبات-الخلفية.md`، مع تجنب تفاصيل التنفيذ مثل مواصفات النقطة النهائية وهيكل واجهة برمجة التطبيقات"},"useCases":{"en":["Documenting data requirements for new features","Communicating frontend needs to backend teams","Generating backend requirements documents in Markdown"],"zh":["记录新功能的数据要求","将前端需求传达给后端团队","在Markdown中生成后端要求文档"],"ja":["新機能のデータ要件を文書化する","フロントエンドの要件をバックエンドチームに伝える","Markdownでバックエンド要件ドキュメントを生成する"],"ko":["새로운 기능의 데이터 요구 사항을 문서화하는 것","프론트 엔드 요구 사항을 백 엔드 팀에 전달하는 것","Markdown에서 백엔드 요구 사항 문서를 생성하는 것"],"es":["Documentar requisitos de datos para nuevas características","Comunicar necesidades de frontend a equipos de backend","Generar documentos de requisitos de backend en Markdown"],"fr":["Documenter les besoins de données pour les nouvelles fonctionnalités","Communiquer les besoins de frontend aux équipes de backend","Générer des documents d''exigences de backend en Markdown"],"de":["Dokumentation von Datenanforderungen für neue Funktionen","Kommunikation von Frontend-Anforderungen an Backend-Teams","Generierung von Backend-Anforderungsdokumenten in Markdown"],"pt":["Documentar requisitos de dados para novas funcionalidades","Comunicar necessidades do frontend para equipes de backend","Gerar documentos de requisitos de backend em Markdown"],"ru":["Документирование требований к данным для новых функций","Общение потребностей frontend с командами backend","Генерация документов требований к бэкенду в формате Markdown"],"ar":["توثيق متطلبات البيانات للميزات الجديدة","التواصل بين احتياجات الجانب الأمامي مع فرق الجانب الخلفي","إنشاء مستندات متطلبات الخلفية بالتنسيق Markdown"]},"limitations":{"en":["No implementation details allowed","Output limited to `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md` files","Requires adherence to backend requirements documentation protocol"],"zh":["不允许实现细节","输出仅限于`.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`文件","需要遵守后端要求文档协议"],"ja":["実装の詳細を許可しない","出力は`.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`ファイルに限定される","バックエンド要件ドキュメントプロトコルに従う必要がある"],"ko":["구현 세부 정보를 허용하지 않음","출력은 `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md` 파일로 제한됨","백엔드 요구 사항 문서 프로토콜을 따라야 함"],"es":["No se permiten detalles de implementación","Salida limitada a archivos `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`","Requiere adherencia al protocolo de documentación de requisitos de backend"],"fr":["Aucun détail d''implémentation n''est autorisé","Sortie limitée aux fichiers `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`","Nécessite l''adhésion au protocole de documentation des exigences de backend"],"de":["Keine Implementierungsdetails erlaubt","Ausgabe beschränkt auf Dateien `.claude/docs/ai/<feature-name>/backend-requirements.md`","Erfordert die Einhaltung des Protokolls für die Dokumentation von Backend-Anforderungen"],"pt":["Não são permitidos detalhes de implementação","Saída limitada a arquivos `.claude/docs/ai/<nome-da-funcionalidade>/requisitos-de-backend.md`","Exige aderência ao protocolo de documentação de requisitos de backend"],"ru":["Не допускаются детали реализации","Выход ограничен файлами `.claude/docs/ai/<имя-функции>/требования-бэкенда.md`","Требуется соблюдение протокола документирования требований к бэкенду"],"ar":["لا يسمح بالتفاصيل التنفيذية","الخرج محدد بالملفات `.claude/docs/ai/<اسم-الميزة>/متطلبات-الخلفية.md`","يتطلب اتباع بروتوكول توثيق متطلبات الخلفية"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":65}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('ShouxinZhang/tree-thoughts-notes/build-check', 'community', 'ShouxinZhang', 'tree-thoughts-notes', 'ShouxinZhang/tree-thoughts-notes', 'build-check', 0, 0, 0, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.475Z', '2026-02-18T09:13:12.445Z', NULL, '{"id":"ShouxinZhang/tree-thoughts-notes/build-check","name":"build-check","description":{"zh":"构建检查规范是一套代码检查和测试的标准流程，确保代码质量和稳定性","ja":"ビルドチェック規約はコードのチェックとテストの標準的なプロセスであり、コードの品質と安定性を保証する","ko":"빌드 체크 규약은 코드의 체크와 테스트의 표준적인 프로세스로서 코드의 품질과 안정성을 보장합니다","es":"Build-check es una herramienta que ayuda a los desarrolladores a verificar y corregir errores en su código de manera automática","fr":"Build-check est un outil qui aide les développeurs à vérifier et corriger les erreurs dans leur code de manière automatique","de":"Build-check ist ein Tool, das Entwicklern hilft, Fehler in ihrem Code automatisch zu überprüfen und zu korrigieren","pt":"O skill build-check é uma ferramenta que ajuda a garantir a qualidade do código, executando verificações e testes após cada alteração","ru":"Умение build-check - это инструмент, который помогает обеспечить качество кода, выполняя проверки и тесты после каждого изменения","ar":"مهارة build-check هي أداة تساعد على ضمان جودة الكود من خلال تشغيل الفحوصات والاختبارات بعد كل تعديل","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"构建检查规范 - build-check 技术概览","ja":"ビルドチェック規約 - build-check 技術概要","ko":"빌드 체크 규약 - build-check 기술 개요","es":"build-check: Herramienta de verificación de construcción","fr":"build-check : Outil de vérification de construction","de":"build-check: Build-Überprüfungstool","pt":"Verificação de Construção de Código","ru":"Проверка сборки кода","ar":"فحص بناء الكود","en":"build-check"},"description":{"zh":"构建检查规范是一套代码检查和测试的标准流程，确保代码质量和稳定性","ja":"ビルドチェック規約はコードのチェックとテストの標準的なプロセスであり、コードの品質と安定性を保証する","ko":"빌드 체크 규약은 코드의 체크와 테스트의 표준적인 프로세스로서 코드의 품질과 안정성을 보장합니다","es":"Build