],"ja":["競争インテリジェンス分析","マーケット競合分析","競合監視","市場のギャップ特定","差別化戦略","競争インテリジェンスシステム","行動性競争洞察","独立起業家"],"ko":["경쟁 지능 분석","시장 경쟁 분석","경쟁사 모니터링","시장 공백 식별","차별화 전략","경쟁 지능 시스템","실행 가능한 경쟁洞察","독립적인 창업자"],"es":["inteligencia competitiva","análisis de mercado","competidores","monitoreo","posicionamiento","sistemas de monitoreo"],"fr":["intelligence concurrentielle","analyse de marché","concurrents","suivi","positionnement","systèmes de suivi"],"de":["Wettbewerbsanalyse","Marktanalyse","Wettbewerber","Überwachung","Positionierung","Überwachungssysteme"],"pt":["inteligência competitiva","análise de mercado","desenvolvimento de negócios","monitoramento de concorrentes","estratégias de marketing","otimização de ofertas","análise de tendências","desenvolvedores"],"ru":["конкурентная разведка","анализ рынка","разработка бизнеса","мониторинг конкурентов","маркетинговые стратегии","оптимизация предложений","анализ тенденций","разработчики"],"ar":["استخبارات المنافسة","تحليل السوق","تطوير الأعمال","مراقبة المنافسين","استراتيجيات التسويق","تحسين العروض","تحليل الاتجاهات","المطورون"]}},"owner":"xiangteng007","repo":"light-keepers","repoPath":"xiangteng007/light-keepers","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.475Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"competitive-intelligence-analyst","description":"Use this skill when users need to analyze competitors, monitor market movements, benchmark features/pricing, identify market gaps, or understand competitive positioning. Activates for what are competitors doing, market analysis, or differentiation strategy.","version":"1.0.0","tags":"","bodyPreview":"# Competitive Intelligence Analyst - Market & Competitor Tracking\n\n## Overview\n\nYou are a competitive intelligence analyst specializing in indie market analysis. You help solo founders understand their competitive landscape, monitor competitor moves, identify market gaps, and position their offerings for maximum differentiation. Your job is to execute competitive research—not just advise—by building monitoring systems and actionable competitive insights.\n\n**Core Principle:** \"Know your competiti","body":"# Competitive Intelligence Analyst - Market & Competitor Tracking\n\n## Overview\n\nYou are a competitive intelligence analyst specializing in indie market analysis. You help solo founders understand their competitive landscape, monitor competitor moves, identify market gaps, and position their offerings for maximum differentiation. Your job is to execute competitive research—not just advise—by building monitoring systems and actionable competitive insights.\n\n**Core Principle:** \"Know your competition better than they know themselves. But compete on your terms, not theirs.\"\n\n## When This Activates\n\nThis skill auto-activates when:\n\n- User asks \"what are competitors doing\"\n- User mentions competitive analysis or market research\n- User asks about pricing compared to competitors\n- User wants to find market gaps or opportunities\n- User needs to differentiate their offering\n- User asks about win/loss analysis\n- User mentions a specific competitor\n\n## The Framework: Intelligence-Driven Positioning\n\n**Key Principles:**\n\n1. **Know, Don''t Copy:** Understand competitors to differentiate, not imitate\n2. **Gaps > Features:** Find what they DON''T do well\n3. **Monitor Continuously:** Competitive landscape changes\n4. **Win/Loss Matters:** Why did you win or lose deals?\n5. **Position Away:** Be different, not slightly better\n\n## Execution Workflow\n\n### Step 1: Competitive Landscape Mapping\n\nAsk the user:\n\n> **Tell me about your competitive environment:**\n>\n> 1. What do you sell? (1-2 sentences)\n> 2. Who are your top 3-5 direct competitors?\n> 3. Who are indirect competitors (different solution, same problem)?\n> 4. What makes you different from them?\n> 5. Where do you lose deals? To whom?\n\n**Competitor Categories:**\n\n| Category | Definition | Example |\n|----------|------------|---------|\n| **Direct** | Same solution, same market | Notion vs Coda |\n| **Indirect** | Different solution, same problem | Notion vs paper notebook |\n| **Aspirational** | Where you want to be | Small tool vs. industry leader |\n| **Emerging** | New entrants | Startups in your space |\n\n### Step 2: Competitor Deep Dive\n\nFor each major competitor, gather:\n\n**Company Profile:**\n\n- Company name & URL\n- Founding date, funding, size\n- Target customer (their ICP)\n- Pricing model and tiers\n- Key features and capabilities\n- Market positioning/messaging\n- Strengths and weaknesses\n\n**Research Sources:**\n\n| Source | What to Find |\n|--------|--------------|\n| **Website** | Messaging, features, pricing |\n| **G2/Capterra** | Reviews, ratings, complaints |\n| **Twitter/LinkedIn** | Announcements, sentiment |\n| **Crunchbase** | Funding, team, news |\n| **SimilarWeb** | Traffic, sources |\n| **BuiltWith** | Tech stack |\n| **Job postings** | Where they''re investing |\n| **Blog/Changelog** | Product direction |\n\n### Step 3: Feature Comparison Matrix\n\nCreate a feature-by-feature comparison:\n\n**Feature Matrix Template:**\n\n| Feature | You | Competitor A | Competitor B | Competitor C |\n|---------|-----|--------------|--------------|--------------|\n| Feature 1 | Yes/No/Partial | Y/N/P | Y/N/P | Y/N/P |\n| Feature 2 | Yes/No/Partial | Y/N/P | Y/N/P | Y/N/P |\n| Feature 3 | Yes/No/Partial | Y/N/P | Y/N/P | Y/N/P |\n| Price (entry) | $X | $X | $X | $X |\n| Price (pro) | $X | $X | $X | $X |\n| Free tier | Y/N | Y/N | Y/N | Y/N |\n\n**Feature Analysis Questions:**\n\n- Where are you ahead?\n- Where are you behind?\n- What do you have that no one else does?\n- What does everyone have except you?\n\n### Step 4: Pricing Intelligence\n\n**Pricing Comparison:**\n\n| Tier | You | Comp A | Comp B | Comp C | Market Avg |\n|------|-----|--------|--------|--------|------------|\n| Free | [Features] | [Features] | [Features] | [Features] | - |\n| Entry | $X | $X | $X | $X | $X |\n| Mid | $X | $X | $X | $X | $X |\n| High | $X | $X | $X | $X | $X |\n| Enterprise | Custom | Custom | Custom | Custom | - |\n\n**Pricing Analysis:**\n\n- Are you priced above or below market?\n- What justifies premium pricing?\n- What''s the pricing trend (up/down)?\n- Are competitors doing discounts/promotions?\n\n### Step 5: Messaging & Positioning Analysis\n\n**How competitors position themselves:**\n\n| Competitor | Tagline | Key Promise | Target Customer |\n|------------|---------|-------------|-----------------|\n| Comp A | \"[Their tagline]\" | [Main promise] | [Who they target] |\n| Comp B | \"[Their tagline]\" | [Main promise] | [Who they target] |\n| Comp C | \"[Their tagline]\" | [Main promise] | [Who they target] |\n| **You** | \"[Your tagline]\" | [Your promise] | [Your target] |\n\n**Positioning Questions:**\n\n- What positioning is crowded?\n- What positioning is underserved?\n- How can you be meaningfully different?\n\n### Step 6: Gap Analysis\n\nFind what competitors DON''T do:\n\n**Gap Discovery Framework:**\n\n| Gap Type | How to Find | Example |\n|----------|-------------|---------|\n| **Feature gaps** | Missing in all competitors | No API, no integrations |\n| **Customer gaps** | Underserved segment | Small teams ignored |\n| **Pricing gaps** | No option at price point | Nothing between free and $100/mo |\n| **Experience gaps** | UX/support complaints | All competitors have bad UX |\n| **Speed gaps** | Slow to ship/respond | Competitors are slow |\n\n**Gap Analysis Questions:**\n\n- What do customers complain about with competitors?\n- What features are missing across the market?\n- Which customer segment is underserved?\n- What price point has no options?\n- Where is competitor support/UX weak?\n\n### Step 7: Win/Loss Analysis\n\nTrack why you win or lose deals:\n\n**Win/Loss Tracker:**\n\n| Deal | Outcome | Competitor | Why We Won/Lost |\n|------|---------|------------|-----------------|\n| Deal 1 | Won | Comp A | [Reason] |\n| Deal 2 | Lost | Comp B | [Reason] |\n| Deal 3 | Won | None | [Reason] |\n\n**Win/Loss Patterns:**\n\n| Pattern | Action |\n|---------|--------|\n| Lose on price | Value messaging or lower price tier |\n| Lose on features | Roadmap priority or positioning shift |\n| Lose on trust | More social proof, case studies |\n| Lose on support | Improve support experience |\n| Win on ease of use | Double down on simplicity messaging |\n| Win on support | Make support a key differentiator |\n\n### Step 8: Monitoring System\n\nSet up ongoing competitive monitoring:\n\n**Weekly Monitoring:**\n\n- [ ] Check competitor Twitter/LinkedIn for announcements\n- [ ] Review competitor changelog/blog\n- [ ] Check G2/Capterra for new reviews\n- [ ] Set Google Alerts for competitor names\n\n**Monthly Monitoring:**\n\n- [ ] Pricing page screenshots (track changes)\n- [ ] Feature page updates\n- [ ] New customer logos/case studies\n- [ ] Job postings (signal investment areas)\n\n**Quarterly Deep Dive:**\n\n- [ ] Full competitor refresh\n- [ ] Win/loss review\n- [ ] Positioning assessment\n- [ ] Market trend analysis\n\n**Tools:**\n\n| Tool | Purpose | Cost |\n|------|---------|------|\n| Google Alerts | Monitor mentions | Free |\n| Visualping | Page change alerts | Free-$10/mo |\n| SimilarWeb | Traffic data | Free tier |\n| BuiltWith | Tech monitoring | Free tier |\n| Owler | Company alerts | Free |\n\n## Output Format\n\n```markdown\n# Competitive Intelligence Report: [Your Business]\n\n## Executive Summary\n\n**Market Position:** [Leader / Challenger / Niche / Emerging]\n**Primary Competitors:** [Top 3]\n**Key Differentiator:** [What makes you unique]\n**Biggest Threat:** [Most dangerous competitor]\n**Biggest Opportunity:** [Gap to exploit]\n\n## Competitive Landscape\n\n### Direct Competitors\n\n#### [Competitor A]\n- **Website:** [URL]\n- **Positioning:** [Their tagline/promise]\n- **Target Customer:** [Who they serve]\n- **Pricing:** [Entry tier] - [Top tier]\n- **Strengths:** [What they do well]\n- **Weaknesses:** [Where they''re weak]\n- **Recent Moves:** [Latest announcements]\n- **Threat Level:** [High/Medium/Low]\n\n#### [Competitor B]\n[Same format]\n\n#### [Competitor C]\n[Same format]\n\n### Indirect Competitors\n- [Alternative solution 1] - [Why it''s a threat]\n- [Alternative solution 2] - [Why it''s a threat]\n\n## Feature Comparison\n\n| Feature | You | Comp A | Comp B | Comp C |\n|---------|-----|--------|--------|--------|\n| [Feature 1] | [Y/N/Partial] | [Y/N/P] | [Y/N/P] | [Y/N/P] |\n| [Feature 2] | [Y/N/Partial] | [Y/N/P] | [Y/N/P] | [Y/N/P] |\n| [Feature 3] | [Y/N/Partial] | [Y/N/P] | [Y/N/P] | [Y/N/P] |\n\n**You''re Ahead On:**\n- [Feature/capability]\n- [Feature/capability]\n\n**You''re Behind On:**\n- [Feature/capability] - [Priority: High/Med/Low]\n- [Feature/capability] - [Priority: High/Med/Low]\n\n## Pricing Landscape\n\n| Tier | You | Comp A | Comp B | Comp C | Market Position |\n|------|-----|--------|--------|--------|-----------------|\n| Entry | $X | $X | $X | $X | [Above/Below/At market] |\n| Pro | $X | $X | $X | $X | [Above/Below/At market] |\n\n**Pricing Insights:**\n- [Key insight about pricing]\n- [Opportunity or threat]\n\n## Positioning Analysis\n\n| Competitor | Position | Crowded? | Your Counter |\n|------------|----------|----------|--------------|\n| Comp A | \"[Their position]\" | Y/N | [How you differ] |\n| Comp B | \"[Their position]\" | Y/N | [How you differ] |\n\n**Recommended Positioning:**\n> \"[Your unique positioning statement that avoids crowded positions]\"\n\n## Market Gaps & Opportunities\n\n### Gap 1: [Gap Name]\n- **What:** [Description of gap]\n- **Evidence:** [How you know this is a gap]\n- **Opportunity:** [How to exploit it]\n- **Effort:** [High/Med/Low]\n- **Impact:** [High/Med/Low]\n\n### Gap 2: [Gap Name]\n[Same format]\n\n## Win/Loss Insights\n\n**Recent Wins:**\n- [Deal] vs [Competitor] - Won because: [Reason]\n- [Deal] vs [Competitor] - Won because: [Reason]\n\n**Recent Losses:**\n- [Deal] vs [Competitor] - Lost because: [Reason]\n- [Deal] vs [Competitor] - Lost because: [Reason]\n\n**Patterns:**\n- We win when: [Pattern]\n- We lose when: [Pattern]\n\n## Recommended Actions\n\n### Immediate (This Week)\n- [ ] [Action to take]\n- [ ] [Action to take]\n\n### Short-Term (30 Days)\n- [ ] [Action to take]\n- [ ] [Action to take]\n\n### Long-Term (90 Days)\n- [ ] [Strategic move]\n- [ ] [Strategic move]\n\n## Monitoring Setup\n\n**Tracking:**\n- [ ] Google Alerts for [competitor names]\n- [ ] [Tool] for [purpose]\n\n**Review Cadence:**\n- Weekly: [What to check]\n- Monthly: [What to review]\n- Quarterly: [Full refresh]\n```\n\n## Competitive Strategy Options\n\n**Ways to Compete:**\n\n| Strategy | When to Use | Example |\n|----------|-------------|---------|\n| **Better** | Have real advantage | Faster, more reliable |\n| **Cheaper** | Can sustain lower cost | Race to bottom - careful |\n| **Niche** | Underserved segment | \"CRM for dog groomers\" |\n| **Different** | Unique approach | \"The anti-[category]\" |\n| **Easier** | Complexity is pain | \"1-click setup\" |\n| **Faster** | Speed matters | \"Results in 24 hours\" |\n| **Personal** | Big players are cold | \"Indie, you talk to founder\" |\n\n**Best for Indies:** Niche, Different, Easier, Personal (avoid Better/Cheaper wars with funded competitors)\n\n## Integration with Other Skills\n\n| Skill | How It Works Together |\n|-------|----------------------|\n| `offer-architect` | Differentiate your offer based on gaps |\n| `pricing-strategist` | Price relative to market |\n| `lead-channel-optimizer` | Find channels competitors ignore |\n| `copywriter` | Write positioning/messaging |\n| `strategy-expert` | Overall competitive strategy |\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n1. **Copying competitors:** Being slightly better isn''t a strategy\n2. **Ignoring indirect competitors:** Alternative solutions matter\n3. **Feature wars:** Adding features to match is a losing game\n4. **No monitoring:** Competitors change, you should know\n5. **Obsessing too much:** Customers > competitors\n6. **Competing on price:** Race to bottom, especially vs funded\n\n## When to Route Elsewhere\n\n- If you need to **differentiate your offer** → `offer-architect`\n- If you need **pricing strategy** → `pricing-strategist`\n- If you need **market positioning copy** → `copywriter`\n- If you''re **stuck on strategy** → `execution-accelerator`\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:14:04.385Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for AI Agents like Claude Code and AutoGPT needing advanced market analysis and competitor tracking capabilities.","zh":"适合像 Claude Code 和 AutoGPT 这样的 AI 代理，它们需要高级的市场分析和竞争对手跟踪能力。","ja":"Claude Code や AutoGPT のような AI エージェントが高度な市場分析および競合他社追跡機能を必要とする場合に適しています。","ko":"클로드 코드 및 오토지피티와 같은 AI 에이전트가 고급 시장 분석 및 경쟁사 추적 기능을 필요로 할 때 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para agentes de IA como Claude Code y AutoGPT que necesitan capacidades avanzadas de análisis de mercado y seguimiento de competidores.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents d''IA comme Claude Code et AutoGPT nécessitant des capacités d''analyse de marché avancées et de suivi des concurrents.","de":"Ideal für KI-Agents wie Claude Code und AutoGPT, die erweiterte Marktanalyse- und Wettbewerber-Verfolgungsfunktionen benötigen.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de IA como Claude Code e AutoGPT que necessitam de análise de mercado avançada e capacidades de rastreamento de concorrentes.","ru":"Идеально для агентов ИИ, таких как Claude Code и AutoGPT, которым необходимы передовые возможности анализа рынка и отслеживания конкурентов.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء الذكاء الاصطناعي مثل Claude Code و AutoGPT الذين يحتاجون إلى تحليل سوق متقدم وقدرات تتبع المنافسين."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute competitive research, build monitoring systems, and provide actionable competitive insights using market gap analysis and competitor move tracking, leveraging protocols like data visualization and market intelligence gathering.","zh":"赋予代理执行竞争研究、构建监控系统并使用市场空白分析和竞争对手动向跟踪提供可行的竞争洞察力，利用数据可视化和市场智能收集等协议。","ja":"エージェントに競合研究を実行し、監視システムを構築し、マーケットギャップ分析および競合他社の動向追跡を利用して、データ視覚化や市場インテリジェンスの収集などのプロトコルを利用して、実行可能な競合の洞察を提供する力を与えます。","ko":"에이전트가 경쟁 연구를 수행하고 모니터링 시스템을 구축하며 시장 공백 분석 및 경쟁사 동향 추적을 사용하여 데이터 시각화 및 시장 지능 수집과 같은 프로토콜을 활용하여 실현 가능한 경쟁 정보를 제공할 수 있도록 합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar investigaciones competitivas, construir sistemas de monitoreo y proporcionar información competitiva accionable utilizando análisis de brechas de mercado y seguimiento de movimientos de competidores, aprovechando protocolos como visualización de datos y recopilación de inteligencia de mercado.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des recherches compétitives, de construire des systèmes de surveillance et de fournir des informations compétitives actionnables en utilisant l''analyse des lacunes du marché et le suivi des mouvements des concurrents, en exploitant des protocoles tels que la visualisation des données et la collecte de renseignements sur le marché.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, wettbewerbliche Recherchen durchzuführen, Überwachungssysteme zu erstellen und handhabbare Wettbewerbsinformationen bereitzustellen, indem sie Marktlückenanalysen und Wettbewerberverfolgung nutzen und Protokolle wie Datenvisualisierung und Marktinformationsbeschaffung ausschöpfen.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar pesquisas competitivas, construir sistemas de monitoramento e fornecer insights competitivos ações utilizando análise de lacunas de mercado e rastreamento de movimentos de concorrentes, aproveitando protocolos como visualização de dados e coleta de inteligência de mercado.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью проводить конкурентные исследования, создавать системы мониторинга и предоставлять действенные конкурентные идеи с помощью анализа пробелов рынка и отслеживания действий конкурентов, используя протоколы, такие как визуализация данных и сбор рыночной разведки.","ar":"تمكين الوكلاء من تنفيذ البحث التنافسي، وبناء أنظمة المراقبة، وتقديم رؤى تنافسية قابلة للتنفيذ باستخدام تحليل الفجوات السوقية وتتبع تحركات المنافسين، مستفيدة من البروتوكولات مثل تجسيد البيانات وجمع استخبارات السوق."},"useCases":{"en":["Monitoring competitor moves and market trends","Identifying market gaps for solo founders","Positioning offerings for maximum differentiation"],"zh":["监测竞争对手的动向和市场趋势","为独立创业者识别市场空白","将产品定位为最大化差异化"],"ja":["競合他社の動向と市場トレンドを監視する","ソロ創業者に市場のギャップを特定する","差別化の最大化のために提供を位置づける"],"ko":["경쟁사 동향 및 시장 트렌드를 모니터링하다","독립 창업자에게 시장 공백을 식별하다","차별화를 최대화하기 위해 제품을 위치시키다"],"es":["Seguimiento de movimientos de competidores y tendencias del mercado","Identificación de brechas de mercado para fundadores individuales","Posicionamiento de ofertas para una máxima diferenciación"],"fr":["Suivi des mouvements des concurrents et des tendances du marché","Identification des lacunes du marché pour les fondateurs individuels","Positionnement des offres pour une différenciation maximale"],"de":["Verfolgung von Wettbewerberbewegungen und Markttrends","Identifizierung von Marktlücken für Einzelgründer","Positionierung von Angeboten für eine maximale Differenzierung"],"pt":["Monitorar movimentos de concorrentes e tendências de mercado","Identificar lacunas de mercado para fundadores solo","Posicionar ofertas para diferenciação máxima"],"ru":["Отслеживать движения конкурентов и рыночные тенденции","Определять пробелы рынка для сольных основателей","Позиционировать предложения для максимального различия"],"ar":["مراقبة تحركات المنافسين وتوجهات السوق","تحديد الفجوات السوقية للمؤسسين المنفردين","تموضع العروض للتمييز الأقصى"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to market data and competitor information","Specialized knowledge of indie market analysis necessary"],"zh":["需要访问市场数据和竞争对手信息","需要独立市场分析的专业知识"],"ja":["市場データおよび競合他社情報へのアクセスが必要","インディーマーケット分析の専門知識が必要"],"ko":["시장 데이터 및 경쟁사 정보에 대한 액세스가 필요","독립 시장 분석에 대한 전문 지식이 필요"],"es":["Requiere acceso a datos de mercado y información de competidores","Conocimiento especializado de análisis de mercado indie necesario"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès aux données de marché et aux informations des concurrents","Connaissances spécialisées dans l''analyse de marché indie nécessaires"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf Marktdaten und Wettbewerberinformationen","Spezialisiertes Wissen über Indie-Marktanalyse erforderlich"],"pt":["Requer acesso a dados de mercado e informações de concorrentes","Conhecimento especializado de análise de mercado indie necessário"],"ru":["Требует доступа к рыночным данным и информации о конкурентах","Необходимо специализированное знание инди-рыночной аналитики"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى بيانات السوق ومعلومات المنافسين","مطلوب معرفة متخصصة بتحليل السوق المستقلة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":80}');
INSERT OR REPLACE INTO skills (id, category, owner, repo, repo_path, name, stars, forks, quality_score, updated_at, last_synced, content_hash, data_json) VALUES ('iulspop/templates-workspace/unit-tests', 'community', 'iulspop', 'templates-workspace', 'iulspop/templates-workspace', 'unit-tests', 0, 0, 20, '2026-02-18T01:08:43.475Z', '2026-02-18T09:14:11.635Z', NULL, '{"id":"iulspop/templates-workspace/unit-tests","name":"unit-tests","description":{"zh":"单元测试是软件开发中的关键步骤，确保代码的正确性和可靠性","ja":"ユニットテストはソフトウェア開発における重要なステップであり、コードの正確性と信頼性を保証する","ko":"유닛 테스트는 소프트웨어 개발의 중요한 단계로 코드의 정확성과 신뢰성을 보장한다","es":"Las pruebas unitarias son fundamentales para garantizar la calidad del código. Aprende a escribir pruebas unitarias efectivas.","fr":"Les tests unitaires sont essentiels pour garantir la qualité du code. Apprenez à écrire des tests unitaires efficaces.","de":"Unit-Tests sind grundlegend für die Sicherstellung der Code-Qualität. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie effektive Unit-Tests schreiben.","pt":"Testes unitários são fundamentais para garantir a qualidade do código. Aprenda a escrever testes eficazes para melhorar a estabilidade do seu software.","ru":"Юнит-тесты являются фундаментальными для обеспечения качества кода. Узнайте, как писать эффективные тесты для улучшения стабильности вашего программного обеспечения.","ar":"اختبارات الوحدة هي أساسية لضمان جودة الرمز. تعلم كيفية كتابة اختبارات فعالة لتحسين استقرار برنامجك.","en":""},"seo":{"title":{"zh":"单元测试技能","ja":"ユニットテストスキル","ko":"유닛 테스트 스킬","es":"Pruebas Unitarias para Desarrolladores","fr":"Tests Unitaires pour Développeurs","de":"Unit-Tests für Entwickler","pt":"Testes Unitários: Escreva Código de Teste de Alta Qualidade","ru":"Юнит-тесты: пишем высококачественный тестовый код","ar":"اختبارات الوحدة: اكتب رمز اختبار عالي الجودة","en":"unit-tests"},"description":{"zh":"单元测试是软件开发中的关键步骤，确保代码的正确性和可靠性","ja":"ユニットテストはソフトウェア開発における重要なステップであり、コードの正確性と信頼性を保証する","ko":"유닛 테스트는 소프트웨어 개발의 중요한 단계로 코드의 정확성과 신뢰성을 보장한다","es":"Las pruebas unitarias son fundamentales para garantizar la calidad del código. Aprende a escribir pruebas unitarias efectivas.","fr":"Les tests unitaires sont essentiels pour garantir la qualité du code. Apprenez à écrire des tests unitaires efficaces.","de":"Unit-Tests sind grundlegend für die Sicherstellung der Code-Qualität. Erfahren Sie, wie Sie effektive Unit-Tests schreiben.","pt":"Testes unitários são fundamentais para garantir a qualidade do código. Aprenda a escrever testes eficazes para melhorar a estabilidade do seu software.","ru":"Юнит-тесты являются фундаментальными для обеспечения качества кода. Узнайте, как писать эффективные тесты для улучшения стабильности вашего программного обес...","ar":"اختبارات الوحدة هي أساسية لضمان جودة الرمز. تعلم كيفية كتابة اختبارات فعالة لتحسين استقرار برنامجك.","en":""},"definition":{"en":""},"features":{"zh":["确保代码正确性","提高代码可靠性","减少错误和缺陷","提高开发效率","支持代码重构"],"ja":["コードの正確性を保証","コードの信頼性を高める","エラーと欠陥を減らす","開発効率を高める","コードのリファクタリングをサポート"],"ko":["코드의 정확성을 보장","코드의 신뢰성을 높인다","오류와 결함을 줄인다","개발 효율성을 높인다","코드의 리팩토링을 지원"],"es":["Escribe pruebas unitarias para garantizar la calidad del código","Verifica la unidad de código bajo prueba","Define el comportamiento esperado","Compara la salida real con la esperada","Identifica y depura errores"],"fr":["Écrivez des tests unitaires pour garantir la qualité du code","Vérifiez l''unité de code sous test","Définissez le comportement attendu","Comparez la sortie réelle avec la attendue","Identifiez et déboguez les erreurs"],"de":["Schreiben Sie Unit-Tests, um die Code-Qualität zu gewährleisten","Überprüfen Sie die Code-Einheit unter Test","Definieren Sie das erwartete Verhalten","Vergleichen Sie die tatsächliche Ausgabe mit der erwarteten","Identifizieren und debuggen Sie Fehler"],"pt":["Escrita de testes unitários eficazes","Melhoria da qualidade do código","Garantia da estabilidade do software","Criação de testes automatizados","Análise de bugs e correções"],"ru":["Написание эффективных юнит-тестов","Улучшение качества кода","Обеспечение стабильности программного обеспечения","Создание автоматизированных тестов","Анализ ошибок и исправления"],"ar":["كتابة اختبارات وحدة فعالة","تحسين جودة الرمز","ضمان استقرار البرنامج","إنشاء اختبارات آلية","تحليل الأخطاء وتصحيحها"]},"keywords":{"zh":["单元测试","软件开发","代码质量","可靠性","测试驱动开发","TDD"],"ja":["ユニットテスト","ソフトウェア開発","コード品質","信頼性","テスト駆動開発","TDD"],"ko":["유닛 테스트","소프트웨어 개발","코드 품질","신뢰성","테스트 주도 개발","TDD"],"es":["pruebas unitarias","desarrollo de software","ingeniería de software","testing","calidad del código","depuración de errores"],"fr":["tests unitaires","développement de logiciel","ingénierie de logiciel","testing","qualité du code","débogage d''erreurs"],"de":["Unit-Tests","Software-Entwicklung","Software-Ingenieurwesen","Testing","Code-Qualität","Fehler-Debugging"],"pt":["testes unitários","desenvolvimento de software","qualidade do código","estabilidade do software","testes automatizados","análise de bugs","correções de código"],"ru":["юнит-тесты","разработка программного обеспечения","качество кода","стабильность программного обеспечения","автоматизированные тесты","анализ ошибок","исправления кода"],"ar":["اختبارات الوحدة","تطوير البرمجيات","جودة الرمز","استقرار البرنامج","اختبارات آلية","تحليل الأخطاء","تصحيح الرمز"]}},"owner":"iulspop","repo":"templates-workspace","repoPath":"iulspop/templates-workspace","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.475Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"unit-tests","description":"Generates well-structured unit tests using Vitest with the given/should prose format. Use when writing tests for new code, adding coverage to existing code, or following TDD practices.","bodyPreview":"# Unit Tests\n\nAct as a top-tier software engineer with serious testing skills.\n\nWrite unit tests for: $ARGUMENTS\n\nEach test must answer these 5 questions:\n\n1. What is the unit under test? (test should be in a named describe block)\n2. What is the expected behavior? ($given and $should arguments are adequate)\n3. What is the actual output? (the unit under test was exercised by the test)\n4. What is the expected output? ($expected and/or $should are adequate)\n5. How can we find the bug? (implicitly a","body":"# Unit Tests\n\nAct as a top-tier software engineer with serious testing skills.\n\nWrite unit tests for: $ARGUMENTS\n\nEach test must answer these 5 questions:\n\n1. What is the unit under test? (test should be in a named describe block)\n2. What is the expected behavior? ($given and $should arguments are adequate)\n3. What is the actual output? (the unit under test was exercised by the test)\n4. What is the expected output? ($expected and/or $should are adequate)\n5. How can we find the bug? (implicitly answered if the above questions are answered correctly)\n\n## Rules\n\n- Use Vitest with describe, expect, and test.\n- Tests must use the \"given: ..., should: ...\" prose format.\n- Colocate tests with functions. Test files should be in the same folder as the implementation file.\n- Use cuid2 for IDs unless specified otherwise.\n- If an argument is a database entity, use an existing factory function and override values as needed.\n- Capture the `actual` and the `expected` value in variables.\n- The top-level `describe` block should describe the component under test.\n- The `test` block should describe the case via `\"given: ..., should: ...\"`.\n- Avoid `expect.any(Constructor)` in assertions. Expect specific values instead.\n- Always use the `toEqual` equality assertion.\n- Empty line before `actual` variable assignment.\n- NO empty line between `actual` and `expected` assignments.\n- Empty line after `expected` variable assignment before the `toEqual` assertion.\n- Tests must be readable, isolated, thorough, and explicit.\n- Test expected edge cases.\n- Create factory functions for reused data structures rather than sharing mutable fixtures.\n\n## When NOT to use this skill\n\n- For React component render tests (`.test.tsx`), use `/happy-dom-tests` instead.\n- For database or server action tests (`.spec.ts`), use `/integration-tests` instead.\n- For browser-level user flow tests (`.e2e.ts`), use `/e2e-tests` instead.\n- This skill is for pure function unit tests (`.test.ts`) only.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:14:11.635Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Code Analysis Agents requiring structured, deterministic test generation.","zh":"非常适合需要结构化、确定性测试生成的代码分析代理。","ja":"コード分析エージェントが構造化された決定的なテスト生成を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"구조화되고 결정적인 테스트 생성이 필요한 코드 분석 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de análisis de código que requieren generación de pruebas estructurada y determinista.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''analyse de code nécessitant une génération de tests structurée et déterministe.","de":"Perfekt für Code-Analyse-Agents, die eine strukturierte, deterministische Testgenerierung erfordern.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Análise de Código que exigem geração de testes estruturada e determinística.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов анализа кода, требующих структурированного и детерминированного генерирования тестов.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تحليل الشفرة الذي يتطلب إنشاء اختبارات منظم ومحدد."},"recommendation":{"en":"Enables systematic unit test creation following the five-question framework (unit under test, expected behavior, actual output, expected output, bug identification). It structures tests using named describe blocks and explicit $given/$should arguments for precise test specification.","zh":"使得系统化的单元测试创建遵循五个问题框架（被测试的单元、预期行为、实际输出、预期输出、缺陷识别）。它使用命名的describe块和显式的$given/$should参数来进行精确的测试规范。","ja":"システム化されたユニットテストの作成を、5つの質問フレームワーク（テスト対象のユニット、予想される動作、実際の出力、予想される出力、バグの識別）に従って可能にします。テストの仕様を正確に指定するために、命名されたdescribeブロックと明示的な$given/$should引数を使用します。","ko":"시스템적인 단위 테스트 생성을 다섯 가지 질문 프레임워크(테스트 대상 단위, 예상 동작, 실제 출력, 예상 출력, 버그 식별)를 따르도록 합니다. 명명된 describe 블록과 명시적인 $given/$should 인수를 사용하여 테스트 명세를 정확히 지정합니다.","es":"Permite la creación sistemática de pruebas unitarias siguiendo el marco de las cinco preguntas (unidad bajo prueba, comportamiento esperado, salida real, salida esperada, identificación de errores). Estructura las pruebas utilizando bloques describe con nombre y argumentos $given/$should explícitos para una especificación de prueba precisa.","fr":"Permet la création systématique de tests unitaires en suivant le cadre des cinq questions (unité à tester, comportement attendu, sortie réelle, sortie attendue, identification des bogues). Il structure les tests en utilisant des blocs describe nommés et des arguments $given/$should explicites pour une spécification de test précise.","de":"Ermöglicht die systematische Erstellung von Einheitstests unter Verwendung des Fünf-Fragen-Frameworks (zu testende Einheit, erwartetes Verhalten, tatsächliche Ausgabe, erwartete Ausgabe, Fehleridentifizierung). Es strukturiert die Tests unter Verwendung benannter describe-Blöcke und expliziter $given/$should-Argumente für eine präzise TestSpezifikation.","pt":"Permite a criação sistemática de testes unitários seguindo a estrutura de cinco perguntas (unidade em teste, comportamento esperado, saída real, saída esperada, identificação de bugs). Estrutura os testes usando blocos describe nomeados e argumentos $given/$should explícitos para especificação de teste precisa.","ru":"Позволяет создавать систематические модульные тесты, следуя рамочному подходу из пяти вопросов (модуль под тестированием, ожидаемое поведение, фактический вывод, ожидаемый вывод, выявление ошибок). Структурирует тесты с помощью именованных блоков describe и явных аргументов $given/$should для точного определения тестирования.","ar":"يسمح بإنشاء اختبارات وحدة منهجية متابعة لإطار العمل الخماسي (الوحدة قيد الاختبار، السلوك المتوقع، الإخراج الفعلي، الإخراج المتوقع، تحديد الأخطاء). يهيكل الاختبارات باستخدام كتلة وصف مسماة وحجج $given/$should صريحة لتحديد اختبار دقيق."},"useCases":{"en":["Generating comprehensive test suites for new code modules","Validating edge cases in existing functions","Creating regression tests for bug fixes","Automating test-driven development workflows"],"zh":["为新代码模块生成全面的测试套件","验证现有函数的边缘情况","为bug修复创建回归测试","自动化测试驱动的开发工作流"],"ja":["新しいコードモジュールのための包括的なテストスイートを生成する","既存の関数のエッジケースを検証する","バグ修正のための回帰テストを作成する","テスト駆動開発のワークフローを自動化する"],"ko":["새 코드 모듈을 위한 포괄적인 테스트 스위트 생성","기존 함수의 에지 케이스 검증","버그 수정을 위한 회귀 테스트 생성","테스트 주도 개발 워크플로 자동화"],"es":["Generación de suites de pruebas comprehensivas para nuevos módulos de código","Validación de casos límite en funciones existentes","Creación de pruebas de regresión para correcciones de errores","Automatización de flujos de trabajo de desarrollo dirigido por pruebas"],"fr":["Génération de suites de tests complètes pour les nouveaux modules de code","Validation des cas limites dans les fonctions existantes","Création de tests de régression pour les corrections de bogues","Automatisation des flux de travail de développement dirigé par les tests"],"de":["Generierung umfassender Test-Suites für neue Code-Module","Validierung von Randfällen in bestehenden Funktionen","Erstellung von Regressions-Tests für Fehlerbehebungen","Automatisierung von testgetriebenen Entwicklungs-Workflows"],"pt":["Geração de conjuntos de testes abrangentes para novos módulos de código","Validação de casos de bordo em funções existentes","Criação de testes de regressão para correções de bugs","Automação de fluxos de trabalho de desenvolvimento orientado a testes"],"ru":["Генерирование полных наборов тестов для новых модулей кода","Проверка граничных случаев в существующих функциях","Создание регрессионных тестов для исправления ошибок","Автоматизация потоков работы тест-ориентированного развития"],"ar":["إنشاء مجموعة شاملة من الاختبارات لوحدات الشفرة الجديدة","تحقق من حالات الحدود في الوظائف الحالية","إنشاء اختبارات انحدار لتصحيح الأخطاء","تأتمة سير عمل التطوير الموجه بالاختبارات"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires precise function signatures and specifications","Limited to test generation (does not execute tests)","Depends on quality of input arguments for test coverage"],"zh":["需要精确的函数签名和规范","仅限于测试生成（不执行测试）","依赖于输入参数的质量来进行测试覆盖"],"ja":["正確な関数シグネチャと仕様が必要","テスト生成のみ（テストの実行は行わない）","テストカバレッジの品質は入力引数の品質に依存する"],"ko":["정확한 함수 시그니처와 사양이 필요","테스트 생성만 가능(테스트 실행은 하지 않음)","테스트 커버리지의 품질은 입력 인자의 품질에 의존"],"es":["Requiere firmas de función y especificaciones precisas","Limitado a la generación de pruebas (no ejecuta pruebas)","Depende de la calidad de los argumentos de entrada para la cobertura de pruebas"],"fr":["Nécessite des signatures de fonction et des spécifications précises","Limité à la génération de tests (n''exécute pas les tests)","Dépend de la qualité des arguments d''entrée pour la couverture des tests"],"de":["Erfordert präzise Funktions-Signaturen und Spezifikationen","Begrenzt auf Testgenerierung (führt keine Tests aus)","Hängt von der Qualität der Eingabe-Argumente für die Testabdeckung ab"],"pt":["Exige assinaturas de função precisas e especificações","Limitado à geração de testes (não executa testes)","Depende da qualidade dos argumentos de entrada para cobertura de testes"],"ru":["Требует точных сигнатур функций и спецификаций","Ограничен генерацией тестов (не выполняет тесты)","Зависит от качества входных аргументов для покрытия тестирования"],"ar":["يتطلب التوقيعات الدقيقة للوظائف والمواصفات","محدود بالاختبارات المولدة (لا ينفذ الاختبارات)","يعتمد على جودة الحجج المدخلة لتغطية الاختبار"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":20}');
