námicos que mejora la productividad en proyectos de desarrollo","fr":"Invowk Schema est un outil d''exécution de commandes dynamiques qui améliore la productivité dans les projets de développement","de":"Invowk Schema ist ein Werkzeug für die dynamische Ausführung von Befehlen, das die Produktivität in Entwicklungsprojekten verbessert","pt":"O Invowk Schema é uma ferramenta para gerenciar comandos e implementações em projetos de desenvolvimento de software","ru":"Invowk Schema — это инструмент для управления командами и реализациями в проектах разработки программного обеспечения","ar":"إينفوك سكيما هو أداة لإدارة الأوامر والتنفيذ في مشاريع تطوير البرمجيات","en":"''invowk'' is a dynamically extensible command runner, kinda like ''task'' and ''just'' but with its own superpowers."},"definition":{"en":"''invowk'' is a dynamically extensible command runner, kinda like ''task'' and ''just'' but with its own superpowers."},"features":{"zh":["动态可扩展","命令结构管理","跨平台支持","虚拟运行时支持","模块化设计"],"ja":["動的に拡張可能","コマンド構造管理","クロスプラットフォーム対応","仮想ランタイム対応","モジュール化設計"],"ko":["동적으로 확장 가능","명령 구조 관리","크로스 플랫폼 지원","가상 런타임 지원","모듈화 설계"],"es":["Ejecución de comandos dinámicos","Compatibilidad con módulos de ejemplo"," Selección de tiempo de ejecución en diferentes plataformas","Actualización automática de ejemplos","Soporte para definiciones de invowkfile"],"fr":["Exécution de commandes dynamiques","Compatibilité avec les modules d''exemple","Sélection du runtime sur différentes plateformes","Mise à jour automatique des exemples","Prise en charge des définitions de invowkfile"],"de":["Dynamische Ausführung von Befehlen","Kompatibilität mit Beispielmodulen","Auswahl des Laufzeitumfelds auf verschiedenen Plattformen","Automatische Aktualisierung von Beispielen","Unterstützung für invowkfile-Definitionen"],"pt":["Edição do arquivo invowkfile.cue","Trabalho com módulos de exemplo em modules/","Adição ou modificação de estruturas de comando e implementação","Seleção de tempo de execução cruzada-plataforma"],"ru":["Редактирование файла invowkfile.cue","Работа с примерами модулей в modules/","Добавление или изменение структур команд и реализаций","Выбор кросс-платформенного времени выполнения"],"ar":["تحرير ملف invowkfile.cue","العمل مع نماذج الوحدات في modules/","إضافة أو تعديل هياكل الأوامر والتنفيذ","اختيار وقت تشغيل متقاطع-المنصات"]},"keywords":{"zh":["Invowk Schema","命令运行器","动态可扩展","跨平台支持","虚拟运行时","模块化设计","开发工具"],"ja":["Invowk スキーマ","コマンド実行器","動的に拡張可能","クロスプラットフォーム対応","仮想ランタイム","モジュール化設計","開発ツール"],"ko":["Invowk 스키마","명령 실행기","동적으로 확장 가능","크로스 플랫폼 지원","가상 런타임","모듈화 설계","개발 도구"],"es":["invowk schema","ejecución de comandos dinámicos","desarrollo de software","productividad en desarrollo","herramientas de desarrollo","invowkfile","módulos de ejemplo","selección de runtime"],"fr":["invowk schema","exécution de commandes dynamiques","développement de logiciels","productivité en développement","outils de développement","invowkfile","modules d''exemple","sélection de runtime"],"de":["invowk schema","dynamische Befehlsausführung","Softwareentwicklung","Produktivität in der Entwicklung","Entwicklungstools","invowkfile","Beispielmodule","Laufzeitumfeldauswahl"],"pt":["Invowk Schema","configuração de invowk","gerenciamento de comandos","desenvolvimento de software","produtividade do projeto","exemplos de invowkfile"],"ru":["Invowk Schema","конфигурация invowk","управление командами","разработка программного обеспечения","производительность проекта","примеры invowkfile"],"ar":["إينفوك سكيما","تهيئة إينفوك","إدارة الأوامر","تطوير البرمجيات","إنتاجية المشروع","أمثلة invowkfile"]}},"owner":"invowk","repo":"invowk","repoPath":"invowk/invowk","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-02-18T01:08:43.476Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"invowk-schema","description":"Schema guidelines for invowkfile.cue and modules/*.invowkmod, cross-platform runtime patterns, command implementations, capability checks, environment variables.","bodyPreview":"# Invowk Schema Guidelines\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Editing the `invowkfile.cue` root example file\n- Working with sample modules in `modules/`\n- Adding or modifying command/implementation structures\n- Handling cross-platform runtime selection (native vs virtual runtimes on different platforms)\n\n---\n\n## Invowkfile Examples\n\n### Built-in Examples (`invowkfile.cue` at project root)\n\n- Always update the example file when invowkfile definitions or features are added, modified, or removed.\n- All comman","body":"# Invowk Schema Guidelines\n\nUse this skill when:\n- Editing the `invowkfile.cue` root example file\n- Working with sample modules in `modules/`\n- Adding or modifying command/implementation structures\n- Handling cross-platform runtime selection (native vs virtual runtimes on different platforms)\n\n---\n\n## Invowkfile Examples\n\n### Built-in Examples (`invowkfile.cue` at project root)\n\n- Always update the example file when invowkfile definitions or features are added, modified, or removed.\n- All commands should be idempotent and not cause any side effects on the host.\n- No commands should be related to building invowk itself or manipulating any of its source code.\n- Examples should range from simple (e.g., native \"hello-world\") to complex (e.g., container \"hello-world\" with `enable_host_ssh`).\n- Examples should cover different features, such as:\n  - Native vs. container execution.\n  - Volume mounts for container execution.\n  - Environment variables.\n  - Host SSH access enabled vs. disabled.\n  - Capabilities checks (with and without alternatives).\n  - Tools checks (with and without alternatives).\n  - Custom checks (with and without alternatives).\n  - Runtime-level `depends_on` (container only — validated inside the container environment, not on host).\n- Module metadata does not belong in invowkfile examples; it lives in `invowkmod.cue` for modules.\n\n### Runtime-Level `depends_on` Pattern (Container Only)\n\n`depends_on` can be placed inside a **container** runtime block to validate against the **container''s own environment** (not the host). This is distinct from root/command/implementation-level `depends_on`, which always validates against the **host system**. Runtime-level `depends_on` is only available for the container runtime — native and virtual runtimes do not support it (CUE schema rejects it at parse time).\n\n```cue\nruntimes: [{\n    name: \"container\"\n    image: \"debian:stable-slim\"\n    // Validated INSIDE the container\n    depends_on: {\n        tools: [{alternatives: [\"python3\"]}]\n    }\n}]\n// Validated on the HOST\ndepends_on: {\n    tools: [{alternatives: [\"docker\"]}]\n}\n```\n\n### Command Structure Validation\n\n#### Leaf-Only Args Constraint\n\n**Commands with positional arguments (`args`) cannot have subcommands.** This is enforced during command discovery and module validation.\n\nWhy: CLI parsers interpret positional arguments after a command name as potential subcommand names. If `deploy` has both `args: [{name: \"env\"}]` and a subcommand `deploy staging`, running `invowk cmd deploy prod` is ambiguous—is `prod` an argument or a subcommand name?\n\n**Valid:**\n```cue\n// Leaf command with args (no subcommands)\ncmds: [\n    {name: \"deploy\", args: [{name: \"env\"}], ...}\n]\n\n// Parent command with subcommands (no args on parent)\ncmds: [\n    {name: \"deploy\"},           // No args here\n    {name: \"deploy staging\"},   // Subcommand\n    {name: \"deploy prod\"},      // Subcommand\n]\n```\n\n**Invalid:**\n```cue\ncmds: [\n    {name: \"deploy\", args: [{name: \"env\"}], ...},  // Has args\n    {name: \"deploy staging\", ...}                   // Is a subcommand of deploy\n]\n// Error: command ''deploy'' has both args and subcommands\n```\n\nThis validation runs:\n1. During `invowk cmd` execution (command discovery)\n2. During `invowk module validate --deep`\n\n### Cross-Platform Runtime Selection\n\n**Bash scripts with native+virtual runtimes must use platform-specific implementations.**\n\n**The problem:** The native runtime on Windows uses PowerShell (or `cmd`), which cannot parse bash syntax. When a command declares `runtimes: [{name: \"native\"}, {name: \"virtual\"}]`, the first runtime (native) becomes the default. This causes bash scripts to fail on Windows with PowerShell parser errors.\n\n**The solution:** Split implementations by platform:\n- **Linux/macOS**: Use `runtimes: [{name: \"native\"}, {name: \"virtual\"}]` with `platforms: [{name: \"linux\"}, {name: \"macos\"}]`\n- **Windows**: Use `runtimes: [{name: \"virtual\"}]` with `platforms: [{name: \"windows\"}]` (virtual runtime uses `mvdan/sh`, a cross-platform POSIX shell)\n\n**Valid (platform-specific implementations):**\n```cue\nimplementations: [\n    {\n        script: \"\"\"\n            echo \"Hello from bash\"\n            if [ -f /etc/os-release ]; then\n                cat /etc/os-release\n            fi\n            \"\"\"\n        runtimes:  [{name: \"native\"}, {name: \"virtual\"}]\n        platforms: [{name: \"linux\"}, {name: \"macos\"}]\n    },\n    {\n        script: \"\"\"\n            echo \"Hello from bash\"\n            if [ -f /etc/os-release ]; then\n                cat /etc/os-release\n            fi\n            \"\"\"\n        runtimes:  [{name: \"virtual\"}]\n        platforms: [{name: \"windows\"}]\n    },\n]\n```\n\n**Invalid (bash script without platform restriction):**\n```cue\nimplementations: [\n    {\n        script: \"\"\"\n            echo \"Hello from bash\"\n            if [ -f /etc/os-release ]; then\n                cat /etc/os-release\n            fi\n            \"\"\"\n        runtimes: [{name: \"native\"}, {name: \"virtual\"}]\n        // Missing platforms restriction - will fail on Windows!\n    },\n]\n```\n\n**When to apply this pattern:**\n- Any command with bash/POSIX shell scripts\n- That declares both native and virtual runtimes\n- And should work on Windows\n\n**Exceptions (no split needed):**\n- Commands with `runtimes: [{name: \"virtual\"}]` only (already cross-platform)\n- Commands with `runtimes: [{name: \"native\"}]` only and `platforms: [{name: \"linux\"}, {name: \"macos\"}]` (Linux/macOS only)\n- Commands with PowerShell scripts intended for Windows\n\n**Native-only platform-split pattern (for testing):**\n\nWhen writing native runtime mirror tests (`native_*.txtar`), use native-only implementations without a virtual fallback:\n\n```cue\nimplementations: [\n    {\n        script: \"\"\"\n            echo \"Hello from native shell\"\n            echo \"VAR=$MY_VAR\"\n            \"\"\"\n        runtimes:  [{name: \"native\"}]\n        platforms: [{name: \"linux\"}, {name: \"macos\"}]\n    },\n    {\n        script: \"\"\"\n            Write-Output \"Hello from native shell\"\n            Write-Output \"VAR=$($env:MY_VAR)\"\n            \"\"\"\n        runtimes:  [{name: \"native\"}]\n        platforms: [{name: \"windows\"}]\n    },\n]\n```\n\n**When to use native-only vs native+virtual:**\n- **Native-only** (`runtimes: [{name: \"native\"}]`): For test files that specifically validate native shell behavior on each platform. Used in `native_*.txtar` mirror tests.\n- **Native+virtual** (`runtimes: [{name: \"native\"}, {name: \"virtual\"}]`): For production commands that prefer native shell but fall back to virtual shell. Requires the standard platform-split pattern (see above) to avoid PowerShell parsing bash syntax on Windows.\n\n## Invowkmod Modules\n\n### Samples (`modules/` directory)\n\nThe `modules/` directory contains sample modules that serve as reference implementations and validation tests.\n\n- A module is a `.invowkmod` directory containing `invowkmod.cue` (metadata) and `invowkfile.cue` (commands).\n- The invowkmod schema lives in `pkg/invowkmod/invowkmod_schema.cue` and the invowkfile schema in `pkg/invowkfile/invowkfile_schema.cue`.\n- Always update sample modules when the invowkmod schema, validation rules, or module behavior changes.\n- Modules should demonstrate module-specific features (script file references, cross-platform paths, requirements).\n- After module-related changes, run validation: `go run . module validate modules/<module-name>.invowkmod --deep`.\n\n### Current Sample Modules\n\n- `io.invowk.sample.invowkmod` - Minimal cross-platform module with a simple greeting command.\n\n### Module Validation Checklist\n\nWhen modifying module-related code, verify:\n1. All modules in `modules/` pass validation: `go run . module validate modules/*.invowkmod --deep`.\n2. Module naming conventions and module ID matching are enforced.\n3. `invowkmod.cue` is required and parsed; `invowkfile.cue` contains only commands.\n4. Script path resolution works correctly (forward slashes, relative paths).\n5. Nested module detection works correctly.\n6. The `pkg/invowkmod/` tests pass: `go test -v ./pkg/invowkmod/...`.\n\n## Common Pitfalls\n\n| Pitfall | Symptom | Fix |\n|---------|---------|-----|\n| Stale sample modules | Validation fails after schema changes | Update modules in `modules/` after module-related changes |\n| Missing platform restrictions | Bash scripts fail on Windows | Add platform-specific implementations for native+virtual runtimes |\n| Args with subcommands | Discovery validation error | Commands with positional args cannot have subcommands |\n| Treating Unix `/...` paths as universally absolute in config tests | Windows short CI fails on include path validation | For `includes` fixtures, use `t.TempDir()` + `filepath.Join(...)` and keep relative negatives explicit |\n\nFor path handling in implementations, see `.agents/rules/windows.md`.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-02-18T09:18:37.474Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Task Automation Agents needing dynamic command running and cross-platform compatibility.","zh":"非常适合需要动态命令运行和跨平台兼容性的任务自动化代理。","ja":"タスクの自動化エージェントが動的なコマンド実行とクロスプラットフォームの互換性を必要とする場合に最適です。","ko":"동적 명령 실행 및 크로스 플랫폼 호환성이 필요한 태스크 자동화 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de automatización de tareas que necesitan ejecución de comandos dinámicos y compatibilidad entre plataformas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents d''automatisation de tâches nécessitant l''exécution de commandes dynamiques et la compatibilité multi-plateforme.","de":"Perfekt für Task-Automatisierungsagenten, die dynamische Befehlsausführung und Plattformübergreifende Kompatibilität benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Automação de Tarefas que necessitam de execução de comandos dinâmicos e compatibilidade entre plataformas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов автоматизации задач, требующих динамического выполнения команд и跨платформенной совместимости.","ar":"مثالي لعميل تلقائي للقيام بالمهام الذي يحتاج إلى تشغيل الأوامر الديناميكي وتوافق عبر المنصات."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to execute tasks with invowk''s superpowers, utilizing `invowkfile.cue` for configuration and handling native vs virtual runtimes on different platforms via cross-platform runtime selection.","zh":"赋予代理执行任务的能力，利用invowk的超级能力，使用`invowkfile.cue`进行配置，并通过跨平台运行时选择在不同平台上处理本地和虚拟运行时。","ja":"エージェントにタスクを実行する能力を与え、invowkの超能力を利用し、`invowkfile.cue`を使用して構成し、クロスプラットフォームランタイム選択を介してさまざまなプラットフォームでネイティブと仮想ランタイムを処理します。","ko":"에이전트가 태스크를 실행할 수 있는 능력을 부여하여 invowk의 초월적인 능력을 활용하고 `invowkfile.cue`를 사용하여 구성하며 다양한 플랫폼에서 네이티브와 가상 런타임을 처리하기위한 크로스 플랫폼 런타임 선택을 통해 처리합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a ejecutar tareas con los superpoderes de invowk, utilizando `invowkfile.cue` para la configuración y el manejo de entornos de ejecución nativos y virtuales en diferentes plataformas a través de la selección de entorno de ejecución multiplataforma.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''exécuter des tâches avec les superpouvoirs d''invowk, en utilisant `invowkfile.cue` pour la configuration et la gestion des environnements d''exécution natifs et virtuels sur différentes plateformes via la sélection d''environnement d''exécution multi-plateforme.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Aufgaben mit den Superkräften von invowk auszuführen, indem sie `invowkfile.cue` für die Konfiguration und die Handhabung von nativen und virtuellen Laufzeitumgebungen auf verschiedenen Plattformen über die Auswahl der Laufzeitumgebung für mehrere Plattformen verwenden.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a executar tarefas com os superpoderes do invowk, utilizando `invowkfile.cue` para configuração e tratamento de ambientes de tempo de execução nativos e virtuais em diferentes plataformas via seleção de tempo de execução entre plataformas.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью выполнять задачи с помощью суперспособностей invowk, используя `invowkfile.cue` для конфигурации и обработки родных и виртуальных сред выполнения на разных платформах через выбор среды выполнения между платформами.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء القدرة على تشغيل المهام باستخدام صلاحيات invowk الفائقة، وذلك باستخدام `invowkfile.cue` للكوين والتلاعب بالبيئات الأصلية والإفتراضية في منصات مختلفة عبر اختيار وقت تشغيل بين المنصات."},"useCases":{"en":["Editing invowkfile definitions","Implementing command structures in modules","Handling runtime selection for native and virtual environments"],"zh":["编辑invowkfile定义","在模块中实现命令结构","处理运行时选择以适应本地和虚拟环境"],"ja":["invowkfile定義の編集","モジュール内でコマンド構造を実装","ネイティブ環境と仮想環境の両方に対応するランタイム選択の処理"],"ko":["invowkfile 정의 편집","모듈 내에서 명령 구조 구현","네이티브 환경 및 가상 환경을 위한 런타임 선택 처리"],"es":["Edición de definiciones de invowkfile","Implementación de estructuras de comandos en módulos","Manejo de la selección de entorno de ejecución para entornos nativos y virtuales"],"fr":["Édition des définitions d''invowkfile","Mise en œuvre des structures de commandes dans les modules","Gestion de la sélection d''environnement d''exécution pour les environnements natifs et virtuels"],"de":["Bearbeitung von invowkfile-Definitionen","Implementierung von Befehlsstrukturen in Modulen","Handhabung der Laufzeitumgebungsauswahl für native und virtuelle Umgebungen"],"pt":["Edição de definições do invowkfile","Implementação de estruturas de comando em módulos","Tratamento da seleção de tempo de execução para ambientes nativos e virtuais"],"ru":["Редактирование определений invowkfile","Реализация структур команд в модулях","Обработка выбора среды выполнения для родных и виртуальных окружений"],"ar":["تحرير تعريفات invowkfile","تنفيذ هياكل الأوامر في الوحدات","معالجة اختيار وقت التشغيل للبيئات الأصلية والإفتراضية"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires invowkfile.cue configuration","Cross-platform compatibility may vary depending on the platform"],"zh":["需要invowkfile.cue配置","跨平台兼容性可能会根据平台而有所不同"],"ja":["invowkfile.cue構成が必要","クロスプラットフォームの互換性はプラットフォームによって異なる場合があり"],"ko":["invowkfile.cue 구성이 필요","크로스 플랫폼 호환성은 플랫폼에 따라 다를 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere configuración de invowkfile.cue","La compatibilidad entre plataformas puede variar dependiendo de la plataforma"],"fr":["Nécessite une configuration de invowkfile.cue","La compatibilité multi-plateforme peut varier en fonction de la plateforme"],"de":["Benötigt invowkfile.cue-Konfiguration","Die Plattformübergreifende Kompatibilität kann je nach Plattform variieren"],"pt":["Requer configuração do invowkfile.cue","A compatibilidade entre plataformas pode variar dependendo da plataforma"],"ru":["Требует конфигурации invowkfile.cue","Совместимость между платформами может варьироваться в зависимости от платформы"],"ar":["يتطلب تكوين invowkfile.cue","يمكن أن تختلف التوافقية بين المنصات حسب المنصة"]},"version":3},"qualityScore":50}');
